  "Angel's Envy Cask Strength|Swordfish": "Angel's Envy Cask Strength's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Angel's Envy Cask Strength lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Angel's Envy Cask Strength|The Tomahawk": "Angel's Envy Cask Strength's cask-strength juniper-maple character finds register with the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the whiskey weight settles into the bone-in cut, and the juniper sharpens the char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Angel's Envy Cask Strength|Tomato Basil": "Angel's Envy Cask Strength's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the bourbon backbone carries the tomato basil, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; curated character over-specified.",
  "Angel's Envy Cask Strength|Truffle Fries": "AE Cask Strength with truffle fries — cask-strength AE against truffle-parmesan. Strong; AE CS's port-finish at cask-strength meets the earthy-rich at premium register.",
  "Angel's Envy Cask Strength|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Angel's Envy Cask Strength's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Angel's Envy Cask Strength belongs on the steak course.",
  "Angel's Envy Cask Strength|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Angel's Envy Cask Strength's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the bourbon backbone carries the curry, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; EHT Full Proof is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Asparagus": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the oak depth lays under the asparagus, and the oak frames the side. Works; Old World complexity wasted on salad simplicity.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet triple-cask-finished AE. Works; AE Triple Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Beignets": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the caramel-spice register matches the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; multi-distillery complexity doesn't drive.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Bone Marrow": "AE Triple Cask with bone marrow — triple-cask AE against umami fat. Works; AE Triple Cask's layered character sits alongside marrow; AE Cask Strength handles marrow intensity better.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Bone-In Filet": "AE Triple Cask with the bone-in filet — AE triple-cask against tenderloin-with-bone. Excellent; AE Triple Cask's layered-finish character frames the cut at distinctive register.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Broccoli Cheddar": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the brown-spirit warmth threads the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; CC 43 Year is over-specified for a soup; save the rare bottle.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Broccolini": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the bourbon depth settles into the broccolini, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Brussels and Belly": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the bourbon weight handles the pork-belly plate, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Works; the complex character gives the dessert a refined frame; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Burrata": "AE Triple Cask with burrata — AE triple-cask against fresh dairy. Avoid; bourbon weight wrong for burrata.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Butternut Squash": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bourbon weight handles the squash bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; extended-aged home-state pour wasted on salad.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Carrot Cake": "AE Triple Cask with carrot cake — multi-cask-finished AE against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; AE Triple Cask's layered-cask character threads the cake with more complexity than flagship AE's port-only approach.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Cheesecake": "AE Triple Cask with cheesecake — AE triple-cask against custard. Strong; AE Triple Cask's layered-cask character threads the cheesecake with distinctive complexity.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Chilean Seabass": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Angel's Envy Triple Cask for the steak course.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Chocolate Brownie": "Chocolate Brownie: warm cocoa meets AE's triple-cask-finished limited release (port + additional casks), multi-cask layered finish. AE Triple Cask's layered multi-cask character is the featured distinctive-wine-finished-chocolate pairing — the additional cask layers add complexity to port-and-chocolate no other AE expression matches. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Chocolate Cake": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the bourbon weight handles the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the extra proof overpowers this dish.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Clam Chowder": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon body sits with the chowder, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; the smooth character gives the dessert a composed frame.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Cowboy Ribeye": "AE Triple Cask with the cowboy ribeye — multi-cask-finished AE against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Strong; AE Triple Cask frames the ribeye at distinctive register; AE Cask Strength's 117+ proof is better for cap-fat.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Crab Cake": "AE Triple Cask with crab cake — multi-cask AE against delicate lump crab. Avoid; bourbon wrong for seafood. Reach for a vodka or gin.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Creamed Spinach": "AE Triple Cask with creamed spinach — multi-cask AE against dairy-rich side. Works; AE Triple Cask's layered character rides the cream at distinctive register.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Creamy Potato": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the bourbon backbone carries the potato soup, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Creme Brulee": "Creme Brulee: vanilla custard and caramelized sugar meet triple-cask-finished AE. Strong; AE Triple Cask's multi-cask layers find the caramel with distinctive complexity.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Escargot": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's spice-vanilla character holds steady against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon weight grips the savory plate, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Faroe Island Salmon": "AE Triple Cask with the salmon — triple-cask AE against oily salmon. Avoid; wine-finished bourbon wrong for fish.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Filet Mignon": "AE Triple Cask with the filet — triple-cask-finished AE against tenderloin. Excellent; AE Triple Cask's multi-cask layered character frames tenderloin with distinctive triple-finish gravitas.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|French Onion": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the bourbon depth settles into the French onion, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; craft-blend over-specified.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Grilled Caesar": "AE Triple Cask with the grilled Caesar — multi-cask AE against charred romaine and anchovy. Works; AE Triple Cask meets the char at distinctive register.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Gumbo": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the bourbon depth settles into the gumbo, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; AE's fruity-jammy character engages the bleu at wine-finish register.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the bourbon body sits with the honey carrots, and the oak softens the caramelized sugar. Works; complexity wasted on salad.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|House Wedge": "AE Triple Cask with the House Wedge — AE triple-cask against iceberg and bleu. Works; AE Triple Cask's layered character engages the bleu at distinctive register.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Kansas City": "AE Triple Cask with the KC — triple-cask AE against an 18oz strip. Strong; AE Triple Cask handles the strip with layered-finish character; AE Cask Strength is the featured wine-finished-KC match.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Loaded Potato": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the bourbon backbone carries the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; the match is gentle and approachable.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Lobster Mac": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the lobster mac, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; boutique at matched register.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Market Fish": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Angel's Envy Triple Cask lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Mocha Creme": "AE Triple Cask with mocha creme — AE triple-cask finish against coffee-chocolate dessert. Excellent; AE Triple Cask's layered-cask character is the featured AE-mocha pairing — additional cask complexity threads coffee-and-cocoa distinctively.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Mushroom Bisque": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the bourbon depth settles into the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Mushrooms": "AE Triple Cask with mushrooms — AE triple-cask finish against earthy umami. Strong; AE Triple Cask's layered-cask character threads mushrooms at distinctive register.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Peanut Butter Brownie: peanut butter and cocoa meet triple-cask AE. AE Triple Cask's multi-cask layers handle dessert density with distinctive layered character. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Porterhouse": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character: the bourbon depth settles into the dual-cut steak, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; composed premium match.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Prime Tartare": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's spice-vanilla character finds register with the tartare's raw beef and brine — the bourbon depth cuts the umami fat, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Rainbow Trout": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Angel's Envy Triple Cask for the steak course.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Roast Half Chicken": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the bourbon depth settles into the roast chicken, and the vanilla softens the plate. Works; flagship depth gives the dessert premium aged character.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the oak depth lays under the chickpea soup, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; JW Blue is over-specified for the side — save the rare-cask bottle for the protein course.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Angel's Envy Triple Cask lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the bourbon depth settles into the garlic spinach, and the oak frames the side. Works; narrative-bourbon doesn't drive.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Seafood Tower": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Angel's Envy Triple Cask belongs on the steak course.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Seared Scallops": "AE Triple Cask with seared scallops — triple-cask-finished AE against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Seasonal Soup": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the caramel-spice register matches the seasonal soup, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; bonded weight a touch ambitious for the dessert.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Seasonal Vegetables": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the bourbon weight handles the seasonal vegetables, and the rounded sweetness brightens the side. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Shrimp Bisque": "AE Triple Cask with shrimp bisque — multi-cask AE against cream-shrimp soup. Avoid; wine-fruit clashes with seafood soup.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Shrimp Cocktail": "AE Triple Cask with shrimp cocktail — multi-cask AE against cold shrimp. Avoid; bourbon wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Swordfish": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon's sweet weight crowds the rare crust's clean char. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Angel's Envy Triple Cask lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|The Tomahawk": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's spice-vanilla character holds the line with the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the aged-oak weight carries the flame-grilled char, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Tomato Basil": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the oak depth lays under the tomato basil, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Truffle Fries": "AE Triple Cask with truffle fries — multi-cask AE against truffle-parmesan. Strong; AE Triple Cask's layered character meets the earthy-rich with distinctive complexity.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Angel's Envy Triple Cask on the steak course instead.",
  "Angel's Envy Triple Cask|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the oak depth lays under the curry, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; milestone-release covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Angel's Envy|Asparagus": "Angel's Envy's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the oak depth lays under the asparagus, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the side. Works; Voyage 23 frames the two-cut plate at ocean-finish register.",
  "Angel's Envy|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Angel's Envy with the au gratin — flagship AE against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; AE's port-finish handles the richness at wine-finish register.",
  "Angel's Envy|Beignets": "Angel's Envy's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the caramel-spice register matches the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; stout-barrel story wasted on salad.",
  "Angel's Envy|Bone Marrow": "Angel's Envy with bone marrow — port-finished bourbon against umami fat. Works; AE at 86.6 proof is under-specified for marrow intensity; AE Cask Strength handles marrow better.",
