  "Angel's Envy|Broccolini": "Angel's Envy's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the broccolini's tender green stalks: the bourbon backbone carries the broccolini, and the oak-and-spice register settles the side. Works; JD Bonded's backbone handles the richness at Bonded register.",
  "Angel's Envy|Brussels and Belly": "Angel's Envy: port-finished Kentucky bourbon, the flagship. Excellent on Brussels and Belly; port-finish-sweetness amplifies maple-glaze at flagship register — textbook AE-on-Brussels. Gold standard; pour without second-guessing.",
  "Angel's Envy|Burrata": "Angel's Envy with burrata — port-finished bourbon against fresh dairy. Avoid; bourbon weight wrong for burrata.",
  "Angel's Envy|Butternut Squash": "Angel's Envy's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bourbon depth settles into the squash bisque, and the caramel softens the cream. Works; HH 20's aged character meets the glaze at collector register.",
  "Angel's Envy|Carrot Cake": "Angel's Envy with carrot cake — port-finished bourbon against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; AE's port-derived jammy-fruit is the featured wine-finished-carrot-cake pairing — the port-and-cake bridge works where straight-bourbon doesn't.",
  "Angel's Envy|Cheesecake": "Angel's Envy with cheesecake — flagship AE port-finish against custard. Strong; AE's jammy-fruit threads the cheesecake at wine-finish register.",
  "Angel's Envy|Chilean Seabass": "Angel's Envy's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Angel's Envy for the steak course.",
  "Angel's Envy|Chocolate Brownie": "Angel's Envy with the chocolate brownie — flagship Angel's Envy port-finished bourbon, Louisville KY, 86.6 proof, fruity-jammy softer-oak from Portuguese port casks. Excellent; AE's port-derived jammy-fruit marries cocoa at the featured wine-finished-bourbon-chocolate pairing — port-and-chocolate is textbook, and AE brings it at flagship register.",
