  "Asparagus|Crab Cake": "Crab Cake alongside the asparagus -- the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust meets the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: both light, the meal stays composed. Works; no conflict, the meal builds.",
  "Asparagus|Cragganmore 12": "Cragganmore 12's complex Speyside character finds neutral with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the malt-and-oak threads the asparagus, and the heather brightens the side. Works; CC 43 Year is over-specified for a soup; save the rare bottle.",
  "Asparagus|Creamy Potato": "The potato soup alongside the asparagus -- the bright cuts the rich cleanly. Works; the table can build them in order or together.",
  "Asparagus|Creme Brulee": "Asparagus and the brulee -- bright meets sweet, the contrast stays light. Works; clean transition or together if the table wants.",
  "Asparagus|Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée": "Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée's cherry-earth tannin sits alongside the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the medium-body red frames the green plate, and the spice lifts the green plate. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Asparagus|Crown Royal": "Crown Royal's classic Canadian blend smoothness leans against the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the Canadian-whisky body sits with the asparagus, and the caramel rounds the side. Works; save the collector bottle for the protein course.",
  "Asparagus|Cucumber Gimlet": "Hendrick's, cucumber, lime, ginger syrup, soda. The garden-fresh profile meshes with asparagus's vegetal character directly and the citrus cuts the char. Works as gin cocktail for asparagus — garden-to-plate route; Sauv Blanc and Sancerre peak higher on sulfur notes.",
  "Asparagus|Dalmore 12": "Dalmore 12's sherry-finished Highland character sits alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the malt-and-oak threads the asparagus, and the malt edge frames the side. Works; KBS distinctiveness is slightly over-specified for the two-cut plate.",
  "Asparagus|Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge": "Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge's crisp earth-mineral tannin sits beside the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the medium-body red frames the green plate, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Asparagus|Darioush Cabernet Franc": "Darioush Cabernet Franc's herbaceous Cab Franc with red-fruit and bell-pepper overshadows the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- red weight crowds a green side without lifting it — needs crisp register, not tannin. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Darioush Cabernet Franc on the steak course instead.",
  "Asparagus|Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- tannin on raw green vegetable reads astringent without payoff. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Asparagus|Detroit City Gin": "Detroit City Gin's bold char-juniper botanicals plays cleanly against the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the spice lifts the green plate. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
