  "Asparagus|Les Pallières Raciné": "Les Pallières Raciné's bold earth-mineral cassis holds with the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the spice lifts the green plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Asparagus|Liberator Gin": "Liberator Gin's citrus-juniper botanicals leans against the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the botanicals echo the green plate. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Asparagus|Licor 43": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character clashes with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- sugar on a clean vegetable side is wrong direction — needs herb-acid lift, not sweetness. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a digestif. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Licor 43 for the steak course.",
  "Asparagus|Limoncello": "Limoncello's sweet liqueur character clashes with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a digestif. Avoid; one of those is the move. Limoncello lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Asparagus|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Willamette Pinot — dark cherry, forest floor, refined structure, low tannin. The low-tannin silk lifts asparagus's tender spears and the forest-floor earth plays against the vegetal char — the rare red that handles asparagus without clashing. Works tier on this wine's card — solid fit for Asparagus but below the wine's peaks with duck, lamb, and mushroom-sauced proteins.",
  "Asparagus|Little Book": "Little Book's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overshadows the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- sweet-oak depth has nothing to bridge into green vegetable freshness. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Little Book for the steak course.",
  "Asparagus|Loaded Potato": "The loaded potato alongside the asparagus -- the bright register cleaves the heavy course, the table breathes. Works; the table can build them in order or together.",
