  "Asparagus|Sesti Brunello di Montalcino": "Sesti Brunello di Montalcino's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity crowds the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- the side needs a crisper register to carry it cleanly. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Sesti Brunello di Montalcino for the steak course.",
