  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Alexander Valley Chardonnay": "Alexander Valley Chardonnay's apple-butter acidity leans against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Alexander Valley Cyrus": "Au Gratin Potatoes: dark-fruit Cab body settles into the cream-rich side; firm tannin cuts the lactic edge and the oak threads the indulgence. A capable pair; richness aligns if not perfectly. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Alexander Valley Homestead Red": "Alexander Valley Sonoma Bordeaux blend — plum, blackberry, mocha, soft tannin, smooth. The soft tannin cuts gruyère-cream weight and the mocha plays against the lactic richness. Strong crowd-pleaser Bordeaux blend for au gratin — Sonoma softness on the cheesy side.",
