  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Ancho Reyes": "Ancho Reyes' sweet liqueur character clashes with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Ancho Reyes on the steak course instead.",
