  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Bodega Noemia A Lisa": "Au Gratin Potatoes: structured red meets dairy-driven side: the bold tannin scrubs the cream, the dark fruit lifts the indulgence into balance. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Bombay Dry Gin": "Bombay Dry Gin's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals sits alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Bombay Sapphire Gin": "Bombay Sapphire Gin's crisp London-Dry-citrus botanicals reads alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Bone Marrow": "The bone marrow opens the meal, the au gratin with the entree -- the marrow-and-gremolata plate wraps the cheese-and-cream side. Strong; the starter sets the table before the side lands.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Bone-In Filet": "* The bone-in filet with the au gratin -- the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness frames the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust. Gold standard; the side that defines the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Booker's": "Booker's with the au gratin — Beam cask-strength against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Booker's intensity handles the richness at barrel-proof register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Botanist Gin": "Botanist Gin's crisp Islay-gentle-botanical botanicals reads alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Bowdie's Old Fashioned": "Bowdie's Old Fashioned's bold caramel-char build finds neutral with the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the whiskey-build weight settles into the rich side, and the oak frames the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark": "Bowdie's Private Select Maker's Mark with au gratin potatoes — cheese-and-cream meets house-pick oak. Strong; matched registers with the private-select's extra depth.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Bowman Brothers Small Batch": "Bowman Brothers Small Batch with au gratin potatoes — 90-proof Virginia small-batch against cheese-and-cream. Strong; smooth match at the small-batch register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Bowmore 12": "Bowmore 12's lighter-Islay peat character reads alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the Highland register carries the au gratin, and the oak threads the cream. Works; the 10-year BIB depth gives the dessert substantial weight.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Braida Montebruna Barbera": "Piedmont Monferrato Barbera d'Asti — Braida benchmark, juicy dark cherry, blackberry, high acid, low tannin. The high acid cuts gruyère-cream weight and the blackberry plays against the lactic richness. Works as benchmark Barbera for au gratin — food-wine acidity on the cheesy side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon": "Au Gratin Potatoes: dark-fruit Cab body settles into the cream-rich side; firm tannin cuts the lactic edge and the oak threads the indulgence. A capable pair; richness aligns if not perfectly. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Broccoli Cheddar": "The broccoli cheddar and the au gratin share cheese as the primary character. Avoid; the meal doubles down without contrast. Route the broccoli cheddar with Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay or the au gratin with Bone-In Filet, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Keenan Chardonnay instead.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Bruichladdich": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay reads alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the scotch depth settles into the au gratin, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; bold intensity slightly over-specified.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Brussels and Belly": "Au Gratin Potatoes and Brussels + Belly together -- the cheese cream holds beside the charred-sprouts-and-belly opener. Works; the two sides share the meal without competing.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Buffalo Trace": "Buffalo Trace with au gratin potatoes — flagship bourbon against cheese-and-cream. Strong; clean match at the register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Buffalo Trace Cream": "Buffalo Trace Cream's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- the liqueur's sugar buries the side's cream instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Buffalo Trace Cream belongs on the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Bulleit Bourbon": "Bulleit Bourbon with au gratin potatoes — 90-proof high-rye against cheese-and-cream. Strong; rye spice distinct from wheated-caramel approaches.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Burrata": "The burrata alongside the au gratin -- both bring cheese as the headline. Avoid; one is enough. Pair the burrata with Il Colle Prosecco Superiore, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc; pair the au gratin with Bone-In Filet, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Keenan Chardonnay.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Butternut Squash": "The butternut squash and the au gratin on the same meal -- rich dairy yields to dessert weight, the close composes thickly. Works; sequence or share, the build holds.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Cade Cabernet Sauvignon": "Au Gratin Potatoes: structured red meets dairy-driven side: the bold tannin scrubs the cream, the dark fruit lifts the indulgence into balance. A capable pair; richness aligns if not perfectly. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Camarena Tequila": "Camarena Tequila's rested-agave body sits alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the oak-aged tequila body threads the au gratin, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; the 70th's clarity is too delicate to drive the pairing.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Campari": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- amaro bitterness on dairy reads metallic — needs warmth or sweetness to balance. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Canadian Club": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet traditional Canadian. Works; Canadian Club's grain-forward character handles the richness at heritage register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Canadian Club 43 Year": "CC 43 Year with the au gratin — aged collector Canadian against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; CC 43 Year is over-specified for a side; save the rare bottle for the main.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Captain Morgan Rum": "Captain Morgan Rum's green-agave-and-cane lift finds neutral with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the unaged-cane register matches the au gratin, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Caribou Crossing": "Caribou Crossing with the au gratin — distinctive Canadian against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Caribou Crossing's craft character handles the richness at single-barrel register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Carrot Cake": "The au gratin and the carrot cake -- the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust hands off cleanly to the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: cream-and-sugar build the close, the meal finishes generous. Works; sequence them or share the table, no clash.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Casa LBV Port": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a dessert wine. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Casamigos Mezcal": "Casamigos Mezcal's wood-fire mezcal body sits alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the smoky agave register handles the au gratin, and the wood-smoke note underlines the side. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon": "Napa Rutherford Cab — concentrated black fruit, cocoa, mocha, velvety tannin. The opulent body cuts au gratin's cheese-and-cream weight and the cocoa-mocha plays against the golden crust. Strong iconic Napa Cab for au gratin — Caymus lushness meets the decadent side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Chambord": "Chambord's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- the liqueur's sugar buries the side's cream instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Chambord for the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Cheesecake": "Au Gratin Potatoes and the cheesecake -- the cream rounds into the sweet close, the meal lands rich and full. Works; clean transition or together if the table wants.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Chilean Seabass": "The seabass alongside the au gratin -- the meal layers rich on rich, the table carries weight cleanly when the registers match. Works; the side sits without pulling focus.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Chocolate Brownie": "Au Gratin Potatoes and the brownie -- the cream rounds into the sweet close, the meal lands rich and full. Works; clean transition or together if the table wants.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Chocolate Cake": "The au gratin alongside the chocolate cake -- the cream rounds into the sweet close, the meal lands rich and full. Works; the contrast holds, neither course overshadows the other.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Chopin Vodka": "Chopin Vodka's bold char-cream neutrality sits beside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Christian Bros Brandy": "Christian Brothers with the au gratin — value brandy against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Christian Bros handles the richness at approachable register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Château Batailley": "Pauillac 5ème Cru Classé Bordeaux — blackcurrant, tobacco, cedar, graphite, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts gruyère-cream weight and the cedar plays against the lactic richness. Strong classified Bordeaux for au gratin — Pauillac structure on the cheesy side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Château Beaucastel": "Châteauneuf-du-Pape Rhône — Beaucastel, all 13 permitted varieties, dark fruit, leather, truffle, Provençal herbs, medium tannin. The medium tannin cuts gruyere-cream richness and the truffle plays with the cheese. Works for au gratin — pouring Beaucastel on a dairy side underuses the estate's complexity.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Château Gombaude-Guillot": "Au Gratin Potatoes: dark-fruit Cab body settles into the cream-rich side; firm tannin cuts the lactic edge and the oak threads the indulgence. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Château Haut Segottes": "Saint-Émilion right-bank Bordeaux — plum, dark cherry, truffle, clayey earth, soft tannin. The soft tannin cuts gruyère-cream weight and the clayey earth plays against the lactic richness. Strong right-bank Bordeaux for au gratin — Merlot-led roundness on the cheesy side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Château de Rouillac": "Pessac-Léognan left-bank Bordeaux — blackcurrant, cedar, graphite, tobacco, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts gruyère-cream weight and the cedar plays against the lactic richness. Strong left-bank Bordeaux for au gratin — French structure on the classic cheesy side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Clam Chowder": "The chowder and the au gratin share potato as the primary character. Avoid; the meal doubles down without contrast. Route the chowder with Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis or the au gratin with Bone-In Filet, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Keenan Chardonnay instead.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Clase Azul Anejo": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet Clase Azul Anejo. Works; sherry-butt-finished complexity handles richness at luxury register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Clase Azul Durango": "Clase Azul Durango with au gratin potatoes — Durango-artisanship against cheese-and-cream. Works; ceremonial over-specified.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Clase Azul Gold": "Clase Azul Gold with au gratin potatoes — joven blend against cheese-and-cream. Works; ceremonial over-specified.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's rustic mezcal weight sits alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the smoky agave register handles the au gratin, and the earthy backbone threads the side. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Clase Azul Plata": "Clase Azul Plata's silky Jalisco blanco with ceramic-decanter presentation reads alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the au gratin, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Clase Azul Reposado": "Clase Azul Reposado's ceramic-icon reposado character finds neutral with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the oak-aged tequila body threads the au gratin, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the side. Works; the 70th's smoothness is an unusual but interesting counterpoint.",
