  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Corazon Blanco": "Corazon Blanco's green-agave-and-cane lift reads alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the silver-spirit register lifts the au gratin, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Corazon Reposado": "Corazon Reposado's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the au gratin, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; multi-cask depth composed with this dish.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Corazon Sazerac": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet Corazon Sazerac. Works; ex-rye-barrel spice handles richness at Expresiones register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Corazon Stagg": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet Corazon Stagg. Works; heavy-caramel-GTS character handles richness at intense register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Corazon Weller": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet Corazon Weller. Works; wheated-soft character handles richness at gentler-Expresiones register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Corazón del Sol Malbec": "Mendoza Argentina Malbec — Corazón del Sol, dark plum, blackberry jam, violet, velvety tannin, full body. The velvety tannin handles gruyere-cream weight, but the jam-forward Malbec reads bolder than the side demands. Works for au gratin — Muga's vanilla-leather plays with the cheese harder.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Corpse Reviver": "Corpse Reviver's anise-citrus build plays cleanly against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Courvoisier Cognac": "Courvoisier with the au gratin — drier oak cognac against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Courvoisier's backbone handles the richness.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Cowboy Ribeye": "Cowboy Ribeye with the au gratin -- the 26oz cut handles the rich potato side. Excellent; the side that completes the steak plate.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Crab Cake": "The crab cake and the au gratin -- delicate gives way to rich, the table earns its weight. Works; the call holds whether the table sequences them or shares.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Cragganmore 12": "Cragganmore 12 with the au gratin — distinctive Speyside against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Strong; Cragganmore's layered complexity handles the richness at Classic Malt register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Creamy Potato": "The potato soup and the au gratin -- both potato-forward, the table doubles up on potato. Avoid; pick one or the other. Pair the potato soup with Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis; pair the au gratin with Bone-In Filet, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Keenan Chardonnay.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Creme Brulee": "The au gratin and the brulee -- the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust hands off cleanly to the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: cream-and-sugar build the close, the meal finishes generous. Works; sequence them or share the table, no clash.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée": "Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée's cherry-earth tannin reads alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Crown Royal": "Crown Royal with the au gratin — iconic Canadian against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Crown Royal's smoothness handles the richness at crowd-pleasing register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Cucumber Gimlet": "Cucumber Gimlet's crisp citrus-ginger build leans against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Dalmore 12": "Dalmore 12 with the au gratin — Highland luxury against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Dalmore's sherry-finish depth handles the richness at luxury register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge": "Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge's crisp earth-mineral tannin sits beside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Darioush Cabernet Franc": "Mount Veeder Napa Cab Franc (rare) — Darioush elegant aromatic, violet, dark cherry, dried rose, savory herb, medium tannin. The medium tannin cuts gruyère-cream weight and the savory herb plays against the lactic richness. Works as rare-Napa CF for au gratin — Darioush aromatic precision on the cheesy side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon": "Silverado Trail Cab — blackcurrant, dark plum, mocha, spice, plush. The opulent body cuts au gratin's cheese-and-cream weight and the mocha-spice plays against the golden crust. Works as opulent Napa Cab for au gratin — Darioush Persian-inspired plushness on the decadent side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Detroit City Gin": "Detroit City Gin's bold char-juniper botanicals stays alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Detroit City Vodka": "Detroit City Vodka's crisp grain-juniper neutrality reads alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the botanicals cut the cheese richness. Works; the match holds without overshooting. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
