  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Dewar's White Label": "Dewar's White Label with the au gratin — honey-vanilla blend against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Dewar's White handles the richness at benchmark register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Disaronno": "Disaronno's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- sweet liqueur and dairy-rich side double the indulgence with no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Disaronno for the steak course.",
