  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum": "Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum's high-proof pour register leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the rich pour wraps the au gratin, and the layered body brightens the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Domaine Serene Grand Cheval": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin leans against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Domaine Tempier Bandol": "Provence Bandol AOC Mourvèdre blend — Tempier, dark plum, game, olive, wild herbs, smoky mineral, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts gruyere-cream richness but the cult-producer complexity is spent on a dairy side. Works for au gratin — Muga's vanilla-leather fits the cheese harder.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé": "Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé's citrus-mineral acidity stays alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Domaine du Grand Tinel": "Châteauneuf-du-Pape Rhône GSM blend — Grand Tinel, ripe red fruit, black pepper, garrigue, herbal earth, full body, medium tannin. The medium tannin cuts gruyere-cream richness and the full body handles dairy. Works for au gratin — Muga's vanilla-leather fits the cheese harder.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Don Fulano Anejo": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet Don Fulano. Works; extended-aged complexity handles richness at Los-Altos register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Don Fulano Blanco": "Don Fulano Blanco's clean silver register reads alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the blanco-tequila body matches the au gratin, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the side. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Don Fulano Reposado": "Don Fulano Reposado's barrel-aged tequila weight reads alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the oak-aged tequila body threads the au gratin, and the caramel-agave register brightens the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Don Julio 1942": "Don Julio 1942 with au gratin potatoes — benchmark extra añejo against cheese-and-cream. Works; iconic pour over-specified.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Don Julio 70th": "Don Julio 70th's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the au gratin, and the caramel-agave register brightens the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Don Julio Blanco": "Don Julio Blanco's workhorse blanco with clean agave snap leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the au gratin, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Don Julio Reposado": "Don Julio Reposado's añejo-pour depth leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the au gratin, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the side. Works; ceremonial over-specified.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Drambuie": "Drambuie's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- the liqueur's sugar buries the side's cream instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Drambuie on the steak course instead.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Dunville's Single Malt": "Dunville's Single Malt's Irish whiskey smoothness leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the smooth triple-distilled register matches the au gratin, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; Remus 15 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|E.H. Taylor Full Proof": "E.H. Taylor Full Proof with the au gratin — BT Bottled-in-Bond against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; EHT Full Proof handles the richness at historic Kentucky register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|E.H. Taylor Rye": "E.H. Taylor Rye with au gratin potatoes — bonded BT rye against cheese-and-cream. Works; BIB over-specified for side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|E.H. Taylor Small Batch": "E.H. Taylor Small Batch with au gratin potatoes — 100-proof BIB against cheese-and-cream. Strong; bonded weight at matched premium register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Eagle Rare 10 Year": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese and cream richness meet Eagle Rare 10 Year's refined oak. Strong; balance against richness.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Eastern Kille Dry Gin": "Eastern Kille Dry Gin's crisp char-citrus botanicals sits beside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|El Cabo": "El Cabo's cooked-agave-and-oak register leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the rested-agave depth sits with the au gratin, and the caramel-agave register brightens the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|El Mayor Extra Anejo": "El Mayor Extra Anejo with au gratin potatoes — aged El Mayor against cheese-and-cream. Works; accessible aged sits with richness.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|El Mayor Reposado": "El Mayor Reposado's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the rested-agave depth sits with the au gratin, and the caramel-agave register brightens the side. Works; the pour is a touch over-specified for the side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Elephant Gin": "Elephant Gin's crisp char-herbal botanicals sits alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Elijah Craig 18 Year": "Elijah Craig 18 with the au gratin — HH aged single-barrel against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Excellent; EC 18's 18yr depth handles the richness at aged-HH register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Elijah Craig Private Barrel": "Elijah Craig Private Barrel with au gratin potatoes — private-selection single-barrel against cheese-and-cream. Strong; matched register with curated depth.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Elijah Craig Single Barrel": "Elijah Craig Single Barrel with au gratin potatoes — 94-proof single-barrel against cheese-and-cream. Strong; composed match at premium Heaven Hill register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Elijah Craig Small Batch": "Elijah Craig Small Batch with au gratin potatoes — small-batch against cheese-and-cream. Strong; clean match.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Elijah Craig Straight Rye": "Elijah Craig Straight Rye with au gratin potatoes — HH rye against cheese-and-cream. Works; spice over-specified for side's character.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Elk Cove Five Mountain": "Elk Cove Five Mountain's cherry-clove tannin leans against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Elk Cove Pinot Blanc": "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc's apple-char acidity stays alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Elmer T. Lee": "Elmer T. Lee with au gratin potatoes — 90-proof single-barrel against cheese-and-cream. Strong; composed namesake match.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Empress 1908 Gin": "Empress 1908 Gin's bold anise-butter botanicals stays alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Epoch Ingenuity": "Paso Robles Rhône blend — Epoch Ingenuity, Templeton Gap Syrah-Grenache-Mourvèdre, blackberry, smoked meat, olive, crushed pepper, medium tannin. The medium tannin cuts gruyere-cream richness and the full body handles dairy. Works for au gratin — Muga's vanilla-leather fits the cheese harder.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Escargot": "The escargot and the au gratin -- cream meets umami, the table goes deep. Works; the call holds whether the table sequences them or shares.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Espresso Martini": "Espresso Martini's roasted-coffee martini richness crowds the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- the cocktail needs the cut, not the supporting side. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a spirit-forward cocktail. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Espresso Martini for the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Espresso Old Fashioned": "Espresso Old Fashioned's spirit-forward cocktail register doubles down on the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- cocktail whiskey and dairy side meet without contrast — both heavy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a spirit-forward cocktail. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Espresso Old Fashioned belongs on the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Evening Land Seven Springs": "Evening Land Seven Springs's cherry-earth tannin plays cleanly against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the smoke meets the umami depth. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon": "Oakville luxurious Cab — blackcurrant, dark chocolate, espresso, violet, smooth powerful. The opulent body cuts au gratin's cheese-and-cream weight and the chocolate-espresso plays against the golden crust. Works as luxurious Oakville Cab for au gratin — Far Niente opulence on the decadent side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Far Niente Chardonnay": "* Far Niente Chardonnay -- Napa Chardonnay, tropical fruit, oak. The cool-climate register carries the au gratin, and the chalky minerality plays against the side. Peak pour. Gold standard; the call that earns the regular.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Faroe Island Salmon": "The salmon into the au gratin -- the meal layers rich on rich, the table carries weight cleanly when the registers match. Works; safe alongside, but not the headline pick.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi": "Super Tuscan — Le Pupille Saffredi Maremma, Cab-Merlot-Petit Verdot, 2021, blackcurrant, tobacco, graphite, Mediterranean herbs, firm-tannin finish. The firm tannin cuts manchego-cream weight but reads heavier than the gratin strictly demands. Works for au gratin — Cabernet fits the dense dairy harder.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Faust Napa Valley Cabernet": "Agustin Huneeus's elegant Napa Cab. Moderate tannin, fruit-forward. Works with the gratin but the bigger Cabs (Caymus, Far Niente) peak higher against the 90-minute-baked richness. Fine for a mid-tier Cab guest.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía": "Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía's cherry-earth tannin plays cleanly against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Fernet Branca": "Fernet Branca's nuclear bitter-menthol intensity sits beside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the bitter herb edge cuts the rich side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Fernet Menta": "Fernet Menta's crisp mint-menthol edge sits beside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the bitter herb edge cuts the rich side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Filet Mignon": "The filet with the au gratin -- cream and protein share the meal, the build reads full. Works; the side sits without pulling focus.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Fireball Whisky": "Fireball Whisky's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- sweet liqueur and dairy-rich side double the indulgence with no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Fireball Whisky for the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Fisher Unity Pinot Noir": "Fisher Unity Pinot Noir's cherry-earth tannin reads alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Four Roses Small Batch Select": "Four Roses Small Batch Select with au gratin potatoes — 104-proof premium Four Roses against cheese-and-cream. Strong; concentrated character at premium register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Four Roses Yellow Label": "Four Roses Yellow Label with au gratin potatoes — entry-level bourbon against cheese-and-cream. Strong; accessible everyday match.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Fox & Oden": "Fox & Oden with au gratin potatoes — craft bourbon against cheese-and-cream. Strong; boutique match at craft-small-batch register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Fox & Oden Double Oaked": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet Double Oaked Fox & Oden. Works; Fox & Oden handles the richness at Double-Oaked register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Frangelico": "Frangelico's Piedmont hazelnut depth to mocha at after-dinner register clashes with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Frangelico belongs on the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Freemark Abbey Bosché": "Rutherford Cab — Bosché Vineyard since 1970, blackcurrant, tobacco, graphite, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts gruyère-cream weight and the tobacco plays against the lactic richness. Works as Bosché Vineyard Cab for au gratin — 1970-legacy Rutherford on the cheesy side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|French 75": "French 75's citrus-earth build sits alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the oak frames the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|French Onion": "The French onion alongside the au gratin -- both bring cheese as the headline. Avoid; one is enough. Pair the French onion with Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée; pair the au gratin with Bone-In Filet, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Keenan Chardonnay.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Frias Block 5": "Au Gratin Potatoes: dark-fruit Cab body settles into the cream-rich side; firm tannin cuts the lactic edge and the oak threads the indulgence. A capable pair; richness aligns if not perfectly. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo": "Piedmont Barolo DOCG Nebbiolo — G.D. Vajra Albe La Morra, tar, rose petal, dried cherry, firm tannic backbone, high acid. The high acid cuts gruyère-cream weight and the tar plays against the lactic richness. Strong classic Barolo for au gratin — Vajra prestige on the cheesy side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti": "Piedmont sweet sparkling — peach, honey, floral. The sweetness is catastrophic against a 180°C 90-minute-baked manchego cream gratin; the dish has too much savory weight and cream body. Route Moscato to dessert where sugar makes sense. Avoid; pair this elsewhere on the menu.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|G4 Blanco": "G4 Blanco's clean silver register sits alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the blanco-tequila body matches the au gratin, and the agave-citrus thread frames the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|G4 High Proof": "G4 High Proof's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the oak-aged tequila body threads the au gratin, and the oak threads the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Garavogue Irish Whiskey": "Garavogue Irish Whiskey's Irish whiskey smoothness leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the gentle Irish body threads the au gratin, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|George T. Stagg": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet BTAC collector. Works; save the BTAC bottle for the protein course — the side doesn't deserve the pour.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon": "Oakville Cab — blackcurrant, dark cherry, graphite, toasted oak, firm tannin. The dense body cuts au gratin's cheese-and-cream weight and the graphite-oak plays against the golden crust. Works as Oakville Cab for au gratin — Napa golden-strip structure on the decadent side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Ghost Block Zinfandel": "Napa Oakville Zinfandel — Ghost Block, ripe jammy fruit, blackberry preserves, cracked pepper, full body, medium tannin. The medium tannin cuts gruyere-cream richness and the full body handles dairy. Works for au gratin — a Chardonnay's cream-on-cream fits softer.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Glenfiddich 12": "Glenfiddich 12 with the au gratin — gateway Speyside against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Strong; Fiddich's light vanilla handles the richness at approachable register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Glenfiddich 14": "Glenfiddich 14 with the au gratin — Bourbon Barrel Reserve against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Strong; the charred-oak finish handles the richness at aged register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Glenfiddich 18": "Glenfiddich 18 with the au gratin — Small Batch Reserve against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Strong; Fiddich 18's depth handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with the au gratin — Cuvée-cask Speyside against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Strong; Gran Cru's refinement handles the richness at premium aged register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Glenglassaugh 12": "Glenglassaugh 12 with the au gratin — Sandend-coast Highland against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Glenglassaugh 12 handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Glenlivet 12": "Glenlivet 12 with the au gratin — softer Speyside against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Strong; Glenlivet handles the richness at benchmark register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Glenmorangie 10": "Glenmorangie 10 with the au gratin — tallest-stills Highland against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Glenmorangie 10's vanilla-honey handles the richness at entry-Highland register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Glenmorangie 18": "Glenmorangie 18 with the au gratin — 18yr bourbon + sherry-finish Highland against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Glenmorangie 18 handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Graham's 10 Year Tawny": "Graham's 10 Year Tawny's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a dessert wine. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Graham's 10 Year Tawny belongs on the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Graham's 20 Year Tawny": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth clashes with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a dessert wine. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Graham's 20 Year Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Graham's 2017 Vintage Port": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight doubles down on the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- sweet wine and a dairy side compound the richness — dessert energy on savory plate. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Gran Patron Platinum": "Gran Patron Platinum's clean silver register leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the silver-spirit register lifts the au gratin, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Grand Marnier": "Grand Marnier's sweet liqueur character clashes with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Grand Marnier for the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Gray Whale Gin": "Gray Whale Gin's bold citrus-herbal botanicals sits alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Green Chartreuse": "Green Chartreuse's cask-strength herbal-high-proof sweetness holds with the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the sweet character sits at digestif register, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Grey Goose Vodka": "Grey Goose Vodka's crisp French-wheat-soft neutrality reads alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the clean profile lets the cheese speak. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Grilled Caesar": "The Caesar and the au gratin -- both cheese-forward, the table doubles up on cheese. Avoid; pick one or the other. Pair the Caesar with Green Chartreuse, Tanqueray Gin, or Scavino Barolo; pair the au gratin with Bone-In Filet, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Keenan Chardonnay.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Gumbo": "The gumbo alongside the au gratin -- the spiced course breaks the cream, the table reads balanced. Works; the table can build them in order or together.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet": "Au Gratin Potatoes: the side's cream pulls the bold red's tannin through; cassis and dark fruit catch the dairy's weight without overshooting. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the pairing reads at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|HDW 100 Vodka": "HDW 100 Vodka's char-herbal neutrality plays cleanly against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Hakushu 12 Year": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the Mizunara-influenced register sits with the au gratin, and the oak threads the cream. Works; Fortuna's NZ terroir meets the glaze at distinctive register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with au gratin potatoes — 88.9-proof BT single-barrel against cheese-and-cream. Strong; Blanton's-mash character at premium register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Hangar 1 Vodka": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality stays alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the floral notes lift the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Head Fake": "Wheatley vodka, limoncello, triple sec, lemon, simple syrup, sugar rim. Sweet lemon-drop style clashes on every axis with manchego-cream gratin. Route this cocktail to dessert or to the lighter starters. Avoid; the pairing fights at the table — point the guest elsewhere.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Heaven Hill 20 Year": "Heaven Hill 20 Year with the au gratin — HH 20yr against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Strong; HH 20's 20-year depth handles the richness at collector register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond": "Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond with au gratin potatoes — 100-proof BIB against cheese-and-cream. Strong; classic match with sturdy bonded character.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Heaven's Door 10 Year": "Heaven's Door 10 Year with au gratin potatoes — 100-proof 10-year against cheese-and-cream. Strong; aged premium at matched register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Heitz Martha's Vineyard": "Au Gratin Potatoes: the structured red's grip carries the rich side's dairy load; oak-driven body absorbs the cream and tannin clears the finish. A capable pair; richness aligns if not perfectly. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Heitz Trailside Vineyard": "Au Gratin Potatoes: dark-fruit Cab body settles into the cream-rich side; firm tannin cuts the lactic edge and the oak threads the indulgence. A capable pair; richness aligns if not perfectly. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Hendricks Flora Adora": "Hendricks Flora Adora's crisp char-elderflower botanicals sits alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the honey threads the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Hendricks Gin": "Hendricks Gin's crisp cucumber-rose botanicals plays cleanly against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the floral notes lift the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Hendricks Grand Cabaret": "Hendricks Grand Cabaret's bold anise-char botanicals reads alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the anise underlines the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Hendricks Neptunia": "Hendricks Neptunia's crisp anise-brine botanicals stays alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; capable alongside. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Hendricks Orbium": "Hendricks Orbium's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals leans against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Hennessy Cognac": "Hennessy with the au gratin — benchmark cognac against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Hennessy's oak handles the richness at functional register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with au gratin potatoes — 10-year bonded against cheese-and-cream. Strong; aged BIB at matched premium register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Hibiki Japanese Harmony": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the precise Japanese craft body wraps the au gratin, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; retailer-pick wasted on salad.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|House Wedge": "The wedge and the au gratin -- both cheese-forward, the table doubles up on cheese. Avoid; pick one or the other. Pair the wedge with St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Weller 12 Year, or Le Garenne Rosé; pair the au gratin with Bone-In Filet, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Keenan Chardonnay.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|I.W. Harper 15 Year": "I.W. Harper 15 with the au gratin — BT-distilled 15yr against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Excellent; IW Harper 15's aged cherry-oak handles the richness at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Il Colle Prosecco Superiore": "Il Colle Prosecco Superiore's crisp apple-citrus acidity finds neutral with the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Inhibited": "Tito's, Kahlúa, Bailey's, chocolate liqueur, espresso, chocolate-drizzled glass. The cocktail's cream-and-coffee weight meets the gratin's cheesy dairy richness; Kahlúa's bitter edge cuts through. Strong unconventional pairing — both dishes share indulgent richness as defining trait.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Inverroche Gin": "Inverroche Gin's crisp earth-floral botanicals leans against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Iron Fish Gin": "Iron Fish Gin's cask-strength citrus-earth botanicals plays cleanly against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the honey threads the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet northern MI mezcal-cask. Works; Ironfish Mezcal handles the richness at Michigan-hometown register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Isaac Bowman Port Finish": "Isaac Bowman Port Finish with the au gratin — Sazerac-owned Virginia port-finish against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Isaac Bowman handles the richness at Virginia-heritage register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|J Davies Ferrington Vineyards": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards's cherry-coffee tannin sits alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon": "Diamond Mountain Cab — dark fruit, graphite, mineral backbone, firm tannin. The structured body cuts au gratin's cheese-and-cream weight and the graphite plays against the golden crust. Strong mountain Cab for au gratin — volcanic-soil complexity on the decadent side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Jack Daniel's 12 Year": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with the au gratin — aged Tennessee against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; JD 12 handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Jack Daniel's Bonded": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet 100-proof Tennessee. Works; JD Bonded's backbone handles the richness at Bonded register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Jack Daniel's Old No. 7": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7 with the au gratin — iconic Tennessee against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Old No. 7's vanilla-caramel handles the richness at iconic register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Jack Daniel's Sinatra Select": "JD Sinatra Select with the au gratin — Sinatra-tribute Tennessee against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Sinatra Select handles the richness at Sinatra-tribute register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Jameson Irish Whiskey": "Jameson Irish Whiskey's classic Irish blend smoothness reads alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the soft malt-and-grain weight wraps the au gratin, and the oak softens the cream. Works; annual-release complexity over-specified.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir": "Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir's cherry-earth tannin leans against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; the match holds without overshooting. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis": "Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis's crisp apple-char acidity reads alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E.": "Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E. with the au gratin — sea-aged L.E. against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Marian McLain L.E. handles the richness at collector register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Jefferson's Ocean Voyage 23": "Jefferson's Ocean Voyage 23 with the au gratin — sea-aged Jefferson's against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Voyage 23 handles the richness at ocean-finish register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Jefferson's Reserve": "Jefferson's Reserve with au gratin potatoes — blended elegance against cheese-and-cream. Strong; sophisticated everyday match.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Jefferson's Reserve VR Twin Oak": "Jefferson's Reserve VR Twin Oak with au gratin potatoes — premium oak against cheese-and-cream. Strong; the Twin Oak finish gives the side more dimension than standard Jefferson's brings.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Jim Beam Black Label": "Jim Beam Black Label with au gratin potatoes — 86-proof aged Beam against cheese-and-cream. Strong; aging gives a solid match.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Jim Beam White Label": "Jim Beam White Label with au gratin potatoes — 80-proof Beam against cheese-and-cream. Strong; entry tier clean match.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Johnnie Walker Black": "JW Black with the au gratin — 12yr balanced JW against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; JW Black handles the richness at premium-blend register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Johnnie Walker Blue": "JW Blue with the au gratin — hand-selected rare-cask JW against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; the side is not the place for JW Blue — save the bottle for the filet or KC.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Johnnie Walker Red": "JW Red with the au gratin — peat-influenced JW against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; JW Red's smoke cuts the richness at entry register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon": "Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon: this elegant red's cherry-bright, silky-tannin frame meets this rich, creamy side's dairy-driven indulgence. The elegant red's acidity cuts the dairy fat while its cherry lifts the earthy umami. A bright-meets-rich headliner. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Joseph Mellot Sancerre": "Joseph Mellot Sancerre's crisp citrus-mineral acidity plays cleanly against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Jubilation by Colgin": "Jubilation — Colgin cult Napa, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violets, espresso, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts gruyère-cream weight and the espresso plays against the lactic richness. Works as cult Napa for au gratin — Colgin prestige on the cheesy side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Jung and Wulff Guyana": "Jung and Wulff Guyana's rich layered-spirit body reads alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the high-proof register matches the au gratin, and the dense weight underlines the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Jung and Wulff Trinidad": "Jung and Wulff Trinidad's heavy aged-spirit weight sits alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the layered spirit body sits with the au gratin, and the dense weight underlines the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Kahlua": "Kahlua's sweet liqueur character clashes with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Kahlua for the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Kansas City": "The KC into the au gratin -- the KC's lean-bold strip with savory grain meets the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust. Excellent; reliable headline side for the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Keenan Chardonnay": "Keenan Chardonnay — Spring Mountain Napa, green apple, lemon curd, subtle oak, bright acid. The bright acid cuts the au gratin's cheese-and-cream weight and the subtle oak complements the golden crust. Works well as balanced Chardonnay for au gratin — Napa structure on the indulgent side. Gold standard; pour without second-guessing.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Keenan Mernet": "Spring Mountain Napa Mernet — Merlot-Cab, mountain structure, plush dark cherry, plum, medium tannin. The medium tannin cuts gruyère-cream weight and the mountain-earth plays against the lactic richness. Works as mountain Merlot-Cab for au gratin — Keenan on the cheesy side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the dry rye body wraps the au gratin, and the oak threads the cream. Works; aging wasted on the salad.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Kentucky Owl Confiscated": "Kentucky Owl Confiscated with au gratin potatoes — KO Confiscated against cheese-and-cream. Works; craft-blend over-specified.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's": "Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's' Irish whiskey smoothness sits alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the approachable Irish character carries the au gratin, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; EHT Full Proof is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône": "Rhône Valley Côtes du Rhône Grenache-Syrah-Mourvèdre — Kermit Lynch, red cherry, wild herbs, pepper, garrigue, medium body. The pepper cuts gruyere-cream richness and the medium body handles dairy weight. Works for au gratin — Muga Reserva's vanilla-leather plays with the cheese harder.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Ketel One Vodka": "Ketel One Vodka's Dutch-wheat-crisp neutrality sits beside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the clean profile lets the cheese speak. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Knickerbocker Gin": "Knickerbocker Gin's bold citrus-juniper botanicals leans against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Knob Creek": "Knob Creek with au gratin potatoes — bold high-rye against cheese-and-cream. Strong; the 100-proof handles the side's richness cleanly.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Knob Creek 12 Year": "Knob Creek 12 Year with au gratin potatoes — 12-year high-rye against cheese-and-cream. Strong; aged Beam matches richness cleanly.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Knob Creek 15 Year": "Knob Creek 15 with the au gratin — Beam aged single-barrel against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Excellent; KC 15's aged character handles the richness at aged-Beam register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Knob Creek 18 Year": "Knob Creek 18 with the au gratin — 18yr Beam aged KC against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Strong; KC 18 handles the richness at collector register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye": "Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye with au gratin potatoes — blend complexity against cheese-and-cream. Strong; the layered profile sits with the richness at full register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Knob Creek Rye": "Knob Creek Rye with au gratin potatoes — 100-proof rye against cheese-and-cream. Works; bold rye slightly over-specified.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Komos Anejo Reserva": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet Komos Anejo Reserva. Works; multi-cask complexity handles richness at luxury register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Komos Crystallino Anejo": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet Komos Crystallino. Works; crystallino-filtered complexity handles richness at trendy-luxury register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Komos Extra Anejo": "Komos Extra Añejo with au gratin potatoes — aged Komos against cheese-and-cream. Works; Riedel-luxury over-specified.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Komos Rosa Reposado": "Komos Rosa Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register reads alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the añejo register carries the au gratin, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; the wine-cask character adds interest but isn't a standout.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Lagavulin 8": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character sits alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the scotch backbone matches the au gratin, and the oak softens the cream. Works; the pour is a touch ambitious for the salad.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Lail Vineyards Blueprint": "Napa Cab — Lail entry-level, polished blackcurrant, cedar, dark cherry, refined medium tannin. The refined tannin cuts gruyère-cream weight and the cedar plays against the lactic richness. Works as historically-pedigreed Napa Cab for au gratin — Lail family polish on the cheesy side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée": "Lail flagship multi-appellation Napa Cab — dark fruit, cassis, graphite, dried violet, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts gruyère-cream weight and the dried violet plays against the lactic richness. Works as historically-significant Napa Cab for au gratin — Daniel Cuvée structure on the cheesy side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Lalo Silver": "Lalo Silver's green-agave-and-cane lift finds neutral with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the unaged body brightens the au gratin, and the unaged-cane note plays against the side. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Laphroaig 10": "Laphroaig 10's classic Islay peat finds neutral with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the malt-and-oak threads the au gratin, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; aging wasted on the salad.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Larceny Small Batch": "Larceny Small Batch with au gratin potatoes — 92-proof wheated against cheese-and-cream. Solid, composed match at the register. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé": "Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé's crisp berry-cherry acidity reads alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; the pairing reads neutral at the table. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut": "Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut: this versatile sparkling's bright acidity, toasty lees character, and cleansing bubbles meets this rich, creamy side's dairy-driven indulgence. Acid and bubbles scrub the side's fat while brightness keeps the palate clear. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Le Garenne Rosé": "Le Garenne Rosé's crisp floral-rose acidity leans against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Le Ragnaie Brunello": "Au Gratin Potatoes: structured red meets dairy-driven side: the bold tannin scrubs the cream, the dark fruit lifts the indulgence into balance. A capable pair; richness aligns if not perfectly. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Le Volte dell'Ornellaia": "Au Gratin Potatoes: dark-fruit Cab body settles into the cream-rich side; firm tannin cuts the lactic edge and the oak threads the indulgence. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the pairing reads at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Lemon Lavender Gin Martini": "Lemon Lavender Gin Martini's citrus-floral build sits beside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the honey threads the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Les Pallières Raciné": "Gigondas Rhône Valley Grenache — Les Pallières Raciné, Brunier-family old-vine, wild red fruit, garrigue, iron, earthy mineral, medium tannin. The medium tannin cuts gruyere-cream richness and the full body handles dairy. Works for au gratin — Muga's vanilla-leather fits the cheese harder.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Liberator Gin": "Liberator Gin's citrus-juniper botanicals stays alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Licor 43": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- sweet liqueur and dairy-rich side double the indulgence with no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Licor 43 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Limoncello": "Limoncello's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- the liqueur's sugar buries the side's cream instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Limoncello for the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir: this elegant red's cherry-bright, silky-tannin frame meets this rich, creamy side's dairy-driven indulgence. The elegant red's acidity cuts the dairy fat while its cherry lifts the earthy umami. Works — clean if not dominant.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Little Book": "Little Book with the au gratin — Beam blended cask-strength against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Little Book handles the richness at chapter-series register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Loaded Potato": "The loaded potato and the au gratin -- both potato-forward, the table doubles up on potato. Avoid; pick one or the other. Pair the loaded potato with Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir; pair the au gratin with Bone-In Filet, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Keenan Chardonnay.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Loch Lomond 20 Year": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with the au gratin — complex 20yr Highland against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Loch Lomond 20's aged character handles the richness at collector register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Lock Stock & Barrel Rye": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye's rye-spice character leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the au gratin, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; JW Blue is over-specified for the side — save the rare-cask bottle for the protein course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Long Road Gin": "Long Road Gin's crisp citrus-juniper botanicals leans against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Los Vecinos Mezcal": "Los Vecinos Mezcal's earthen-pit smoke profile finds neutral with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the espadín-and-smoke body wraps the au gratin, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; too light for dessert density at this level.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Louis XIII Cognac": "Louis XIII with the au gratin — Grande Champagne luxury icon against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; the side is not the place to pour Louis XIII — the bottle demands main-course or sipping-alone attention.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Lucano Amaro": "Lucano Amaro's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- amaro bitterness on dairy reads metallic — needs warmth or sweetness to balance. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Lucano Amaro for the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Lunaria Coste di Moro": "Abruzzo Montepulciano d'Abruzzo — Lunaria earthy grippy, dark cherry, dried herbs, rustic medium body, medium tannin. The medium tannin cuts gruyère-cream weight and the dried herbs play against the lactic richness. Strong Italian-approachable red for au gratin — rustic character on the cheesy side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Macallan 12 Sherry": "Macallan 12 Sherry with the au gratin — entry-sherried Speyside against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Macallan 12's sherry depth handles the richness.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Macallan 18": "Macallan 18 with the au gratin — 18yr Oloroso-cask Speyside against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Macallan 18's aged sherry handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Macallan Estate": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet distinctive Estate-oak Macallan. Works; Macallan Estate handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Macauley Petite Syrah": "Napa Petite Sirah — Macauley, inky color, dense powerful tannin (not Syrah), blackberry, blueberry, dark chocolate, black pepper, full body. The dense tannin cuts gruyere-cream richness but runs aggressive on a dairy side. Works for au gratin — Muga's softer oak-vanilla fits the cheese gentler.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Macauley Pinot Noir": "Macauley Pinot Noir's crisp cherry-floral tannin leans against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Macauley Stagecoach Vineyard": "Au Gratin Potatoes: structured red meets dairy-driven side: the bold tannin scrubs the cream, the dark fruit lifts the indulgence into balance. A capable pair; richness aligns if not perfectly. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Mahon Gin": "Mahon Gin's bold herbal-juniper botanicals plays cleanly against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Maker's Mark": "Maker's Mark with au gratin potatoes — cheese and cream meet Maker's 90-proof softness. Cleanly matched; not the most interesting pairing but perfectly solid. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Maker's Mark Cellar Aged": "Maker's Mark Cellar Aged with au gratin potatoes — cheese and cream meet the Cellar Aged's mature caramel. Strong; the side and the pour meet at the same register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Malibu Rum": "Malibu Rum's clean silver register sits alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the unaged body brightens the au gratin, and the light-rum lift plays against the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye": "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye's rye-spice character leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the high-rye spice register matches the au gratin, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; the bourbon's character is distinctive but the pairing isn't a standout.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Marc Brédif Chinon": "Marc Brédif Chinon's cherry-earth tannin plays cleanly against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Margarita": "Margarita's crisp agave-brine build sits alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Marimar Estate Christina": "Marimar Estate Christina's cherry-earth tannin reads alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Market Fish": "Market Fish with the au gratin -- the market fish's clean white-fish flesh meets the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: restrained yields to cream, the table arcs cleanly. Works; the side reads as a measured plate companion.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Mata Hari Absinthe": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- amaro bitterness on dairy reads metallic — needs warmth or sweetness to balance. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Mata Hari Absinthe belongs on the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Michter's 10 Year Bourbon": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet Michter's flagship single-barrel. Strong; Michter's 10 handles the richness at prestigious-independent register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Michter's 10 Year Rye": "Michter's 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the rye spice cuts the au gratin, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; annual-release wasted on salad.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Michter's US*1 Rye": "Michter's US*1 Rye with au gratin potatoes — smooth small-batch against cheese-and-cream. Works; refined rye sits with richness at matched register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Mijenta Blanco": "Mijenta Blanco's unaged silver-spirit body reads alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the unaged body brightens the au gratin, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Milagro Anejo": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet Milagro Anejo. Works; triple-distilled character handles richness at French-oak register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Milagro Reposado": "Milagro Reposado's aged-agave character finds neutral with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the aged-agave weight wraps the au gratin, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; bold agave is a distinctive counterpoint but slightly overpowering.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet Mister Sam Bronfman tribute. Mister Sam's aged-blended character handles the richness at collector register. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Mocha Creme": "Au Gratin Potatoes and the mocha creme -- rich cream gives way to sweet, the close lands generously. Works; clean transition or together if the table wants.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Monkey 47 Gin": "Monkey 47 Gin's crisp Black-Forest-botanical botanicals sits alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Monkey Shoulder": "Monkey Shoulder with the au gratin — triple-Speyside-malt blend against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Monkey Shoulder's Speyside-malt fruit handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Montenegro Amaro": "Montenegro Amaro's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- bitter aperitivo on the supporting side reads as wrong register for the course. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Montenegro Amaro for the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Mount Gay Rum": "Mount Gay Rum's cane-and-citrus register finds neutral with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the bright cane-and-citrus weight carries the au gratin, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the side. Works; craft character composes cleanly.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Muga Reserva": "Rioja Alta Reserva Tempranillo-blend — Muga, American-French oak, strawberry, dried cherry, vanilla, leather. The vanilla-oak wraps around gruyere-cream and the medium body handles dairy weight. Works for au gratin — a Chardonnay's cream-on-cream lifts higher.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Mushroom Bisque": "The mushroom bisque and the au gratin -- dairy plays against umami, the table reads layered. Works; sequence them or share the table, the call holds either way.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Myers's Rum": "Myers's Rum's rich layered-spirit body leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the rich pour wraps the au gratin, and the dense weight underlines the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Negroni": "Negroni's citrus-herbal build stays alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Never Say Die Rye": "Never Say Die Rye with au gratin potatoes — Yorkshire-aged against cheese-and-cream. Works; novelty maturation at matched register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Never Say Die Small Batch": "Never Say Die Small Batch with au gratin potatoes — Yorkshire-aged bourbon against cheese-and-cream. Strong; the novel maturation gives the side a unique voice.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|New Holland Beer Barrel Bourbon": "New Holland Beer Barrel Bourbon with the au gratin — Michigan beer-barrel against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; NH Beer Barrel handles the richness at Michigan-hometown register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|New York Sour": "New York Sour's spirit-forward cocktail register doubles down on the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- cocktail whiskey and dairy side meet without contrast — both heavy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a spirit-forward cocktail. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. New York Sour lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Nickel & Nickel Cabernet": "Au Gratin Potatoes: structured red meets dairy-driven side: the bold tannin scrubs the cream, the dark fruit lifts the indulgence into balance. A capable pair; richness aligns if not perfectly. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Nolets Dry Gin": "Nolets Dry Gin's bold char-floral botanicals leans against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Not a Paper Plane": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build finds neutral with the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Oban 14": "Oban 14 with the au gratin — West Highland against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Oban's subtle smoke handles the richness at maritime-Highland register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Oban 18": "Oban 18 with the au gratin — 18yr aged West Highland against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Oban 18's aged sherry-finish handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Ocho Anejo": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet Ocho Anejo. Works; single-estate character handles richness at craft register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Odette Cabernet Sauvignon": "Au Gratin Potatoes: the structured red's grip carries the rich side's dairy load; oak-driven body absorbs the cream and tannin clears the finish. A capable pair; richness aligns if not perfectly. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Old Elk Cigar Cut": "Old Elk Cigar Cut with the au gratin — cigar-paired bourbon against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Old Elk Cigar Cut handles the richness at cigar-companion register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Old Emmer": "Old Emmer with the au gratin — ancient-grain wheated bourbon against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Old Emmer handles the richness at craft register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Old Fitzgerald 7 Year": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with au gratin potatoes — 100-proof wheated against cheese-and-cream. Strong; the bonded wheat honey sits with richness cleanly.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Old Fitzgerald 9 Year": "Old Fitzgerald 9 Year with au gratin potatoes — aged wheated BIB against cheese-and-cream. Strong; mature honey and oak sit with richness at full register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Old Grand-Dad 16 Year": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet aged OGD. Strong; OGD 16's rye-spice handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Opus One": "Opus One — Oakville Bordeaux blend, dark fruit, mocha, cedar, dried violet, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts gruyère-cream weight and the mocha plays against the lactic richness. Works as collector Napa blend for au gratin — prestige wine on the cheesy side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Our Lady of Guadalupe Acolytes": "Our Lady of Guadalupe Acolytes's bold butter-char acidity reads alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Pablo Sour": "Pablo Sour's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift crowds the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- a light cocktail belongs with the opener or aperitif, not a savory side. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a light cocktail. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Pablo Sour on the steak course instead.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Paloma": "Reposado tequila, vanilla syrup, fresh grapefruit. The grapefruit's bitterness and the reposado's citrus profile fight our manchego gratin's savory cream. Paloma belongs with chicken, salmon, or lighter seafood — not potato sides. Avoid; the call reads off-register; recommend an alternative.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the allocated rye depth threads the au gratin, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; no driver pairing.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with the au gratin — HH collector cask-strength against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Parker's Heritage 16th handles the richness at annual-release register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Patron Anejo": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet Patron Anejo. Works; vanilla-caramel handles richness at workhorse register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Patron Silver": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the blanco-tequila body matches the au gratin, and the agave-citrus thread frames the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Patron XO Cafe": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Patron XO Cafe for the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Paul Bara Grand Rosé Brut": "Paul Bara Grand Rosé Brut's crisp mineral-raspberry acidity stays alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Au Gratin Potatoes and the PB brownie -- rich dairy yields to dessert weight, the close composes thickly. Works; clean transition or together if the table wants.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Peju Cabernet Sauvignon": "Napa Rutherford Cab — dark cherry, cassis, dusty cocoa, refined tannin. The elegant body cuts au gratin's cheese-and-cream weight and the cocoa plays against the golden crust. Strong elegant Napa Cab for au gratin — family-estate refinement on the decadent side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Pierre Ferrand Cognac": "Pierre Ferrand with the au gratin — artisanal cognac against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Ferrand's craft character handles the richness.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut": "Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut's char-citrus acidity sits alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Pikesville Rye": "Pikesville Rye with au gratin potatoes — 110-proof Maryland-style against cheese-and-cream. Works; high proof over-specified.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Pineau des Charentes": "Pineau des Charentes' sweet liqueur character doubles down on the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- sweet liqueur and dairy-rich side double the indulgence with no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Pineau des Charentes for the steak course.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Pio Cesare Barbaresco": "Au Gratin Potatoes: the side's cream pulls the bold red's tannin through; cassis and dark fruit catch the dairy's weight without overshooting. A capable pair; richness aligns if not perfectly. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Plymouth Gin": "Plymouth Gin's Plymouth-style-rounder botanicals sits alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate. Works; the match holds without overshooting. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Poderi Aldo Conterno Nebbiolo": "Piedmont Barolo DOCG Nebbiolo — Aldo Conterno Bussia Monforte d'Alba, rose petal, tar, dried cherry, orange peel, iron minerality, firm tannin, high acid. The high acid cuts gruyère-cream weight and the tar plays against the lactic richness. Works as serious-Barolo for au gratin — Aldo Conterno prestige on the cheesy side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Pommery Cuvée Louise": "Pommery Cuvée Louise's mineral-prestige acidity sits beside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Porterhouse": "Porterhouse with the au gratin -- the strip-and-tender frames the gruyere-baked potato. Excellent; the side that completes the steak plate.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Prime Tartare": "The tartare and the au gratin -- dairy plays against umami, the table reads layered. Works; sequence them or share the table, no concern either way.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Quilt Cabernet Sauvignon": "Napa Cab — ripe blackberry, dark chocolate, toasted vanilla, soft tannin. The lush body cuts au gratin's cheese-and-cream weight and the chocolate-vanilla plays against the golden crust. Strong polished Napa Cab for au gratin — indulgent lushness on the decadent side.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|RAEN Royal St Robert": "RAEN Royal St Robert's cherry-mineral tannin stays alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Rainbow Trout": "The trout alongside the au gratin -- the delicate plate yields to rich, the meal builds. Works; the side sits without pulling focus.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Raventós Cava de NIT Rosé Brut": "Raventós Cava de NIT Rosé Brut's crisp brine-mineral acidity sits beside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Redbreast 12 Year": "Redbreast 12 Year's single pot still Irish character sits alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the gentle Irish body threads the au gratin, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; bold character slightly over-specified for the soup.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Redbreast 21 Year": "Redbreast 21 Year's aged single pot still Irish sits alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the Irish whiskey body sits with the au gratin, and the oak softens the cream. Works; JW Black handles the richness at premium-blend register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Remus 15 Year Gatsby Reserve": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet George Remus tribute MGP. Strong; Remus 15 handles the richness at Gatsby-tribute register.",
  "Au Gratin Potatoes|Remy VSOP Cognac": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet refined cognac. Works; Rémy's elegance handles the richness at premium register.",
