  "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel|Rainbow Trout": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's First Fill American Oak flattens the trout's delicate flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a scotch. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Balvenie 16 Single Barrel on the steak course instead.",
  "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel|Roast Half Chicken": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's Highland-scotch character leans against the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the malt-and-oak threads the roast chicken, and the malt edge frames the plate. Works; the pour's brightness is a gentle counterpoint to the dessert's richness.",
