  "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the scotch depth settles into the garlic spinach, and the oak-and-smoke underlines the side. Works; AE Triple Cask meets the char at distinctive register.",
  "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel|Seafood Tower": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's First Fill American Oak fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Balvenie 16 Single Barrel for the steak course.",
  "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel|Seared Scallops": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel with seared scallops — single-barrel Speyside against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel|Seasonal Soup": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the scotch depth settles into the seasonal soup, and the malt edge frames the bowl. Works; polished 10-year gives the dessert small-batch premium character.",
  "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel|Seasonal Vegetables": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the seasonal vegetables, and the honey rounds the side. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel|Shrimp Bisque": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel with shrimp bisque — First Fill American Oak against cream-shrimp soup. Works; Balvenie 16 rides the bisque at collector register.",
  "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel|Shrimp Cocktail": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel with shrimp cocktail — First Fill American Oak against cold shrimp. Avoid; Scotch wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel|Swordfish": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's First Fill American Oak flattens the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Balvenie 16 Single Barrel belongs on the steak course.",
  "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel|The Tomahawk": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's First Fill American Oak leans against the Tomahawk's theatrical bone-in marbling and smoky char: the scotch depth settles into the 36oz showpiece, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; Parker's Heritage 16th's cask-strength character threads mushrooms at annual-release register.",
  "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel|Tomato Basil": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the malt-and-oak threads the tomato basil, and the oak-and-smoke underlines the bowl. Works; the pour's refinement is underused by the salad.",
  "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel|Truffle Fries": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel with truffle fries — single-barrel American Oak Speyside against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; the deeper vanilla and first-fill character meet the earthy-rich at collector register.",
  "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's First Fill American Oak overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Balvenie 16 Single Barrel for the steak course.",
  "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's First Fill American Oak finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the scotch depth settles into the curry, and the malt edge frames the bowl. Works; neutral, not elevating.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Asparagus": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside leans against the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the scotch depth settles into the asparagus, and the heather brightens the side. Works; annual-release wasted on salad.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with the au gratin — 21yr port-cask Speyside against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Portwood is over-specified for sides.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Beignets": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the Highland register carries the beignets, and the oak-and-smoke underlines the dessert. Works; save the BTAC bottle for the protein course — the side doesn't deserve the pour.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Bone Marrow": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with bone marrow — 21yr port-cask-finished Speyside against umami fat. Strong; Portwood's port red-berry depth frames marrow at collector register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Bone-In Filet": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with the bone-in filet — 21yr port-cask-finished Speyside against tenderloin-with-bone. Excellent; Portwood's port-richness and 21-year aging frame the cut with ultra-premium gravitas.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Broccoli Cheddar": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside leans against the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the broccoli cheddar, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; boutique-sourced doesn't drive.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Broccolini": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside reads alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the scotch backbone matches the broccolini, and the smoke threads the side. Works; EC 18's aged character meets the glaze at aged-HH register.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Brussels and Belly": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with Brussels + Belly — 21yr port-cask Speyside against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Portwood handles the glaze but Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask's rum-cask maple-bridge is the featured match.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Burrata": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with burrata — port-cask ultra-premium Speyside against fresh dairy. Avoid; Scotch weight wrong for burrata's cream.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Butternut Squash": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside reads alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the malt-driven body wraps the squash bisque, and the oak threads the cream. Works; polished aged character doesn't drive.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Carrot Cake": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with carrot cake — 21yr port-finished Speyside against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; Portwood's port-richness threads the cake's spice at collector register.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Cheesecake": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with cheesecake — 21yr port-cask Speyside against custard. Strong; Portwood's port red-berry frames the cheesecake at collector register.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Chilean Seabass": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; the better calls are above. Pour the Balvenie 21 Portwood on the steak course instead.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Chocolate Brownie": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with the chocolate brownie — 21yr port-cask Speyside against cocoa. Excellent; port-and-chocolate is a famous pairing — Portwood's port-derived red-berry fruit is the featured Sherried Speyside-chocolate-brownie match across the cluster.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Chocolate Cake": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside finds neutral with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the chocolate cake, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the dessert. Works; the fruit character gives the dessert a subtle counterpoint.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Clam Chowder": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the malt-and-oak threads the chowder, and the oak softens the cream. Works; light body doesn't overshoot.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Cowboy Ribeye": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with the cowboy ribeye — 21yr port-finished Speyside against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Excellent; Portwood is the featured Sherried Speyside-ribeye pairing — the port-cask red-berry richness and 21-year depth are built for fattier cuts where even Macallan 18 only catches up.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Crab Cake": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with crab cake — ultra-premium port-cask Speyside against delicate crab. Avoid; Scotch wrong for seafood — save the collector bottle.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Creamed Spinach": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with creamed spinach — ultra-premium 21yr port-cask Speyside against dairy-rich side. Works; Portwood is over-specified for a side — save for main course.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Creamy Potato": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the malt-driven body wraps the potato soup, and the oak threads the cream. Works; accessible gentle match.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Creme Brulee": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with creme brulee — 21yr port-finished Speyside against vanilla custard and caramelized sugar. Works; Portwood handles the brulee but Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask's rum-caramel is the featured brulee match.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Escargot": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's berry-juniper character sits with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; a steady recommendation at the table.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Faroe Island Salmon": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside smothers the salmon's rich oily flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a scotch. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Balvenie 21 Portwood for the steak course.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Filet Mignon": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with the filet — 21yr Speyside finished in port casks, red-berry-fruit and port-richness, ultra-premium collector-register. Excellent; port-and-beef is a classical marriage — Portwood's port-derived red-berry fruit frames tenderloin with the most premium Sherried Speyside-filet pairing in the cluster.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|French Onion": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside reads alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the scotch depth settles into the French onion, and the oak-and-smoke underlines the bowl. Works; the complex profile is over-specified for this dish.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Grilled Caesar": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside finds neutral with the Caesar's charred-romaine and anchovy edge: the malt-driven body wraps the grilled Caesar, and the smoke meets the char. Works; milestone-edition over-specified.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Gumbo": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside sits alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the gumbo, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the bowl. Works; distinctive character doesn't drive but adds interest.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside finds neutral with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the malt-and-oak threads the honey carrots, and the oak threads the caramelized sugar. Works; fruit-cask doesn't drive.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|House Wedge": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside leans against the wedge's iceberg-and-bleu cool crunch: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the wedge, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the bowl. Works; the 10-year's restraint lets the soup lead.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Kansas City": "Kansas City: strip marbling meets 21yr port-cask Speyside. Portwood's port-derived richness is tied with Macallan 18 as the featured Sherried Speyside-KC pairing — where Macallan 18 brings Oloroso dried-fruit, Portwood brings port red-berry. Both are built for strip marbling. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Loaded Potato": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside reads alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the scotch backbone matches the loaded potato soup, and the oak softens the cream. Works; the pour's toasted warmth threads through the char without overpowering.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Lobster Mac": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the lobster mac, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; curated character over-specified.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Market Fish": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside flattens the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a scotch. Avoid; one of those is the move. Balvenie 21 Portwood belongs on the steak course.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Mocha Creme": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with mocha creme — 21yr port-finished Speyside against coffee-chocolate dessert. Excellent; port's red-berry-fruit marries coffee and chocolate with collector-register depth — the featured Sherried Speyside-mocha pairing in the cluster.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Mushroom Bisque": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside finds neutral with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the malt-and-oak threads the mushroom bisque, and the oak frames the umami. Works; the pour's assertiveness is a bit much for the soup but doesn't clash.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Mushrooms": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with mushrooms — 21yr port-finished Speyside against earthy umami. Strong; Portwood's port-richness threads mushroom earthiness at collector register.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Peanut Butter Brownie: peanut butter and cocoa meet ultra-premium 21yr port-cask Speyside. Strong; Portwood's port-richness handles the dessert density at collector register; Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask's rum-cask brown-sugar is the featured PB-brownie match.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Porterhouse": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with the porterhouse — 21yr port-cask Speyside against strip-and-filet. Strong; Portwood's port-richness frames the two-cut plate at ultra-premium register.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Prime Tartare": "Balvenie 21 Portwood -- aged 21yr Speyside, port-finish, red fruit. The malt-driven body wraps the tartare, and the oak balances the umami register. Strong; Kentucky Owl St; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Rainbow Trout": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside swallows the trout's delicate flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a scotch. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Balvenie 21 Portwood lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Roast Half Chicken": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside reads alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the scotch depth settles into the roast chicken, and the heather brightens the plate. Works; the spicy-sweet character gives the dessert a Barton frame.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside finds neutral with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the port-cask depth wraps the chickpea soup, and the red-fruit frames the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Balvenie 21 Portwood for the steak course.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside sits alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the scotch depth settles into the garlic spinach, and the malt edge frames the side. Works; AE meets the char at wine-finish register.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Seafood Tower": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Balvenie 21 Portwood on the steak course instead.",
