  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Seasonal Soup": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside reads alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the Highland register carries the seasonal soup, and the heather brightens the bowl. Works; the match is gentle and approachable.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Seasonal Vegetables": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside sits alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the scotch backbone matches the seasonal vegetables, and the smoke threads the side. Works; boutique character doesn't drive.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Shrimp Bisque": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the port-cask depth wraps the shrimp bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; BIB over-specified for side.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Shrimp Cocktail": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with shrimp cocktail — 21yr port-finished Speyside against cold shrimp. Avoid; Scotch wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|Swordfish": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside overwhelms the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Balvenie 21 Portwood for the steak course.",
  "Balvenie 21 Portwood|The Tomahawk": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's berry-juniper character lifts the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the bourbon character meets the rendered fat, and the juniper sharpens the char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
