  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Carrot Cake": "Bardstown Château Laboude with carrot cake — French-wine-cask Bardstown against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Bardstown Château Laboude's French-wine-fruit threads the cake with contemporary-craft character.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Cheesecake": "Bardstown Château Laboude with cheesecake — French-wine-cask Bardstown against custard. Strong; Bardstown Château Laboude's French-wine-fruit threads the cheesecake at contemporary-craft register.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Chilean Seabass": "Bardstown Château Laboude's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Reserve the Bardstown Château Laboude for the steak course.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Chocolate Brownie": "Chocolate Brownie: warm cocoa meets Bardstown Bourbon Company's wine-cask finish release, French wine cask (Château Laboude), contemporary craft wine-finish approach. Bardstown Château Laboude's French-wine-cask character is the distinctive craft-wine-finished-chocolate pairing — the French-wine provenance distinguishes it from AE's Portuguese port approach. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Chocolate Cake": "Bardstown Château Laboude's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the oak depth lays under the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Fortuna handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Clam Chowder": "Bardstown Château Laboude's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chowder, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; OGD 16 handles dessert density at distinctive register.",
