  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Loaded Potato": "Bardstown Château Laboude's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the bourbon depth settles into the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; wine-cask complexity gives the dessert layered premium character.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Lobster Mac": "Bardstown Château Laboude's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon depth settles into the lobster mac, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the cream. Works; Caribbean Cask frames the two-cut plate at distinctive register.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Market Fish": "Bardstown Château Laboude's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Bardstown Château Laboude on the steak course instead.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Mocha Creme": "Bardstown Château Laboude with mocha creme — Bardstown Bourbon Co. French-wine finish against coffee-chocolate dessert. Works; Bardstown Château Laboude's French-wine-fruit threads mocha at contemporary-craft register.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Mushroom Bisque": "Bardstown Château Laboude's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the brown-spirit warmth threads the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the pairing is pleasant but not a standout.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Mushrooms": "Bardstown Château Laboude with mushrooms — Bardstown French-wine-cask finish against earthy umami. Strong; Bardstown Château Laboude's French-wine character threads mushrooms at contemporary-craft register.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Bardstown Château Laboude with the PB brownie — Bardstown Bourbon Co. French-wine finish against peanut butter and cocoa. Excellent; Bardstown Château Laboude's French-wine character handles dessert density at contemporary-craft register.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Porterhouse": "Bardstown Château Laboude's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character: the bourbon depth settles into the dual-cut steak, and the vanilla brightens the grilled char-edge. Strong; reliable headline pairing across the table.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Prime Tartare": "Bardstown Château Laboude's vanilla character lifts the tartare's raw beef and brine — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Rainbow Trout": "Bardstown Château Laboude's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the trout's delicate flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Bardstown Château Laboude on the steak course instead.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Roast Half Chicken": "Bardstown Château Laboude's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the brown-spirit warmth threads the roast chicken, and the oak-and-spice register settles the plate. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Bardstown Château Laboude's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the bourbon weight handles the chickpea soup, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; bonded weight pushes slightly past the soup.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Bardstown Château Laboude's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Bardstown Château Laboude for the steak course.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Bardstown Château Laboude's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the brown-spirit warmth threads the garlic spinach, and the rounded sweetness brightens the side. Works; premium KO story wasted on salad.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Seafood Tower": "Bardstown Château Laboude's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Bardstown Château Laboude for the steak course.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Seared Scallops": "Bardstown Château Laboude with seared scallops — Bardstown Bourbon Co. French-wine finish against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Seasonal Soup": "Bardstown Château Laboude's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the seasonal soup, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; the pour's complexity is underused by the salad.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Seasonal Vegetables": "Bardstown Château Laboude's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the bourbon body sits with the seasonal vegetables, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the side. Works; accessible gentle match.",
