  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Swordfish": "Bardstown Château Laboude's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Bardstown Château Laboude for the steak course.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|The Tomahawk": "Bardstown Château Laboude's vanilla character holds steady against the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the caramel-and-oak weight rises with the cap-fat, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Tomato Basil": "Bardstown Château Laboude's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the bourbon backbone carries the tomato basil, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; premium proof overpowers this dish.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Truffle Fries": "Bardstown Château Laboude with truffle fries — Bardstown French-wine-cask against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Bardstown Château Laboude's French-wine-fruit meets the earthy-rich with contemporary-craft distinction.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Bardstown Château Laboude's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Bardstown Château Laboude belongs on the steak course.",
  "Bardstown Château Laboude|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Bardstown Château Laboude's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the bourbon backbone carries the curry, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; the aging is wasted on the salad.",
