  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Faroe Island Salmon": "Bardstown Founders KBS's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Bardstown Founders KBS lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Filet Mignon": "Bardstown Founders KBS with the filet — stout-barrel-finished against the 10oz cut. Strong; KBS's beer-barrel distinctiveness is a conversation-starter but single-distillery aged bourbons (Weller 12, Blanton's) bring more traditional filet character.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|French Onion": "Bardstown Founders KBS's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the brown-spirit warmth threads the French onion, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; oak slightly over-specified for this dish.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Grilled Caesar": "Bardstown Founders KBS with the grilled Caesar — stout-barrel against charred romaine. Works; KBS character doesn't drive the Caesar.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Gumbo": "Bardstown Founders KBS's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the caramel-spice register matches the gumbo, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Bardstown Founders KBS's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the honey carrots, and the oak threads the caramelized sugar. Works; mid-proof pour is slightly over-specified.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|House Wedge": "Bardstown Founders KBS with the House Wedge — KBS-finished against iceberg and bleu. Works; stout-barrel story wasted on salad.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Kansas City": "Bardstown Founders KBS with the KC — Bardstown's collab release finished in Founders Brewing's KBS (Kentucky Breakfast Stout) barrels. Coffee, chocolate, and stout-beer notes atop bourbon; a genuinely distinctive stout-barrel-finished bourbon that nothing else on the menu replicates. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Loaded Potato": "Bardstown Founders KBS's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the bourbon depth settles into the loaded potato soup, and the oak frames the cream. Works; doesn't drive.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Lobster Mac": "Bardstown Founders KBS's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the caramel-spice register matches the lobster mac, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; IW Harper 15 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Market Fish": "Bardstown Founders KBS's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Bardstown Founders KBS for the steak course.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Mocha Creme": "Bardstown Founders KBS's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the bourbon depth settles into the mocha creme, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; accessible gentle match.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Mushroom Bisque": "Bardstown Founders KBS's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the bourbon backbone carries the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Mushrooms": "Bardstown Founders KBS with the mushrooms — KBS-finished against earthy umami. Strong; coffee-stout notes layer into mushroom depth with beer-barrel distinctiveness.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Bardstown Founders KBS with the PB brownie — stout-barrel-finished bourbon against peanut butter and cocoa. The KBS coffee and chocolate notes find the dessert's cocoa and PB in a way no other bourbon on the menu does; standout dessert pairing. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Porterhouse": "Bardstown Founders KBS with the porterhouse — stout-barrel-finished across strip and filet. Works; KBS distinctiveness is slightly over-specified for the two-cut plate.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Prime Tartare": "Bardstown Founders KBS's chocolate-cocoa character lifts the tartare's raw beef and brine — the bourbon depth cuts the umami fat, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Rainbow Trout": "Bardstown Founders KBS's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Bardstown Founders KBS for the steak course.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Roast Half Chicken": "Bardstown Founders KBS's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the bourbon backbone carries the roast chicken, and the oak-and-spice register settles the plate. Works; 100-proof complexity sits beside the soup.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Bardstown Founders KBS's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chickpea soup, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; Old Fitz 9 brings more depth here.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Bardstown Founders KBS's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Bardstown Founders KBS for the steak course.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Bardstown Founders KBS's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the bourbon backbone carries the garlic spinach, and the oak-and-spice register settles the side. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Bardstown Founders KBS|Seafood Tower": "Bardstown Founders KBS's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Bardstown Founders KBS for the steak course.",
