  "Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the oak depth lays under the curry, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; richer profile is over-specified for this dish.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Asparagus": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the asparagus, and the oak-and-spice register settles the side. Works; the VR Twin Oak is over-specified for the soup's register.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with au gratin potatoes — aged high-rye against cheese-and-cream. Strong; the 10-year gives the pour weight the side can accept.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Beignets": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the brown-spirit warmth threads the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the single-barrel depth is slightly over-specified for the dessert.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Bone Marrow": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with bone marrow — aged depth gives the pour the weight the starter demands. Where standard Basil Hayden's is outmatched, 10-year's maturity meets the marrow's umami fat cleanly. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Bone-In Filet": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's crisp char-juniper character lifts the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the bourbon depth carries the cut, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Broccoli Cheddar": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the oak depth lays under the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; EC 18's aged character meets the glaze at aged-HH register.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Broccolini": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's aged oak and rye spice reads alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the bourbon depth settles into the broccolini, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Brussels and Belly": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with Brussels + Belly — aged rye spice meets maple-glazed pork belly. The 10-year gives the pairing backbone that standard Basil Hayden's doesn't; a refined small-plate pour. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Burrata": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with burrata — fresh dairy can't carry aged rye spice. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Butternut Squash": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the oak depth lays under the squash bisque, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; BIB structure is a touch over-specified for this dish.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Carrot Cake": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with carrot cake — aged rye spice against cream cheese and cinnamon. The 10-year's maturity picks up the cake's raisins; more layered than standard Basil Hayden's with this dessert. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Cheesecake": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with cheesecake — aged high-rye against custard. Works; the 10-year's oak adds dimension but the match is still gentle.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Chilean Seabass": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's aged oak and rye spice smothers the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Basil Hayden's 10 Year for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Chocolate Brownie": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with the chocolate brownie — aged rye against cocoa. Works; for more interplay with chocolate, Basil Hayden's Toast (in the family) or Weller 107 is the call.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Chocolate Cake": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the bourbon depth settles into the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Clam Chowder": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon backbone carries the chowder, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; bonded weight pushes slightly past the soup.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Cowboy Ribeye": "Cowboy Ribeye: cap fat and char meet aged Basil Hayden's. Aging gives the pour more body, but 80-proof caps the match. Strong; Weller 12 or Eagle Rare 10 Year remain stronger.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Crab Cake": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with crab cake — aged bourbon against delicate crab. Avoid; even refined Basil Hayden's overshoots the starter.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Creamed Spinach": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with creamed spinach — aged rye spice against dairy richness. The 10-year adds oak depth to Basil Hayden's brighter-than-wheated profile; strong. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Creamy Potato": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the caramel-spice register matches the potato soup, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Creme Brulee": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the brown-spirit warmth threads the brulee, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; smooth character is slightly over-specified for this dish.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Escargot": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's aged oak and rye spice leans against the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the bourbon depth settles into the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; aged BIB at matched premium register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Faroe Island Salmon": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's aged oak and rye spice clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Basil Hayden's 10 Year lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Filet Mignon": "Filet Mignon: the 10oz center-cut meets Basil Hayden's 10 Year's aged 80-proof depth. More refined than standard Basil Hayden's; the aged high-rye pour for filet. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|French Onion": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the bourbon weight handles the French onion, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Grilled Caesar": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with the grilled Caesar — aged rye spice against charred romaine and anchovy. Works; the 10-year earns a bit more of the Caesar than standard Basil Hayden's but not as much as Weller 12.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Gumbo": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the bourbon depth settles into the gumbo, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; annual-release covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth leans against the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the brown-spirit warmth threads the honey carrots, and the oak threads the caramelized sugar. Works; the aging is wasted on the salad.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|House Wedge": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with the House Wedge — aged high-rye against iceberg and bleu. Works; the pour's refinement is underused by the salad.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Kansas City": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with the KC — the aged body finally gives Basil Hayden's the weight to match the strip's marbling. Where standard Basil Hayden's is underpowered here, the 10-year earns it. The high-rye alternate to Weller 12 for strip pairings. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Loaded Potato": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the oak depth lays under the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; accessible gentle match.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Lobster Mac": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon depth settles into the lobster mac, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Market Fish": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's aged oak and rye spice flattens the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Basil Hayden's 10 Year for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Mocha Creme": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the caramel-spice register matches the mocha creme, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; allocated character doesn't drive.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Mushroom Bisque": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's aged oak and rye spice finds neutral with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the bourbon depth settles into the mushroom bisque, and the caramel softens the cream. Works; the toast adds a warmth the dessert can accept.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Mushrooms": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with the mushrooms — aged high-rye against earthy umami. The 10-year's depth layers into mushroom character; the most refined Basil Hayden's for this side. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the bourbon backbone carries the PB brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the smooth character gives the dessert a composed frame.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Porterhouse": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with the porterhouse — aged high-rye handles both strip and filet sides more evenly than standard Basil Hayden's. Strong; a refined Basil Hayden's call for this plate.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Prime Tartare": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's crisp char-juniper character holds the line with the tartare's raw beef and brine — the bourbon weight grips the savory plate, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Rainbow Trout": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's aged oak and rye spice overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Basil Hayden's 10 Year for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Roast Half Chicken": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the bourbon weight handles the roast chicken, and the caramel rounds the plate. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the bourbon weight handles the chickpea soup, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; the match is gentle and approachable.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's aged oak and rye spice overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Basil Hayden's 10 Year for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the garlic spinach, and the caramel rounds the side. Works; rare-release wasted on salad.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Seafood Tower": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's aged oak and rye spice drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Basil Hayden's 10 Year belongs on the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Seared Scallops": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against aged high-rye. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Seasonal Soup": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the bourbon backbone carries the seasonal soup, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Seasonal Vegetables": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the bourbon depth settles into the seasonal vegetables, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; friendly accessible match.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Shrimp Bisque": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with shrimp bisque — aged light high-rye against cream-based seafood. Works; the 10-year's restraint lets the soup lead.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Shrimp Cocktail": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp and aged bourbon don't bridge. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Swordfish": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's aged oak and rye spice swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Basil Hayden's 10 Year for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|The Tomahawk": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's crisp char-juniper character holds steady against the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the bourbon depth grips the marbled cut, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Tomato Basil": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the brown-spirit warmth threads the tomato basil, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Truffle Fries": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with truffle fries — aged oak and rye spice against truffle-parmesan. The 10-year brings more vocabulary than standard Basil Hayden's; a sophisticated light-bourbon pairing for this side. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's aged oak and rye spice swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Basil Hayden's 10 Year for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's 10 Year|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the bourbon backbone carries the curry, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; high proof over-specified for the soup.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Asparagus": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the rye backbone drives the asparagus, and the dry-spice register brightens the side. Works; the bourbon's character is distinctive but the pairing isn't a standout.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with au gratin potatoes — malted grain against cheese-and-cream. Bread-and-dairy again; the pairing works on grain logic in a way wheated bourbons don't touch. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Beignets": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the rye backbone drives the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Remus 15 handles dessert density at Gatsby-tribute register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Bone Marrow": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with bone marrow — bready malted grain against umami fat. Distinctive but outmatched by Weller 12 on weight; the pour's character is the draw, not the match for marrow's intensity. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Bone-In Filet": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the rye spice cuts the bone-enhanced filet, and the rye edge frames the cut. Strong; accessible everyday match.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Broccoli Cheddar": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the rye-and-oak weight handles the broccoli cheddar, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; Parker's Heritage 16th handles the richness at annual-release register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Broccolini": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the broccolini's tender green stalks: the rye-and-oak weight handles the broccolini, and the rye-grain bite cuts the side. Works; bold intensity slightly over-specified.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Brussels and Belly": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with Brussels + Belly — spicy-sweet malted rye meets maple-glazed pork belly. The bready character picks up the Brussels' char and the pork belly's maple; distinctive and specifically Basil Hayden's Malted Rye. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Burrata": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with burrata — fresh dairy against bready malted. Avoid; the pour's character can't find the burrata's gentleness.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Butternut Squash": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the rye-and-oak weight handles the squash bisque, and the oak softens the cream. Works; Portwood is over-specified for sides.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Carrot Cake": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with carrot cake — spicy-sweet malted rye against cream cheese and cinnamon. The malted character and cake warmth find common ground; a distinctive within-family dessert pairing. Strong; the pairing reads at register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Cheesecake": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with cheesecake — bready malted notes against custard. Works; the bread-and-custard pairing is capable without being remarkable.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Chilean Seabass": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character smothers the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Basil Hayden's Malted Rye for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Chocolate Brownie": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with the chocolate brownie — malted grain against cocoa. Works; for chocolate interplay, Basil Hayden's Toast is the family call.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Chocolate Cake": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the high-rye spice register matches the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Clam Chowder": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the rye backbone drives the chowder, and the oak threads the cream. Works; Fortuna's NZ terroir meets the glaze at distinctive register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Cowboy Ribeye": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with the Cowboy Ribeye — malted character against cap fat. Underpowered for the cut; Weller 12 or Eagle Rare 10 Year remain stronger, but the malted rye offers a distinct flavor proposition. Strong; the pairing reads at register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Crab Cake": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with crab cake — malted rye against crab delicacy. Avoid; even distinctive character doesn't rescue the register mismatch.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Creamed Spinach": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with creamed spinach — bready malted grain against dairy richness. The bread-and-dairy pairing logic is built-in; malted rye's grain character threads through the cream in a way no other Basil Hayden's reaches here. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Creamy Potato": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the high-rye spice register matches the potato soup, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; multi-distillery complexity doesn't drive.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Creme Brulee": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character leans against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the rye spice cuts the brulee, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Escargot": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's crisp char-earth character holds steady against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the caramel-oak depth threads the savory plate, and the spice frames the umami depth. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Faroe Island Salmon": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character swallows the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Basil Hayden's Malted Rye for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Filet Mignon": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with the filet — malted rye mash gives this pour a bready, distinctive grain character that nothing else on the menu brings. 80-proof light body frames the filet with a grain vocabulary standard Basil Hayden's doesn't have. A distinctive, unexpected filet pour. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|French Onion": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the rye spice cuts the French onion, and the rye-grain bite cuts the bowl. Works; Discovery complexity wasted on salad simplicity.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Grilled Caesar": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with the grilled Caesar — malted rye against charred romaine and anchovy. Works; grain notes pick up the char but the Caesar's weight still pushes against 80-proof light-body.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Gumbo": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the high-rye spice register matches the gumbo, and the rye edge frames the bowl. Works; bold rye slightly over-specified.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the rye spice cuts the honey carrots, and the oak frames the caramelized sugar. Works; boutique-sourced wasted on salad.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|House Wedge": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with the House Wedge — malted bread notes against iceberg and bleu. Works; the grain character adds something standard Basil Hayden's can't, but the salad's simplicity still caps the match.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Kansas City": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with the KC — malted grain character against the strip's marbling. 80-proof still caps the weight, but the malted rye brings a grain-forward dimension no other Basil Hayden's has for this cut. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Loaded Potato": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character leans against the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the high-rye spice register matches the loaded potato soup, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; spice over-specified for side's character.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Lobster Mac": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the lobster mac, and the oak softens the cream. Works; milestone-release covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Market Fish": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Basil Hayden's Malted Rye belongs on the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Mocha Creme": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character leans against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the rye-and-oak weight handles the mocha creme, and the oak softens the cream. Works; BH Red Wine Cask's softer-proof character rides the cream at distinctive register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Mushroom Bisque": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the rye spice cuts the mushroom bisque, and the oak threads the umami plate. Works; narrative-bourbon doesn't drive.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Mushrooms": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with the mushrooms — malted grain bread notes against earthy umami. The bready malted character echoes the mushroom's depth; a distinctive pairing within the Basil Hayden's family. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the rye backbone drives the PB brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; collector-bottle depth gives the dessert ultra-premium character.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Porterhouse": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with the porterhouse — malted bready character across both cuts. The grain notes give both sides something distinctive; strong and specifically character-forward. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Prime Tartare": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's crisp char-earth character finds register with the tartare's raw beef and brine — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the spice frames the umami depth. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Rainbow Trout": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Basil Hayden's Malted Rye for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Roast Half Chicken": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the rye spice cuts the roast chicken, and the rye-pepper note underlines the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the rye spice cuts the chickpea soup, and the rye edge frames the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Basil Hayden's Malted Rye lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character leans against the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the dry rye body wraps the garlic spinach, and the rye edge frames the side. Works; Fortuna handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Seafood Tower": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Basil Hayden's Malted Rye for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Seared Scallops": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with seared scallops — malted grain against caramelized scallop. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Seasonal Soup": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character leans against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the rye spice cuts the seasonal soup, and the dry-spice register brightens the bowl. Works; 100-proof complexity sits beside the soup.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Seasonal Vegetables": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the seasonal vegetables, and the rye-grain bite cuts the side. Works; OGD 16 frames the two-cut plate at distinctive register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Shrimp Bisque": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with shrimp bisque — malted character against cream-based seafood. Works; grain notes don't really engage the soup but don't clash.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Shrimp Cocktail": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against malted rye. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Swordfish": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Save the Basil Hayden's Malted Rye for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|The Tomahawk": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's crisp char-earth character holds the line with the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the bourbon weight matches the cap-fat, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Tomato Basil": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the rye backbone drives the tomato basil, and the rye-grain bite cuts the bowl. Works; PNW character doesn't drive.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Truffle Fries": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with truffle fries — bready malted grain against truffle-parmesan. The malted character finds the truffle's earthiness in a way no other Basil Hayden's does; distinctive, layered. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Basil Hayden's Malted Rye belongs on the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the dry rye body wraps the curry, and the rye edge frames the bowl. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Asparagus": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the bourbon depth settles into the asparagus, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; AE Triple Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with the au gratin — BH high-rye red-wine finish against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; BH Red Wine Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Beignets": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon backbone carries the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; high proof over-specified.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Bone Marrow": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with bone marrow — Beam 80-proof BH against umami fat. Works; BH Red Wine Cask is under-specified for marrow at softer proof; AE Cask Strength handles marrow better.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Bone-In Filet": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with the bone-in filet — Beam's BH red-wine finish against tenderloin-with-bone. Excellent; BH Red Wine Cask's rye-spice + red-wine-fruit frames the cut at distinctive register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Broccoli Cheddar": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the oak depth lays under the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the pour's refinement is underused by the salad.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Broccolini": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the broccolini's tender green stalks: the caramel-spice register matches the broccolini, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; novelty maturation at matched register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Brussels and Belly": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the bourbon depth settles into the pork-belly plate, and the vanilla brightens the grilled char-edge. Works; boutique-sourced wasted on salad; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Burrata": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with burrata — BH high-rye red-wine finish against fresh dairy. Avoid; bourbon weight wrong for burrata.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Butternut Squash": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bourbon depth settles into the squash bisque, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the 10-year holds without lifting.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Carrot Cake": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with carrot cake — high-rye BH red-wine finish against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; BH Red Wine Cask's rye-spice marries cinnamon + the red-wine fruit marries raisins — a dual-complement featured pairing.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Cheesecake": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with cheesecake — high-rye BH red-wine finish against custard. Strong; BH Red Wine Cask's red-wine-fruit threads the cheesecake with rye-spice dimension.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Chilean Seabass": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Pour the Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask on the steak course instead.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Chocolate Brownie": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with the chocolate brownie — Beam's Basil Hayden finished in red wine casks, high-rye mash bill base, 80-proof softer approach. Excellent; BH Red Wine Cask's high-rye + red-wine-finish is the featured rye-forward wine-finished-chocolate pairing — the high-rye base + red-wine fruit adds dimension where AE's wheated-style port-finish doesn't reach.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Chocolate Cake": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the bourbon depth settles into the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Clam Chowder": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chowder, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the distinctive character is underused by the salad's simplicity.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Cowboy Ribeye": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with the cowboy ribeye — 80-proof BH red-wine finish against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Strong; BH Red Wine Cask is under-specified for cap-fat at 80-proof; AE Cask Strength handles ribeye better.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Crab Cake": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with crab cake — high-rye BH red-wine finish against delicate lump crab. Avoid; bourbon wrong for seafood. Reach for a vodka or gin.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Creamed Spinach": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with creamed spinach — Beam BH red-wine finish against dairy-rich side. Works; BH Red Wine Cask's softer-proof character rides the cream at distinctive register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Creamy Potato": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the caramel-spice register matches the potato soup, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; gentle composed match.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Creme Brulee": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with creme brulee — BH high-rye red-wine finish against vanilla custard and caramelized sugar. Strong; BH Red Wine Cask's red-wine-fruit + rye-spice meets the caramel at distinctive register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Escargot": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's crisp oak character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the caramel-oak depth threads the savory plate, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Faroe Island Salmon": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with the salmon — high-rye BH red-wine finish against oily salmon. Avoid; wine-finished bourbon wrong for fish.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Filet Mignon": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with the filet — BH high-rye with red-wine finish against tenderloin. Excellent; BH Red Wine Cask's rye-forward + red-wine-fruit frames tenderloin with distinctive wine-finish character.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|French Onion": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the bourbon weight handles the French onion, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; the toast adds a warmth the dessert can accept.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Grilled Caesar": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with the grilled Caesar — high-rye BH red-wine finish against charred romaine and anchovy. Works; BH Red Wine Cask meets the char at distinctive register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Gumbo": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the bourbon depth settles into the gumbo, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the brown-spirit warmth threads the honey carrots, and the oak balances the burnt-sugar edge. Works; the pour's toasted warmth threads through the char without overpowering.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|House Wedge": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with the House Wedge — Beam BH red-wine finish against iceberg and bleu. Works; BH Red Wine Cask's red-wine-fruit engages the bleu at distinctive register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Kansas City": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with the KC — BH red-wine finish against an 18oz strip. Strong; BH Red Wine Cask handles the strip with rye-spice + red-wine character; AE Cask Strength is the featured wine-finished-KC match.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Loaded Potato": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the oak depth lays under the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the 10-year's oak adds dimension but the match is still gentle.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Lobster Mac": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon depth settles into the lobster mac, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; boutique covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Market Fish": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask belongs on the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Mocha Creme": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with mocha creme — BH red-wine finish against coffee-chocolate dessert. Works; BH Red Wine Cask's red-wine-fruit + rye-spice threads mocha at distinctive register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Mushroom Bisque": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; no driver pairing.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Mushrooms": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with mushrooms — Beam high-rye red-wine finish against earthy umami. Strong; BH Red Wine Cask's rye + red-wine character threads mushrooms at distinctive register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with the PB brownie — BH high-rye red-wine finish against peanut butter and cocoa. Excellent; BH Red Wine Cask's rye-spice + red-wine-fruit handles dessert density with dimension.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Porterhouse": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character: the oak depth lays under the dual-cut steak, and the vanilla underlines the rendered char. Strong; EHT Full Proof meets the earthy-rich at historic Kentucky register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Prime Tartare": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami: the bourbon depth settles into the tartare, and the oak threads the umami plate. Strong; the WP-core aged depth is a refined counterpoint to tartare; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Rainbow Trout": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the trout's delicate flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Roast Half Chicken": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the bourbon depth settles into the roast chicken, and the vanilla softens the plate. Works; the 10-year's oak adds dimension but the match is still gentle.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the bourbon weight handles the chickpea soup, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the garlic spinach, and the rounded sweetness brightens the side. Works; pour's narrative is underused by the salad.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Seafood Tower": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Seared Scallops": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with seared scallops — Beam BH red-wine finish against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Seasonal Soup": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the bourbon backbone carries the seasonal soup, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; craft-blend over-specified.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Seasonal Vegetables": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the bourbon depth settles into the seasonal vegetables, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Shrimp Bisque": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with shrimp bisque — Beam BH red-wine finish against cream-shrimp soup. Avoid; red-wine-fruit clashes with seafood soup.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Shrimp Cocktail": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with shrimp cocktail — Beam BH against cold shrimp. Avoid; bourbon wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Swordfish": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask belongs on the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|The Tomahawk": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's crisp oak character holds steady against the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the caramel-and-oak weight rises with the cap-fat, and the oak underlines the char. Strong; a steady recommendation at the table.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Tomato Basil": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the bourbon backbone carries the tomato basil, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Truffle Fries": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with truffle fries — Beam high-rye red-wine finish against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; BH Red Wine Cask's rye-spice + red-wine-fruit meets the earthy-rich with distinctive dimension.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask belongs on the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the brown-spirit warmth threads the curry, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; EC 18 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Asparagus": "Basil Hayden's Toast's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the bourbon depth settles into the asparagus, and the oak frames the side. Works; bonded weight a touch ambitious for the dessert.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Basil Hayden's Toast with au gratin potatoes — toast character against cheese-and-cream. Strong; the toast notes add a layer standard Basil Hayden's can't bring.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Beignets": "Basil Hayden's Toast's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon depth settles into the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; regional craft at matched register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Bone Marrow": "Basil Hayden's Toast with bone marrow — toasted caramel notes against umami fat. The toast adds dessert-adjacent sweetness to the starter; more interesting than standard Basil Hayden's but still outmatched by Weller 12's depth. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Bone-In Filet": "Basil Hayden's Toast's crisp caramel-smoke character finds register with the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the bourbon depth supports the lean cut without overpowering, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Broccoli Cheddar": "Basil Hayden's Toast's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the pour's assertiveness is a bit much for the soup but doesn't clash.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Broccolini": "Basil Hayden's Toast's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight sits alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the brown-spirit warmth threads the broccolini, and the rounded sweetness brightens the side. Works; boutique-blend depth gives composed dessert character.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Brussels and Belly": "Basil Hayden's Toast with Brussels + Belly — toasted caramel meets maple-glazed pork belly. The toast-finish echoes the dish's sweetness without the pour going heavy; a clean, light, signature-flavored small-plate pairing. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Burrata": "Basil Hayden's Toast with burrata — fresh dairy against toasted caramel. Avoid; the pour's warmth doesn't find the burrata's coolness.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Butternut Squash": "Basil Hayden's Toast's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth leans against the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bourbon backbone carries the squash bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; distinctive character doesn't drive but adds interest.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Carrot Cake": "Basil Hayden's Toast with carrot cake — toasted marshmallow sweetness against cream cheese frosting and cinnamon. The toast character and cake spice find each other; a distinct dessert pairing within the Basil Hayden's family. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Cheesecake": "Basil Hayden's Toast with cheesecake — toast-barrel caramel against clean custard. Works; the toast adds a warmth the dessert can accept.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Chilean Seabass": "Basil Hayden's Toast's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Basil Hayden's Toast belongs on the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Chocolate Brownie": "Basil Hayden's Toast with the chocolate brownie — toast-barrel caramel and marshmallow notes against cocoa and fudge. The toast character is built for this dessert; the most remarkable Basil Hayden's for chocolate brownie. Distinct from Weller 107's bigger-body version — lighter, more toasted-sweet. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Chocolate Cake": "Basil Hayden's Toast's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the bourbon weight handles the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; curated character over-specified.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Clam Chowder": "Basil Hayden's Toast's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the caramel-spice register matches the chowder, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the blend's complexity is underused by the salad.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Cowboy Ribeye": "Basil Hayden's Toast with the Cowboy Ribeye — toast finish against the cut's cap fat. Still underpowered for the ribeye's scale, but the toast notes give the pour more to say than standard Basil Hayden's does. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Crab Cake": "Basil Hayden's Toast with crab cake — toasted caramel against delicate crab is a mismatch. Avoid; choose a crisp white wine.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Creamed Spinach": "Basil Hayden's Toast with creamed spinach — toast and caramel against dairy. The toasted finish softens the side's richness with marshmallow warmth; distinct from wheated-caramel takes. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Creamy Potato": "Basil Hayden's Toast's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the bourbon backbone carries the potato soup, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; milestone-collector wasted on salad.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Creme Brulee": "Basil Hayden's Toast's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the caramel-spice register matches the brulee, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; the bonded richness gives the dessert more than lighter pours do.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Escargot": "Basil Hayden's Toast's crisp caramel-smoke character sits with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the caramel-oak depth threads the savory plate, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; a steady recommendation at the table.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Faroe Island Salmon": "Basil Hayden's Toast's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the salmon's rich oily flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Basil Hayden's Toast on the steak course instead.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Filet Mignon": "Filet Mignon: the 10oz center-cut meets Basil Hayden's Toast's toasted-barrel caramel and marshmallow notes over the 80-proof base. Distinct from standard Basil Hayden's — more caramel, less bare rye. A light filet pour with signature character. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|French Onion": "Basil Hayden's Toast's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the bourbon depth settles into the French onion, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; the pairing is pleasant but not a standout.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Grilled Caesar": "Basil Hayden's Toast with the grilled Caesar — toast and marshmallow against charred romaine. Works; the pour's toasted warmth threads through the char without overpowering.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Gumbo": "Basil Hayden's Toast's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the bourbon weight handles the gumbo, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; a composed but not remarkable match.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Basil Hayden's Toast's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the caramel-spice register matches the honey carrots, and the oak threads the caramelized sugar. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|House Wedge": "Basil Hayden's Toast with the House Wedge — toast notes against iceberg and bleu. Works; the toast gives the salad a little more than standard Basil Hayden's would.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Kansas City": "Basil Hayden's Toast with the KC — toast-barrel character against the strip's marbling. The 80-proof light body still pushes against the strip's weight, but the toast finish adds dimension standard Basil Hayden's doesn't have. Strong.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Loaded Potato": "Basil Hayden's Toast's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the bourbon depth settles into the loaded potato soup, and the rounded sweetness brightens the cream. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Lobster Mac": "Basil Hayden's Toast's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the lobster mac, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the richer pour finds more with the dessert than Original brings.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Market Fish": "Basil Hayden's Toast's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Basil Hayden's Toast lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Mocha Creme": "Basil Hayden's Toast's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the brown-spirit warmth threads the mocha creme, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; save the bottle for the protein course — a soup is wrong for a $200 pour.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Mushroom Bisque": "Basil Hayden's Toast's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the bourbon body sits with the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; the complex profile is over-specified for this dish.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Mushrooms": "Basil Hayden's Toast with the mushrooms — toast-barrel caramel and light high-rye against earthy umami. The toasted sweetness gives mushroom depth a counterpoint; distinct from standard Basil Hayden's, more forthcoming. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Basil Hayden's Toast's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the oak depth lays under the PB brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; bold intensity slightly over-specified.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Porterhouse": "Basil Hayden's Toast with the porterhouse — toasted caramel across the strip-and-filet split. Works better than standard Basil Hayden's on this plate; the toast character gives both cuts something to meet.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Prime Tartare": "Basil Hayden's Toast's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami: the bourbon depth settles into the tartare, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; EHT Full Proof threads mushrooms at historic Kentucky-bourbon register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Rainbow Trout": "Basil Hayden's Toast's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the trout's delicate flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Basil Hayden's Toast lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Roast Half Chicken": "Basil Hayden's Toast's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the bourbon body sits with the roast chicken, and the vanilla softens the plate. Works; cleaner than wheated versions but not exceptional.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Basil Hayden's Toast's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the bourbon depth settles into the chickpea soup, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; OGD 16 handles dessert density at distinctive register.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Basil Hayden's Toast's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Basil Hayden's Toast for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Basil Hayden's Toast's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth leans against the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the bourbon body sits with the garlic spinach, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the side. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Seafood Tower": "Basil Hayden's Toast's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Basil Hayden's Toast for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Seared Scallops": "Basil Hayden's Toast with seared scallops — caramelized scallop doesn't need the pour's added toast sweetness. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Seasonal Soup": "Basil Hayden's Toast's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the bourbon body sits with the seasonal soup, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; the 10-year's oak adds dimension but the match is still gentle.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Seasonal Vegetables": "Basil Hayden's Toast's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the bourbon weight handles the seasonal vegetables, and the oak-and-spice register settles the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Shrimp Bisque": "Basil Hayden's Toast with shrimp bisque — toasted caramel against cream-based seafood. Works; the toast notes don't really interplay with the soup but don't clash.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Shrimp Cocktail": "Basil Hayden's Toast with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against toasted bourbon. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Swordfish": "Basil Hayden's Toast's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Basil Hayden's Toast on the steak course instead.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|The Tomahawk": "Basil Hayden's Toast's crisp caramel-smoke character holds the line with the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the bourbon character meets the rendered fat, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Tomato Basil": "Basil Hayden's Toast's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the caramel-spice register matches the tomato basil, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; X Commandments story wasted on salad.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Truffle Fries": "Basil Hayden's Toast with truffle fries — toasted caramel notes against truffle-parmesan fat. The toast finish lifts the side with a different vocabulary than straight Basil Hayden's; a more layered light-bourbon pairing for this side. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Basil Hayden's Toast's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Basil Hayden's Toast on the steak course instead.",
  "Basil Hayden's Toast|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Basil Hayden's Toast's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth leans against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the caramel-spice register matches the curry, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; cleaner than wheated versions but not exceptional.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Asparagus": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the bourbon weight handles the asparagus, and the oak-and-spice register settles the side. Works; the bonded richness gives the dessert more than lighter pours do.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Basil Hayden's with au gratin potatoes — light high-rye against cheese-and-cream depth. Strong; the rye pepper threads through the richness differently than wheated does.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Beignets": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon weight handles the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; EC 18 frames the two-cut plate at aged-HH register.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Bone Marrow": "Basil Hayden's with bone marrow — rye spice against umami fat. Capable, but the 80-proof light body can't quite match the marrow's intensity. Reach for Weller 12 or Maker's Mark Cellar Aged for more alignment; Basil Hayden's is the lighter alternate. Strong; the pairing reads at register.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Bone-In Filet": "Basil Hayden's crisp high-rye-pepper character frames the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the bourbon depth carries the cut. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Broccoli Cheddar": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the bourbon depth settles into the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the blend's complexity is underused by the salad.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Broccolini": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the broccolini's tender green stalks: the oak depth lays under the broccolini, and the oak frames the side. Works; boutique over-specified.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Brussels and Belly": "Basil Hayden's with Brussels + Belly — rye spice meets maple-glazed pork belly sweetness. The 80-proof lightness doesn't compete with the small plate; it balances the dish's richness with pepper and brightness. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Burrata": "Basil Hayden's with burrata — fresh dairy against rye spice. Avoid; even 80-proof light-bodied bourbon is too much for the burrata's register.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Butternut Squash": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the caramel-spice register matches the squash bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the bourbon-and-side match sits without pulling focus.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Carrot Cake": "Basil Hayden's with carrot cake — rye spice against cream cheese frosting and cinnamon. The spice in the pour picks up the cake's warmth; a distinct dessert pairing from the wheated takes — less sweet-on-sweet, more spice-on-spice. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Cheesecake": "Basil Hayden's with cheesecake — rye spice against clean custard. Works; the pour's brightness is a gentle counterpoint to the dessert's richness.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Chilean Seabass": "Basil Hayden's light high-rye and cocoa swallows the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Basil Hayden's lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Chocolate Brownie": "Basil Hayden's with the chocolate brownie — light high-rye and cocoa. Works; Basil Hayden's Toast is the family member that actually lifts this dessert (toast-barrel caramel + cocoa). Standard Basil Hayden's is neutral here.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Chocolate Cake": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the oak depth lays under the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the story is wasted on the salad.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Clam Chowder": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chowder, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; premium proof overpowers this dish.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Cowboy Ribeye": "Basil Hayden's with the Cowboy Ribeye — the 80-proof gateway high-rye against the ribeye's cap fat. Underpowered for the cut's weight; capable but Weller 12 or Eagle Rare 10 Year are the premium alternates for this cut. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Crab Cake": "Basil Hayden's with crab cake — even light high-rye overshoots crab delicacy. Avoid; the pour's spice doesn't find the crab's sweetness. Reach for a white wine or a gin.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Creamed Spinach": "Basil Hayden's with creamed spinach — rye spice against dairy richness. Cleaner and brighter than the Wellers' caramel-wheat take on this side; the 80-proof delicacy lets the cream lead. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Creamy Potato": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the bourbon body sits with the potato soup, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; JW Blue is over-specified for the side — save the rare-cask bottle for the protein course.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Creme Brulee": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the bourbon backbone carries the brulee, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; flagship depth gives the dessert premium aged character.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Escargot": "Basil Hayden's crisp high-rye-pepper character finds register with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Faroe Island Salmon": "Basil Hayden's light high-rye and cocoa swallows the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Basil Hayden's belongs on the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Filet Mignon": "Basil Hayden's with the filet — the 80-proof gateway high-rye. Light body and rye-pepper brightness give the filet a pairing that lets the cut lead. Distinct from the wheated Wellers and Maker's — more spice, less caramel softness. The light-rye call for filet. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Basil Hayden's|French Onion": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the bourbon backbone carries the French onion, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; master-blender doesn't drive.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Grilled Caesar": "Basil Hayden's with the grilled Caesar — rye pepper meets charred romaine and anchovy. Works; the light body lets the Caesar lead, distinct from the Wellers' wheated-and-heavy take.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Gumbo": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the oak depth lays under the gumbo, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; the smooth character gives the dessert a composed frame.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the brown-spirit warmth threads the honey carrots, and the oak balances the burnt-sugar edge. Works; complex profile overshoots the dessert's delicacy.",
  "Basil Hayden's|House Wedge": "Basil Hayden's with the House Wedge — light-bodied rye against iceberg and bleu. Works; the 80-proof softness doesn't overshoot the salad the way heavier bourbons do.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Kansas City": "Basil Hayden's with the KC — the strip's marbling pushes slightly past Basil Hayden's 80-proof light register. Capable; the rye spice gives the strip a different dimension than the Wellers, but the pour doesn't carry the cut's full weight. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Loaded Potato": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the bourbon depth settles into the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Lobster Mac": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon body sits with the lobster mac, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; IW Harper 15 handles dessert density at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Market Fish": "Basil Hayden's light high-rye and cocoa smothers the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Basil Hayden's for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Mocha Creme": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the oak depth lays under the mocha creme, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; craft-blender complexity over-specified.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Mushroom Bisque": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the bourbon backbone carries the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; boutique-blend depth gives composed dessert character.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Mushrooms": "Basil Hayden's with the mushrooms — light-bodied high-rye against earthy umami. The rye spice threads through the mushroom's depth; distinct from wheated takes, with less sweetness and more brightness. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the PB brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; single-barrel depth gives the dessert more than Small Batch.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Porterhouse": "Basil Hayden's with the porterhouse — the filet side takes the light high-rye beautifully; the strip side is a touch underpowered. Lighter than the Wellers here; a distinct alternate for the porterhouse but not the strongest call. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Prime Tartare": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami: the oak depth lays under the tartare, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; smooth character covers both cuts cleanly; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Rainbow Trout": "Basil Hayden's light high-rye and cocoa swallows the trout's delicate flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Basil Hayden's for the steak course.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Roast Half Chicken": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the brown-spirit warmth threads the roast chicken, and the caramel rounds the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the bourbon weight handles the chickpea soup, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; gentle match.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Basil Hayden's light high-rye and cocoa overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Basil Hayden's lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the brown-spirit warmth threads the garlic spinach, and the oak-and-spice register settles the side. Works; premium KO story wasted on salad.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Seafood Tower": "Basil Hayden's light high-rye and cocoa smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Basil Hayden's on the steak course instead.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Seared Scallops": "Basil Hayden's with seared scallops — scallop caramelized sweetness against rye pepper. Avoid; the register mismatch is structural.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Seasonal Soup": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the bourbon weight handles the seasonal soup, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; a gentle composed match.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Seasonal Vegetables": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the oak depth lays under the seasonal vegetables, and the oak frames the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Shrimp Bisque": "Basil Hayden's with shrimp bisque — light high-rye against cream-based seafood. Works; the pour's delicacy doesn't overpower the soup, but doesn't particularly elevate it either.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Shrimp Cocktail": "Basil Hayden's with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against high-rye. Avoid; separate courses.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Swordfish": "Basil Hayden's light high-rye and cocoa swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Basil Hayden's lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Basil Hayden's|The Tomahawk": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the Tomahawk's theatrical bone-in marbling and smoky char: the brown-spirit warmth threads the 36oz showpiece, and the vanilla balances the char-and-fat. Strong; regional character covers both cuts.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Tomato Basil": "Basil Hayden's' light high-rye and cocoa leans against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the bourbon depth settles into the tomato basil, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; richer profile overshoots the dessert's delicacy.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Truffle Fries": "Basil Hayden's with truffle fries — rye pepper against truffle-parmesan fat. The 80-proof delicacy lets the truffle lead; the spice notes give the side a lift the Wellers' wheated sweetness can't. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Basil Hayden's light high-rye and cocoa flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Basil Hayden's lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Basil Hayden's|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the brown-spirit warmth threads the curry, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; mid-proof pour is slightly over-specified.",
  "Bee's Knees|Asparagus": "Empress Indigo gin, lemon, honey lavender syrup — three ingredients, no filler. The honey-lavender plays against asparagus's vegetal char and the lemon cuts the sulfur edge. Works as gin cocktail for asparagus — floral-and-bright route; wines peak higher on the wine-tricky vegetable.",
  "Bee's Knees|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build plays cleanly against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the honey threads the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Bee's Knees|Beignets": "Bee's Knees' citrus-and-bright cocktail lift clashes with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- light cocktail citrus is wrong direction for the dessert's richness. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a light cocktail. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Bee's Knees for the steak course.",
  "Bee's Knees|Bone Marrow": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build plays cleanly against the marrow's umami-fat depth — the cocktail lift refreshes the starter, and the honey threads the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Bee's Knees|Bone-In Filet": "Bee's Knees' citrus-and-bright cocktail lift underclubs the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- light cocktail lands short of any prime cut. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a light cocktail. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Bee's Knees for another course.",
  "Bee's Knees|Broccoli Cheddar": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build stays alongside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the honey threads the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Bee's Knees|Broccolini": "Empress Indigo gin, lemon, honey lavender syrup — three ingredients, no filler. The honey plays against broccolini's vegetal char and the lemon cuts the tender-stem weight. Works as gin cocktail for broccolini — simple-and-floral route; wines peak higher as dedicated pairings.",
  "Bee's Knees|Brussels and Belly": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the honey rounds the grilled char. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Bee's Knees|Burrata": "Empress Indigo gin with lemon and honey lavender syrup. The honey works seasonally with whatever fruit the kitchen has on the plate; the Indigo's butterfly-pea color-shift is a detail to mention alongside a vegetarian starter. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Bee's Knees|Butternut Squash": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build leans against the squash soup's silky sweet — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the honey threads the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Bee's Knees|Carrot Cake": "Bee's Knees' citrus-and-bright cocktail lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- light cocktail citrus is wrong direction for the dessert's richness. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a light cocktail. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Bee's Knees lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Bee's Knees|Cheesecake": "Bee's Knees' citrus-and-bright cocktail lift clashes with the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- light cocktail citrus is wrong direction for the dessert's richness. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not a light cocktail. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Bee's Knees for the steak course.",
  "Bee's Knees|Chilean Seabass": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build reads alongside the seabass's buttery flesh — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Bee's Knees|Chocolate Brownie": "Bee's Knees' citrus-and-bright cocktail lift clashes with the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- light cocktail citrus is wrong direction for the dessert's richness. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not a light cocktail. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Bee's Knees on the steak course instead.",
  "Bee's Knees|Chocolate Cake": "Bee's Knees' citrus-and-bright cocktail lift clashes with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- light cocktail citrus is wrong direction for the dessert's richness. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not a light cocktail. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Bee's Knees for the steak course.",
  "Bee's Knees|Clam Chowder": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build sits beside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the honey threads the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Bee's Knees|Cowboy Ribeye": "Empress Indigo gin, lemon, honey lavender syrup. Delicate floral-citrus cocktail crushed by Cowboy's marbled rendered-fat profile. Never pair — the Bee's Knees belongs with the raw bar or opener course, not with the fattiest steak on the menu.",
  "Bee's Knees|Crab Cake": "Empress Indigo gin (butterfly-pea blue-grey), lemon, honey lavender syrup. The honey softens the lemon's bite and meets crab's sweet meat directly; lavender adds floral complexity to the romesco. Peak opener cocktail for crab cake — lightness with visual interest in the glass.",
  "Bee's Knees|Creamed Spinach": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build plays cleanly against the spinach's dairy-rich cream — the cocktail lift sits with the light side, and the honey threads the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Bee's Knees|Creamy Potato": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build plays cleanly against the potato soup's silky body — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the honey threads the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Bee's Knees|Creme Brulee": "Bee's Knees' citrus-and-bright cocktail lift clashes with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- light cocktail citrus is wrong direction for the dessert's richness. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not a light cocktail. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Bee's Knees for the steak course.",
  "Bee's Knees|Escargot": "Empress Indigo gin with lemon and honey lavender syrup. The honey pairs subtly with our escargot's absinthe-finish anise note; the lemon cuts the butter weight. Three ingredients, zero filler — matches the escargot's clean flavor structure. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Bee's Knees|Faroe Island Salmon": "Empress Indigo gin with lemon and honey lavender syrup. Honey sweetness and lemon against Faroe salmon's rich fat works when the prep leans lighter. The Indigo color-shift is a talking point; ask the kitchen first. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Bee's Knees|Filet Mignon": "Empress Indigo gin, lemon, honey lavender syrup. The cocktail's delicate three-ingredient build has no structural match for grilled beef. Works only if guest stays on the cocktail through the entrée; route filet pairing to Cab, Pinot, or Manhattan.",
  "Bee's Knees|French Onion": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build stays alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the cocktail lift refreshes against the hearty soup, and the rounded sweetness threads the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Bee's Knees|Grilled Caesar": "Empress Indigo gin, lemon, honey lavender syrup. The honey's sweetness balances anchovy-parmesan dressing and the lemon cuts the dressing's salinity; lavender plays against grilled-romaine char. Strong unconventional pairing — cocktail's simplicity handles the salad's layered flavors.",
  "Bee's Knees|Gumbo": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build leans against the gumbo's spiced Creole stew — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the honey balances the spice. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Bee's Knees|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build leans against the carrots' honeyed sweetness — the cocktail lift sits with the light side, and the rounded sweetness softens the green edge. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Bee's Knees|House Wedge": "Empress Indigo gin, lemon, honey lavender syrup. The lemon cuts iceberg-and-bacon crunch and honey-lavender plays against blue cheese's funk; the blue-grey hue adds visual interest. Strong opener cocktail — keeps palate fresh for the steak course ahead.",
  "Bee's Knees|Kansas City": "Bee's Knees' citrus-and-bright cocktail lift underclubs the KC's lean-bold strip with savory grain -- cocktail citrus reads thin against the cut's structure. The plate deserves Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, Pio Cesare Barbaresco, or Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye, not a light cocktail. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Bee's Knees for another course.",
  "Bee's Knees|Loaded Potato": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build stays alongside the loaded potato's richness — the cocktail lift refreshes against the hearty soup, and the honey threads the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Bee's Knees|Lobster Mac": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the honey threads the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Bee's Knees|Market Fish": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build reads alongside the fish's clean flesh — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Bee's Knees|Mocha Creme": "Bee's Knees' citrus-and-bright cocktail lift clashes with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- light cocktail citrus is wrong direction for the dessert's richness. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not a light cocktail. Avoid; one of those is the move. Bee's Knees lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Bee's Knees|Mushroom Bisque": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build finds neutral with the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the cocktail lift refreshes against the hearty soup, and the honey threads the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Bee's Knees|Mushrooms": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build reads alongside the mushrooms' earthy umami — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Bee's Knees|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Bee's Knees' citrus-and-bright cocktail lift clashes with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- light cocktail citrus is wrong direction for the dessert's richness. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not a light cocktail. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Save the Bee's Knees for the steak course.",
  "Bee's Knees|Porterhouse": "Bee's Knees' citrus-and-bright cocktail lift underclubs the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character -- a light citrus cocktail can't carry the marbled char — needs whiskey or red wine weight. The plate deserves Odette Cabernet Sauvignon, Weller 12 Year, or Domaine du Grand Tinel, not a light cocktail. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Bee's Knees for another course.",
  "Bee's Knees|Prime Tartare": "Empress Indigo gin, lemon, honey lavender syrup. The cocktail's citrus-and-honey cuts raw prime beef's iron richness and lavender adds aromatic complexity. Strong pre-dinner pairing — the Empress's color adds visual drama alongside the hand-cut beef presentation.",
  "Bee's Knees|Rainbow Trout": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build reads alongside the trout's delicate flesh — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; the match carries without overshooting.",
  "Bee's Knees|Roast Half Chicken": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build stays alongside the chicken's herbed crisp skin — the cocktail lift carries the herb-crisped bird, and the honey rounds the grilled char. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Bee's Knees|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build sits alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper warmth — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the honey balances the spice. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Bee's Knees|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Bee's Knees' citrus-and-bright cocktail lift sits alongside the halibut's salt-cured flesh: the bright build frames the halibut, and the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Bee's Knees|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Empress Indigo gin with lemon and honey lavender syrup. The honey softness against the escargot butter's garlic-shallot depth; clean cocktail for the lightest shareable. The Indigo color-change is a talking point. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Bee's Knees|Seafood Tower": "Empress Indigo gin with lemon and honey lavender syrup. Honey sweetness against brine works; the Indigo's butterfly-pea color-change adds visual interest next to the tower. Cocktail route for guests who don't want sparkling. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Bee's Knees|Seared Scallops": "Empress Indigo gin, lemon, honey lavender syrup. The three-ingredient purity meets scallops' clean-seared simplicity; honey aligns with the scallops' natural sweetness and lavender adds aromatic depth. Peak minimalist pairing for the cleanest seafood on the menu.",
  "Bee's Knees|Seasonal Soup": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build leans against the seasonal soup's house build — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Bee's Knees|Seasonal Vegetables": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build leans against the seasonal garden plate — the cocktail lift sits with the light side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Bee's Knees|Shrimp Bisque": "Empress Indigo gin, lemon, honey lavender syrup. The honey softens against cream-shellfish soup and lemon brightens shrimp sweetness; lavender adds aromatic complexity. Works as a light starter pairing — though Sauv Blanc and Champagne peak higher for bisque.",
  "Bee's Knees|Shrimp Cocktail": "Empress Indigo gin with lemon and honey lavender syrup. Honey against brine works and the Indigo's color-change is a conversation starter. Not the peak — the sparkling options do more — but a valid cocktail-route choice. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Bee's Knees|Swordfish": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build sits with the swordfish's meaty flesh — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Bee's Knees|The Tomahawk": "Light three-ingredient gin cocktail against the biggest steak on the menu — complete mismatch. The Bee's Knees has no weight to handle marbled tomahawk fat. Never pair — route Tomahawk to heavy Cabs, Barolo, or spirit-forward bourbon cocktails.",
  "Bee's Knees|Tomato Basil": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build leans against the tomato basil's bright acid — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus lifts the herbs. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Bee's Knees|Truffle Fries": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build plays cleanly against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Bee's Knees|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build sits with the tuna's seared rare crust — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the honey rounds the grilled char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Bee's Knees|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build plays cleanly against the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the honey balances the spice. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Asparagus": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals sits beside the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the botanicals echo the green plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals stays alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals cut the cheese richness. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Beignets": "Beefeater with beignets — 40% London Dry against fried dough. Works; juniper-sugar contrast at approachable register.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Bone Marrow": "Beefeater with bone marrow — balanced gin against umami fat. Avoid; gin can't cut marrow. Reach for Fernet Branca.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Bone-In Filet": "Beefeater Gin's botanical-driven lift underclubs the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- gin reads light against the prime cut's weight — needs a red or whiskey. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a gin. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Beefeater Gin on another course instead.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Broccoli Cheddar": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals stays alongside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Broccolini": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals sits beside the broccolini's tender green — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the botanicals echo the green plate. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Brussels and Belly": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals leans against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals echo the green plate. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Burrata": "Beefeater with burrata — 40% balanced London Dry against fresh dairy. Excellent; Beefeater threads the cream cleanly without Tanq's intensity or Plymouth's sweetness.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Butternut Squash": "Beefeater Gin's herbal-botanical edge reads alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the floral edge frames the squash bisque, and the juniper threads the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Carrot Cake": "Beefeater Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Beefeater Gin for the steak course.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Cheesecake": "Beefeater Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not a gin. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Beefeater Gin on the steak course instead.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Chilean Seabass": "Beefeater Gin's herbal-botanical edge leans against the seabass' buttery seabass flesh: the floral edge frames the seabass, and the juniper threads the plate. Strong; Beefeater's balance meets the char cleanly.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Chocolate Brownie": "Beefeater Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- gin botanicals jar against the chocolate's sweetness with no bridge. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not a gin. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Beefeater Gin for the steak course.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Chocolate Cake": "Beefeater Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- gin botanicals jar against the chocolate's sweetness with no bridge. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not a gin. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Beefeater Gin for the steak course.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Clam Chowder": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals sits beside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the juniper carries the shellfish. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Cowboy Ribeye": "Beefeater Gin's botanical-driven lift falls short of the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness -- botanical-citrus can't stand up to 26+ ounces — a Cab or bourbon earns it. The plate deserves Macallan 18, Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon, or Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon, not a gin. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Beefeater Gin for another course.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Crab Cake": "Beefeater with crab cake — 40% London Dry, 9 botanicals, 24-hour steep. Excellent; Beefeater's balanced juniper-citrus is the democratic workhorse for crab — where Tanq lifts with proof and Plymouth softens, Beefeater just works reliably at approachable register.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Creamed Spinach": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals sits alongside the spinach's dairy-rich cream — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the botanicals echo the green plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Creamy Potato": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals leans against the potato soup's silky body — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals cut the cheese richness. Works; capable alongside. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Creme Brulee": "Beefeater Gin's botanical-driven lift jars against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- sharp botanicals cut through dairy custard without resolving — the dessert reads broken. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not a gin. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Beefeater Gin for the steak course.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Escargot": "Beefeater with escargot — 9-botanical London Dry against garlic-butter snails. Excellent; the 24-hour botanical steep gives Beefeater enough depth to match the butter while staying democratic.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Faroe Island Salmon": "Beefeater with the salmon — 9-botanical London Dry against oily salmon. Strong; Beefeater's balance frames the fish at approachable register.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Filet Mignon": "Beefeater with the filet — 40% London Dry against tenderloin. Works; gin over-specified; Beefeater's balance is a functional match when guests insist.",
  "Beefeater Gin|French Onion": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals sits beside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals cut the cheese richness. Works; the pairing reads neutral at the table. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Grilled Caesar": "Beefeater with the grilled Caesar — classic 40% against charred romaine and anchovy. Strong; Beefeater's balance meets the char cleanly.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Gumbo": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals stays alongside the gumbo's spiced Creole stew — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals plays cleanly against the carrots' honeyed sweetness — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the botanicals echo the green plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Beefeater Gin|House Wedge": "Beefeater with the House Wedge — classic 40% London Dry against iceberg and bleu. Strong; Beefeater's balance is a democratic wedge pairing — neither too sharp nor too sweet.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Kansas City": "Beefeater Gin's botanical-driven lift mis-pairs with the KC's lean-bold strip with savory grain -- gin's clean lift reads thin against the cut's weight. The plate deserves Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, Pio Cesare Barbaresco, or Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye, not a gin. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Beefeater Gin for another course.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Loaded Potato": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals stays alongside the loaded potato's richness — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals cut the cheese richness. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Lobster Mac": "Beefeater Gin's botanical-driven lift leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the botanical-citrus register matches the lobster mac, and the coriander-and-cardamom edge frames the side. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Market Fish": "Beefeater with the market fish — classic London Dry against featured fish. Works; Beefeater handles most fish preparations reliably.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Mocha Creme": "Beefeater Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- gin botanicals jar against the chocolate's sweetness with no bridge. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not a gin. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Beefeater Gin lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Mushroom Bisque": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals stays alongside the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Mushrooms": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals reads alongside the mushrooms' earthy umami — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Beefeater Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Beefeater Gin belongs on the steak course.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Porterhouse": "Beefeater Gin's botanical-driven lift falls short of the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character -- botanical-citrus can't stand up to 26+ ounces — a Cab or bourbon earns it. The plate deserves Odette Cabernet Sauvignon, Weller 12 Year, or Domaine du Grand Tinel, not a gin. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Beefeater Gin for another course.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Prime Tartare": "Beefeater with the tartare — 40% balanced London Dry against raw beef. Strong; Beefeater's balance supports tartare, though Bombay Dry's juniper-assertiveness is the featured gin-tartare match.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Rainbow Trout": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals finds register with the trout's delicate flesh — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the botanicals lift the savory weight. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Roast Half Chicken": "Beefeater with the chicken — 9-botanical against roasted poultry. Works; Beefeater's balance supports chicken cleanly.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals plays cleanly against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper warmth — the gin botanicals sit with the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals lifts the halibut's salt-cured flesh — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the botanicals lift the savory weight. Strong; the match carries without overshooting.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals leans against the garlic-spinach's buttered greens — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the botanicals echo the green plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Seafood Tower": "Beefeater with the seafood tower — classic London Dry against the raw bar. Excellent; Beefeater is the approachable tower-gin pairing when Tanq feels too heavy and Plymouth too soft.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Seared Scallops": "Beefeater with seared scallops — 24-hour-steeped London Dry against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Beefeater's balance of juniper and citrus frames scallops at accessible register — where Tanq overpowers slightly and Plymouth softens.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Seasonal Soup": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals sits beside the seasonal soup's house build — the gin botanicals sit with the plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Seasonal Vegetables": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals leans against the seasonal garden plate — the botanical edge sits with the light side. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Shrimp Bisque": "Beefeater with shrimp bisque — balanced London Dry against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Beefeater cuts the bisque without Tanq's aggression.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Shrimp Cocktail": "Beefeater with shrimp cocktail — classic 40% London Dry against cold shrimp. Excellent; Beefeater's balance is the textbook gin-shrimp pairing — the English institution delivering on expectation.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Swordfish": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals reads alongside the swordfish's meaty flesh — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the botanicals lift the savory weight. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Beefeater Gin|The Tomahawk": "Beefeater with the Tomahawk — 40% against 32oz bone-in. Avoid; gin has no answer for cap-fat intensity. Reach for a bourbon or cab.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Tomato Basil": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals leans against the tomato basil's bright acid — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals lift the savory weight. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Truffle Fries": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals sits alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals lifts the tuna's seared rare crust — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the juniper sharpens the char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Beefeater Gin|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals stays alongside the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the gin botanicals sit with the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Beignets|1792 Small Batch": "1792 Small Batch's caramel-spice character finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the brown-spirit warmth threads the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Parker's Heritage 16th handles the richness at annual-release register.",
  "Beignets|1792 Sweet Wheat": "1792 Sweet Wheat's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon backbone carries the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Vermont-brand character doesn't drive.",
  "Beignets|1881 Napa Valley": "1881 Napa Valley's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the 1881 Napa Valley on the steak course instead.",
  "Beignets|2 James Gin": "2 James with beignets — Michigan craft gin against fried dough. Works; juniper-sugar contrast at local-craft register.",
  "Beignets|A Midnight's Winter Dram": "A Midnight's Winter Dram's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the malt-driven body wraps the beignets, and the smoke threads the dessert. Works; boutique-blend depth gives composed dessert character.",
  "Beignets|Aberlour 16": "Aberlour 16's double-matured Speyside balance leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon-plus-sherry depth wraps the beignets, and the balanced sweetness frames the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Beignets|Adictivo Cristalino": "Adictivo Cristalino's aged-agave character clashes with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- aged tequila has nothing to bridge into dessert. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Adictivo Cristalino lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Beignets|Adictivo Reposado": "Adictivo Reposado's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the oak-aged tequila body threads the beignets, and the oak threads the dessert. Works; aged-but-clear character composes with the dish.",
  "Beignets|Alexander Valley Chardonnay": "Alexander Valley Chardonnay's crisp white-wine character clashes with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- a dry white belongs with the main course, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a white wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Alexander Valley Chardonnay lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Beignets|Alexander Valley Cyrus": "Alexander Valley Cyrus' red-fruit-and-spice elegance jars against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Alexander Valley Cyrus belongs on the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Alexander Valley Homestead Red": "Alexander Valley Homestead Red's red-fruit-and-spice elegance fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- tannin can't pivot to warm pastry sugar — the pour reads dry, the dessert reads heavy. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Alexander Valley Homestead Red for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Amaro Nonino": "Amaro Nonino with beignets — Friulian amaro against fried dough and powdered sugar. Works; the botanical complexity adds refinement to the casual dessert.",
  "Beignets|Ancho Reyes": "Beignets: sugar-dusted pastry meets Ancho Reyes. Excellent; smoky-sweet-chile plays with sugar-dust at Mexican register.",
  "Beignets|Angel's Envy": "Angel's Envy's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the caramel-spice register matches the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; stout-barrel story wasted on salad.",
  "Beignets|Angel's Envy Cask Strength": "Angel's Envy Cask Strength's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; AE Triple Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Beignets|Angel's Envy Triple Cask": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the caramel-spice register matches the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; multi-distillery complexity doesn't drive.",
  "Beignets|Aperol": "Aperol with beignets — soft aperitivo against fried dough. Works; Aperol's gentle character doesn't overwhelm the casual sweet but doesn't feature.",
  "Beignets|Asparagus": "The asparagus and the beignets -- the asparagus' green-vegetal edge hands off cleanly to the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bright register lifts the sweet, the meal closes clean. Works; sequence them or share the table, no clash.",
  "Beignets|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Au Gratin Potatoes and the beignets -- the cream rounds into the sweet close, the meal lands rich and full. Works; the meal closes cleanly from the side.",
  "Beignets|Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon": "Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- tannin can't pivot to warm pastry sugar — the pour reads dry, the dessert reads heavy. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Beignets|Averna Amaro": "Beignets: fried dough and powdered sugar meet Sicilian amaro. Works; caramel-orange classic-amaro character pairs with sugar-coated beignets.",
  "Beignets|Aviation": "Aviation's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift clashes with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- light cocktail citrus is wrong direction for the dessert's richness. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a light cocktail. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Aviation for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Aviation Gin": "Aviation with beignets — smooth American craft gin against fried dough. Excellent; Aviation's soft lavender-cardamom is the crowd-pleasing craft-gin-beignets pairing — Empress 1908's rose notes edge it on distinctiveness.",
  "Beignets|Avion 44": "Avion 44's añejo-pour depth leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the rested-agave depth sits with the beignets, and the soft-spice note softens the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Beignets|Avion Silver": "Avion Silver's unaged blanco-tequila lift with agave-citrus snap falls short of the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- light spirit reads thin against dessert sweetness. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a light spirit. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Avion Silver on the steak course instead.",
  "Beignets|Bacardi Rum": "Bacardi Rum's crisp workhorse-clean character sits with the beignet's warm sugar-dusted pastry — the crisp body underclubs the dessert. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Beignets|Baileys Irish Cream": "Baileys Irish Cream's after-dinner liqueur weight leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the digestif body mirrors the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Beignets|Baker's": "Baker's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon body sits with the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Voyage 23 frames the cut at ocean-finish register.",
  "Beignets|Balvenie 12 American Oak": "Balvenie 12 American Oak's bourbon-cask Speyside softness sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the beignets, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the dessert. Works; craft-blend over-specified.",
  "Beignets|Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask": "Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask's rum-finished Speyside character finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the malt-driven body wraps the beignets, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the dessert. Works; the match is gentle and approachable.",
  "Beignets|Balvenie 16 Single Barrel": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the malt-and-oak threads the beignets, and the malt edge frames the dessert. Works; rare-release wasted on salad.",
  "Beignets|Balvenie 21 Portwood": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the Highland register carries the beignets, and the oak-and-smoke underlines the dessert. Works; save the BTAC bottle for the protein course — the side doesn't deserve the pour.",
  "Beignets|Bardstown Château Laboude": "Bardstown Château Laboude's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon weight handles the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; bonded weight a touch ambitious for the dessert.",
  "Beignets|Bardstown Discovery #6": "Bardstown Discovery #6's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the caramel-spice register matches the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; pour is a touch over-specified for the dessert.",
  "Beignets|Bardstown Founders KBS": "Bardstown Founders KBS's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon weight handles the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; richer profile is slightly over-specified for the dessert.",
  "Beignets|Bardstown Foursquare": "Bardstown Foursquare's rum-cask + cocoa is textbook — tropical-rum + chocolate leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon depth settles into the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Old World complexity wasted on salad simplicity.",
  "Beignets|Bardstown Fusion #7": "Bardstown Fusion #7's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Beignets|Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel": "Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon depth settles into the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Beignets|Basil Hayden's": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon weight handles the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; EC 18 frames the two-cut plate at aged-HH register.",
  "Beignets|Basil Hayden's 10 Year": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the brown-spirit warmth threads the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the single-barrel depth is slightly over-specified for the dessert.",
  "Beignets|Basil Hayden's Malted Rye": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the rye backbone drives the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Remus 15 handles dessert density at Gatsby-tribute register.",
  "Beignets|Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon backbone carries the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; high proof over-specified.",
  "Beignets|Basil Hayden's Toast": "Basil Hayden's Toast's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon depth settles into the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; regional craft at matched register.",
  "Beignets|Bee's Knees": "Bee's Knees' citrus-and-bright cocktail lift clashes with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- light cocktail citrus is wrong direction for the dessert's richness. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a light cocktail. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Bee's Knees for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Beefeater Gin": "Beefeater with beignets — 40% London Dry against fried dough. Works; juniper-sugar contrast at approachable register.",
  "Beignets|Belvedere Vodka": "Belvedere Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a vodka. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Belvedere Vodka on the steak course instead.",
  "Beignets|Blade & Bow": "Blade & Bow's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the brown-spirit warmth threads the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Beignets|Blanton's Gold": "Blanton's Gold's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the brown-spirit warmth threads the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; IW Harper 15 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Beignets|Blanton's Original": "Blanton's Original's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon body sits with the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; AE Triple Cask meets the char at distinctive register.",
  "Beignets|Blanton's Straight from the Barrel": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the oak depth lays under the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Old Fitz 9 brings more depth here.",
  "Beignets|Blood Oath Pact 10": "Blood Oath Pact 10's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon body sits with the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the toast notes don't really interplay with the soup but don't clash.",
  "Beignets|Blood Oath Pact 8": "Blood Oath Pact 8's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the brown-spirit warmth threads the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; JW Blue is over-specified for a side — save the bottle for the main course.",
  "Beignets|Blood Oath Pact 9": "Blood Oath Pact 9's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the caramel-spice register matches the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; premium single-barrel wasted on the salad.",
  "Beignets|Bluecoat Gin": "Bluecoat with beignets — Philadelphia 4-citrus craft against fried dough. Works; Bluecoat's citrus is a functional finisher; Empress 1908's rose is more distinctive.",
  "Beignets|Bodega Noemia A Lisa": "Bodega Noemia A Lisa's plush Malbec with plum-and-violet weight jars against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Bodega Noemia A Lisa on the steak course instead.",
  "Beignets|Bombay Dry Gin": "Bombay Dry with beignets — angular London Dry against fried dough. Works; the juniper-sugar contrast is sharper than Beefeater's approach.",
  "Beignets|Bombay Sapphire Gin": "Bombay Sapphire with beignets — vapor-infused floral gin against fried dough. Works; Sapphire's softer character makes the juniper-sugar pairing more accessible than Bombay Dry's angular version.",
  "Beignets|Bone Marrow": "The bone marrow alongside the beignets -- the savory course resolves into sugar, the meal closes with contrast. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Beignets|Bone-In Filet": "After the bone-in filet, the beignets -- the elevated cut hands off to warm choux and powdered sugar, the dipping sauce easing the close. Works; the meal closes light after the marrow-edged main.",
  "Beignets|Booker's": "Booker's' cask-strength bourbon depth finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; IW Harper 15 frames the two-cut plate at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Beignets|Botanist Gin": "Botanist with beignets — Bruichladdich Islay craft gin against fried dough. Works; the foraged-herbal profile is over-specified for casual dessert.",
  "Beignets|Bowdie's Old Fashioned": "Buffalo Trace, rum-soaked cherries, orange, Angostura. Bourbon weight overwhelms the beignet's airy choux interior; the cocktail belongs with marrow or Tomahawk. Route beignet guest to Champagne, Moscato, Prosecco, or an Espresso Martini. Avoid; the pairing fights at the table — point the guest elsewhere.",
  "Beignets|Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark": "Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon weight handles the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Beignets|Bowman Brothers Small Batch": "Bowman Brothers Small Batch's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the Millennium's register overshoots the dessert's.",
  "Beignets|Bowmore 12": "Bowmore 12's lighter-Islay peat character finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the malt-driven body wraps the beignets, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the dessert. Works; complex profile overshoots the dessert's delicacy.",
  "Beignets|Braida Montebruna Barbera": "Braida Montebruna Barbera's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- tannin can't pivot to warm pastry sugar — the pour reads dry, the dessert reads heavy. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Braida Montebruna Barbera lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Beignets|Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- tannin can't pivot to warm pastry sugar — the pour reads dry, the dessert reads heavy. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Broccoli Cheddar": "Broccoli Cheddar and the beignets -- rich dairy yields to dessert weight, the close composes thickly. Works; either timing holds, the table builds either way.",
  "Beignets|Broccolini": "Broccolini and the beignets -- acid and sugar share the table, neither course pulls heavy. Works; clean transition or together if the table wants.",
  "Beignets|Bruichladdich": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the beignets, and the smoke threads the dessert. Works; EC 18 frames the two-cut plate at aged-HH register.",
  "Beignets|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly and the beignets -- savory-into-sweet, the classic close lands intact. Works; the meal closes cleanly from the side.",
  "Beignets|Buffalo Trace": "Buffalo Trace's rounded vanilla-and-toffee character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the brown-spirit warmth threads the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Beignets|Buffalo Trace Cream": "Buffalo Trace Cream's sweet bourbon-cream-caramel character holds steady against the beignet's warm sugar-dusted pastry — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar, and the caramel deepens the dessert sugar. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Beignets|Bulleit Bourbon": "Bulleit Bourbon's high-rye spice-forward depth finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon weight handles the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Fortuna's NZ terroir meets the glaze at distinctive register.",
  "Beignets|Burrata": "Burrata and the beignets -- the delicate course resolves into the close, the meal stays unburdened. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Beignets|Butternut Squash": "The butternut squash alongside the beignets -- both desserts pull the same lever, the table doubles the sugar. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Beignets|Cade Cabernet Sauvignon": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- tannin can't pivot to warm pastry sugar — the pour reads dry, the dessert reads heavy. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Camarena Tequila": "Camarena Tequila's rested-agave body finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the aged-agave weight wraps the beignets, and the oak threads the dessert. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Beignets|Campari": "Campari with beignets — ruby bitter against fried dough. Works; aperitivo bitterness cuts the sugar but Campari is over-specified for casual dessert.",
  "Beignets|Canadian Club": "Canadian Club's workhorse Canadian blend reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the easygoing Canadian character handles the beignets, and the easy Canadian register softens the dessert. Works; the aging is wasted on the salad.",
  "Beignets|Canadian Club 43 Year": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the Canadian whisky weight matches the beignets, and the soft profile rounds the dessert. Works; the extra proof overpowers this dish.",
  "Beignets|Captain Morgan Rum": "Captain Morgan Rum: Diageo's iconic Original Spiced rum, Caribbean-origin blend with warm-spice profile — vanilla, cinnamon, clove, molasses. Excellent on beignets; the warm-spice character plays directly into the fresh sugar-dust and pastry warmth at cocktail-workhorse register — spice meets sugar textbook.",
  "Beignets|Caribou Crossing": "Caribou Crossing's Canadian whisky character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the Canadian whisky weight matches the beignets, and the soft profile rounds the dessert. Works; boutique character doesn't drive.",
  "Beignets|Carrot Cake": "The beignets alongside the carrot cake -- the powdered-sugar beignets reads beside the spiced carrot close, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the dessert split holds at neutral register.",
  "Beignets|Casa LBV Port": "Late Bottled Vintage Port — Casa LBV, 4-6 year cask, dark cherry, plum, smooth moderate structure. The smooth structure clings to hot choux-fried dough and the plum lifts powdered-sugar simplicity. Strong LBV for beignets — Graham's 10 Year's toffee fits airy choux cleaner.",
  "Beignets|Casamigos Mezcal": "Casamigos Mezcal's earthen-pit smoke profile finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the espadín-and-smoke body wraps the beignets, and the campfire register frames the dessert. Works; the courses share the table without crowding.",
  "Beignets|Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon": "Caymus — cocoa, mocha, velvety tannins. Cab tannin against a light choux beignet is catastrophically wrong; the wine obliterates the dessert's delicacy. Save Caymus for the steak course; route beignet pairing to Champagne, Moscato, or Prosecco. Avoid; pair this elsewhere on the menu.",
  "Beignets|Chambord": "Chambord: this sweet cream liqueur's dessert-adjacent lushness meets the beignets' light, airy, powdered-sugar sweetness. Sweet liqueur's dessert-adjacent sweetness amplifies the dessert — doubles up on sugar. Strong when the dessert is restrained.",
  "Beignets|Chilean Seabass": "After the seabass, the beignets -- the butter-rich flesh yields to warm choux and powdered sugar, the dipping sauce closing the meal cleanly. Works; the rich main hands off to a measured close, the table breathes.",
  "Beignets|Chopin Vodka": "Chopin Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a vodka. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Chopin Vodka for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Christian Bros Brandy": "Christian Brothers with beignets — sweeter American brandy against fried dough and powdered sugar. Excellent; Christian Bros and casual fried dessert is a natural American-pub pairing — the value brandy finds its register here.",
  "Beignets|Château Batailley": "Château Batailley's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Château Batailley on the steak course instead.",
  "Beignets|Château Beaucastel": "Château Beaucastel's old-world Châteauneuf-du-Pape gravitas fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- tannin can't pivot to warm pastry sugar — the pour reads dry, the dessert reads heavy. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Château Beaucastel lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Beignets|Château Gombaude-Guillot": "Château Gombaude-Guillot's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- tannin can't pivot to warm pastry sugar — the pour reads dry, the dessert reads heavy. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Château Gombaude-Guillot lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Beignets|Château Haut Segottes": "Château Haut Segottes' Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit jars against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Château Haut Segottes lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Beignets|Château de Rouillac": "Château de Rouillac's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit flattens the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Château de Rouillac for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Clam Chowder": "The chowder and the beignets -- the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base bookends with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Beignets|Clase Azul Anejo": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the aged-agave weight wraps the beignets, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the dessert. Works; accessible match.",
  "Beignets|Clase Azul Durango": "Clase Azul Durango's barrel-aged tequila weight reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the barrel-rested body handles the beignets, and the oak threads the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Beignets|Clase Azul Gold": "Clase Azul Gold's rested-agave body leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the beignets, and the caramel-agave register brightens the dessert. Works; accessible character doesn't drive.",
  "Beignets|Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's earthen-pit smoke profile finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the espadín-and-smoke body wraps the beignets, and the wood-smoke note underlines the dessert. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Beignets|Clase Azul Plata": "Clase Azul Plata's silky Jalisco blanco with ceramic-decanter presentation falls short of the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- light spirit reads thin against dessert sweetness. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a light spirit. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Clase Azul Plata belongs on the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Clase Azul Reposado": "Clase Azul Reposado's ceramic-icon reposado character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the rested-agave depth sits with the beignets, and the cooked-agave note underlines the dessert. Works; the call holds at register.",
