  "Beignets|French Onion": "French Onion and the beignets -- sugar plays against the savory weight, the table earns its lift. Works; either timing holds, the table builds either way.",
  "Beignets|Frias Block 5": "Frias Block 5's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- tannin can't pivot to warm pastry sugar — the pour reads dry, the dessert reads heavy. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Reserve the Frias Block 5 for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo": "G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo's high-acid Nebbiolo with rose-and-tar grip flattens the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti": "Piedmont Moscato — peach blossom, apricot, lychee, gentle effervescence. The bubbles mirror the choux steam-risen airiness and the peach-honey profile lifts powdered-sugar sweetness. Peak sparkling-dessert pairing; both beignet and Moscato share lightness as their defining trait. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Beignets|G4 Blanco": "G4 Blanco's unaged blanco-tequila lift with agave-citrus snap falls short of the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- light spirit reads thin against dessert sweetness. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a light spirit. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. G4 Blanco lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Beignets|G4 High Proof": "G4 High Proof's barrel-aged tequila weight finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the rested-agave depth sits with the beignets, and the cooked-agave note underlines the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Beignets|Garavogue Irish Whiskey": "Garavogue Irish Whiskey's Irish whiskey smoothness leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the approachable Irish character carries the beignets, and the grain register softens the dessert. Works; the pour's refinement is underused by the salad.",
  "Beignets|George T. Stagg": "George T. Stagg's cask-strength BTAC bourbon power reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon depth settles into the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Caribbean Cask frames the two-cut plate at distinctive register.",
  "Beignets|Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon": "Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Ghost Block Zinfandel": "Ghost Block Zinfandel's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift jars against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Ghost Block Zinfandel on the steak course instead.",
  "Beignets|Glenfiddich 12": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the beignets, and the smoke threads the dessert. Works; complexity wasted on salad.",
  "Beignets|Glenfiddich 14": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the scotch backbone matches the beignets, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the dessert. Works; Caribbean Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Beignets|Glenfiddich 18": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the beignets, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the dessert. Works; BIB slightly over-specified.",
  "Beignets|Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the scotch backbone matches the beignets, and the honey rounds the dessert. Works; gentle composed match.",
  "Beignets|Glenglassaugh 12": "Glenglassaugh 12's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the beignets, and the smoke threads the dessert. Works; distinctive character doesn't drive.",
  "Beignets|Glenlivet 12": "Glenlivet 12's entry Speyside character sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the malt-and-oak threads the beignets, and the malt edge frames the dessert. Works; JW Black handles the richness at premium-blend register.",
  "Beignets|Glenmorangie 10": "Glenmorangie 10's tallest-stills Highland bourbon-cask character finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the malt-and-oak threads the beignets, and the heather brightens the dessert. Works; the richer pour finds more with the dessert than Original brings.",
  "Beignets|Glenmorangie 18": "Glenmorangie 18's aged Highland with Oloroso finish reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the Highland register carries the beignets, and the malt edge frames the dessert. Works; pour's narrative is underused by the salad.",
  "Beignets|Graham's 10 Year Tawny": "10-year oak-cask oxidative Tawny — Graham's entry-point, dried apricot, walnut, toffee, gentle spice. The toffee clings to hot choux-fried dough and the gentle spice lifts powdered-sugar simplicity. Strong Tawny for beignets — Taylor Fladgate's cleaner fruit sits neater on the light airy bite.",
  "Beignets|Graham's 20 Year Tawny": "20-year oak-cask oxidative Tawny — Graham's step-up, concentrated dried fruit, roasted hazelnut, orange peel, silky finish. The silky finish clings to hot choux-fried dough and the orange peel lifts powdered-sugar. Strong step-up Tawny for beignets — twenty-year complexity is over-spent on the light airy bite.",
  "Beignets|Graham's 2017 Vintage Port": "2017 declared-vintage Port — Graham's bottle-aged, dense inky, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, powerful structured. The dense inky structure overwhelms hot choux-fried dough and powdered-sugar simplicity. Strong Vintage Port for beignets — Tawny's lighter caramel lift sits cleaner on the airy bite.",
  "Beignets|Gran Patron Platinum": "Gran Patron Platinum's silver-spirit lift with agave-citrus edge reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the unaged body brightens the beignets, and the unaged-cane note plays against the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Beignets|Grand Marnier": "Grand Marnier alongside beignets — orange peel and cognac warmth against warm fried dough and powdered sugar. A New Orleans-register pairing that sells itself; the citrus cuts the fat and the cognac depth anchors the sweetness. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Beignets|Gray Whale Gin": "Gray Whale with beignets — California 6-botanical craft against fried dough. Works; Gray Whale is over-specified for casual dessert; Empress 1908's rose and Aviation's soft lavender are better dessert matches.",
  "Beignets|Green Chartreuse": "Beignets: warm sugar-dusted pastry meets Green Chartreuse. Excellent; the herbal-bitter-complex digestif cuts through sugar-and-fried-dough at 55% register — textbook green-digestif move.",
  "Beignets|Grey Goose Vodka": "Grey Goose Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a vodka. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Grey Goose Vodka for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Grilled Caesar": "Grilled Caesar and the beignets -- sugar plays against the savory weight, the table earns its lift. Works; sequence them as opener and close or share the table, no clash.",
  "Beignets|Gumbo": "Gumbo and the beignets -- two registers in contrast, the meal earns its shape. Works; either timing holds, the table builds either way.",
  "Beignets|Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet": "Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Beignets|HDW 100 Vodka": "HDW 100 Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a vodka. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the HDW 100 Vodka for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Hakushu 12 Year": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the precise Japanese craft body wraps the beignets, and the precision rounds the dessert. Works; premium single-barrel wasted on the salad.",
  "Beignets|Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the caramel-spice register matches the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; bonded weight pushes past the soup's register slightly.",
  "Beignets|Hangar 1 Vodka": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a vodka. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hangar 1 Vodka belongs on the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Head Fake": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build leans against the beignet's warm sugar-dusted pastry — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Beignets|Heaven Hill 20 Year": "Heaven Hill 20 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon body sits with the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; too light for dessert density at this level.",
  "Beignets|Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond": "Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; too light for dessert density at this level.",
  "Beignets|Heaven's Door 10 Year": "Heaven's Door 10 Year's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the oak depth lays under the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; curated single-barrel covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Beignets|Heitz Martha's Vineyard": "Heitz Martha's Vineyard's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Heitz Martha's Vineyard on the steak course instead.",
  "Beignets|Heitz Trailside Vineyard": "Heitz Trailside Vineyard's Napa-icon Cab character fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- tannin can't pivot to warm pastry sugar — the pour reads dry, the dessert reads heavy. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Heitz Trailside Vineyard lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Beignets|Hendricks Flora Adora": "Flora Adora with beignets — Hendrick's lavish-floral Spring release against fried dough. Excellent; Flora Adora's honeysuckle-chamomile-elderflower is a distinctive floral-with-sugar bridge more dimensional than flagship Hendrick's.",
  "Beignets|Hendricks Gin": "Hendricks with beignets — perfumed low-juniper against fried dough. Excellent; Hendrick's rose-cucumber is the democratic Hendrick's dessert pairing; Grand Cabaret's black currant-and-rhubarb edges it for distinctiveness.",
  "Beignets|Hendricks Grand Cabaret": "Grand Cabaret with beignets — absinthe-style Hendrick's fruit-forward against fried dough. Excellent; Grand Cabaret's black currant-and-rhubarb is the featured Hendrick's Family-beignets pairing — fruit-and-sugar distinctive bridge flagship Hendrick's can't reach.",
  "Beignets|Hendricks Neptunia": "Neptunia with beignets — Scottish-coast Hendrick's against fried dough. Strong; Neptunia's coastal profile is interesting with sugar but over-specified for casual dessert; Grand Cabaret's black-currant is better.",
  "Beignets|Hendricks Orbium": "Orbium with beignets — quinine-wormwood Hendrick's against fried dough. Works; Orbium's bitter profile contrasts sugar but Grand Cabaret's fruit is the featured Hendrick's-beignets match.",
  "Beignets|Hennessy Cognac": "Hennessy with beignets — default-call cognac against fried dough and powdered sugar. Works; Hennessy's dried-fruit-vanilla is a comfortable finisher.",
  "Beignets|Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's aged 100-proof bonded single-barrel finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon depth settles into the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Beignets|Hibiki Japanese Harmony": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the elegant Suntory/Nikka register matches the beignets, and the green-fruit edge brightens the dessert. Works; neutral, not elevating.",
  "Beignets|Honey Roasted Carrots": "The honey carrots alongside the beignets -- sugar on sugar, the close reads heavy with sweetness. Works; the contrast holds, neither course overshadows the other.",
  "Beignets|House Wedge": "House Wedge and the beignets -- sugar and umami share the table, the contrast carries the meal. Works; sequence them as opener and close or share the table, no clash.",
  "Beignets|I.W. Harper 15 Year": "I.W. Harper 15 Year's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the oak depth lays under the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; collector-bottle depth gives ultra-premium character.",
  "Beignets|Il Colle Prosecco Superiore": "Veneto Glera — floral Prosecco with white peach, green apple, and crisp citrus finish. The bright acidity cuts beignets' fried-dough weight and the effervescence plays against powdered sugar and berry jam. Peak approachable bubbles for beignets — sweet-tart contrast without the Champagne price tag.",
  "Beignets|Inhibited": "Tito's, Kahlúa, Bailey's, chocolate liqueur, espresso, chocolate-drizzled glass. Heavy coffee-cream cocktail against light choux-based beignets — the cocktail's weight is higher than the beignets strictly want, but Bailey's cream softens the contrast. Peak if guest wants indulgent over elegant. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Beignets|Inverroche Gin": "Inverroche with beignets — South African fynbos gin against fried dough. Works; the floral-herbal profile is over-specified for casual dessert.",
  "Beignets|Iron Fish Gin": "Iron Fish Gin's botanical-driven lift fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- gin's herbal edge has no foil against warm pastry sugar — sharp meets sweet, neither wins. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a gin. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Iron Fish Gin for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon depth settles into the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Vermont-brand at matched register.",
  "Beignets|Isaac Bowman Port Finish": "Isaac Bowman Port Finish's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon body sits with the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; JD 12 handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Beignets|J Davies Ferrington Vineyards": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards' silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift jars against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. J Davies Ferrington Vineyards belongs on the steak course.",
  "Beignets|J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character jars against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Jack Daniel's 12 Year": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon backbone carries the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Beignets|Jack Daniel's Bonded": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon backbone carries the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; high proof over-specified for the soup.",
  "Beignets|Jack Daniel's Old No. 7": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the caramel-spice register matches the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; save the BTAC bottle for the protein course — the side doesn't deserve the pour.",
  "Beignets|Jack Daniel's Sinatra Select": "Jack Daniel's Sinatra Select's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the brown-spirit warmth threads the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Beignets|Jameson Irish Whiskey": "Jameson Irish Whiskey's classic Irish blend smoothness finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the approachable Irish character carries the beignets, and the triple-distilled smoothness brightens the dessert. Works; annual-release story wasted on salad.",
  "Beignets|Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir": "Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift flattens the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis": "Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis' Burgundy Chablis flinty minerality clashes with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- a dry white belongs with the main course, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a white wine. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Beignets|Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E.": "Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E.'s oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the caramel-spice register matches the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the sweetness is a touch much for the salad's simplicity.",
  "Beignets|Jefferson's Ocean Voyage 23": "Jefferson's Ocean Voyage 23's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the brown-spirit warmth threads the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; save the bottle for the protein course — a soup is wrong for a $200 pour.",
  "Beignets|Jefferson's Reserve": "Jefferson's Reserve's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Beignets|Jefferson's Reserve VR Twin Oak": "Jefferson's Reserve VR Twin Oak's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the caramel-spice register matches the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; blend character covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Beignets|Jim Beam Black Label": "Jim Beam Black Label's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Beignets|Jim Beam White Label": "Jim Beam White Label's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the brown-spirit warmth threads the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; 10-year depth overshoots delicacy.",
  "Beignets|Johnnie Walker Black": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the malt-driven body wraps the beignets, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the dessert. Works; the pour's refinement is underused by the salad.",
  "Beignets|Johnnie Walker Blue": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the Highland register carries the beignets, and the heather brightens the dessert. Works; save the collector bottle for the protein course.",
  "Beignets|Johnnie Walker Red": "Johnnie Walker Red's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the malt-driven body wraps the beignets, and the honey rounds the dessert. Works; the extra proof overpowers this dish.",
  "Beignets|Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon": "Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon's classical-Napa Cab elegance fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- tannin can't pivot to warm pastry sugar — the pour reads dry, the dessert reads heavy. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Joseph Mellot Sancerre": "Joseph Mellot Sancerre's classic Loire Sauvignon Blanc clashes with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- a dry white belongs with the main course, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a white wine. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Joseph Mellot Sancerre lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Beignets|Jubilation by Colgin": "Jubilation by Colgin's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- tannin can't pivot to warm pastry sugar — the pour reads dry, the dessert reads heavy. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Jubilation by Colgin for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Jung and Wulff Guyana": "Jung and Wulff Guyana's high-proof pour register sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the heavy body handles the beignets, and the rich character softens the dessert. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Beignets|Jung and Wulff Trinidad": "Jung and Wulff Trinidad's caramel-char character holds steady against the beignet's warm sugar-dusted pastry — the crisp body underclubs the dessert, and the vanilla amplifies the dessert sugar. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Beignets|Kahlua": "★ Kahlua's sweet coffee-rum-base depth meets head-on the beignet's warm sugar-dusted pastry — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar. Gold standard; the unskippable match for this combo.",
  "Beignets|Kansas City": "After the KC, the beignets -- the lean-bold strip yields to warm fried choux and powdered sugar, the dipping sauce closing the meal at register. Works; the table closes light after the bold main.",
  "Beignets|Keenan Chardonnay": "Keenan Chardonnay's oaked Spring Mountain Chardonnay clashes with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- a dry white belongs with the main course, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a white wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Keenan Chardonnay on the steak course instead.",
  "Beignets|Keenan Mernet": "Keenan Mernet's herbaceous Cab Franc with red-fruit and bell-pepper flattens the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Keenan Mernet for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the rye-and-oak weight handles the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; GTS is over-specified for a side — save the collector bottle.",
  "Beignets|Kentucky Owl Confiscated": "Kentucky Owl Confiscated's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon depth settles into the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Beignets|Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's": "Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's' Irish whiskey smoothness sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the gentle Irish body threads the beignets, and the soft malt rounds the dessert. Works; Fortuna's NZ terroir meets the glaze at distinctive register.",
  "Beignets|Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône": "Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- tannin can't pivot to warm pastry sugar — the pour reads dry, the dessert reads heavy. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Beignets|Ketel One Vodka": "Ketel One Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a vodka. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Ketel One Vodka for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Knickerbocker Gin": "Knickerbocker Gin's botanical-driven lift fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- gin's herbal edge has no foil against warm pastry sugar — sharp meets sweet, neither wins. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a gin. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Knickerbocker Gin for the steak course.",
  "Beignets|Knob Creek": "Knob Creek's oak-and-vanilla 100-proof depth reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon weight handles the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Beignets|Knob Creek 12 Year": "Knob Creek 12 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the brown-spirit warmth threads the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; EHT Full Proof is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Beignets|Knob Creek 15 Year": "Knob Creek 15 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon depth settles into the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the toast notes don't really interplay with the soup but don't clash.",
  "Beignets|Knob Creek 18 Year": "Knob Creek 18 Year's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon backbone carries the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Beignets|Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye": "Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the high-rye spice register matches the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Voyage 23 frames the cut at ocean-finish register.",
