  "Beignets|Laphroaig 10": "Laphroaig 10's classic Islay peat reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the scotch backbone matches the beignets, and the smoke threads the dessert. Works; the pour's assertiveness is a bit much for the soup but doesn't clash.",
  "Beignets|Larceny Small Batch": "Larceny Small Batch's Heaven Hill wheated caramel sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon depth settles into the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; JW Black handles the richness at premium-blend register.",
  "Beignets|Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé": "Tours-sur-Marne Pinot Noir rosé Champagne — silky mousse, red berry, long finish. The strawberry-raspberry complements beignets' berry-jam filling directly and bubbles cut fried-dough weight. Strong Champagne-and-beignets pairing — the dessert mirrors the berry profile of the rosé.",
  "Beignets|Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut": "Tours-sur-Marne Chardonnay-blend Champagne — precise green apple, lemon zest, whisper of brioche, vibrant acidity. The high-acid finish cuts beignets' fried-dough weight and the brioche complements the pastry directly. Strong elegant Champagne-with-dessert pairing — bubbles reset the palate at the sweet course.",
  "Beignets|Le Garenne Rosé": "Le Garenne Rosé's crisp white-wine character clashes with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- a dry white belongs with the main course, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a white wine. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Le Garenne Rosé for the steak course.",
