  "Beignets|Opus One": "Mondavi-Rothschild's $950 prestige Cabernet. Extreme mismatch — the beignet cannot carry the wine's structure and the occasion doesn't earn the pour. Never pair; Opus belongs with Tomahawk or Porterhouse where it performs.",
  "Beignets|Our Lady of Guadalupe Acolytes": "Our Lady of Guadalupe Acolytes' crisp white-wine character clashes with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- a dry white belongs with the main course, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a white wine. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Our Lady of Guadalupe Acolytes for the steak course.",
