  "Blanton's Gold|Swordfish": "Blanton's Gold's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Blanton's Gold for the steak course.",
  "Blanton's Gold|The Tomahawk": "Blanton's Gold with the Tomahawk — 103-proof export Blanton's against the bone-in ribeye. The richer profile and extra proof earn this cut where Blanton's Original is slightly outmatched; a premium single-barrel Tomahawk pour. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
