  "Blanton's Gold|Truffle Fries": "Blanton's Gold with truffle fries — 103-proof single-barrel against truffle-parmesan. The richer caramel-vanilla gives the side more grip than Original's balance brings. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Blanton's Gold|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Blanton's Gold's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Blanton's Gold for the steak course.",
  "Blanton's Gold|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Blanton's Gold's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the brown-spirit warmth threads the curry, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; smooth character is slightly over-specified for this dish.",
  "Blanton's Original|Asparagus": "Blanton's Original's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the bourbon depth settles into the asparagus, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; Remus 15 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Blanton's Original|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Blanton's Original with au gratin potatoes — 93-proof single-barrel against cheese-and-cream. Strong; composed premium match.",
  "Blanton's Original|Beignets": "Blanton's Original's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon body sits with the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; AE Triple Cask meets the char at distinctive register.",
  "Blanton's Original|Bone Marrow": "Blanton's Original with bone marrow — single-barrel against umami fat. Strong; the marrow's intensity pushes against the 93-proof balance — Blanton's Gold or E.H. Taylor handle marrow more fully.",
  "Blanton's Original|Bone-In Filet": "Blanton's Original's single-barrel-caramel character lifts the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the whiskey character holds register with the tenderloin, and the caramel echoes the grilled char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Blanton's Original|Broccoli Cheddar": "Blanton's Original's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; CC 43 Year is over-specified for a side — save the rare bottle for the main course.",
  "Blanton's Original|Broccolini": "Blanton's Original's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight sits alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the bourbon depth settles into the broccolini, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; cleaner than wheated versions but not exceptional.",
  "Blanton's Original|Brussels and Belly": "Blanton's Original with Brussels + Belly — 93-proof single-barrel meets maple-glazed pork belly. The benchmark honey-and-caramel threads through the glaze distinctively. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Blanton's Original|Burrata": "Blanton's Original with burrata — fresh dairy against premium single-barrel. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
