  "Blanton's Original|Carrot Cake": "Blanton's Original with carrot cake — single-barrel caramel-vanilla against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; a gentle composed match at the premium tier.",
  "Blanton's Original|Cheesecake": "Blanton's Original with cheesecake — iconic single-barrel against clean custard. Works; gentle composed match.",
  "Blanton's Original|Chilean Seabass": "Blanton's Original's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Blanton's Original lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Blanton's Original|Chocolate Brownie": "Blanton's Original with the chocolate brownie — 93-proof single-barrel against cocoa. Works; the balance is slightly underserved by the brownie — reach for Blanton's Gold's richer profile.",
  "Blanton's Original|Chocolate Cake": "Blanton's Original's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Blanton's Original|Clam Chowder": "Blanton's Original's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the caramel-spice register matches the chowder, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Blanton's Original|Cowboy Ribeye": "Blanton's Original with the Cowboy Ribeye — 93-proof single-barrel against cap fat and bold char. The Blanton's caramel-vanilla depth handles the ribeye cleanly; the benchmark single-barrel for this cut. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Blanton's Original|Crab Cake": "Blanton's Original with crab cake — premium single-barrel against delicate crab. Avoid; pour a crisp white wine.",
  "Blanton's Original|Creamed Spinach": "Blanton's Original with creamed spinach — single-barrel caramel-vanilla against dairy richness. Strong; the premium character sits with the side at matched register.",
  "Blanton's Original|Creamy Potato": "Blanton's Original's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the brown-spirit warmth threads the potato soup, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; EC 18 frames the two-cut plate at aged-HH register.",
  "Blanton's Original|Creme Brulee": "Blanton's Original's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the caramel-spice register matches the brulee, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; distinctive character doesn't drive.",
  "Blanton's Original|Escargot": "Blanton's Original's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the bourbon depth settles into the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; EHT Full Proof meets the earthy-rich at historic Kentucky register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Blanton's Original|Faroe Island Salmon": "Blanton's Original's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Blanton's Original for the steak course.",
  "Blanton's Original|Filet Mignon": "Blanton's Original with the filet — the benchmark premium single-barrel from Buffalo Trace. 93-proof, iconic horse-topper bottle. Caramel, vanilla, honey; balanced enough to frame the filet's clean beef without overpowering. The marquee single-barrel pour for filet orders. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Blanton's Original|French Onion": "Blanton's Original's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the bourbon body sits with the French onion, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Blanton's Original|Grilled Caesar": "Blanton's Original with the grilled Caesar — 93-proof single-barrel against charred romaine. Works; the premium pour doesn't quite drive the Caesar — Blanton's Gold or E.H. Taylor earn it more fully.",
  "Blanton's Original|Gumbo": "Blanton's Original's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the bourbon weight handles the gumbo, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; the unique maturation story adds interest to a gentle dessert match.",
  "Blanton's Original|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Blanton's Original's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the caramel-spice register matches the honey carrots, and the oak underlines the burnt sugar. Works; BIB slightly over-specified.",
  "Blanton's Original|House Wedge": "Blanton's Original with the House Wedge — iconic single-barrel against iceberg and bleu. Works; the premium pour is wasted on the salad's simplicity.",
  "Blanton's Original|Kansas City": "Blanton's Original with the KC — iconic 93-proof single-barrel against the strip's marbling. The barrel character gives the strip more depth than standard Buffalo Trace's flagship; a premium single-barrel strip pour. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Blanton's Original|Loaded Potato": "Blanton's Original's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the bourbon weight handles the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; single-barrel depth gives the dessert more than Small Batch.",
  "Blanton's Original|Lobster Mac": "Blanton's Original's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon weight handles the lobster mac, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the toast adds a warmth the dessert can accept.",
  "Blanton's Original|Market Fish": "Blanton's Original's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Blanton's Original belongs on the steak course.",
  "Blanton's Original|Mocha Creme": "Blanton's Original's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the brown-spirit warmth threads the mocha creme, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Blanton's Original|Mushroom Bisque": "Blanton's Original's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the oak depth lays under the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; premium single-barrel wasted on the salad.",
  "Blanton's Original|Mushrooms": "Blanton's Original with the mushrooms — single-barrel depth against earthy umami. The honey and vanilla layer into mushroom character at the premium register. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Blanton's Original|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Blanton's Original with the PB brownie — single-barrel caramel-vanilla against peanut butter and cocoa. Works; the pairing is pleasant but not a standout.",
  "Blanton's Original|Porterhouse": "Blanton's Original with the porterhouse — single-barrel across strip and filet. Strong; Blanton's handles both sides cleanly, though Blanton's Gold brings more grip for the strip.",
  "Blanton's Original|Prime Tartare": "Blanton's Original's single-barrel-caramel character finds register with the tartare's raw beef and brine — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Blanton's Original|Rainbow Trout": "Blanton's Original's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the trout's delicate flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Blanton's Original for the steak course.",
  "Blanton's Original|Roast Half Chicken": "Blanton's Original's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the bourbon body sits with the roast chicken, and the oak frames the plate. Works; richer profile overshoots the dessert's delicacy.",
  "Blanton's Original|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Blanton's Original's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the bourbon depth settles into the chickpea soup, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; boutique covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Blanton's Original|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Blanton's Original's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Blanton's Original for the steak course.",
  "Blanton's Original|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Blanton's Original's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the oak depth lays under the garlic spinach, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; IW Harper 15 handles dessert density at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Blanton's Original|Seafood Tower": "Blanton's Original's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Blanton's Original for the steak course.",
  "Blanton's Original|Seared Scallops": "Blanton's Original with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 93-proof single-barrel. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Blanton's Original|Seasonal Soup": "Blanton's Original's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the oak depth lays under the seasonal soup, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; multi-distillery complexity doesn't drive.",
  "Blanton's Original|Seasonal Vegetables": "Blanton's Original's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the bourbon weight handles the seasonal vegetables, and the rounded sweetness brightens the side. Works; Caribbean Cask frames the two-cut plate at distinctive register.",
  "Blanton's Original|Shrimp Bisque": "Blanton's Original's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon backbone carries the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; annual-release complexity over-specified.",
  "Blanton's Original|Shrimp Cocktail": "Blanton's Original with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against iconic single-barrel. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Blanton's Original|Swordfish": "Blanton's Original's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon's sweet weight crowds the rare crust's clean char. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Blanton's Original for the steak course.",
  "Blanton's Original|The Tomahawk": "Blanton's Original with the Tomahawk — 93-proof single-barrel against the bone-in ribeye. Strong; the scale is slightly ambitious for Blanton's Original — Blanton's Gold's 103 proof or E.H. Taylor's BIB weight are the stronger Tomahawk calls.",
  "Blanton's Original|Tomato Basil": "Blanton's Original's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the caramel-spice register matches the tomato basil, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Blanton's Original|Truffle Fries": "Blanton's Original with truffle fries — iconic single-barrel against truffle-parmesan fat. The benchmark caramel-vanilla gives the side a refined frame; the premium single-barrel truffle-fries pairing. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Blanton's Original|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Blanton's Original's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Blanton's Original on the steak course instead.",
  "Blanton's Original|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Blanton's Original's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the caramel-spice register matches the curry, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; sweet character distinctive but not driving.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Asparagus": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- the side reads small under oak-and-vanilla density. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Blanton's Straight from the Barrel on the steak course instead.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet cask-strength Blanton's. Works; Blanton's SfB handles the richness at barrel-proof register.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Beignets": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the oak depth lays under the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Old Fitz 9 brings more depth here.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Bone Marrow": "Blanton's SfB with bone marrow — export cask-strength Blanton's against umami fat. Excellent; Blanton's SfB cuts marrow at barrel-proof register with distinctive Blanton's character.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Bone-In Filet": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits at register with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the bone-enhanced filet, and the rounded sweetness brightens the cut. Strong; JW Blue's silky-complex character meets the earthy-rich at collector register; consider whether the side deserves a $200 pour or if Blue is better spent on the main.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Broccoli Cheddar": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the bourbon backbone carries the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for a side — save the collector bottle for the main.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Broccolini": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overshadows the broccolini's tender green stalks -- sweet-oak depth has nothing to bridge into green vegetable freshness. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Blanton's Straight from the Barrel for the steak course.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet cask-strength Blanton's. Blanton's SfB meets the glaze with distinctive honey-vanilla character at cask-strength. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Burrata": "Blanton's SfB with burrata — cask-strength Blanton's against fresh dairy. Avoid; barrel-proof obliterates burrata.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Butternut Squash": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the squash bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Carrot Cake": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet cask-strength Blanton's. Works; Blanton's SfB meets the cake at barrel-proof register.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Cheesecake": "Blanton's SfB with cheesecake — cask-strength Blanton's against custard. Avoid; barrel-proof intensity wrong for custard's delicate character.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Chilean Seabass": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Blanton's Straight from the Barrel on the steak course instead.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Chocolate Brownie": "Blanton's SfB with the chocolate brownie — cask-strength Blanton's against cocoa. Excellent; Blanton's SfB's distinctive character meets cocoa at barrel-proof register.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Chocolate Cake": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Caribbean Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Clam Chowder": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon depth settles into the chowder, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; craft-blender complexity over-specified.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Cowboy Ribeye": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel with the cowboy ribeye — export-market cask-strength Blanton's, 130+ proof, distinctive horse-and-jockey stopper design, honey-vanilla-citrus Blanton's character at cask-strength intensity. Excellent; Blanton's SfB's distinctive Blanton's-character-at-full-proof is the featured conversation-piece barrel-proof-ribeye pairing — where the Staggs are BT-traditional, SfB is Blanton's-distinctive with the collector stopper.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Crab Cake": "Blanton's SfB with crab cake — cask-strength Blanton's against delicate lump crab. Avoid; barrel-proof obliterates crab. Reach for a vodka or gin.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Creamed Spinach": "Blanton's SfB with creamed spinach — export cask-strength Blanton's against dairy-rich side. Strong; Blanton's SfB cuts the cream at barrel-proof register.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Creamy Potato": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the potato soup, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; a gentle, everyday match.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Creme Brulee": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the bourbon depth settles into the brulee, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; bonded weight slightly over-specified.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Escargot": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's cask-strength char-citrus character sits with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon weight grips the savory plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Faroe Island Salmon": "Blanton's SfB with the salmon — cask-strength Blanton's against oily salmon. Avoid; barrel-proof bourbon too intense for fish.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Filet Mignon": "Blanton's SfB with the filet — cask-strength Blanton's against tenderloin. Works; Blanton's SfB's intensity is over-specified for filet — save for the ribeye/Tomahawk.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|French Onion": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the bourbon body sits with the French onion, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; boutique-sourced doesn't drive.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Grilled Caesar": "Grilled Caesar: charred romaine and anchovy meet export cask-strength Blanton's. Works; Blanton's SfB is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Gumbo": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight sits alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the brown-spirit warmth threads the gumbo, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth crowds the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- the spirit needs the cut, not the supporting side. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Blanton's Straight from the Barrel lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|House Wedge": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the wedge's iceberg-and-bleu cool crunch: the brown-spirit warmth threads the wedge, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; craft-blend over-specified.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Kansas City": "Blanton's SfB with the KC — cask-strength Blanton's against an 18oz strip. Excellent; Blanton's SfB handles strip marbling with distinctive Blanton's-character at barrel-proof register.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Loaded Potato": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the brown-spirit warmth threads the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Lobster Mac": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the brown-spirit warmth threads the lobster mac, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Market Fish": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Blanton's Straight from the Barrel for the steak course.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Mocha Creme": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the bourbon weight handles the mocha creme, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; a gentle composed match at the premium tier.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Mushroom Bisque": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the oak depth lays under the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; narrative-bourbon doesn't drive.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Mushrooms": "Blanton's SfB with mushrooms — cask-strength Blanton's against earthy umami. Strong; Blanton's SfB threads mushrooms with distinctive character at barrel-proof register.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Peanut Butter Brownie: peanut butter and cocoa meet cask-strength Blanton's. Strong; Blanton's SfB handles dessert density at barrel-proof register.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Porterhouse": "Blanton's SfB with the porterhouse — export cask-strength Blanton's against strip-and-filet. Strong; Blanton's SfB frames the two-cut plate with distinctive Blanton's character at barrel-proof register.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Prime Tartare": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's cask-strength char-citrus character finds register with the tartare's raw beef and brine — the caramel-oak depth threads the savory plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
