  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Roast Half Chicken": "Blanton's SfB with the chicken — cask-strength Blanton's against roasted poultry. Avoid; barrel-proof is over-specified for chicken.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the caramel-spice register matches the chickpea soup, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; namesake pour is wasted on the salad.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Blanton's Straight from the Barrel for the steak course.",
