  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Seasonal Vegetables": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overshadows the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate -- sweet-oak depth has nothing to bridge into green vegetable freshness. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Blanton's Straight from the Barrel belongs on the steak course.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Shrimp Bisque": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon weight handles the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Shrimp Cocktail": "Blanton's SfB with shrimp cocktail — cask-strength Blanton's against cold shrimp. Avoid; barrel-proof wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Swordfish": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon's sweet weight crowds the rare crust's clean char. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Blanton's Straight from the Barrel for the steak course.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|The Tomahawk": "Blanton's SfB with the Tomahawk — export cask-strength Blanton's against 32oz bone-in cap-fat. Excellent; Blanton's SfB handles the Tomahawk with distinctive honey-vanilla-citrus character at 130+ proof.",
  "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel|Tomato Basil": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the bourbon depth settles into the tomato basil, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; the Millennium's register overshoots the dessert's.",
