  "Bone-In Filet|Heaven's Door 10 Year": "Heaven's Door 10 Year's caramel-vanilla character finds register with the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the aged-oak weight frames the lean cut, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Bone-In Filet|Heitz Martha's Vineyard": "Bone-In Filet: the filet's lean, buttery tenderness and delicate mineral edge meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The dark-fruit frame supports the filet, but the tannin rides harder than the lean profile demands. A strong match — the tannin and filet tenderness align cleanly. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Bone-In Filet|Heitz Trailside Vineyard": "Heitz Trailside Vineyard's bold cherry-mint cassis reads alongside the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the concentrated body carries the strip, and the cassis plays against the grilled char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Bone-In Filet|Hendricks Flora Adora": "Hendricks Flora Adora's botanical-driven lift mis-pairs with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- gin's clean lift reads thin against the cut's weight. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a gin. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Hendricks Flora Adora for another course.",
