  "Bone-In Filet|Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks": "Ironfish Bourbon Mezcal Casks with the bone-in filet — northern MI mezcal-cask against tenderloin-with-bone. Works; Ironfish Mezcal frames the cut at Michigan-hometown register.",
  "Bone-In Filet|Isaac Bowman Port Finish": "Isaac Bowman Port Finish with the bone-in filet — A. Smith Bowman Sazerac-owned against tenderloin-with-bone. Excellent; Isaac Bowman's port-finish frames the cut at Virginia-heritage register.",
  "Bone-In Filet|J Davies Ferrington Vineyards": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards's cherry-coffee tannin sits with the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the medium-body red frames the lean cut, and the cassis plays against the grilled char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Bone-In Filet|J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon -- Davies Estate, Diamond Mountain, mineral. The Diamond-Mountain-Cab body wraps the bone-enhanced filet, and the mineral edge frames the cut. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Bone-In Filet|Jack Daniel's 12 Year": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year -- aged Tennessee whiskey, 12yr premium tier, deeper vanilla-caramel depth. The bourbon depth settles into the bone-enhanced filet, and the vanilla softens the cut. Strong; bonded weight at matched premium register.",
  "Bone-In Filet|Jack Daniel's Bonded": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's bold char-spice character matches the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the bourbon depth supports the lean cut without overpowering, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
