  "Bone-In Filet|Jack Daniel's Sinatra Select": "Jack Daniel's Sinatra Select's bold char-malt character matches the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the bourbon weight grips the lean cut, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Bone-In Filet|Jameson Irish Whiskey": "Jameson Irish Whiskey's classic Irish blend smoothness finds neutral with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the gentle Irish body threads the bone-enhanced filet, and the soft malt rounds the cut. Works; HH 20's aged character meets the glaze at collector register.",
  "Bone-In Filet|Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir": "Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir's cherry-earth tannin lifts the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the medium-body red frames the lean cut, and the cherry-fruit cuts the char. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Bone-In Filet|Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis": "Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis' Burgundy Chablis flinty minerality underclubs the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- white wine reads thin against any prime cut. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a white wine. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis for another course.",
  "Bone-In Filet|Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E.": "Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E. with the bone-in filet — sea-aged L.E. against tenderloin-with-bone. Works; Marian McLain L.E. frames the cut at collector register.",
