  "Bone-In Filet|Vesper": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build sits alongside the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the cocktail is outweighed by the cut, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Bone-In Filet|Veuve Clicquot Brut": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's classic yellow-label Champagne body underclubs the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- sparkling sits short of the prime cut's weight. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a sparkling. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Veuve Clicquot Brut for another course.",
