  "Bone-In Filet|Villon Cognac": "Villon Cognac's barrel-aged cognac character sits alongside the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the aged-grape brandy body sits with the bone-enhanced filet, and the orchard-fruit thread frames the cut. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Bone-In Filet|Vin Santo": "Vin Santo's Tuscan dried-fruit-and-honey sweetness clashes with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- dessert wine belongs after the meal, not alongside the steak. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Vin Santo belongs on another course.",
  "Bone-In Filet|Weller 107": "Weller 107's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the brown-spirit warmth threads the bone-enhanced filet, and the oak-and-spice register settles the cut. Strong; aged premium at matched register.",
  "Bone-In Filet|Weller 12 Year": "Weller 12 Year's wheated-vanilla character matches the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the whiskey character holds register with the tenderloin, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Bone-In Filet|Weller Millennium": "Weller Millennium: 20-year wheated bourbon, heavily allocated, the white-whale of the Weller family. Excellent on bone-in filet; wheated softness frames the marrow-adjacent cut at luxury register — save the bottle for guests who know the family.",
  "Bone-In Filet|Weller Special Reserve": "Weller Special Reserve -- wheated, soft vanilla, gentle oak. The oak depth lays under the bone-enhanced filet, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the cut. Strong; craft-blend narrative covers the cut with KO authority.",
  "Bone-In Filet|Wheatley Vodka": "Wheatley Vodka's crystalline neutrality underclubs the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- vodka is too neutral to carry any prime cut. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a vodka. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Wheatley Vodka on another course instead.",
  "Bone-In Filet|WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel Rye": "WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel Rye's pepper-spice character lifts the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the aged-oak weight frames the lean cut, and the oak underlines the char. Strong; the call lands cleanly.",
  "Bone-In Filet|WhistlePig 12 Year Old World": "WhistlePig 12 Year Old World's sweet char-honey character sits with the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the sweet character meets the cut at digestif register, and the honey rounds the grilled char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Bone-In Filet|WhistlePig 15 Year": "WhistlePig 15 Year -- WP's 15-year premium flagship, 92 proof, Vermont oak barrel finish. The rye spice cuts the bone-enhanced filet, and the rye edge frames the cut. Strong; extended-maturation character sits with richness.",
  "Bone-In Filet|WhistlePig Boss Hog IX 17 Year": "WhistlePig Boss Hog IX 17 Year's rye-spice character sits alongside the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the rye spice cuts the bone-enhanced filet, and the rye edge frames the cut. Strong; EHT Full Proof threads mushrooms at historic Kentucky-bourbon register.",
  "Bone-In Filet|WhistlePig Boss Hog X Commandments": "WhistlePig Boss Hog X Commandments's cask-strength spice character frames the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the whiskey character holds register with the tenderloin, and the oak underlines the char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
