  "Broccoli Cheddar|Blood Oath Pact 9": "Blood Oath Pact 9's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the brown-spirit warmth threads the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; smooth gentle match.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Bluecoat Gin": "Bluecoat Gin's botanical-driven lift sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the floral edge frames the broccoli cheddar, and the juniper threads the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Bodega Noemia A Lisa": "Bodega Noemia A Lisa's concentrated dark-fruit and tannin reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the structured body wraps the broccoli cheddar, and the cassis frames the bowl. Works; the dessert sits cleanly against the meal's register.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Bombay Dry Gin": "Bombay Dry Gin's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals leans against the broccoli cheddar's cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Bombay Sapphire Gin": "Bombay Sapphire Gin's crisp London-Dry-citrus botanicals reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Bone Marrow": "The bone marrow with the broccoli cheddar -- the bone marrow's unctuous rendered-marrow richness meets the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: cream and protein share the meal, the build reads full. Works; both opening courses earn their place.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Bone-In Filet": "Bone-In Filet into the broccoli cheddar -- cream meets protein, the meal builds with weight. Works; safe opener, the meal builds without crowding.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Booker's": "Booker's' cask-strength bourbon depth leans against the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the bourbon depth settles into the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; Old Fitz 9 brings more depth here.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Botanist Gin": "Botanist Gin's crisp Islay-gentle-botanical botanicals sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Bowdie's Old Fashioned": "Buffalo Trace Old Fashioned against a cream-and-cheddar broccoli soup — bourbon vanilla-caramel has no hook into a vegetable-cheese classic. Never layer. Route the cocktail to fatted steaks or marrow; take broccoli cheddar with Chardonnay, Pinot Blanc, or Chablis.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark": "Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the bourbon depth settles into the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; neutral, not elevating.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Bowman Brothers Small Batch": "Bowman Brothers Small Batch's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the bourbon depth settles into the broccoli cheddar, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Bowmore 12": "Bowmore 12's lighter-Islay peat character leans against the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the malt-and-oak threads the broccoli cheddar, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; bold proof overshoots delicacy.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Braida Montebruna Barbera": "Braida Montebruna Barbera's cherry-earth tannin leans against the broccoli cheddar's cream — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Broccolini": "The broccoli cheddar alongside the broccolini -- both bring broccoli as the headline. Avoid; one is enough. Pair the broccoli cheddar with Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay; pair the broccolini with St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Bruichladdich": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the malt-and-oak threads the broccoli cheddar, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; aging wasted on the salad.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Brussels and Belly": "Broccoli Cheddar and Brussels + Belly -- the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream meets Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: two rich courses on the same plate, the table earns its substance. Works; no conflict however the table orders them.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Buffalo Trace": "Buffalo Trace's rounded vanilla-and-toffee character leans against the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the caramel-spice register matches the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; collector-bottle depth gives the dessert ultra-premium character.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Buffalo Trace Cream": "Buffalo Trace Cream's sweet liqueur character clashes with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; the better calls are above. Buffalo Trace Cream belongs on the steak course.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Bulleit Bourbon": "Bulleit Bourbon's high-rye spice-forward depth finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the oak depth lays under the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; Gran Cru's brioche meets the glaze at refined register.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Burrata": "The burrata and the broccoli cheddar -- both cheese-forward, the table doubles up on cheese. Avoid; pick one or the other. Pair the burrata with Il Colle Prosecco Superiore, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc; pair the broccoli cheddar with Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Cade Cabernet Sauvignon": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character overwhelms the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Cade Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Camarena Tequila": "Camarena Tequila's rested-agave body reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the oak-aged tequila body threads the broccoli cheddar, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; cedar and maple don't quite align.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Campari": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook fights the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- bitter herbs cut the bisque's round cream without lifting it. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Campari belongs on the steak course.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Canadian Club": "Canadian Club's workhorse Canadian blend sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the easygoing Canadian character handles the broccoli cheddar, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Canadian Club 43 Year": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the smooth Canadian register carries the broccoli cheddar, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; wine-cask complexity gives the dessert layered premium character.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Captain Morgan Rum": "Captain Morgan Rum's light-rum register with cane and citrus lift mis-pairs with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- the light spirit doesn't add to the soup-salad course — neutral but wrong. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a light spirit. Avoid; the better calls are above. Captain Morgan Rum lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Caribou Crossing": "Caribou Crossing's Canadian whisky character reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the smooth Canadian register carries the broccoli cheddar, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; annual-release wasted on salad.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Carrot Cake": "Broccoli Cheddar and the carrot cake -- the cream rounds into the sweet close, the meal lands rich and full. Works; either timing holds, the table builds either way.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Casa LBV Port": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness doubles down on the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- sweet wine on cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — heavy, no contrast. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Casamigos Mezcal": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character clashes with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- mezcal smoke fights the soup's cream — smoke has no bridge into dairy delicacy. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a mezcal. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Casamigos Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon": "Napa Rutherford Cab against a cream-and-cheddar broccoli soup — concentrated cocoa-mocha body crushes the vegetable-cheese classic. Never pair. Route Caymus to the steak course and take broccoli cheddar with Chardonnay, Pinot Blanc, or Chablis.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Chambord": "Chambord's sweet liqueur character clashes with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Chambord on the steak course instead.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Cheesecake": "Broccoli Cheddar and the cheesecake -- the cream rounds into the sweet close, the meal lands rich and full. Works; either timing holds, the table builds either way.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Chilean Seabass": "Chilean Seabass after the broccoli cheddar -- the cheddar-and-broccoli cream opens with rich-savory weight, the seabass following with buttery pan-finished flesh that meets the cream in matching register. Strong; cream into butter reads doubled in the right key.",
