  "Broccoli Cheddar|Château Batailley": "Château Batailley's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overwhelms the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Château Batailley lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Château Beaucastel": "Château Beaucastel's old-world Châteauneuf-du-Pape gravitas clashes with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Château Beaucastel lands on the steak course — not here.",
