  "Broccoli Cheddar|Le Ragnaie Brunello": "Le Ragnaie Brunello's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity overwhelms the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Le Ragnaie Brunello for the steak course.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Le Volte dell'Ornellaia": "Le Volte dell'Ornellaia's cherry-coffee tannin leans against the broccoli cheddar's cream — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
