  "Broccoli Cheddar|Limoncello": "Limoncello's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- the liqueur's sweetness buries the soup's creamy base instead of supporting it. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Limoncello for the steak course.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Willamette Pinot — dark cherry, forest floor, refined structure, low tannin. The low-tannin silk lifts the soup's cheddar weight and the forest-floor earth plays against broccoli vegetal base. Works tier on this wine's card — solid fit for Broccoli Cheddar but below the wine's peaks with duck, lamb, and mushroom-sauced proteins.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Little Book": "Little Book's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the single-barrel depth is over-specified for this dish.",
