  "Broccoli Cheddar|Raventós Cava de NIT Rosé Brut": "Catalan Cava rosé — wild strawberry, raspberry, saline finish. The bright acid cuts the soup's cheddar-cream weight and the berry profile plays against broccoli vegetal base. Works as Cava for broccoli cheddar — rosé sparkler on the classic.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Redbreast 12 Year": "Redbreast 12 Year's single pot still Irish character leans against the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the pot-still depth wraps the broccoli cheddar, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; Parker's Heritage 16th handles the richness at annual-release register.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Redbreast 21 Year": "Redbreast 21 Year's aged single pot still Irish sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the Irish whiskey body sits with the broccoli cheddar, and the oak threads the cream. Works; the pour's sweetness meets the dessert without pushing past.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Remus 15 Year Gatsby Reserve": "Remus 15 Year Gatsby Reserve's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the bourbon weight handles the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Remy VSOP Cognac": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the eau-de-vie body carries the broccoli cheddar, and the orchard-fruit thread frames the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Rey Sol Anejo": "Rey Sol Anejo's barrel-aged tequila weight sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the añejo register carries the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Reyka Vodka": "Reyka Vodka's crisp Icelandic-glacial neutrality stays alongside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Rishi's Old Antique": "Rishi's Old Antique's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the brown-spirit warmth threads the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; friendly accessible match.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Roast Half Chicken": "Roast Half Chicken after the broccoli cheddar -- the cheddar-and-broccoli cream opens with rich-savory weight, the chicken following with herbed crisp-skin roast the cream primed without crowding. Strong; cream into roast reads classic.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs's crisp apple-char acidity sits beside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the mousse refreshes against the broth, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Roku Gin": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals sits beside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Ron Zacapa Rum": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum leans against the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the dense-spirit weight carries the broccoli cheddar, and the layered body brightens the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Russell's Reserve 10 Year": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the oak depth lays under the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; the complex character gives the dessert a refined frame.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Salt-Cured Halibut after the broccoli cheddar -- the cheddar-and-broccoli cream opens with rich-savory weight, the halibut following with firm cured flesh the cream gave room for. Strong; cream cleans for the cured main.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Sambuca": "Sambuca's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- sugar piled onto cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — no contrast. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Sambuca on the steak course instead.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|San Simeon Stormwatch": "San Simeon Stormwatch's bold cherry-coffee cassis plays cleanly against the broccoli cheddar's cream — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir": "Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir's cherry-earth tannin stays alongside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "The broccoli cheddar alongside the garlic spinach -- the bright register cleaves the heavy course, the table breathes. Works; the table can build them in order or together.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Sauternes Glass": "Sauternes Glass' dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Sauternes Glass belongs on the steak course.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Sazerac": "Sazerac's bold anise-cherry build reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the whiskey-build weight overshoots the light soup, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Sazerac Rye": "Sazerac Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the rye spice cuts the broccoli cheddar, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; Remus 15's rye-spice meets the glaze at Gatsby-tribute register.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Scapegrace Fortuna": "Scapegrace Fortuna's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the bourbon backbone carries the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; smooth character is slightly over-specified for this dish.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Scavino Barolo": "Piedmont Barolo's tar-and-tannin intensity against a cream-and-cheddar soup — firm-tannin Nebbiolo annihilates the vegetable-cheese classic. Never pair. Route Scavino to the Tomahawk or Porterhouse; take broccoli cheddar with Chardonnay, Pinot Blanc, or Chablis.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Schloss Vollrads Riesling": "Schloss Vollrads Riesling's crisp apricot-floral acidity stays alongside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the mineral edge cuts the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters": "Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters's bold cherry-chocolate cassis finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cream — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Seafood Tower": "The seafood tower with the broccoli cheddar -- the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup meets the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the bright cuts the rich cleanly. Works; both opening courses earn their place.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Seared Scallops": "Seared Scallops and the broccoli cheddar together -- the caramelized sear meets the cream-and-cheddar soup. Strong; both openers earn their place on the meal.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Seasonal Vegetables": "The broccoli cheddar and the seasonal vegetables on the same meal -- a quiet call, the meal carries without strain. Works; sequence or share, the build holds.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Sesti Brunello di Montalcino": "Sesti Brunello di Montalcino's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity clashes with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Sesti Brunello di Montalcino for the steak course.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Shafer 1.5": "Shafer 1.5's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- the wine's structure sits on top of the bisque's cream instead of integrating. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Shafer 1.5 for the steak course.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Shafer Hillside Select": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power clashes with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Shafer Hillside Select on the steak course instead.",
  "Broccoli Cheddar|Shrimp Cocktail": "Shrimp Cocktail and the broccoli cheddar together -- bright-acid breaks the weight, the plate finds its lift. Works; the table opens with both, no clash either way.",
