  "Bruichladdich|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay reads alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the scotch depth settles into the au gratin, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; bold intensity slightly over-specified.",
  "Bruichladdich|Beignets": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the beignets, and the smoke threads the dessert. Works; EC 18 frames the two-cut plate at aged-HH register.",
  "Bruichladdich|Bone Marrow": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets this rich, umami-forward starter's bold fat and concentrated savory depth. Whiskey depth meets the starter's fat and umami — both land heavy. Avoid.",
  "Bruichladdich|Bone-In Filet": "Bruichladdich's crisp char-citrus character lifts the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the bourbon depth carries the cut, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; the match carries without overshooting.",
  "Bruichladdich|Broccoli Cheddar": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the malt-and-oak threads the broccoli cheddar, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; aging wasted on the salad.",
  "Bruichladdich|Broccolini": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay sits alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the scotch depth settles into the broccolini, and the heather brightens the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Bruichladdich|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight. Whiskey's oak and sweetness mirror the side's dairy and umami depth. Works cleanly.",
  "Bruichladdich|Burrata": "Burrata: the burrata's creamy, fresh dairy mildness meets this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight. Bold whiskey's weight meets the starter — register depends on the plate's richness. A headliner match — context-driven peak. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Bruichladdich|Butternut Squash": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay reads alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the scotch depth settles into the squash bisque, and the oak softens the cream. Works; namesake pour is wasted on the salad.",
  "Bruichladdich|Carrot Cake": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets the carrot cake's warm-spice, cream-cheese indulgence. Bold whiskey meets rich chocolate — cross-category depth that plays. Strong — dark-on-dark.",
  "Bruichladdich|Cheesecake": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets the cheesecake's dense, tangy dairy richness. Bold whiskey meets rich chocolate — cross-category depth that plays. Works cleanly.",
  "Bruichladdich|Chilean Seabass": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon weight needs red meat, not the salmon's already-rich oils. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Bruichladdich lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Bruichladdich|Chocolate Brownie": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay leans against the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight: the malt-and-oak threads the brownie, and the oak-and-smoke underlines the dessert. Works; the spicy-sweet character gives the dessert a Barton frame.",
  "Bruichladdich|Chocolate Cake": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay finds neutral with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the Highland register carries the chocolate cake, and the heather brightens the dessert. Works; save the bottle for the protein course — a soup is wrong for a $200 pour.",
  "Bruichladdich|Clam Chowder": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the scotch backbone matches the chowder, and the oak threads the cream. Works; BIB slightly over-specified.",
  "Bruichladdich|Cowboy Ribeye": "Bruichladdich -- unpeated Islay, progressive, malt. The unpeated Islay body sits with the cap-fat ribeye, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; composed premium match.",
  "Bruichladdich|Crab Cake": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets this delicate seafood starter's briny-fresh sweetness. The whiskey sits heavy against a starter; the match depends on whether the plate has fat to scrub. Works as a parallel pour.",
  "Bruichladdich|Creamed Spinach": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay finds neutral with the creamed spinach's rich bechamel-laced greens: the scotch backbone matches the creamed spinach, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; blended character doesn't drive.",
  "Bruichladdich|Creamy Potato": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay sits alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the scotch depth settles into the potato soup, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; extended-aged home-state pour wasted on salad.",
  "Bruichladdich|Creme Brulee": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay leans against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the malt-driven body wraps the brulee, and the oak threads the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Bruichladdich|Escargot": "Bruichladdich's crisp char-citrus character holds the line with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the smoke meets the umami depth. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Bruichladdich|Faroe Island Salmon": "Bruichladdich with the salmon — clean barley notes and soft citrus against the salmon's richness. Without the peat, the pairing keeps the fish centered. One of the best non-peated Islay pairings on the card. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Bruichladdich|Filet Mignon": "Bruichladdich Classic Laddie with the filet — unpeated Islay is a revelation for guests who assume all Islay smokes. The barley sweetness and orchard fruit frame the filet cleanly. Pour when a guest wants something distinctive but doesn't want the peat. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Bruichladdich|French Onion": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the French onion, and the honey rounds the bowl. Works; annual-release complexity over-specified.",
  "Bruichladdich|Grilled Caesar": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets the Grilled Caesar's charred romaine, anchovy umami, and bold creamy dressing. Bold whiskey against the Caesar's char and umami — weight matches, but the flavors compete. A headliner match — context-driven peak. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Bruichladdich|Gumbo": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay sits alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the malt-and-oak threads the gumbo, and the malt edge frames the bowl. Works; the pour's complexity is underused by the salad.",
  "Bruichladdich|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay leans against the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the unpeated Islay body sits with the honey carrots, and the oak frames the caramelized sugar. Works; HH 20 frames the two-cut plate at collector register.",
  "Bruichladdich|House Wedge": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets the House Wedge's crisp iceberg against creamy bleu dressing. Heavy whiskey on a crisp wedge — the drink steamrolls the salad. Strong — the interaction lands despite the axis challenge.",
  "Bruichladdich|Kansas City": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets this bold, beefy strip's firm texture and savory char. The whiskey's barrel depth and the steak's flame-grilled fat run at the same intensity — a classic steakhouse move. Works — cocktail-on-steak coherence.",
  "Bruichladdich|Loaded Potato": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay sits alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the scotch depth settles into the loaded potato soup, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; extended-aged premium wasted on salad simplicity.",
  "Bruichladdich|Lobster Mac": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the Highland register carries the lobster mac, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; concentrated blend slightly over-specified.",
  "Bruichladdich|Market Fish": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay swallows the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a scotch. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Bruichladdich for the steak course.",
  "Bruichladdich|Mocha Creme": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay reads alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the malt-and-oak threads the mocha creme, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; extended maturation gives the dessert home-state aged character.",
  "Bruichladdich|Mushroom Bisque": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the scotch backbone matches the mushroom bisque, and the oak depth meets the umami. Works; premium KO story wasted on salad.",
  "Bruichladdich|Mushrooms": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets this earthy, umami-packed side's mushroom-and-truffle depth. Whiskey's oak and sweetness mirror the side's dairy and umami depth. A headliner match — context-driven peak. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Bruichladdich|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay finds neutral with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the PB brownie, and the honey rounds the dessert. Works; BTAC story wasted on salad.",
  "Bruichladdich|Porterhouse": "Bruichladdich's crisp char-citrus character lifts the porterhouse's two-cut character — the bourbon weight matches the cap-fat, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Bruichladdich|Prime Tartare": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets this rich, umami-forward starter's bold fat and concentrated savory depth. Whiskey depth meets the starter's fat and umami — both land heavy. Strong — aligned weight.",
  "Bruichladdich|Rainbow Trout": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a scotch. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Bruichladdich belongs on the steak course.",
  "Bruichladdich|Roast Half Chicken": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets this roasted chicken's savory, rich poultry-skin flavor. Bold whiskey against roasted chicken — the drink outweighs but oak and savory can mesh. Strong — aligned depth.",
  "Bruichladdich|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay finds neutral with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the malt-driven body wraps the chickpea soup, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the bowl. Works; JD Bonded's backbone handles the richness at Bonded register.",
  "Bruichladdich|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay swallows the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Bruichladdich for the steak course.",
  "Bruichladdich|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay leans against the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the unpeated Islay body sits with the garlic spinach, and the malt edge frames the side. Works; JW Blue is over-specified for a side — save the bottle for the main course.",
  "Bruichladdich|Seafood Tower": "Seafood Tower: this delicate seafood starter's briny-fresh sweetness meets this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight. Whiskey's oak and caramel are only going to land if the starter can carry weight — check the plate. Works as a parallel pour.",
  "Bruichladdich|Seared Scallops": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay fights the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a scotch. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Bruichladdich lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Bruichladdich|Seasonal Soup": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay sits alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the seasonal soup, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; private-selection wasted on the salad.",
  "Bruichladdich|Seasonal Vegetables": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay finds neutral with the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the scotch depth settles into the seasonal vegetables, and the heather brightens the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Bruichladdich|Shrimp Bisque": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets this rich, creamy seafood soup's sweet-briny depth over dairy-rich base. Cocktail against a creamy seafood soup — acidity and lift cut the dairy base while the spirit carries its own weight. Strong — bright cuts rich.",
  "Bruichladdich|Shrimp Cocktail": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets this delicate seafood starter's briny-fresh sweetness. Whiskey's oak and caramel are only going to land if the starter can carry weight — check the plate. Strong for rich-umami starters.",
  "Bruichladdich|Swordfish": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Bruichladdich on the steak course instead.",
  "Bruichladdich|The Tomahawk": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay underclubs the Tomahawk's theatrical bone-in marbling and smoky char -- the bottle's register lands at a lower tier than the cut deserves. The plate deserves Corazon Stagg, Opus One, or George T. Stagg, not a scotch. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Bruichladdich on another course instead.",
  "Bruichladdich|Tomato Basil": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the scotch backbone matches the tomato basil, and the honey rounds the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Bruichladdich|Truffle Fries": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets this earthy, umami-packed side's mushroom-and-truffle depth. Whiskey's oak and sweetness mirror the side's dairy and umami depth. A headliner match — context-driven peak. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Bruichladdich|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Bruichladdich for the steak course.",
  "Bruichladdich|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay reads alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the scotch backbone matches the curry, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the bowl. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|1792 Small Batch": "1792 Small Batch with Brussels + Belly — Barton small-batch meets maple-glazed pork belly. The spicy-sweet 1792 character cuts the glaze with high-rye balance. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|1792 Sweet Wheat": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet sweet-wheat. Distinctive wheat-sweetness and maple find each other; sweet-on-sweet that works. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|1881 Napa Valley": "Napa Cab — dark cherry, blackcurrant, mocha, smooth tannin. The approachable body handles pork-belly fat and the mocha plays against charred brussels. Strong entry Napa Cab for Brussels and Belly — reliable step-up pour cuts through the rich starter confidently.",
  "Brussels and Belly|2 James Gin": "2 James Gin's crisp char-juniper botanicals reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals echo the green plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|A Midnight's Winter Dram": "A Midnight's Winter Dram with Brussels + Belly — rare limited-release meets maple-glazed pork belly. The boutique-craft character cuts the glaze with rare-release distinctiveness. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Aberlour 16": "Aberlour 16 with Brussels + Belly — 16yr double-matured Speyside against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Aberlour 16's balance meets the glaze; Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask is the featured match.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Adictivo Cristalino": "Adictivo Cristalino's añejo-pour depth finds neutral with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the oak-aged tequila body threads the pork-belly plate, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; brightness can cut the glaze but wheated bourbons sit better with this dish.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Adictivo Reposado": "Adictivo Reposado with Brussels + Belly — extended-aged reposado against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; the aged character is a different register than the dish calls for.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Alexander Valley Chardonnay": "Alexander Valley Chardonnay's apple-butter acidity reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the vanilla amplifies the dessert sugar. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Alexander Valley Cyrus": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Alexander Valley Homestead Red": "Alexander Valley Sonoma Bordeaux blend — plum, blackberry, mocha, soft tannin, smooth. The soft tannin cuts pork-belly fat and the blackberry plays against charred brussels. Strong crowd-pleaser Bordeaux blend for Brussels and Belly — Sonoma softness on the rich starter.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Amaro Nonino": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet grappa-based amaro. Works; Friulian amaro cuts the glaze's sweetness with digestif brightness.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Ancho Reyes": "Ancho Reyes's ancho-chile-smoke sweetness plays cleanly against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the sweet character sits at digestif register, and the smoke meets the umami depth. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Angel's Envy": "Angel's Envy: port-finished Kentucky bourbon, the flagship. Excellent on Brussels and Belly; port-finish-sweetness amplifies maple-glaze at flagship register — textbook AE-on-Brussels. Gold standard; pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Angel's Envy Cask Strength": "Angel's Envy Cask Strength's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight sits alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the bourbon body sits with the pork-belly plate, and the vanilla balances the char-and-fat. Works; the pour's assertiveness is a bit much for the soup but doesn't clash; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Angel's Envy Triple Cask": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the bourbon weight handles the pork-belly plate, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Works; the complex character gives the dessert a refined frame; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Aperol": "Aperol with Brussels + Belly — soft orange-rhubarb against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; Aperol's orange meets the glaze's sweetness rather than cutting it.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Asparagus": "The asparagus alongside Brussels + Belly -- the bright green spear rests against the glazed pork starter, and the bitter herb edge cuts the umami fat. Works; both sides hold at neutral register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Au Gratin Potatoes and Brussels + Belly together -- the cheese cream holds beside the charred-sprouts-and-belly opener. Works; the two sides share the meal without competing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Averna Amaro": "Averna with Brussels + Belly — Sicilian amaro against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; caramel-orange doubles the dish's sweetness; Nonino cuts it better.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Aviation": "Aviation's crisp almond-cherry build plays cleanly against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Aviation Gin": "Aviation Gin's floral-juniper botanicals leans against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Avion 44": "Avion 44 with Brussels + Belly — 44-month aged meets maple-glazed pork belly. Works; extended Avion over-specified for small plate.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Avion Silver": "Avion Silver's blanco-tequila or blanco-tequila register leans against Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the pork-belly plate, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bacardi Rum": "Bacardi Rum's crisp workhorse-clean character reads alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the light-rum body cuts the pork-belly plate, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Baileys Irish Cream": "Baileys Irish Cream's sweet liqueur character clashes with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Baileys Irish Cream on the steak course instead.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Baker's": "Baker's with Brussels + Belly — 107-proof Beam small-batch meets maple-glazed pork belly. The high-proof rich vanilla cuts the glaze with small-batch authority. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Balvenie 12 American Oak": "Balvenie 12 Am Oak with Brussels + Belly — first-fill American Oak Speyside against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Balvenie's vanilla meets the glaze with sweet-oak resonance.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet tropical-sweet Caribbean-rum-cask Speyside. The rum-cask brown-sugar-and-tropical-sweetness meets maple glaze with featured resonance — maple-and-rum-cask is the textbook pairing, and the Caribbean Cask brings it uniquely in the Sherried Speyside cluster. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Balvenie 16 Single Barrel": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel with Brussels + Belly — single-barrel Speyside against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Balvenie 16's depth meets the glaze at collector register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Balvenie 21 Portwood": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with Brussels + Belly — 21yr port-cask Speyside against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Portwood handles the glaze but Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask's rum-cask maple-bridge is the featured match.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bardstown Château Laboude": "Bardstown Château Laboude's soft-oak bourbon body leans against Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the oak depth lays under the pork-belly plate, and the vanilla brightens the grilled char-edge. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for a side — save the collector bottle for the main; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bardstown Discovery #6": "Bardstown Discovery #6 with Brussels + Belly — Bardstown Discovery meets maple-glazed pork belly. The multi-distillery complexity cuts the glaze with craft-blender distinctiveness. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bardstown Founders KBS": "Bardstown Founders KBS with Brussels + Belly — stout-barrel finish meets maple-glazed pork belly. The KBS coffee and stout notes cut the glaze with beer-barrel distinctiveness. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bardstown Foursquare": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet Foursquare rum-cask Bardstown. Bardstown Foursquare is the featured exotic-cask-pork-belly pairing — Barbados rum-cask brown-sugar amplifies maple glaze with tropical-finish intensity. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bardstown Fusion #7": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet Fusion blend. Bardstown own-plus-sourced cuts the glaze with fusion-blender distinctiveness. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel": "Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel with Brussels + Belly — Rishi's-picked Bardstown meets maple-glazed pork belly. The retailer-selected single-barrel cuts the glaze with curated Bardstown distinctiveness. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Basil Hayden's": "Basil Hayden's with Brussels + Belly — rye spice meets maple-glazed pork belly sweetness. The 80-proof lightness doesn't compete with the small plate; it balances the dish's richness with pepper and brightness. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Basil Hayden's 10 Year": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with Brussels + Belly — aged rye spice meets maple-glazed pork belly. The 10-year gives the pairing backbone that standard Basil Hayden's doesn't; a refined small-plate pour. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Basil Hayden's Malted Rye": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with Brussels + Belly — spicy-sweet malted rye meets maple-glazed pork belly. The bready character picks up the Brussels' char and the pork belly's maple; distinctive and specifically Basil Hayden's Malted Rye. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the bourbon depth settles into the pork-belly plate, and the vanilla brightens the grilled char-edge. Works; boutique-sourced wasted on salad; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Basil Hayden's Toast": "Basil Hayden's Toast with Brussels + Belly — toasted caramel meets maple-glazed pork belly. The toast-finish echoes the dish's sweetness without the pour going heavy; a clean, light, signature-flavored small-plate pairing. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bee's Knees": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the honey rounds the grilled char. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Beefeater Gin": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals leans against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals echo the green plate. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Beignets": "Brussels and Belly and the beignets -- savory-into-sweet, the classic close lands intact. Works; the meal closes cleanly from the side.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Belvedere Vodka": "Belvedere Vodka's bold Polish-rye-clean neutrality leans against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Blade & Bow": "Blade & Bow with Brussels + Belly — Stitzel-Weller revival blend meets maple-glazed pork belly. The blend's honey threads through the dish's maple; a heritage-story small-plate pairing. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Blanton's Gold": "Blanton's Gold with Brussels + Belly — 103-proof Blanton's meets maple-glazed pork belly. The richer profile cuts the glaze with more authority than Original. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Blanton's Original": "Blanton's Original with Brussels + Belly — 93-proof single-barrel meets maple-glazed pork belly. The benchmark honey-and-caramel threads through the glaze distinctively. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Blanton's Straight from the Barrel": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet cask-strength Blanton's. Blanton's SfB meets the glaze with distinctive honey-vanilla character at cask-strength. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Blood Oath Pact 10": "Blood Oath Pact 10 with Brussels + Belly — 10th-Pact milestone meets maple-glazed pork belly. The decennial-release character cuts the glaze with milestone-collector distinctiveness. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Blood Oath Pact 8": "Blood Oath Pact 8 with Brussels + Belly — Pact 8 meets maple-glazed pork belly. The Mizunara-finish character cuts the glaze with master-blender distinctiveness. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Blood Oath Pact 9": "Blood Oath Pact 9 with Brussels + Belly — Pact 9 meets maple-glazed pork belly. The wine-cask fruit character cuts the glaze with master-blender distinctiveness. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bluecoat Gin": "Bluecoat Gin's char-citrus botanicals plays cleanly against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; safe call, no friction. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bodega Noemia A Lisa": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bombay Dry Gin": "Bombay Dry Gin's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals plays cleanly against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bombay Sapphire Gin": "Bombay Sapphire Gin's crisp London-Dry-citrus botanicals reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bone Marrow": "The bone marrow opens the meal, Brussels + Belly with the entree -- the beefy bone-broth richness meets the maple-glazed belly. Strong; both items.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bone-In Filet": "The bone-in filet alongside Brussels + Belly -- the 14oz bone-enhanced cut's deeper marrow character meets the maple-pork-belly glaze, sweet-savory richness against bone-deepened beef. Strong; the side reads built for the bone-in version.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Booker's": "Booker's with Brussels + Belly — cask-strength Beam against maple-glazed pork belly. Excellent; Booker's 125+ proof meets the glaze's sweetness with barrel-proof intensity — the bourbon that originated the category meets one of its featured dessert-adjacent pairings.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Botanist Gin": "Botanist Gin's crisp Islay-gentle-botanical botanicals leans against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bowdie's Old Fashioned": "Buffalo Trace, rum-soaked cherries, orange, bitters, large cube. The bourbon's vanilla-caramel profile meets pork belly's rendered fat and brussels char; cherry sweetness bridges the sweet-savory glaze. Peak pairing when guest wants whiskey alongside the belly's smoke-and-sear depth. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark": "Bowdie's Private Select Maker's Mark with Brussels + Belly — house-pick wheated depth against maple-glazed pork belly. The stave selection gives this pairing a signature Bowdie's character; richer than standard Maker's, more specific than Cellar Aged. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bowman Brothers Small Batch": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet Virginia-aged small-batch. Smooth character handles the dish at everyday register. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bowmore 12": "Bowmore 12 with Brussels + Belly — sherry-finish honeyed notes meet the maple glaze cleanly. Gentler peat than Lagavulin or Laphroaig lets the dish's sweetness still lead. A guest-friendly Islay pour with a savory-sweet small plate. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Braida Montebruna Barbera": "Piedmont Monferrato Barbera d'Asti — Braida benchmark, juicy dark cherry, blackberry, high acid, low tannin. The high acid cuts pork-belly fat and the blackberry plays against charred brussels. Strong benchmark Barbera for Brussels and Belly — food-wine acidity on the rich starter.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the pairing reads at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Broccoli Cheddar": "Broccoli Cheddar and Brussels + Belly -- the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream meets Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: two rich courses on the same plate, the table earns its substance. Works; no conflict however the table orders them.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Broccolini": "The broccolini alongside Brussels + Belly -- the lemon-finished broccolini holds beside the charred-sprouts-and-belly opener. Works; both sides hold at neutral register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bruichladdich": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight. Whiskey's oak and sweetness mirror the side's dairy and umami depth. Works cleanly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Buffalo Trace": "Buffalo Trace with Brussels + Belly — flagship bourbon meets maple-glazed pork belly. BT's caramel and oak handle the dish's sweetness without over-matching; a reliable, clean small-plate pour. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Buffalo Trace Cream": "Buffalo Trace Cream's sweet liqueur character doubles down on Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet liqueur and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no contrast left. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Buffalo Trace Cream for the steak course.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Bulleit Bourbon": "Bulleit Bourbon with Brussels + Belly — high-rye spice meets maple-glazed pork belly. The rye cuts the glaze's sweetness in a way wheated can't; a distinctive small-plate pairing at the approachable tier. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Butternut Squash": "The butternut squash alongside Brussels + Belly -- savory-into-sweet, the classic close lands intact. Works; the table can build them in order or together.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Cade Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Camarena Tequila": "Camarena Tequila with Brussels + Belly — value reposado against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; approachable agave cuts the glaze but not marquee.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Campari": "Campari with Brussels + Belly — bitter orange-rhubarb against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; the orange-bitter cuts the glaze's sweetness with aperitivo lift.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Canadian Club": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet heritage grain-forward Canadian. Strong; Canadian Club's traditional character meets the glaze at heritage register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Canadian Club 43 Year": "CC 43 Year with Brussels + Belly — ultra-premium aged Canadian against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; CC 43 Year's aged character meets the glaze at collector register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Captain Morgan Rum": "Captain Morgan Rum's cane-and-lime lift with rum brightness finds neutral with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the unaged-cane body sits with the pork-belly plate, and the rum-and-lime thread plays against the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Caribou Crossing": "Caribou Crossing with Brussels + Belly — Sazerac single-barrel Canadian against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; Caribou Crossing's hand-selected character meets the glaze at craft register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Carrot Cake": "Brussels + Belly and the carrot cake -- Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts hands off cleanly to the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: savory-into-sweet, the classic close lands intact. Works; sequence them or share the table, no clash.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Casa LBV Port": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness doubles down on Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet wine and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no foil. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Casamigos Mezcal": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and crispy pork belly meet Clooney-Gerber mezcal. Excellent; Casamigos Mezcal's polished-smoke rides the glaze-and-belly fat at gateway register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon": "Napa Rutherford Cab — concentrated black fruit, cocoa, mocha, velvety tannin. The opulent body handles pork-belly fat and the cocoa-mocha plays against charred brussels directly. Peak iconic Napa Cab for Brussels and Belly — the 2020 vintage opulence frames the rich starter with recognizable Napa character. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Chambord": "Chambord's sweet liqueur character clashes with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Chambord on the steak course instead.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Cheesecake": "Brussels and Belly and the cheesecake -- the entree yields to the dessert, the meal arc reads on-key. Works; clean transition or together if the table wants.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Chilean Seabass": "The seabass alongside Brussels + Belly -- the seabass' buttery seabass flesh meets Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts cleanly. Strong; the pairing lands at register without strain against the main.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Chocolate Brownie": "Brussels and Belly and the brownie -- savory-into-sweet, the classic close lands intact. Works; the meal closes cleanly from the side.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Chocolate Cake": "Brussels and Belly and the chocolate cake -- protein hands off to dessert, the close builds without conflict. Works; clean transition or together if the table wants.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Chopin Vodka": "Chopin Vodka's bold char-cream neutrality holds with the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the vanilla amplifies the dessert sugar. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Christian Bros Brandy": "Christian Bros Brandy's eau-de-vie body with oak leans against Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the brandy depth wraps the pork-belly plate, and the dried-fruit note underlines the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Château Batailley": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Château Beaucastel": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Château Gombaude-Guillot": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A capable pair; richness aligns if not perfectly. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Château Haut Segottes": "Saint-Émilion right-bank Bordeaux — plum, dark cherry, truffle, clayey earth, soft tannin. The soft tannin cuts pork-belly fat and the truffle plays against charred brussels. Strong right-bank Bordeaux for Brussels and Belly — Merlot-led roundness cuts through the rich starter.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Château de Rouillac": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Clam Chowder": "Clam Chowder and Brussels + Belly -- the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base meets Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: cream meets protein, the meal builds with weight. Works; no conflict however the table orders them.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Clase Azul Anejo": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed meets Clase Azul Anejo. Excellent; caramel-dried-fruit-maple-butterscotch rides the maple glaze at ultra-premium register — the sherry-butt finish amplifies the glaze's sweetness.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Clase Azul Durango": "Clase Azul Durango with Brussels + Belly — ceremonial extra añejo meets maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Durango ceremony over-specified for small plate.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Clase Azul Gold": "Clase Azul Gold with Brussels + Belly — 24K gold blend meets maple-glazed pork belly. Works; ceremonial over-specified.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet Clase Azul Guerrero. Excellent; the fruit-forward smoke rides the glaze at luxury-mezcal register — Guerrero's softer character finds the maple thread.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Clase Azul Plata": "Clase Azul Plata's silky Jalisco blanco with ceramic-decanter presentation sits alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the blanco-tequila body matches the pork-belly plate, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Clase Azul Reposado": "Clase Azul Reposado with Brussels + Belly — premium reposado against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; the smoothness doesn't drive the pairing but the theatrics do.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Clase Azul Ultra": "Clase Azul Ultra with Brussels + Belly — 5-year top-tier meets maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Ultra over-specified for small plate.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Clermont Steep": "Clermont Steep with Brussels + Belly — Beam wheated meets maple-glazed pork belly. The wheated profile handles the glaze's sweetness with approachable warmth. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Clos Petit Ona Grenache": "Roussillon Southern France Grenache — Clos Petit Ona, wild raspberry, kirsch, garrigue, warm spice, medium body. The warm spice plays with pork-belly fat and the garrigue matches brussels-char bitterness. Strong Southern-French for brussels-and-belly — Mediterranean polish on fat-and-char.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Codigo 1530 Rosa": "Codigo 1530 Rosa with Brussels + Belly — Cabernet-cask rosé against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; the wine fruit doesn't align cleanly with the maple.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Contratto Vermouth": "Contratto Vermouth's gentian-driven cut sits alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the herbal cut works the pork-belly plate, and the amaro backbone frames the side. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Corazon Blanco": "Corazon Blanco's clean silver register finds neutral with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the unaged body brightens the pork-belly plate, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Corazon Reposado": "Corazon Reposado with Brussels + Belly — highland agave against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; the brightness cuts the glaze but pork belly earns fuller-bodied pours.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Corazon Sazerac": "Corazon Sazerac's agave-pepper character sits with the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the añejo weight settles into the rich side, and the oak underlines the char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Corazon Stagg": "Corazon Stagg's aged-agave character leans against Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the barrel-rested body handles the pork-belly plate, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Strong; accessible agave cuts the dairy at the entry register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Corazon Weller": "★ Corazon Weller's agave-char character anchors against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the añejo weight settles into the rich side, and the vanilla amplifies the dessert sugar. Gold standard; pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Corazón del Sol Malbec": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Corpse Reviver": "Corpse Reviver's anise-citrus build reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Courvoisier Cognac": "Courvoisier Cognac's classic VS cognac reads alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the aged-grape brandy body sits with the pork-belly plate, and the dried-fruit note underlines the side. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Cowboy Ribeye": "Cowboy Ribeye with Brussels + Belly -- the 26oz cap-and-fat richness meets the maple-glazed pork belly, the smoke from the grilled cut threading the glaze's sweet edge. Strong; the side mirrors the cut's indulgence note for note.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Cragganmore 12": "Cragganmore 12 with Brussels + Belly — Diageo Classic Malt against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Cragganmore's subtle smoke finds the glaze with distinctive character.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Creamed Spinach": "Brussels + Belly and the creamed spinach across the plate -- the sweet-savory build holds beside the rich greens. Works; safe call when the table doubles up on sides.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Creamy Potato": "The potato soup alongside Brussels + Belly -- cream and protein share the meal, the build reads full. Works; the table can build them in order or together.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Creme Brulee": "Brussels + Belly alongside the brulee -- the savory course resolves into sugar, the meal closes with contrast. Works; the contrast holds, neither course overshadows the other.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée": "Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée's Willamette Pinot elegance reads alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the silky red-fruit body wraps the pork-belly plate, and the cherry-fruit frames the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Crown Royal": "Crown Royal with Brussels + Belly — smooth Canadian icon against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; Crown Royal's vanilla-honey meets the glaze at crowd-pleasing register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Cucumber Gimlet": "Hendrick's muddled with cucumber, lime, ginger syrup, topped with soda. Cucumber-light cocktail for a pork-belly-forward side — the weights mismatch. Keep the Gimlet for lighter seafood; lean into Negroni or bourbon cocktails here. Avoid; the call reads off-register; recommend an alternative.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Dalmore 12": "Dalmore 12 with Brussels + Belly — sherry-finish Highland against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Dalmore's Matusalem-cask dried-fruit meets the glaze at Highland-luxury register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge": "Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge's crisp earth-mineral tannin leans against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Darioush Cabernet Franc": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Detroit City Gin": "Detroit City Gin's Detroit urban-craft gin finds neutral with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the city-distilled juniper frames the pork-belly plate, and the local-spirit character meets the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
