  "Brussels and Belly|Dewar's White Label": "Dewar's White Label with Brussels + Belly — Highland entry blend against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; Dewar's White's honey-vanilla meets the glaze at benchmark register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Disaronno": "Disaronno's sweet liqueur character doubles down on Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet liqueur and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no contrast left. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Disaronno on the steak course instead.",
