  "Brussels and Belly|E.H. Taylor Small Batch": "E.H. Taylor Small Batch with Brussels + Belly — bonded 100-proof meets maple-glazed pork belly. The oak-forward richness cuts the glaze with authority. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Eagle Rare 10 Year": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet Eagle Rare 10 Year's oak and spice. Structured enough to frame the dish's sweetness without being outsweetened. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Eastern Kille Dry Gin": "Eastern Kille Dry Gin's crisp char-citrus botanicals stays alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Brussels and Belly|El Cabo": "El Cabo with Brussels + Belly — boutique reposado against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; craft character doesn't compete with dish density.",
  "Brussels and Belly|El Mayor Extra Anejo": "El Mayor Extra Anejo with Brussels + Belly — aged El Mayor meets maple-glazed pork belly. Works; accessible aged composes with the plate.",
  "Brussels and Belly|El Mayor Reposado": "El Mayor Reposado with Brussels + Belly — value reposado against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; the agave cuts the glaze but the pairing isn't marquee.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Elephant Gin": "Elephant Gin's crisp char-herbal botanicals plays cleanly against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs frame the grilled char. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Elijah Craig 18 Year": "Elijah Craig 18 with Brussels + Belly — 18yr HH single-barrel against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; EC 18's aged character meets the glaze at aged-HH register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Elijah Craig Private Barrel": "Elijah Craig Private Barrel with Brussels + Belly — house-pick single-barrel meets maple-glazed pork belly. The curated profile cuts the glaze at the private-selection register. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Elijah Craig Single Barrel": "Elijah Craig Single Barrel with Brussels + Belly — single-barrel Heaven Hill meets maple-glazed pork belly. The 94-proof oak-spice cuts the glaze cleanly. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Elijah Craig Small Batch": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet spicy-sweet small-batch. Oak cuts the glaze's sweetness cleanly; grown-up bourbon for the small plate. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Elijah Craig Straight Rye": "Elijah Craig Straight Rye with Brussels + Belly — 94-proof HH rye meets maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; HH rye spice cuts the glaze distinctly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Elk Cove Five Mountain": "Elk Cove Five Mountain's cherry-clove tannin stays alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice lifts the green plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Elk Cove Pinot Blanc": "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc's apple-char acidity plays cleanly against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the mineral edge frames the green plate. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Elmer T. Lee": "Elmer T. Lee with Brussels + Belly — Buffalo Trace single-barrel meets maple-glazed pork belly. The smooth balance handles the dish's sweetness cleanly. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Empress 1908 Gin": "Empress 1908 Gin's bold anise-butter botanicals leans against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Epoch Ingenuity": "Paso Robles Rhône blend — Epoch Ingenuity, Templeton Gap Syrah-Grenache-Mourvèdre, blackberry, smoked meat, olive, crushed pepper, medium tannin. The medium tannin cuts pork-belly fat and the smoked meat echoes brussels-char bitterness. Strong Paso-Rhône for brussels-and-belly — Epoch smoke-on-char match.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Espresso Martini": "Tito's, espresso, Grind liqueur, Averna amaro, vanilla syrup, Angostura. The coffee and Averna's bitter edge cut pork-belly fat and vanilla syrup plays against the belly's glaze. Strong unconventional pairing for the sweet-savory belly build when guest wants coffee-forward.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Espresso Old Fashioned": "Buffalo Trace, Buffalo Bourbon Cream, Frangelico, espresso, brown sugar, Angostura. Brown sugar meets the belly's glaze directly; espresso cuts the rendered pork fat and Frangelico bridges the brussels char. Peak cocktail for the sweet-savory belly build.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Evening Land Seven Springs": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this elegant red's cherry-bright, silky-tannin frame. The elegant red's acidity cuts the dairy fat while its cherry lifts the earthy umami. Works — clean if not dominant.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the pairing reads at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Far Niente Chardonnay": "Far Niente Chardonnay's bold butter-char acidity holds with the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Faroe Island Salmon": "Faroe Island Salmon with Brussels + Belly -- the buttery salmon sits cleanly with the sweet-savory build. Strong; reliable side for the salmon.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Faust Napa Valley Cabernet": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the pairing reads at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía": "Galicia Ribeira Sacra Mencía — Fento, fresh red cherry, slate minerality, light body, high acid. The high acid cuts pork-belly fat and the red-cherry lifts against brussels-char. Strong Galician-Mencía for brussels-and-belly — bright-acid contrast on the fat-and-char side.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Fernet Branca": "Fernet Branca with Brussels + Belly — nuclear bitter against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; Branca cuts the glaze's sweetness harder than sipping amari and makes the side read savory.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Fernet Menta": "Fernet Menta with Brussels + Belly — mint Fernet against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; the mint cools the glaze, though Branca cuts it harder.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Filet Mignon": "Filet Mignon with Brussels + Belly -- the 10oz tenderloin's lean butter meets the maple-glazed pork belly over charred sprouts, the glaze lending the richness the lean cut leaves room for. Strong; the side rounds out the filet's clean register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Fireball Whisky": "Fireball Whisky's sweet liqueur character doubles down on Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet liqueur and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no contrast left. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Fireball Whisky for the steak course.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Fisher Unity Pinot Noir": "Fisher Unity Pinot Noir's cherry-earth tannin sits beside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice lifts the green plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Four Roses Small Batch Select": "Four Roses Small Batch Select with Brussels + Belly — 104-proof premium 4R meets maple-glazed pork belly. The concentrated blend cuts the glaze with premium small-batch authority. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Four Roses Yellow Label": "Four Roses Yellow Label with Brussels + Belly — 80-proof floral-honey against maple-glazed pork belly. The light body doesn't compete; a friendly, approachable small-plate pairing. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Fox & Oden": "Fox & Oden with Brussels + Belly — craft small-batch meets maple-glazed pork belly. The boutique character handles the dish at the craft-spirit register. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Fox & Oden Double Oaked": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet Detroit-brand Double Oaked. Works; Fox & Oden's intensified-caramel meets the glaze at Double-Oaked register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Frangelico": "Frangelico's Piedmont hazelnut depth to mocha at after-dinner register clashes with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Frangelico lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Freemark Abbey Bosché": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Brussels and Belly|French 75": "French 75's citrus-earth build plays cleanly against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the vanilla amplifies the dessert sugar. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|French Onion": "French Onion and Brussels + Belly -- the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth meets Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: protein meets umami, the table builds substance. Works; no conflict however the table orders them.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Frias Block 5": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Brussels and Belly|G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo": "Piedmont Barolo DOCG Nebbiolo — G.D. Vajra Albe La Morra, tar, rose petal, dried cherry, firm tannic backbone, high acid. The firm tannin cuts pork-belly fat and the tar plays against charred brussels. Strong classic Barolo for Brussels and Belly — Vajra's exceptional range on the rich starter.",
  "Brussels and Belly|G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti": "Piedmont sweet sparkling — peach, honey, floral. The sweetness fights the brussels' bitterness and the cumin-paprika lardon rub; wrong wine on every axis. Route Moscato to dessert where it belongs. Avoid; the pairing fights at the table — point the guest elsewhere.",
  "Brussels and Belly|G4 Blanco": "G4 Blanco's silver-spirit lift with agave-citrus edge leans against Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the pork-belly plate, and the bright blanco register underlines the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Brussels and Belly|G4 High Proof": "G4 High Proof with Brussels + Belly — high-proof reposado against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; the bold pour cuts the glaze but is slightly much for the small plate.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Garavogue Irish Whiskey": "Garavogue with Brussels + Belly — western Ireland craft Irish against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; Garavogue meets the glaze at craft-Irish register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|George T. Stagg": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet 130+ proof BTAC. Strong; GTS meets the glaze at collector register, though Stagg Jr. handles this pairing more economically.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon": "Oakville Cab — blackcurrant, dark cherry, graphite, toasted oak, firm tannin. The dense body handles pork-belly fat and the graphite-oak plays against charred brussels. Strong Oakville Cab for Brussels and Belly — Napa's golden-strip structure cuts the rich starter.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Ghost Block Zinfandel": "Napa Oakville Zinfandel — Ghost Block, ripe jammy fruit, blackberry preserves, cracked pepper, full body, medium tannin. The cracked pepper cuts pork-belly fat and the jammy fruit plays with brussels-char bitterness. Peak California-Zin for brussels-and-belly — bold Napa handles fat-and-char. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Glenfiddich 12": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet ex-bourbon-cask Speyside. Works; Fiddich's honey-apple meets the glaze at approachable register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Glenfiddich 14": "Glenfiddich 14 with Brussels + Belly — Bourbon Barrel Reserve against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Fiddich 14's baking-spice meets the glaze with more dimension than the 12.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Glenfiddich 18": "Glenfiddich 18 with Brussels + Belly — Oloroso-marriage Speyside against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Fiddich 18's dried-fruit finds the glaze naturally.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with Brussels + Belly — 23yr champagne-cask Speyside against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Gran Cru's brioche meets the glaze at refined register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Glenglassaugh 12": "Glenglassaugh 12 with Brussels + Belly — tropical-coastal Highland against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Glenglassaugh 12's tropical-fruit meets the glaze at distinctive register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Glenlivet 12": "Glenlivet 12 with Brussels + Belly — honey-pineapple Speyside against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Glenlivet's honey meets the glaze at benchmark register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Glenmorangie 10": "Glenmorangie 10 with Brussels + Belly — honey-floral Highland against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Glenmorangie 10's honeysuckle meets the glaze at entry-Highland register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Glenmorangie 18": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet aged Glenmorangie with Oloroso finish. Works; Glenmorangie 18's Oloroso dried-fruit meets the glaze at premium register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Graham's 10 Year Tawny": "Graham's 10 Year Tawny's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Graham's 10 Year Tawny belongs on the steak course.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Graham's 20 Year Tawny": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth doubles down on Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet wine and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no foil. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Graham's 20 Year Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Graham's 2017 Vintage Port": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight doubles down on Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet wine and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no foil. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Gran Patron Platinum": "Gran Patron Platinum's unaged silver-spirit body sits alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the silver-spirit register lifts the pork-belly plate, and the unaged-cane note plays against the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Grand Marnier": "Grand Marnier's sweet liqueur character doubles down on Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet liqueur and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no contrast left. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Grand Marnier for the steak course.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Gray Whale Gin": "Gray Whale Gin's bold citrus-herbal botanicals reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Green Chartreuse": "Green Chartreuse's aperitivo herb-and-bitter cut leans against Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the herbal cut works the pork-belly plate, and the amaro backbone frames the side. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Grey Goose Vodka": "Grey Goose Vodka's crisp French-wheat-soft neutrality leans against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Grilled Caesar": "The Caesar and Brussels + Belly on the same meal -- umami plays against the protein, the table earns its depth. Works; sequence or share, the build holds.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Gumbo": "The gumbo and Brussels + Belly on the same meal -- heat lifts the rich course, the table earns the warmer note. Works; sequence or share, the build holds.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Brussels and Belly|HDW 100 Vodka": "HDW 100 Vodka's char-herbal neutrality sits alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the herbs frame the grilled char. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Hakushu 12 Year": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character sits alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the Japanese whisky balance frames the pork-belly plate, and the green-fruit edge brightens the side. Works; the blend's complexity is underused by the salad; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with Brussels + Belly — BT single-barrel meets maple-glazed pork belly. The complex profile cuts the glaze with Blanton's-adjacent character. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Hangar 1 Vodka": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Head Fake": "Wheatley vodka, limoncello, triple sec, lemon, simple syrup, sugar rim. Sweet lemon-drop style clashes with cumin-smoked-paprika lardons; the rub's spice profile fights every component of the cocktail. Route to dessert. Avoid; pair this elsewhere on the menu.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Heaven Hill 20 Year": "Heaven Hill 20 Year with Brussels + Belly — 20yr HH against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; HH 20's aged character meets the glaze at collector register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond": "Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond with Brussels + Belly — 100-proof bond meets maple-glazed pork belly. BIB's structure handles the dish's sweetness with more grip than Wellers' wheated softness. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Heaven's Door 10 Year": "Heaven's Door 10 Year with Brussels + Belly — 10-year 100-proof meets maple-glazed pork belly. The aged depth cuts the glaze with premium Dylan-brand character. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Heitz Martha's Vineyard": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A capable pair; richness aligns if not perfectly. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Heitz Trailside Vineyard": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Hendricks Flora Adora": "Hendricks Flora Adora's crisp char-elderflower botanicals plays cleanly against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the honey rounds the grilled char. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Hendricks Gin": "Hendricks Gin's crisp cucumber-rose botanicals sits alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Hendricks Grand Cabaret": "Hendricks Grand Cabaret's bold anise-char botanicals plays cleanly against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the anise frames the char. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Hendricks Neptunia": "Hendricks Neptunia's crisp anise-brine botanicals stays alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs frame the grilled char. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Hendricks Orbium": "Hendricks Orbium's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals sits beside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Hennessy Cognac": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac sits alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the aged-grape brandy body sits with the pork-belly plate, and the rancio register softens the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with Brussels + Belly — bonded 10-year HH meets maple-glazed pork belly. The aged BIB weight cuts the glaze with authority. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Hibiki Japanese Harmony": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony finds neutral with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the Mizunara-influenced register sits with the pork-belly plate, and the precision rounds the side. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Brussels + Belly alongside the honey carrots -- the maple-glazed belly runs alongside the honey-roasted carrot, and the honey rounds the grilled char. Works; both sides hold at neutral register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|House Wedge": "The wedge alongside Brussels + Belly -- protein meets umami, the table builds substance. Works; the table can build them in order or together.",
  "Brussels and Belly|I.W. Harper 15 Year": "I.W. Harper 15 with Brussels + Belly — historic-Kentucky 15yr against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; IW Harper 15's cherry-oak meets the glaze at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Il Colle Prosecco Superiore": "Il Colle Prosecco Superiore's crisp apple-citrus acidity reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Inhibited": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this coffee-driven cocktail's bitter roast, rich texture, and dessert-adjacent sweetness. Coffee cocktail against a savory plate — wrong register entirely. Works only as a transition pour.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Inverroche Gin": "Inverroche Gin's crisp earth-floral botanicals reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs frame the grilled char. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Iron Fish Gin": "Iron Fish Gin's cask-strength citrus-earth botanicals reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the honey rounds the grilled char. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks": "Ironfish Bourbon Mezcal Casks with Brussels + Belly — Iron Fish MI mezcal-cask bourbon against maple-glazed pork belly. Excellent; Ironfish Mezcal's smoky character meets the glaze with distinctive mezcal-smoke + maple-sweetness resonance.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Isaac Bowman Port Finish": "Isaac Bowman Port Finish's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the pork-belly plate, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Works; neutral companion; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Brussels and Belly|J Davies Ferrington Vineyards": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards's cherry-coffee tannin sits alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the coffee meets the caramel. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon": "J. Davies — Diamond Mountain Cab with dark fruit, graphite, mineral, firm tannin. The structured body handles pork-belly fat and the graphite plays against charred brussels. Strong mountain Cab for Brussels and Belly — volcanic complexity cuts the rich starter with Schramsberg provenance depth.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Jack Daniel's 12 Year": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with Brussels + Belly — aged charcoal-mellowed Tennessee against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; JD 12's aged vanilla-caramel meets the glaze at premium register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Jack Daniel's Bonded": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with Brussels + Belly — 100-proof Tennessee against maple-glazed pork belly. Excellent; JD Bonded's backbone cuts the glaze harder than Old No. 7 can.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Jack Daniel's Old No. 7": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7 with Brussels + Belly — charcoal-mellowed Tennessee against maple-glazed pork belly. Excellent; Old No. 7's vanilla-caramel meets the maple glaze with iconic Tennessee resonance — maple-and-charcoal is a featured textbook pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Jack Daniel's Sinatra Select": "JD Sinatra Select with Brussels + Belly — Sinatra Barrels Tennessee against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; Sinatra Select's richer oak meets the glaze at Sinatra-tribute register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Jameson Irish Whiskey": "Jameson with Brussels + Belly — smooth Irish against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; Jameson's triple-distilled sherry+bourbon-cask meets the glaze at entry register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir": "Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir's cherry-earth tannin stays alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis": "Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis's crisp apple-char acidity reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; capable alongside. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E.": "Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E. with Brussels + Belly — limited-edition ocean-finish against maple-glazed pork belly. Excellent; Marian McLain L.E. meets the glaze at collector register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Jefferson's Ocean Voyage 23": "Jefferson's Ocean Voyage 23 with Brussels + Belly — sea-aged bourbon against maple-glazed pork belly. Excellent; Voyage 23's ocean-motion character meets the glaze with distinctive ocean-finish story.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Jefferson's Reserve": "Jefferson's Reserve with Brussels + Belly — blended bourbon meets maple-glazed pork belly. The elegance handles the dish's sweetness without the Wellers' wheat-on-maple doubling; a different logic for the same plate. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Jefferson's Reserve VR Twin Oak": "Jefferson's Reserve VR Twin Oak with Brussels + Belly — Twin Oak depth against maple-glazed pork belly. The complex oak frames the dish's sweetness without the doubling of wheated pours; sophisticated. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Jim Beam Black Label": "Jim Beam Black Label with Brussels + Belly — 86-proof aged Beam meets maple-glazed pork belly. The oak cuts the glaze's sweetness more cleanly than White Label manages; a solid small-plate pairing. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Jim Beam White Label": "Jim Beam White Label with Brussels + Belly — 80-proof Beam against maple-glazed pork belly. Approachable and capable; the entry tier at work. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Johnnie Walker Black": "JW Black with Brussels + Belly — 12yr balanced JW against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; JW Black's balanced smoke-and-sherry cuts the glaze at premium-blend register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Johnnie Walker Blue": "JW Blue with Brussels + Belly — luxury collector JW against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; JW Blue is over-specified for the side — save the rare-cask bottle for the protein course.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Johnnie Walker Red": "JW Red with Brussels + Belly — bold-smoke JW against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; JW Red's smoke cuts the glaze's sweetness with distinctive peat-influence.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon": "Jordan — Sonoma Cab with cassis, plum, cedar, mint, fine tannin. The elegant body handles pork-belly fat and the cedar-mint plays against charred brussels. Strong elegant Cab for Brussels and Belly — refined balance cuts the rich starter without overpowering.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Joseph Mellot Sancerre": "Joseph Mellot Sancerre's crisp citrus-mineral acidity stays alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Jubilation by Colgin": "Jubilation — Colgin cult Napa, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violets, espresso, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts pork-belly fat and the dark chocolate plays against charred brussels. Works as cult Napa for Brussels and Belly — Colgin prestige cuts through the rich starter.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Jung and Wulff Guyana": "Jung and Wulff Guyana's deep-bodied spirit register leans against Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the rich pour wraps the pork-belly plate, and the rich character softens the side. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Jung and Wulff Trinidad": "Jung and Wulff Trinidad's caramel-char character lifts the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the crisp body sits with the plate, and the vanilla amplifies the dessert sugar. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Kahlua": "Kahlua's sweet liqueur character doubles down on Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet liqueur and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no contrast left. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Kahlua belongs on the steak course.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Kansas City": "* The KC with Brussels + Belly -- the KC's lean-bold strip with savory grain frames Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts. Gold standard; the side that defines the steak course.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Keenan Chardonnay": "Keenan Chardonnay's bold apple-butter acidity plays cleanly against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Keenan Mernet": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye with Brussels + Belly — allocated KO meets maple-glazed pork belly. The premium KY rye character cuts the glaze with KO distinctiveness. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Kentucky Owl Confiscated": "Kentucky Owl Confiscated with Brussels + Belly — KO Confiscated meets maple-glazed pork belly. The storytelling-brand character cuts the glaze with KO distinctiveness. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet Kentucky Owl luxury Irish. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for the side — save the collector bottle for the protein course.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône": "Rhône Valley Côtes du Rhône Grenache-Syrah-Mourvèdre — Kermit Lynch, red cherry, wild herbs, pepper, garrigue, medium body. The pepper cuts pork-belly fat and the garrigue echoes brussels-char. Strong Southern-French for brussels-and-belly — Rhône savory polish on a fat-and-char side.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Ketel One Vodka": "Ketel One Vodka's Dutch-wheat-crisp neutrality plays cleanly against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Knickerbocker Gin": "Knickerbocker Gin's bold citrus-juniper botanicals stays alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Knob Creek": "Knob Creek with Brussels + Belly — 100-proof high-rye meets maple-glazed pork belly. The rye spice cuts the glaze's sweetness in a way wheated can't; a bolder small-plate pour. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Knob Creek 12 Year": "Knob Creek 12 Year with Brussels + Belly — 12-year aged high-rye meets maple-glazed pork belly. The aged nutty-oak cuts the glaze with premium Beam authority. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Knob Creek 15 Year": "Knob Creek 15 with Brussels + Belly — 15yr Beam KC against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; KC 15's aged character meets the glaze at aged-Beam register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Knob Creek 18 Year": "Knob Creek 18 with Brussels + Belly — 18yr Beam limited KC against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; KC 18's aged character meets the glaze at collector register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye": "Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye with Brussels + Belly — bourbon-and-rye blend meets maple-glazed pork belly. The rye portion cuts the glaze's sweetness while the bourbon portion meets the pork fat; a layered small-plate pairing. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Knob Creek Rye": "Knob Creek Rye with Brussels + Belly — 100-proof Beam rye meets maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; bold rye cuts the glaze with extra-proof authority.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Komos Anejo Reserva": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed meets Komos Anejo Reserva. Excellent; the wine-cask-distinctive character rides the maple glaze at luxury register — wine-cask depth amplifies glaze.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Komos Crystallino Anejo": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed meets Komos Crystallino. Excellent; the crystallino-filtered-anejo character plays the maple glaze at trendy register — unexpected pairing through filtered-depth.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Komos Extra Anejo": "Komos Extra Añejo with Brussels + Belly — Riedel-luxury aged Komos meets maple-glazed pork belly. Works; luxury over-specified for small plate.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Komos Rosa Reposado": "Komos Rosa Reposado with Brussels + Belly — rosé-finished reposado against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; the wine-cask notes don't compete with the dish's sweetness effectively.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Lagavulin 8": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and crispy pork belly meet Lagavulin 8's vibrant peat in a clean back-and-forth. Brightness over brute force; the maple-sweetness still leads, the 8-year's smoke frames without crushing. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Lail Vineyards Blueprint": "Napa Cab — Lail entry-level, polished blackcurrant, cedar, dark cherry, refined medium tannin. The refined tannin cuts pork-belly fat and the cedar plays against charred brussels. Strong historically-pedigreed Napa Cab for Brussels and Belly — Lail family polish on the rich starter.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée": "Lail flagship multi-appellation Napa Cab — dark fruit, cassis, graphite, dried violet, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts pork-belly fat and the dried violet plays against charred brussels. Strong historically-significant Napa Cab for Brussels and Belly — Daniel Cuvée structure on the rich starter.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Lalo Silver": "Lalo Silver's silver-spirit lift with agave-citrus edge leans against Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the unaged body brightens the pork-belly plate, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Laphroaig 10": "Laphroaig 10 with Brussels + Belly — the medicinal edge slices through the pork belly's maple-glazed fat like nothing else on the spirit list. Not for every guest; for the right guest, unforgettable. The other two Islays are more approachable; Laphroaig is the statement. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Larceny Small Batch": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet Larceny's 92-proof wheated. Clean everyday pairing; approachable without being underwhelming. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé": "Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé's crisp berry-cherry acidity plays cleanly against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut": "Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut: this versatile sparkling's bright acidity, toasty lees character, and cleansing bubbles meets the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts. Acid and bubbles scrub the side's fat while brightness keeps the palate clear. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Le Garenne Rosé": "Le Garenne Rosé's crisp floral-rose acidity leans against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Le Ragnaie Brunello": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Le Volte dell'Ornellaia": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Lemon Lavender Gin Martini": "Lemon Lavender Gin Martini's citrus-floral build holds with the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the honey rounds the grilled char. Works; the pairing reads neutral at the table. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Les Pallières Raciné": "Gigondas Rhône Valley Grenache — Les Pallières Raciné, Brunier-family old-vine, wild red fruit, garrigue, iron, earthy mineral, medium tannin. The medium tannin cuts pork-belly fat and the garrigue matches brussels-char. Strong Gigondas for brussels-and-belly — Rhône polish on fat-and-char.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Liberator Gin": "Liberator Gin's citrus-juniper botanicals sits beside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Licor 43": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character clashes with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Licor 43 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Limoncello": "Limoncello's sweet liqueur character doubles down on Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet liqueur and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no contrast left. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Limoncello for the steak course.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Willamette Pinot — dark cherry, forest floor, spice, medium body. The acid cuts pork-belly fat and the forest-floor plays against charred brussels. Strong by-the-glass Oregon Pinot for Brussels and Belly — elegant counterpoint to the rich starter.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Little Book": "Little Book with Brussels + Belly — Jim Beam Fred Noe blended cask-strength against maple-glazed pork belly. Excellent; Little Book meets the glaze with chapter-series intensity.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Loaded Potato": "The loaded potato and Brussels + Belly -- cream rounds the protein, the plate composes thick. Works; sequence them or share the table, the call holds either way.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Lobster Mac": "Brussels + Belly alongside the lobster mac -- the bourbon-maple glaze reads alongside the lobster-cheese-cream build. Works; both sides hold at neutral register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Loch Lomond 20 Year": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with Brussels + Belly — 20yr aged varied-still Highland against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Loch Lomond 20's aged complexity meets the glaze at collector register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Lock Stock & Barrel Rye": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye with Brussels + Belly — sourced boutique rye meets maple-glazed pork belly. The premium-blend character cuts the glaze with boutique distinctiveness. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Long Road Gin": "Long Road Gin's crisp citrus-juniper botanicals reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Los Vecinos Mezcal": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet Los Vecinos. Excellent; the traditional-smoke rides the glaze and belly at craft-mezcal register — smoke meets smoke-adjacent belly fat.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Louis XIII Cognac": "Louis XIII Cognac's luxury-icon cognac depth mis-pairs with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- a luxury cognac belongs alone after the meal, not alongside a side. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not an icon cognac. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Louis XIII Cognac for the steak course.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Lucano Amaro": "Lucano with Brussels + Belly — floral-anise amaro against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; the anise character cuts the glaze distinctively.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Lunaria Coste di Moro": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this medium-bodied red's approachable fruit and food-friendly acidity. The elegant red's acidity cuts the dairy fat while its cherry lifts the earthy umami. Strong — the wine refreshes the side's richness.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Macallan 12 Sherry": "Macallan 12 Sherry with Brussels + Belly — sherried Speyside against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Macallan 12's dried-fruit meets the glaze at benchmark register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Macallan 18": "Macallan 18 with Brussels + Belly — 18yr aged sherried Speyside against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Macallan 18's dried-fruit meets the glaze at premium register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Macallan Estate": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet Easter Elchies Estate-oak Macallan. Works; Macallan Estate's distinctive depth meets the glaze at premium register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Macauley Petite Syrah": "Napa Petite Sirah — Macauley, inky color, dense powerful tannin (not Syrah), blackberry, blueberry, dark chocolate, black pepper, full body. The dense tannin slices pork-belly fat and the black pepper matches brussels-char bitterness. Strong Petite-Sirah for brussels-and-belly — powerful Napa on fat-and-char.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Macauley Pinot Noir": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this elegant red's cherry-bright, silky-tannin frame. The elegant red's acidity cuts the dairy fat while its cherry lifts the earthy umami. Strong — the wine refreshes the side's richness.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Macauley Stagecoach Vineyard": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Mahon Gin": "Mahon Gin's bold herbal-juniper botanicals sits beside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs frame the grilled char. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Maker's Mark": "Maker's Mark with Brussels + Belly — iconic wheated sweetness meets maple-glazed pork belly. A clean, crowd-pleasing match; the gateway Maker's alongside Weller Special Reserve. Gold standard; pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Maker's Mark Cellar Aged": "Maker's Mark Cellar Aged with Brussels + Belly — the bourbon's deeper wax-caramel meets maple glaze and pork belly fat. More considered than standard Maker's here; the Cellar Aged earns the small plate. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Malibu Rum": "Malibu Rum's green-agave-and-cane lift finds neutral with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the light-rum body matches the pork-belly plate, and the bright cane edge brightens the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye": "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye with Brussels + Belly — 16-year home-state rye meets maple-glazed pork belly. The extended maturation cuts the glaze with Michigan-distillery distinctiveness. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Marc Brédif Chinon": "Marc Brédif Chinon's cherry-earth tannin reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the herbs frame the grilled char. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Margarita": "Margarita's crisp agave-brine build plays cleanly against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Marimar Estate Christina": "Marimar Estate Christina's cherry-earth tannin leans against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice lifts the green plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Market Fish": "Market Fish into Brussels + Belly -- the white-fish body plays against the sweet-savory build. Strong; the side composes cleanly with the main.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Mata Hari Absinthe": "Mata Hari Absinthe's sweet wormwood-anise character finds register with the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the sweet character sits at digestif register, and the anise frames the char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Michter's 10 Year Bourbon": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet Michter's single-barrel 10yr. Works; Michter's 10's aged character meets the glaze at prestigious-independent register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Michter's 10 Year Rye": "Michter's 10 Year Rye with Brussels + Belly — aged Michter's meets maple-glazed pork belly. The 10-year polish cuts the glaze with premium small-batch authority. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Michter's US*1 Rye": "Michter's US*1 Rye with Brussels + Belly — smooth pot-still rye meets maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; the Michter's polish handles the dish with refined rye character.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Mijenta Blanco": "Mijenta Blanco's silver-spirit lift with agave-citrus edge reads alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the pork-belly plate, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; clean composes cleanly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Milagro Anejo": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed meets Milagro Anejo. Excellent; French-oak vanilla-refined character rides the maple glaze at craft register — softer sugar pairing than Patron.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Milagro Reposado": "Milagro Reposado with Brussels + Belly — modern reposado against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; clean agave cuts the glaze but isn't a standout.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet Mister Sam Bronfman tribute. Works; Mister Sam's blended character meets the glaze at tribute register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Mocha Creme": "Brussels + Belly alongside the mocha creme -- savory gives way to sweet, the close lands cleanly. Works; the contrast holds, neither course overshadows the other.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Monkey 47 Gin": "Monkey 47 Gin's crisp Black-Forest-botanical botanicals sits beside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Monkey Shoulder": "Monkey Shoulder with Brussels + Belly — triple-Speyside-malt blend against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; Monkey Shoulder's rich-fruit-and-vanilla meets the glaze with distinctive Speyside-malt character.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Montenegro Amaro": "Montenegro with Brussels + Belly — vanilla-orange amaro against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; the sweeter amaro style doubles the dish's sweetness slightly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Mount Gay Rum": "Mount Gay Rum's green-agave-and-cane lift sits alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the light-rum body cuts the pork-belly plate, and the Caribbean-rum register underlines the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Muga Reserva": "Rioja Alta Reserva Tempranillo-blend — Muga, American-French oak, strawberry, dried cherry, vanilla, leather, savory-earthy. The leather plays with pork-belly fat and the vanilla-oak matches brussels-char bitterness. Strong Rioja for brussels-and-belly — traditional-oak polish on fat-and-char.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Mushroom Bisque": "Mushroom Bisque and Brussels + Belly -- the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream meets Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: protein meets umami, the table builds substance. Works; no conflict however the table orders them.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Mushrooms": "Brussels + Belly and the mushrooms across the plate -- the charred sprouts runs alongside the mushrooms. Works; safe call when the table doubles up on sides.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Myers's Rum": "Myers's Rum's heavy aged-spirit weight reads register-aligned with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the high-proof register matches the pork-belly plate, and the dense weight underlines the side. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Negroni": "Gin, Contratto vermouth, Campari. The bitter-orange cuts belly's rendered fat and Contratto's herbal depth plays against brussels char. Works well — though the Bowdie's Old Fashioned or Espresso OF peak higher with the belly's sweet glaze.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Never Say Die Rye": "Never Say Die Rye with Brussels + Belly — Yorkshire-aged rye meets maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; distinctive maturation story cuts the glaze with UK-cask voice.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Never Say Die Small Batch": "Never Say Die Small Batch with Brussels + Belly — Yorkshire-aged Kentucky bourbon meets maple-glazed pork belly. The distinctive maturation story is the draw; a conversation-starter small-plate pour. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|New Holland Beer Barrel Bourbon": "New Holland Beer Barrel Bourbon with Brussels + Belly — Holland MI hop-influenced bourbon against maple-glazed pork belly. Excellent; NH Beer Barrel is the featured Michigan-exotic-finish-pork-belly pairing — beer-barrel hops meet maple glaze with brewer-heritage distinction.",
  "Brussels and Belly|New York Sour": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this bold whiskey-forward cocktail's oak, spice, and spirit depth. Whiskey's oak and sweetness mirror the side's dairy and umami depth. Works cleanly.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Nickel & Nickel Cabernet": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the pairing reads at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Nolets Dry Gin": "Nolets Dry Gin's bold char-floral botanicals sits beside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Not a Paper Plane": "Bulleit bourbon, Nonino amaro, Aperol, Angostura. The bourbon meets belly's rendered fat and Nonino's herbal bitterness cuts against the belly's sweet glaze; Aperol plays with brussels char. Works — though Bowdie's Old Fashioned and Espresso OF peak higher for this build.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Oban 14": "Oban 14 with Brussels + Belly — coastal West Highland against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; Oban's sea-salt-and-honey meets the glaze with distinctive maritime character.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Oban 18": "Oban 18 with Brussels + Belly — aged coastal Highland with sherry-finish against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; Oban 18's aged maritime + sherry-finish meets the glaze at premium register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Ocho Anejo": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed meets Ocho Anejo. Excellent; ex-American-whiskey cask character rides the maple glaze at Los-Altos-craft register — whiskey-cask aging echoes bourbon-adjacent notes into the glaze.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Odette Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Old Elk Cigar Cut": "Old Elk Cigar Cut with Brussels + Belly — Fort Collins craft bourbon designed for cigar pairing against maple-glazed pork belly. Excellent; Old Elk Cigar Cut's purpose-built character meets the glaze at distinctive cigar-companion register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Old Emmer": "Old Emmer's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the bourbon weight handles the pork-belly plate, and the vanilla brightens the grilled char-edge. Works; distinctive character gives the dessert a unique story-frame; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Old Fitzgerald 7 Year": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with Brussels + Belly — wheated BIB meets maple-glazed pork belly. The bonded weight and wheat honey handle the dish's sweetness with more structure than standard wheated pours. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Old Fitzgerald 9 Year": "Old Fitzgerald 9 Year with Brussels + Belly — aged wheated BIB meets maple-glazed pork belly. The mature honey threads through the dish's maple sweetness with more dimension than the 7-year brings. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Old Grand-Dad 16 Year": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet aged OGD. Works; OGD 16's rye-spice meets the glaze at distinctive register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Opus One": "Opus One — Oakville Bordeaux blend, dark fruit, mocha, cedar, dried violet, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts pork-belly fat and the mocha plays against charred brussels. Strong collector Napa blend for Brussels and Belly — prestige wine cuts through the rich starter.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Our Lady of Guadalupe Acolytes": "Our Lady of Guadalupe Acolytes's bold butter-char acidity leans against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the herbs frame the grilled char. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Pablo Sour": "Pablo Sour's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift crowds Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- a light cocktail belongs with the opener or aperitif, not a savory side. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a light cocktail. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pablo Sour lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Paloma": "Paloma's crisp agave-citrus build stays alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the vanilla amplifies the dessert sugar. Works; the pairing reads neutral at the table. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with Brussels + Belly — Van Winkle Family Reserve meets maple-glazed pork belly. The 13-year Pappy depth cuts the glaze with unicorn Van Winkle authority. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with Brussels + Belly — HH annual cask-strength against maple-glazed pork belly. Excellent; Parker's Heritage 16th meets the glaze with collector-register intensity.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Patron Anejo": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed meets Patron Anejo. Excellent; vanilla-caramel rides the maple glaze at accessible register — sugar on sugar through American-oak.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Patron Silver": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift sits alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the silver-spirit register lifts the pork-belly plate, and the unaged-cane note plays against the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Patron XO Cafe": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character doubles down on Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet liqueur and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no contrast left. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Patron XO Cafe lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Paul Bara Grand Rosé Brut": "Paul Bara Grand Rosé Brut's mineral-driven sparkling lift finds neutral with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the fine bubbles lift the pork-belly plate, and the citrus frames the side. Works; the two desserts share the close without crowding.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Brussels + Belly and the PB brownie -- Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts hands off cleanly to the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: savory-into-sweet, the classic close lands intact. Works; sequence them or share the table, no clash.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Peju Cabernet Sauvignon": "Rutherford Cab — dark cherry, cassis, dusty cocoa, refined tannin. The elegant body handles pork-belly fat and the cocoa plays against charred brussels. Strong elegant Napa Cab for Brussels and Belly — family-estate refinement cuts the rich starter with Rutherford-dust depth.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Pierre Ferrand Cognac": "Pierre Ferrand Cognac's artisan cognac with orange peel leans against Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the artisan-cognac depth wraps the pork-belly plate, and the orange-peel frames the side. Works; Rémy's elegance handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut": "Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut's char-citrus acidity reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Pikesville Rye": "Pikesville Rye with Brussels + Belly — 110-proof Maryland-style rye meets maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; the high-proof boldness cuts the glaze with serious authority.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Pineau des Charentes": "Pineau des Charentes' sweet liqueur character doubles down on Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet liqueur and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no contrast left. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; the better calls are above. Pineau des Charentes lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Pio Cesare Barbaresco": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
