  "Brussels and Belly|San Simeon Stormwatch": "Paso Robles Cab-dominant Bordeaux blend — dark cherry, blackcurrant, mocha, medium tannin. The medium tannin cuts pork-belly fat and the mocha plays against charred brussels. Strong Paso value Bordeaux blend for Brussels and Belly — solid full-body cuts through the rich starter.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir": "Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir's cherry-earth tannin leans against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Brussels and Belly with the garlic spinach on the plate -- the pork-belly plate rests against the green-and-garlic side. Works; the call composes without crowding.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Sauternes Glass": "Sauternes Glass' dessert-wine sweetness clashes with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Sauternes Glass on the steak course instead.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Sazerac": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this bold whiskey-forward cocktail's oak, spice, and spirit depth. Whiskey's oak and sweetness mirror the side's dairy and umami depth. Works cleanly.",
