  "Brussels and Belly|Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon": "Alexander Valley Cab — American-oak vanilla, coconut, dill, ripe cassis, plum. The lush body handles pork-belly fat and the vanilla-dill plays against charred brussels. Strong recognizable Cab for Brussels and Belly — Silver Oak's American-oak signature cuts the rich starter with distinctive lushness.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Simon Family Estate Reserve": "Boutique Napa family estate Cab — dark plum, cassis, toasted oak, long refined finish, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts pork-belly fat and the toasted oak plays against charred brussels. Strong boutique Napa Cab for Brussels and Belly — Simon Family estate structure on the rich starter.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Spottswoode Lyndenhurst": "St. Helena Napa Cab — Spottswoode organic family estate, plum, dark cherry, violet, silky medium tannin. The silky tannin cuts pork-belly fat and the violet plays against charred brussels. Strong organic Napa Cab for Brussels and Belly — Spottswoode family story cuts through the rich starter.",
  "Brussels and Belly|St Supéry Cabernet Sauvignon": "Napa Rutherford Cab — blackberry, cassis, mocha, firm tannin. The full body handles pork-belly fat and the mocha plays against charred brussels. Strong by-the-glass Cab for Brussels and Belly — classic Napa character cuts through the rich starter at accessible price.",
  "Brussels and Belly|St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc": "St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc's citrus-lemon acidity reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Brussels and Belly|St Supéry Élu Meritage": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Stagg Jr. Batch #15": "Stagg Jr. Batch #15 with Brussels + Belly — BT cask-strength against maple-glazed pork belly. Excellent; Stagg Jr. meets the glaze at barrel-proof register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Stoli Elit Vodka": "Stoli Elit Vodka's crisp ultra-filtered-luxury neutrality leans against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc": "Marlborough Sauvignon Blanc — grassy, green, light-bodied. The weight class is wrong for pork-belly lardons and cumin-paprika-cayenne rub; Stoneleigh disappears underneath the smoky depth. Keep this wine for the wedge salad or lighter starters where it fits. Avoid; route the table to a better-matched pour.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Swordfish": "The swordfish and Brussels + Belly on the plate -- the dense fish steak sits cleanly with the sweet-savory build. Strong; the side holds the swordfish's weight without competing.",
