  "Brussels and Belly|Tanqueray Gin": "Tanqueray Gin's bold London-Dry-juniper botanicals sits beside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals echo the green plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Taylor Fladgate Tawny": "Taylor Fladgate Tawny's classic tawny with caramel-nut sweetness doubles down on Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet wine and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no foil. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Taylor Fladgate Tawny lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle": "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle on the steak course instead.",
