  "Brussels and Belly|Teeter Totter Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Tenuta di Arceno Chianti Classico": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|The BG": "Traveller whiskey, honey lavender, grapefruit, black walnut bitters, ginger beer top. The grapefruit cuts belly's rendered fat and honey lavender plays against the belly's sweet glaze; black walnut depth meets brussels char. Strong refreshing whiskey pairing for the sweet-savory build.",
  "Brussels and Belly|The Happy Wife": "The Happy Wife's crisp citrus-ginger build stays alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Brussels and Belly|The Manhattan": "Maker's Mark private barrel, Contratto, vanilla syrup, Angostura. The bourbon depth meets pork belly's rendered fat and brussels char; Contratto's herbal-sweet side bridges the glaze. Works well — though the Bowdie's Old Fashioned or Espresso version peak higher for this specific sweet-savory build.",
  "Brussels and Belly|The Prisoner Red Blend": "Napa Red Blend — The Prisoner, Zin-Cab-Petite Sirah-Syrah-Charbono, layered dark fruit, smooth integrated tannin, full body, lush finish. The integrated tannin cuts pork-belly fat and the layered dark fruit plays with brussels-char. Strong Prisoner for brussels-and-belly — Napa lush polish on fat-and-char.",
  "Brussels and Belly|The Tomahawk": "The Tomahawk alongside Brussels + Belly -- the 36oz long-bone showpiece's theatrical char meets the maple-glazed pork belly, the bone-in smoke matching the glaze's sweet-savory edge. Strong; the side holds the table's theater.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Thomas H. Handy Sazerac Rye": "Thomas H. Handy Sazerac Rye with Brussels + Belly — BTAC unfiltered rye meets maple-glazed pork belly. The barrel-proof uncut character cuts the glaze with allocated BT authority. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Thomas S. Moore Chardonnay Cask": "Thomas S. Moore Chardonnay Cask's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the caramel-spice register matches the pork-belly plate, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Works; sweet character distinctive but not driving; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Titos Vodka": "Titos Vodka's Texas-corn-workhorse neutrality stays alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Toki Suntory Japanese Whisky": "Toki Suntory Japanese Whisky's entry Suntory Toki character leans against Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the precise Japanese craft body wraps the pork-belly plate, and the precision rounds the side. Works; the smooth character gives the dessert a composed frame; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Tomato Basil": "The tomato basil and Brussels + Belly on the same meal -- acid lifts the richness, the meal gets the contrast it needs. Works; sequence or share, the build holds.",
  "Brussels and Belly|Transfusion": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build sits alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; the call holds at register.",
