  "Butternut Squash|Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Butternut Squash|Broccolini": "Butternut Squash and the broccolini -- the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream meets the broccolini's tender green stalks: acid plays against sweetness, the close stays unburdened. Works; no conflict however the table orders them.",
  "Butternut Squash|Bruichladdich": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay reads alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the scotch depth settles into the squash bisque, and the oak softens the cream. Works; namesake pour is wasted on the salad.",
  "Butternut Squash|Brussels and Belly": "The butternut squash alongside Brussels + Belly -- savory-into-sweet, the classic close lands intact. Works; the table can build them in order or together.",
  "Butternut Squash|Buffalo Trace": "Buffalo Trace's rounded vanilla-and-toffee character sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bourbon depth settles into the squash bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; milestone-edition over-specified.",
  "Butternut Squash|Buffalo Trace Cream": "Buffalo Trace Cream's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- sugar piled onto cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — no contrast. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Buffalo Trace Cream on the steak course instead.",
  "Butternut Squash|Bulleit Bourbon": "Bulleit Bourbon's high-rye spice-forward depth sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the oak depth lays under the squash bisque, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; AE Triple Cask's layered character rides the cream at distinctive register.",
  "Butternut Squash|Burrata": "Burrata and the butternut squash together -- delicate gives way to sweet, the close lands light. Works; the table opens with both, no clash either way.",
  "Butternut Squash|Cade Cabernet Sauvignon": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character clashes with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Butternut Squash|Camarena Tequila": "Camarena Tequila's barrel-aged tequila weight finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the añejo register carries the squash bisque, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Butternut Squash|Campari": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Campari lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Butternut Squash|Canadian Club": "Canadian Club's workhorse Canadian blend reads alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the blended whisky body wraps the squash bisque, and the oak softens the cream. Works; JW Black handles the richness at premium-blend register.",
  "Butternut Squash|Canadian Club 43 Year": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the smooth Canadian register carries the squash bisque, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; extended maturation gives the dessert home-state aged character.",
  "Butternut Squash|Captain Morgan Rum": "Captain Morgan Rum's light-rum register with cane and citrus lift mis-pairs with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- the light spirit doesn't add to the soup-salad course — neutral but wrong. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a light spirit. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Captain Morgan Rum on the steak course instead.",
  "Butternut Squash|Caribou Crossing": "Caribou Crossing's Canadian whisky character finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the Canadian whisky weight matches the squash bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; Vermont-brand character doesn't drive.",
