  "Butternut Squash|Espresso Martini": "Espresso Martini's roasted-coffee martini richness flattens the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- whiskey-cocktail register buries the soup's cream instead of carrying it. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a spirit-forward cocktail. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Espresso Martini for the steak course.",
  "Butternut Squash|Espresso Old Fashioned": "Espresso Old Fashioned's spirit-forward cocktail register clashes with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- soup-salad course needs lift — bitters-and-whiskey brings weight instead. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a spirit-forward cocktail. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Espresso Old Fashioned for the steak course.",
  "Butternut Squash|Evening Land Seven Springs": "Willamette Pinot — savory Eola-Amity Pinot, medium tannin, elegant delicate. The savory edge plays against butternut's caramelized sweetness and the medium tannin lifts the cream base. Works tier on this wine's card — solid fit for Butternut Squash but below the wine's peaks with duck, lamb, and mushroom-sauced proteins.",
  "Butternut Squash|Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon": "Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon's estate-Cab Napa character clashes with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Butternut Squash|Far Niente Chardonnay": "Oakville Chardonnay — buttered citrus, toasted hazelnut, crème brûlée, lush. The opulent oak aligns with butternut's cream-sweet weight and the hazelnut plays against nutmeg-cinnamon warmth. Strong special-occasion Chardonnay for butternut squash — Napa opulence on the autumn classic.",
  "Butternut Squash|Faroe Island Salmon": "Faroe Island Salmon after the butternut squash -- the silky sweet squash cream opens with autumnal warmth, the salmon following with rich oily flesh that the squash's sweetness echoes without doubling. Strong; sweet cream sets the table for oily fish.",
  "Butternut Squash|Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi": "Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi's deep dark-fruit and grippy tannin sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the structured body wraps the squash bisque, and the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; the call holds at neutral register.",
