  "Butternut Squash|Licor 43": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- the liqueur's sweetness buries the soup's creamy base instead of supporting it. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a digestif. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Licor 43 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Butternut Squash|Limoncello": "Limoncello's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- the liqueur's sweetness buries the soup's creamy base instead of supporting it. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a digestif. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Limoncello for the steak course.",
  "Butternut Squash|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Willamette Pinot — dark cherry, forest floor, refined structure, low tannin. The low-tannin silk lifts the soup's cream weight and the forest-floor earth plays against caramelized-squash sweetness. Peaks from the dish's side; on this wine's card it's strong — below peaks with duck, lamb, and mushroom-sauced proteins. Confident pour when a guest anchors on Butternut Squash. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Butternut Squash|Little Book": "Little Book's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the brown-spirit warmth threads the squash bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the bonded richness gives the dessert more than lighter pours do.",
