  "Butternut Squash|Thomas H. Handy Sazerac Rye": "Thomas H. Handy Sazerac Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the high-rye spice register matches the squash bisque, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; multi-distillery complexity doesn't drive.",
  "Butternut Squash|Thomas S. Moore Chardonnay Cask": "Thomas S. Moore Chardonnay Cask's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bourbon body sits with the squash bisque, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Butternut Squash|Titos Vodka": "Titos Vodka's Texas-corn-workhorse neutrality plays cleanly against the squash soup's silky sweet — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Butternut Squash|Toki Suntory Japanese Whisky": "Toki Suntory Japanese Whisky's entry Suntory Toki character sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the restrained whisky body threads the squash bisque, and the oak softens the cream. Works; the complex profile is over-specified for this dish.",
  "Butternut Squash|Transfusion": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build sits beside the squash soup's silky sweet — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Butternut Squash|Trombo Cedano Reposado": "Trombo Cedano Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the rested-agave depth sits with the squash bisque, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Butternut Squash|Truffle Fries": "The butternut squash and the truffle fries -- sugar and umami share the table, the contrast carries the meal. Works; sequence them or share the table, the call holds either way.",
  "Butternut Squash|Tullamore D.E.W.": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the approachable Irish character carries the squash bisque, and the oak threads the cream. Works; Voyage 23 handles the richness at ocean-finish register.",
  "Butternut Squash|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna after the butternut squash -- the silky sweet squash cream opens with autumnal warmth, the tuna following with seared-rare flesh and sesame crust the squash's sweetness primes cleanly. Strong; sweet cream sets up the seared-rare main.",
  "Butternut Squash|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Butternut Squash and the curry together -- soup-and-salad open the meal. Works; both courses share the opening without crowding.",
  "Butternut Squash|Venge Family Reserve": "Venge Family Reserve's powerful blackcurrant body sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the structured body wraps the squash bisque, and the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Butternut Squash|Venge Scout's Honor": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis finds neutral with the squash soup's silky sweet — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the caramel-spice settles the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Butternut Squash|Venge Silencieux": "Venge Silencieux's bold cherry-chocolate cassis stays alongside the squash soup's silky sweet — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the cocoa deepens the fudge. Works; capable alongside. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Butternut Squash|Vesper": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build plays cleanly against the squash soup's silky sweet — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Butternut Squash|Veuve Clicquot Brut": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's biscuit-apple acidity stays alongside the squash soup's silky sweet — the mousse refreshes against the broth, and the apple notes lift the custard. Works; the pairing reads neutral at the table. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Butternut Squash|Vieux Carré": "Vieux Carré's bold herbal-spice build finds neutral with the squash soup's silky sweet — the whiskey-build weight overshoots the light soup, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Butternut Squash|Villon Cognac": "Villon Cognac's aged-grape brandy depth leans against the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the brandy depth wraps the squash bisque, and the dried-fruit note underlines the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Butternut Squash|Vin Santo": "Vin Santo's Tuscan dried-fruit-and-honey sweetness doubles down on the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- sweet wine on cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — heavy, no contrast. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Vin Santo for the steak course.",
  "Butternut Squash|Weller 107": "Weller 107's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the brown-spirit warmth threads the squash bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; the blend's complexity is underused by the salad.",
  "Butternut Squash|Weller 12 Year": "Weller 12 Year's aged wheated honey-vanilla character finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the wheated weight wraps the squash bisque, and the caramel softens the cream. Works; BH Red Wine Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Butternut Squash|Weller Millennium": "Weller Millennium's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bourbon weight handles the squash bisque, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; narrative-bourbon doesn't drive.",
  "Butternut Squash|Weller Special Reserve": "Weller Special Reserve's wheated soft-vanilla character sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bourbon body sits with the squash bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; save the BTAC bottle for the protein course — the side doesn't deserve the pour.",
  "Butternut Squash|Wheatley Vodka": "Wheatley Vodka's crisp cream neutrality plays cleanly against the squash soup's silky sweet — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Butternut Squash|WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel Rye": "WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the rye backbone drives the squash bisque, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; complexity wasted on salad.",
  "Butternut Squash|WhistlePig 12 Year Old World": "WhistlePig 12 Year Old World's rye-spice character finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the squash bisque, and the oak threads the cream. Works; JW Black handles the richness at premium-blend register.",
  "Butternut Squash|WhistlePig 15 Year": "WhistlePig 15 Year's rye-spice character sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the rye spice cuts the squash bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Butternut Squash|WhistlePig Boss Hog IX 17 Year": "WhistlePig Boss Hog IX 17 Year's rye-spice character sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the rye-and-oak weight handles the squash bisque, and the oak threads the cream. Works; the single-barrel depth is over-specified for this dish.",
  "Butternut Squash|WhistlePig Boss Hog X Commandments": "WhistlePig Boss Hog X Commandments' rye-spice character sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the rye-and-oak weight handles the squash bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; Remus 15 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Butternut Squash|WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year": "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year's rye-spice character sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the rye spice cuts the squash bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Butternut Squash|Willett Pot Still Reserve": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the oak depth lays under the squash bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; wine-cask over-specified.",
  "Butternut Squash|Woodford Reserve": "Woodford Reserve's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the oak depth lays under the squash bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; OGD 16 handles dessert density at distinctive register.",
  "Butternut Squash|Woodford Reserve Double Oaked": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bourbon weight handles the squash bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; not revelatory but well-matched registers.",
  "Butternut Squash|Woodford Reserve Rye": "Woodford Reserve Rye's rye-spice character leans against the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the rye backbone drives the squash bisque, and the oak threads the cream. Works; Boss Hog's allocation story is wasted on the salad.",
  "Butternut Squash|Woodinville Rye": "Woodinville Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the rye spice cuts the squash bisque, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Butternut Squash|Yamazaki 12 Year": "Yamazaki 12 Year's Suntory Japanese flagship character reads alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the restrained whisky body threads the squash bisque, and the oak softens the cream. Works; aged premium slightly over-specified.",
  "Butternut Squash|Yamazaki 18 Year": "Yamazaki 18 Year's aged Suntory mizunara character finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the Mizunara-influenced register sits with the squash bisque, and the oak threads the cream. Works; gentle match.",
  "Butternut Squash|Yellow Chartreuse": "Yellow Chartreuse's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- amaro bitterness on dairy cream reads metallic — no bridge from herbal sharp to soft fat. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Yellow Chartreuse for the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Asparagus": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character crowds the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- the side needs a crisper register to carry it cleanly. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Cade Cabernet Sauvignon lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Au Gratin Potatoes: structured red meets dairy-driven side: the bold tannin scrubs the cream, the dark fruit lifts the indulgence into balance. A capable pair; richness aligns if not perfectly. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Beignets": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- tannin can't pivot to warm pastry sugar — the pour reads dry, the dessert reads heavy. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Bone Marrow": "Bone Marrow: this rich, umami-forward starter's bold fat and concentrated savory depth meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's tannin scrubs the starter's fat while dark fruit picks up the umami notes. An excellent opening pour — weight and fruit both land. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Bone-In Filet": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon -- Howell Mountain Cab, cassis, mountain tannin. The Howell-Mountain Cab tannin frames the bone-enhanced filet, and the cassis grips the cut. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Broccoli Cheddar": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character overwhelms the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Cade Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Broccolini": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character crowds the broccolini's tender green stalks -- the side needs a crisper register to carry it cleanly. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Cade Cabernet Sauvignon lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Burrata": "Howell Mountain Cab against burrata's creamy-delicate center — firm iron-mineral body crushes the milk and basil-tomato-pistachio clashes with blackberry-plum. Never pair. Route burrata to rosé, Pinot Blanc, or Sancerre and keep Cade for the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Butternut Squash": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character clashes with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Carrot Cake": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Cade Cabernet Sauvignon lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Cheesecake": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character pulls against the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- the red's dry-fruit register has no bridge to dessert tang or sugar. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Chilean Seabass": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Chocolate Brownie": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character clashes with the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- savory tannin sits awkwardly on cocoa weight without resolving. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Cade Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Chocolate Cake": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character fights the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- the dry red and the chocolate's sugar refuse each other — tannin reads bitter on the finish. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Clam Chowder": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Cowboy Ribeye": "Cade — Howell Mountain Cab from one of Napa's first LEED-certified wineries. High-elevation fruit: blackberry, dark plum, iron, volcanic mineral, firm age-worthy tannin. The mountain-fruit body handles Cowboy's marbled bone-in richness and the iron-mineral meets rendered fat. Peak mountain Cab for Cowboy — compelling story, serious bottle. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Crab Cake": "Howell Mountain Cab against crab cake's delicate sweet shellfish — firm-tannin iron-mineral crushes romesco-and-crab. Never pair. Route crab cake to Chablis, Sancerre, or Champagne and keep Cade for the steak course where its LEED-estate Howell Mountain character shines.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Creamed Spinach": "Creamed Spinach: dark-fruit Cab body settles into the cream-rich side; firm tannin cuts the lactic edge and the oak threads the indulgence. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Creamy Potato": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character clashes with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Creme Brulee": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character jars against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Escargot": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon -- Howell Mountain Cab, cassis, mountain tannin. The Howell-Mountain Cab tannin frames the buttered escargot, and the cassis grips the starter. Strong; reliable opener for the cut.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Faroe Island Salmon": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character jars against the salmon's rich oily flesh -- tannin on oily fish goes bitter, where a Pinot at the right register would carry it. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Filet Mignon": "Howell Mountain Cab — blackberry, dark plum, iron, volcanic mineral, firm age-worthy tannin. The structured body meets butter-tender filet's lean sweetness and the iron-mineral echoes escargot-butter toppers. Strong mountain Cab for filet — Cade's LEED-certified Howell Mountain character, though lighter Cabs peak higher on the delicate cut.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|French Onion": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's bold juniper-mineral cassis finds neutral with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Grilled Caesar": "Grilled Caesar: the Grilled Caesar's charred romaine, anchovy umami, and bold creamy dressing meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's structure meets the Caesar's charred romaine, anchovy umami, and bold dressing — weight on weight. Works — the Caesar can hold the tannin.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Gumbo": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character overwhelms the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character crowds the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- the side needs a crisper register to carry it cleanly. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|House Wedge": "House Wedge: the House Wedge's crisp iceberg against creamy bleu dressing meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The wedge's crisp iceberg and creamy dressing sit light against the bold red's dense tannin — the wine overwhelms the salad. Works only as a second-thought pairing.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Kansas City": "Kansas City: the Cab's oak-driven weight matches the strip's char-and-fat; firm tannin clears the rendered edge. A headliner steakhouse pour. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Loaded Potato": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's bold juniper-mineral cassis plays cleanly against the loaded potato's richness — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the mineral edge cuts the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Lobster Mac": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's bold juniper-mineral cassis finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Market Fish": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character clashes with the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Mocha Creme": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character fights the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- the dry red and the chocolate's sugar refuse each other — tannin reads bitter on the finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Mushroom Bisque": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's bold juniper-mineral cassis leans against the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the mineral edge cuts the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Mushrooms": "Mushrooms: the bold red's cassis grip carries the mushroom-and-truffle depth — structured weight on the earthy side. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the pairing reads at register.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character clashes with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- savory tannin sits awkwardly on cocoa weight without resolving. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Porterhouse": "Porterhouse: the strip's marbled-and-char richness finds the bold red's grip; cassis carries the savory weight cleanly. A confident choice — steakhouse symmetry. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Prime Tartare": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's bold juniper-mineral cassis finds register with the tartare's raw beef and brine — the Cab structure meets the savory depth, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Rainbow Trout": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Roast Half Chicken": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character reads alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the Howell-Mountain Cab tannin frames the roast chicken, and the cassis grips the plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character overwhelms the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character clashes with the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character clashes with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- tannin on raw green vegetable reads astringent without payoff. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Seafood Tower": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Seared Scallops": "Cade Howell Mountain Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — firm iron-mineral obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save Cade for the steak course where its LEED-estate Howell character peaks.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Seasonal Soup": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character jars against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Seasonal Vegetables": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character overshadows the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate -- red weight crowds a green side without lifting it — needs crisp register, not tannin. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Shrimp Bisque": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's bold juniper-mineral cassis leans against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Shrimp Cocktail": "Cade Howell Mountain Cab against chilled sweet-briny shrimp — firm iron-mineral is the wrong axis for cold shellfish and cocktail sauce. Never layer. Route shrimp cocktail to Champagne, Sancerre, or Chablis and save Cade for steak where its LEED-estate Howell character belongs.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Swordfish": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Cade Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|The Tomahawk": "The Tomahawk: this marbled ribeye's fatty richness, smoky crust, and bold beef expression meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The tannin scrubs rendered fat while dark fruit echoes the savory char. A headliner steakhouse pour. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Tomato Basil": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character jars against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Le Garenne Rosé, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Truffle Fries": "Truffle Fries: the mushroom's umami depth meets the bold red's structured tannin; dark fruit threads the truffle-and-earth without crowding. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character overshadows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- dark-fruit weight crowds the seared sesame crust — needs a sparkling or crisp white for lift. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character jars against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Le Garenne Rosé, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Cade Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Asparagus": "Camarena Tequila's aged-agave character sits alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the barrel-rested body handles the asparagus, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Camarena Tequila's rested-agave body sits alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the oak-aged tequila body threads the au gratin, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; the 70th's clarity is too delicate to drive the pairing.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Beignets": "Camarena Tequila's rested-agave body finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the aged-agave weight wraps the beignets, and the oak threads the dessert. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Bone Marrow": "Camarena Tequila with bone marrow — value reposado against umami fat. Strong; the accessible character is outmatched by marrow's intensity.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Bone-In Filet": "Camarena Tequila's crisp character finds register with the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the añejo weight grips the lean cut. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Broccoli Cheddar": "Camarena Tequila's rested-agave body reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the oak-aged tequila body threads the broccoli cheddar, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; cedar and maple don't quite align.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Broccolini": "Camarena Tequila's aged-agave character reads alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the oak-aged tequila body threads the broccolini, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the side. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Brussels and Belly": "Camarena Tequila with Brussels + Belly — value reposado against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; approachable agave cuts the glaze but not marquee.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Burrata": "Camarena Tequila's añejo-pour depth sits alongside the burrata's fresh basil-tomato-cream delicacy: the rested-agave depth sits with the burrata, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the starter. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Butternut Squash": "Camarena Tequila's barrel-aged tequila weight finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the añejo register carries the squash bisque, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Carrot Cake": "Camarena Tequila's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the rested-agave depth sits with the carrot cake, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Cheesecake": "Camarena Tequila's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the rested-agave depth sits with the cheesecake, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the dessert. Works; the earthy craft character doesn't quite lift the truffle the way polished reposados suggest they might.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Chilean Seabass": "Camarena Tequila's cooked-agave-and-oak register sits alongside the seabass' buttery seabass flesh: the añejo register carries the seabass, and the oak threads the plate. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Chocolate Brownie": "Camarena Tequila's rested-agave body sits alongside the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the brownie, and the caramel-agave register brightens the dessert. Works; distinctive ceremony over-specified.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Chocolate Cake": "Camarena Tequila's barrel-aged tequila weight reads alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the oak-aged tequila body threads the chocolate cake, and the oak threads the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Clam Chowder": "Camarena Tequila's aged-agave character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the barrel-rested body handles the chowder, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; luxury ceremony over-specified for two-cut plate.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Cowboy Ribeye": "Camarena Tequila with the Cowboy Ribeye — 80-proof value reposado against cap fat. Strong; underpowered for the cut — G4 High Proof (the premium Camarena sibling) or Adictivo are the ribeye calls.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Crab Cake": "Camarena Tequila with crab cake — entry reposado against lump crab. The approachable agave lifts the crab at the value tier. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Creamed Spinach": "Camarena Tequila's rested-agave body finds neutral with the creamed spinach's rich bechamel-laced greens: the aged-agave weight wraps the creamed spinach, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; the pour is a touch over-specified for the side.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Creamy Potato": "Camarena Tequila's cooked-agave-and-oak register leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the oak-aged tequila body threads the potato soup, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Creme Brulee": "Camarena Tequila's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the aged-agave weight wraps the brulee, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the dessert. Works; the wine-cask character adds dimension but not standout.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Escargot": "Camarena Tequila's crisp character holds steady against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the añejo depth cuts the umami fat. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Faroe Island Salmon": "Camarena Tequila with the salmon — value reposado against salmon richness. Strong; accessible agave frames the salmon at entry tier.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Filet Mignon": "Camarena Tequila with the filet — value Camarena-family reposado against the 10oz cut. The approachable character meets the filet at the entry register. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Camarena Tequila|French Onion": "Camarena Tequila's barrel-aged tequila weight sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the barrel-rested body handles the French onion, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; distinctive-bottle over-specified.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Grilled Caesar": "Camarena Tequila with the grilled Caesar — value reposado against charred romaine. Strong; approachable agave finds the Caesar at the everyday tier.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Gumbo": "Camarena Tequila's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the añejo register carries the gumbo, and the caramel-agave register brightens the bowl. Works; the 70th's smoothness is an unusual but interesting counterpoint.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Camarena Tequila's barrel-aged tequila weight finds neutral with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the aged-agave weight wraps the honey carrots, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; accessible aged composed with this dish.",
  "Camarena Tequila|House Wedge": "Camarena Tequila with the House Wedge — Camarena-family value reposado against iceberg and bleu. The approachable agave cuts the bleu at the entry tier. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Kansas City": "Camarena Tequila with the KC — Camarena family's value brand. 80-proof, approachable, everyday entry reposado. Distinct from G4 High Proof (their premium): Camarena is the accessible entry call for strip orders. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Loaded Potato": "Camarena Tequila's aged-agave character leans against the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the añejo register carries the loaded potato soup, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; accessible aged composed with this dish.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Lobster Mac": "Camarena Tequila's añejo-pour depth leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the añejo register carries the lobster mac, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Market Fish": "Camarena Tequila's añejo-pour depth sits alongside the market fish's clean white-fish flesh: the oak-aged tequila body threads the market fish, and the oak threads the plate. Works; ceremonial over-specified.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Mocha Creme": "Camarena Tequila's cooked-agave-and-oak register sits alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the mocha creme, and the caramel-agave register brightens the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Mushroom Bisque": "Camarena Tequila's añejo-pour depth sits alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the rested-agave depth sits with the mushroom bisque, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; distinctive-packaging composed.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Mushrooms": "Camarena Tequila with the mushrooms — value reposado against earthy umami. Strong; approachable agave layers cleanly into mushroom depth.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Camarena Tequila's rested-agave body sits alongside the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the rested-agave depth sits with the PB brownie, and the soft-spice note softens the dessert. Works; covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Porterhouse": "Camarena Tequila's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character: the barrel-rested body handles the dual-cut steak, and the oak threads the cut. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Prime Tartare": "Camarena Tequila with the tartare — value reposado against raw beef. Works; approachable agave is a gentle counterpoint.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Rainbow Trout": "Camarena Tequila's añejo-pour depth leans against the trout's delicate flesh: the añejo register carries the trout, and the cooked-agave note underlines the plate. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Roast Half Chicken": "Camarena Tequila with the roast half chicken — value reposado against roasted chicken. Works; clean entry match.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Camarena Tequila's rested-agave body reads alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the aged-agave weight wraps the chickpea soup, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Camarena Tequila's rested-agave body finds neutral with the halibut's salt-cured flesh: the aged-agave weight wraps the halibut, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the plate. Works; luxury over-specified for small plate.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Camarena Tequila's rested-agave body reads alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the barrel-rested body handles the garlic spinach, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; the aged depth is an unusual but interesting match.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Seafood Tower": "Camarena Tequila's añejo-pour depth sits alongside the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the añejo register carries the seafood tower, and the oak threads the starter. Works; brightness can cut the glaze but wheated bourbons sit better with this dish.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Seared Scallops": "Camarena Tequila with seared scallops — value reposado against caramelized scallop. The accessible agave meets the sear at the entry register. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Seasonal Soup": "Camarena Tequila's aged-agave character finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the rested-agave depth sits with the seasonal soup, and the caramel-agave register brightens the bowl. Works; clean accessible match.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Seasonal Vegetables": "Camarena Tequila's rested-agave body finds neutral with the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the seasonal vegetables, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Shrimp Bisque": "Camarena Tequila with shrimp bisque — value reposado against cream-based seafood. Strong; accessible agave cuts the dairy at the entry register.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Shrimp Cocktail": "Camarena Tequila with shrimp cocktail — value reposado against cold shrimp. The entry-tier agave threads through the cocktail sauce cleanly. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Swordfish": "Camarena Tequila's rested-agave body leans against the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak: the barrel-rested body handles the swordfish, and the oak threads the plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Camarena Tequila|The Tomahawk": "Camarena Tequila with the Tomahawk — value reposado against massive cut. Avoid; demands bourbon or scotch.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Tomato Basil": "Camarena Tequila's cooked-agave-and-oak register leans against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the barrel-rested body handles the tomato basil, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; the wine-cask character adds dimension but not standout.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Truffle Fries": "Camarena Tequila with truffle fries — value reposado against truffle-parmesan. Works; accessible character doesn't drive.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Camarena Tequila's aged-agave character reads alongside the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the barrel-rested body handles the tuna, and the soft-spice note softens the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Camarena Tequila|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Camarena Tequila's barrel-aged tequila weight sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the aged-agave weight wraps the curry, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; Durango presentation slightly over-specified.",
  "Campari|Asparagus": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook doubles down on the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- bitter herbs and a green vegetable side compound the same register — no contrast. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Campari belongs on the steak course.",
  "Campari|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- amaro bitterness on dairy reads metallic — needs warmth or sweetness to balance. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|Beignets": "Campari with beignets — ruby bitter against fried dough. Works; aperitivo bitterness cuts the sugar but Campari is over-specified for casual dessert.",
  "Campari|Bone Marrow": "Campari with bone marrow — aperitivo bitter against umami fat. Avoid; aperitivo is the wrong register for the biggest appetizer — Campari at 24% can't cut marrow the way Branca does. Reach for Fernet Branca.",
  "Campari|Bone-In Filet": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook mis-pairs with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- bitter botanicals on the cut fight the savory char without payoff. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Campari belongs on another course.",
  "Campari|Broccoli Cheddar": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook fights the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- bitter herbs cut the bisque's round cream without lifting it. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Campari belongs on the steak course.",
  "Campari|Broccolini": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook doubles down on the broccolini's tender green stalks -- bitter herbs and a green vegetable side compound the same register — no contrast. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|Brussels and Belly": "Campari with Brussels + Belly — bitter orange-rhubarb against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; the orange-bitter cuts the glaze's sweetness with aperitivo lift.",
  "Campari|Burrata": "Campari with burrata — 24% bitter against fresh dairy. Avoid; Campari's bitterness is still too heavy for burrata. Reach for Aperol instead.",
  "Campari|Butternut Squash": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Campari lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Campari|Carrot Cake": "Campari with carrot cake — bitter orange-rhubarb against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; the orange notes marry the cinnamon and the bitterness threads cream cheese cleanly — a featured dessert match for the aperitivo cornerstone.",
  "Campari|Cheesecake": "Campari with cheesecake — ruby bitter against custard. Strong; the orange notes lift the cheesecake at aperitivo register.",
  "Campari|Chilean Seabass": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook jars against the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bitter herbs on oily fish read metallic — the rich flesh deserves a crisp white. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Campari on the steak course instead.",
  "Campari|Chocolate Brownie": "Campari with the chocolate brownie — ruby bitter against cocoa. Strong; orange-and-chocolate is the resonance, though Campari is lighter on dessert than the sipping amari.",
  "Campari|Chocolate Cake": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the herbal cut works the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Campari|Clam Chowder": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|Cowboy Ribeye": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook underclubs the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness -- amaro reads light against the marbled char — the cut deserves wine or whiskey weight. The plate deserves Macallan 18, Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon, or Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Campari for another course.",
  "Campari|Crab Cake": "Campari with crab cake — ruby bitter against delicate crab. Avoid; even the aperitivo bitter is too much for crab.",
  "Campari|Creamed Spinach": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the creamed spinach's rich bechamel-laced greens -- amaro bitterness on dairy reads metallic — needs warmth or sweetness to balance. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Weller 12 Year, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|Creamy Potato": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|Creme Brulee": "Campari with creme brulee — bitter orange-rhubarb against vanilla custard and caramelized sugar. Strong; the bitter-orange finds the caramel with aperitivo character.",
  "Campari|Escargot": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook doubles down on the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- aperitivo herbs and a herb-bright opener compound the bitter register — no contrast. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|Faroe Island Salmon": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bitter aperitivo is for before or after the meal — not on a main protein. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|Filet Mignon": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook overwhelms the filet's lean buttery tenderness -- amaro bitterness flattens the lean cut's buttery delicacy. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Maker's Mark Cellar Aged, or Yamazaki 18 Year, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Campari for another course.",
  "Campari|French Onion": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook jars against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth -- bitter botanicals on savory broth pull against the salt-and-spice frame without resolving. The plate deserves Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Campari belongs on the steak course.",
  "Campari|Grilled Caesar": "Campari with the grilled Caesar — ruby bitter orange-rhubarb against charred romaine and anchovy. Excellent; Campari is aperitivo at its most textbook, and the bitter-orange lifts the Caesar's anchovy-char in a way the Fernets can't reach. The aperitivo amaro finds its clearest app.",
  "Campari|Gumbo": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- bitter aperitivo on the supporting side reads as wrong register for the course. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|House Wedge": "Campari with the House Wedge — 24% bitter orange-rhubarb against iceberg and bleu. Excellent; this is aperitivo country — Campari's ruby bitter was built for crisp greens and blue cheese bite, where the sipping amari would feel heavy.",
  "Campari|Kansas City": "Campari with the KC — aperitivo bitter against an 18oz strip. Avoid; Campari is meant to open the meal, not close a heavy steak. Save for before dinner or redirect to Fernet Branca post-strip.",
  "Campari|Loaded Potato": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|Lobster Mac": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- bitter aperitivo on the supporting side reads as wrong register for the course. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|Market Fish": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- bitter herbs flatten delicate fish — the protein can't lift the amaro's register. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|Mocha Creme": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook leans against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the herbal cut works the mocha creme, and the spice threads the dessert. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Campari|Mushroom Bisque": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream -- amaro bitterness on dairy cream reads metallic — no bridge from herbal sharp to soft fat. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; one of those is the move. Campari lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Campari|Mushrooms": "Campari with mushrooms — ruby bitter against earthy umami. Strong; aperitivo bitterness frames the mushrooms rather than deepening them the way Fernet Branca would.",
  "Campari|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Peanut Butter Brownie: peanut butter and cocoa meet bitter orange-rhubarb. Works; Campari is lighter than sipping amari want to be against PB density.",
  "Campari|Porterhouse": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook underclubs the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character -- amaro reads light against the marbled char — the cut deserves wine or whiskey weight. The plate deserves Odette Cabernet Sauvignon, Weller 12 Year, or Domaine du Grand Tinel, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Campari for another course.",
  "Campari|Prime Tartare": "Campari with the tartare — bitter orange-rhubarb against raw beef. Excellent; the Negroni-spine amaro lifts tartare's minerality with aperitivo brightness the classic amari can't match.",
  "Campari|Rainbow Trout": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bitter herbs flatten delicate fish — the protein can't lift the amaro's register. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|Roast Half Chicken": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast -- bitter aperitivo is for before or after the meal — not on a main protein. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Campari on the steak course instead.",
  "Campari|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Campari belongs on the steak course.",
  "Campari|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bitter herbs flatten delicate fish — the protein can't lift the amaro's register. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook doubles down on the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- bitter herbs and a green vegetable side compound the same register — no contrast. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|Seafood Tower": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bitter aperitivo flattens the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|Seared Scallops": "Campari with seared scallops — bitter orange-rhubarb against scallop delicacy. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Campari|Seasonal Soup": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook jars against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build -- bitter botanicals on savory broth pull against the salt-and-spice frame without resolving. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Campari lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Campari|Seasonal Vegetables": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate -- bitter aperitivo on the supporting side reads as wrong register for the course. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Campari belongs on the steak course.",
  "Campari|Shrimp Bisque": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- amaro bitterness on dairy cream reads metallic — no bridge from herbal sharp to soft fat. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; one of those is the move. Campari belongs on the steak course.",
  "Campari|Shrimp Cocktail": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- amaro bitterness on cold shellfish flattens the delicate brine — needs sparkling instead. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Campari on the steak course instead.",
  "Campari|Swordfish": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bitter aperitivo is for before or after the meal — not on a main protein. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|The Tomahawk": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the Tomahawk's theatrical bone-in marbling and smoky char -- bitter aperitivo belongs before or after the meal, not alongside the steak. The plate deserves Corazon Stagg, Opus One, or George T. Stagg, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the better calls are above. Campari belongs on another course.",
  "Campari|Tomato Basil": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook jars against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid -- bitter botanicals on savory broth pull against the salt-and-spice frame without resolving. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Le Garenne Rosé, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Campari on the steak course instead.",
  "Campari|Truffle Fries": "Campari with truffle fries — ruby bitter against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; aperitivo bitterness against earthy-rich fries is Italian bar logic — this outperforms on a side where other amari just coexist.",
  "Campari|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bitter botanicals fight the savory sear — bitter against char without resolution. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Campari|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Le Garenne Rosé, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Asparagus": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character sits alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the smooth Canadian register carries the asparagus, and the gentle rye thread underlines the side. Works; boutique at matched register.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Au Gratin Potatoes": "CC 43 Year with the au gratin — aged collector Canadian against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; CC 43 Year is over-specified for a side; save the rare bottle for the main.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Beignets": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the Canadian whisky weight matches the beignets, and the soft profile rounds the dessert. Works; the extra proof overpowers this dish.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Bone Marrow": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character finds neutral with the bone marrow's unctuous rendered-marrow richness: the easygoing Canadian character handles the rich marrow, and the soft profile rounds the starter. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for a soup — save the collector bottle for the main course; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Bone-In Filet": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character finds neutral with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the rye-blended Canadian body sits with the bone-enhanced filet, and the soft profile rounds the cut. Works; grain notes don't really engage the soup but don't clash.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Broccoli Cheddar": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the smooth Canadian register carries the broccoli cheddar, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; wine-cask complexity gives the dessert layered premium character.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Broccolini": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character sits alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the smooth Canadian register carries the broccolini, and the light caramel edge frames the side. Works; milestone-collector wasted on salad.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Brussels and Belly": "CC 43 Year with Brussels + Belly — ultra-premium aged Canadian against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; CC 43 Year's aged character meets the glaze at collector register.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Burrata": "CC 43 Year with burrata — rare aged Canadian against fresh dairy. Avoid; save the collector bottle — burrata doesn't deserve a 43yr pour.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Butternut Squash": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the smooth Canadian register carries the squash bisque, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; extended maturation gives the dessert home-state aged character.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Carrot Cake": "CC 43 Year with carrot cake — 43yr aged Canadian against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; CC 43 Year's aged depth is the featured Canadian-carrot-cake pairing at collector register — the aged dried-fruit notes marry the cake's spice.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Cheesecake": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character leans against the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the Canadian whisky weight matches the cheesecake, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; own-plus-sourced covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Chilean Seabass": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Canadian Club 43 Year lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Chocolate Brownie": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character finds neutral with the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight: the Canadian whisky weight matches the brownie, and the light caramel edge frames the dessert. Works; Voyage 23 frames the two-cut plate at ocean-finish register.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Chocolate Cake": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the easygoing Canadian character handles the chocolate cake, and the soft profile rounds the dessert. Works; distinctive character doesn't drive.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Clam Chowder": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the easygoing Canadian character handles the chowder, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; collector-bottle depth gives ultra-premium character.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Cowboy Ribeye": "CC 43 Year with the cowboy ribeye — rare 43yr aged Canadian against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Strong; CC 43 Year's aged depth handles the ribeye at collector register — where Crown Royal and CC feel underspecified, the 43 gives the cut proper weight.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Crab Cake": "CC 43 Year with crab cake — 43yr ultra-premium Canadian against delicate lump crab. Works; save the collector bottle for the protein course.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Creamed Spinach": "CC 43 Year with creamed spinach — ultra-premium aged Canadian against dairy-rich side. Works; CC 43 Year is over-specified for a side — save the rare bottle for the main course.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Creamy Potato": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character sits alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the Canadian whisky weight matches the potato soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the richer pour finds more with the dessert than Original brings.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Creme Brulee": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character reads alongside the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the Canadian whisky weight matches the brulee, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; annual-release wasted on salad.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Escargot": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character reads alongside the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the Canadian whisky weight matches the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Works; Vermont-brand at matched register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Faroe Island Salmon": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Save the Canadian Club 43 Year for the steak course.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Filet Mignon": "CC 43 Year with the filet — rare aged Canadian Club (43 years), ultra-premium Canadian, collector-register. Excellent; CC 43 Year's rare aged character is the featured Canadian-filet pairing at collector register — 43 years of aging is unusual for Canadian whisky, and the depth frames tenderloin with distinctive aged-Canadian gravitas.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|French Onion": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character leans against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the blended whisky body wraps the French onion, and the gentle rye thread underlines the bowl. Works; GTS is over-specified for a side — save the collector bottle.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Grilled Caesar": "CC 43 Year with the grilled Caesar — rare aged Canadian against charred romaine and anchovy. Strong; CC 43 Year's aged character meets the char at collector register; CC's entry grain-forward is still the featured Canadian-Caesar at lower register.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Gumbo": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character finds neutral with the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the Canadian whisky weight matches the gumbo, and the soft profile rounds the bowl. Works; the Millennium's register overshoots the dessert's.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character leans against the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the blended whisky body wraps the honey carrots, and the oak softens the caramelized sugar. Works; mature honey slightly over-specified for dessert simplicity.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|House Wedge": "CC 43 Year with the House Wedge — aged collector Canadian against iceberg and bleu. Excellent; CC 43 Year's 43yr character engages the bleu at collector register.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Kansas City": "CC 43 Year with the KC — 43yr aged ultra-premium Canadian against an 18oz strip. Excellent; CC 43 Year's aged depth handles strip marbling at collector register — where CC handles it at heritage register, the 43 closes with rare-aged gravity.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Loaded Potato": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character leans against the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the rye-blended Canadian body sits with the loaded potato soup, and the oak threads the cream. Works; pour is a touch over-specified for this dish.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Lobster Mac": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the blended whisky body wraps the lobster mac, and the oak softens the cream. Works; complexity wasted on salad.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Market Fish": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Canadian Club 43 Year for the steak course.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Mocha Creme": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character reads alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the blended whisky body wraps the mocha creme, and the oak softens the cream. Works; cleaner than wheated versions but not exceptional.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Mushroom Bisque": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the easygoing Canadian character handles the mushroom bisque, and the oak depth meets the umami. Works; HH 20 is over-specified for an app; save the collector bottle for the main.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Mushrooms": "CC 43 Year with mushrooms — rare 43yr aged Canadian against earthy umami. Excellent; CC 43 Year's aged character threads mushroom earthiness at collector register.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character reads alongside the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the rye-blended Canadian body sits with the PB brownie, and the easy Canadian register softens the dessert. Works; grain notes don't really engage the soup but don't clash.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Porterhouse": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character reads alongside the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character: the Canadian whisky weight matches the dual-cut steak, and the soft profile rounds the cut. Works; Portwood is over-specified for a side — save for main course.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Prime Tartare": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character finds neutral with the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami: the smooth Canadian register carries the tartare, and the oak underlines the umami weight. Works; richer profile overshoots the dessert's delicacy; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Rainbow Trout": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character flattens the trout's delicate flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Canadian Club 43 Year lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Roast Half Chicken": "CC 43 Year with the chicken — ultra-premium aged Canadian against roasted poultry. Excellent; CC 43 Year's aged depth frames chicken at collector register — Crown Royal handles this pairing at crowd-pleasing register, the CC 43 elevates it.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character sits alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the blended whisky body wraps the chickpea soup, and the easy Canadian register softens the bowl. Works; smooth gentle match.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character flattens the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Canadian Club 43 Year for the steak course.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character sits alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the blended whisky body wraps the garlic spinach, and the gentle rye thread underlines the side. Works; boutique-release covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Seafood Tower": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Canadian Club 43 Year lands on the steak course — not here.",
