  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Shrimp Cocktail": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character smothers the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Canadian Club 43 Year on the steak course instead.",
  "Canadian Club 43 Year|Swordfish": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon's sweet weight crowds the rare crust's clean char. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Canadian Club 43 Year on the steak course instead.",
