  "Carrot Cake|Corazón del Sol Malbec": "Corazón del Sol Malbec's plush Malbec with plum-and-violet weight jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Corazón del Sol Malbec for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Corpse Reviver": "Corpse Reviver's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- light cocktail citrus is wrong direction for the dessert's richness. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a light cocktail. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Corpse Reviver on the steak course instead.",
  "Carrot Cake|Courvoisier Cognac": "Courvoisier with carrot cake — traditional Jarnac cognac against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Courvoisier's oak threads the spice cleanly at drier register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Cowboy Ribeye": "The cowboy ribeye into the carrot cake -- the rendered cap-fat hands off to spiced cake and cream-cheese frosting, walnut crunch on the close. Works; the bold cut and the spiced cake share weight without crowding.",
  "Carrot Cake|Crab Cake": "The crab cake alongside the carrot cake -- restrained meets sugar, the close composes light. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Carrot Cake|Cragganmore 12": "Cragganmore 12 with carrot cake — layered Speyside against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Cragganmore's complexity threads the cake's spice with Classic Malt distinction.",
  "Carrot Cake|Creamed Spinach": "The creamed spinach alongside the carrot cake -- rich cream gives way to sweet, the close lands generously. Works; the contrast holds, neither course overshadows the other.",
  "Carrot Cake|Creamy Potato": "Creamy Potato and the carrot cake -- cream-and-sugar build the close, the meal finishes generous. Works; either timing holds, the table builds either way.",
  "Carrot Cake|Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée": "Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée's Willamette Pinot elegance clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- red structure flattens the spice cake's cinnamon-and-cream-cheese delicacy. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée on the steak course instead.",
  "Carrot Cake|Crown Royal": "Crown Royal with carrot cake — vanilla-honey Canadian against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; Crown Royal's vanilla-honey meets the cake at crowd-pleasing register; Canadian Club 43 Year's aged depth edges this dessert.",
  "Carrot Cake|Cucumber Gimlet": "Cucumber Gimlet's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- light cocktail citrus is wrong direction for the dessert's richness. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a light cocktail. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Cucumber Gimlet belongs on the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Dalmore 12": "Dalmore 12 with carrot cake — sherry-finish Highland against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Dalmore's Matusalem-sherry dried-fruit and orange-marmalade marry the cake's raisins and spice — the featured Highland Scotch-carrot-cake pairing, parallel to Macallan 12's sherried-Speyside approach.",
  "Carrot Cake|Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge": "Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge's Loire Valley Pinot Noir clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- red structure flattens the spice cake's cinnamon-and-cream-cheese delicacy. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge belongs on the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Darioush Cabernet Franc": "Darioush Cabernet Franc's herbaceous Cab Franc with red-fruit and bell-pepper clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- red structure flattens the spice cake's cinnamon-and-cream-cheese delicacy. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Darioush Cabernet Franc lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Carrot Cake|Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Detroit City Gin": "Detroit City Gin's Detroit urban-craft gin clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- juniper-citrus and warm cake spices pull in opposite directions. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Detroit City Gin on the steak course instead.",
  "Carrot Cake|Detroit City Vodka": "Detroit City Vodka's hometown craft vodka falls short of the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a vodka. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Detroit City Vodka for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Dewar's 15": "Dewar's 15 with carrot cake — aged sherry-finish Dewar's against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Dewar's 15's sherry-cask dried-fruit is the featured Dewar's-carrot-cake pairing — parallel to Monkey Shoulder's Speyside-malt fruit for the blended-Scotch-carrot-cake lane at aged register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Dewar's White Label": "Dewar's White Label with carrot cake — Aberfeldy-core blend against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; Dewar's White's honey-vanilla meets the cake at benchmark register; Monkey Shoulder's Speyside-malt dried-fruit edges this pairing.",
  "Carrot Cake|Disaronno": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Disaronno. Strong; amaretto-marzipan-almond plays cake spice at Italian register — almond-cake pairing classic. Gold standard; the recommendation that earns the regular.",
  "Carrot Cake|Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye": "Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye with carrot cake — craft sourced rye against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; craft rye spice and cake spice find each other.",
  "Carrot Cake|Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Doctor Bird Jamaica. Excellent; the Jamaican pot-still funk brings tropical-fruit dimension to the carrot-cake spice register — most character-forward rum-dessert on the menu.",
  "Carrot Cake|Domaine Serene Grand Cheval": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- red structure flattens the spice cake's cinnamon-and-cream-cheese delicacy. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval on the steak course instead.",
  "Carrot Cake|Domaine Tempier Bandol": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Domaine Tempier Bandol on the steak course instead.",
  "Carrot Cake|Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé": "Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé's crisp white-wine character clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- a dry white belongs with the main course, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a white wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Domaine du Grand Tinel": "Domaine du Grand Tinel's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Domaine du Grand Tinel lands on the steak course — not here.",
