  "Carrot Cake|Elk Cove Pinot Blanc": "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc's crisp white-wine character clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- a dry white belongs with the main course, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a white wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Elk Cove Pinot Blanc for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Elmer T. Lee": "Elmer T. Lee with carrot cake — smooth single-barrel against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; gentle composed match.",
  "Carrot Cake|Empress 1908 Gin": "Empress 1908 Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Empress 1908 Gin for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Epoch Ingenuity": "Epoch Ingenuity's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Epoch Ingenuity belongs on the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Escargot": "Escargot and the carrot cake -- the sweet register lifts the umami, the contrast holds without crowding. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Carrot Cake|Espresso Martini": "Tito's, espresso, Grind Espresso Liqueur, Averna amaro, vanilla syrup, Angostura. The Averna's bitter herbal edge meets carrot-cake warm spice and the vanilla echoes the bean-paste frosting. Peak cocktail route when guest wants coffee with a spiced dessert. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Carrot Cake|Espresso Old Fashioned": "Buffalo Trace, Buffalo Bourbon Cream, Frangelico, espresso, brown sugar, Angostura. The brown sugar ties into the cake's build; Frangelico's hazelnut meets the warm-spice profile; espresso anchors. Strong cocktail route for guests wanting spirit-forward with spiced dessert.",
  "Carrot Cake|Evening Land Seven Springs": "Evening Land Seven Springs' red-fruit-and-spice elegance clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- red structure flattens the spice cake's cinnamon-and-cream-cheese delicacy. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Evening Land Seven Springs belongs on the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon": "Carrot Cake: the carrot cake's warm-spice, cream-cheese indulgence meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. Dark chocolate and spice echo the bold red's fruit, but the tannin fights the sugar unless the dessert is dry-cocoa-bitter. Works when the dessert leans bitter rather than sweet.",
  "Carrot Cake|Far Niente Chardonnay": "Far Niente Chardonnay's estate Napa Chardonnay character clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- a dry white belongs with the main course, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a white wine. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Far Niente Chardonnay belongs on the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Faroe Island Salmon": "The salmon into the carrot cake -- the pan-finished Atlantic flesh hands off to spiced cake and cream-cheese frosting, walnut crunch on the close. Works; the rich fish and the spice cake share the meal at separate registers.",
  "Carrot Cake|Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi": "Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- red structure flattens the spice cake's cinnamon-and-cream-cheese delicacy. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Faust Napa Valley Cabernet": "Faust Napa Valley Cabernet's structured Napa Cab with cassis depth jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Faust Napa Valley Cabernet for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía": "Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Fernet Branca": "Fernet Branca with carrot cake — 27-herb bitter against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; Branca finds the spice notes but the cream cheese softens less than with Averna or Montenegro.",
  "Carrot Cake|Fernet Menta": "Fernet Menta with carrot cake — cooling mint Fernet against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; mint threads through spice cleanly.",
  "Carrot Cake|Filet Mignon": "The filet into the carrot cake -- the butter-tender 10oz yields to spiced cake and cream-cheese frosting, walnut adding crunch on the close. Works; the spice-and-frosting weight outsizes the steak, but the table builds cleanly across courses.",
  "Carrot Cake|Fireball Whisky": "Fireball with carrot cake — cinnamon on cinnamon is the whole play. The cream cheese frosting absorbs the whisky heat and the spice registers line up cleanly. This is the Fireball pairing that actually earns its place on the dessert list. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Carrot Cake|Fisher Unity Pinot Noir": "Fisher Unity Pinot Noir's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Fisher Unity Pinot Noir for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Four Roses Small Batch Select": "Four Roses Small Batch Select with carrot cake — 104-proof premium 4R against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; concentrated blend slightly over-specified.",
  "Carrot Cake|Four Roses Yellow Label": "Four Roses Yellow Label with carrot cake — floral-and-honey entry bourbon against cream cheese and cinnamon. The floral notes pick up the cake's raisins lightly; a friendly dessert pairing within the entry tier. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Carrot Cake|Fox & Oden": "Fox & Oden with carrot cake — craft small-batch against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; gentle composed match.",
  "Carrot Cake|Fox & Oden Double Oaked": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Detroit Double Oaked. Strong; Fox & Oden's intensified-caramel threads the cake at Double-Oaked register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Frangelico": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Frangelico. Strong; hazelnut-vanilla-cocoa plays cake spice at Italian-liqueur register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Freemark Abbey Bosché": "Freemark Abbey Bosché's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Freemark Abbey Bosché on the steak course instead.",
  "Carrot Cake|French 75": "French 75's gin-and-Champagne lift with citrus snap clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- light cocktail citrus is wrong direction for the dessert's richness. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a light cocktail. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the French 75 for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|French Onion": "French Onion and the carrot cake -- the sweet register lifts the umami, the contrast holds without crowding. Works; sequence them as opener and close or share the table, no clash.",
  "Carrot Cake|Frias Block 5": "Frias Block 5's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- red structure flattens the spice cake's cinnamon-and-cream-cheese delicacy. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Frias Block 5 for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo": "G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo's high-acid Nebbiolo with rose-and-tar grip clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- red structure flattens the spice cake's cinnamon-and-cream-cheese delicacy. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Carrot Cake|G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti": "The Moscato's stone-fruit and honey notes echo the cake's brown sugar and warm spice, while the effervescence lifts through the dense cream cheese frosting so it reads as airy rather than thick. That interplay makes the spice linger longer on the finish than it would with a still wine. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Carrot Cake|G4 Blanco": "G4 Blanco's unaged blanco-tequila lift with agave-citrus snap falls short of the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- light spirit reads thin against dessert sweetness. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a light spirit. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the G4 Blanco for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|G4 High Proof": "G4 High Proof's rested-agave body finds neutral with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the rested-agave depth sits with the carrot cake, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the dessert. Works; multi-cask complexity over-specified.",
  "Carrot Cake|Garavogue Irish Whiskey": "Garavogue with carrot cake — western Ireland craft Irish against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; Garavogue's small-batch character threads the cake at craft-Irish register.",
  "Carrot Cake|George T. Stagg": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet BTAC. Works; GTS is over-specified for dessert — save the collector bottle for the ribeye/Tomahawk.",
  "Carrot Cake|Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon": "Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Ghost Block Zinfandel": "Ghost Block Zinfandel's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Ghost Block Zinfandel for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Glenfiddich 12": "Glenfiddich 12 with carrot cake — gateway Speyside against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Fiddich's honey-apple finds the cake's raisins and spice with approachable character.",
  "Carrot Cake|Glenfiddich 14": "Glenfiddich 14 with carrot cake — new-charred-oak Speyside against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Fiddich 14's baking-spice character marries the cake's cinnamon naturally — more dimensional than the 12's honey-apple approach.",
  "Carrot Cake|Glenfiddich 18": "Glenfiddich 18 with carrot cake — Oloroso sherry-cask Speyside against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Oloroso dried fruit + cinnamon + nutmeg marry the cake's raisins and spice — the featured Speyside-carrot-cake match in the aged batch, edging even Balvenie 12 Am Oak.",
  "Carrot Cake|Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with carrot cake — French Cuvée cask finish against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Gran Cru's brioche-pastry notes marry the cake's raisins and spice with champagne-style pastry elegance — unique to this 23yr expression.",
  "Carrot Cake|Glenglassaugh 12": "Glenglassaugh 12 with carrot cake — Sandend coast Highland against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Glenglassaugh 12's tropical-fruit-and-honey marries the cake's raisins and spice with distinctive coastal register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Glenlivet 12": "Glenlivet 12 with carrot cake — honey-pineapple Speyside against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Glenlivet's tropical-honey notes meet the cake's spice with benchmark finesse.",
  "Carrot Cake|Glenmorangie 10": "Glenmorangie 10 with carrot cake — Highland bourbon-cask entry against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; Glenmorangie 10's vanilla-honey meets the cake at entry register; Dalmore 12's sherry-finish is the featured Highland-carrot-cake match.",
  "Carrot Cake|Glenmorangie 18": "Glenmorangie 18 with carrot cake — 18yr Highland with Oloroso sherry finish against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Glenmorangie 18's Oloroso-cask dried-fruit and spice marry the cake's raisins and cinnamon — a featured aged-Highland carrot-cake pairing alongside Dalmore 12's sherry-finish approach.",
  "Carrot Cake|Graham's 10 Year Tawny": "10-year oak-cask oxidative Tawny — Graham's entry-point, dried apricot, walnut, toffee, gentle spice, smooth finish. The gentle spice echoes allspice-and-cinnamon directly and the toffee plays with cream-cheese frosting's vanilla-bean paste. Peak Tawny for carrot cake — spice-on-spice harmony. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Carrot Cake|Graham's 20 Year Tawny": "20-year oak-cask oxidative Tawny — Graham's step-up, concentrated dried fruit, roasted hazelnut, orange peel, silky long finish. The orange peel echoes allspice-cinnamon-brightness and the roasted hazelnut plays with cream-cheese frosting. Peak step-up Tawny for carrot cake — twenty-year depth on the spiced bake. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Carrot Cake|Graham's 2017 Vintage Port": "2017 declared-vintage Port — Graham's bottle-aged, dense inky, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, powerful structured. The violet lifts allspice-cinnamon aromatics and the dark chocolate plays with cream-cheese frosting. Strong Vintage Port for carrot cake — Tawny's spice-on-spice match fits softer.",
  "Carrot Cake|Gran Patron Platinum": "Gran Patron Platinum's silver-spirit lift with agave-citrus edge leans against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the silver-tequila register lifts the carrot cake, and the agave-citrus thread frames the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Carrot Cake|Grand Marnier": "Carrot Cake: the carrot cake's warm-spice, cream-cheese indulgence meets this sweet cream liqueur's dessert-adjacent lushness. Sweet liqueur's dessert-adjacent sweetness amplifies the dessert — doubles up on sugar. Strong when the dessert is restrained.",
  "Carrot Cake|Gray Whale Gin": "Gray Whale Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Gray Whale Gin on the steak course instead.",
  "Carrot Cake|Green Chartreuse": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Green Chartreuse. Works; the 130-botanical spice-herbal character amplifies the cake's own spice register at digestif level.",
  "Carrot Cake|Grey Goose Vodka": "Grey Goose Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a vodka. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Grey Goose Vodka belongs on the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Grilled Caesar": "The Caesar alongside the carrot cake -- sugar plays against the savory weight, the table earns its lift. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Carrot Cake|Gumbo": "Gumbo and the carrot cake -- different registers compose without clash. Works; sequence them as opener and close or share the table, no clash.",
  "Carrot Cake|Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet": "Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet on the steak course instead.",
  "Carrot Cake|HDW 100 Vodka": "HDW 100 Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a vodka. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. HDW 100 Vodka belongs on the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Hakushu 12 Year": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character reads alongside the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the precise Japanese craft body wraps the carrot cake, and the precision rounds the dessert. Works; accessible gentle match.",
  "Carrot Cake|Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with carrot cake — BT single-barrel against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; the complex profile is slightly over-specified for the dessert.",
  "Carrot Cake|Hangar 1 Vodka": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a vodka. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Hangar 1 Vodka for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Head Fake": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build sits beside the carrot cake's spiced cream cheese — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; safe call, no friction. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Carrot Cake|Heaven Hill 20 Year": "Heaven Hill 20 Year with carrot cake — HH 20yr collector against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; HH 20's aged dried-fruit threads the cake at collector register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond": "Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond with carrot cake — 100-proof traditional against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; the BIB oak and vanilla frame the cake cleanly, distinct from wheated-cake-spice pairings.",
  "Carrot Cake|Heaven's Door 10 Year": "Heaven's Door 10 Year with carrot cake — 100-proof 10-year against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; aged premium slightly over-specified.",
  "Carrot Cake|Heitz Martha's Vineyard": "Heitz Martha's Vineyard's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- red structure flattens the spice cake's cinnamon-and-cream-cheese delicacy. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Heitz Martha's Vineyard for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Heitz Trailside Vineyard": "Heitz Trailside Vineyard's Napa-icon Cab character clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- red structure flattens the spice cake's cinnamon-and-cream-cheese delicacy. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Heitz Trailside Vineyard belongs on the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Hendricks Flora Adora": "Hendricks Flora Adora's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hendricks Flora Adora lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Carrot Cake|Hendricks Gin": "Hendricks Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Hendricks Gin for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Hendricks Grand Cabaret": "Hendricks Grand Cabaret's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Hendricks Grand Cabaret for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Hendricks Neptunia": "Hendricks Neptunia's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- juniper-citrus and warm cake spices pull in opposite directions. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Hendricks Neptunia for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Hendricks Orbium": "Hendricks Orbium's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- juniper-citrus and warm cake spices pull in opposite directions. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hendricks Orbium lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Carrot Cake|Hennessy Cognac": "Hennessy with carrot cake — ubiquitous cognac against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Hennessy's dried-fruit and vanilla meet the cake's raisins and spice with benchmark comfort.",
  "Carrot Cake|Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with carrot cake — aged bonded HH against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; BIB slightly over-specified.",
  "Carrot Cake|Hibiki Japanese Harmony": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony leans against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the Japanese whisky balance frames the carrot cake, and the Japanese-craft balance underlines the dessert. Works; OGD 16 handles dessert density at distinctive register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Honey Roasted Carrots": "The honey carrots alongside the carrot cake -- both bring carrot as the headline. Avoid; one is enough. Pair the honey carrots with Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée; pair the carrot cake with Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny.",
  "Carrot Cake|House Wedge": "The wedge and the carrot cake -- the wedge's iceberg-and-bleu cool crunch bookends with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Carrot Cake|I.W. Harper 15 Year": "I.W. Harper 15 with carrot cake — 15yr historic-KY against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; IW Harper 15's aged cherry-oak threads the cake at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Il Colle Prosecco Superiore": "Veneto Glera, Conegliano Valdobbiadene DOCG — floral, white peach, green apple, clean citrus. The Prosecco's lift cuts cream-cheese frosting without adding sweetness; works when the table wants bubbles rather than a dessert wine. Serviceable finisher. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Carrot Cake|Inhibited": "Tito's, Kahlúa, Bailey's, chocolate liqueur, espresso, chocolate-drizzled glass. Rich coffee-cream cocktail — the Bailey's cream mirrors the cream-cheese frosting and the warm-spice notes in the coffee roast echo the cake's cinnamon. Strong cocktail route.",
  "Carrot Cake|Inverroche Gin": "Inverroche Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Inverroche Gin for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Iron Fish Gin": "Iron Fish Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- juniper-citrus and warm cake spices pull in opposite directions. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Iron Fish Gin for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet northern MI mezcal-cask. Works; Ironfish Mezcal threads the cake at Michigan-hometown register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Isaac Bowman Port Finish": "Isaac Bowman Port Finish with carrot cake — Virginia port-finished bourbon against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Isaac Bowman's port-derived jammy-fruit threads the cake at Virginia-heritage register.",
  "Carrot Cake|J Davies Ferrington Vineyards": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards' silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. J Davies Ferrington Vineyards lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Carrot Cake|J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Jack Daniel's 12 Year": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with carrot cake — 12yr aged Tennessee against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; JD 12's aged depth threads the cake at premium register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Jack Daniel's Bonded": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet 100-proof Tennessee. Works; JD Bonded's backbone threads the cake at Bonded register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Jack Daniel's Old No. 7": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7 with carrot cake — Tennessee whiskey against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; Old No. 7's vanilla-caramel meets the cake at iconic register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Jack Daniel's Sinatra Select": "JD Sinatra Select with carrot cake — Sinatra Barrels Tennessee against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; Sinatra Select's grooved-barrel character threads the cake at Sinatra-tribute register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Jameson Irish Whiskey": "Jameson with carrot cake — smooth triple-distilled Irish against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; Jameson's sherry-cask character threads the cake at entry register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir": "Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis": "Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis' Burgundy Chablis flinty minerality clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- a dry white belongs with the main course, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a white wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E.": "Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E. with carrot cake — limited-edition sea-aged against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; Marian McLain L.E. threads the cake at collector register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Jefferson's Ocean Voyage 23": "Jefferson's Ocean Voyage 23 with carrot cake — Voyage #23 sea-aged against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; Voyage 23 threads the cake at ocean-finish register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Jefferson's Reserve": "Jefferson's Reserve with carrot cake — blended honey and vanilla against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; Jefferson's VR Twin Oak brings deeper oak for this dessert when the call is richness.",
  "Carrot Cake|Jefferson's Reserve VR Twin Oak": "Jefferson's Reserve VR Twin Oak with carrot cake — Twin Oak complexity against cream cheese and cinnamon. The deeper oak and vanilla frame the cake's spice; a premium non-wheated dessert pairing. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Carrot Cake|Jim Beam Black Label": "Jim Beam Black Label with carrot cake — aged Beam's oak and vanilla against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; the aging lets the pour sit with the cake cleanly.",
  "Carrot Cake|Jim Beam White Label": "Jim Beam White Label with carrot cake — entry caramel-vanilla against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; accessible dessert pairing at the entry register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Johnnie Walker Black": "JW Black with carrot cake — 12yr balanced JW against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; JW Black's balanced character threads the cake; Monkey Shoulder's Speyside-malt fruit and Dewar's 15's sherry-finish are the featured blended-Scotch-carrot-cake matches.",
  "Carrot Cake|Johnnie Walker Blue": "JW Blue with carrot cake — 60+yr rare-cask JW against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; save the bottle for the protein course — Dewar's 15 or Monkey Shoulder is the right Scotch for carrot cake at appropriate register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Johnnie Walker Red": "JW Red with carrot cake — bold-smoke entry JW against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; JW Red's smoke contrasts the cake's sweetness — distinctive but not featured; Monkey Shoulder's Speyside-malt fruit is the blended-Scotch-carrot-cake match.",
  "Carrot Cake|Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon": "Carrot Cake: the carrot cake's warm-spice, cream-cheese indulgence meets this elegant red's cherry-bright, silky-tannin frame. Cherry fruit echoes dark chocolate, but the elegant red's acidity fights refined sugar. Works for a specific guest — fruit-forward cocoa.",
  "Carrot Cake|Joseph Mellot Sancerre": "Joseph Mellot Sancerre's classic Loire Sauvignon Blanc clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- a dry white belongs with the main course, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a white wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Joseph Mellot Sancerre for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Jubilation by Colgin": "Jubilation by Colgin's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Jubilation by Colgin lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Carrot Cake|Jung and Wulff Guyana": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Jung and Wulff Guyana. Excellent; the earthy-woody Demerara depth threads carrot-cake spice at heavy-molasses register — the deeper, more brooding rum pairing.",
  "Carrot Cake|Jung and Wulff Trinidad": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Jung and Wulff Trinidad. Excellent; the refined-caramel character threads carrot-cake spice at cleaner-than-Demerara register.",
