  "Carrot Cake|Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the high-rye spice register matches the carrot cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; save the bottle for the protein course — a soup is wrong for a $200 pour.",
  "Carrot Cake|Kentucky Owl Confiscated": "Kentucky Owl Confiscated with carrot cake — KO Confiscated against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; craft-blend finds cake spice with KO narrative character.",
  "Carrot Cake|Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's": "Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's with carrot cake — luxury Irish against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for dessert — Redbreast 21's aged sherry-cask is the featured Irish-carrot-cake match.",
  "Carrot Cake|Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône": "Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Ketel One Vodka": "Ketel One Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a vodka. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Ketel One Vodka for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Knickerbocker Gin": "Knickerbocker Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- juniper-citrus and warm cake spices pull in opposite directions. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Knickerbocker Gin on the steak course instead.",
  "Carrot Cake|Knob Creek": "Knob Creek with carrot cake — 100-proof high-rye spice against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; the rye spice and cake spice find each other in a way wheated caramel can't.",
