  "Carrot Cake|Mount Gay Rum": "Mount Gay Rum's clean silver register finds neutral with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the unaged body brightens the carrot cake, and the Caribbean-rum register underlines the dessert. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Muga Reserva": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Muga Reserva on the steak course instead.",
