  "Carrot Cake|Old Elk Cigar Cut": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Fort Collins craft bourbon. Works; Old Elk Cigar Cut threads the cake at cigar-companion register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Old Emmer": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet ancient-grain wheated bourbon. Strong; Old Emmer's emmer-wheat character meets the cake at craft-wheated register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Old Fitzgerald 7 Year": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with carrot cake — wheated BIB's honey against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; the bonded weight adds dimension the 90-proof wheated pours don't bring.",
  "Carrot Cake|Old Fitzgerald 9 Year": "Old Fitzgerald 9 Year with carrot cake — aged wheated BIB's mature honey against cream cheese and cinnamon. The 9-year's depth earns the cake as excellent where the 7-year is only strong; a standout wheated-BIB dessert pairing. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Old Grand-Dad 16 Year": "OGD 16 with carrot cake — aged OGD high-rye against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; OGD 16's rye-forward aged spice is the featured aged-bourbon-carrot-cake pairing — the rye spice marries the cake's cinnamon naturally where non-rye aged bourbons don't.",
  "Carrot Cake|Opus One": "Opus One's Bordeaux-blend allocated-icon power flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Opus One for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Our Lady of Guadalupe Acolytes": "Our Lady of Guadalupe Acolytes' crisp white-wine character clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- a dry white belongs with the main course, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a white wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Our Lady of Guadalupe Acolytes belongs on the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Pablo Sour": "Pablo Sour's citrus-lemon build reads alongside the carrot cake's spiced cream cheese — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the cream. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Carrot Cake|Paloma": "Paloma's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- light cocktail citrus is wrong direction for the dessert's richness. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a light cocktail. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Paloma lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Carrot Cake|Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character leans against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the carrot cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; wine-cask over-specified.",
  "Carrot Cake|Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with carrot cake — HH collector against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; Parker's Heritage 16th meets the cake at annual-release register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Patron Anejo": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Patron Anejo. Strong; American-oak vanilla-caramel amplifies cake spice at accessible-premium register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Patron Silver": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift falls short of the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- light spirit reads thin against dessert sweetness. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a light spirit. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Patron Silver on the steak course instead.",
  "Carrot Cake|Patron XO Cafe": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Patron XO Cafe. Works; the drier-tequila-coffee profile plays cake spice at spirit-forward register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Paul Bara Grand Rosé Brut": "Paul Bara Grand Rosé Brut's bright sparkling effervescence clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- a dry sparkling belongs with the opener, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a sparkling. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Paul Bara Grand Rosé Brut for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Peju Cabernet Sauvignon": "Peju Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Peju Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Pierre Ferrand Cognac": "Pierre Ferrand with carrot cake — artisanal Grande Champagne against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Ferrand's honey-floral marries the spice and raisins with craft character.",
  "Carrot Cake|Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut": "Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut's grand cru blanc-de-blancs with mineral lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- a dry sparkling belongs with the opener, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a sparkling. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut belongs on the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Pikesville Rye": "Pikesville Rye with carrot cake — 110-proof HH rye against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; bold rye spice finds cake spice at high-impact register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Pineau des Charentes": "Cognac-region fortified — Pineau des Charentes, grape juice plus young Cognac oak-aged, white grape, honey, warm nutty Cognac finish. The warm nutty Cognac matches allspice-cinnamon spice and the honey plays with cream-cheese frosting. Strong Pineau for carrot cake — Tawny's toffee fits the spice-on-spice match harder.",
  "Carrot Cake|Pio Cesare Barbaresco": "Pio Cesare Barbaresco's firm-tannin tar structure buries the delicate shellfish jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Pio Cesare Barbaresco on the steak course instead.",
  "Carrot Cake|Plymouth Gin": "Plymouth Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Plymouth Gin for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Poderi Aldo Conterno Nebbiolo": "Poderi Aldo Conterno Nebbiolo's high-acid Nebbiolo with rose-and-tar grip flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Poderi Aldo Conterno Nebbiolo for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Pommery Cuvée Louise": "Pommery Cuvée Louise's prestige cuvée Champagne elegance clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- a dry sparkling belongs with the opener, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a sparkling. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Pommery Cuvée Louise for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Porterhouse": "The Porterhouse into the carrot cake -- the dual strip-and-tender hands off to spiced cake and cream-cheese frosting, walnut crunch on the close. Works; the table-share build and the spice cake share the meal across courses.",
  "Carrot Cake|Prime Tartare": "Prime Tartare and the carrot cake -- sugar plays against the savory weight, the table earns its lift. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Carrot Cake|Quilt Cabernet Sauvignon": "Quilt Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Quilt Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Carrot Cake|RAEN Royal St Robert": "RAEN Royal St Robert's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the RAEN Royal St Robert for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Rainbow Trout": "The trout into the carrot cake -- the lemon-finished delicate flesh hands off to spiced cake and cream-cheese frosting, walnut crunch on the close. Works; the lighter main yields to the spiced close, the meal arcs cleanly.",
  "Carrot Cake|Raventós Cava de NIT Rosé Brut": "Raventós Cava de NIT Rosé Brut's bright sparkling effervescence clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- a dry sparkling belongs with the opener, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a sparkling. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Raventós Cava de NIT Rosé Brut on the steak course instead.",
  "Carrot Cake|Redbreast 12 Year": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet sherry+bourbon-cask pot still Irish. Works; Redbreast 12's sherry-cask and pot still spice thread the cake at premium register; Redbreast 21's aged depth edges this dessert pairing.",
  "Carrot Cake|Redbreast 21 Year": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet aged sherry-cask pot still Irish. Strong; Redbreast 21's aged sherry-cask dried-fruit is the featured Irish-carrot-cake pairing — 21 years of aging deepens what Redbreast 12 starts.",
  "Carrot Cake|Remus 15 Year Gatsby Reserve": "Remus 15 Gatsby with carrot cake — MGP high-rye Gatsby Reserve against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Remus 15's rye-spice + cherry is the featured MGP-aged-carrot-cake pairing — where OGD 16 brings aged-Beam rye-spice, Remus brings MGP's rye-and-cherry.",
  "Carrot Cake|Remy VSOP Cognac": "Rémy VSOP with carrot cake — elegant Grande Champagne cognac against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Rémy's floral notes thread the spice with refined character.",
  "Carrot Cake|Rey Sol Anejo": "Rey Sol Anejo with carrot cake — Moorish-inspired aged against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; distinctive-bottle meets the cake.",
  "Carrot Cake|Reyka Vodka": "Reyka Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a vodka. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Reyka Vodka for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Rishi's Old Antique": "Rishi's Old Antique with carrot cake — retailer-label against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; boutique-sourced finds cake spice with retailer-label character.",
  "Carrot Cake|Roast Half Chicken": "The chicken into the carrot cake -- the herb-butter bird hands off to spiced cake and cream-cheese frosting, walnut crunch on the close. Strong; the savory-herb main and the spiced cake share register cleanly across the meal.",
  "Carrot Cake|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea and the carrot cake -- separate registers share the plate, the contrast settles the build. Works; either timing holds, the table builds either way.",
  "Carrot Cake|Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs' bright sparkling effervescence clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- a dry sparkling belongs with the opener, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a sparkling. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs belongs on the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Roku Gin": "Roku Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Roku Gin for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Ron Zacapa Rum": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon spice meet Ron Zacapa. Excellent; the Solera-23 caramel and tropical-spice threads run directly into the carrot-cake warmth at luxury register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Russell's Reserve 10 Year": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with carrot cake — aged caramel-vanilla against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Carrot Cake|Salt-Cured Halibut": "The halibut into the carrot cake -- the salt-cured firm flesh hands off to spiced cake and cream-cheese frosting, walnut crunch on the close. Works; the cured main and the spiced dessert share the meal at separate registers.",
  "Carrot Cake|Sambuca": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Sambuca. Works; elderflower-anise-botanicals amplify cake spice at Italian-dessert register.",
  "Carrot Cake|San Simeon Stormwatch": "San Simeon Stormwatch's red-fruit-and-spice elegance flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. San Simeon Stormwatch belongs on the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir": "Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir belongs on the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "The garlic spinach alongside the carrot cake -- the bright register lifts the sweet, the meal closes clean. Works; the contrast holds, neither course overshadows the other.",
  "Carrot Cake|Sauternes Glass": "Sauternes — Sémillon-Sauvignon Blanc with noble rot (botrytis cinerea), apricot, honey, orange marmalade, luscious unctuous, bright acid. The orange marmalade lifts allspice-cinnamon spice and the apricot plays with cream-cheese frosting. Peak Sauternes for carrot cake — botrytis-on-spice match. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Carrot Cake|Sazerac": "Sazerac rye, Peychaud's, sugar, absinthe-rinsed glass. Spirit-forward classic — the anise-rye edge clashes with the cream-cheese frosting and overwhelms the cake's spice profile. Never pair Sazerac with dessert; keep it as a pre-dinner spirit-forward pour.",
  "Carrot Cake|Sazerac Rye": "Sazerac Rye with carrot cake — 90-proof iconic rye against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; the rye spice and cake spice find each other but not a marquee pairing.",
  "Carrot Cake|Scapegrace Fortuna": "Scapegrace Fortuna with carrot cake — NZ single malt against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; Fortuna's distinctive NZ terroir threads the cake at craft register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Scavino Barolo": "Piedmont Nebbiolo — tar, dried rose, firm tannin. Barolo obliterates the cake's spiced sweetness and cream-cheese frosting. Never pair — Barolo belongs with Tomahawk or Porterhouse. Route guest to tawny or Moscato for carrot cake.",
  "Carrot Cake|Schloss Vollrads Riesling": "Schloss Vollrads Riesling's crisp apricot-floral acidity holds with the carrot cake's spiced cream cheese — the dry white underclubs the dessert sugar, and the mineral edge lifts the dish. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Carrot Cake|Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters": "Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters' red-fruit-and-spice elegance flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Carrot Cake|Seafood Tower": "The seafood tower and the carrot cake -- the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup bookends with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Carrot Cake|Seared Scallops": "Seared Scallops and the carrot cake -- the savory course resolves into sugar, the meal closes with contrast. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Carrot Cake|Seasonal Soup": "The seasonal soup alongside the carrot cake -- a quiet call, the meal carries without strain. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Carrot Cake|Seasonal Vegetables": "Seasonal Vegetables and the carrot cake -- a clean call, no friction either way. Works; clean transition or together if the table wants.",
  "Carrot Cake|Sesti Brunello di Montalcino": "Sesti Brunello di Montalcino's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- red structure flattens the spice cake's cinnamon-and-cream-cheese delicacy. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Sesti Brunello di Montalcino for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Shafer 1.5": "Shafer 1.5's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Shafer 1.5 for the steak course.",
