  "Carrot Cake|Siete Leguas Blanco": "Siete Leguas Blanco's unaged blanco-tequila lift with agave-citrus snap falls short of the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- light spirit reads thin against dessert sweetness. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a light spirit. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Siete Leguas Blanco lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Carrot Cake|Siete Leguas Reposado": "Siete Leguas Reposado's aged-agave character leans against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the oak-aged tequila body threads the carrot cake, and the caramel-agave register brightens the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Carrot Cake|Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Simon Family Estate Reserve": "Simon Family Estate Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Simon Family Estate Reserve on the steak course instead.",
  "Carrot Cake|Spottswoode Lyndenhurst": "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst's Napa estate Cab with structured cassis flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Spottswoode Lyndenhurst lands on the steak course — not here.",
