  "Carrot Cake|St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc": "St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc's crisp white-wine character clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- a dry white belongs with the main course, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a white wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|St Supéry Élu Meritage": "St Supéry Élu Meritage's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. St Supéry Élu Meritage lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Carrot Cake|Stagg Jr. Batch #15": "Stagg Jr. Batch #15 with carrot cake — BT cask-strength against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; Stagg Jr. meets the cake at barrel-proof register.",
