  "Carrot Cake|Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc": "Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc's crisp NZ Sauvignon Blanc clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- a dry white belongs with the main course, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a white wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Carrot Cake|Swordfish": "The swordfish into the carrot cake -- the meaty grilled steak hands off to spiced cake and cream-cheese frosting, walnut crunch on the close. Works; the lemon-bright fish and the spice cake share separate registers across the meal.",
  "Carrot Cake|Tanq 10 Gin": "Tanq 10 Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- juniper-citrus and warm cake spices pull in opposite directions. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Tanq 10 Gin for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Tanqueray Gin": "Tanqueray Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Tanqueray Gin lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Carrot Cake|Taylor Fladgate Tawny": "Classic Douro Tawny — Taylor Fladgate (founded 1692), smooth balanced, dried fruit, almond, warm clean finish. The warm clean finish matches allspice-cinnamon spice and the almond plays with cream-cheese frosting's vanilla bean paste. Peak heritage-Tawny for carrot cake — balanced spice match. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Carrot Cake|Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle": "Flagship Vintage Port — Taylor Fladgate bottle, extraordinarily rich, dark fruit, chocolate, tobacco, minutes-long evolving finish. The tobacco lifts allspice-cinnamon spice and the chocolate plays with cream-cheese frosting. Strong flagship-Vintage for carrot cake — extraordinarily rich reads heavy, Tawny fits the spice softer.",
  "Carrot Cake|Tears of Llorona": "Tears of Llorona with carrot cake — triple-cask aged against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; sherry and cognac cask influences find the cake's raisins at multi-cask craft register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Teeter Totter Cabernet Sauvignon": "Teeter Totter Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- red structure flattens the spice cake's cinnamon-and-cream-cheese delicacy. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Teeter Totter Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Tenuta di Arceno Chianti Classico": "Tenuta di Arceno Chianti Classico's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Tenuta di Arceno Chianti Classico for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|The BG": "The BG's high-acid cocktail register leans against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the bright build frames the carrot cake, and the citrus cuts the dessert. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Carrot Cake|The Happy Wife": "The Happy Wife's crisp citrus-ginger build stays alongside the carrot cake's spiced cream cheese — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Carrot Cake|The Manhattan": "The Manhattan's bold oak-vanilla build holds with the carrot cake's spiced cream cheese — the whiskey-build sweetness threads the dessert, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Carrot Cake|The Prisoner Red Blend": "The Prisoner Red Blend's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve The Prisoner Red Blend for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|The Tomahawk": "The Tomahawk into the carrot cake -- the smoky bone-in marbling hands off to spiced cake and cream-cheese frosting, walnut crunch on the close. Works; the showpiece cut and the spiced cake share the meal at separate registers.",
  "Carrot Cake|Thomas H. Handy Sazerac Rye": "Thomas H. Handy Sazerac Rye's rye-spice character leans against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the rye spice cuts the carrot cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; cleaner than wheated versions but not exceptional.",
  "Carrot Cake|Thomas S. Moore Chardonnay Cask": "Thomas S. Moore Chardonnay Cask with carrot cake — chardonnay-cask bourbon against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; TSM Chardonnay Cask's chardonnay-derived crisp-apple-butter threads the cake with DISTINCTIVE white-wine character — more subtle than red-wine-finish + raisins bridge, more complementary than port approaches.",
  "Carrot Cake|Titos Vodka": "Titos Vodka's American corn-based vodka falls short of the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a vodka. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Titos Vodka belongs on the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Toki Suntory Japanese Whisky": "Toki Suntory Japanese Whisky's entry Suntory Toki character finds neutral with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the elegant Suntory/Nikka register matches the carrot cake, and the Japanese-craft balance underlines the dessert. Works; BH Red Wine Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Tomato Basil": "The tomato basil alongside the carrot cake -- acid and sugar share the table, neither course pulls heavy. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Carrot Cake|Transfusion": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build finds neutral with the carrot cake's spiced cream cheese — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Carrot Cake|Trombo Cedano Reposado": "Trombo Cedano Reposado's rested-agave body reads alongside the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the añejo register carries the carrot cake, and the oak threads the dessert. Works; the pour is a touch over-specified for the side.",
  "Carrot Cake|Truffle Fries": "The truffle fries alongside the carrot cake -- sugar plays against the savory weight, the table earns its lift. Works; the contrast holds, neither course overshadows the other.",
  "Carrot Cake|Tullamore D.E.W.": "Tullamore D.E.W. with carrot cake — drier traditional Irish against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; Tullamore's heritage character threads the cake at drier register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "The tuna into the carrot cake -- the seared-rare flesh and sesame crust hand off to spiced cake and cream-cheese frosting, walnut crunch on the close. Works; the cleaner main and the spiced dessert share the meal at separate registers.",
  "Carrot Cake|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "The curry and the carrot cake -- the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth bookends with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Carrot Cake|Venge Family Reserve": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Venge Family Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Venge Scout's Honor": "Venge Scout's Honor's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Venge Scout's Honor lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Carrot Cake|Venge Silencieux": "Venge Silencieux's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Venge Silencieux lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Carrot Cake|Vesper": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build leans against the carrot cake's spiced cream cheese — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Carrot Cake|Veuve Clicquot Brut": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's classic yellow-label Champagne body clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- a dry sparkling belongs with the opener, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a sparkling. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Veuve Clicquot Brut belongs on the steak course.",
  "Carrot Cake|Vieux Carré": "Vieux Carré's bold herbal-spice build sits alongside the carrot cake's spiced cream cheese — the whiskey-build sweetness threads the dessert, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Carrot Cake|Villon Cognac": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet saffron/elderflower-infused cognac spirit. Villon's saffron marries the cake's spice with distinctive modern character — the featured Villon pairing where the infusion actively shines. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Carrot Cake|Vin Santo": "* Vin Santo -- Tuscan dessert wine, dried-fruit and honey, biscotti pour. The sticky-sweet pour sits with the carrot cake, and the late-harvest sugar rounds the dessert. Serious peak dessert pour. Gold standard; the call that earns the regular.",
  "Carrot Cake|Weller 107": "Carrot Cake: the cake's cream cheese and cinnamon meet Weller 107's higher-proof caramel. More energetic than Weller Special Reserve; heat gives the dessert spice-and-warmth dimension. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Carrot Cake|Weller 12 Year": "Carrot Cake: the cake's raisins, cream cheese frosting, and cinnamon warmth meet Weller 12 Year's aged oak, caramel, and vanilla. A dessert pairing that shows what aged wheated bourbon does with cake spice; balance over intensity. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Weller Millennium": "Weller Millennium with carrot cake — deep wheated honey and the Millennium's oak against cream cheese and raisins. A dessert pairing that shows what rare wheated bourbon can do; reserved for guests who care about the detail. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Weller Special Reserve": "Carrot Cake: the cake's cream cheese and cinnamon meet Weller Special Reserve's caramel and vanilla. Balanced but accessible; Weller 12 brings more layers here. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Carrot Cake|Wheatley Vodka": "Wheatley Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a vodka. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Wheatley Vodka on the steak course instead.",
  "Carrot Cake|WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel Rye": "WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the high-rye spice register matches the carrot cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Carrot Cake|WhistlePig 12 Year Old World": "WhistlePig 12 Year Old World's rye-spice character finds neutral with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the rye backbone drives the carrot cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for the side — save the collector bottle for the protein course.",
  "Carrot Cake|WhistlePig 15 Year": "WhistlePig 15 Year's rye-spice character leans against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the rye backbone drives the carrot cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; bonded weight slightly over-specified.",
  "Carrot Cake|WhistlePig Boss Hog IX 17 Year": "WhistlePig Boss Hog IX 17 Year's rye-spice character finds neutral with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the rye spice cuts the carrot cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; flagship depth gives the dessert premium aged character.",
  "Carrot Cake|WhistlePig Boss Hog X Commandments": "WhistlePig Boss Hog X Commandments' rye-spice character leans against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the dry rye body wraps the carrot cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; BIB structure is a touch over-specified for the dessert.",
  "Carrot Cake|WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year": "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year with carrot cake — WP accessible rye against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; rye spice and cake spice find each other.",
  "Carrot Cake|Willett Pot Still Reserve": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with carrot cake — craft high-rye spice against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; oak spice and cake spice find each other in a distinctive way.",
  "Carrot Cake|Woodford Reserve": "Woodford Reserve with carrot cake — small-batch fruit and floral against cream cheese and cinnamon. The bourbon's fruit character picks up the cake's raisins; a distinctive dessert pairing within the everyday premium tier. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Carrot Cake|Woodford Reserve Double Oaked": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Brown-Forman Double Oaked. Strong; Woodford Double Oaked's intensified-caramel threads the cake at KY-benchmark register.",
  "Carrot Cake|Woodford Reserve Rye": "Woodford Reserve Rye with carrot cake — Woodford fruit-forward rye against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; small-batch fruit and cake spice find each other.",
  "Carrot Cake|Woodinville Rye": "Woodinville Rye with carrot cake — PNW craft rye against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; regional rye spice and cake spice find each other.",
  "Carrot Cake|Yamazaki 12 Year": "Yamazaki 12 Year's Suntory Japanese flagship character reads alongside the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the precise Japanese craft body wraps the carrot cake, and the Japanese-craft balance underlines the dessert. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Carrot Cake|Yamazaki 18 Year": "Yamazaki 18 Year's aged Suntory mizunara character finds neutral with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the mizunara-cask depth wraps the carrot cake, and the silky precision frames the dessert. Works; polished aged character doesn't drive.",
  "Carrot Cake|Yellow Chartreuse": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Yellow Chartreuse. Works; the honey-saffron-herbal character amplifies the cake's spice with sweeter dimension.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Asparagus": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- sweet wine on green vegetable is wrong direction — needs crisp white. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a dessert wine. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a dessert wine. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Beignets": "Late Bottled Vintage Port — Casa LBV, 4-6 year cask, dark cherry, plum, smooth moderate structure. The smooth structure clings to hot choux-fried dough and the plum lifts powdered-sugar simplicity. Strong LBV for beignets — Graham's 10 Year's toffee fits airy choux cleaner.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Bone Marrow": "Never pair Casa LBV with bone marrow — entry-port residual sugar drowns roasted-marrow unctuousness and the smooth structure clashes with beefy-bone savory. Lead with Scavino Barolo or Lail Daniel Cuvée. LBV belongs at dessert, not the start of the meal.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Bone-In Filet": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- dessert wine is post-meal — wrong register for the steak course. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Casa LBV Port for another course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Broccoli Cheddar": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness doubles down on the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- sweet wine on cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — heavy, no contrast. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Broccolini": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the broccolini's tender green stalks -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Brussels and Belly": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness doubles down on Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet wine and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no foil. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Burrata": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the burrata's fresh basil-tomato-cream delicacy -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Il Colle Prosecco Superiore, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, not a dessert wine. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Casa LBV Port lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Butternut Squash": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a dessert wine. Avoid; one of those is the move. Casa LBV Port belongs on the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Carrot Cake": "Late Bottled Vintage Port — Casa LBV, 4-6 year cask, dark cherry, plum, smooth moderate structure, entry-port approachable. The dark cherry lifts allspice-cinnamon spice and the smooth structure plays with cream-cheese frosting. Peak LBV for carrot cake — approachable port on the spiced bake. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Cheesecake": "Late Bottled Vintage Port — Casa LBV, 4-6 year cask, dark cherry, plum, smooth moderate structure, entry-port approachable. The plum lifts cream-cheese density and the smooth structure plays with graham-cracker brown-sugar crust. Peak LBV for cheesecake — approachable port on the water-bath bake. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Chilean Seabass": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- dessert wine on a main protein is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Chocolate Brownie": "Late Bottled Vintage Port — Casa LBV, 4-6 year cask, dark cherry, plum, smooth moderate structure, entry-port approachable. The dark cherry wraps around fudge-brownie cocoa and the smooth structure handles whipped-chocolate frosting. Peak LBV for chocolate brownie — approachable port lineup on the dense bake. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Chocolate Cake": "Late Bottled Vintage Port — Casa LBV, 4-6 year cask, dark cherry, plum, smooth moderate structure. The dark cherry wraps fudgy chocolate-cake crumb and the smooth structure handles buttermilk-dairy depth. Strong LBV for chocolate cake — Vintage Port's structured intensity fits cocoa-on-cocoa harder.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Clam Chowder": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Cowboy Ribeye": "Never pair Casa LBV with Cowboy Ribeye — entry-port residual sugar muddles marbled-ribeye char and the smooth structure loses against grilled-beef protein weight. Lead with Silver Oak Cabernet or Caymus for the 26oz bone-in. The LBV is an after-meal pour.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Crab Cake": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness overwhelms the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- dessert sugar on cold shellfish is wrong direction — needs sparkling or Sancerre. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Casa LBV Port on the steak course instead.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Creamed Spinach": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness doubles down on the creamed spinach's rich bechamel-laced greens -- sweet wine and a dairy side compound the richness — dessert energy on savory plate. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Weller 12 Year, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Casa LBV Port lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Creamy Potato": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a dessert wine. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Casa LBV Port on the steak course instead.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Creme Brulee": "Late Bottled Vintage Port — Casa LBV, 4-6 year cask, dark cherry, plum, smooth moderate structure, entry-port approachable. The plum plays with torched-sugar crust caramelization and the smooth structure won't overwhelm vanilla-custard delicacy. Peak LBV for creme brulee — approachable port on the classic match. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Escargot": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a dessert wine. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Faroe Island Salmon": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- dessert wine on a main protein is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Filet Mignon": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the filet's lean buttery tenderness -- dessert wine is post-meal — wrong register for the steak course. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Maker's Mark Cellar Aged, or Yamazaki 18 Year, not a dessert wine. Avoid; one of those is the move. Casa LBV Port belongs on another course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|French Onion": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Casa LBV Port on the steak course instead.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Grilled Caesar": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness jars against the Caesar's charred-romaine and anchovy edge -- sweet wine on cold lettuce refuses the salad's clean register. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Tanqueray Gin, or Scavino Barolo, not a dessert wine. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Gumbo": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- honeyed sugar on savory broth jars — wrong direction for the course. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not a dessert wine. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness doubles down on the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- sweet wine and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no foil. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a dessert wine. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Casa LBV Port on the steak course instead.",
  "Casa LBV Port|House Wedge": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness jars against the wedge's iceberg-and-bleu cool crunch -- sweet wine on cold lettuce refuses the salad's clean register. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Weller 12 Year, or Le Garenne Rosé, not a dessert wine. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Kansas City": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the KC's lean-bold strip with savory grain -- dessert wine is post-meal — wrong register for the steak course. The plate deserves Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, Pio Cesare Barbaresco, or Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Casa LBV Port belongs on another course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Loaded Potato": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness doubles down on the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup -- sweet wine on cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — heavy, no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Lobster Mac": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness doubles down on the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- sweet wine and a dairy side compound the richness — dessert energy on savory plate. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Market Fish": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- dessert wine on a main protein is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Pour the Casa LBV Port on the steak course instead.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Mocha Creme": "Mocha Creme: this dense chocolate dessert's deep cocoa richness meets this LBV port's approachable dark-fruit sweetness and structured grip. The fortified sweetness and complexity anchor the dessert; weight carries weight. Strong — the classic finish.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Mushroom Bisque": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a dessert wine. Avoid; one of those is the move. Casa LBV Port lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Mushrooms": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the mushrooms' earthy umami weight -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Los Vecinos Mezcal, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a dessert wine. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Casa LBV Port on the steak course instead.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Late Bottled Vintage Port — Casa LBV, 4-6 year cask, dark cherry, plum, smooth moderate structure, entry-port approachable. The plum bridges peanut-butter-frosting richness and the dark cherry lifts dense fudge-brownie base. Peak LBV for peanut butter brownie — approachable depth on the dense bake. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Porterhouse": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character -- dessert wine is post-meal — wrong register for the steak course. The plate deserves Odette Cabernet Sauvignon, Weller 12 Year, or Domaine du Grand Tinel, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Casa LBV Port for another course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Prime Tartare": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness flattens the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami -- honeyed sugar dulls the savory meat opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Belvedere Vodka, not a dessert wine. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Rainbow Trout": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- dessert wine on a main protein is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Roast Half Chicken": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast -- dessert wine on a main protein is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; one of those is the move. Casa LBV Port lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a dessert wine. Avoid; one of those is the move. Casa LBV Port belongs on the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness smothers the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the wine's sweetness buries the gentle flesh's lift. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- sweet wine on green vegetable is wrong direction — needs crisp white. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not a dessert wine. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Seafood Tower": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- dessert sugar on cold shellfish is wrong direction — needs sparkling or Sancerre. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Casa LBV Port belongs on the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Seared Scallops": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness overwhelms the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- dessert sugar on cold shellfish is wrong direction — needs sparkling or Sancerre. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a dessert wine. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Casa LBV Port belongs on the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Seasonal Soup": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Seasonal Vegetables": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate -- sweet wine on green vegetable is wrong direction — needs crisp white. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Shrimp Bisque": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness doubles down on the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- sweet wine on cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — heavy, no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Shrimp Cocktail": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Casa LBV Port belongs on the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Swordfish": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness flattens the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- sweet wine dulls the sear's clean char — savory main deserves a dry pour. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|The Tomahawk": "Never pair Casa LBV with Tomahawk — entry-port buries the massive 36oz bone-in ribeye and residual sugar clashes with smoky char. Lead with Scavino Barolo or Beaucastel Châteauneuf for the grand cut. LBV is a dessert pour, not a steak wine.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Tomato Basil": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid -- honeyed sugar on savory broth jars — wrong direction for the course. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Le Garenne Rosé, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Casa LBV Port belongs on the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Truffle Fries": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness flattens the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- dessert sugar on starch is wrong-course energy for the supporting plate. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Casa LBV Port on the steak course instead.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- sweet wine dulls the sear's clean char — savory main deserves a dry pour. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a dessert wine. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Casa LBV Port belongs on the steak course.",
  "Casa LBV Port|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Le Garenne Rosé, not a dessert wine. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Casa LBV Port lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Asparagus": "Casamigos Mezcal's rustic mezcal weight reads alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the wood-fire body meets the asparagus, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Casamigos Mezcal's wood-fire mezcal body sits alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the smoky agave register handles the au gratin, and the wood-smoke note underlines the side. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Beignets": "Casamigos Mezcal's earthen-pit smoke profile finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the espadín-and-smoke body wraps the beignets, and the campfire register frames the dessert. Works; the courses share the table without crowding.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Bone Marrow": "Casamigos Mezcal: the Clooney-Gerber gateway to agave smoke. Excellent on marrow; Casamigos Mezcal's softened-smoke character meets the umami fat without overwhelming — the entry point for a guest who wants mezcal but dialed back.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Bone-In Filet": "Casamigos Mezcal's rustic mezcal weight matches register with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the earthen-pit smoke carries the bone-enhanced filet, and the earthy backbone threads the cut. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Broccoli Cheddar": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character clashes with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- mezcal smoke fights the soup's cream — smoke has no bridge into dairy delicacy. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a mezcal. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Casamigos Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Broccolini": "Casamigos Mezcal's espadín-and-smoke register leans against the broccolini's tender green stalks: the espadín-and-smoke body wraps the broccolini, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and crispy pork belly meet Clooney-Gerber mezcal. Excellent; Casamigos Mezcal's polished-smoke rides the glaze-and-belly fat at gateway register.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Burrata": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character clashes with the burrata's fresh basil-tomato-cream delicacy -- smoke and fresh dairy refuse each other — texture reads broken. The plate deserves Il Colle Prosecco Superiore, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, not a mezcal. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Casamigos Mezcal on the steak course instead.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Butternut Squash": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character clashes with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- mezcal smoke fights the soup's cream — smoke has no bridge into dairy delicacy. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a mezcal. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Casamigos Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Carrot Cake": "Casamigos Mezcal's earthen-pit smoke profile reads alongside the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the smoky agave register handles the carrot cake, and the campfire register frames the dessert. Works; a measured close to the meal.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Cheesecake": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character overpowers the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- the plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not a mezcal. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Save the Casamigos Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Chilean Seabass": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- mezcal smoke is wrong register for the main fish course. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a mezcal. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Casamigos Mezcal lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Chocolate Brownie": "Casamigos Mezcal's earthen-pit smoke profile sits alongside the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight: the espadín-and-smoke body wraps the brownie, and the wood-smoke note underlines the dessert. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Chocolate Cake": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character leans against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the wood-fire body meets the chocolate cake, and the campfire register frames the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Clam Chowder": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- mezcal smoke fights the soup's cream — smoke has no bridge into dairy delicacy. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a mezcal. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Casamigos Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Cowboy Ribeye": "Cowboy Ribeye: 26oz bone-in cap-fat meets Casamigos Mezcal's polished-agave register. Excellent; the accessible smoke kisses the char without bullying it — the mezcal a tequila drinker will actually finish.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Crab Cake": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- mezcal smoke obliterates delicate shellfish — needs sparkling or sancerre. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not a mezcal. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Casamigos Mezcal on the steak course instead.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Creamed Spinach": "Casamigos Mezcal's rustic mezcal weight finds neutral with the creamed spinach's rich bechamel-laced greens: the smoky agave register handles the creamed spinach, and the earthy backbone threads the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Creamy Potato": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character clashes with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- mezcal smoke fights the soup's cream — smoke has no bridge into dairy delicacy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a mezcal. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Casamigos Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Creme Brulee": "Casamigos Mezcal's espadín-and-smoke register finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the wood-fire body meets the brulee, and the wood-smoke note underlines the dessert. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Escargot": "Casamigos Mezcal's bold agave-soft-smoke character finds register with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the agave smoke cuts the umami fat, and the smoke meets the umami depth. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Faroe Island Salmon": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- mezcal smoke and the fish's natural oils refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a mezcal. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Casamigos Mezcal belongs on the steak course.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Filet Mignon": "Casamigos Mezcal's rustic mezcal weight sits alongside the filet's lean buttery tenderness: the earthen-pit smoke carries the lean buttery filet, and the green-agave edge brightens the cut. Works; the close composes without strain.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|French Onion": "Casamigos Mezcal's earthen-pit smoke profile leans against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the espadín-and-smoke body wraps the French onion, and the green-agave edge brightens the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Grilled Caesar": "Casamigos Mezcal's bold agave-soft-smoke character finds register with the Caesar's char-and-anchovy — the agave smoke meets the plate. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Gumbo": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character clashes with the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- mezcal smoke is wrong register for the soup-salad course. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not a mezcal. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Casamigos Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Casamigos Mezcal's wood-fire mezcal body reads alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the smoky agave register handles the honey carrots, and the wood-smoke note underlines the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|House Wedge": "Casamigos Mezcal's earthen-pit smoke profile reads alongside the wedge's iceberg-and-bleu cool crunch: the earthen-pit smoke carries the wedge, and the wood-smoke note underlines the bowl. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Kansas City": "Casamigos Mezcal's earthen-pit smoke profile sits alongside the KC's lean-bold strip with savory grain: the earthen-pit smoke carries the strip steak, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Loaded Potato": "Casamigos Mezcal's earthen-pit smoke profile reads alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the espadín-and-smoke body wraps the loaded potato soup, and the mineral smoke plays against the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Lobster Mac": "Casamigos Mezcal's rustic mezcal weight finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the wood-fire body meets the lobster mac, and the earthy backbone threads the side. Works; the side-salad call holds.",
  "Casamigos Mezcal|Market Fish": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- mezcal smoke buries the delicate flesh — the fish has no foil against agave + smoke. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a mezcal. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Casamigos Mezcal for the steak course.",
