  "Cheesecake|Ocho Anejo": "Ocho Anejo's añejo-pour depth reads alongside the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the barrel-rested body handles the cheesecake, and the oak threads the dessert. Works; 1942 aged depth is a touch over-specified for the small plate.",
  "Cheesecake|Odette Cabernet Sauvignon": "Odette Cabernet Sauvignon's Stags Leap Cab with iron-fist-in-a-velvet-glove quality pulls against the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- the red's dry-fruit register has no bridge to dessert tang or sugar. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Odette Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
