  "Chilean Seabass|Detroit City Gin": "Detroit City Gin's bold char-juniper botanicals lifts the seabass's buttery flesh — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the spice meets the herb butter. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Detroit City Vodka": "Detroit City Vodka's crisp grain-juniper neutrality plays cleanly against the seabass's buttery flesh — the neutral profile frames the fish cleanly, and the botanicals lift the savory weight. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Dewar's 15": "Dewar's 15's 15yr aged Highland blend swallows the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Dewar's 15 for the steak course.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Dewar's White Label": "Dewar's White Label's Highland blend with Aberfeldy-malt core overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon weight needs red meat, not the salmon's already-rich oils. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; one of those is the move. Dewar's White Label lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Disaronno": "Disaronno's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the liqueur's sugar piles onto the fish's natural oils with no lift. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Disaronno for the steak course.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye": "Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye's rye-spice character swallows the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Save the Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye for the steak course.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum": "Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum's aged-rum register with molasses and oak depth overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- heavy spirit weight buries the main protein — needs a wine or lighter spirit. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum for the steak course.",
