  "Chilean Seabass|Johnnie Walker Black": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Johnnie Walker Black on the steak course instead.",
