  "Chilean Seabass|Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon": "Sonoma Cab — cassis, plum, cedar, mint, fine tannin, elegant balance. The fine tannin meets seabass's buttery flesh and the cedar plays against the rich texture. Works as approachable Cab for Chilean seabass — Jordan's fine tannin makes it the fish-friendliest Cab; Chardonnays and Pinots peak higher.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Joseph Mellot Sancerre": "Joseph Mellot Sancerre's crisp citrus-mineral acidity plays cleanly against the seabass's buttery flesh — the crisp acidity frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Jubilation by Colgin": "Jubilation by Colgin's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- tannin on oily fish goes bitter, where a Pinot at the right register would carry it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Jubilation by Colgin for the steak course.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Jung and Wulff Guyana": "Jung and Wulff Guyana's aged-rum register with molasses and oak depth overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- heavy spirit weight buries the main protein — needs a wine or lighter spirit. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Jung and Wulff Guyana belongs on the steak course.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Jung and Wulff Trinidad": "Jung and Wulff Trinidad's aged-rum register with molasses and oak depth overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- heavy spirit weight buries the main protein — needs a wine or lighter spirit. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Jung and Wulff Trinidad for the steak course.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Kahlua": "Kahlua's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the liqueur's sugar piles onto the fish's natural oils with no lift. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Kahlua for the steak course.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Keenan Chardonnay": "Spring Mountain Napa Chardonnay — green apple, lemon curd, subtle oak, bright acid. The bright acid lifts seabass's buttery rich flesh and the subtle oak plays against the melt-in-mouth texture. Peak balanced Chardonnay for Chilean seabass — Napa structure on the rich classic. Gold standard; pour without second-guessing.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Keenan Mernet": "Keenan Mernet's herbaceous Cab Franc with red-fruit and bell-pepper jars against the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- tannin on oily fish goes bitter, where a Pinot at the right register would carry it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Reserve the Keenan Mernet for the steak course.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon weight needs red meat, not the salmon's already-rich oils. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye lands on the steak course — not here.",
