  "Chilean Seabass|Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône": "Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register fights the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the red's tannin and the salmon's rich oils refuse to integrate. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône for the steak course.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Ketel One Vodka": "Ketel One Vodka's clean cold-distilled body matches register with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh: the neutral-spirit weight handles the seabass, and the silky neutrality lifts the plate. Strong; Ketel handles the tower cleanly, though Goose's luxury softness wins the flagship pairing.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Knickerbocker Gin": "Knickerbocker Gin's gin lift with floral-and-pepper sits at register with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh: the bright botanical edge handles the seabass, and the floral-and-herb register brightens the plate. Strong; Knickerbocker's brewer's-heritage character is a story-driven tower pairing.",
