  "Chilean Seabass|Komos Anejo Reserva": "Komos Anejo Reserva's aged-agave character clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- agave and oily fish refuse each other — the fish needs acid, not aged spirit. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Komos Anejo Reserva lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Komos Crystallino Anejo": "Komos Crystallino Anejo's crisp char-floral character frames the seabass's buttery flesh — the añejo weight overshoots the fish, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Komos Extra Anejo": "Komos Extra Anejo's aged-agave character clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- aged tequila is wrong register for a main fish or poultry course. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Komos Extra Anejo lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Komos Rosa Reposado": "Komos Rosa Reposado's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the seabass' buttery seabass flesh: the añejo register carries the seabass, and the oak threads the plate. Works; the 70th's clarity is too delicate to drive the pairing.",
