  "Chilean Seabass|Laphroaig 10": "Laphroaig 10's classic Islay peat overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Laphroaig 10 on the steak course instead.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Larceny Small Batch": "Larceny Small Batch's Heaven Hill wheated caramel clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Larceny Small Batch lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé": "Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé's crisp berry-cherry acidity reads alongside the seabass's buttery flesh — the bright acidity frames the fish without weight, and the cherry-fruit lifts the herb edge. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut": "Tours-sur-Marne Chardonnay-blend Champagne — precise green apple, lemon zest, whisper of brioche, vibrant acidity. The high-acid finish cuts seabass's buttery richness and the brioche plays against the melt-in-mouth texture. Strong Champagne for Chilean seabass — bubbles reset the palate between bites.",
