  "Chilean Seabass|Limoncello": "Limoncello's sweet liqueur character clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- dessert-grade sugar refuses the rich-fish course — needs a crisp white instead. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Limoncello lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Chilean Seabass|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Willamette Pinot — dark cherry, forest floor, refined structure, low tannin. The low-tannin silk lifts seabass's buttery flesh and the forest-floor earth plays against the rich texture. Peak Oregon Pinot for Chilean seabass — refined red on the buttery classic. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
