  "Chilean Seabass|Loch Lomond 20 Year": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's complex 20yr aged Highland overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Loch Lomond 20 Year belongs on the steak course.",
