  "Chocolate Brownie|El Cabo": "El Cabo's barrel-aged tequila weight reads alongside the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight: the rested-agave depth sits with the brownie, and the oak threads the dessert. Works; the bold pour cuts the glaze but is slightly much for the small plate.",
  "Chocolate Brownie|El Mayor Extra Anejo": "El Mayor Extra Anejo with the chocolate brownie — aged El Mayor against cocoa. The accessible extra añejo meets the brownie at value-adjacent premium register. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Chocolate Brownie|El Mayor Reposado": "El Mayor Reposado's añejo-pour depth leans against the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight: the barrel-rested body handles the brownie, and the soft-spice note softens the dessert. Works; aged depth is refined but not a standout.",
  "Chocolate Brownie|Elephant Gin": "Elephant Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- gin botanicals jar against the chocolate's sweetness with no bridge. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not a gin. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Elephant Gin for the steak course.",
  "Chocolate Brownie|Elijah Craig 18 Year": "Elijah Craig 18 with the chocolate brownie — 18yr HH single-barrel against cocoa. Strong; EC 18's leather-tobacco character meets cocoa at aged-premium register.",
  "Chocolate Brownie|Elijah Craig Private Barrel": "Elijah Craig Private Barrel with the chocolate brownie — private-barrel single-barrel against cocoa. Works; curated depth meets the brownie at the private-selection register.",
