  "Chocolate Cake|Baileys Irish Cream": "★ Baileys Irish Cream's sweet cream-cocoa character commands the meeting with the cake's layered chocolate — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar, and the cocoa underlines the chocolate. Gold standard; pour without second-guessing.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Baker's": "Baker's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; a gentle composed match.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Balvenie 12 American Oak": "Balvenie 12 American Oak's bourbon-cask Speyside softness sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the scotch depth settles into the chocolate cake, and the oak-and-smoke underlines the dessert. Works; extended-aged home-state pour wasted on salad.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask": "Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask's rum-finished Speyside character leans against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the Highland register carries the chocolate cake, and the heather brightens the dessert. Works; the aging is wasted on the salad.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Balvenie 16 Single Barrel": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the chocolate cake, and the smoke threads the dessert. Works; Gran Cru's brioche meets the glaze at refined register.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Balvenie 21 Portwood": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside finds neutral with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the chocolate cake, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the dessert. Works; the fruit character gives the dessert a subtle counterpoint.",
