  "Chocolate Cake|Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon": "Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon's estate-Cab Napa character flattens the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Far Niente Chardonnay": "Far Niente Chardonnay's estate Napa Chardonnay character clashes with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- a dry white belongs with the main course, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not a white wine. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Far Niente Chardonnay for the steak course.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Faroe Island Salmon": "After the salmon, the chocolate cake -- the rich oily flesh hands off to layered cocoa-and-ganache, the vanilla scoop softening the close. Works; the oily fish softens before the chocolate weight, the meal builds toward the close.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi": "Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity jars against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi for the steak course.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Faust Napa Valley Cabernet": "Faust Napa Valley Cabernet's structured Napa Cab with cassis depth flattens the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Faust Napa Valley Cabernet belongs on the steak course.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía": "Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth jars against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía for the steak course.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Fernet Branca": "Fernet Branca's nuclear bitter-menthol intensity finds neutral with the cake's layered chocolate — the bitter herb edge cuts dessert sweetness, and the bitter cuts the sweet edge. Works; capable alongside. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Fernet Menta": "Fernet Menta's crisp mint-menthol edge holds with the cake's layered chocolate — the bitter herb edge cuts dessert sweetness. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Filet Mignon": "After the filet, the chocolate cake -- the savory course resolves into sugar, the meal closes with contrast. Works; the heavy close after a heavy main, both courses share register.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Fireball Whisky": "Fireball Whisky: this sweet cream liqueur's dessert-adjacent lushness meets this dense chocolate dessert's deep cocoa richness. Sweet liqueur's dessert-adjacent sweetness amplifies the dessert — doubles up on sugar. Works as an indulgence.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Fisher Unity Pinot Noir": "Fisher Unity Pinot Noir's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift fights the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- the dry red and the chocolate's sugar refuse each other — tannin reads bitter on the finish. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Fisher Unity Pinot Noir for the steak course.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Four Roses Small Batch Select": "Four Roses Small Batch Select's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the bourbon weight handles the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; bonded weight a touch ambitious for the dessert.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Four Roses Yellow Label": "Four Roses Yellow Label's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the bourbon body sits with the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; distinctive character doesn't drive but adds interest.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Fox & Oden": "Fox & Oden's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; premium single-barrel wasted on the salad.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Fox & Oden Double Oaked": "Fox & Oden Double Oaked's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the bourbon depth settles into the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; stout-barrel story wasted on salad.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Frangelico": "Frangelico's sweet hazelnut-cocoa character holds the line with the cake's layered chocolate — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar, and the cocoa underlines the chocolate. Strong; the call lands cleanly.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Freemark Abbey Bosché": "Freemark Abbey Bosché's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- savory tannin sits awkwardly on cocoa weight without resolving. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Freemark Abbey Bosché on the steak course instead.",
  "Chocolate Cake|French 75": "French 75's gin-and-Champagne lift with citrus snap fights the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- citrus-cocktail brightness pulls against chocolate weight — no bridge between sour-sweet and rich-sweet. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not a light cocktail. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the French 75 on the steak course instead.",
  "Chocolate Cake|French Onion": "The French onion and the chocolate cake -- the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth bookends with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Frias Block 5": "Frias Block 5's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth fights the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- the dry red and the chocolate's sugar refuse each other — tannin reads bitter on the finish. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Frias Block 5 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Chocolate Cake|G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo": "G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo's high-acid Nebbiolo with rose-and-tar grip jars against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo belongs on the steak course.",
  "Chocolate Cake|G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti": "Piedmont Moscato — peach blossom, apricot, lychee, gentle sweetness. Bubbles cut cocoa density and peach softens bitter chocolate. Strong alternative when guest wants sparkling rather than coffee — but the cake is currently unavailable.",
  "Chocolate Cake|G4 Blanco": "G4 Blanco's unaged blanco-tequila lift with agave-citrus snap falls short of the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- light spirit reads thin against dessert sweetness. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not a light spirit. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the G4 Blanco for the steak course.",
  "Chocolate Cake|G4 High Proof": "G4 High Proof's cooked-agave-and-oak register leans against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the chocolate cake, and the oak threads the dessert. Works; the bold agave overpowers the dish's restraint.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Garavogue Irish Whiskey": "Garavogue Irish Whiskey's Irish whiskey smoothness sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the Irish whiskey body sits with the chocolate cake, and the soft malt rounds the dessert. Works; private-selection wasted on the salad.",
  "Chocolate Cake|George T. Stagg": "George T. Stagg's cask-strength BTAC bourbon power leans against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; bold intensity slightly over-specified.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon": "Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- savory tannin sits awkwardly on cocoa weight without resolving. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Ghost Block Zinfandel": "Ghost Block Zinfandel's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift flattens the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Ghost Block Zinfandel for the steak course.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Glenfiddich 12": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the Highland register carries the chocolate cake, and the heather brightens the dessert. Works; the light body doesn't overshoot the salad.",
  "Chocolate Cake|Glenfiddich 14": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character leans against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the Highland register carries the chocolate cake, and the heather brightens the dessert. Works; bonded weight a touch ambitious for the dessert.",
