  "Château Batailley|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Château Batailley's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth crowds the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- the side needs a crisper register to carry it cleanly. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Château Batailley for the steak course.",
  "Château Batailley|House Wedge": "Pauillac 5ème Cru Classé Bordeaux — blackcurrant, tobacco, cedar, graphite, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts iceberg-and-bacon and the graphite plays against blue cheese dressing. Works as classified Bordeaux for the wedge — Pauillac structure reframes the classic salad; whites peak higher.",
  "Château Batailley|Kansas City": "Pauillac 5ème Cru Classé left-bank Bordeaux — blackcurrant, tobacco, cedar, graphite, firm tannin. The firm tannin handles Kansas City's lean-bold marbled strip and the graphite plays against the beefy char. Peak classified Bordeaux for the strip — 1855 French prestige on the American steakhouse cut. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
