  "Château de Rouillac|Creme Brulee": "Château de Rouillac's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit pulls against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- the red's dry-fruit register has no bridge to dessert tang or sugar. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Château de Rouillac lands on the steak course — not here.",
