  "Château de Rouillac|Filet Mignon": "Pessac-Léognan left-bank Bordeaux — classic blackcurrant, cedar, graphite, tobacco finish, firm tannin, medium body. The firm structure handles butter-tender filet's delicate sweetness and the cedar-graphite plays against escargot-butter. Peak left-bank Bordeaux for filet — classified French classic for the delicate cut. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
