  "Château de Rouillac|Porterhouse": "Pessac-Léognan left-bank Bordeaux — blackcurrant, cedar, graphite, tobacco, firm tannin. The firm tannin handles Porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet and the graphite plays against both lean-and-fatty sides. Strong left-bank Bordeaux for Porterhouse — French structure on the dual-cut classic.",
  "Château de Rouillac|Prime Tartare": "Château de Rouillac's leather-tobacco tannin lifts the tartare's raw beef and brine — the medium-body red meets the savory plate, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Château de Rouillac|Rainbow Trout": "Château de Rouillac's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Château de Rouillac for the steak course.",
  "Château de Rouillac|Roast Half Chicken": "Château de Rouillac's leather-tobacco tannin leans against the chicken's herbed crisp skin — the medium-body red supports the herb-crisped bird, and the cassis plays against the grilled char. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Château de Rouillac|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Château de Rouillac's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit overwhelms the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Château de Rouillac for the steak course.",
  "Château de Rouillac|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Château de Rouillac's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit clashes with the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Château de Rouillac for the steak course.",
  "Château de Rouillac|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Château de Rouillac's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit overshadows the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- red weight crowds a green side without lifting it — needs crisp register, not tannin. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Château de Rouillac lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Château de Rouillac|Seafood Tower": "Château de Rouillac's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Château de Rouillac belongs on the steak course.",
  "Château de Rouillac|Seared Scallops": "Left-bank Bordeaux against scallop sweetness — firm-tannin blackcurrant-cedar buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Château de Rouillac for the steak course.",
  "Château de Rouillac|Seasonal Soup": "Château de Rouillac's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit jars against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Château de Rouillac for the steak course.",
  "Château de Rouillac|Seasonal Vegetables": "Château de Rouillac's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit overshadows the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate -- red weight crowds a green side without lifting it — needs crisp register, not tannin. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Château de Rouillac for the steak course.",
  "Château de Rouillac|Shrimp Bisque": "Château de Rouillac's leather-tobacco tannin sits beside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the medium-body red frames the hearty soup. Works; capable alongside. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Château de Rouillac|Shrimp Cocktail": "Left-bank Bordeaux against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — firm-tannin red and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Château de Rouillac for the steak course.",
  "Château de Rouillac|Swordfish": "Château de Rouillac's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Château de Rouillac for the steak course.",
  "Château de Rouillac|The Tomahawk": "Château de Rouillac's leather-tobacco tannin holds the line with the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the medium-body red meets the cap-fat at lighter register, and the cassis plays against the grilled char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Château de Rouillac|Tomato Basil": "Château de Rouillac's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit overwhelms the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Le Garenne Rosé, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Château de Rouillac on the steak course instead.",
  "Château de Rouillac|Truffle Fries": "Pessac-Léognan left-bank Bordeaux — blackcurrant, cedar, graphite, tobacco, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the graphite plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak left-bank Bordeaux for truffle fries — French earth doubles the fries' earthy hit. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Château de Rouillac|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Château de Rouillac's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit overshadows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- dark-fruit weight crowds the seared sesame crust — needs a sparkling or crisp white for lift. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Château de Rouillac belongs on the steak course.",
  "Château de Rouillac|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Château de Rouillac's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit overwhelms the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Le Garenne Rosé, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Château de Rouillac for the steak course.",
  "Clam Chowder|1792 Small Batch": "1792 Small Batch's caramel-spice character sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chowder, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the complex profile is over-specified for this dish.",
  "Clam Chowder|1792 Sweet Wheat": "1792 Sweet Wheat's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the chowder, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; the toast notes don't really interplay with the soup but don't clash.",
  "Clam Chowder|1881 Napa Valley": "1881 Napa Valley's bold cherry-coffee cassis holds with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Clam Chowder|2 James Gin": "2 James Gin's crisp char-juniper botanicals reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the juniper carries the shellfish. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Clam Chowder|A Midnight's Winter Dram": "A Midnight's Winter Dram's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the malt-driven body wraps the chowder, and the oak softens the cream. Works; the aging is wasted on the salad.",
  "Clam Chowder|Aberlour 16": "Aberlour 16's double-matured Speyside balance reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the malt-and-oak threads the chowder, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; annual-release covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Clam Chowder|Adictivo Cristalino": "Adictivo Cristalino's cooked-agave-and-oak register reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the barrel-rested body handles the chowder, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Clam Chowder|Adictivo Reposado": "Adictivo Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the oak-aged tequila body threads the chowder, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Clam Chowder|Alexander Valley Chardonnay": "Sonoma Chardonnay — ripe apple, pear, warm vanilla oak, smooth balanced texture. The oak-vanilla weight aligns with the chowder's cream weight and the apple-pear lifts the clam-potato base. Strong accessible Chardonnay for clam chowder — California oak on the classic.",
  "Clam Chowder|Alexander Valley Cyrus": "Alexander Valley Cyrus's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the opulent body overshoots the light soup. Works; the match holds without overshooting. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Clam Chowder|Alexander Valley Homestead Red": "Alexander Valley Homestead Red's silky red-fruit lift leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the silky body carries the chowder, and the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Clam Chowder|Amaro Nonino": "Amaro Nonino's crisp orange-peel-grappa sweetness fights the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- bitter herbs cut the bisque's round cream without lifting it. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Amaro Nonino lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Clam Chowder|Ancho Reyes": "Ancho Reyes' sweet liqueur character doubles down on the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- sugar piled onto cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — no contrast. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Ancho Reyes lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Clam Chowder|Angel's Envy": "Angel's Envy's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon depth settles into the chowder, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the cream. Works; EC 18 frames the two-cut plate at aged-HH register.",
  "Clam Chowder|Angel's Envy Cask Strength": "Angel's Envy Cask Strength's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chowder, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; Boss Hog's allocation story is wasted on the salad.",
  "Clam Chowder|Angel's Envy Triple Cask": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon body sits with the chowder, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; the smooth character gives the dessert a composed frame.",
  "Clam Chowder|Aperol": "Aperol's crisp bitter-orange-aperitivo edge clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Aperol belongs on the steak course.",
  "Clam Chowder|Asparagus": "The chowder and the asparagus on the same meal -- the bright register cleaves the heavy course, the table breathes. Works; sequence or share, the build holds.",
  "Clam Chowder|Au Gratin Potatoes": "The chowder and the au gratin share potato as the primary character. Avoid; the meal doubles down without contrast. Route the chowder with Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis or the au gratin with Bone-In Filet, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Keenan Chardonnay instead.",
  "Clam Chowder|Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon": "Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the wine's structure sits on top of the bisque's cream instead of integrating. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Clam Chowder|Averna Amaro": "Averna Amaro's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- amaro bitterness on dairy cream reads metallic — no bridge from herbal sharp to soft fat. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Averna Amaro belongs on the steak course.",
  "Clam Chowder|Aviation": "Aviation's crisp almond-cherry build sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Clam Chowder|Aviation Gin": "Aviation Gin's floral-juniper botanicals reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals lift the shellfish. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Clam Chowder|Avion 44": "Avion 44's cooked-agave-and-oak register sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the aged-agave weight wraps the chowder, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Clam Chowder|Avion Silver": "Avion Silver's silver-spirit lift with agave-citrus edge leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the unaged body brightens the chowder, and the agave-citrus thread frames the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bacardi Rum": "Bacardi Rum's crisp workhorse-clean character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the unaged body brightens the chowder, and the unaged-cane note frames the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Clam Chowder|Baileys Irish Cream": "Baileys Irish Cream's sweet liqueur character clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Baileys Irish Cream on the steak course instead.",
  "Clam Chowder|Baker's": "Baker's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon depth settles into the chowder, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the smooth character gives the dessert a composed frame.",
  "Clam Chowder|Balvenie 12 American Oak": "Balvenie 12 American Oak's bourbon-cask Speyside softness sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the malt-driven body wraps the chowder, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; boutique-craft doesn't drive.",
  "Clam Chowder|Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask": "Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask's rum-finished Speyside character reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the scotch backbone matches the chowder, and the oak threads the cream. Works; complexity wasted on salad.",
  "Clam Chowder|Balvenie 16 Single Barrel": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's Highland-scotch character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the Highland register carries the chowder, and the oak threads the cream. Works; OGD 16 frames the two-cut plate at distinctive register.",
  "Clam Chowder|Balvenie 21 Portwood": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the malt-and-oak threads the chowder, and the oak softens the cream. Works; light body doesn't overshoot.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bardstown Château Laboude": "Bardstown Château Laboude's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chowder, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; OGD 16 handles dessert density at distinctive register.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bardstown Discovery #6": "Bardstown Discovery #6's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon body sits with the chowder, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; HH 20 is over-specified for an app; save the collector bottle for the main.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bardstown Founders KBS": "Bardstown Founders KBS's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon weight handles the chowder, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bardstown Foursquare": "Bardstown Foursquare's rum-cask + cocoa is textbook — tropical-rum + chocolate leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon depth settles into the chowder, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the 80-proof softness doesn't overshoot the salad the way heavier bourbons do.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bardstown Fusion #7": "Bardstown Fusion #7's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon weight handles the chowder, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; AE Triple Cask meets the char at distinctive register.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel": "Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon body sits with the chowder, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Clam Chowder|Basil Hayden's": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chowder, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; premium proof overpowers this dish.",
  "Clam Chowder|Basil Hayden's 10 Year": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon backbone carries the chowder, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; bonded weight pushes slightly past the soup.",
  "Clam Chowder|Basil Hayden's Malted Rye": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the rye backbone drives the chowder, and the oak threads the cream. Works; Fortuna's NZ terroir meets the glaze at distinctive register.",
  "Clam Chowder|Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chowder, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the distinctive character is underused by the salad's simplicity.",
  "Clam Chowder|Basil Hayden's Toast": "Basil Hayden's Toast's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the caramel-spice register matches the chowder, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the blend's complexity is underused by the salad.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bee's Knees": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build sits beside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the honey threads the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Clam Chowder|Beefeater Gin": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals sits beside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the juniper carries the shellfish. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Clam Chowder|Beignets": "The chowder and the beignets -- the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base bookends with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Clam Chowder|Belvedere Vodka": "Belvedere Vodka's bold Polish-rye-clean neutrality reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Clam Chowder|Blade & Bow": "Blade & Bow's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon backbone carries the chowder, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; concentrated blend slightly over-specified.",
  "Clam Chowder|Blanton's Gold": "Blanton's Gold's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon backbone carries the chowder, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; the complex character gives the dessert a refined frame.",
  "Clam Chowder|Blanton's Original": "Blanton's Original's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the caramel-spice register matches the chowder, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Clam Chowder|Blanton's Straight from the Barrel": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon depth settles into the chowder, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; craft-blender complexity over-specified.",
  "Clam Chowder|Blood Oath Pact 10": "Blood Oath Pact 10's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the caramel-spice register matches the chowder, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Clam Chowder|Blood Oath Pact 8": "Blood Oath Pact 8's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon weight handles the chowder, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Clam Chowder|Blood Oath Pact 9": "Blood Oath Pact 9's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the oak depth lays under the chowder, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the premium pour is wasted on the salad's simplicity.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bluecoat Gin": "Bluecoat Gin's char-citrus botanicals sits beside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bodega Noemia A Lisa": "Bodega Noemia A Lisa's bold earth-floral cassis stays alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the floral edge frames the shellfish. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bombay Dry Gin": "Bombay Dry Gin's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals lift the shellfish. Works; reliable companion, low risk. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bombay Sapphire Gin": "Bombay Sapphire Gin's crisp London-Dry-citrus botanicals leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bone Marrow": "The bone marrow preceded by the chowder -- cream meets protein, the meal builds with weight. Works; safe opening pair, the meal builds without strain.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bone-In Filet": "Bone-In Filet preceded by the chowder -- two rich courses on the same plate, the table earns its substance. Works; the opener primes the cut without strain.",
  "Clam Chowder|Booker's": "Booker's' cask-strength bourbon depth finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chowder, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; milestone-edition over-specified.",
  "Clam Chowder|Botanist Gin": "Botanist Gin's crisp Islay-gentle-botanical botanicals sits beside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals lift the shellfish. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bowdie's Old Fashioned": "Buffalo Trace Old Fashioned against a cream-based clam chowder — bourbon vanilla-caramel has no hook into shellfish-cream classic. Never layer. Route the cocktail to fatted steaks or marrow; take chowder with Chardonnay, Chablis, or Pinot Blanc.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark": "Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon backbone carries the chowder, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; rare-release wasted on salad.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bowman Brothers Small Batch": "Bowman Brothers Small Batch's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon weight handles the chowder, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bowmore 12": "Bowmore 12's lighter-Islay peat character sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the malt-driven body wraps the chowder, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; the Dylan-brand story is wasted on the salad.",
  "Clam Chowder|Braida Montebruna Barbera": "Braida Montebruna Barbera's cherry-earth tannin reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Clam Chowder|Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Clam Chowder|Broccolini": "The chowder alongside the broccolini -- bright-acid breaks the weight, the plate finds its lift. Works; the table can build them in order or together.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bruichladdich": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the scotch backbone matches the chowder, and the oak threads the cream. Works; BIB slightly over-specified.",
  "Clam Chowder|Brussels and Belly": "Clam Chowder and Brussels + Belly -- the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base meets Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: cream meets protein, the meal builds with weight. Works; no conflict however the table orders them.",
  "Clam Chowder|Buffalo Trace": "Buffalo Trace's rounded vanilla-and-toffee character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the chowder, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; Marian McLain L.E.",
  "Clam Chowder|Buffalo Trace Cream": "Buffalo Trace Cream's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- sugar piled onto cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — no contrast. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Buffalo Trace Cream lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Clam Chowder|Bulleit Bourbon": "Bulleit Bourbon's high-rye spice-forward depth finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon weight handles the chowder, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; spice over-specified for side's character.",
  "Clam Chowder|Burrata": "Burrata and the chowder together -- restrained yields to cream, the table arcs cleanly. Works; the table opens with both, no clash either way.",
  "Clam Chowder|Cade Cabernet Sauvignon": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Clam Chowder|Camarena Tequila": "Camarena Tequila's aged-agave character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the barrel-rested body handles the chowder, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; luxury ceremony over-specified for two-cut plate.",
  "Clam Chowder|Campari": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Clam Chowder|Canadian Club": "Canadian Club's workhorse Canadian blend leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the rye-blended Canadian body sits with the chowder, and the oak threads the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Clam Chowder|Canadian Club 43 Year": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the easygoing Canadian character handles the chowder, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; collector-bottle depth gives ultra-premium character.",
  "Clam Chowder|Captain Morgan Rum": "Captain Morgan Rum's light-rum register with cane and citrus lift mis-pairs with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the light spirit doesn't add to the soup-salad course — neutral but wrong. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a light spirit. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Captain Morgan Rum for the steak course.",
  "Clam Chowder|Caribou Crossing": "Caribou Crossing's Canadian whisky character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the Canadian whisky weight matches the chowder, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; bonded weight pushes past the soup's register slightly.",
  "Clam Chowder|Carrot Cake": "Clam Chowder and the carrot cake -- cream-and-sugar build the close, the meal finishes generous. Works; either timing holds, the table builds either way.",
  "Clam Chowder|Casa LBV Port": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Clam Chowder|Casamigos Mezcal": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- mezcal smoke fights the soup's cream — smoke has no bridge into dairy delicacy. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a mezcal. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Casamigos Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Clam Chowder|Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon": "Napa Rutherford Cab against a cream-based clam chowder — concentrated cocoa-mocha body crushes the delicate shellfish soup. Never pair. Route Caymus to the steak course and take chowder with Chardonnay, Chablis, or Pinot Blanc.",
  "Clam Chowder|Chambord": "Chambord's sweet liqueur character clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Chambord for the steak course.",
  "Clam Chowder|Cheesecake": "Clam Chowder and the cheesecake -- rich dairy yields to dessert weight, the close composes thickly. Works; sequence them as opener and close or share the table, no clash.",
  "Clam Chowder|Chilean Seabass": "The seabass after the chowder -- the silky-flesh seabass composes with the silky chowder bowl. Works; the opener sits without competing.",
  "Clam Chowder|Chocolate Brownie": "Clam Chowder and the brownie -- rich dairy yields to dessert weight, the close composes thickly. Works; sequence them as opener and close or share the table, no clash.",
  "Clam Chowder|Chocolate Cake": "The chowder and the chocolate cake -- the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base bookends with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Clam Chowder|Chopin Vodka": "Chopin Vodka's bold char-cream neutrality leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the caramel-spice settles the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Clam Chowder|Christian Bros Brandy": "Christian Bros Brandy's rancio-edged cognac weight leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the brandy depth wraps the chowder, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Clam Chowder|Château Batailley": "Château Batailley's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the wine's structure sits on top of the bisque's cream instead of integrating. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Château Batailley lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Clam Chowder|Château Beaucastel": "Château Beaucastel's old-world Châteauneuf-du-Pape gravitas flattens the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the wine's structure sits on top of the bisque's cream instead of integrating. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Château Beaucastel for the steak course.",
  "Clam Chowder|Château Gombaude-Guillot": "Château Gombaude-Guillot's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit overwhelms the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Château Gombaude-Guillot for the steak course.",
  "Clam Chowder|Château Haut Segottes": "Château Haut Segottes' Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit flattens the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the wine's structure sits on top of the bisque's cream instead of integrating. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Château Haut Segottes on the steak course instead.",
  "Clam Chowder|Château de Rouillac": "Château de Rouillac's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Château de Rouillac for the steak course.",
