  "Clam Chowder|Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon": "Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon's classical-Napa Cab elegance flattens the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the wine's structure sits on top of the bisque's cream instead of integrating. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Clam Chowder|Joseph Mellot Sancerre": "Loire Sancerre — refined tension-filled mineral, citrus, flint. The flinty citrus tension cuts the chowder's cream weight and the mineral plays against clam brine. Works as Sancerre for clam chowder — Loire precision on the classic; Chardonnays peak higher on the cream-forward base.",
  "Clam Chowder|Jubilation by Colgin": "Jubilation by Colgin's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Jubilation by Colgin belongs on the steak course.",
  "Clam Chowder|Jung and Wulff Guyana": "Jung and Wulff Guyana's high-proof pour register reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the dense-spirit weight carries the chowder, and the dense weight underlines the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Clam Chowder|Jung and Wulff Trinidad": "Jung and Wulff Trinidad's dense-spirit weight sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the heavy body handles the chowder, and the dense weight underlines the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Clam Chowder|Kahlua": "Kahlua's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- sugar piled onto cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — no contrast. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Kahlua lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Clam Chowder|Kansas City": "The KC after the chowder -- the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base sets the table for the KC's lean-bold strip with savory grain: two rich courses on the same plate, the table earns its substance. Works; the opener carries before the cut.",
  "Clam Chowder|Keenan Chardonnay": "Spring Mountain Napa Chardonnay — green apple, lemon curd, subtle oak, bright acid. The bright acid cuts the chowder's cream weight and the lemon curd lifts the clam brine. Peak balanced Chardonnay for clam chowder — Napa structure on the creamy classic. Gold standard; the headline call at the table.",
  "Clam Chowder|Keenan Mernet": "Keenan Mernet's bold cherry-earth cassis plays cleanly against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Clam Chowder|Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the chowder, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; GTS is over-specified for an app; save the collector bottle for the main course.",
  "Clam Chowder|Kentucky Owl Confiscated": "Kentucky Owl Confiscated's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon body sits with the chowder, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; OGD 16 frames the two-cut plate at distinctive register.",
  "Clam Chowder|Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's": "Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's Irish whiskey smoothness clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the soup-salad course needs lift, not oak-and-vanilla depth. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's for the steak course.",
  "Clam Chowder|Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône": "Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône's cherry-earth tannin sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the botanicals lift the shellfish. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Clam Chowder|Ketel One Vodka": "Ketel One Vodka's Dutch-wheat-crisp neutrality leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Clam Chowder|Knickerbocker Gin": "Knickerbocker Gin's bold citrus-juniper botanicals stays alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Clam Chowder|Knob Creek": "Knob Creek's oak-and-vanilla 100-proof depth sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chowder, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the toast notes don't really interplay with the soup but don't clash.",
  "Clam Chowder|Knob Creek 12 Year": "Knob Creek 12 Year's aged 12 years at 100 proof leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon depth settles into the chowder, and the rounded sweetness brightens the cream. Works; annual-release complexity over-specified.",
  "Clam Chowder|Knob Creek 15 Year": "Knob Creek 15 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon body sits with the chowder, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; the Millennium's register overshoots the dessert's.",
  "Clam Chowder|Knob Creek 18 Year": "Knob Creek 18 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chowder, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; bonded weight pushes slightly past the soup.",
  "Clam Chowder|Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye": "Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the chowder, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; annual-release covers both cuts without standing out.",
