  "Clam Chowder|Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut": "Tours-sur-Marne Chardonnay-blend Champagne — precise green apple, lemon zest, whisper of brioche, vibrant acidity. The high-acid finish cuts the chowder's cream weight and the brioche plays against potato-bacon base. Strong Champagne for clam chowder — bubbles on the creamy shellfish classic.",
  "Clam Chowder|Le Garenne Rosé": "Loire Pinot Noir rosé — delicate fresh-fruit, strawberry, crisp. The crisp body cuts the chowder's cream weight and the fresh fruit plays against the clam brine. Works as summer rosé for clam chowder — Loire delicacy on the shellfish classic.",
  "Clam Chowder|Le Ragnaie Brunello": "Le Ragnaie Brunello's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity flattens the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the wine's structure sits on top of the bisque's cream instead of integrating. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Le Ragnaie Brunello on the steak course instead.",
  "Clam Chowder|Le Volte dell'Ornellaia": "Le Volte dell'Ornellaia's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bright Sangiovese body lifts the chowder, and the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; the side sits without pulling focus.",
  "Clam Chowder|Lemon Lavender Gin Martini": "Lemon Lavender Gin Martini's citrus-floral build leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the honey threads the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Clam Chowder|Les Pallières Raciné": "Les Pallières Raciné's bold earth-mineral cassis sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Clam Chowder|Liberator Gin": "Liberator Gin's citrus-juniper botanicals leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Clam Chowder|Licor 43": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the liqueur's sweetness buries the soup's creamy base instead of supporting it. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Licor 43 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Clam Chowder|Limoncello": "Limoncello's sweet liqueur character clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Limoncello on the steak course instead.",
  "Clam Chowder|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Willamette Pinot — dark cherry, forest floor, refined structure, low tannin. The low-tannin silk lifts the chowder's cream weight and the forest-floor earth plays against bacon-potato base. Works as Oregon Pinot for clam chowder — unconventional red on the shellfish-cream classic.",
  "Clam Chowder|Little Book": "Little Book's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the oak depth lays under the chowder, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; distinctive finish over-specified.",
  "Clam Chowder|Lobster Mac": "The chowder alongside the lobster mac -- both bring shellfish as the headline. Avoid; one is enough. Pair the chowder with Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis; pair the lobster mac with Cowboy Ribeye, Far Niente Chardonnay, or The Tomahawk.",
