  "Clam Chowder|Los Vecinos Mezcal": "Los Vecinos Mezcal's smoky agave character clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- mezcal smoke fights the soup's cream — smoke has no bridge into dairy delicacy. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a mezcal. Avoid; the better calls are above. Pour the Los Vecinos Mezcal on the steak course instead.",
  "Clam Chowder|Louis XIII Cognac": "Louis XIII Cognac's luxury-icon cognac depth mis-pairs with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- an icon cognac on a soup-salad course is wrong moment — its register demands the close, not the open. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an icon cognac. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Louis XIII Cognac on the steak course instead.",
