  "Clam Chowder|Truffle Fries": "The chowder and the truffle fries share potato as the primary character. Avoid; the meal doubles down without contrast. Route the chowder with Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis or the truffle fries with The Tomahawk, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Belvedere Vodka instead.",
  "Clam Chowder|Tullamore D.E.W.": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the soft malt-and-grain weight wraps the chowder, and the oak threads the cream. Works; boutique covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Clam Chowder|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna preceded by the chowder -- the seared-rare yellowfin holds beside the chowder. Works; the call holds at neutral register.",
  "Clam Chowder|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "The chowder alongside the curry -- the clam-and-potato body composes with the curry. Works; the opening pair holds at table register.",
  "Clam Chowder|Venge Family Reserve": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis holds with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Clam Chowder|Venge Scout's Honor": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Clam Chowder|Venge Silencieux": "Venge Silencieux's bold cherry-chocolate cassis stays alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Clam Chowder|Vesper": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build sits beside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Clam Chowder|Veuve Clicquot Brut": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's biscuit-apple acidity reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the mousse refreshes against the broth, and the apple notes lift the custard. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Clam Chowder|Vieux Carré": "Vieux Carré's bold herbal-spice build stays alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the whiskey-build weight overshoots the light soup, and the botanicals lift the shellfish. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Clam Chowder|Villon Cognac": "Villon Cognac's barrel-aged cognac character reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the brandy depth wraps the chowder, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; Ferrand's craft character handles the richness.",
  "Clam Chowder|Vin Santo": "Vin Santo's Tuscan dried-fruit-and-honey sweetness clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Vin Santo for the steak course.",
  "Clam Chowder|Weller 107": "Weller 107's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon body sits with the chowder, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Clam Chowder|Weller 12 Year": "Weller 12 Year's aged wheated honey-vanilla character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the oak depth lays under the chowder, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; Vermont-brand character doesn't drive.",
  "Clam Chowder|Weller Millennium": "Weller Millennium's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon depth settles into the chowder, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; namesake pour is wasted on the salad.",
  "Clam Chowder|Weller Special Reserve": "Weller Special Reserve's wheated soft-vanilla character finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon backbone carries the chowder, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Clam Chowder|Wheatley Vodka": "Wheatley Vodka's crisp cream neutrality stays alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Clam Chowder|WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel Rye": "WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the chowder, and the oak threads the cream. Works; the bourbon-and-side match sits without pulling focus.",
  "Clam Chowder|WhistlePig 12 Year Old World": "WhistlePig 12 Year Old World's rye-spice character sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the dry rye body wraps the chowder, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; rye spice doesn't particularly elevate the soup.",
  "Clam Chowder|WhistlePig 15 Year": "WhistlePig 15 Year's rye-spice character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the rye backbone drives the chowder, and the oak threads the cream. Works; accessible gentle match.",
  "Clam Chowder|WhistlePig Boss Hog IX 17 Year": "WhistlePig Boss Hog IX 17 Year's rye-spice character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the dry rye body wraps the chowder, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Clam Chowder|WhistlePig Boss Hog X Commandments": "WhistlePig Boss Hog X Commandments' rye-spice character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the rye spice cuts the chowder, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; the pour's delicacy doesn't overpower the soup, but doesn't particularly elevate it either.",
  "Clam Chowder|WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year": "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year's rye-spice character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the chowder, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Clam Chowder|Willett Pot Still Reserve": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon weight handles the chowder, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for a soup — save the collector bottle for the main course.",
  "Clam Chowder|Woodford Reserve": "Woodford Reserve's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the chowder, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Clam Chowder|Woodford Reserve Double Oaked": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon depth settles into the chowder, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; CC 43 Year is over-specified for a side; save the rare bottle for the main.",
  "Clam Chowder|Woodford Reserve Rye": "Woodford Reserve Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the chowder, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; AE Triple Cask meets the char at distinctive register.",
  "Clam Chowder|Woodinville Rye": "Woodinville Rye's rye-spice character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the high-rye spice register matches the chowder, and the oak softens the cream. Works; the pour's brightness is a gentle counterpoint to the dessert's richness.",
  "Clam Chowder|Yamazaki 12 Year": "Yamazaki 12 Year's Suntory Japanese flagship character finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the Japanese whisky balance frames the chowder, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; JD Bonded's backbone handles the richness at Bonded register.",
  "Clam Chowder|Yamazaki 18 Year": "Yamazaki 18 Year's aged Suntory mizunara character reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the Japanese whisky balance frames the chowder, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; single-barrel depth gives the dessert more than Small Batch.",
  "Clam Chowder|Yellow Chartreuse": "Yellow Chartreuse's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the better calls are above. Yellow Chartreuse belongs on the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Asparagus": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character finds neutral with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the barrel-rested body handles the asparagus, and the caramel-agave register brightens the side. Works; refinement is underserved by the dish density.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet Clase Azul Anejo. Works; sherry-butt-finished complexity handles richness at luxury register.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Beignets": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the aged-agave weight wraps the beignets, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the dessert. Works; accessible match.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Bone Marrow": "Clase Azul Anejo's caramel-butterscotch character sits with the marrow's umami-fat depth — the añejo depth cuts the umami fat, and the caramel echoes the grilled char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Bone-In Filet": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character leans against the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the barrel-rested body handles the bone-enhanced filet, and the oak threads the cut. Strong; reliable opener for the cut.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Broccoli Cheddar": "Clase Azul Anejo's añejo-pour depth reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the oak-aged tequila body threads the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Broccolini": "Clase Azul Anejo's rested-agave body reads alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the oak-aged tequila body threads the broccolini, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed meets Clase Azul Anejo. Excellent; caramel-dried-fruit-maple-butterscotch rides the maple glaze at ultra-premium register — the sherry-butt finish amplifies the glaze's sweetness.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Burrata": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character overwhelms the burrata's fresh basil-tomato-cream delicacy -- aged tequila is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Il Colle Prosecco Superiore, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Clase Azul Anejo for the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Butternut Squash": "Clase Azul Anejo's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the oak-aged tequila body threads the squash bisque, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; approachable agave cuts the glaze but not marquee.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Carrot Cake": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Clase Azul Anejo. Strong; caramel-dried-fruit-butterscotch amplifies cake spice at sherry-butt-finished register.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Cheesecake": "Clase Azul Anejo's rested-agave body leans against the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the barrel-rested body handles the cheesecake, and the cooked-agave note underlines the dessert. Works; Durango ceremony over-specified for small plate.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Chilean Seabass": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- aged tequila is wrong register for a main fish or poultry course. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Clase Azul Anejo on the steak course instead.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Chocolate Brownie": "Chocolate Brownie: warm dark chocolate meets Clase Azul Anejo. Excellent; the sherry-butt-finished dried-fruit-butterscotch character threads chocolate at luxury-icon register.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Chocolate Cake": "Clase Azul Anejo's barrel-aged tequila weight sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the chocolate cake, and the oak threads the dessert. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Clam Chowder": "Clase Azul Anejo's añejo-pour depth finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the rested-agave depth sits with the chowder, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; Durango presentation slightly over-specified.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Cowboy Ribeye": "Clase Azul Anejo's caramel-butterscotch character finds register with the ribeye's cap fat and char — the añejo weight matches the cap-fat, and the caramel echoes the grilled char. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Crab Cake": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character overwhelms the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- añejo weight has no foil against cold shellfish — needs sparkling or crisp white. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Clase Azul Anejo lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Creamed Spinach": "Clase Azul Anejo's caramel-butterscotch character frames the spinach's dairy-rich cream — the añejo weight overshoots the light side, and the caramel pairs into the cream. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Creamy Potato": "Clase Azul Anejo's barrel-aged tequila weight reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the potato soup, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; distinctive composed with this dish.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Creme Brulee": "Clase Azul Anejo's añejo-pour depth finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the barrel-rested body handles the brulee, and the caramel-agave register brightens the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Escargot": "Clase Azul Anejo's rested-agave body sits alongside the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the oak-aged tequila body threads the buttered escargot, and the soft-spice note softens the starter. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Faroe Island Salmon": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- aged tequila is wrong register for a main fish or poultry course. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Clase Azul Anejo for the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Filet Mignon": "Filet Mignon: tender lean cut meets Clase Azul Anejo. Excellent; the 25-month American-oak + sherry-butt character with its caramel-butterscotch depth frames filet at ultra-premium register — the ceramic-decanter añejo on the most refined cut.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|French Onion": "Clase Azul Anejo's barrel-aged tequila weight finds neutral with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the barrel-rested body handles the French onion, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; Ultra over-specified for small plate.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Grilled Caesar": "Clase Azul Anejo's añejo-pour depth finds neutral with the Caesar's charred-romaine and anchovy edge: the añejo register carries the grilled Caesar, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Gumbo": "Clase Azul Anejo's cooked-agave-and-oak register leans against the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the añejo register carries the gumbo, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; the aged depth is an unusual but interesting match.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Clase Azul Anejo's rested-agave body reads alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the barrel-rested body handles the honey carrots, and the oak threads the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|House Wedge": "Clase Azul Anejo's añejo-pour depth reads alongside the wedge's iceberg-and-bleu cool crunch: the oak-aged tequila body threads the wedge, and the caramel-agave register brightens the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Kansas City": "Clase Azul Anejo: ultra-premium Los Altos tequila, 25 months American oak + 2 months sherry butts, hand-painted ceramic decanter by Mexican artisans. Excellent on KC strip; the caramel-dried-fruit-maple-butterscotch character frames the lean cut at luxury-icon register — save the bottle for the guest who wants ceremony with their añejo.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Loaded Potato": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character leans against the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the loaded potato soup, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Lobster Mac": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak-aged tequila body threads the lobster mac, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; Durango presentation slightly over-specified.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Market Fish": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character clashes with the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- aged tequila is wrong register for a main fish or poultry course. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Clase Azul Anejo belongs on the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Mocha Creme": "Clase Azul Anejo's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the mocha creme, and the caramel-agave register brightens the dessert. Works; the wine-cask notes don't compete with the dish's sweetness effectively.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Mushroom Bisque": "Clase Azul Anejo's cooked-agave-and-oak register sits alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the aged-agave weight wraps the mushroom bisque, and the caramel-agave register brightens the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Mushrooms": "Mushrooms: earthy umami meets Clase Azul Anejo. Excellent; the 25-month-aged estate-terroir threads mushroom-earth at luxury-icon register — earth meets ceremonial-earth.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Clase Azul Anejo's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the aged-agave weight wraps the PB brownie, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the dessert. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Porterhouse": "Clase Azul Anejo's cooked-agave-and-oak register sits alongside the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character: the oak-aged tequila body threads the dual-cut steak, and the caramel-agave register brightens the cut. Strong; Clase Azul's refinement is slightly underserved by the cut's scale, but the ceremony is still the draw.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Prime Tartare": "Clase Azul Anejo's caramel-butterscotch character sits with the tartare's raw beef and brine — the añejo depth cuts the umami fat, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Rainbow Trout": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- aged tequila is wrong register for a main fish or poultry course. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Clase Azul Anejo lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Roast Half Chicken": "Clase Azul Anejo's cooked-agave-and-oak register sits alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the barrel-rested body handles the roast chicken, and the caramel-agave register brightens the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character leans against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the barrel-rested body handles the chickpea soup, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; the bold agave overpowers the dish's restraint.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character clashes with the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- aged tequila is wrong register for a main fish or poultry course. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Clase Azul Anejo for the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character sits alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the barrel-rested body handles the garlic spinach, and the caramel-agave register brightens the side. Works; covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Seafood Tower": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- aged tequila is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Clase Azul Anejo for the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Seared Scallops": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Clase Azul Anejo. Avoid; luxury-añejo too heavy for scallops. Save the bottle — reach for a blanco, light rum, or vodka.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Seasonal Soup": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the barrel-rested body handles the seasonal soup, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Seasonal Vegetables": "Clase Azul Anejo's rested-agave body reads alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the añejo register carries the seasonal vegetables, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; benchmark extra añejo is slightly ambitious for the two-cut plate.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Shrimp Bisque": "Clase Azul Anejo's barrel-aged tequila weight reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the shrimp bisque, and the caramel-agave register brightens the bowl. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Shrimp Cocktail": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- añejo weight has no foil against cold shellfish — needs sparkling or crisp white. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Clase Azul Anejo for the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Swordfish": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character fights the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the cask-aged agave register pulls against the savory sear. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Clase Azul Anejo for the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|The Tomahawk": "Clase Azul Anejo: ceramic-decanter añejo, 25 months American oak + 2 months sherry butts. Excellent on the Tomahawk; luxury-icon character matches showpiece cut at ceremonial register — save the bottle.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Tomato Basil": "Clase Azul Anejo's rested-agave body finds neutral with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the aged-agave weight wraps the tomato basil, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; wheated-soft character handles richness at gentler-Expresiones register.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Truffle Fries": "Truffle Fries: Parmesan-and-truffle meets Clase Azul Anejo. Excellent; the luxury-craftsmanship character with sherry-butt-finish complexity handles truffle-salt-fat at ceremonial register.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character fights the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the cask-aged agave register pulls against the savory sear. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Clase Azul Anejo for the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Anejo|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Clase Azul Anejo's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the barrel-rested body handles the curry, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Clase Azul Durango|Asparagus": "Clase Azul Durango's aged-agave character reads alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the asparagus, and the oak threads the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Clase Azul Durango|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Clase Azul Durango with au gratin potatoes — Durango-artisanship against cheese-and-cream. Works; ceremonial over-specified.",
  "Clase Azul Durango|Beignets": "Clase Azul Durango's barrel-aged tequila weight reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the barrel-rested body handles the beignets, and the oak threads the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Clase Azul Durango|Bone Marrow": "Clase Azul Durango with bone marrow — Durango-artisanship extra añejo against umami fat. The ceramic-bottle ceremony meets marrow at the ultra-premium Clase Azul register. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Clase Azul Durango|Bone-In Filet": "Clase Azul Durango with the bone-in filet — ceramic-bottle luxury against bone-in cut. The Durango-artisanship ceremony frames the cut with regional-Mexican craft presentation. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Clase Azul Durango|Broccoli Cheddar": "Clase Azul Durango's aged-agave character reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the barrel-rested body handles the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; Durango presentation slightly over-specified.",
  "Clase Azul Durango|Broccolini": "Clase Azul Durango's aged-agave character reads alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the rested-agave depth sits with the broccolini, and the oak threads the side. Works; clean and refined but not a marquee pairing.",
