  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Broccolini": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's wood-fire mezcal body leans against the broccolini's tender green stalks: the rustic mezcal weight sits with the broccolini, and the earthy backbone threads the side. Works; the close holds, neither soars nor fights.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet Clase Azul Guerrero. Excellent; the fruit-forward smoke rides the glaze at luxury-mezcal register — Guerrero's softer character finds the maple thread.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Burrata": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the burrata's fresh basil-tomato-cream delicacy -- mezcal smoke is too forward for the table's opener. The plate deserves Il Colle Prosecco Superiore, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, not a mezcal. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Save the Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Butternut Squash": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character clashes with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- mezcal smoke is wrong register for the soup-salad course. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a mezcal. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Carrot Cake": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's earthen-pit smoke profile sits alongside the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the smoky agave register handles the carrot cake, and the wood-smoke note underlines the dessert. Works; the dessert sits cleanly against the meal's register.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Cheesecake": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character overpowers the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- the plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not a mezcal. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Chilean Seabass": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- mezcal smoke and the fish's natural oils refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a mezcal. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Chocolate Brownie": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's earthen-pit smoke profile reads alongside the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight: the smoky agave register handles the brownie, and the earthy backbone threads the dessert. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Chocolate Cake": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's earthen-pit smoke profile sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the earthen-pit smoke carries the chocolate cake, and the mineral smoke plays against the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Clam Chowder": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- mezcal smoke fights the soup's cream — smoke has no bridge into dairy delicacy. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a mezcal. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal on the steak course instead.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Cowboy Ribeye": "Cowboy Ribeye: 26oz bone-in cap-fat meets Clase Azul Guerrero's luxury-mezcal polish. Excellent; the fruitier-Guerrero character frames the ribeye at ceremonial register — smoke softened, fruit amplified.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Crab Cake": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- mezcal smoke obliterates delicate shellfish — needs sparkling or sancerre. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not a mezcal. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Creamed Spinach": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's earthen-pit smoke profile leans against the creamed spinach's rich bechamel-laced greens: the wood-fire body meets the creamed spinach, and the campfire register frames the side. Works; a measured close to the meal.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Creamy Potato": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character clashes with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- mezcal smoke fights the soup's cream — smoke has no bridge into dairy delicacy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a mezcal. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal on the steak course instead.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Creme Brulee": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's wood-fire mezcal body sits alongside the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the smoky agave register handles the brulee, and the mineral smoke plays against the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Escargot": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character leans against the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the espadín-and-smoke body wraps the buttered escargot, and the earthy backbone threads the starter. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Faroe Island Salmon": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- mezcal smoke is wrong register for the main fish course. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a mezcal. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal belongs on the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Filet Mignon": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character reads alongside the filet's lean buttery tenderness: the espadín-and-smoke body wraps the lean buttery filet, and the campfire register frames the cut. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|French Onion": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's espadín-and-smoke register finds neutral with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the earthen-pit smoke carries the French onion, and the wood-smoke note underlines the bowl. Works; the two desserts share the close without crowding.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Grilled Caesar": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's espadín-and-smoke register meets at register with the Caesar's charred-romaine and anchovy edge: the earthen-pit smoke carries the grilled Caesar, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Gumbo": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- mezcal's smoke crowds the broth's clean register without lifting it. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not a mezcal. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal belongs on the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character reads alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the wood-fire body meets the honey carrots, and the wood-smoke note underlines the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
