  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Loaded Potato": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's espadín-and-smoke register reads alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the wood-fire body meets the loaded potato soup, and the mineral smoke plays against the bowl. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Lobster Mac": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's espadín-and-smoke register finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the espadín-and-smoke body wraps the lobster mac, and the campfire register frames the side. Works; too light for dessert density at this level.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Market Fish": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- mezcal smoke is wrong register for the main fish course. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a mezcal. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal for the steak course.",
