  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Prime Tartare": "Prime Tartare: hand-cut raw beef meets Clase Azul Guerrero. Excellent; the softer Guerrero-fruit smoke frames the tartare at ultra-premium register — luxury pour for a luxury raw plate.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Rainbow Trout": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- mezcal smoke is wrong register for the main fish course. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a mezcal. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal on the steak course instead.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Roast Half Chicken": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's earthen-pit smoke profile reads alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the smoky agave register handles the roast chicken, and the green-agave edge brightens the plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character clashes with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth -- mezcal smoke is wrong register for the soup-salad course. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a mezcal. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal on the steak course instead.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- mezcal smoke buries the delicate flesh — the fish has no foil against agave + smoke. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a mezcal. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's rustic mezcal weight reads alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the earthen-pit smoke carries the garlic spinach, and the earthy backbone threads the side. Works; the dessert sits cleanly against the meal's register.",
  "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal|Seafood Tower": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- mezcal smoke is too forward for the table's opener. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a mezcal. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal for the steak course.",
