  "Clase Azul Ultra|Chilean Seabass": "Clase Azul Ultra's aged-agave character clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- agave and oily fish refuse each other — the fish needs acid, not aged spirit. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Clase Azul Ultra for the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Ultra|Chocolate Brownie": "Clase Azul Ultra with the chocolate brownie — 5-year top-tier Clase Azul against cocoa. The Ultra's aged depth meets the brownie at the absolute ceremonial register; one of the menu's most layered dessert pairings. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
