  "Clase Azul Ultra|Faroe Island Salmon": "Clase Azul Ultra's aged-agave character clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- agave and oily fish refuse each other — the fish needs acid, not aged spirit. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Clase Azul Ultra for the steak course.",
  "Clase Azul Ultra|Filet Mignon": "Clase Azul Ultra with the filet — 5-year extra añejo, the top-tier Clase Azul with platinum/gold accents on hand-painted ceramic. Above Durango and Gold in the Clase Azul hierarchy; the collector-grade ceremonial pour. For guests who ask for the ultimate Clase Azul; the Ultra justifies its tier with actual 5-year aging. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
