  "Corazon Blanco|Broccolini": "Corazon Blanco's blanco-tequila or blanco-tequila register reads alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the broccolini, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Corazon Blanco|Brussels and Belly": "Corazon Blanco's clean silver register finds neutral with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the unaged body brightens the pork-belly plate, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Corazon Blanco|Burrata": "Corazon Blanco with burrata — Sazerac single-estate against fresh mozzarella. The highland character lifts the burrata distinctly from the big-brand blancos. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Corazon Blanco|Butternut Squash": "Corazon Blanco's silver-spirit lift with agave-citrus edge sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the unaged blanco body cuts the squash bisque, and the green-agave edge brightens the bowl. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Corazon Blanco|Carrot Cake": "Corazon Blanco's unaged blanco-tequila lift with agave-citrus snap falls short of the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- light spirit reads thin against dessert sweetness. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a light spirit. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Corazon Blanco on the steak course instead.",
  "Corazon Blanco|Cheesecake": "Corazon Blanco's unaged blanco-tequila lift with agave-citrus snap falls short of the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- light spirit reads thin against dessert sweetness. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not a light spirit. Avoid; one of those is the move. Corazon Blanco lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Corazon Blanco|Chilean Seabass": "Corazon Blanco's agave-citrus character sits with the seabass's buttery flesh — the crisp body frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Corazon Blanco|Chocolate Brownie": "Corazon Blanco's unaged blanco-tequila lift with agave-citrus snap falls short of the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- light spirit can't carry chocolate's weight — needs a richer pour like an aged rum or tawny. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not a light spirit. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Corazon Blanco belongs on the steak course.",
  "Corazon Blanco|Chocolate Cake": "Corazon Blanco's unaged blanco-tequila lift with agave-citrus snap falls short of the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- light spirit can't carry chocolate's weight — needs a richer pour like an aged rum or tawny. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not a light spirit. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Corazon Blanco lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Corazon Blanco|Clam Chowder": "Corazon Blanco's unaged silver-spirit body sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the chowder, and the unaged-cane note plays against the bowl. Works; refined craft composes cleanly.",
  "Corazon Blanco|Cowboy Ribeye": "Corazon Blanco's unaged blanco-tequila lift with agave-citrus snap underclubs the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness -- light spirit can't stand up to the marbled char — needs a Cab, bourbon, or añejo. The plate deserves Macallan 18, Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon, or Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon, not a light spirit. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Corazon Blanco for another course.",
  "Corazon Blanco|Crab Cake": "Crab Cake: lump crab meets Corazon Blanco — Sazerac's tequila brand, single-estate highland agave, 80-proof. Distinct from Don Julio Blanco's benchmark polish — more agave-forward highland character. Sister-pour to Corazon Reposado. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
