  "Creamy Potato|Keenan Chardonnay": "Spring Mountain Napa Chardonnay — green apple, lemon curd, subtle oak, bright acid. The bright acid cuts the soup's buttery cream weight and the subtle oak plays against the potato base. Peak balanced Chardonnay for creamy potato — Napa structure on the rich classic. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Creamy Potato|Keenan Mernet": "Keenan Mernet's bold cherry-earth cassis sits beside the potato soup's silky body — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Creamy Potato|Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the rye spice cuts the potato soup, and the oak threads the cream. Works; pour slightly over-specified for this dish.",
  "Creamy Potato|Kentucky Owl Confiscated": "Kentucky Owl Confiscated's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the bourbon backbone carries the potato soup, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; boutique at matched register.",
  "Creamy Potato|Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's": "Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's Irish whiskey smoothness clashes with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- the soup-salad course needs lift, not oak-and-vanilla depth. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's for the steak course.",
  "Creamy Potato|Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône": "Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône's cherry-earth tannin sits beside the potato soup's silky body — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Creamy Potato|Ketel One Vodka": "Ketel One Vodka's Dutch-wheat-crisp neutrality reads alongside the potato soup's silky body — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the clean profile lets the cheese speak. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Creamy Potato|Knickerbocker Gin": "Knickerbocker Gin's bold citrus-juniper botanicals sits beside the potato soup's silky body — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; safe call, no friction. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Creamy Potato|Knob Creek": "Knob Creek's oak-and-vanilla 100-proof depth reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the bourbon body sits with the potato soup, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; grain notes don't really engage the soup but don't clash.",
  "Creamy Potato|Knob Creek 12 Year": "Knob Creek 12 Year's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the bourbon body sits with the potato soup, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Creamy Potato|Knob Creek 15 Year": "Knob Creek 15 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the potato soup, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; IW Harper 15 handles dessert density at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Creamy Potato|Knob Creek 18 Year": "Knob Creek 18 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the caramel-spice register matches the potato soup, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; distinctive character doesn't drive but adds interest.",
  "Creamy Potato|Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye": "Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye's rye-spice character leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the rye spice cuts the potato soup, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Creamy Potato|Knob Creek Rye": "Knob Creek Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the rye backbone drives the potato soup, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Creamy Potato|Komos Anejo Reserva": "Komos Anejo Reserva's cooked-agave-and-oak register reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the aged-agave weight wraps the potato soup, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; accessible aged composes with the plate.",
  "Creamy Potato|Komos Crystallino Anejo": "Komos Crystallino Anejo's rested-agave body reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the barrel-rested body handles the potato soup, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; aged-but-clear character composes with the dish.",
  "Creamy Potato|Komos Extra Anejo": "Komos Extra Anejo's rested-agave body reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the barrel-rested body handles the potato soup, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; clean and refined but not a marquee pairing.",
  "Creamy Potato|Komos Rosa Reposado": "Komos Rosa Reposado's barrel-aged tequila weight finds neutral with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the barrel-rested body handles the potato soup, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; maturation depth composed with this dish.",
  "Creamy Potato|Lagavulin 8": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the peat-smoke meets the potato soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; AE CS meets the char at premium wine-finish register.",
  "Creamy Potato|Lail Vineyards Blueprint": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis stays alongside the potato soup's silky body — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Creamy Potato|Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée": "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée's bold floral-oak cassis holds with the potato soup's silky body — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Creamy Potato|Lalo Silver": "Lalo Silver's silver-spirit lift with agave-citrus edge finds neutral with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the unaged body brightens the potato soup, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the bowl. Works; craft character composes cleanly.",
  "Creamy Potato|Laphroaig 10": "Laphroaig 10's classic Islay peat reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the malt-and-oak threads the potato soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; PNW character doesn't drive.",
  "Creamy Potato|Larceny Small Batch": "Larceny Small Batch's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the potato soup, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; the bourbon-and-dessert match settles as a soft alongside.",
  "Creamy Potato|Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé": "Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé's bright sparkling effervescence finds neutral with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the fine bubbles lift the potato soup, and the citrus frames the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Creamy Potato|Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut": "Tours-sur-Marne Chardonnay-blend Champagne — precise green apple, lemon zest, whisper of brioche, vibrant acidity. The high-acid finish cuts the soup's cream weight and the brioche plays against the potato base. Strong Champagne for creamy potato — bubbles reset the palate between spoons.",
  "Creamy Potato|Le Garenne Rosé": "Loire Pinot Noir rosé — delicate fresh-fruit, strawberry, crisp. The crisp acid cuts the soup's cream weight and the fresh fruit plays against the potato base. Works as summer rosé for creamy potato — Loire delicacy on the rich classic.",
  "Creamy Potato|Le Ragnaie Brunello": "Le Ragnaie Brunello's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity clashes with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Le Ragnaie Brunello belongs on the steak course.",
  "Creamy Potato|Le Volte dell'Ornellaia": "Le Volte dell'Ornellaia's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity sits alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the bright Sangiovese body lifts the potato soup, and the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Creamy Potato|Lemon Lavender Gin Martini": "Lemon Lavender Gin Martini's citrus-floral build sits alongside the potato soup's silky body — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the honey threads the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Creamy Potato|Les Pallières Raciné": "Les Pallières Raciné's bold earth-mineral cassis reads alongside the potato soup's silky body — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the mineral edge cuts the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Creamy Potato|Liberator Gin": "Liberator Gin's citrus-juniper botanicals reads alongside the potato soup's silky body — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Creamy Potato|Licor 43": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character clashes with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Licor 43 on the steak course instead.",
  "Creamy Potato|Limoncello": "Limoncello's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- the liqueur's sweetness buries the soup's creamy base instead of supporting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Limoncello belongs on the steak course.",
  "Creamy Potato|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Willamette Pinot — dark cherry, forest floor, refined structure, low tannin. The low-tannin silk lifts the soup's cream-potato weight and the forest-floor earth plays against the dairy base. Works tier on this wine's card — solid fit for Creamy Potato but below the wine's peaks with duck, lamb, and mushroom-sauced proteins.",
  "Creamy Potato|Little Book": "Little Book's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the potato soup, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Creamy Potato|Lobster Mac": "The potato soup alongside the lobster mac -- cream stacked on cream, the plate reads dense across the meal. Works; the table can build them in order or together.",
  "Creamy Potato|Loch Lomond 20 Year": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the Highland register carries the potato soup, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; collector-bottle doesn't drive.",
  "Creamy Potato|Lock Stock & Barrel Rye": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the rye spice cuts the potato soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; Remus 15's rye-spice meets the glaze at Gatsby-tribute register.",
  "Creamy Potato|Long Road Gin": "Long Road Gin's crisp citrus-juniper botanicals sits alongside the potato soup's silky body — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Creamy Potato|Los Vecinos Mezcal": "Los Vecinos Mezcal's smoky agave character clashes with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- mezcal smoke is wrong register for the soup-salad course. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a mezcal. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Los Vecinos Mezcal on the steak course instead.",
  "Creamy Potato|Louis XIII Cognac": "Louis XIII Cognac's luxury-icon cognac depth mis-pairs with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- an icon cognac on a soup-salad course is wrong moment — its register demands the close, not the open. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an icon cognac. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Louis XIII Cognac lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Creamy Potato|Lucano Amaro": "Lucano Amaro's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- amaro bitterness on dairy cream reads metallic — no bridge from herbal sharp to soft fat. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Save the Lucano Amaro for the steak course.",
  "Creamy Potato|Lunaria Coste di Moro": "Lunaria Coste di Moro's char-cherry tannin leans against the potato soup's silky body — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
