  "Creamy Potato|Malibu Rum": "Malibu Rum's light-rum register with cane and citrus lift mis-pairs with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- the light spirit doesn't add to the soup-salad course — neutral but wrong. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a light spirit. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Malibu Rum for the steak course.",
  "Creamy Potato|Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye": "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the high-rye spice register matches the potato soup, and the oak threads the cream. Works; Old Fitz 9 brings more depth here.",
