  "Creamy Potato|Patron Anejo": "Patron Anejo's rested-agave body finds neutral with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the oak-aged tequila body threads the potato soup, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; wheated-soft character handles richness at gentler-Expresiones register.",
  "Creamy Potato|Patron Silver": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the silver-spirit register lifts the potato soup, and the green-agave edge brightens the bowl. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Creamy Potato|Patron XO Cafe": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- sugar piled onto cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Patron XO Cafe lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Creamy Potato|Paul Bara Grand Rosé Brut": "Paul Bara Grand Rosé Brut's crisp mineral-raspberry acidity reads alongside the potato soup's silky body — the mousse refreshes against the broth, and the mineral edge cuts the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Creamy Potato|Peanut Butter Brownie": "The potato soup and the PB brownie -- the potato soup's silky-bodied cream bookends with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Creamy Potato|Peju Cabernet Sauvignon": "Peju Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overwhelms the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Peju Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Creamy Potato|Pierre Ferrand Cognac": "Pierre Ferrand Cognac's artisan cognac with orange peel leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the Limousin-oak weight handles the potato soup, and the oak-and-vanilla edge brightens the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Creamy Potato|Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut": "Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut's char-citrus acidity sits alongside the potato soup's silky body — the mousse refreshes against the broth, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Creamy Potato|Pikesville Rye": "Pikesville Rye's rye-spice character leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the rye spice cuts the potato soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the 80-proof softness doesn't overshoot the salad the way heavier bourbons do.",
  "Creamy Potato|Pineau des Charentes": "Pineau des Charentes' sweet liqueur character clashes with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Pineau des Charentes for the steak course.",
  "Creamy Potato|Pio Cesare Barbaresco": "Pio Cesare Barbaresco's firm-tannin tar structure buries the delicate shellfish overwhelms the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Pio Cesare Barbaresco belongs on the steak course.",
  "Creamy Potato|Plymouth Gin": "Plymouth Gin's Plymouth-style-rounder botanicals plays cleanly against the potato soup's silky body — the gin botanicals sit with the plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Creamy Potato|Poderi Aldo Conterno Nebbiolo": "Poderi Aldo Conterno Nebbiolo's high-acid Nebbiolo with rose-and-tar grip clashes with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Poderi Aldo Conterno Nebbiolo on the steak course instead.",
  "Creamy Potato|Pommery Cuvée Louise": "Pommery Cuvée Louise's mineral-prestige acidity sits alongside the potato soup's silky body — the mousse refreshes against the broth, and the mineral edge cuts the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Creamy Potato|Porterhouse": "The porterhouse after the potato soup -- the potato soup's silky-bodied cream sets the table for the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character: cream rounds the protein, the plate composes thick. Works; the opener carries before the cut.",
  "Creamy Potato|Prime Tartare": "Prime Tartare alongside the potato soup -- cream and umami share the plate, the build reads dense and clean. Works; the openers share the table cleanly, sequence or share.",
