  "Creme Brulee|Escargot": "The escargot alongside the brulee -- sugar plays against the savory weight, the table earns its lift. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Creme Brulee|Espresso Martini": "Tito's, espresso, Grind Espresso Liqueur, Averna amaro, vanilla syrup, Angostura. The Averna's bitter herbal backbone cuts through the crème brûlée's cream and the vanilla-on-vanilla axis aligns. Strong cocktail route for guests who want coffee with dessert.",
  "Creme Brulee|Espresso Old Fashioned": "Espresso Old Fashioned's sweet coffee-cream build finds register with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar, and the nut character deepens the cream. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Creme Brulee|Evening Land Seven Springs": "Evening Land Seven Springs' red-fruit-and-spice elegance jars against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Evening Land Seven Springs for the steak course.",
  "Creme Brulee|Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon": "Creme Brulee: this delicate custard's creamy, vanilla sweetness meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. Creamy vanilla or airy beignets get run over by bold-red tannin. Works as an unconventional pour — set expectations.",
  "Creme Brulee|Far Niente Chardonnay": "Far Niente Chardonnay's estate Napa Chardonnay character clashes with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- dry-white acidity and dessert tang refuse each other without sweetness to bridge. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not a white wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Far Niente Chardonnay for the steak course.",
  "Creme Brulee|Faroe Island Salmon": "After the salmon, the brulee -- the oily-rich Faroe yields to vanilla-bean custard and torched-sugar crust, berries lifting the close. Strong; the rich fish meets the silky dessert, the close lands clean.",
