  "Creme Brulee|Jameson Irish Whiskey": "Jameson Irish Whiskey's classic Irish blend smoothness finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the smooth triple-distilled register matches the brulee, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; pour is a touch over-specified for the dessert.",
  "Creme Brulee|Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir": "Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift jars against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- tannin reads astringent next to dairy custard, the custard reads sour back. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir for the steak course.",
  "Creme Brulee|Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis": "Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis' Burgundy Chablis flinty minerality clashes with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- dry-white acidity and dessert tang refuse each other without sweetness to bridge. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not a white wine. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis for the steak course.",
  "Creme Brulee|Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E.": "Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E.'s rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the bourbon body sits with the brulee, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; milestone-release doesn't drive.",
