  "Creme Brulee|Malibu Rum": "Malibu Rum's clean silver register sits alongside the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the silver-rum body cuts the brulee, and the bright sugarcane edge underlines the dessert. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Creme Brulee|Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye": "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the dry rye body wraps the brulee, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; the spicy-sweet character gives the dessert a Barton frame.",
  "Creme Brulee|Marc Brédif Chinon": "Marc Brédif Chinon's herbaceous Cab Franc with red-fruit and bell-pepper jars against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Marc Brédif Chinon lands on the steak course — not here.",
