  "Creme Brulee|Mushroom Bisque": "Mushroom Bisque and the brulee -- sugar plays against the savory weight, the table earns its lift. Works; either timing holds, the table builds either way.",
  "Creme Brulee|Mushrooms": "Mushrooms and the brulee -- sugar and umami share the table, the contrast carries the meal. Works; the meal closes cleanly from the side.",
  "Creme Brulee|Myers's Rum": "Myers's Rum's high-proof pour register sits alongside the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the heavy body handles the brulee, and the heavy-pour register grips the dessert. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Creme Brulee|Negroni": "Equal parts gin, Contratto vermouth, Campari. The Campari's bitterness clashes with vanilla custard and the gin adds nothing helpful. Wrong cocktail for crème brûlée — keep Negroni with the mushrooms or marrow where it meets savory depth. Avoid; pair this elsewhere on the menu.",
