  "Darioush Cabernet Franc|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Darioush Cabernet Franc's herbaceous Cab Franc with red-fruit and bell-pepper clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- tannin against rare-seared crust reads astringent without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Darioush Cabernet Franc belongs on the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Franc|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Darioush Cabernet Franc's herbaceous Cab Franc with red-fruit and bell-pepper jars against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Le Garenne Rosé, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Darioush Cabernet Franc for the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Asparagus": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- tannin on raw green vegetable reads astringent without payoff. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Silverado Trail Cab — blackcurrant, dark plum, mocha, spice, plush. The opulent body cuts au gratin's cheese-and-cream weight and the mocha-spice plays against the golden crust. Works as opulent Napa Cab for au gratin — Darioush Persian-inspired plushness on the decadent side.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Beignets": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Bone Marrow": "Silverado Trail Cab — blackcurrant, dark plum, mocha, spice, rich plush. The opulent body meets marrow's rendered-fat richness and the mocha-spice frames the bone depth. Peak opulent Napa Cab for marrow — Darioush Persian-inspired story plus plush concentration handles the rich starter. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Bone-In Filet": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's bold coffee-mocha cassis frames the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the firm tannin reads cleanly against the lean cut, and the cassis plays against the grilled char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Broccoli Cheddar": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Broccolini": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overshadows the broccolini's tender green stalks -- red weight crowds a green side without lifting it — needs crisp register, not tannin. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Burrata": "Opulent Silverado Trail Cab against burrata's creamy-delicate center — plush mocha-spice body crushes the milk and basil-tomato-pistachio clashes with blackcurrant-plum. Never pair. Route burrata to rosé, Pinot Blanc, or Sancerre and keep Darioush for the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Butternut Squash": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Carrot Cake": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Cheesecake": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Chilean Seabass": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- tannin on oily fish goes bitter, where a Pinot at the right register would carry it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Chocolate Brownie": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- savory tannin sits awkwardly on cocoa weight without resolving. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Chocolate Cake": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Clam Chowder": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Cowboy Ribeye": "Darioush — Silverado Trail Cab from one of Napa's most architecturally striking Persian-inspired estates. Rich opulent: blackcurrant, dark plum, mocha, spice, plush full finish. The opulent body handles Cowboy's marbled bone-in richness and the mocha-spice meets rendered fat. Peak opulent Napa Cab for Cowboy — estate-story adds occasion. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Crab Cake": "Opulent Silverado Trail Cab against crab cake's delicate sweet shellfish — plush mocha-spice crushes romesco-and-crab. Never pair. Route crab cake to Chablis, Sancerre, or Champagne and keep Darioush for the steak course where its Persian-inspired plush character shines.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Creamed Spinach": "Darioush — Silverado Trail Cab with blackcurrant, dark plum, mocha, spice. The opulent body cuts creamed spinach's dairy weight and the mocha-spice plays against the earthy sauce. Strong opulent Napa Cab for creamed spinach — Persian-inspired estate story on the classic steakhouse side.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Creamy Potato": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- the wine's structure sits on top of the bisque's cream instead of integrating. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Creme Brulee": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Escargot": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's bold coffee-mocha cassis holds steady against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the Cab structure meets the savory depth, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Faroe Island Salmon": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Filet Mignon": "Silverado Trail Cab — blackcurrant, dark plum, mocha, spice, rich plush. The opulent body meets butter-tender filet's lean sweetness and the mocha-spice echoes escargot-butter toppers. Strong opulent Napa Cab for filet — Darioush Persian-inspired story, though leaner Cabs like Jordan peak higher on the delicate cut.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|French Onion": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's bold coffee-mocha cassis sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the coffee meets the caramel. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Grilled Caesar": "Darioush — Silverado Trail Cab with blackcurrant, dark plum, mocha, spice. The opulent body meets anchovy-parmesan dressing and the mocha-spice plays against grilled-romaine char. Works as opulent Napa Cab for grilled Caesar — Persian-inspired estate story on the classic layered salad.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Gumbo": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overwhelms the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth crowds the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- the side needs a crisper register to carry it cleanly. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|House Wedge": "Darioush — Silverado Trail Cab, blackcurrant, dark plum, mocha, spice. The opulent body cuts iceberg-and-bacon and the mocha-spice plays against blue cheese dressing. Works as opulent Napa Cab for the wedge — Persian-inspired estate story red, though whites peak higher for the classic wedge.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Kansas City": "Darioush — Silverado Trail Cab with blackcurrant, dark plum, mocha, spice, rich plush. The opulent body meets Kansas City's lean-bold marbled strip and the mocha-spice plays against the beefy char. Peak opulent Napa Cab for Kansas City — Persian-inspired estate story on the classic strip. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Loaded Potato": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's bold coffee-mocha cassis stays alongside the loaded potato's richness — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Lobster Mac": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's bold coffee-mocha cassis stays alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Market Fish": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Mocha Creme": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Mushroom Bisque": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's bold coffee-mocha cassis holds with the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Mushrooms": "Silverado Trail Cab — blackcurrant, dark plum, mocha, spice, rich plush. The opulent body meshes with mushroom umami and the mocha-spice frames the sauté earth. Strong opulent Napa Cab for mushrooms — Darioush Persian-inspired story plus plush concentration on the earthy side.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Porterhouse": "Darioush — Silverado Trail Cab, blackcurrant, dark plum, mocha, spice, rich plush. The opulent body frames Porterhouse's dual-texture strip-and-filet and the mocha-spice plays against both lean and fatty sides. Strong opulent Napa Cab for Porterhouse — Persian-inspired estate story on the dual-cut classic.",
