  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Pour the Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- tannin on raw green vegetable reads astringent without payoff. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Seafood Tower": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon|Seared Scallops": "Darioush Silverado Trail Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — plush mocha-spice obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save Darioush for the steak course where its Persian-inspired character peaks.",
