  "Detroit City Gin|Asparagus": "Detroit City Gin's bold char-juniper botanicals plays cleanly against the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the spice lifts the green plate. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Detroit City Gin|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Detroit City Gin's bold char-juniper botanicals stays alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Detroit City Gin|Beignets": "Detroit City Gin's Detroit urban-craft gin clashes with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a gin. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Detroit City Gin for the steak course.",
  "Detroit City Gin|Bone Marrow": "Detroit City Gin with bone marrow — Detroit juniper against umami fat. Avoid; gin can't cut marrow. Reach for Fernet Branca.",
