  "Detroit City Gin|House Wedge": "Detroit City Gin with the House Wedge — Detroit urban craft against iceberg and bleu. Excellent; Detroit City threads the wedge with hometown pride.",
  "Detroit City Gin|Kansas City": "Detroit City Gin's Detroit urban-craft gin underclubs the KC's lean-bold strip with savory grain -- gin reads light against the prime cut's weight — needs a red or whiskey. The plate deserves Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, Pio Cesare Barbaresco, or Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye, not a gin. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Detroit City Gin on another course instead.",
  "Detroit City Gin|Loaded Potato": "Detroit City Gin's bold char-juniper botanicals sits beside the loaded potato's richness — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Detroit City Gin|Lobster Mac": "Detroit City Gin's bold char-juniper botanicals sits beside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the juniper carries the shellfish. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Detroit City Gin|Market Fish": "Detroit City Gin -- Detroit Distillery, hometown craft, urban juniper. The city-distilled juniper frames the market fish, and the local-spirit character meets the plate. Strong; Sapphire's softer character frames the fish without the aggression of flagship London Drys.",
  "Detroit City Gin|Mocha Creme": "Detroit City Gin's Detroit urban-craft gin clashes with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- gin botanicals jar against the chocolate's sweetness with no bridge. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not a gin. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Detroit City Gin for the steak course.",
  "Detroit City Gin|Mushroom Bisque": "Detroit City Gin's bold char-juniper botanicals reads alongside the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Detroit City Gin|Mushrooms": "Detroit City Gin's bold char-juniper botanicals leans against the mushrooms' earthy umami — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the spice frames the umami depth. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Detroit City Gin|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Detroit City Gin's Detroit urban-craft gin clashes with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- gin botanicals jar against the chocolate's sweetness with no bridge. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Detroit City Gin on the steak course instead.",
  "Detroit City Gin|Porterhouse": "Detroit City Gin's Detroit urban-craft gin falls short of the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character -- botanical-citrus can't stand up to 26+ ounces — a Cab or bourbon earns it. The plate deserves Odette Cabernet Sauvignon, Weller 12 Year, or Domaine du Grand Tinel, not a gin. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Detroit City Gin belongs on another course.",
  "Detroit City Gin|Prime Tartare": "Detroit City Gin with the tartare — Detroit City Distillery against raw beef. Strong; Detroit City's juniper supports tartare at hometown register.",
