  "Detroit City Vodka|Bone-In Filet": "Detroit City Vodka's hometown craft vodka mis-pairs with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- clean vodka reads thin against the cut's weight — needs a wine or whiskey. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a vodka. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Detroit City Vodka for another course.",
