  "Dewar's 15|Creme Brulee": "Dewar's 15's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the malt-and-oak threads the brulee, and the oak threads the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Dewar's 15|Escargot": "Dewar's 15's honey-sherry character holds steady against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the caramel-oak depth threads the savory plate, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Dewar's 15|Faroe Island Salmon": "Dewar's 15's 15yr aged Highland blend overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a scotch. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Dewar's 15 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Dewar's 15|Filet Mignon": "Filet Mignon: tenderloin meets aged sherry-finish Highland blend. Dewar's 15's sherry-cask finish layers depth beyond the White Label's honey-vanilla entry — the upgraded Dewar's-filet pairing for guests who know the brand and want the aged expression. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Dewar's 15|French Onion": "Dewar's 15's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the Highland register carries the French onion, and the heather brightens the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Dewar's 15|Grilled Caesar": "Dewar's 15 with the grilled Caesar — aged Highland blend with sherry-finish against charred romaine and anchovy. Excellent; Dewar's 15's aged character meets the char with premium-blend resonance.",
  "Dewar's 15|Gumbo": "Dewar's 15's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the malt-driven body wraps the gumbo, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the bowl. Works; the pour's assertiveness is a bit much for the soup but doesn't clash.",
  "Dewar's 15|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Dewar's 15's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the scotch depth settles into the honey carrots, and the oak frames the caramelized sugar. Works; IW Harper 15 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Dewar's 15|House Wedge": "Dewar's 15 with the House Wedge — sherry-finish Highland blend against iceberg and bleu. Excellent; Dewar's 15's aged + sherry-finish threads the wedge with premium-blend distinction.",
  "Dewar's 15|Kansas City": "Kansas City: strip marbling meets 15yr aged Dewar's with sherry-cask finish, richer than White Label with Highland-blend-premium character. Dewar's 15's aged-with-sherry-finish depth is the upgraded blended-Scotch-KC pairing — where White Label's honey-vanilla handles the strip at entry register, the 15 closes the deal with sherry-cask weight. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Dewar's 15|Loaded Potato": "Dewar's 15's Highland-scotch character leans against the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the malt-driven body wraps the loaded potato soup, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; bold character slightly over-specified for the soup.",
  "Dewar's 15|Lobster Mac": "Dewar's 15's Highland-scotch character leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the lobster mac, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; the pour's delicacy doesn't overpower the soup, but doesn't particularly elevate it either.",
  "Dewar's 15|Market Fish": "Dewar's 15's 15yr aged Highland blend smothers the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a scotch. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Save the Dewar's 15 for the steak course.",
  "Dewar's 15|Mocha Creme": "Dewar's 15's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the mocha creme, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the extra proof overpowers this dish.",
  "Dewar's 15|Mushroom Bisque": "Dewar's 15's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the scotch depth settles into the mushroom bisque, and the oak depth meets the umami. Works; JW Black handles the richness at premium-blend register.",
  "Dewar's 15|Mushrooms": "Dewar's 15 with mushrooms — 15yr aged Highland blend against earthy umami. Excellent; Dewar's 15's sherry-finish dried-fruit and aged depth thread mushroom earthiness with premium-blend character.",
  "Dewar's 15|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Dewar's 15's Highland-scotch character leans against the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the scotch depth settles into the PB brownie, and the heather brightens the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Dewar's 15|Porterhouse": "Dewar's 15 with the porterhouse — aged Highland blend against strip-and-filet. Strong; Dewar's 15 frames the two-cut plate at premium-blend register.",
  "Dewar's 15|Prime Tartare": "Dewar's 15's honey-sherry character finds register with the tartare's raw beef and brine — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; a steady recommendation at the table.",
  "Dewar's 15|Rainbow Trout": "Dewar's 15's 15yr aged Highland blend flattens the trout's delicate flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a scotch. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Dewar's 15 for the steak course.",
  "Dewar's 15|Roast Half Chicken": "Dewar's 15's Highland-scotch character leans against the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the malt-and-oak threads the roast chicken, and the malt edge frames the plate. Works; annual-release covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Dewar's 15|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Dewar's 15's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the malt-and-oak threads the chickpea soup, and the malt edge frames the bowl. Works; complexity wasted on salad.",
