  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Asparagus": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin finds neutral with the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the medium-body red frames the green plate, and the spice lifts the green plate. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin leans against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Beignets": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift jars against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval for the steak course.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Bone Marrow": "Willamette flagship Pinot Blend against pure collagen-fat marrow — silky layered Pinot lacks the tannin needed to cut the render. Never pair. Route marrow to Cabs, Bordeaux, Meritage, or structured bold reds; keep Grand Cheval for the filet, chicken, or seafood course.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Bone-In Filet": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin lifts the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the medium-body red frames the lean cut, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
