  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Broccolini": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin holds with the broccolini's tender green — the medium-body red frames the green plate, and the spice lifts the green plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Brussels and Belly": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin stays alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice lifts the green plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Burrata": "Willamette flagship Pinot Blend — dark cherry, Bing cherry, toasted spice, forest floor, silky soft tannin. The silky tannin meets burrata's creamy-delicate center and the Bing cherry plays against basil-tomato. Works as flagship Willamette Pinot for burrata — Oregon elegance; whites peak higher for the starter.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Butternut Squash": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin leans against the squash soup's silky sweet — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the pairing reads neutral at the table. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Carrot Cake": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- red structure flattens the spice cake's cinnamon-and-cream-cheese delicacy. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval on the steak course instead.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Cheesecake": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift jars against the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- tannin reads astringent next to dairy custard, the custard reads sour back. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval for the steak course.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Chilean Seabass": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift fights the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the red's tannin and the salmon's rich oils refuse to integrate. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval for the steak course.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Chocolate Brownie": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift clashes with the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- savory tannin sits awkwardly on cocoa weight without resolving. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Save the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval for the steak course.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Chocolate Cake": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift clashes with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- savory tannin sits awkwardly on cocoa weight without resolving. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval for the steak course.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Clam Chowder": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; capable alongside. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Cowboy Ribeye": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift leans against the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness: the Pinot body brightens the cap-fat ribeye, and the cherry-and-earth note frames the cut. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Crab Cake": "Willamette flagship Pinot Blend — dark cherry, Bing cherry, toasted spice, forest floor, silky soft tannin. The soft tannin doesn't fight crab's sweet meat and the forest-floor plays against romesco. Strong flagship Willamette Pinot for crab cake — layered Oregon red on shellfish.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Creamed Spinach": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin holds with the spinach's dairy-rich cream — the medium-body red frames the green plate, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Creamy Potato": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin reads alongside the potato soup's silky body — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Creme Brulee": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift jars against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- tannin reads astringent next to dairy custard, the custard reads sour back. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval for the steak course.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Escargot": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin holds the line with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the medium-body red meets the savory plate, and the spice frames the umami depth. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Faroe Island Salmon": "Willamette flagship Pinot Blend — dark cherry, Bing cherry, toasted spice, forest floor, silky layered. The layered structure plays against salmon's oil-rich flesh; preparation changes seasonally — check with kitchen for today's build. Peak flagship Willamette Pinot for salmon across most seasonal preparations. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Filet Mignon": "Willamette flagship Pinot Blend — Dundee & Eola-Amity, dark cherry, Bing cherry, toasted spice, forest floor, silky, layered finish. The silky layered body meets butter-tender filet's lean sweetness and the forest-floor echoes escargot-butter. Peak flagship Willamette Pinot for filet — Domaine Serene elegance. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|French Onion": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin reads alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the medium-body red frames the hearty soup, and the rye spice cuts the cheese richness. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Grilled Caesar": "Willamette flagship Pinot Blend — dark cherry, Bing cherry, toasted spice, forest floor, silky. The acid cuts anchovy-parmesan dressing and the toasted-spice plays against grilled-romaine char. Strong flagship Willamette Pinot for grilled Caesar — Domaine Serene layering on the salad.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Gumbo": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin leans against the gumbo's spiced Creole stew — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the spice frames the umami depth. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin reads alongside the carrots' honeyed sweetness — the medium-body red frames the green plate, and the spice lifts the green plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|House Wedge": "Willamette flagship Pinot Blend — dark cherry, Bing cherry, toasted spice, forest floor, silky. The acid cuts iceberg-and-bacon and the toasted-spice plays against blue cheese dressing. Peak flagship Willamette Pinot for the wedge — Domaine Serene elegance reframes the salad. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Kansas City": "Willamette flagship Pinot Blend — dark cherry, Bing cherry, toasted spice, forest floor, silky, medium body. The layered body works against Kansas City's lean-bold strip though low tannin falls short of bolder Cabs. Works as flagship Willamette Pinot for the strip — Domaine Serene elegance for Pinot-preferring guest.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Loaded Potato": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin sits alongside the loaded potato's richness — the medium-body red frames the hearty soup, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Lobster Mac": "Willamette flagship Pinot Blend — dark cherry, Bing cherry, toasted spice, forest floor, silky. The acid cuts lobster-mac's cream-cheese richness and the toasted-spice plays against the dense pasta. Works as flagship Willamette Pinot for the lobster mac side — Oregon layering; accessible Chard peaks higher.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Market Fish": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift clashes with the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval on the steak course instead.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Mocha Creme": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift jars against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Domaine Serene Grand Cheval belongs on the steak course.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Mushroom Bisque": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin sits beside the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the medium-body red frames the hearty soup, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Mushrooms": "Willamette flagship Pinot Blend — dark cherry, Bing cherry, toasted spice, forest floor, silky. The forest-floor echoes roasted-mushroom glutamate and the Bing cherry plays against the earth depth. Strong flagship Willamette Pinot for mushrooms — elevated Pinot-and-mushroom terroir pairing.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift fights the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- the dry red and the chocolate's sugar refuse each other — tannin reads bitter on the finish. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval for the steak course.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Porterhouse": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin frames the porterhouse's two-cut character — the medium-body red meets the cap-fat at lighter register. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Prime Tartare": "Willamette flagship Pinot Blend — dark cherry, Bing cherry, toasted spice, forest floor, silky, low tannin. The soft tannin leaves room for raw-beef delicacy and the forest-floor plays against egg yolk and capers. Strong flagship Willamette Pinot for tartare — layered Oregon on the raw-beef classic.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Rainbow Trout": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval for the steak course.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Roast Half Chicken": "Willamette flagship Pinot Blend — dark cherry, Bing cherry, toasted spice, forest floor, silky. The toasted-spice plays against roasted chicken's skin-and-jus build; preparation changes seasonally — check with kitchen for today's build. Peak flagship Willamette Pinot for chicken across most seasonal builds. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift sits alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the Pinot body brightens the chickpea soup, and the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the red's structure is wrong for delicate flesh — built for red meat. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval on the steak course instead.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin leans against the garlic-spinach's buttered greens — the medium-body red frames the green plate, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Seafood Tower": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval on the steak course instead.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Seared Scallops": "Willamette flagship Pinot Blend — dark cherry, Bing cherry, toasted spice, forest floor, silky soft tannin. The silky tannin leaves room for scallop sweetness and the toasted-spice plays against caramelized-exterior char. Peak flagship Willamette Pinot for scallops — layered elegance on delicate shellfish. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Seasonal Soup": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin sits alongside the seasonal soup's house build — the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Seasonal Vegetables": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift finds neutral with the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the Pinot body brightens the seasonal vegetables, and the cherry-and-earth note frames the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Shrimp Bisque": "Willamette flagship Pinot Blend — dark cherry, Bing cherry, toasted spice, forest floor, silky. The acid cuts bisque's cream weight and the forest-floor plays against shellfish umami and sherry. Strong flagship Willamette Pinot for shrimp bisque — layered Oregon against the rich soup.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Shrimp Cocktail": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift crowds out the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval for the steak course.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Swordfish": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- tannin against rare-seared crust reads astringent without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval for the steak course.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|The Tomahawk": "Willamette flagship Pinot Blend against Tomahawk's massive bone-in ribeye — silky low-tannin Pinot has no grip for the cut's fat-and-char. Never pair. Route Tomahawk to Napa Cabs, Bordeaux, Meritage, or bold Italian reds; keep Grand Cheval for the salmon, chicken, or seafood course.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Tomato Basil": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin plays cleanly against the tomato basil's bright acid — the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Truffle Fries": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin sits beside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice frames the umami depth. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift overshadows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- dark-fruit weight crowds the seared sesame crust — needs a sparkling or crisp white for lift. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval for the steak course.",
  "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin sits beside the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; safe call, no friction. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Asparagus": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's bold earth-mineral cassis stays alongside the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Provence Bandol AOC Mourvèdre blend — Tempier, dark plum, game, olive, wild herbs, smoky mineral, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts gruyere-cream richness but the cult-producer complexity is spent on a dairy side. Works for au gratin — Muga's vanilla-leather fits the cheese harder.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Beignets": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- tannin can't pivot to warm pastry sugar — the pour reads dry, the dessert reads heavy. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Domaine Tempier Bandol on the steak course instead.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Bone Marrow": "Bone Marrow: this rich, umami-forward starter's bold fat and concentrated savory depth meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's tannin scrubs the starter's fat while dark fruit picks up the umami notes. An excellent opening pour — weight and fruit both land. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Bone-In Filet": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's bold earth-mineral cassis sits with the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the velvety body lifts the lean cut, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Broccoli Cheddar": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's bold earth-mineral cassis sits beside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the smoke meets the umami depth. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Broccolini": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's bold earth-mineral cassis reads alongside the broccolini's tender green — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; the pairing reads neutral at the table. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Burrata": "Never pair Tempier with burrata — game, olive, and smoky mineral clash with fresh cream and the full-body firm tannin buries tomato-basil brightness. Lead with Santa Margherita Pinot Grigio's clean lift or a Rosé's strawberry-to-tomato-sweetness bridge.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Butternut Squash": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's bold earth-mineral cassis sits beside the squash soup's silky sweet — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the mineral edge cuts the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Carrot Cake": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Domaine Tempier Bandol on the steak course instead.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Cheesecake": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register jars against the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Domaine Tempier Bandol for the steak course.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Chilean Seabass": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register fights the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the red's tannin and the salmon's rich oils refuse to integrate. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Domaine Tempier Bandol lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Chocolate Brownie": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register jars against the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Domaine Tempier Bandol on the steak course instead.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Chocolate Cake": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register jars against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Domaine Tempier Bandol for the steak course.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Clam Chowder": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's bold earth-mineral cassis sits beside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the smoke wraps the briny shellfish. Works; safe call, no friction. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Cowboy Ribeye": "Provence Bandol AOC Mourvèdre blend — Tempier, dark plum, game, olive, wild herbs, smoky mineral, full body, firm tannin. The firm tannin slices Cowboy's marbled 26oz bone-in and the smoky mineral echoes grilled char. Peak cult-Bandol for ribeye — exceptional with Cowboy per the card's own call-out. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Crab Cake": "Never pair Tempier with crab cake — game, olive, and smoky mineral bury delicate lump crab and firm tannin fights the romesco. Lead with Heitz Sauvignon Blanc's citrus lift or Reverdy Sancerre's mineral edge for shellfish clarity.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Creamed Spinach": "Creamed Spinach: the structured red's grip carries the rich side's dairy load; oak-driven body absorbs the cream and tannin clears the finish. A capable pair; richness aligns if not perfectly. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Creamy Potato": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's bold earth-mineral cassis sits beside the potato soup's silky body — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the mineral edge cuts the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Creme Brulee": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register jars against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- tannin reads astringent next to dairy custard, the custard reads sour back. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Domaine Tempier Bandol on the steak course instead.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Escargot": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's bold earth-mineral cassis holds steady against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the Cab structure meets the savory depth. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Faroe Island Salmon": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register fights the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the red's tannin and the salmon's rich oils refuse to integrate. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Domaine Tempier Bandol lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Filet Mignon": "Provence Bandol AOC Mourvèdre blend — Tempier, dark plum, game, olive, wild herbs, smoky mineral, full body, firm tannin. The firm tannin meets butter-tender filet's delicate sweetness and the olive plays with escargot-butter. Strong cult-Bandol for filet — full body is bold but structure threads the needle.",
