  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Seafood Tower": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Domaine Tempier Bandol lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Seared Scallops": "Never pair Tempier with seared scallops — game and smoky mineral overwhelm delicate sweet shellfish and firm tannin fights browned-butter sweetness. Lead with Clos de la Chapelle Chardonnay or Rombauer's creamy richness for sear-seared harmony.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Seasonal Soup": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's dense blackberry-and-cassis tannin reads alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the structured body wraps the seasonal soup, and the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; the dessert sits cleanly against the meal's register.",
  "Domaine Tempier Bandol|Seasonal Vegetables": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's bold earth-mineral cassis reads alongside the seasonal garden plate — the opulent body overshoots the light side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
