  "Don Julio 1942|Clam Chowder": "Don Julio 1942's icon extra-añejo character sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the oak-aged tequila body threads the chowder, and the caramel-agave register brightens the bowl. Works; wheated-soft character handles richness at gentler-Expresiones register.",
  "Don Julio 1942|Cowboy Ribeye": "Don Julio 1942 with the Cowboy Ribeye — 1942 against cap fat. Strong; iconic extra añejo covers the ribeye with benchmark character.",
  "Don Julio 1942|Crab Cake": "Don Julio 1942's icon extra-añejo character overwhelms the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- añejo weight has no foil against cold shellfish — needs sparkling or crisp white. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Don Julio 1942 for the steak course.",
