  "Elephant Gin|Asparagus": "Elephant Gin's crisp char-herbal botanicals sits beside the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Elephant Gin|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Elephant Gin's crisp char-herbal botanicals sits alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Elephant Gin|Beignets": "Elephant Gin with beignets — African-botanical gin against fried dough. Works; the herbal-wormwood profile contrasts sugar at contemporary register.",
  "Elephant Gin|Bone Marrow": "Elephant Gin with bone marrow — African-botanical gin against umami fat. Avoid; gin can't cut marrow. Reach for Fernet Branca.",
  "Elephant Gin|Bone-In Filet": "Elephant Gin's botanical-driven lift mis-pairs with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- gin's clean lift reads thin against the cut's weight. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a gin. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Elephant Gin lands on another course — not here.",
  "Elephant Gin|Broccoli Cheddar": "Elephant Gin's crisp char-herbal botanicals plays cleanly against the broccoli cheddar's cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Elephant Gin|Broccolini": "Elephant Gin's crisp char-herbal botanicals reads alongside the broccolini's tender green — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Elephant Gin|Brussels and Belly": "Elephant Gin's crisp char-herbal botanicals plays cleanly against the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs frame the grilled char. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Elephant Gin|Burrata": "Elephant Gin with burrata — African craft gin against fresh dairy. Excellent; the baobab and lion's tail botanicals complement cream with distinctive contemporary character — distinct from Plymouth's sweetness or Nolet's rose-peach approach.",
  "Elephant Gin|Butternut Squash": "Elephant Gin's crisp char-herbal botanicals reads alongside the squash soup's silky sweet — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Elephant Gin|Carrot Cake": "Elephant Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- juniper-citrus and warm cake spices pull in opposite directions. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Elephant Gin belongs on the steak course.",
  "Elephant Gin|Cheesecake": "Elephant Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not a gin. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Elephant Gin lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Elephant Gin|Chilean Seabass": "Elephant Gin's herbal-botanical edge sits alongside the seabass' buttery seabass flesh: the floral edge frames the seabass, and the juniper threads the plate. Strong; Elephant's contemporary botanicals engage the bleu with distinctive character.",
  "Elephant Gin|Chocolate Brownie": "Elephant Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- gin botanicals jar against the chocolate's sweetness with no bridge. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not a gin. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Elephant Gin for the steak course.",
  "Elephant Gin|Chocolate Cake": "Elephant Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not a gin. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Elephant Gin belongs on the steak course.",
  "Elephant Gin|Clam Chowder": "Elephant Gin's crisp char-herbal botanicals reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals lift the shellfish. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Elephant Gin|Cowboy Ribeye": "Elephant Gin's botanical-driven lift underclubs the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness -- gin reads light against the prime cut's weight — needs a red or whiskey. The plate deserves Macallan 18, Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon, or Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon, not a gin. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Elephant Gin for another course.",
  "Elephant Gin|Crab Cake": "Elephant Gin with crab cake — German craft distillery, African botanicals (baobab, buchu, lion's tail, devil's claw, African wormwood). Excellent; Elephant's distinctive African-botanical profile frames delicate crab with a story no London Dry tells — the conservation-charity gin with distinctive character, a conversation-starter pairing.",
  "Elephant Gin|Creamed Spinach": "Elephant Gin's crisp char-herbal botanicals sits alongside the spinach's dairy-rich cream — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
