  "Elephant Gin|Creme Brulee": "Elephant Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not a gin. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Elephant Gin on the steak course instead.",
  "Elephant Gin|Escargot": "Elephant Gin with escargot — African-botanical gin against garlic-butter snails. Excellent; the savanna-herbal profile (wormwood, devil's claw) cuts butter with a different character than Tanqueray's juniper proof-cut.",
  "Elephant Gin|Faroe Island Salmon": "Elephant Gin with the salmon — German-distilled African-botanical gin against oily salmon. Strong; Elephant's distinctive profile frames the fish at contemporary register.",
