  "Elephant Gin|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Elephant Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- gin botanicals jar against the chocolate's sweetness with no bridge. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Elephant Gin belongs on the steak course.",
  "Elephant Gin|Porterhouse": "Elephant Gin's botanical-driven lift falls short of the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character -- botanical-citrus can't stand up to 26+ ounces — a Cab or bourbon earns it. The plate deserves Odette Cabernet Sauvignon, Weller 12 Year, or Domaine du Grand Tinel, not a gin. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Elephant Gin on another course instead.",
  "Elephant Gin|Prime Tartare": "Elephant Gin with the tartare — German craft African-botanical gin against raw beef. Strong; Elephant's distinctive herbal profile supports tartare; Bombay Dry's angular juniper is still the featured gin-tartare match.",
  "Elephant Gin|Rainbow Trout": "Elephant Gin's botanical-driven lift meets at register with the trout's delicate flesh: the bright botanical edge handles the trout, and the coriander-and-cardamom edge frames the plate. Strong; Elephant Gin on the trout -- workhorse pairing, no surprises.",
