  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Bone Marrow": "Elijah Craig 18 with bone marrow — aged HH single-barrel against umami fat. Excellent; EC 18's 18yr depth engages marrow at aged-premium register.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Bone-In Filet": "Elijah Craig 18 with the bone-in filet — HH aged single-barrel against tenderloin-with-bone. Excellent; EC 18's 18yr character frames the cut with aged-HH polish.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Broccoli Cheddar": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the brown-spirit warmth threads the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; bonded weight a touch ambitious for the dessert.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Broccolini": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the broccolini's tender green stalks: the bourbon depth settles into the broccolini, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; richer profile overshoots the dessert's delicacy.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Brussels and Belly": "Elijah Craig 18 with Brussels + Belly — 18yr HH single-barrel against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; EC 18's aged character meets the glaze at aged-HH register.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Burrata": "Elijah Craig 18 with burrata — HH 18yr against fresh dairy. Avoid; bourbon weight wrong for burrata.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Butternut Squash": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bourbon weight handles the squash bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; premium KO story wasted on salad.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Carrot Cake": "Elijah Craig 18 with carrot cake — HH 18yr against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; EC 18's aged dried-fruit threads the cake at aged-HH register.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Cheesecake": "Elijah Craig 18 with cheesecake — aged HH single-barrel against custard. Works; EC 18's aged character threads the cheesecake at aged-HH register.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Chilean Seabass": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon weight needs red meat, not the salmon's already-rich oils. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Elijah Craig 18 Year for the steak course.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Chocolate Brownie": "Elijah Craig 18 with the chocolate brownie — 18yr HH single-barrel against cocoa. Strong; EC 18's leather-tobacco character meets cocoa at aged-premium register.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Chocolate Cake": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Clam Chowder": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon depth settles into the chowder, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Cowboy Ribeye": "Elijah Craig 18 with the cowboy ribeye — 18yr HH single-barrel against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Strong; EC 18 frames the ribeye at aged-HH register. Gold standard; the recommendation that earns the regular.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Crab Cake": "Elijah Craig 18 with crab cake — HH 18yr against delicate lump crab. Avoid; bourbon wrong for seafood. Reach for a vodka or gin.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Creamed Spinach": "Elijah Craig 18 with creamed spinach — HH aged single-barrel against dairy-rich side. Strong; EC 18's aged character rides the cream at aged-HH register.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Creamy Potato": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the bourbon weight handles the potato soup, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; Fortuna handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Creme Brulee": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the bourbon depth settles into the brulee, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; cleaner than wheated versions but not exceptional.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Escargot": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight sits alongside the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the bourbon backbone carries the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; reliable match across the courses; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Faroe Island Salmon": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Elijah Craig 18 Year for the steak course.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Filet Mignon": "Elijah Craig 18 with the filet — Heaven Hill aged single-barrel, 18-year premium with distinctive aged HH character (leather, tobacco, dried fruit). Excellent; EC 18's refined 18yr depth frames tenderloin with aged-HH-single-barrel gravitas — the polished sibling to Elijah Craig Small Batch at collector register.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|French Onion": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the bourbon body sits with the French onion, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; save the bottle for the protein course — a soup is wrong for a $200 pour.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Grilled Caesar": "Elijah Craig 18 with the grilled Caesar — 18yr HH single-barrel against charred romaine and anchovy. Works; EC 18 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Gumbo": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the bourbon backbone carries the gumbo, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the bourbon depth settles into the honey carrots, and the oak balances the burnt-sugar edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|House Wedge": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth leans against the wedge's iceberg-and-bleu cool crunch: the brown-spirit warmth threads the wedge, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; collector-bottle depth gives ultra-premium character.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Kansas City": "Elijah Craig 18 with the KC — HH 18yr single-barrel against an 18oz strip. Strong; EC 18 handles the strip at aged-HH register; HH 20yr is the aged-HH-KC upgrade.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Loaded Potato": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the brown-spirit warmth threads the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; save the collector bottle for the protein course.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Lobster Mac": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the brown-spirit warmth threads the lobster mac, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; gentle composed match.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Market Fish": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Elijah Craig 18 Year belongs on the steak course.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Mocha Creme": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the mocha creme, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; distinctive character is worth mentioning tableside, even if the pairing isn't marquee.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Mushroom Bisque": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the bourbon depth settles into the mushroom bisque, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the cream. Works; fruit-forward at matched register.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Mushrooms": "Elijah Craig 18 with mushrooms — aged HH single-barrel against earthy umami. Excellent; EC 18's 18yr leather-tobacco notes thread mushroom earthiness at aged-HH register.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Peanut Butter Brownie: peanut butter and cocoa meet HH 18yr. Works; EC 18 handles dessert density at aged-HH register.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Porterhouse": "Elijah Craig 18 with the porterhouse — HH 18yr against strip-and-filet. Works; EC 18 frames the two-cut plate at aged-HH register.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Prime Tartare": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's bold single-barrel-oak character finds register with the tartare's raw beef and brine — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Rainbow Trout": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Elijah Craig 18 Year on the steak course instead.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Roast Half Chicken": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the oak depth lays under the roast chicken, and the oak frames the plate. Works; craft-blend covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the caramel-spice register matches the chickpea soup, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; distinctive character doesn't drive.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Elijah Craig 18 Year for the steak course.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the bourbon body sits with the garlic spinach, and the oak frames the side. Works; extended maturation gives the dessert home-state aged character.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Seafood Tower": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Elijah Craig 18 Year belongs on the steak course.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Seared Scallops": "Elijah Craig 18 with seared scallops — aged HH against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Seasonal Soup": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the bourbon body sits with the seasonal soup, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; polished aged character doesn't drive.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Seasonal Vegetables": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the bourbon backbone carries the seasonal vegetables, and the oak-and-spice register settles the side. Works; smooth character is slightly over-specified for this dish.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Shrimp Bisque": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the unique maturation story adds interest to a gentle dessert match.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Shrimp Cocktail": "Elijah Craig 18 with shrimp cocktail — aged HH single-barrel against cold shrimp. Avoid; bourbon wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Swordfish": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon's sweet weight crowds the rare crust's clean char. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Elijah Craig 18 Year for the steak course.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|The Tomahawk": "Elijah Craig 18 with the Tomahawk — HH aged single-barrel against 32oz cap-fat. Works; EC 18's aged character is under-specified for Tomahawk intensity; reach for a barrel-proof bourbon.",
  "Elijah Craig 18 Year|Tomato Basil": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the bourbon depth settles into the tomato basil, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; distinctive character doesn't drive but adds interest.",
