  "Elk Cove Five Mountain|Faroe Island Salmon": "Faroe Island Salmon: this rich, fatty seafood's buttery flesh and delicate-yet-substantial texture meets this elegant red's cherry-bright, silky-tannin frame. The elegant red's cherry-bright, low-tannin frame threads cleanly through the fish — classic Burgundy logic. A headliner fish pair. Gold standard; the headline call at the table.",
  "Elk Cove Five Mountain|Filet Mignon": "Chehalem Mountains Willamette Pinot — five-AVA blend, cherry, violet, clove, structured age-worthy backbone, medium tannin. The structure meets butter-tender filet's lean sweetness and the violet-clove plays against escargot-butter. Peak step-up Willamette Pinot for filet — serious Oregon red on the delicate cut. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
