  "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc|Kansas City": "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc's crisp white-wine character underclubs the KC's lean-bold strip with savory grain -- white wine reads light against the cut's weight — a Pinot or Cab would carry it. The plate deserves Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, Pio Cesare Barbaresco, or Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye, not a white wine. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Elk Cove Pinot Blanc for another course.",
