  "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc|Lobster Mac": "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc: this crisp white's citrus-driven acidity and mineral edge meets this rich, creamy side's dairy-driven indulgence. Crisp white acidity cuts dairy richness — palate-cleansing counterpoint. Strong — the acid refreshes the fat.",
  "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc|Market Fish": "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc: this crisp white's citrus-driven acidity and mineral edge meets this delicate seafood's mild, flaky flesh. Crisp acidity and mineral edge mirror fish's own brininess — clean, classic alignment. Strong — textbook match.",
  "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc|Mocha Creme": "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc's crisp white-wine character falls short of the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- dry white can't carry chocolate's weight — needs a tawny or sweet wine for the close. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not a white wine. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Elk Cove Pinot Blanc for the steak course.",
