  "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc|Mushrooms": "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc's apple-char acidity plays cleanly against the mushrooms' earthy umami — the crisp acidity sits with the plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc's crisp white-wine character clashes with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- a dry white belongs with the main course, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not a white wine. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Elk Cove Pinot Blanc on the steak course instead.",
  "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc|Porterhouse": "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc's crisp white-wine character falls short of the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character -- crisp white reads thin against 26+ ounces of cap-fat ribeye. The plate deserves Odette Cabernet Sauvignon, Weller 12 Year, or Domaine du Grand Tinel, not a white wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Elk Cove Pinot Blanc lands on another course — not here.",
  "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc|Prime Tartare": "Willamette Pinot Blanc — soft pear, white peach, floral, medium body. The refreshing acid cuts raw prime beef's iron richness and the pear-peach fruit plays against the seasoned tartare. Strong medium-body white for tartare — unconventional choice that works without weighing down.",
  "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc|Rainbow Trout": "Willamette Pinot Blanc — delicate Oregon white, stone-fruit, crisp. The crisp acid lifts trout's delicate flaky flesh and the stone-fruit plays against the clean freshwater character. Peak Pinot Blanc for rainbow trout — Oregon white on the delicate classic. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
