  "Escargot|Bombay Dry Gin": "Bombay Dry with escargot — angular 8-botanical against garlic-butter snails. Excellent; Bombay Dry's juniper cuts butter with purity the softer siblings don't match.",
  "Escargot|Bombay Sapphire Gin": "Bombay Sapphire with escargot — floral-softer gin against garlic-butter snails. Excellent; the cubeb-pepper notes cut through butter while the floral botanicals complement it — a distinctive escargot pairing vs Tanq's proof-cutting approach.",
  "Escargot|Bone-In Filet": "The bone-in filet after the escargot -- the herb-butter snail plate opens with garlic-and-parsley lift, the 14oz bone-deepened cut meeting it with a richer butter that the herbs cut through. Strong; the snail opener primes the marrow cut.",
  "Escargot|Booker's": "Booker's cask-strength caramel-juniper character frames the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon depth cuts the umami fat, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Escargot|Botanist Gin": "Botanist with escargot — 22 foraged Islay botanicals against garlic-butter snails. Excellent; the wildcrafted herbal lift cuts butter with distinctive Hebridean character — a different depth than the French/British traditional approaches.",
  "Escargot|Bowdie's Old Fashioned": "Bowdie's Old Fashioned: this bold whiskey-forward cocktail's oak, spice, and spirit depth meets this rich, umami-forward starter's bold fat and concentrated savory depth. Whiskey depth meets the starter's fat and umami — both land heavy. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Escargot|Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark": "Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark's char-oak character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the caramel-oak depth threads the savory plate, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
