  "Escargot|Bruichladdich": "Bruichladdich's crisp char-citrus character holds the line with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the smoke meets the umami depth. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Escargot|Buffalo Trace": "Buffalo Trace's caramel-workhorse character frames the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon weight grips the savory plate, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Escargot|Buffalo Trace Cream": "Buffalo Trace Cream's sweet liqueur character clashes with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- sweet liqueur is dessert energy — wrong place for the table's first course. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a digestif. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Buffalo Trace Cream for the steak course.",
  "Escargot|Bulleit Bourbon": "Bulleit Bourbon's bold spice-vanilla character holds the line with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
