  "Escargot|Cade Cabernet Sauvignon": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon -- Howell Mountain Cab, cassis, mountain tannin. The Howell-Mountain Cab tannin frames the buttered escargot, and the cassis grips the starter. Strong; reliable opener for the cut.",
  "Escargot|Camarena Tequila": "Camarena Tequila's crisp character holds steady against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the añejo depth cuts the umami fat. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|Campari": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook doubles down on the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- aperitivo herbs and a herb-bright opener compound the bitter register — no contrast. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Escargot|Canadian Club": "Canadian Club's workhorse Canadian blend finds neutral with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the easygoing Canadian character handles the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Works; the pour's brightness is a gentle counterpoint to the dessert's richness; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|Canadian Club 43 Year": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character reads alongside the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the Canadian whisky weight matches the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Works; Vermont-brand at matched register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|Captain Morgan Rum": "Captain Morgan Rum's light-rum register with cane and citrus lift mis-pairs with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- this light spirit's register is wrong for the starter — try a different pour. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a light spirit. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Captain Morgan Rum belongs on the steak course.",
  "Escargot|Caribou Crossing": "Caribou Crossing's Canadian whisky character sits alongside the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the Canadian whisky weight matches the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Works; multi-distillery complexity doesn't drive; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
