  "Escargot|Casa LBV Port": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a dessert wine. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Escargot|Casamigos Mezcal": "Casamigos Mezcal's bold agave-soft-smoke character finds register with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the agave smoke cuts the umami fat, and the smoke meets the umami depth. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon": "Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon: this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight meets this rich, umami-forward starter's bold fat and concentrated savory depth. The bold red's tannin scrubs the starter's fat while dark fruit picks up the umami notes. Not the sharpest pairing. Avoid; the call reads off-register; recommend an alternative.",
  "Escargot|Chambord": "Chambord's sweet liqueur character buries the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- sweet liqueur smothers the herb-bright opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a digestif. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Chambord on the steak course instead.",
  "Escargot|Cheesecake": "The escargot and the cheesecake -- the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight bookends with the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
