  "Escargot|Crown Royal": "Crown Royal's classic Canadian blend smoothness leans against the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the blended whisky body wraps the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Escargot|Cucumber Gimlet": "Hendrick's gin, cucumber, lime, ginger syrup, soda top. The fresh cucumber-and-lime structure cuts garlic-butter escargot cleanly and ginger adds aromatic warmth against the snails' earth. Strong opener cocktail when guest wants something garden-fresh before heavier starters.",
  "Escargot|Dalmore 12": "Dalmore 12's crisp chocolate-citrus character sits with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the caramel-oak depth threads the savory plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge": "Sancerre Rouge — Loire red Pinot, raspberry, chalk, dried herbs, light body, high acid. The chalk-minerality cuts escargot's garlic-parsley butter and the dried-herbs echo the Burgundy-classic preparation. Peak Loire red for escargot — French Pinot on the French classic. Gold standard; pour without second-guessing.",
  "Escargot|Darioush Cabernet Franc": "Darioush Cabernet Franc's cherry-floral tannin holds steady against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the medium-body red meets the savory plate, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
