  "Escargot|Drambuie": "Escargot: garlic-herb butter meets Drambuie. Excellent; the spiced-herbal profile of Drambuie engages the garlic-herb butter at scotch-base register — a herbal-spice counterpoint unique to this liqueur.",
  "Escargot|Dunville's Single Malt": "Dunville's Single Malt's crisp char-malt character sits with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|E.H. Taylor Full Proof": "E.H. Taylor Full Proof's cask-strength oak-spice character sits with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon depth cuts the umami fat, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|E.H. Taylor Rye": "E.H. Taylor Rye's rye-spice character sits at register with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the dry rye body wraps the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; the call holds its register at the table against the cut; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|E.H. Taylor Small Batch": "E.H. Taylor Small Batch's caramel-honey character holds the line with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; a steady recommendation at the table.",
  "Escargot|Eagle Rare 10 Year": "Eagle Rare 10 Year's aged-oak character holds steady against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon depth cuts the umami fat, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Escargot|Eastern Kille Dry Gin": "Eastern Kille with escargot — classic London Dry Grand Rapids craft against garlic-butter snails. Excellent; Eastern Kille's juniper-forward classic profile is the featured Local MI Gin-escargot pairing — small-batch family-operated character that cuts butter like the British classics do.",
  "Escargot|El Cabo": "El Cabo's crisp agave-char character lifts the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the añejo depth cuts the umami fat, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Escargot|El Mayor Extra Anejo": "El Mayor Extra Anejo's caramel-oak character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the añejo depth cuts the umami fat, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Escargot|El Mayor Reposado": "El Mayor Reposado -- value 80-proof reposado, agave-forward with light oak. The barrel-rested body handles the buttered escargot, and the oak threads the starter. Strong; agave cuts the dairy at the accessible register.",
  "Escargot|Elephant Gin": "Elephant Gin with escargot — African-botanical gin against garlic-butter snails. Excellent; the savanna-herbal profile (wormwood, devil's claw) cuts butter with a different character than Tanqueray's juniper proof-cut.",
  "Escargot|Elijah Craig 18 Year": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight sits alongside the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the bourbon backbone carries the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; reliable match across the courses; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|Elijah Craig Private Barrel": "Elijah Craig Private Barrel's bold char-oak character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon weight grips the savory plate, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Escargot|Elijah Craig Single Barrel": "Elijah Craig Single Barrel's bold caramel-char character sits with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|Elijah Craig Small Batch": "Elijah Craig Small Batch's caramel-char character holds the line with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Escargot|Elijah Craig Straight Rye": "Elijah Craig Straight Rye's crisp char-spice character holds steady against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon depth cuts the umami fat, and the spice frames the umami depth. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|Elk Cove Five Mountain": "Elk Cove Five Mountain's cherry-clove tannin lifts the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the medium-body red meets the savory plate, and the spice frames the umami depth. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Escargot|Elk Cove Pinot Blanc": "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc — Willamette Oregon with soft pear, white peach, floral lift, refreshing acidity. The medium-body acid cuts escargot's garlic-parsley butter and the pear-peach fruit plays against the snail richness. Peak unoaked white for escargot — fresher than Chard, more body than Sauv Blanc.",
  "Escargot|Elmer T. Lee": "Elmer T. Lee's botanical-honey character holds the line with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|Empress 1908 Gin": "Empress 1908 with escargot — floral-citrus Victoria craft against garlic-butter snails. Works; Empress's rose-profile is over-specified for escargot — Mahón's Mediterranean juniper cuts butter sharper.",
  "Escargot|Epoch Ingenuity": "Epoch Ingenuity's structured dark-fruit weight reads register-aligned with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the powerful body carries the buttered escargot, and the espresso-cocoa note rounds the starter. Strong; reliable opener for the cut.",
  "Escargot|Espresso Martini": "Espresso Martini's roasted-coffee martini richness overshadows the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- whiskey-cocktail register buries the herb-bright opener. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a spirit-forward cocktail. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Espresso Martini for the steak course.",
  "Escargot|Espresso Old Fashioned": "Espresso Old Fashioned's spirit-forward cocktail register overshadows the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- whiskey-cocktail register buries the herb-bright opener. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a spirit-forward cocktail. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Espresso Old Fashioned belongs on the steak course.",
  "Escargot|Evening Land Seven Springs": "Evening Land Seven Springs's cherry-earth tannin lifts the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the medium-body red meets the savory plate. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Escargot|Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon": "Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis lifts the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the firm tannin cuts the rich starter, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Escargot|Far Niente Chardonnay": "Oakville Chardonnay — buttered citrus, toasted hazelnut, crème brûlée, lush velvety. The opulent oak-butter weight cuts escargot's garlic-parsley and the hazelnut plays against the snail's rich texture. Strong special-occasion Chardonnay for escargot — Napa weight on the French classic.",
  "Escargot|Faroe Island Salmon": "Faroe Island Salmon with the escargot as the lead-in -- the rich oily flesh anchors against the butter-bath starter. Strong; the starter sets the table for the salmon.",
  "Escargot|Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi": "Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi's bold herbal-leather cassis holds the line with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the firm tannin cuts the rich starter, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Escargot|Faust Napa Valley Cabernet": "Faust Napa Valley Cabernet's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis holds the line with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the concentrated body grips the savory plate. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Escargot|Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía": "Galicia Ribeira Sacra Mencía — Fento, fresh red cherry, slate minerality, light body, high acid, Burgundian lift. The high acid cuts garlic-butter richness and the slate plays with parsley-herb. Strong Galician-Mencía for escargot — Burgundian sensibility on a French classic.",
  "Escargot|Fernet Branca": "Fernet Branca's nuclear bitter-menthol intensity sits with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bitter herb edge cuts the umami fat. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|Fernet Menta": "Fernet Menta's bitter-herb aperitivo edge leans against the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the herbal cut works the buttered escargot, and the amaro backbone frames the starter. Strong; Branca cuts the glaze's sweetness harder than sipping amari and makes the side read savory.",
  "Escargot|Filet Mignon": "Filet Mignon after the escargot -- the herb-butter snail plate opens with garlic-and-parsley lift, the 10oz tenderloin meeting it with the same butter register, scaled down. Strong; both courses speak the same gentle language.",
  "Escargot|Fireball Whisky": "Fireball Whisky's sweet liqueur character buries the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- sweet liqueur smothers the herb-bright opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a digestif. Avoid; the better calls are above. Fireball Whisky lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Escargot|Fisher Unity Pinot Noir": "Fisher Unity Pinot Noir's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift reads alongside the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the Pinot body brightens the buttered escargot, and the cherry-and-earth note frames the starter. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Escargot|Four Roses Small Batch Select": "Four Roses Small Batch Select's floral-rose character finds register with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon weight grips the savory plate, and the spice frames the umami depth. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|Four Roses Yellow Label": "Four Roses Yellow Label's crisp caramel-floral character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Escargot|Fox & Oden": "Fox & Oden's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the bourbon weight handles the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; the curated single-barrel is capable but single-distillery aged bourbons bring more traditional focused character; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|Fox & Oden Double Oaked": "Fox & Oden Double Oaked's bold caramel-char character frames the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon weight grips the savory plate, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Escargot|Frangelico": "Frangelico's Piedmont hazelnut depth to mocha at after-dinner register buries the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- sweet liqueur smothers the herb-bright opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Frangelico for the steak course.",
  "Escargot|Freemark Abbey Bosché": "Freemark Abbey Bosché's bold juniper-leather cassis frames the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the concentrated body grips the savory plate. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Escargot|French 75": "Inverroche gin shaken with lemon and vanilla syrup, topped with Prosecco. Bubbles and lemon against our escargot butter's garlic weight; the vanilla rounds the edges. Ceremonial cocktail route for a French classic — acid and sparkle do the work. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Escargot|French Onion": "Escargot and the French onion together -- both build on umami, the plate carries weight without contrast. Works; the table opens with both, no clash either way.",
  "Escargot|Frias Block 5": "Frias Block 5's bold herbal-umami cassis finds register with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the opulent body settles into the umami plate, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo": "G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo's powerful blackcurrant body reads register-aligned with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the powerful body carries the buttered escargot, and the cassis frames the starter. Strong; the pairing carries its register cleanly against the cut.",
  "Escargot|G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti": "G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti's peach-and-honey frizzante sweetness mis-pairs with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- this specific sparkling fights the starter — a different brut or rosé would carry it. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a sparkling. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti on the steak course instead.",
  "Escargot|G4 Blanco": "G4 Blanco with escargot — Camarena craft against garlic-butter snails. Strong; agave-forward cuts the garlic-butter with craft distinctiveness.",
  "Escargot|G4 High Proof": "G4 High Proof's cooked-agave-and-oak register sits at register with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the añejo register carries the buttered escargot, and the caramel-agave register brightens the starter. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Escargot|Garavogue Irish Whiskey": "Garavogue Irish Whiskey's crisp char-honey character holds the line with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
