  "Escargot|Glenfiddich 18": "Glenfiddich 18's caramel-cinnamon character lifts the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Escargot|Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's bold almond-apple character holds the line with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Escargot|Glenglassaugh 12": "Glenglassaugh 12's crisp char-honey character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon weight grips the savory plate, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Escargot|Glenlivet 12": "Glenlivet 12 -- entry Speyside, pear, honey. The bourbon-cask pear lifts the buttered escargot, and the honey rounds the starter. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Escargot|Glenmorangie 10": "Glenmorangie 10's crisp Highland-orange-peel character finds register with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon weight grips the savory plate. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Escargot|Glenmorangie 18": "Glenmorangie 18 -- aged Highland, Oloroso finish, dried-fruit depth. The Oloroso-cask depth wraps the buttered escargot, and the aged-Highland weight frames the starter. Strong; multi-distillery complexity sits with richness at craft-blender register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|Graham's 10 Year Tawny": "Graham's 10 Year Tawny's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a dessert wine. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Graham's 10 Year Tawny on the steak course instead.",
  "Escargot|Graham's 20 Year Tawny": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth buries the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- dessert sugar buries the herb-bright opener — wait for dessert. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a dessert wine. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Graham's 20 Year Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Escargot|Graham's 2017 Vintage Port": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port on the steak course instead.",
  "Escargot|Gran Patron Platinum": "Gran Patron Platinum with escargot — ultra-premium Patron against garlic-butter snails. Strong; refined concentrated agave frames the starter.",
  "Escargot|Grand Marnier": "Grand Marnier's sweet liqueur character buries the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- sweet liqueur smothers the herb-bright opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Grand Marnier for the steak course.",
  "Escargot|Gray Whale Gin": "Gray Whale with escargot — Mendocino-kombu California craft against garlic-butter snails. Strong; Gray Whale's kombu-umami cuts butter with thematic-distinct character — more complex than Aviation's soft juniper, less classic than Mahón's Mediterranean.",
  "Escargot|Green Chartreuse": "Escargot: garlic-herb butter and snails meet Green Chartreuse. Excellent; the 130-botanical herbal profile ties directly to the herb butter at Carthusian register — the French digestif on the French classic. Gold standard; pour without second-guessing.",
  "Escargot|Grey Goose Vodka": "Grey Goose with escargot — soft French wheat against garlic-butter snails. Strong; the silkiness sits with butter; Belvedere's pepper still cuts the dish harder.",
  "Escargot|Grilled Caesar": "Escargot and the Caesar together -- savory-on-savory, the table reads dense and earnest. Works; the table opens with both, no clash either way.",
  "Escargot|Gumbo": "Escargot alongside the gumbo -- the courses pull from different keys but share the table cleanly. Works; the openers share the table cleanly, sequence or share.",
  "Escargot|Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet": "Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet's bold earth-umami cassis frames the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the firm tannin cuts the rich starter, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Escargot|HDW 100 Vodka": "HDW 100 with escargot — 100-proof craft vodka against garlic-butter snails. Excellent; HDW 100's extra ABV cuts butter harder than Detroit City or Hangar 1 can — the featured craft-vodka-escargot pairing.",
  "Escargot|Hakushu 12 Year": "Hakushu 12 Year -- Suntory Hakushu, lightly peated, forest. The lightly-peated Hakushu meets the buttered escargot, and the forest-floor frames the starter. Strong; JW Blue's luxury character frames the two-cut plate at collector register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits at register with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the bourbon backbone carries the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; the annual-release complexity is capable but single-distillery premium bourbons bring more focused character; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|Hangar 1 Vodka": "Hangar 1 with escargot — California floral craft against garlic-butter snails. Strong; Hangar 1's grape-component lift meets the butter at craft register; HDW 100's proof cuts it sharper.",
  "Escargot|Head Fake": "Wheatley vodka, limoncello, triple sec, lemon, simple syrup — sugar rim. The bright lemon cuts garlic-butter escargot and limoncello adds aromatic Italian-citrus complexity against the snails. Strong bright cocktail for escargot when guest wants sweet-and-citrus-forward alternative to classic pairings.",
  "Escargot|Heaven Hill 20 Year": "Heaven Hill 20 Year's bold aged-oak character sits with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond": "Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond's bold caramel-rye-spice character lifts the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon depth cuts the umami fat, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; the call lands cleanly.",
  "Escargot|Heaven's Door 10 Year": "Heaven's Door 10 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth leans against the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the bourbon depth settles into the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; GTS frames the two-cut plate at collector register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|Heitz Martha's Vineyard": "Heitz Martha's Vineyard's bold eucalyptus-herbal cassis finds register with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the Cab structure meets the savory depth, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|Heitz Trailside Vineyard": "Heitz Trailside Vineyard's bold cherry-mint cassis plays cleanly against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the Cab structure meets the savory depth, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|Hendricks Flora Adora": "Flora Adora with escargot — lavish-floral Hendrick's against garlic-butter snails. Works; Flora Adora's floral profile is over-specified for escargot.",
  "Escargot|Hendricks Gin": "Hendricks with escargot — perfumed low-juniper gin against garlic-butter snails. Works; Hendrick's signature is over-specified for escargot.",
