  "Escargot|Hennessy Cognac": "Hennessy Cognac's bold cognac-vanilla character holds the line with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the barrel-aged depth cuts the umami fat, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Escargot|Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's bold caramel-spice character finds register with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Escargot|Hibiki Japanese Harmony": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's Japanese-blend-honey character holds steady against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon depth cuts the umami fat, and the rounded sweetness meets the herb butter. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Escargot|Honey Roasted Carrots": "The escargot and the honey carrots -- the sweet register lifts the umami, the contrast holds without crowding. Works; the call holds whether the table sequences them or shares.",
  "Escargot|House Wedge": "The escargot preceded by the wedge -- savory-on-savory, the table reads dense and earnest. Works; safe opening pair, the meal builds without strain.",
  "Escargot|I.W. Harper 15 Year": "I.W. Harper 15 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register rests at register with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the bourbon weight handles the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; aged premium at matched register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|Il Colle Prosecco Superiore": "Veneto Glera — dry Prosecco with white peach, green apple, and crisp citrus finish. The bright acidity cuts escargot's garlic-parsley butter weight and the light effervescence lifts the snail's richness. Strong approachable pour — though Champagne peaks higher for the escargot course.",
