  "Escargot|Jung and Wulff Trinidad": "Jung and Wulff Trinidad's caramel-char character holds the line with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the light body is outpaced by the savory plate, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; the match carries without overshooting.",
  "Escargot|Kahlua": "Kahlua's sweet liqueur character clashes with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- sweet liqueur is dessert energy — wrong place for the table's first course. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a digestif. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Kahlua for the steak course.",
