  "Escargot|Lemon Lavender Gin Martini": "Plymouth gin, lemon, honey lavender syrup, Prosecco float. The honey's sweetness softens garlic-butter escargot and lavender's floral note lifts the snails' earth; Prosecco adds effervescent lift. Peak aromatic pairing for escargot with approachable gin profile.",
  "Escargot|Les Pallières Raciné": "Les Pallières Raciné's bold earth-mineral cassis lifts the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the firm tannin cuts the rich starter, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Escargot|Liberator Gin": "Liberator with escargot — Michigan 100%-grain craft against garlic-butter snails. Works; Liberator meets butter at hometown register; Mahón's Mediterranean juniper and Eastern Kille's classic London Dry cut it harder.",
  "Escargot|Licor 43": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character buries the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- sweet liqueur smothers the herb-bright opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a digestif. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Licor 43 for the steak course.",
  "Escargot|Limoncello": "Limoncello's sweet liqueur character buries the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- sweet liqueur smothers the herb-bright opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a digestif. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Limoncello on the steak course instead.",
  "Escargot|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir: this elegant red's cherry-bright, silky-tannin frame meets this rich, umami-forward starter's bold fat and concentrated savory depth. Elegant red's cherry and silk mirror the starter's register — light-on-light or bright-on-rich depending on the plate. Works cleanly.",
