  "Escargot|Monkey 47 Gin": "Monkey 47 with escargot — 47-botanical Black Forest gin against garlic-butter snails. Excellent; Monkey 47's complex herbal-forest profile cuts butter with Schwarzwald terroir — richer-layered than Botanist's Islay approach.",
  "Escargot|Monkey Shoulder": "Monkey Shoulder -- blended Speyside malts, soft, honey. The blended-malt body sits with the buttered escargot, and the honey rounds the starter. Strong; balance against richness; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|Montenegro Amaro": "Montenegro Amaro's bitter-herb aperitivo edge overwhelms the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- bitter aperitivo flattens the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Montenegro Amaro lands on the steak course — not here.",
