  "Escargot|Muga Reserva": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth sits at register with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the Rioja American-oak register matches the buttered escargot, and the vanilla-leather edge frames the starter. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Escargot|Mushroom Bisque": "The escargot with the mushroom bisque -- the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight meets the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: both build on umami, the plate carries weight without contrast. Works; both opening courses earn their place.",
  "Escargot|Mushrooms": "The escargot and the mushrooms -- savory-on-savory, the table reads dense and earnest. Works; the call holds whether the table sequences them or shares.",
  "Escargot|Myers's Rum": "Myers's Rum's bold molasses-Jamaican character frames the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Escargot|Negroni": "Gin, Contratto vermouth, Campari. The Negroni's bitter-herbal profile cuts garlic-butter escargot and Campari's orange adds aromatic depth against the snails' earth. Peak bitter-cocktail pairing for escargot — sophistication with palate structure.",
  "Escargot|Never Say Die Rye": "Never Say Die Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; aged 100-proof covers both cuts with premium rye character; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|Never Say Die Small Batch": "Never Say Die Small Batch's caramel-vanilla character lifts the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon depth cuts the umami fat, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Escargot|New Holland Beer Barrel Bourbon": "New Holland Beer Barrel Bourbon's juniper-malt character holds steady against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon weight grips the savory plate, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|New York Sour": "New York Sour's spirit-forward cocktail register overshadows the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- whiskey-cocktail register buries the herb-bright opener. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a spirit-forward cocktail. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the New York Sour on the steak course instead.",
  "Escargot|Nickel & Nickel Cabernet": "Nickel & Nickel Cabernet's bold oak cassis frames the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the firm tannin cuts the rich starter, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Escargot|Nolets Dry Gin": "Nolet's with escargot — Turkish rose + peach + raspberry against garlic-butter snails. Strong; Nolet's fruit-floral meets butter with contemporary character, though flagship Tanq's proof cuts sharper.",
  "Escargot|Not a Paper Plane": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build reads alongside the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the cocktail lift refreshes the starter, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the match holds without overshooting. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Escargot|Oban 14": "Oban 14's crisp Highland-sea-salt character finds register with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Escargot|Oban 18": "Oban 18's bold brine-honey character finds register with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon depth cuts the umami fat, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Escargot|Ocho Anejo": "Ocho Anejo's agave-char character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the añejo depth cuts the umami fat, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Escargot|Odette Cabernet Sauvignon": "Odette Cabernet Sauvignon -- Stags Leap Cab, dark fruit, sage, cedar. The structured body wraps the buttered escargot, and the cassis frames the starter. Strong; reliable match across the courses.",
  "Escargot|Old Elk Cigar Cut": "Old Elk Cigar Cut's bold char-chocolate character holds steady against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon depth cuts the umami fat, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Escargot|Old Emmer": "Old Emmer's crisp char-earth character sits with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon weight grips the savory plate. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|Old Fitzgerald 7 Year": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character sits at register with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the bourbon backbone carries the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; distinctive character sits with richness at novelty register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|Old Fitzgerald 9 Year": "Old Fitzgerald 9 Year's aged wheated BIB's mature honey sits alongside the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the bourbon depth settles into the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; PNW regional character sits with richness; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|Old Grand-Dad 16 Year": "Old Grand-Dad 16 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the bourbon backbone carries the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; boutique character covers both cuts; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|Opus One": "Mondavi-Rothschild's $950 prestige Cabernet. Same weight-class problem as Caymus but multiplied — the wine flattens every subtle note in the dish. Never pour on the escargot; reserve for the Tomahawk or Porterhouse. Avoid; the pairing fights at the table — point the guest elsewhere.",
  "Escargot|Our Lady of Guadalupe Acolytes": "Our Lady of Guadalupe Acolytes — Willamette Trappist Chard with pear, butterscotch, oak, rich layered. The rich oak-butterscotch cuts escargot's garlic-parsley butter and the toasted oak plays against the French classic. Strong provenance-forward Chardonnay for escargot — monastery story, French dish, opulent pairing.",
  "Escargot|Pablo Sour": "Pablo Sour's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift mis-pairs with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- this cocktail's register doesn't lift the opener — try a sparkling or crisp white. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a light cocktail. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Reserve the Pablo Sour for the steak course.",
  "Escargot|Paloma": "Paloma's crisp agave-citrus build plays cleanly against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the cocktail lift refreshes the starter, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Escargot|Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's bold allocated-caramel character frames the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; the call lands cleanly.",
  "Escargot|Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads register-aligned with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the brown-spirit warmth threads the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|Patron Anejo": "Patron Anejo's cooked-agave-and-oak register sits alongside the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the barrel-rested body handles the buttered escargot, and the oak threads the starter. Strong; accessible agave cuts the dairy at the entry register.",
  "Escargot|Patron Silver": "Patron Silver with escargot — 80-proof Patron against garlic-butter snails. The clean citrus cuts the garlic-butter at the accessible register. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Escargot|Patron XO Cafe": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- sweet liqueur is dessert energy — wrong place for the table's first course. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Patron XO Cafe belongs on the steak course.",
  "Escargot|Paul Bara Grand Rosé Brut": "Bouzy Grand Cru Pinot Noir grower Champagne — structured with ripe raspberry, red currant, and minerally finish. The Burgundian weight and fine bubbles cut escargot's garlic-parsley butter richness and the red-fruit complements the French classic. Strong serious rosé Champagne for escargot.",
  "Escargot|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Escargot and the PB brownie -- sugar and umami share the table, the contrast carries the meal. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Escargot|Peju Cabernet Sauvignon": "Peju Cabernet Sauvignon's bold char-cherry cassis frames the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the firm tannin cuts the rich starter, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Escargot|Pierre Ferrand Cognac": "Pierre Ferrand Cognac's cognac-orange-peel character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the barrel-aged depth cuts the umami fat. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Escargot|Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut": "Pierre Gimonnet Special Club 2015 — prestige grower Champagne from Côte des Blancs. Citrus zest, toasted brioche, white flowers, creamy texture. The brioche echoes escargot's buttered-bread tradition and the vintage depth frames the garlic-parsley. Peak Champagne for escargot — classical French pairing elevated. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Escargot|Pikesville Rye": "Pikesville Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the dry rye body wraps the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; covers both cuts cleanly; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|Pineau des Charentes": "Cognac-region fortified — Pineau des Charentes in aperitif mode, grape juice plus young Cognac oak-aged, white grape, honey, warm nutty Cognac. The warm nutty Cognac plays with garlic-butter richness and the honey lifts parsley-herb. Strong Pineau for escargot — aperitif mode on the French classic, Cognac-region on Cognac-region.",
  "Escargot|Pio Cesare Barbaresco": "Pio Cesare Barbaresco's bold Nebbiolo-cherry cassis finds register with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the opulent body settles into the umami plate, and the cherry-fruit lifts the herb edge. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Escargot|Plymouth Gin": "Plymouth with escargot — softer English gin against garlic-butter snails. Strong; Plymouth's softness meets the butter, though Tanq's proof cuts it harder and Bombay Dry's juniper contrasts more sharply.",
  "Escargot|Poderi Aldo Conterno Nebbiolo": "Poderi Aldo Conterno Nebbiolo's bold cherry-citrus cassis finds register with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the opulent body settles into the umami plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Escargot|Pommery Cuvée Louise": "2004 Pommery Cuvée Louise — aged 20-year Reims Champagne. Toasted almond, dried apricot, honey, brioche-rich. The aged complexity and brioche echo escargot's buttered-bread French tradition directly; almond adds depth. Peak occasion Champagne for escargot — treat the pairing accordingly. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Escargot|Porterhouse": "Porterhouse after the escargot -- umami plays against the protein, the table earns its depth. Works; the opener sits cleanly before the steak.",
  "Escargot|Quilt Cabernet Sauvignon": "Quilt Cabernet Sauvignon's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis holds steady against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the Cab structure meets the savory depth, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Escargot|RAEN Royal St Robert": "RAEN Royal St Robert's cherry-mineral tannin reads alongside the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the medium-body red meets the savory plate, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Escargot|Rainbow Trout": "The trout after the escargot -- the delicate flesh meets the herb-bright snail plate. Strong; the starter composes cleanly before the main.",
  "Escargot|Raventós Cava de NIT Rosé Brut": "Catalan Cava rosé — dry elegant with wild strawberry, raspberry, and saline finish. The mineral spine cuts escargot's garlic-parsley butter and the saline hooks into the French-Mediterranean tradition directly. Strong rosé Cava for escargot — accessible sophistication on the French classic.",
  "Escargot|Redbreast 12 Year": "Redbreast 12 Year's pot-still-fruit character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon weight grips the savory plate. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Escargot|Redbreast 21 Year": "Redbreast 21 Year -- aged single pot still, sherry-cask, rich. The soft malt-and-grain weight wraps the buttered escargot, and the soft malt rounds the starter. Strong; bonded weight at matched premium register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|Remus 15 Year Gatsby Reserve": "Remus 15 Year Gatsby Reserve's bold cherry-juniper character sits with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon weight grips the savory plate, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
