  "Escargot|Sambuca": "Escargot: garlic-herb butter meets Sambuca. Excellent; the Italian-anise-botanical character engages herb butter at Italian register — sweeter and less bracing than Green Chartreuse or Mata Hari.",
  "Escargot|San Simeon Stormwatch": "San Simeon Stormwatch's powerful blackcurrant body meets at register with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the concentrated dark-fruit weight handles the buttered escargot, and the espresso-cocoa note rounds the starter. Strong; reliable opener for the cut.",
  "Escargot|Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir": "Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir's cherry-earth tannin holds with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the medium-body red meets the savory plate, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Escargot|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "The escargot and the garlic spinach -- acid lifts the umami, the meal carries lift without losing depth. Works; sequence them or share the table, no concern either way.",
  "Escargot|Sauternes Glass": "Sauternes Glass' dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Reserve the Sauternes Glass for the steak course.",
  "Escargot|Sazerac": "Sazerac's rye weight and anise-edge sits alongside the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the bold-mix depth handles the buttered escargot, and the bitters edge frames the starter. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|Sazerac Rye": "Sazerac Rye's crisp floral-pepper character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the spice frames the umami depth. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|Scapegrace Fortuna": "Scapegrace Fortuna's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the brown-spirit warmth threads the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Works; milestone-release doesn't drive; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Escargot|Scavino Barolo": "Scavino Barolo: this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight meets this rich, umami-forward starter's bold fat and concentrated savory depth. The bold red's tannin scrubs the starter's fat while dark fruit picks up the umami notes. Not the sharpest pairing. Avoid; route the table to a better-matched pour.",
  "Escargot|Schloss Vollrads Riesling": "Escargot: this rich, umami-forward starter's bold fat and concentrated savory depth meets this off-dry Riesling's stone-fruit sweetness and mineral backbone. Crisp or off-dry white's acidity lifts the starter — classic opening-course move. Strong — clean lift.",
  "Escargot|Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters": "Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters's bold cherry-chocolate cassis plays cleanly against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the opulent body settles into the umami plate, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
