  "Escargot|St Supéry Cabernet Sauvignon": "St Supéry Cabernet Sauvignon's bold char-coffee cassis holds steady against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the Cab structure meets the savory depth, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Escargot|St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc": "St Supéry — Napa Dollarhide Sauv Blanc, lemon, grapefruit, gooseberry, lively finish. The lively acid cuts escargot's garlic-parsley butter and the lemon-grapefruit plays against the snail richness. Strong Napa Sauv Blanc for escargot — rounded body handles the richness better than lean Sauv Blancs.",
  "Escargot|St Supéry Élu Meritage": "St Supéry Élu Meritage's concentrated dark-fruit and tannin leans against the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the structured body wraps the buttered escargot, and the cassis frames the starter. Strong; the match stays in its register.",
  "Escargot|Stagg Jr. Batch #15": "Stagg Jr. Batch #15 -- BT non-age-statement cask-strength, premium batch. The bourbon depth settles into the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; BIB weight cuts the bleu with premium authority; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
