  "Escargot|Tanqueray Gin": "Tanqueray with escargot — juniper-forward Tanq against garlic-butter snails. Excellent; juniper-and-butter is a classic British pairing and Tanq's proof cuts the butter sharper than Plymouth's softer profile can.",
  "Escargot|Taylor Fladgate Tawny": "Taylor Fladgate Tawny's classic tawny with caramel-nut sweetness clashes with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Taylor Fladgate Tawny lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Escargot|Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle": "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a dessert wine. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle on the steak course instead.",
