  "Faroe Island Salmon|Angel's Envy Triple Cask": "AE Triple Cask with the salmon — triple-cask AE against oily salmon. Avoid; wine-finished bourbon wrong for fish.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Aperol": "Aperol's crisp bitter-orange-aperitivo edge jars against the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bitter herbs on oily fish read metallic — the rich flesh deserves a crisp white. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Aperol for the steak course.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Asparagus": "Faroe Island Salmon alongside the asparagus -- the salmon's rich oily flesh carries cleanly into the asparagus' green-vegetal edge. Excellent; the headline side pairing for the salmon.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Au Gratin Potatoes": "The salmon into the au gratin -- the meal layers rich on rich, the table carries weight cleanly when the registers match. Works; safe alongside, but not the headline pick.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon": "Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth fights the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the red's tannin and the salmon's rich oils refuse to integrate. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Averna Amaro": "Averna Amaro's bitter-herb aperitivo edge jars against the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bitter herbs on oily fish read metallic — the rich flesh deserves a crisp white. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Averna Amaro on the steak course instead.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Aviation": "Aviation's crisp almond-cherry build sits with the salmon's rich oily flesh — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Aviation Gin": "Aviation with the salmon — Portland Oregon soft-juniper craft against oily salmon. Excellent; Aviation's balanced approach frames the fish at crowd-pleasing register; Empress 1908's floral and Inverroche's fynbos are more distinctive choices.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Avion 44": "Avion 44's rested-agave body leans against the salmon's rich oily flesh: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the salmon, and the oak threads the plate. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Avion Silver": "Avion Silver with the salmon — 80-proof Jalisco-highlands against salmon's richness. Strong; filtered clean agave frames the fish at accessible register.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Bacardi Rum": "Bacardi Rum's crisp workhorse-clean character finds register with the salmon's rich oily flesh — the crisp body frames the fish cleanly, and the clean profile carries the herb butter. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Baileys Irish Cream": "Baileys Irish Cream's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the liqueur's sugar piles onto the fish's natural oils with no lift. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Baileys Irish Cream belongs on the steak course.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Baker's": "Baker's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Baker's lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Balvenie 12 American Oak": "Balvenie 12 American Oak's bourbon-cask Speyside softness smothers the salmon's rich oily flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a scotch. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Balvenie 12 American Oak lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask": "Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask's rum-finished Speyside character overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon weight needs red meat, not the salmon's already-rich oils. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a scotch. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Balvenie 16 Single Barrel": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's First Fill American Oak smothers the salmon's rich oily flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a scotch. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Balvenie 16 Single Barrel lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Balvenie 21 Portwood": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside smothers the salmon's rich oily flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a scotch. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Balvenie 21 Portwood for the steak course.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Bardstown Château Laboude": "Bardstown Château Laboude with the salmon — Bardstown Bourbon Co. French-wine finish against oily salmon. Avoid; wine-finished bourbon wrong for fish.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Bardstown Discovery #6": "Bardstown Discovery #6's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Bardstown Discovery #6 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Bardstown Founders KBS": "Bardstown Founders KBS's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Bardstown Founders KBS lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Bardstown Foursquare": "Bardstown Foursquare's rum-cask + cocoa is textbook — tropical-rum + chocolate smothers the salmon's rich oily flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Bardstown Foursquare on the steak course instead.",
