  "Faroe Island Salmon|Basil Hayden's": "Basil Hayden's light high-rye and cocoa swallows the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Basil Hayden's belongs on the steak course.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Basil Hayden's 10 Year": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's aged oak and rye spice clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Basil Hayden's 10 Year lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Basil Hayden's Malted Rye": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character swallows the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Basil Hayden's Malted Rye for the steak course.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with the salmon — high-rye BH red-wine finish against oily salmon. Avoid; wine-finished bourbon wrong for fish.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Basil Hayden's Toast": "Basil Hayden's Toast's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the salmon's rich oily flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Basil Hayden's Toast on the steak course instead.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Bee's Knees": "Empress Indigo gin with lemon and honey lavender syrup. Honey sweetness and lemon against Faroe salmon's rich fat works when the prep leans lighter. The Indigo color-shift is a talking point; ask the kitchen first. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Beefeater Gin": "Beefeater with the salmon — 9-botanical London Dry against oily salmon. Strong; Beefeater's balance frames the fish at approachable register.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Beignets": "After the salmon, the beignets -- the rich oily flesh yields to warm choux and powdered sugar, the dipping sauce closing the meal light. Works; the substantial fish hands off to a measured close.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Belvedere Vodka": "Belvedere with the salmon — Polish rye against oily salmon. Strong; the rye pepper lifts the fish's richness with dimension the softer vodkas lack.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Blade & Bow": "Blade & Bow's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Blade & Bow lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Blanton's Gold": "Blanton's Gold's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Blanton's Gold for the steak course.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Blanton's Original": "Blanton's Original's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Blanton's Original for the steak course.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Blanton's Straight from the Barrel": "Blanton's SfB with the salmon — cask-strength Blanton's against oily salmon. Avoid; barrel-proof bourbon too intense for fish.",
