  "Faroe Island Salmon|Heitz Martha's Vineyard": "Heitz Martha's Vineyard's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Heitz Martha's Vineyard for the steak course.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Heitz Trailside Vineyard": "Heitz Trailside Vineyard's Napa-icon Cab character jars against the salmon's rich oily flesh -- tannin on oily fish goes bitter, where a Pinot at the right register would carry it. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Heitz Trailside Vineyard for the steak course.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Hendricks Flora Adora": "Flora Adora with the salmon — Spring-release floral Hendrick's against oily salmon. Excellent; Flora Adora's honeysuckle-elderflower-chamomile profile lifts the fish with lavish-floral distinction beyond flagship Hendrick's.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Hendricks Gin": "Hendricks with the salmon — flagship cucumber-rose against oily salmon. Excellent; Hendrick's cucumber-cools-fish approach at crowd-pleasing register.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Hendricks Grand Cabaret": "Grand Cabaret with the salmon — Hendrick's black currant + rhubarb against oily salmon. Excellent; Grand Cabaret's fruit-forward profile lifts the fish at distinctive register — fruit-and-fish less traditional than citrus-and-fish but cohesive.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Hendricks Neptunia": "Neptunia with the salmon — Scottish-coast Hendrick's against oily salmon. Excellent; Neptunia's bladderwrack-Ayrshire-thyme profile is the thematically-perfect salmon pairing — Scottish-coast gin against North-Atlantic fish.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Hendricks Orbium": "Orbium with the salmon — quinine-wormwood Hendrick's against oily salmon. Strong; Orbium's bitter-tonic profile cuts the fish's richness with distinctive contrast.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Hennessy Cognac": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- cognac is post-meal energy — wrong register for a main protein. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a cognac. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hennessy Cognac belongs on the steak course.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's aged 100-proof bonded single-barrel overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond belongs on the steak course.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Hibiki Japanese Harmony": "Hibiki Harmony with the salmon — refined premium Suntory blend against oily salmon. Excellent; Hibiki's elegant-delicate character frames fish at premium Japanese register — Japanese whisky's category advantage with the refinement to elevate.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Faroe Island Salmon with the honey carrots -- the buttery salmon holds with the glazed carrot side. Strong; reliable side for the salmon.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|House Wedge": "Faroe Island Salmon after the wedge -- the iceberg-and-bleu cool crunch refreshes the palate, the salmon following with rich oily flesh that the cold opener cleared room for. Strong; the salad's bite primes the rich fish course.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|I.W. Harper 15 Year": "I.W. Harper 15 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. I.W. Harper 15 Year lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Il Colle Prosecco Superiore": "Il Colle Prosecco Superiore's crisp apple-citrus acidity reads alongside the salmon's rich oily flesh — the bright acidity frames the fish without weight, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Inhibited": "Inhibited's chocolate-cocoa build reads alongside the salmon's rich oily flesh — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly. Strong; the match carries without overshooting.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Inverroche Gin": "Inverroche with the salmon — Western Cape fynbos gin against oily salmon. Excellent; Inverroche's floral-herbal profile is the featured Botanical-Forward Craft Gin-salmon pairing — the Cape-fynbos lift frames the fish with terroir specificity.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Iron Fish Gin": "Iron Fish with the salmon — Thompsonville farm-to-bottle gin against oily salmon. Excellent; Iron Fish's northern-Michigan farm character meets Faroe Island salmon thematically — the featured Local MI Gin-salmon pairing, where the geography-echoes-geography logic lands naturally.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|Isaac Bowman Port Finish": "Isaac Bowman Port Finish with the salmon — Sazerac-owned port-finish against oily salmon. Avoid; port-finished bourbon wrong for fish.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|J Davies Ferrington Vineyards": "Anderson Valley Pinot — concentrated, dark cherry, blackberry, mocha, refined tannin. The concentrated structure plays against salmon's oil-rich flesh; preparation changes seasonally — check with kitchen for today's build. Peak Anderson Valley Pinot for salmon — cool-climate depth across seasonal preparations. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Faroe Island Salmon|J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character fights the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the red's tannin and the salmon's rich oils refuse to integrate. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
