  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Loaded Potato": "Four Roses Yellow Label's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the caramel-spice register matches the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; EC 18 frames the two-cut plate at aged-HH register.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Lobster Mac": "Four Roses Yellow Label's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon body sits with the lobster mac, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; AE CS handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Market Fish": "Four Roses Yellow Label's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Four Roses Yellow Label belongs on the steak course.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Mocha Creme": "Four Roses Yellow Label's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the bourbon body sits with the mocha creme, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the toast adds a warmth the dessert can accept.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Mushroom Bisque": "Four Roses Yellow Label's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; gentle composed match.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Mushrooms": "Four Roses Yellow Label with the mushrooms — floral, light-bodied entry bourbon against earthy umami. The lightness lets mushroom depth lead; an accessible everyday pairing. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Four Roses Yellow Label's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the brown-spirit warmth threads the PB brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; HH 20's aged character meets the glaze at collector register.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Porterhouse": "Four Roses Yellow Label with the porterhouse — entry bourbon across strip and filet sides. Strong for the filet side; underpowered for the strip. Buffalo Trace or Woodford Reserve are more balanced calls here.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Prime Tartare": "Four Roses Yellow Label's crisp caramel-floral character lifts the tartare's raw beef and brine — the bourbon depth cuts the umami fat, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Rainbow Trout": "Four Roses Yellow Label's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the trout's delicate flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Four Roses Yellow Label belongs on the steak course.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Roast Half Chicken": "Four Roses Yellow Label's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the bourbon weight handles the roast chicken, and the rounded sweetness brightens the plate. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Four Roses Yellow Label's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the bourbon backbone carries the chickpea soup, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; the intensity overpowers this dish.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Four Roses Yellow Label's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Four Roses Yellow Label for the steak course.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Four Roses Yellow Label's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the bourbon weight handles the garlic spinach, and the caramel rounds the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Seafood Tower": "Four Roses Yellow Label's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit weight crowds the delicate shellfish — no acid to clean the brine. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Four Roses Yellow Label on the steak course instead.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Seared Scallops": "Four Roses Yellow Label with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 80-proof bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Seasonal Soup": "Four Roses Yellow Label's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the bourbon backbone carries the seasonal soup, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; private-selection wasted on the salad.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Seasonal Vegetables": "Four Roses Yellow Label's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the oak depth lays under the seasonal vegetables, and the oak frames the side. Works; polished 10-year gives the dessert small-batch premium character.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Shrimp Bisque": "Four Roses Yellow Label with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood against entry bourbon. Works neutrally; light body sits with the soup.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Shrimp Cocktail": "Four Roses Yellow Label with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against entry bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Swordfish": "Four Roses Yellow Label's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Four Roses Yellow Label for the steak course.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|The Tomahawk": "Four Roses Yellow Label's crisp caramel-floral character holds steady against the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the caramel-and-oak weight rises with the cap-fat, and the caramel echoes the grilled char. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Tomato Basil": "Four Roses Yellow Label's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth leans against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the bourbon weight handles the tomato basil, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Truffle Fries": "Four Roses Yellow Label with truffle fries — the 10-recipe blend at entry level. 80 proof floral-and-honey meets truffle-parmesan. The light-body lets truffle lead; entry-level but cleanly matched for this side. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Four Roses Yellow Label's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Four Roses Yellow Label lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Four Roses Yellow Label|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Four Roses Yellow Label's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the curry, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; oak spice sits beside the soup without driving.",
