  "Freemark Abbey Bosché|Faroe Island Salmon": "Freemark Abbey Bosché's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth fights the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the red's tannin and the salmon's rich oils refuse to integrate. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Freemark Abbey Bosché lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Freemark Abbey Bosché|Filet Mignon": "Rutherford Cab — Bosché Vineyard since 1970, blackcurrant, tobacco, graphite, firm tannin, full body, age-worthy. The firm structure meets butter-tender filet's delicate sweetness and the tobacco plays against escargot-butter. Peak Bosché Vineyard Cab for filet — 1970-legacy structure on the delicate cut. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
