  "Freemark Abbey Bosché|Market Fish": "Freemark Abbey Bosché's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the red's structure is wrong for delicate flesh — built for red meat. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Freemark Abbey Bosché on the steak course instead.",
  "Freemark Abbey Bosché|Mocha Creme": "Freemark Abbey Bosché's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- savory tannin sits awkwardly on cocoa weight without resolving. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Freemark Abbey Bosché lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Freemark Abbey Bosché|Mushroom Bisque": "Freemark Abbey Bosché's concentrated dark-fruit and tannin finds neutral with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the structured body wraps the mushroom bisque, and the cassis frames the bowl. Works; the call holds at neutral register.",
  "Freemark Abbey Bosché|Mushrooms": "Mushrooms: the structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit anchors the mushroom's umami weight; firm tannin and oak hold their register. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
