  "Freemark Abbey Bosché|Rainbow Trout": "Freemark Abbey Bosché's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Reserve the Freemark Abbey Bosché for the steak course.",
  "Freemark Abbey Bosché|Roast Half Chicken": "Freemark Abbey Bosché's powerful blackcurrant body finds neutral with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the concentrated dark-fruit weight handles the roast chicken, and the blackberry edge underlines the plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
