  "Freemark Abbey Bosché|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Freemark Abbey Bosché's bold juniper-leather cassis holds with the garlic-spinach's buttered greens — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Freemark Abbey Bosché|Seafood Tower": "Freemark Abbey Bosché's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Freemark Abbey Bosché belongs on the steak course.",
  "Freemark Abbey Bosché|Seared Scallops": "Rutherford Bosché Cab against scallop sweetness — firm-tannin blackcurrant-graphite structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Freemark Abbey Bosché for the steak course.",
