  "Freemark Abbey Bosché|Shrimp Cocktail": "Rutherford Bosché Cab against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — firm-tannin full-body red and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Freemark Abbey Bosché for the steak course.",
  "Freemark Abbey Bosché|Swordfish": "Freemark Abbey Bosché's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- tannin against rare-seared crust reads astringent without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Freemark Abbey Bosché on the steak course instead.",
  "Freemark Abbey Bosché|The Tomahawk": "The Tomahawk: this marbled ribeye's fatty richness, smoky crust, and bold beef expression meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The tannin scrubs rendered fat while dark fruit echoes the savory char. A headliner steakhouse pour. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
