  "French 75|Au Gratin Potatoes": "French 75's citrus-earth build sits alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the oak frames the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "French 75|Beignets": "French 75's gin-and-Champagne lift with citrus snap clashes with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- light cocktail citrus is wrong direction for the dessert's richness. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a light cocktail. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. French 75 belongs on the steak course.",
  "French 75|Bone Marrow": "Inverroche gin, lemon, vanilla syrup, Prosecco top. The bubbly, bright cocktail has no structural match for marrow's rendered-fat richness — citrus and bubbles don't cut that deep. Never pair — keep the 75 for raw bar and starters, route marrow to whiskey cocktails.",
  "French 75|Bone-In Filet": "French 75's gin-and-Champagne lift with citrus snap underclubs the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- cocktail citrus reads thin against the cut's structure. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a light cocktail. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the French 75 for another course.",
