  "French 75|Honey Roasted Carrots": "French 75's citrus-earth build stays alongside the carrots' honeyed sweetness — the cocktail lift sits with the light side, and the vanilla amplifies the dessert sugar. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "French 75|House Wedge": "Inverroche gin, lemon, vanilla syrup, Prosecco top. The citrus-and-bubbles lift cuts iceberg-and-bacon weight and the vanilla softens against blue cheese dressing. Strong opener pairing — keeps the palate fresh before the steak course arrives.",
  "French 75|Kansas City": "French 75's gin-and-Champagne lift with citrus snap underclubs the KC's lean-bold strip with savory grain -- light cocktail lands short of any prime cut. The plate deserves Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, Pio Cesare Barbaresco, or Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye, not a light cocktail. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the French 75 on another course instead.",
