  "French Onion|Aperol": "Aperol's crisp bitter-orange-aperitivo edge jars against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth -- bitter botanicals on savory broth pull against the salt-and-spice frame without resolving. The plate deserves Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Aperol on the steak course instead.",
  "French Onion|Asparagus": "The French onion alongside the asparagus -- acid breaks the umami stack, the table earns the brighter note. Works; the table can build them in order or together.",
  "French Onion|Au Gratin Potatoes": "The French onion alongside the au gratin -- both bring cheese as the headline. Avoid; one is enough. Pair the French onion with Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée; pair the au gratin with Bone-In Filet, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Keenan Chardonnay.",
