  "French Onion|Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé": "Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé's crisp berry-cherry acidity stays alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "French Onion|Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut": "Tours-sur-Marne Chardonnay-blend Champagne — precise green apple, lemon zest, whisper of brioche, vibrant acidity. The high-acid finish cuts French Onion's gruyère crust and the brioche plays against the caramelized onion. Works as Champagne-palate-cleanser for French Onion — elegant bubbles reset the rich classic; still wines peak higher as dedicated pairings.",
