  "French Onion|Lemon Lavender Gin Martini": "Lemon Lavender Gin Martini's citrus-floral build leans against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the cocktail lift refreshes against the hearty soup, and the rounded sweetness threads the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "French Onion|Les Pallières Raciné": "Les Pallières Raciné's bold earth-mineral cassis sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the rye spice cuts the cheese richness. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "French Onion|Liberator Gin": "Liberator Gin's citrus-juniper botanicals leans against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals cut the cheese richness. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "French Onion|Licor 43": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character clashes with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Licor 43 belongs on the steak course.",
  "French Onion|Limoncello": "Limoncello's sweet liqueur character clashes with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth -- sweet liqueur on savory broth jars — sugar pulls one way, the salt-and-spice broth pulls the other. The plate deserves Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a digestif. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Limoncello belongs on the steak course.",
  "French Onion|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Willamette Pinot — dark cherry, forest floor, refined structure, low tannin. The low-tannin silk lifts French Onion's caramelized beef-broth weight and the forest-floor earth plays against the sweet onion depth. Peak by-the-glass Pinot for French Onion — Avni's refined Willamette character meets the classic without crushing the gruyère crust. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
