  "French Onion|Lobster Mac": "The French onion and the lobster mac -- both cheese-forward, the table doubles up on cheese. Avoid; pick one or the other. Pair the French onion with Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée; pair the lobster mac with Cowboy Ribeye, Far Niente Chardonnay, or The Tomahawk.",
  "French Onion|Loch Lomond 20 Year": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the scotch backbone matches the French onion, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; extended-aged home-state pour wasted on salad.",
