  "French Onion|Los Vecinos Mezcal": "Los Vecinos Mezcal's espadín-and-smoke register leans against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the rustic mezcal weight sits with the French onion, and the mineral smoke plays against the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "French Onion|Louis XIII Cognac": "Louis XIII Cognac's luxury-icon cognac depth mis-pairs with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth -- an icon cognac on a soup-salad course is wrong moment — its register demands the close, not the open. The plate deserves Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an icon cognac. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Louis XIII Cognac on the steak course instead.",
