  "Garavogue Irish Whiskey|Chilean Seabass": "Garavogue Irish Whiskey's Irish whiskey smoothness swallows the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Garavogue Irish Whiskey belongs on the steak course.",
