  "Garavogue Irish Whiskey|Rainbow Trout": "Garavogue Irish Whiskey's Irish whiskey smoothness smothers the trout's delicate flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Garavogue Irish Whiskey belongs on the steak course.",
