  "Ghost Block Zinfandel|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Ghost Block Zinfandel's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift jars against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Ghost Block Zinfandel on the steak course instead.",
  "Ghost Block Zinfandel|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Ghost Block Zinfandel's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift clashes with the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Ghost Block Zinfandel for the steak course.",
  "Ghost Block Zinfandel|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Ghost Block Zinfandel's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift crowds the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- the side needs a crisper register to carry it cleanly. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Ghost Block Zinfandel belongs on the steak course.",
  "Ghost Block Zinfandel|Seafood Tower": "Ghost Block Zinfandel's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Ghost Block Zinfandel for the steak course.",
  "Ghost Block Zinfandel|Seared Scallops": "Never pair Ghost Block with seared scallops — cracked pepper and jammy fruit overwhelm delicate sweet shellfish and the full body fights browned-butter. Lead with Clos de la Chapelle Chardonnay or Rombauer's creamy richness for sear-seared harmony.",
  "Ghost Block Zinfandel|Seasonal Soup": "Ghost Block Zinfandel's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift overwhelms the seasonal soup's house seasonal build -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Ghost Block Zinfandel for the steak course.",
  "Ghost Block Zinfandel|Seasonal Vegetables": "Ghost Block Zinfandel's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift overshadows the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate -- red weight crowds a green side without lifting it — needs crisp register, not tannin. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Ghost Block Zinfandel for the steak course.",
  "Ghost Block Zinfandel|Shrimp Bisque": "Ghost Block Zinfandel's bold pepper-spice cassis stays alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Ghost Block Zinfandel|Shrimp Cocktail": "Never pair Ghost Block with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp plus cocktail-sauce horseradish gets crushed by jammy fruit, cracked pepper, and full body, and the bold Napa has nowhere to land. Lead with Laurent Perrier Brut Champagne's bubble-driven palate reset.",
  "Ghost Block Zinfandel|Swordfish": "Ghost Block Zinfandel's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift overshadows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- dark-fruit weight crowds the seared sesame crust — needs a sparkling or crisp white for lift. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Ghost Block Zinfandel on the steak course instead.",
  "Ghost Block Zinfandel|The Tomahawk": "Napa Oakville Zinfandel — Ghost Block, ripe jammy fruit, blackberry preserves, cracked pepper, full body, medium tannin. The full body handles Tomahawk's massive 36oz bone-in and the cracked pepper plays with smoky char. Strong California-Zin for Tomahawk — a firmer-tannin Cab edges higher on the grand cut.",
  "Ghost Block Zinfandel|Tomato Basil": "Ghost Block Zinfandel's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift overwhelms the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Le Garenne Rosé, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Ghost Block Zinfandel for the steak course.",
  "Ghost Block Zinfandel|Truffle Fries": "Napa Oakville Zinfandel — Ghost Block, ripe jammy fruit, blackberry preserves, cracked pepper, full body, medium tannin. The cracked pepper cuts parm-richness and the full body handles truffle-oil weight. Strong California-Zin for truffle fries — jammy-Zin polish on the cut.",
  "Ghost Block Zinfandel|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Ghost Block Zinfandel's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift overshadows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- dark-fruit weight crowds the seared sesame crust — needs a sparkling or crisp white for lift. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Ghost Block Zinfandel lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Ghost Block Zinfandel|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Ghost Block Zinfandel's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift jars against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Le Garenne Rosé, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Ghost Block Zinfandel for the steak course.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Asparagus": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark leans against the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the malt-driven body wraps the asparagus, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the side. Works; master-blender doesn't drive.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Glenfiddich 12 with the au gratin — gateway Speyside against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Strong; Fiddich's light vanilla handles the richness at approachable register.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Beignets": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the beignets, and the smoke threads the dessert. Works; complexity wasted on salad.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Bone Marrow": "Glenfiddich 12 with bone marrow — gateway Speyside against umami fat. Works; Fiddich is too light to cut marrow the way Fernet Branca does — reach for Fernet for marrow, Fiddich if the guest specifically wants Speyside alongside.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Bone-In Filet": "Glenfiddich 12 with the bone-in filet — gateway Speyside against tenderloin-with-bone. Excellent; Fiddich's apple/pear lightness frames the cut's marrow-adjacent depth without overwhelming the filet's finesse.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Broccoli Cheddar": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark leans against the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the scotch depth settles into the broccoli cheddar, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; boutique character doesn't drive.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Broccolini": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark leans against the broccolini's tender green stalks: the malt-and-oak threads the broccolini, and the malt edge frames the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet ex-bourbon-cask Speyside. Works; Fiddich's honey-apple meets the glaze at approachable register.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Burrata": "Glenfiddich 12 with burrata — entry Speyside against fresh dairy. Avoid; Scotch weight wrong for burrata's cream.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Butternut Squash": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the malt-and-oak threads the squash bisque, and the oak softens the cream. Works; extended-aged premium wasted on salad simplicity.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Carrot Cake": "Glenfiddich 12 with carrot cake — gateway Speyside against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Fiddich's honey-apple finds the cake's raisins and spice with approachable character.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Cheesecake": "Glenfiddich 12 with cheesecake — apple/pear Speyside against custard. Strong; Fiddich rides the cheesecake with gateway character; Balvenie 12's vanilla-forward profile edges this pairing.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Chilean Seabass": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark swallows the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Glenfiddich 12 on the steak course instead.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Chocolate Brownie": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark reads alongside the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight: the malt-and-oak threads the brownie, and the heather brightens the dessert. Works; Voyage 23 frames the two-cut plate at ocean-finish register.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Chocolate Cake": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the Highland register carries the chocolate cake, and the heather brightens the dessert. Works; the light body doesn't overshoot the salad.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Clam Chowder": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the scotch backbone matches the chowder, and the oak softens the cream. Works; own-plus-sourced covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Cowboy Ribeye": "Glenfiddich 12 with the cowboy ribeye — gateway Speyside against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Strong; Fiddich's apple/pear handles the ribeye at approachable register.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Crab Cake": "Glenfiddich 12 with crab cake — Speyside against delicate crab. Avoid; Scotch is wrong for seafood. Reach for a vodka or gin.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Creamed Spinach": "Glenfiddich 12 with creamed spinach — ex-bourbon-cask Speyside against dairy-rich side. Strong; Fiddich's honey-apple rides the cream at gateway register.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Creamy Potato": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the malt-and-oak threads the potato soup, and the oak softens the cream. Works; BIB structure overshoots the dessert's delicacy.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Creme Brulee": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark reads alongside the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the malt-driven body wraps the brulee, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; AE Triple Cask meets the char at distinctive register.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Escargot": "Glenfiddich 12's crisp apple-honey character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter. Strong; the match carries without overshooting.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Faroe Island Salmon": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a scotch. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Glenfiddich 12 on the steak course instead.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Filet Mignon": "Glenfiddich 12 with the filet — entry Speyside benchmark, ex-bourbon-cask, apple/pear/honey gateway profile. Excellent; Fiddich 12 is the democratic Speyside-filet pairing — the 40% ABV green-apple character lifts tenderloin where heavier Scotches would compete. The bottle guests reach for by name.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|French Onion": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark finds neutral with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the French onion, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; the single-barrel depth is over-specified for this dish.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Grilled Caesar": "Glenfiddich 12 with the grilled Caesar — entry Speyside against charred romaine and anchovy. Excellent; Fiddich's apple/pear lightness meets the char cleanly — the gateway-Speyside Caesar pairing.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Gumbo": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark leans against the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the scotch depth settles into the gumbo, and the oak-and-smoke underlines the bowl. Works; Voyage 23 frames the two-cut plate at ocean-finish register.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark leans against the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the honey carrots, and the oak underlines the burnt sugar. Works; boutique character slightly over-specified.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|House Wedge": "Glenfiddich 12 with the House Wedge — entry Speyside against iceberg and bleu. Works; Fiddich's light profile is a functional wedge pairing.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Kansas City": "Glenfiddich 12 with the KC — entry Speyside against an 18oz strip. Strong; Fiddich handles the strip with gateway character, though the Speyside 18 or Balvenie 16 (next batch) are the distinctive Speyside-KC choices.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Loaded Potato": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark reads alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the Highland register carries the loaded potato soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the aging is wasted on the salad.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Lobster Mac": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the scotch depth settles into the lobster mac, and the oak threads the cream. Works; neutral companion.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Market Fish": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a scotch. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Glenfiddich 12 for the steak course.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Mocha Creme": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark leans against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the Highland register carries the mocha creme, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; the pour is a touch ambitious for the salad.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Mushroom Bisque": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the malt-driven body wraps the mushroom bisque, and the oak balances the umami register. Works; Voyage 23 frames the cut at ocean-finish register.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Mushrooms": "Glenfiddich 12 with mushrooms — apple/pear ex-bourbon-cask Speyside against earthy umami. Excellent; Fiddich's lightness threads the mushrooms at gateway register.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Peanut Butter Brownie: peanut butter and cocoa meet gateway Speyside. Works; Fiddich handles the density at approachable register; Balvenie 12's vanilla is the better match.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Porterhouse": "Glenfiddich 12 with the porterhouse — apple/pear Speyside against strip-and-filet. Strong; Fiddich's gateway lightness frames the two-cut plate without competing.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Prime Tartare": "Glenfiddich 12's crisp apple-honey character frames the tartare's raw beef and brine — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the smoke meets the umami depth. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Rainbow Trout": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a scotch. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Glenfiddich 12 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Roast Half Chicken": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark finds neutral with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the roast chicken, and the smoke threads the plate. Works; the 10-year's restraint lets the soup lead.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark reads alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the malt-driven body wraps the chickpea soup, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the bowl. Works; OGD 16 frames the two-cut plate at distinctive register.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark flattens the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Glenfiddich 12 for the steak course.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark finds neutral with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the malt-driven body wraps the garlic spinach, and the honey rounds the side. Works; doesn't drive.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Seafood Tower": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Glenfiddich 12 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Seared Scallops": "Glenfiddich 12 with seared scallops — apple/pear Speyside against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Seasonal Soup": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark reads alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the scotch backbone matches the seasonal soup, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the bowl. Works; polished aged character doesn't drive.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Seasonal Vegetables": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark leans against the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the Highland register carries the seasonal vegetables, and the malt edge frames the side. Works; the single-barrel depth is over-specified for this dish.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Shrimp Bisque": "Glenfiddich 12 with shrimp bisque — apple/pear Speyside against cream-shrimp soup. Works; Fiddich rides the bisque at gateway register.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Shrimp Cocktail": "Glenfiddich 12 with shrimp cocktail — bourbon-cask Speyside against cold shrimp. Avoid; Scotch wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Swordfish": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Glenfiddich 12 on the steak course instead.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|The Tomahawk": "Glenfiddich 12 -- entry Speyside, apple-pear, ex-bourbon-cask. The bourbon-cask apple lifts the 36oz showpiece, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; composed premium match.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Tomato Basil": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark finds neutral with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the malt-driven body wraps the tomato basil, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for the side — save the collector bottle for the protein course.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Truffle Fries": "Glenfiddich 12 with truffle fries — bourbon-cask apple/pear Speyside against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Fiddich's light vanilla and green-fruit character is the approachable Speyside-truffle pairing — where Balvenie 12 adds vanilla depth, Fiddich keeps it gateway-fresh.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Glenfiddich 12 for the steak course.",
  "Glenfiddich 12|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the scotch backbone matches the curry, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; regional craft at matched register.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Asparagus": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the scotch depth settles into the asparagus, and the malt edge frames the side. Works; IW Harper 15 frames the two-cut plate at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Glenfiddich 14 with the au gratin — Bourbon Barrel Reserve against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Strong; the charred-oak finish handles the richness at aged register.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Beignets": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the scotch backbone matches the beignets, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the dessert. Works; Caribbean Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Bone Marrow": "Glenfiddich 14 with bone marrow — new-charred-oak Speyside against umami fat. Works; Fiddich 14 is still too light to cut marrow the way Fernet Branca does; sits alongside comfortably.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Bone-In Filet": "Glenfiddich 14 with the bone-in filet — Bourbon Barrel Reserve against tenderloin-with-bone. Excellent; the new-charred-oak finish adds spice and vanilla depth that frames the cut's marrow-adjacent richness better than the 12's lighter profile.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Broccoli Cheddar": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the scotch depth settles into the broccoli cheddar, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; premium proof overshoots delicacy.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Broccolini": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the malt-and-oak threads the broccolini, and the oak-and-smoke underlines the side. Works; the sweetness is a touch much for the salad's simplicity.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Brussels and Belly": "Glenfiddich 14 with Brussels + Belly — Bourbon Barrel Reserve against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Fiddich 14's baking-spice meets the glaze with more dimension than the 12.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Burrata": "Glenfiddich 14 with burrata — new-charred-oak Speyside against fresh dairy. Avoid; Scotch weight wrong for burrata's cream.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Butternut Squash": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the scotch depth settles into the squash bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; distinctive character gives the dessert a unique story-frame.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Carrot Cake": "Glenfiddich 14 with carrot cake — new-charred-oak Speyside against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Fiddich 14's baking-spice character marries the cake's cinnamon naturally — more dimensional than the 12's honey-apple approach.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Cheesecake": "Glenfiddich 14 with cheesecake — new-charred-oak-finished Speyside against custard. Strong; Fiddich 14's baking-spice frames the cheesecake more fully than the 12's apple-pear approach; Balvenie 16 Single Barrel still edges this for vanilla-forward dessert.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Chilean Seabass": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character swallows the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Glenfiddich 14 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Chocolate Brownie": "Glenfiddich 14: bourbon-barrel-reserve Speyside. Excellent on chocolate brownie; vanilla-sweet bourbon-finish frames cocoa at Speyside register.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Chocolate Cake": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character leans against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the Highland register carries the chocolate cake, and the heather brightens the dessert. Works; bonded weight a touch ambitious for the dessert.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Clam Chowder": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the malt-driven body wraps the chowder, and the oak softens the cream. Works; premium proof overpowers this dish.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Cowboy Ribeye": "Glenfiddich 14 with the cowboy ribeye — new-charred-oak-finished Speyside against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Strong; Fiddich 14 handles the ribeye, though the 18's Oloroso-cask depth is the featured Speyside-ribeye match.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Crab Cake": "Glenfiddich 14 with crab cake — aged Speyside against delicate crab. Avoid; Scotch wrong for seafood. Reach for a vodka or gin.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Creamed Spinach": "Glenfiddich 14 with creamed spinach — new-charred-oak Speyside against dairy-rich side. Strong; Fiddich 14's baking-spice rides the cream with more backbone than the 12.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Creamy Potato": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the malt-and-oak threads the potato soup, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; HH 20 handles dessert density at collector register.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Creme Brulee": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character leans against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the brulee, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; premium proof overpowers this dish.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Escargot": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character leans against the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the scotch depth settles into the buttered escargot, and the malt edge frames the starter. Strong; clean match; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Faroe Island Salmon": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a scotch. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Glenfiddich 14 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Filet Mignon": "Glenfiddich 14 with the filet — Bourbon Barrel Reserve, finished in new charred oak for richer vanilla and baking spice depth beyond the 12. Excellent; Fiddich 14's intensified vanilla-spice character frames tenderloin with more oak backbone than the 12's gateway apple/pear — the upgrade pour for the guest who knows Fiddich 12 and wants the next level.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|French Onion": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the malt-driven body wraps the French onion, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; light body doesn't overshoot.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Grilled Caesar": "Glenfiddich 14 with the grilled Caesar — Bourbon Barrel Reserve against charred romaine and anchovy. Strong; Fiddich 14's charred-oak finish meets the char with resonance the 12's apple doesn't quite reach; Cragganmore 12's subtle smoke still leads this pairing.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Gumbo": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character leans against the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the Highland register carries the gumbo, and the heather brightens the bowl. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for a side — save the collector bottle for the main.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the honey carrots, and the oak balances the burnt-sugar edge. Works; GTS is over-specified for an app; save the collector bottle for the main course.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|House Wedge": "Glenfiddich 14 with the House Wedge — Bourbon Barrel Reserve against iceberg and bleu. Works; Fiddich 14's depth is over-specified for the wedge.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Kansas City": "Glenfiddich 14 with the KC — Bourbon Barrel Reserve against an 18oz strip. Excellent; the intensified vanilla and charred-oak spice give Fiddich 14 enough backbone for the strip's marbling where the 12 feels under-specified — the entry-aged Speyside-KC match.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Loaded Potato": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the Highland register carries the loaded potato soup, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; the complex character gives the dessert a refined frame.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Lobster Mac": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the Highland register carries the lobster mac, and the oak threads the cream. Works; the complex profile is over-specified for this dish.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Market Fish": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character swallows the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a scotch. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Glenfiddich 14 on the steak course instead.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Mocha Creme": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the malt-and-oak threads the mocha creme, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; the Millennium's register overshoots the dessert's.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Mushroom Bisque": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the scotch backbone matches the mushroom bisque, and the oak underlines the umami weight. Works; complexity wasted on salad.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Mushrooms": "Glenfiddich 14 with mushrooms — new-charred-oak-finished bourbon-cask Speyside against earthy umami. Excellent; Fiddich 14's baking-spice depth engages mushroom earthiness with more dimension than the 12 can reach.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Peanut Butter Brownie: peanut butter and cocoa meet new-charred-oak Speyside. Works; Fiddich 14 handles the density; Balvenie 16's deeper vanilla is still the featured match.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Porterhouse": "Glenfiddich 14 with the porterhouse — Bourbon Barrel Reserve against strip-and-filet. Strong; Fiddich 14's vanilla-spice depth frames the two-cut plate with aged character.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Prime Tartare": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami: the scotch depth settles into the tartare, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; the unicorn WP sits with richness at allocated register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Rainbow Trout": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character swallows the trout's delicate flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a scotch. Avoid; the better calls are above. Glenfiddich 14 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Roast Half Chicken": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character leans against the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the scotch backbone matches the roast chicken, and the honey rounds the plate. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character leans against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the malt-driven body wraps the chickpea soup, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; collector-bottle depth gives ultra-premium character.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character smothers the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Glenfiddich 14 on the steak course instead.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character leans against the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the garlic spinach, and the smoke threads the side. Works; high proof over-specified.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Seafood Tower": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Glenfiddich 14 on the steak course instead.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Seared Scallops": "Glenfiddich 14 with seared scallops — Bourbon Barrel Reserve against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Seasonal Soup": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the scotch backbone matches the seasonal soup, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the bowl. Works; KBS distinctiveness is slightly over-specified for the two-cut plate.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Seasonal Vegetables": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the scotch depth settles into the seasonal vegetables, and the oak-and-smoke underlines the side. Works; boutique-blend depth gives composed dessert character.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Shrimp Bisque": "Glenfiddich 14 with shrimp bisque — new-charred-oak-finished Speyside against cream-shrimp soup. Works; Fiddich 14 rides the bisque at aged register.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Shrimp Cocktail": "Glenfiddich 14 with shrimp cocktail — Bourbon Barrel Reserve against cold shrimp. Avoid; Scotch wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Swordfish": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Glenfiddich 14 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|The Tomahawk": "Glenfiddich 14's char-cinnamon character sits with the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the bourbon depth grips the marbled cut, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Tomato Basil": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the scotch depth settles into the tomato basil, and the malt edge frames the bowl. Works; aged character overshoots delicacy.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Truffle Fries": "Glenfiddich 14 with truffle fries — Bourbon Barrel Reserve against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; the charred-oak finish meets the earthy-rich with richer vanilla than Fiddich 12 offers.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Glenfiddich 14 on the steak course instead.",
  "Glenfiddich 14|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character leans against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the scotch backbone matches the curry, and the honey rounds the bowl. Works; AE meets the char at wine-finish register.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Asparagus": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish finds neutral with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the asparagus, and the smoke threads the side. Works; OGD 16 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Glenfiddich 18 with the au gratin — Small Batch Reserve against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Strong; Fiddich 18's depth handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Beignets": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the beignets, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the dessert. Works; BIB slightly over-specified.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Bone Marrow": "Glenfiddich 18 with bone marrow — Oloroso-cask Speyside against umami fat. Works; Fiddich 18's dried-fruit depth sits alongside marrow comfortably — closer to working than the 12/14 but Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Bone-In Filet": "Glenfiddich 18 with the bone-in filet — Small Batch Reserve against tenderloin-with-bone. Excellent; the Oloroso dried-fruit + nutmeg notes frame the cut's marrow-adjacent depth with premium aged character.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Broccoli Cheddar": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the Highland register carries the broccoli cheddar, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; no driver pairing.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Broccolini": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish sits alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the malt-and-oak threads the broccolini, and the heather brightens the side. Works; aging wasted on the salad.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Brussels and Belly": "Glenfiddich 18 with Brussels + Belly — Oloroso-marriage Speyside against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Fiddich 18's dried-fruit finds the glaze naturally.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Burrata": "Glenfiddich 18 with burrata — sherry-cask Speyside against fresh dairy. Avoid; Scotch weight wrong for burrata's cream.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Butternut Squash": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish leans against the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the malt-and-oak threads the squash bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; annual-release story wasted on salad.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Carrot Cake": "Glenfiddich 18 with carrot cake — Oloroso sherry-cask Speyside against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Oloroso dried fruit + cinnamon + nutmeg marry the cake's raisins and spice — the featured Speyside-carrot-cake match in the aged batch, edging even Balvenie 12 Am Oak.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Cheesecake": "Glenfiddich 18 with cheesecake — Oloroso + bourbon cask marriage against custard. Strong; Fiddich 18's dried-fruit frames the cheesecake with aged gravity; Balvenie 16 and Gran Cru 23 are the featured dessert matches.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Chilean Seabass": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Glenfiddich 18 on the steak course instead.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Chocolate Brownie": "Chocolate Brownie: warm chocolate meets Glenfiddich 18. Excellent; aged sherry-bourbon-cask Speyside brings dried-fruit-cocoa depth to the brownie at aged-Speyside register.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Chocolate Cake": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish finds neutral with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the malt-and-oak threads the chocolate cake, and the malt edge frames the dessert. Works; bonded weight a touch ambitious for the dessert.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Clam Chowder": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the malt-driven body wraps the chowder, and the oak threads the cream. Works; Marian McLain L.E.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Cowboy Ribeye": "Glenfiddich 18 with the cowboy ribeye — Oloroso + bourbon cask marriage against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Excellent; the sherry-cask fruit-and-spice depth is the featured Speyside-ribeye pairing — Fiddich 18 is built for fattier cuts where the lighter siblings feel under-specified.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Crab Cake": "Glenfiddich 18 with crab cake — premium aged Speyside against delicate crab. Avoid; Scotch wrong for seafood. Reach for a vodka or gin.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Creamed Spinach": "Glenfiddich 18 with creamed spinach — Oloroso sherry-cask Speyside against dairy-rich side. Strong; Fiddich 18's nutmeg-and-spice rides the cream with aged character.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Creamy Potato": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the scotch depth settles into the potato soup, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; collector-bottle doesn't drive.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Creme Brulee": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the scotch backbone matches the brulee, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; oak slightly over-specified for this dish.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Escargot": "Glenfiddich 18's caramel-cinnamon character lifts the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Faroe Island Salmon": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish smothers the salmon's rich oily flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a scotch. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Glenfiddich 18 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Filet Mignon": "Glenfiddich 18 with the filet — Oloroso sherry + bourbon cask marriage against tenderloin. Excellent; Fiddich 18's dried-fruit-and-spice depth frames the filet with aged Speyside gravitas — the premium Speyside-filet experience.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|French Onion": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish reads alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the malt-driven body wraps the French onion, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Grilled Caesar": "Glenfiddich 18 with the grilled Caesar — sherry-cask Speyside against charred romaine and anchovy. Strong; Fiddich 18's depth meets the char at premium register; Cragganmore 12's subtle smoke still leads the Speyside-Caesar pairing.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Gumbo": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish reads alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the aged-Speyside depth wraps the gumbo, and the sherry-finish frames the bowl. Works; AE Triple Cask meets the char at distinctive register.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish sits alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the scotch backbone matches the honey carrots, and the oak frames the caramelized sugar. Works; IW Harper 15 frames the two-cut plate at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|House Wedge": "Glenfiddich 18 with the House Wedge — Small Batch Reserve against iceberg and bleu. Works; Fiddich 18 is over-specified for the wedge.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Kansas City": "Glenfiddich 18 with the KC — Small Batch Reserve, Oloroso sherry cask + bourbon cask marriage, dried fruit + cinnamon + nutmeg + oak-spice depth. Excellent; Fiddich 18's Oloroso dried-fruit weight is the featured Speyside-KC pairing in the batch — the aged sherry-cask character is built to frame strip marbling where the 12's apple/pear and 14's vanilla can't.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Loaded Potato": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish reads alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the malt-and-oak threads the loaded potato soup, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; curated single-barrel covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Lobster Mac": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the malt-and-oak threads the lobster mac, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; Parker's Heritage 16th handles the richness at annual-release register.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Market Fish": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish swallows the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a scotch. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Glenfiddich 18 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Mocha Creme": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish sits alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the Highland register carries the mocha creme, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the intensity overpowers this dish.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Mushroom Bisque": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish sits alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the scotch backbone matches the mushroom bisque, and the oak balances the umami register. Works; HH 20 handles dessert density at collector register.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Mushrooms": "Glenfiddich 18 with mushrooms — Small Batch Reserve against earthy umami. Excellent; the Oloroso dried-fruit depth threads mushroom earthiness with aged character the lighter siblings can't match.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Peanut Butter Brownie: peanut butter and cocoa meet Small Batch Reserve. Works; Fiddich 18's dried-fruit handles the density; Balvenie 16's vanilla is still the featured match.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Porterhouse": "Glenfiddich 18 with the porterhouse — Oloroso + bourbon cask marriage against strip-and-filet. Strong; Fiddich 18's depth frames the two-cut plate with premium aged character.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Prime Tartare": "Glenfiddich 18's caramel-cinnamon character frames the tartare's raw beef and brine — the caramel-oak depth threads the savory plate, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Rainbow Trout": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish flattens the trout's delicate flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a scotch. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Glenfiddich 18 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Roast Half Chicken": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish finds neutral with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the roast chicken, and the smoke threads the plate. Works; premium proof overshoots delicacy.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish leans against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the scotch backbone matches the chickpea soup, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; JW Black handles the richness at premium-blend register.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Glenfiddich 18 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish reads alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the malt-driven body wraps the garlic spinach, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the side. Works; the Dylan-brand story is wasted on the salad.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Seafood Tower": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Glenfiddich 18 for the steak course.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Seared Scallops": "Glenfiddich 18 with seared scallops — Oloroso + bourbon cask against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Seasonal Soup": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish leans against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the malt-driven body wraps the seasonal soup, and the honey rounds the bowl. Works; AE CS handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Seasonal Vegetables": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish sits alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the malt-and-oak threads the seasonal vegetables, and the malt edge frames the side. Works; smooth gentle match.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Shrimp Bisque": "Glenfiddich 18 with shrimp bisque — sherry-cask Speyside against cream-shrimp soup. Works; Fiddich 18 rides the bisque at premium register.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Shrimp Cocktail": "Glenfiddich 18 with shrimp cocktail — Small Batch Reserve against cold shrimp. Avoid; Scotch wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Swordfish": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Glenfiddich 18 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|The Tomahawk": "Glenfiddich 18's caramel-cinnamon character finds register with the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the bourbon depth grips the marbled cut, and the caramel echoes the grilled char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Tomato Basil": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish reads alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the tomato basil, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; pour is a touch over-specified for this dish.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Truffle Fries": "Glenfiddich 18 with truffle fries — Small Batch Reserve against truffle-parmesan. Strong; the sherry-cask dried-fruit meets the earthy-rich with premium aged gravitas.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Glenfiddich 18 for the steak course.",
  "Glenfiddich 18|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the scotch backbone matches the curry, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the bowl. Works; aged character overshoots delicacy.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Asparagus": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the malt-driven body wraps the asparagus, and the smoke threads the side. Works; craft-blend covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with the au gratin — Cuvée-cask Speyside against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Strong; Gran Cru's refinement handles the richness at premium aged register.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Beignets": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the scotch backbone matches the beignets, and the honey rounds the dessert. Works; gentle composed match.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Bone Marrow": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with bone marrow — 23yr Cuvée-cask Speyside against umami fat. Works; Gran Cru's refinement sits alongside marrow but doesn't cut it; Fernet Branca remains the featured marrow pairing.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Bone-In Filet": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with the bone-in filet — Cuvée-cask-finished 23yr Speyside against tenderloin-with-bone. Excellent; Gran Cru's refined brioche-pastry character lifts the cut with unique champagne-cask elegance the other Speysides can't match.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Broccoli Cheddar": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Cuvée-finished 23-year Speyside luxury finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the scotch depth settles into the broccoli cheddar, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; boutique covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Broccolini": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Cuvée-finished 23-year Speyside luxury reads alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the scotch depth settles into the broccolini, and the malt edge frames the side. Works; JW Blue is over-specified for the side — save the rare-cask bottle for the protein course.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Brussels and Belly": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with Brussels + Belly — 23yr champagne-cask Speyside against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Gran Cru's brioche meets the glaze at refined register.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Burrata": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with burrata — 23yr champagne-cask Speyside against fresh dairy. Avoid; Scotch weight wrong for burrata — save the Gran Cru bottle.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Butternut Squash": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Cuvée-finished 23-year Speyside luxury leans against the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the scotch depth settles into the squash bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; BTAC story wasted on salad.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Carrot Cake": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with carrot cake — French Cuvée cask finish against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Gran Cru's brioche-pastry notes marry the cake's raisins and spice with champagne-style pastry elegance — unique to this 23yr expression.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Cheesecake": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with cheesecake — champagne-style Cuvée-cask Speyside against custard dessert. Excellent; Gran Cru's brioche-apple-blossom finish is the featured Speyside-cheesecake pairing in the aged batch — the pastry character threads custard with champagne-cask elegance no other Speyside replicates.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Chilean Seabass": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Cuvée-finished 23-year Speyside luxury overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 for the steak course.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Chocolate Brownie": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23: Cuvée-finished 23-year Speyside luxury. Excellent on chocolate brownie; champagne-cask depth frames cocoa at Speyside-luxury register.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Chocolate Cake": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the Highland register carries the chocolate cake, and the malt edge frames the dessert. Works; annual-release wasted on salad.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Clam Chowder": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the scotch backbone matches the chowder, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; milestone-edition over-specified.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Cowboy Ribeye": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with the cowboy ribeye — 23yr champagne-cask Speyside against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Strong; Gran Cru's refinement is over-specified for ribeye — Fiddich 18's Oloroso depth is better suited.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Crab Cake": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with crab cake — rare-release 23yr Speyside against delicate crab. Avoid; Scotch wrong for seafood — save the Gran Cru bottle.",
