  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Creamy Potato": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the malt-and-oak threads the potato soup, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; aging wasted on the salad.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Creme Brulee": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the scotch backbone matches the brulee, and the oak threads the cream. Works; the aging is wasted on the salad.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Escargot": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's bold almond-apple character holds the line with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Faroe Island Salmon": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Cuvée-finished 23-year Speyside luxury overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a scotch. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Filet Mignon": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with the filet — 23 years matured, finished in French Cuvée (champagne) oak casks for distinctive brioche, pastry, and apple-blossom notes. Excellent; Gran Cru's champagne-style finish is unlike any other Speyside in the cluster — its elegant brioche-pastry character frames tenderloin as the thinking-drinker's premium Speyside-filet pairing.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|French Onion": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the malt-driven body wraps the French onion, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; the complex profile is over-specified for this dish.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Grilled Caesar": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with the grilled Caesar — champagne-style 23yr Speyside against charred romaine and anchovy. Strong; Gran Cru's brioche-pastry meets the char at refined register.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Gumbo": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the malt-and-oak threads the gumbo, and the oak-and-smoke underlines the bowl. Works; Remus 15 handles dessert density at Gatsby-tribute register.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the honey carrots, and the oak threads the caramelized sugar. Works; boutique character slightly over-specified.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|House Wedge": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with the House Wedge — French Cuvée-cask Speyside against iceberg and bleu. Works; Gran Cru's rare-release character is wasted on the wedge — save the pour for filet or dessert.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Kansas City": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with the KC — Cuvée-cask 23yr Speyside against an 18oz strip. Strong; Gran Cru handles the strip with refined 23yr character, though Fiddich 18's Oloroso dried-fruit is the featured Speyside-KC match — Gran Cru's elegance is better spent on the filet.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Loaded Potato": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the Highland register carries the loaded potato soup, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; curated single-barrel covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Lobster Mac": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the scotch depth settles into the lobster mac, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; Vermont-brand character doesn't drive.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Market Fish": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Cuvée-finished 23-year Speyside luxury overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a scotch. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 for the steak course.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Mocha Creme": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the scotch depth settles into the mocha creme, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; Voyage 23 frames the two-cut plate at ocean-finish register.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Mushroom Bisque": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the malt-driven body wraps the mushroom bisque, and the oak underlines the umami weight. Works; JW Black handles the richness at premium-blend register.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Mushrooms": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with mushrooms — French Cuvée cask finish against earthy umami. Excellent; Gran Cru's refined 23yr character threads mushroom earthiness with unique champagne-cask lift.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with the PB brownie — French Cuvée-cask Speyside against peanut butter and cocoa. Works; Gran Cru is over-specified for PB brownie — reach for Balvenie 16 if the guest wants aged Speyside with this dessert.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Porterhouse": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with the porterhouse — French Cuvée cask finish against strip-and-filet. Strong; Gran Cru's elegance frames the two-cut plate at rare-release register.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Prime Tartare": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami: the malt-and-oak threads the tartare, and the oak threads the umami plate. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Rainbow Trout": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Cuvée-finished 23-year Speyside luxury overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a scotch. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 for the steak course.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Roast Half Chicken": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the scotch backbone matches the roast chicken, and the honey rounds the plate. Works; bonded weight pushes past the soup's register slightly.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the chickpea soup, and the honey rounds the bowl. Works; annual-release covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Cuvée-finished 23-year Speyside luxury smothers the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 for the steak course.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the malt-driven body wraps the garlic spinach, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the side. Works; IW Harper 15 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Seafood Tower": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Cuvée-finished 23-year Speyside luxury smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Seared Scallops": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with seared scallops — Cuvée-cask Speyside against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Seasonal Soup": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the scotch backbone matches the seasonal soup, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the bowl. Works; retailer-pick wasted on salad.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Seasonal Vegetables": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the Highland register carries the seasonal vegetables, and the malt edge frames the side. Works; the pour's brightness is a gentle counterpoint to the dessert's richness.",
