  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Shrimp Cocktail": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with shrimp cocktail — rare-release Speyside against cold shrimp. Avoid; Scotch wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Swordfish": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Cuvée-finished 23-year Speyside luxury overwhelms the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|The Tomahawk": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's bold almond-apple character sits with the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the whiskey weight settles into the bone-in cut, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Tomato Basil": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Cuvée-finished 23-year Speyside luxury sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the scotch depth settles into the tomato basil, and the malt edge frames the bowl. Works; boutique character doesn't drive.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Truffle Fries": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with truffle fries — 23yr Cuvée-cask Speyside against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Gran Cru's refined brioche-pastry character meets the earthy-rich with champagne-style polish at rare-release register.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Cuvée-finished 23-year Speyside luxury swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 for the steak course.",
  "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character leans against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the scotch backbone matches the curry, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; curated single-barrel covers both cuts without standing out.",
