  "Glenglassaugh 12|Faroe Island Salmon": "Glenglassaugh 12's Highland-scotch character overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a scotch. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Glenglassaugh 12 for the steak course.",
