  "Glenglassaugh 12|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Glenglassaugh 12's Highland-scotch character leans against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the malt-driven body wraps the chickpea soup, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; the Dylan-brand story is wasted on the salad.",
  "Glenglassaugh 12|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Glenglassaugh 12's Highland-scotch character overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; one of those is the move. Glenglassaugh 12 belongs on the steak course.",
