  "Glenglassaugh 12|Seafood Tower": "Glenglassaugh 12's Highland-scotch character overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit weight crowds the delicate shellfish — no acid to clean the brine. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Glenglassaugh 12 for the steak course.",
