  "Glenglassaugh 12|Truffle Fries": "Glenglassaugh 12 with truffle fries — recently-reopened Sandend-coast Highland against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Glenglassaugh 12's tropical-fruit meets the earthy-rich with distinctive coastal-Highland character.",
  "Glenglassaugh 12|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Glenglassaugh 12's Highland-scotch character flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Glenglassaugh 12 for the steak course.",
  "Glenglassaugh 12|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Glenglassaugh 12's Highland-scotch character leans against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the scotch backbone matches the curry, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; single-barrel depth gives the dessert more than Small Batch.",
