  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Mocha Creme": "20-year oak-cask oxidative Tawny — Graham's step-up, concentrated dried fruit, roasted hazelnut, orange peel, silky long finish. The roasted hazelnut echoes espresso-roast directly and the orange peel lifts yolk-cream custard. Strong step-up Tawny for mocha creme — Vintage Port's intensity edges higher on espresso.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Mushroom Bisque": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth doubles down on the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream -- sweet wine on cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — heavy, no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a dessert wine. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Graham's 20 Year Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Mushrooms": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth clashes with the mushrooms' earthy umami weight -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Los Vecinos Mezcal, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a dessert wine. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Graham's 20 Year Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Peanut Butter Brownie": "* Graham's 20 Year Tawny -- aged tawny port, nutty-caramel, Douro classic. The dessert-wine register matches the PB brownie, and the noble-rot register brightens the dessert. One of the more interesting dessert pairings on the list. Gold standard; the pairing that defines the moment.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Porterhouse": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth clashes with the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character -- dessert wine is post-meal — wrong register for the steak course. The plate deserves Odette Cabernet Sauvignon, Weller 12 Year, or Domaine du Grand Tinel, not a dessert wine. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Graham's 20 Year Tawny for another course.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Prime Tartare": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth clashes with the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Belvedere Vodka, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Graham's 20 Year Tawny belongs on the steak course.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Rainbow Trout": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- dessert wine on a main protein is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Graham's 20 Year Tawny belongs on the steak course.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Roast Half Chicken": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth buries the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast -- dessert wine on chicken is wrong course — sugar smothers the herbed-skin frame. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Graham's 20 Year Tawny lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth clashes with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Graham's 20 Year Tawny lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth smothers the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the wine's sweetness buries the gentle flesh's lift. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Graham's 20 Year Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth clashes with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not a dessert wine. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Graham's 20 Year Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Seafood Tower": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth clashes with the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Graham's 20 Year Tawny lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Seared Scallops": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth clashes with the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Graham's 20 Year Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Seasonal Soup": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth clashes with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build -- honeyed sugar on savory broth jars — wrong direction for the course. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Graham's 20 Year Tawny on the steak course instead.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Seasonal Vegetables": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth clashes with the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate -- sweet wine on green vegetable is wrong direction — needs crisp white. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, not a dessert wine. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Graham's 20 Year Tawny lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Shrimp Bisque": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth doubles down on the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- sweet wine on cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — heavy, no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Graham's 20 Year Tawny lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Shrimp Cocktail": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- dessert sugar on cold shellfish is wrong direction — needs sparkling or Sancerre. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Graham's 20 Year Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Swordfish": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth flattens the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- sweet wine dulls the sear's clean char — savory main deserves a dry pour. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Graham's 20 Year Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|The Tomahawk": "Never pair Graham's 20 Year Tawny with Tomahawk — sweet step-up tawny buries the massive 36oz bone-in ribeye and smoky char clashes with twenty-year concentrated fruit. Lead with Scavino Barolo or Beaucastel Châteauneuf. Tawny is a finishing pour.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Tomato Basil": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth clashes with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid -- honeyed sugar on savory broth jars — wrong direction for the course. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Le Garenne Rosé, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Graham's 20 Year Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Truffle Fries": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth flattens the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- dessert sugar on starch is wrong-course energy for the supporting plate. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Graham's 20 Year Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- dessert wine on a main protein is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a dessert wine. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Graham's 20 Year Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 20 Year Tawny|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth clashes with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Le Garenne Rosé, not a dessert wine. Avoid; one of those is the move. Graham's 20 Year Tawny lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Asparagus": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- sweet wine on green vegetable is wrong direction — needs crisp white. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a dessert wine. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Graham's 2017 Vintage Port lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight doubles down on the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- sweet wine and a dairy side compound the richness — dessert energy on savory plate. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Beignets": "2017 declared-vintage Port — Graham's bottle-aged, dense inky, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, powerful structured. The dense inky structure overwhelms hot choux-fried dough and powdered-sugar simplicity. Strong Vintage Port for beignets — Tawny's lighter caramel lift sits cleaner on the airy bite.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Bone Marrow": "Never pair Graham's 2017 Vintage Port with bone marrow — dense inky sugar drowns roasted-marrow unctuousness and the declared-vintage intensity clashes with beefy-bone savory. Lead with Scavino Barolo or Lail Daniel Cuvée. Vintage Port is a dessert pour, not an appetizer.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Bone-In Filet": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- dessert wine belongs after the meal, not alongside the steak. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Graham's 2017 Vintage Port belongs on another course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Broccoli Cheddar": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Broccolini": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the broccolini's tender green stalks -- sweet wine on green vegetable is wrong direction — needs crisp white. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a dessert wine. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Graham's 2017 Vintage Port belongs on the steak course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Brussels and Belly": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight doubles down on Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet wine and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no foil. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Burrata": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight doubles down on the burrata's fresh basil-tomato-cream delicacy -- sweet wine and fresh dairy compound the richness with no foil. The plate deserves Il Colle Prosecco Superiore, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, not a dessert wine. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Butternut Squash": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Carrot Cake": "2017 declared-vintage Port — Graham's bottle-aged, dense inky, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, powerful structured. The violet lifts allspice-cinnamon aromatics and the dark chocolate plays with cream-cheese frosting. Strong Vintage Port for carrot cake — Tawny's spice-on-spice match fits softer.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Cheesecake": "2017 declared-vintage Port — Graham's bottle-aged, dense inky, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, powerful structured. The blackcurrant lifts cream-cheese density and the dark chocolate plays with graham-cracker brown-sugar. Peak Vintage Port for cheesecake — declared-vintage structure on the water-bath bake. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Chilean Seabass": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- dessert sugar refuses the rich-fish course — needs acid, not sweetness. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Graham's 2017 Vintage Port lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Chocolate Brownie": "* Graham's 2017 Vintage Port -- vintage port, structured dark-fruit, cellar-worthy. The Sauternes-or-Port body carries the brownie, and the apricot-and-marmalade note underlines the dessert. Serious peak dessert pour. Gold standard; the headline call at the table.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Chocolate Cake": "* Graham's 2017 Vintage Port -- vintage port, structured dark-fruit, cellar-worthy. The dessert-wine register matches the chocolate cake, and the noble-rot register brightens the dessert. One of the great pairings on the list. Gold standard; the pairing that defines the moment.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Clam Chowder": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight doubles down on the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- sweet wine on cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — heavy, no contrast. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Graham's 2017 Vintage Port lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Cowboy Ribeye": "Never pair Graham's 2017 Vintage Port with Cowboy Ribeye — declared-vintage structure is built for chocolate, not grilled-beef protein char, and the residual sugar clashes with marbled-ribeye savory. Lead with Silver Oak Cabernet or Caymus for the 26oz bone-in. Save the Port for dessert.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Crab Cake": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight overwhelms the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- dessert sugar on cold shellfish is wrong direction — needs sparkling or Sancerre. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not a dessert wine. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Creamed Spinach": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight doubles down on the creamed spinach's rich bechamel-laced greens -- sweet wine and a dairy side compound the richness — dessert energy on savory plate. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Weller 12 Year, not a dessert wine. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Creamy Potato": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a dessert wine. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Creme Brulee": "2017 declared-vintage Port — Graham's bottle-aged, dense inky, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, powerful structured. The blackcurrant plays with torched-sugar crust, but the dense inky structure reads heavy against vanilla-custard delicacy. Strong Vintage Port for creme brulee — Tawny's toffee fits the caramel harder.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Escargot": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port on the steak course instead.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Faroe Island Salmon": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- dessert wine on a main protein is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a dessert wine. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port on the steak course instead.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Filet Mignon": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight overwhelms the filet's lean buttery tenderness -- sweet wine smothers the lean cut's buttery delicacy. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Maker's Mark Cellar Aged, or Yamazaki 18 Year, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for another course.",
