  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- sweet wine on green vegetable is wrong direction — needs crisp white. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Seafood Tower": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Seared Scallops": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Seasonal Soup": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Seasonal Vegetables": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Reserve the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Shrimp Bisque": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight doubles down on the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- sweet wine on cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — heavy, no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Graham's 2017 Vintage Port lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Shrimp Cocktail": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- dessert sugar on cold shellfish is wrong direction — needs sparkling or Sancerre. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port on the steak course instead.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Swordfish": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- dessert wine on a main protein is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|The Tomahawk": "Never pair Graham's 2017 Vintage Port with Tomahawk — powerful bottle-aged structure buries the massive 36oz bone-in ribeye and the residual sugar fights smoky char. Lead with Scavino Barolo or Beaucastel Châteauneuf for the grand cut. Vintage Port lives at dessert.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Tomato Basil": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid -- honeyed sugar on savory broth jars — wrong direction for the course. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Le Garenne Rosé, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Truffle Fries": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- dessert wine on a main protein is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a dessert wine. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port on the steak course instead.",
  "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth -- honeyed sugar on savory broth jars — wrong direction for the course. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Le Garenne Rosé, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Gran Patron Platinum|Asparagus": "Gran Patron Platinum's silver-spirit lift with agave-citrus edge leans against the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the unaged blanco body cuts the asparagus, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Gran Patron Platinum|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Gran Patron Platinum's clean silver register leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the silver-spirit register lifts the au gratin, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Gran Patron Platinum|Beignets": "Gran Patron Platinum's silver-spirit lift with agave-citrus edge reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the unaged body brightens the beignets, and the unaged-cane note plays against the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Gran Patron Platinum|Bone Marrow": "Gran Patron Platinum with bone marrow — refined blanco against umami fat. Avoid; marrow overwhelms blanco at any tier.",
  "Gran Patron Platinum|Bone-In Filet": "Gran Patron Platinum's agave-citrus character lifts the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the light body is outweighed by the cut, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; the call lands cleanly.",
  "Gran Patron Platinum|Broccoli Cheddar": "Gran Patron Platinum's blanco-tequila or blanco-tequila register sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the unaged body brightens the broccoli cheddar, and the unaged-cane note plays against the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Gran Patron Platinum|Broccolini": "Gran Patron Platinum's clean silver register reads alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the broccolini, and the bright blanco register underlines the side. Works; refined craft composes cleanly.",
  "Gran Patron Platinum|Brussels and Belly": "Gran Patron Platinum's unaged silver-spirit body sits alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the silver-spirit register lifts the pork-belly plate, and the unaged-cane note plays against the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Gran Patron Platinum|Burrata": "Gran Patron Platinum with burrata — premium Patron against fresh dairy. The smooth triple-distilled agave lifts the burrata with refined luxury. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Gran Patron Platinum|Butternut Squash": "Gran Patron Platinum's blanco-tequila or blanco-tequila register reads alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the unaged body brightens the squash bisque, and the unaged-cane note plays against the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Gran Patron Platinum|Carrot Cake": "Gran Patron Platinum's silver-spirit lift with agave-citrus edge leans against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the silver-tequila register lifts the carrot cake, and the agave-citrus thread frames the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Gran Patron Platinum|Cheesecake": "Gran Patron Platinum's silver-spirit lift with agave-citrus edge sits alongside the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the unaged body brightens the cheesecake, and the agave-citrus thread frames the dessert. Works; the call holds at register.",
