  "Gray Whale Gin|Truffle Fries": "Gray Whale Gin's bold citrus-herbal botanicals leans against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Gray Whale Gin|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Gray Whale Gin's gin lift with floral-and-pepper leans against the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the floral edge frames the tuna, and the juniper threads the plate. Strong; Gray Whale's California terroir meets the bleu at ocean-conservation register.",
  "Gray Whale Gin|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Gray Whale Gin's bold citrus-herbal botanicals sits beside the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus brightens the spice. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Green Chartreuse|Asparagus": "Green Chartreuse's amaro-bitter register reads alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the herbal cut works the asparagus, and the amaro backbone frames the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Green Chartreuse|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Green Chartreuse's cask-strength herbal-high-proof sweetness holds with the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the sweet character sits at digestif register, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Green Chartreuse|Beignets": "Beignets: warm sugar-dusted pastry meets Green Chartreuse. Excellent; the herbal-bitter-complex digestif cuts through sugar-and-fried-dough at 55% register — textbook green-digestif move.",
