  "Green Chartreuse|Lobster Mac": "Green Chartreuse's bittersweet rhubarb-and-orange edge reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the herbal cut works the lobster mac, and the amaro backbone frames the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Green Chartreuse|Market Fish": "Green Chartreuse's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- aperitivo bitterness fights gentle flesh without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Green Chartreuse for the steak course.",
