  "Gumbo|Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark": "Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the oak depth lays under the gumbo, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; IW Harper 15 handles dessert density at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Gumbo|Bowman Brothers Small Batch": "Bowman Brothers Small Batch's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the caramel-spice register matches the gumbo, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Gumbo|Bowmore 12": "Bowmore 12's lighter-Islay peat character reads alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the lighter peat meets the gumbo, and the sea-salt frames the bowl. Works; EHT Full Proof handles the richness at historic Kentucky register.",
  "Gumbo|Braida Montebruna Barbera": "Piedmont Monferrato Barbera d'Asti — juicy dark cherry, blackberry, high acid, low tannin. The high acid cuts gumbo's dark-roux fat and the juicy fruit plays against andouille-shrimp spice. Strong Barbera for gumbo — Italian food-wine acidity on the Cajun classic.",
  "Gumbo|Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Gumbo|Broccolini": "The gumbo and the broccolini -- the bright cuts through the spice cleanly. Works; sequence them or share the table, the call holds either way.",
  "Gumbo|Bruichladdich": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay sits alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the malt-and-oak threads the gumbo, and the malt edge frames the bowl. Works; the pour's complexity is underused by the salad.",
  "Gumbo|Brussels and Belly": "The gumbo and Brussels + Belly on the same meal -- heat lifts the rich course, the table earns the warmer note. Works; sequence or share, the build holds.",
  "Gumbo|Buffalo Trace": "Buffalo Trace's rounded vanilla-and-toffee character finds neutral with the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the vanilla settles into the gumbo, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; BIB structure overshoots the dessert's delicacy.",
  "Gumbo|Buffalo Trace Cream": "Buffalo Trace Cream's sweet liqueur character clashes with the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Buffalo Trace Cream belongs on the steak course.",
  "Gumbo|Bulleit Bourbon": "Bulleit Bourbon's high-rye spice-forward depth leans against the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the caramel-spice register matches the gumbo, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; IW Harper 15 handles dessert density at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Gumbo|Burrata": "The burrata with the gumbo -- the burrata's fresh basil-tomato-cream delicacy meets the gumbo's spiced creole stew: spice plays against the delicate, the contrast holds. Works; both opening courses earn their place.",
  "Gumbo|Cade Cabernet Sauvignon": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character overwhelms the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Gumbo|Camarena Tequila": "Camarena Tequila's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the añejo register carries the gumbo, and the caramel-agave register brightens the bowl. Works; the 70th's smoothness is an unusual but interesting counterpoint.",
  "Gumbo|Campari": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Gumbo|Canadian Club": "Canadian Club's workhorse Canadian blend sits alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the blended whisky body wraps the gumbo, and the light caramel edge frames the bowl. Works; AE CS meets the char at premium wine-finish register.",
  "Gumbo|Canadian Club 43 Year": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character finds neutral with the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the Canadian whisky weight matches the gumbo, and the soft profile rounds the bowl. Works; the Millennium's register overshoots the dessert's.",
  "Gumbo|Captain Morgan Rum": "Captain Morgan Rum's light-rum register with cane and citrus lift mis-pairs with the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- the light spirit doesn't add to the soup-salad course — neutral but wrong. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not a light spirit. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Captain Morgan Rum belongs on the steak course.",
  "Gumbo|Caribou Crossing": "Caribou Crossing's Canadian whisky character sits alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the blended whisky body wraps the gumbo, and the easy Canadian register softens the bowl. Works; polished aged character doesn't drive.",
  "Gumbo|Carrot Cake": "Gumbo and the carrot cake -- different registers compose without clash. Works; sequence them as opener and close or share the table, no clash.",
  "Gumbo|Casa LBV Port": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- honeyed sugar on savory broth jars — wrong direction for the course. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not a dessert wine. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Gumbo|Casamigos Mezcal": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character clashes with the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- mezcal smoke is wrong register for the soup-salad course. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not a mezcal. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Casamigos Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Gumbo|Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon": "Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon's cocoa-mocha velvety-tannin opulence jars against the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Gumbo|Chambord": "Chambord's sweet liqueur character clashes with the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not a digestif. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Chambord for the steak course.",
  "Gumbo|Cheesecake": "The gumbo and the cheesecake -- the gumbo's spiced creole stew bookends with the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Gumbo|Chilean Seabass": "The seabass after the gumbo -- the pan-finished seabass meets quietly the andouille-and-chicken stew, and the rye spice cuts the rich plate. Works; the opener sits without competing.",
  "Gumbo|Chocolate Brownie": "The gumbo and the brownie -- the gumbo's spiced creole stew bookends with the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Gumbo|Chocolate Cake": "The gumbo alongside the chocolate cake -- the courses pull from different keys but share the table cleanly. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Gumbo|Chopin Vodka": "Chopin Vodka's bold char-cream neutrality leans against the gumbo's spiced Creole stew — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Gumbo|Christian Bros Brandy": "Christian Bros Brandy's barrel-aged cognac character finds neutral with the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the eau-de-vie body carries the gumbo, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; Ferrand's craft character handles the richness.",
  "Gumbo|Château Batailley": "Château Batailley's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Château Batailley for the steak course.",
  "Gumbo|Château Beaucastel": "Château Beaucastel's old-world Châteauneuf-du-Pape gravitas jars against the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Château Beaucastel for the steak course.",
  "Gumbo|Château Gombaude-Guillot": "Gumbo: the Gumbo's smoky, spiced heartiness with tomato and bold seasoning meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. Bold red meets rich, caramelized depth — the wine's dark fruit threads through the savory base. A winning warmth-on-warmth pairing. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
