  "HDW 100 Vodka|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "HDW 100 Vodka's silky vodka body reads register-aligned with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the cold-distilled body wraps the tuna, and the clean register frames the plate. Strong; HDW 100 Vodka on the tuna -- workhorse pairing, no surprises.",
  "HDW 100 Vodka|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "HDW 100 Vodka's char-herbal neutrality plays cleanly against the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Asparagus": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character leans against the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the Mizunara-influenced register sits with the asparagus, and the Japanese-craft balance underlines the side. Works; cleaner than wheated versions but not exceptional.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the Mizunara-influenced register sits with the au gratin, and the oak threads the cream. Works; Fortuna's NZ terroir meets the glaze at distinctive register.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Beignets": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the precise Japanese craft body wraps the beignets, and the precision rounds the dessert. Works; premium single-barrel wasted on the salad.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Bone Marrow": "Hakushu 12 Year -- Suntory Hakushu, lightly peated, forest. The lightly-peated Hakushu meets the rich marrow, and the forest-floor frames the starter. Strong; more body than White Label brings, but still underpowered vs; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Bone-In Filet": "Hakushu 12 with the bone-in filet — Japanese Alps single malt against tenderloin-with-bone. Excellent; Hakushu's lightly-peated pine-forest profile frames the cut with Forest-Distillery distinction.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Broccoli Cheddar": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the restrained whisky body threads the broccoli cheddar, and the oak softens the cream. Works; complexity wasted on salad.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Broccolini": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character sits alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the lightly-peated Hakushu meets the broccolini, and the forest-floor frames the side. Works; the pour's assertiveness is a bit much for the soup but doesn't clash.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Brussels and Belly": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character sits alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the Japanese whisky balance frames the pork-belly plate, and the green-fruit edge brightens the side. Works; the blend's complexity is underused by the salad; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Burrata": "Hakushu 12 with burrata — lightly-peated Japanese single malt against fresh dairy. Works; Hakushu's crisp-green and subtle peat can sit with burrata at edge-of-category register; not featured but distinctive.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Butternut Squash": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the Japanese whisky balance frames the squash bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; Fortuna handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Carrot Cake": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character reads alongside the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the precise Japanese craft body wraps the carrot cake, and the precision rounds the dessert. Works; accessible gentle match.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Cheesecake": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character finds neutral with the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the Mizunara-influenced register sits with the cheesecake, and the oak threads the cream. Works; doesn't drive.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Chilean Seabass": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character sits alongside the seabass' buttery seabass flesh: the Japanese whisky balance frames the seabass, and the umami-tinged finish frames the plate. Works; JD 12 handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Chocolate Brownie": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character sits alongside the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight: the elegant Suntory/Nikka register matches the brownie, and the Japanese-craft balance underlines the dessert. Works; own-plus-sourced over-specified.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Chocolate Cake": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character reads alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the elegant Suntory/Nikka register matches the chocolate cake, and the green-fruit edge brightens the dessert. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Clam Chowder": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the elegant Suntory/Nikka register matches the chowder, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; the complex character gives the dessert a refined frame.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Cowboy Ribeye": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character finds neutral with the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness: the Mizunara-influenced register sits with the cap-fat ribeye, and the green-fruit edge brightens the cut. Works; own-plus-sourced over-specified.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Crab Cake": "Hakushu 12 with crab cake — Forest-Distillery Japanese single malt against delicate lump crab. Works; Hakushu's lightly-peated character is at the edge of crab-possible Japanese whiskies — not featured but distinctive.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Creamed Spinach": "Hakushu 12 with creamed spinach — Japanese Alps single malt against dairy-rich side. Works; Hakushu's crisp-green character rides the cream at distinctive register.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Creamy Potato": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character sits alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the lightly-peated Hakushu meets the potato soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; BH Red Wine Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Creme Brulee": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character reads alongside the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the lightly-peated Hakushu meets the brulee, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Escargot": "Hakushu 12 Year -- Suntory Hakushu, lightly peated, forest. The lightly-peated Hakushu meets the buttered escargot, and the forest-floor frames the starter. Strong; JW Blue's luxury character frames the two-cut plate at collector register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Faroe Island Salmon": "Hakushu 12 with the salmon — Japanese single malt with subtle peat against oily salmon. Excellent; Hakushu's crisp-green + subtle-smoke character frames fish — the pine-forest notes marry salmon's oiliness with Forest-Distillery distinction.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Filet Mignon": "Hakushu 12 with the filet — Suntory single malt from the \"Forest Distillery\" in the Japanese Alps, lightly peated with crisp-green and pine-forest notes. Excellent; Hakushu's Forest-Distillery character frames tenderloin with Japanese-single-malt distinction — the subtle peat + forest notes are unlike anything Scotland makes.",
