  "Hakushu 12 Year|Rainbow Trout": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character finds neutral with the trout's delicate flesh: the precise Japanese craft body wraps the trout, and the green-fruit edge brightens the plate. Works; extended-aged home-state pour wasted on salad.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Roast Half Chicken": "Hakushu 12 with the chicken — Suntory \"Forest Distillery\" single malt against roasted poultry. Strong; Hakushu's crisp-green + subtle peat frames chicken at distinctive single-malt register.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character reads alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the Mizunara-influenced register sits with the chickpea soup, and the Japanese-craft balance underlines the bowl. Works; bonded weight pushes slightly past the soup.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character sits alongside the halibut's salt-cured flesh: the restrained whisky body threads the halibut, and the Japanese-craft balance underlines the plate. Works; Caribbean Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character sits alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the restrained whisky body threads the garlic spinach, and the precision rounds the side. Works; boutique covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Seafood Tower": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character finds neutral with the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the Mizunara-influenced register sits with the seafood tower, and the Japanese-craft balance underlines the starter. Works; premium proof overshoots delicacy.",
  "Hakushu 12 Year|Seared Scallops": "Hakushu 12 with seared scallops — Japanese Alps lightly-peated single malt against scallop delicacy. Excellent; Hakushu's crisp-green + subtle peat is delicate enough to sit with scallops where most peated whiskies can't — Forest-Distillery lightness is the category advantage here.",
