  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Asparagus": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the bourbon body sits with the asparagus, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the side. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for the side — save the collector bottle for the protein course.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with au gratin potatoes — 88.9-proof BT single-barrel against cheese-and-cream. Strong; Blanton's-mash character at premium register.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Beignets": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the caramel-spice register matches the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; bonded weight pushes past the soup's register slightly.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Bone Marrow": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with bone marrow — BT single-barrel against umami fat. Strong; the complex profile is capable but the marrow's intensity earns Blanton's Gold or E.H. Taylor.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Bone-In Filet": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's crisp oak-vanilla character frames the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the whiskey character holds register with the tenderloin, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Broccoli Cheddar": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the bourbon backbone carries the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; smooth character is slightly over-specified for this dish.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Broccolini": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the bourbon backbone carries the broccolini, and the oak-and-spice register settles the side. Works; X Commandments story wasted on salad.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Brussels and Belly": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with Brussels + Belly — BT single-barrel meets maple-glazed pork belly. The complex profile cuts the glaze with Blanton's-adjacent character. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Burrata": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with burrata — fresh dairy against BT single-barrel. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Butternut Squash": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the squash bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; pour slightly over-specified for this dish.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Carrot Cake": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with carrot cake — BT single-barrel against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; the complex profile is slightly over-specified for the dessert.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Cheesecake": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with cheesecake — BT single-barrel against clean custard. Works; complex profile overshoots the dessert's delicacy.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Chilean Seabass": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon weight needs red meat, not the salmon's already-rich oils. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel on the steak course instead.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Chocolate Brownie": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with the chocolate brownie — 88.9-proof BT single-barrel against cocoa. Works; the complex profile meets the brownie cleanly.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Chocolate Cake": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the bourbon weight handles the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the distinctive character is underused by the salad's simplicity.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Clam Chowder": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon body sits with the chowder, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; premium KO story wasted on salad.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Cowboy Ribeye": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with the Cowboy Ribeye — BT single-barrel against cap fat. The 88.9-proof complexity handles the ribeye cleanly; a quieter alternative to Blanton's Original at the same distillery. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Crab Cake": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with crab cake — BT single-barrel against delicate crab. Avoid; pour a crisp white wine.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Creamed Spinach": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with creamed spinach — BT single-barrel against dairy. Strong; complex character at matched register.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Creamy Potato": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the brown-spirit warmth threads the potato soup, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; boutique-release covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Creme Brulee": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the oak depth lays under the brulee, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; boutique character gives the dessert a craft frame.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Escargot": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits at register with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the bourbon backbone carries the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; the annual-release complexity is capable but single-distillery premium bourbons bring more focused character; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Faroe Island Salmon": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel for the steak course.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Filet Mignon": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with the filet — Buffalo Trace single-barrel using the same mash bill as Blanton's. 88.9 proof, rich-complex; a BT single-barrel that's quieter in the market than Blanton's but carries the same distillery DNA. A distinct BT single-barrel filet pour. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|French Onion": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the bourbon depth settles into the French onion, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Grilled Caesar": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with the grilled Caesar — Blanton's-mash BT against charred romaine. Works; the pour is slightly too restrained to drive the Caesar.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Gumbo": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the gumbo, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the bourbon body sits with the honey carrots, and the oak threads the caramelized sugar. Works; IW Harper 15 handles dessert density at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|House Wedge": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with the House Wedge — BT single-barrel against iceberg and bleu. Works; the complex character is wasted on the salad.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Kansas City": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with the KC — BT single-barrel against the strip's marbling. The same mash as Blanton's but at 88.9 proof; carries the strip with restrained single-barrel character. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Loaded Potato": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the bourbon depth settles into the loaded potato soup, and the caramel softens the cream. Works; the toast adds a warmth the dessert can accept.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Lobster Mac": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the lobster mac, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; save the bottle for the protein course — a soup is wrong for a $200 pour.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Market Fish": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel belongs on the steak course.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Mocha Creme": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the brown-spirit warmth threads the mocha creme, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Mushroom Bisque": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the bourbon depth settles into the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Mushrooms": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with the mushrooms — BT single-barrel against earthy umami. The rich-complex profile layers into mushroom depth at the Blanton's-adjacent register. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with the PB brownie — Blanton's-mash BT against peanut butter and cocoa. Works; the complex character gives the dessert a refined frame.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Porterhouse": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with the porterhouse — BT single-barrel across strip and filet. Strong; 88.9-proof balance covers both cuts cleanly.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Prime Tartare": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami: the bourbon depth settles into the tartare, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; boutique character covers the cut with retailer-label authority; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Rainbow Trout": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Roast Half Chicken": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the bourbon depth settles into the roast chicken, and the vanilla softens the plate. Works; premium proof overpowers this dish.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the oak depth lays under the chickpea soup, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel for the steak course.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the bourbon depth settles into the garlic spinach, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Seafood Tower": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel on the steak course instead.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Seared Scallops": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 88.9-proof BT single-barrel. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Seasonal Soup": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the bourbon depth settles into the seasonal soup, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; single-barrel depth gives the dessert more than Small Batch.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Seasonal Vegetables": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the bourbon depth settles into the seasonal vegetables, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; curated single-barrel covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Shrimp Bisque": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; save the bottle for the protein course — a soup is wrong for a $200 pour.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Shrimp Cocktail": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against BT single-barrel. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Swordfish": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel for the steak course.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|The Tomahawk": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with the Tomahawk — 88.9-proof BT single-barrel against bone-in ribeye. Strong; scale pushes against the pour — Blanton's Gold, E.H. Taylor, or Henry McKenna 10 BIB are stronger Tomahawk calls.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Tomato Basil": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the bourbon body sits with the tomato basil, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Truffle Fries": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with truffle fries — Blanton's-mash BT single-barrel against truffle-parmesan. The complex profile gives the side a BT single-barrel frame distinct from the everyday bourbons. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the bourbon body sits with the curry, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; the Dylan-brand story is wasted on the salad.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Asparagus": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality finds neutral with the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the neutral profile sits with the light side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality stays alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the floral notes lift the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Beignets": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a vodka. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hangar 1 Vodka belongs on the steak course.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Bone Marrow": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality holds with the marrow's umami-fat depth — the clean profile cleans the rich starter without crowding, and the floral notes lift the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Bone-In Filet": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crystalline neutrality underclubs the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- vodka is too neutral to carry any prime cut. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a vodka. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Hangar 1 Vodka on another course instead.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Broccoli Cheddar": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the floral notes lift the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Broccolini": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality leans against the broccolini's tender green — the neutral profile sits with the light side. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Brussels and Belly": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Burrata": "Hangar 1 with burrata — California craft blended vodka against fresh dairy. Excellent; Hangar 1's grape-component floral notes complement cream with distinctive craft character — parallel to but different from Nolet's rose-peach approach in the gin category.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Butternut Squash": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crystalline neutrality leans against the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the unflavored body sits with the squash bisque, and the crisp profile carries the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Carrot Cake": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a vodka. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Hangar 1 Vodka for the steak course.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Cheesecake": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not a vodka. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hangar 1 Vodka lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Chilean Seabass": "Hangar 1 Vodka's unflavored crystalline pour meets at register with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh: the clean vodka register matches the seabass, and the bright vodka edge brightens the plate. Strong; the vodka option when the gold call is spoken for.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Chocolate Brownie": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- vodka brings no flavor to bridge the chocolate's weight — neutral but wrong for the close. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not a vodka. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Hangar 1 Vodka on the steak course instead.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Chocolate Cake": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- vodka brings no flavor to bridge the chocolate's weight — neutral but wrong for the close. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not a vodka. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Hangar 1 Vodka for the steak course.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Clam Chowder": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality plays cleanly against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the floral edge frames the shellfish. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Cowboy Ribeye": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crystalline neutrality underclubs the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness -- vodka is too neutral to carry any prime cut. The plate deserves Macallan 18, Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon, or Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon, not a vodka. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Hangar 1 Vodka for another course.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Crab Cake": "Hangar 1 with crab cake — California blended grain+grape vodka against delicate lump crab. Excellent; the Viognier grape component gives Hangar 1 a floral lift that adds dimension to crab the pure-grain vodkas don't reach.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Creamed Spinach": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality sits beside the spinach's dairy-rich cream — the neutral profile sits with the light side, and the floral notes lift the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Creamy Potato": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality finds neutral with the potato soup's silky body — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the floral notes lift the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Creme Brulee": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crystalline neutrality mis-pairs with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- clean vodka has nothing to add against the custard's richness. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not a vodka. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Hangar 1 Vodka on the steak course instead.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Escargot": "Hangar 1 with escargot — California floral craft against garlic-butter snails. Strong; Hangar 1's grape-component lift meets the butter at craft register; HDW 100's proof cuts it sharper.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Faroe Island Salmon": "Hangar 1 with the salmon — Alameda blended vodka against oily salmon. Strong; Hangar 1's floral lift frames the fish with California-craft character.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Filet Mignon": "Hangar 1 with the filet — California craft blended vodka against tenderloin. Works; vodka over-specified; Hangar 1's floral character is a refined case.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|French Onion": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality plays cleanly against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Grilled Caesar": "Grilled Caesar: charred romaine and anchovy meet blended grain+grape California craft. Hangar 1's grape-component floral lift is the featured craft-vodka-Caesar pairing — where flagship Ketel One (Classic Vodka) is the benchmark, Hangar 1 brings the craft floral answer. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Gumbo": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality finds neutral with the gumbo's spiced Creole stew — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality sits beside the carrots' honeyed sweetness — the neutral profile sits with the light side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|House Wedge": "Hangar 1 with the House Wedge — California craft against iceberg and bleu. Strong; Hangar 1's floral notes meet the bleu with California-craft distinction.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Kansas City": "Hangar 1 with the KC — California craft against an 18oz strip. Avoid; vodka can't match strip marbling. Reach for a bourbon.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Loaded Potato": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality leans against the loaded potato's richness — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the floral notes lift the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Lobster Mac": "Hangar 1 Vodka's neutral vodka register reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the unflavored body sits with the lobster mac, and the crisp profile carries the side. Works; the glacial-clean finish is a luxury-register Russian-tradition dessert finisher.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Market Fish": "Hangar 1 with the market fish — California craft blended vodka against featured fish. Works; Hangar 1's floral character handles most fish preparations distinctively.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Mocha Creme": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- vodka brings no flavor to bridge the chocolate's weight — neutral but wrong for the close. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not a vodka. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Hangar 1 Vodka for the steak course.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Mushroom Bisque": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality leans against the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the floral notes lift the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Mushrooms": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality plays cleanly against the mushrooms' earthy umami — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crystalline neutrality falls short of the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- vodka brings no anchor — the dessert needs a flavor partner, not a clean spirit. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not a vodka. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hangar 1 Vodka lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Porterhouse": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crystalline neutrality underclubs the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character -- vodka is neutral by design — the marbled char deserves a pour with character. The plate deserves Odette Cabernet Sauvignon, Weller 12 Year, or Domaine du Grand Tinel, not a vodka. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Hangar 1 Vodka for another course.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Prime Tartare": "Hangar 1 with the tartare — California blended vodka against raw beef. Strong; Hangar 1's floral lift supports tartare; HDW 100's higher proof is still the featured craft-tartare match.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Rainbow Trout": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality sits with the trout's delicate flesh — the neutral profile frames the fish cleanly. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Roast Half Chicken": "Hangar 1 with the chicken — blended grain+grape California craft against roasted poultry. Works; Hangar 1's floral lift supports chicken at craft register.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality plays cleanly against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper warmth — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Hangar 1 Vodka's clean cold-distilled body meets at register with the halibut's salt-cured flesh: the cold-distilled body wraps the halibut, and the clean register frames the plate. Strong; reliable American vodka for the halibut.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality stays alongside the garlic-spinach's buttered greens — the neutral profile sits with the light side, and the floral notes lift the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Seafood Tower": "Hangar 1 Vodka: clean craft vodka from Alameda, CA. Excellent on seafood tower; neutral-clean profile frames shellfish at California-craft register.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Seared Scallops": "Seared Scallops: scallop sweetness meets California craft from Alameda, blended grain + Viognier-grape distillate with distinctive floral lift. Hangar 1's grape-component floral character is the featured craft-vodka-scallop pairing — where Detroit City sits with and HDW 100 lifts, Hangar 1 floralizes the pairing with a register no other Craft Vodka touches. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Seasonal Soup": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality reads alongside the seasonal soup's house build — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Seasonal Vegetables": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality leans against the seasonal garden plate — the neutral profile sits with the light side. Works; the match holds without overshooting. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Shrimp Bisque": "Hangar 1 with shrimp bisque — blended grain+grape vodka against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Hangar 1's floral lift brightens the bisque at craft register.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Shrimp Cocktail": "Hangar 1 with shrimp cocktail — Alameda California craft against cold shrimp. Excellent; Hangar 1's floral lift elevates the classic cold app with California-blended distinctive character.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Swordfish": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality matches the swordfish's meaty flesh — the neutral profile frames the fish cleanly. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|The Tomahawk": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crystalline neutrality underclubs the Tomahawk's theatrical bone-in marbling and smoky char -- vodka is neutral by design — the marbled char deserves a pour with character. The plate deserves Corazon Stagg, Opus One, or George T. Stagg, not a vodka. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Hangar 1 Vodka on another course instead.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Tomato Basil": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality reads alongside the tomato basil's bright acid — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Truffle Fries": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality stays alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality holds the line with the tuna's seared rare crust — the neutral profile frames the fish cleanly, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Hangar 1 Vodka|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality reads alongside the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; safe call, no friction. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Head Fake|Asparagus": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build leans against the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the sweet character sits at digestif register. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Head Fake|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Wheatley vodka, limoncello, triple sec, lemon, simple syrup, sugar rim. Sweet lemon-drop style clashes on every axis with manchego-cream gratin. Route this cocktail to dessert or to the lighter starters. Avoid; the pairing fights at the table — point the guest elsewhere.",
  "Head Fake|Beignets": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build leans against the beignet's warm sugar-dusted pastry — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Head Fake|Bone Marrow": "Wheatley vodka, limoncello, triple sec, lemon, simple syrup. The cocktail's sweet-bright profile has no structural match for marrow's rendered-fat richness — lemon and sugar don't cut bone depth. Never pair — keep Head Fake for starters and raw bar.",
  "Head Fake|Bone-In Filet": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build holds with the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the sweet character meets the cut at digestif register, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Head Fake|Broccoli Cheddar": "Head Fake's lemon-driven cocktail body reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the bright build frames the broccoli cheddar, and the citrus cuts the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Head Fake|Broccolini": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build sits beside the broccolini's tender green — the sweet character sits at digestif register. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Head Fake|Brussels and Belly": "Wheatley vodka, limoncello, triple sec, lemon, simple syrup, sugar rim. Sweet lemon-drop style clashes with cumin-smoked-paprika lardons; the rub's spice profile fights every component of the cocktail. Route to dessert. Avoid; pair this elsewhere on the menu.",
  "Head Fake|Burrata": "Wheatley vodka, limoncello, triple sec, lemon, simple syrup — sugar rim. The limoncello's Italian-citrus rounds the cocktail and plays against burrata's creamy-basil delicacy; lemon cuts without crushing. Peak bright cocktail for burrata — citrus-on-cream plus sugar-rim elegance.",
  "Head Fake|Butternut Squash": "Head Fake's gin-or-tequila cocktail lift reads alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bright build frames the squash bisque, and the citrus cuts the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Head Fake|Carrot Cake": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build sits beside the carrot cake's spiced cream cheese — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; safe call, no friction. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Head Fake|Cheesecake": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build plays cleanly against the cheesecake's custard cream — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Head Fake|Chilean Seabass": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build finds register with the seabass's buttery flesh — the sweet character meets the fish at digestif register, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Head Fake|Chocolate Brownie": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build finds neutral with the brownie's warm cocoa depth — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Head Fake|Chocolate Cake": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build sits alongside the cake's layered chocolate — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Head Fake|Clam Chowder": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the sweet character sits at digestif register, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Head Fake|Cowboy Ribeye": "Head Fake's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift underclubs the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness -- a light citrus cocktail can't carry the marbled char — needs whiskey or red wine weight. The plate deserves Macallan 18, Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon, or Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon, not a light cocktail. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Head Fake for another course.",
  "Head Fake|Crab Cake": "Wheatley vodka, limoncello, triple sec, lemon, simple syrup. The rounded limoncello citrus cuts crab's romesco and the sugar rim plays against the sweet meat; clean Wheatley base doesn't fight. Strong bright-cocktail pairing for crab cake — sophisticated lemon-drop structure.",
  "Head Fake|Creamed Spinach": "Head Fake's lemon-driven cocktail body finds neutral with the creamed spinach's rich bechamel-laced greens: the bright build frames the creamed spinach, and the citrus cuts the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Head Fake|Creamy Potato": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build plays cleanly against the potato soup's silky body — the sweet character sits at digestif register, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Head Fake|Creme Brulee": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Head Fake|Escargot": "Wheatley vodka, limoncello, triple sec, lemon, simple syrup — sugar rim. The bright lemon cuts garlic-butter escargot and limoncello adds aromatic Italian-citrus complexity against the snails. Strong bright cocktail for escargot when guest wants sweet-and-citrus-forward alternative to classic pairings.",
  "Head Fake|Faroe Island Salmon": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build plays cleanly against the salmon's rich oily flesh — the sweet character meets the fish at digestif register, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; a steady recommendation at the table.",
  "Head Fake|Filet Mignon": "Wheatley vodka, limoncello, triple sec, lemon, simple syrup. The cocktail's sweet-citrus profile is wrong for any steak — limoncello has no hook into grilled beef. Works only if guest stays on the cocktail; route filet pairing to Cab, Pinot, or Manhattan for peak.",
  "Head Fake|French Onion": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build finds neutral with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the sweet character sits at digestif register. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Head Fake|Grilled Caesar": "Wheatley vodka, limoncello, triple sec, lemon, simple syrup. The lemon balances anchovy-parmesan dressing and limoncello adds Italian-citrus depth against grilled-romaine char. Works as a bright unconventional cocktail pairing — sweetness and char meet on the rim.",
  "Head Fake|Gumbo": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build sits beside the gumbo's spiced Creole stew — the sweet character sits at digestif register, and the citrus brightens the spice. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Head Fake|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build leans against the carrots' honeyed sweetness — the sweet character sits at digestif register. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Head Fake|House Wedge": "Wheatley vodka, limoncello, triple sec, lemon, simple syrup — sugar rim. The lemon-and-citrus profile cuts iceberg-and-bacon weight and the limoncello rounds against blue cheese. Strong bright opener for the wedge — keeps palate fresh before the steak course.",
