  "Heaven's Door 10 Year|Escargot": "Heaven's Door 10 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth leans against the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the bourbon depth settles into the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; GTS frames the two-cut plate at collector register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Heaven's Door 10 Year|Faroe Island Salmon": "Heaven's Door 10 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Heaven's Door 10 Year on the steak course instead.",
  "Heaven's Door 10 Year|Filet Mignon": "Heaven's Door 10 Year with the filet — Bob Dylan's bourbon brand. 100-proof 10-year Tennessee-sourced, decorative bottle featuring Dylan's ironwork art. A story-driven pour — the 10-year aging frames the filet with aged depth while the bottle theatrics carry tableside conversation. A celebrity-brand premium bourbon with substance. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
