  "Hendricks Gin|Beignets": "Hendricks with beignets — perfumed low-juniper against fried dough. Excellent; Hendrick's rose-cucumber is the democratic Hendrick's dessert pairing; Grand Cabaret's black currant-and-rhubarb edges it for distinctiveness.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Bone Marrow": "Hendricks with bone marrow — perfumed Scottish gin against umami fat. Avoid; gin can't cut marrow. Reach for Fernet Branca.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Bone-In Filet": "Hendricks Gin's botanical-driven lift underclubs the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- gin reads light against the prime cut's weight — needs a red or whiskey. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a gin. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Hendricks Gin for another course.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Broccoli Cheddar": "Hendricks Gin's crisp cucumber-rose botanicals sits beside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the floral notes lift the cream. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Broccolini": "Hendricks Gin's crisp cucumber-rose botanicals reads alongside the broccolini's tender green — the botanical edge sits with the light side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Brussels and Belly": "Hendricks Gin's crisp cucumber-rose botanicals sits alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Burrata": "Hendricks with burrata — flagship Hendrick's Scottish gin, cucumber-rose signature, low-juniper perfumed profile. Excellent; Hendrick's rose-cucumber signature complements cream at the crowd-pleasing register — the default Hendrick's-burrata pairing, where Flora Adora floralizes harder and Grand Cabaret brings fruit.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Butternut Squash": "Hendricks Gin's crisp cucumber-rose botanicals leans against the squash soup's silky sweet — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the floral notes lift the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Carrot Cake": "Hendricks Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Hendricks Gin for the steak course.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Cheesecake": "Hendricks with cheesecake — flagship Scottish gin against custard. Works; Hendrick's cucumber-rose is a soft dessert finisher; Grand Cabaret's black currant is the featured Hendrick's-cheesecake match.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Chilean Seabass": "Hendricks Gin's gin lift with floral-and-pepper matches register with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh: the juniper-led botanicals carry the seabass, and the juniper threads the plate. Strong; Hendricks Gin on the seabass -- workhorse pairing, no surprises.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Chocolate Brownie": "Hendricks Gin's botanical-driven lift fights the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- juniper and cocoa refuse each other — botanical bitterness reads metallic against chocolate. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not a gin. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Hendricks Gin for the steak course.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Chocolate Cake": "Hendricks Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not a gin. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Hendricks Gin for the steak course.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Clam Chowder": "Hendricks Gin's crisp cucumber-rose botanicals stays alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the floral edge frames the shellfish. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Cowboy Ribeye": "Hendricks with the cowboy ribeye — flagship Hendrick's against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Avoid; gin wrong for this cut. Reach for a bourbon.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Crab Cake": "Hendricks with crab cake — flagship Scottish gin against delicate lump crab. Strong; Hendrick's cucumber-rose supports crab at crowd-pleasing register; Flora Adora's lavish floral lifts crab harder.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Creamed Spinach": "Hendricks Gin's crisp cucumber-rose botanicals reads alongside the spinach's dairy-rich cream — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the floral notes lift the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Creamy Potato": "Hendricks Gin's crisp cucumber-rose botanicals stays alongside the potato soup's silky body — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the floral notes lift the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Hendricks Gin|Creme Brulee": "Hendricks Gin's botanical-driven lift jars against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- sharp botanicals cut through dairy custard without resolving — the dessert reads broken. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not a gin. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Hendricks Gin for the steak course.",
