  "Hendricks Neptunia|Brussels and Belly": "Hendricks Neptunia's crisp anise-brine botanicals stays alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs frame the grilled char. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Hendricks Neptunia|Burrata": "Neptunia with burrata — coastal-release Hendrick's against fresh dairy. Excellent; Neptunia's briny-coastal profile complements cream with distinctive maritime character.",
  "Hendricks Neptunia|Butternut Squash": "Hendricks Neptunia's crisp anise-brine botanicals plays cleanly against the squash soup's silky sweet — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Hendricks Neptunia|Carrot Cake": "Hendricks Neptunia's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- juniper-citrus and warm cake spices pull in opposite directions. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Hendricks Neptunia for the steak course.",
  "Hendricks Neptunia|Cheesecake": "Neptunia with cheesecake — coastal-release Hendrick's against custard. Works; Neptunia's briny profile is over-specified for dessert; Grand Cabaret's black-currant is the featured Hendrick's-cheesecake match.",
  "Hendricks Neptunia|Chilean Seabass": "Hendricks Neptunia's crisp anise-brine botanicals holds steady against the seabass's buttery flesh — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the mineral edge lifts the fish. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Hendricks Neptunia|Chocolate Brownie": "Hendricks Neptunia's botanical-driven lift fights the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- juniper and cocoa refuse each other — botanical bitterness reads metallic against chocolate. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not a gin. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Hendricks Neptunia on the steak course instead.",
  "Hendricks Neptunia|Chocolate Cake": "Hendricks Neptunia's botanical-driven lift clashes with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- gin botanicals jar against the chocolate's sweetness with no bridge. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not a gin. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Hendricks Neptunia for the steak course.",
  "Hendricks Neptunia|Clam Chowder": "Hendricks Neptunia's crisp anise-brine botanicals reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Hendricks Neptunia|Cowboy Ribeye": "Neptunia with the cowboy ribeye — Scottish-coast Hendrick's against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Avoid; gin wrong for this cut. Reach for a bourbon.",
  "Hendricks Neptunia|Crab Cake": "Neptunia with crab cake — coastal-release Hendrick's (bladderwrack + Ayrshire thyme) against delicate lump crab. Excellent; Neptunia's maritime profile frames crab with ocean-to-ocean thematic resonance — the most Hendrick's-appropriate crab pairing across the family.",
  "Hendricks Neptunia|Creamed Spinach": "Hendricks Neptunia's crisp anise-brine botanicals stays alongside the spinach's dairy-rich cream — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the mineral edge lifts the dish. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Hendricks Neptunia|Creamy Potato": "Hendricks Neptunia's crisp anise-brine botanicals leans against the potato soup's silky body — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Hendricks Neptunia|Creme Brulee": "Hendricks Neptunia's botanical-driven lift clashes with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not a gin. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hendricks Neptunia lands on the steak course — not here.",
