  "Hendricks Orbium|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Hendricks Orbium's botanical-driven lift clashes with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- gin botanicals jar against the chocolate's sweetness with no bridge. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Hendricks Orbium for the steak course.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Porterhouse": "Hendricks Orbium's botanical-driven lift falls short of the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character -- botanical-citrus can't stand up to 26+ ounces — a Cab or bourbon earns it. The plate deserves Odette Cabernet Sauvignon, Weller 12 Year, or Domaine du Grand Tinel, not a gin. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Hendricks Orbium for another course.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Prime Tartare": "Orbium with the tartare — quinine-wormwood Hendrick's against raw beef. Excellent; Orbium's bitter-tonic profile lifts tartare's minerality with distinctive quinine character — the featured Hendrick's Family-tartare match.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Rainbow Trout": "Hendricks Orbium's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals holds steady against the trout's delicate flesh — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Roast Half Chicken": "Orbium with the chicken — quinine-wormwood Hendrick's against roasted poultry. Works; Orbium's bitter-tonic profile supports chicken at distinctive register.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Hendricks Orbium's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals holds with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper warmth — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the caramel rounds the earthy plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Hendricks Orbium's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals lifts the halibut's salt-cured flesh — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Hendricks Orbium's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals plays cleanly against the garlic-spinach's buttered greens — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Seafood Tower": "Orbium with the seafood tower — bitter-tonic Hendrick's against the raw bar. Excellent; Orbium's quinine-wormwood profile is a cocktail-culture tower choice — perpetual G&T character meets the raw bar.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Seared Scallops": "Orbium with seared scallops — bitter-tonic Hendrick's against scallop sweetness. Strong; Orbium's quinine-wormwood cuts scallop sweetness with distinctive bitter-contrast.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Seasonal Soup": "Hendricks Orbium's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals reads alongside the seasonal soup's house build — the gin botanicals sit with the plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Seasonal Vegetables": "Hendricks Orbium's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals stays alongside the seasonal garden plate — the botanical edge sits with the light side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Shrimp Bisque": "Orbium with shrimp bisque — bitter-tonic Hendrick's against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Orbium's quinine-wormwood cuts the bisque's richness sharply where the floral siblings just ride it.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Shrimp Cocktail": "Orbium with shrimp cocktail — quinine-forward Hendrick's against cold shrimp. Excellent; Orbium's bitter-tonic character elevates the classic cold app with distinctive G-and-T-style lift.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Swordfish": "Hendricks Orbium's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals holds the line with the swordfish's meaty flesh — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Strong; the call lands cleanly.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|The Tomahawk": "Orbium with the Tomahawk — bitter-tonic Hendrick's against 32oz cap-fat. Avoid; gin has no answer. Reach for a bourbon or cab.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Tomato Basil": "Hendricks Orbium's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals stays alongside the tomato basil's bright acid — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Truffle Fries": "Hendricks Orbium's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals sits beside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the oak frames the umami. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Hendricks Orbium's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals lifts the tuna's seared rare crust — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the juniper sharpens the char. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Hendricks Orbium|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Hendricks Orbium's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals sits beside the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the gin botanicals sit with the plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Asparagus": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac clashes with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- cognac on a green vegetable side is wrong direction — needs crisp white instead. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a cognac. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Hennessy Cognac for the steak course.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Hennessy with the au gratin — benchmark cognac against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Hennessy's oak handles the richness at functional register.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Beignets": "Hennessy with beignets — default-call cognac against fried dough and powdered sugar. Works; Hennessy's dried-fruit-vanilla is a comfortable finisher.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Bone Marrow": "Hennessy with bone marrow — ubiquitous cognac against umami fat. Excellent; Hennessy's vanilla-and-oak depth cuts marrow richness at benchmark register — where Courvoisier's drier character does it more aggressively, Hennessy rounds it more comfortably.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Bone-In Filet": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac reads alongside the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the eau-de-vie body carries the bone-enhanced filet, and the orchard-fruit thread frames the cut. Works; Rémy's elegance meets the char at functional register.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Broccoli Cheddar": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the eau-de-vie body carries the broccoli cheddar, and the dried-fruit note underlines the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Broccolini": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac clashes with the broccolini's tender green stalks -- cognac on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a cognac. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Hennessy Cognac on the steak course instead.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Brussels and Belly": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac sits alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the aged-grape brandy body sits with the pork-belly plate, and the rancio register softens the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Burrata": "Hennessy with burrata — cognac against fresh dairy. Avoid; cognac is too heavy for burrata's cream.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Butternut Squash": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac leans against the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the brandy depth wraps the squash bisque, and the dried-fruit note underlines the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Carrot Cake": "Hennessy with carrot cake — ubiquitous cognac against cream cheese and cinnamon. Excellent; Hennessy's dried-fruit and vanilla meet the cake's raisins and spice with benchmark comfort.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Cheesecake": "Hennessy with cheesecake — default-call cognac against custard dessert. Excellent; Hennessy's dried-fruit and vanilla thread the cheesecake with the most-ordered cognac-dessert pairing — textbook French after-dinner finish.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Chilean Seabass": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- cognac and oily fish double up the richness with no foil. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a cognac. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Hennessy Cognac on the steak course instead.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Chocolate Brownie": "Hennessy with the chocolate brownie — VS/VSOP benchmark against cocoa. Excellent; Hennessy's vanilla-and-oak marries cocoa cleanly; the dried-fruit notes build a bridge to chocolate dessert that doesn't overpower.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Chocolate Cake": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac reads alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the cognac register matches the chocolate cake, and the rancio register softens the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Clam Chowder": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the aged-grape brandy body sits with the chowder, and the rancio register softens the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Cowboy Ribeye": "Hennessy Cognac's bold cognac-vanilla character holds steady against the ribeye's cap fat and char — the barrel-aged depth meets the cap-fat, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Crab Cake": "Hennessy with crab cake — ubiquitous cognac against delicate crab. Avoid; cognac weight wrong for seafood. Reach for a vodka or gin.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Creamed Spinach": "Hennessy with creamed spinach — VS/VSOP against dairy-rich side. Strong; Hennessy's vanilla rides the cream at benchmark register.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Creamy Potato": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the Limousin-oak weight handles the potato soup, and the rancio register softens the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Creme Brulee": "Hennessy with creme brulee — default-call cognac against vanilla custard and caramelized sugar. Strong; Hennessy's dried-fruit-vanilla finds the caramel cleanly; Rémy VSOP's elegance still edges this pairing.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Escargot": "Hennessy Cognac's bold cognac-vanilla character holds the line with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the barrel-aged depth cuts the umami fat, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Faroe Island Salmon": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- cognac is post-meal energy — wrong register for a main protein. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a cognac. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hennessy Cognac belongs on the steak course.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Filet Mignon": "Hennessy with the filet — ubiquitous VS/VSOP cognac, dried-fruit-and-vanilla benchmark. Excellent; Hennessy is the default call for a reason — its eaux-de-vie blend delivers enough oak and dried-fruit weight to frame tenderloin without dominating it, the most democratic cognac-and-steak pairing on the menu.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|French Onion": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac finds neutral with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the Limousin-oak weight handles the French onion, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; Ferrand's craft character handles the richness.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Grilled Caesar": "Hennessy with the grilled Caesar — cognac against charred romaine and anchovy. Works; Hennessy's vanilla-oak meets the char without featuring.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Gumbo": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac sits alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the Limousin-oak weight handles the gumbo, and the dried-fruit note underlines the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac clashes with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- cognac on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a cognac. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Hennessy Cognac on the steak course instead.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|House Wedge": "Hennessy with the House Wedge — cognac against iceberg and bleu. Works; Hennessy's oak is over-specified for the wedge but functional.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Kansas City": "Hennessy with the KC — ubiquitous cognac against an 18oz strip. Strong; Hennessy handles the strip with benchmark character, though Courvoisier's drier oak cuts marbling sharper.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Loaded Potato": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac leans against the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the eau-de-vie body carries the loaded potato soup, and the rancio register softens the bowl. Works; Ferrand's craft character handles the richness.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Lobster Mac": "Hennessy with lobster mac — VS/VSOP benchmark against pasta-and-lobster richness. Strong; Hennessy's oak frames the richness without fighting it.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Market Fish": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- cognac's aged-grape weight buries delicate fish — digestif belongs after the meal. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a cognac. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hennessy Cognac belongs on the steak course.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Mocha Creme": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac reads alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the brandy depth wraps the mocha creme, and the orchard-fruit thread frames the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Mushroom Bisque": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac sits alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the cognac register matches the mushroom bisque, and the caramel softens the umami weight. Works; Ferrand's craft character handles the richness.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Mushrooms": "Hennessy with mushrooms — dried-fruit benchmark against earthy umami. Strong; Hennessy's oak threads the mushrooms at default-call register.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Peanut Butter Brownie: peanut butter and cocoa meet ubiquitous cognac. Strong; Hennessy's oak handles the dessert density at benchmark register.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Porterhouse": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac leans against the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character: the cognac register matches the dual-cut steak, and the orchard-fruit thread frames the cut. Works; the close holds, neither soars nor fights.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Prime Tartare": "Hennessy Cognac's bold cognac-vanilla character frames the tartare's raw beef and brine — the barrel-aged depth cuts the umami fat, and the caramel meets the nut character. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Rainbow Trout": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- cognac's aged-grape weight buries delicate fish — digestif belongs after the meal. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a cognac. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hennessy Cognac belongs on the steak course.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Roast Half Chicken": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac sits alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the Limousin-oak weight handles the roast chicken, and the rancio register softens the plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac sits alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the cognac register matches the chickpea soup, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; Hennessy's dried-fruit-vanilla is a comfortable finisher.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac clashes with the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- cognac is post-meal energy — wrong register for a main protein. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a cognac. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Hennessy Cognac on the steak course instead.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac clashes with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- cognac on a green vegetable side is wrong direction — needs crisp white instead. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not a cognac. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Hennessy Cognac for the steak course.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Seafood Tower": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- cognac weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs sparkling or a crisp white. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a cognac. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hennessy Cognac lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Seared Scallops": "Hennessy with seared scallops — VS/VSOP against scallop delicacy. Avoid; cognac oak-depth overwhelms scallops.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Seasonal Soup": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac reads alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the Limousin-oak weight handles the seasonal soup, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Seasonal Vegetables": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac clashes with the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate -- cognac on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, not a cognac. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Hennessy Cognac on the steak course instead.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Shrimp Bisque": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the brandy depth wraps the shrimp bisque, and the dried-fruit note underlines the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Shrimp Cocktail": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac clashes with the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- cognac is wrong-course energy for the table's opener. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a cognac. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Hennessy Cognac for the steak course.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Swordfish": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- cognac is post-meal energy — wrong register for a main protein. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a cognac. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Hennessy Cognac for the steak course.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|The Tomahawk": "Hennessy Cognac -- VS/VSOP cognac, dried-fruit, vanilla. The eau-de-vie body carries the 36oz showpiece, and the dried-fruit note underlines the cut. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Tomato Basil": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the Limousin-oak weight handles the tomato basil, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Truffle Fries": "Hennessy with truffle fries — VS/VSOP against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; the oak-and-vanilla frames the earthy-rich side with the classic after-dinner-bite approach.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac fights the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- cognac's aged register pulls against the savory sear without resolving. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a cognac. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hennessy Cognac belongs on the steak course.",
  "Hennessy Cognac|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the cognac depth wraps the curry, and the dried-fruit-and-vanilla rounds the bowl. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Asparagus": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the bourbon body sits with the asparagus, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the side. Works; no driver pairing.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with au gratin potatoes — 10-year bonded against cheese-and-cream. Strong; aged BIB at matched premium register.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Beignets": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's aged 100-proof bonded single-barrel finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon depth settles into the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Bone Marrow": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with bone marrow — aged 100-proof bonded single-barrel against umami fat. The 10-year depth meets marrow's intensity with BIB authority; premium HH BIB marrow pairing. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Bone-In Filet": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's rounded-oak bourbon character rests at register with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the bourbon backbone carries the bone-enhanced filet, and the caramel rounds the cut. Strong; smooth character sits with richness at matched register.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Broccoli Cheddar": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Broccolini": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's aged 100-proof bonded single-barrel reads alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the bourbon depth settles into the broccolini, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; aged premium slightly over-specified.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Brussels and Belly": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with Brussels + Belly — bonded 10-year HH meets maple-glazed pork belly. The aged BIB weight cuts the glaze with authority. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Burrata": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with burrata — fresh dairy against 10-year BIB. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Butternut Squash": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bourbon backbone carries the squash bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; BH Red Wine Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Carrot Cake": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with carrot cake — aged bonded HH against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; BIB slightly over-specified.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Cheesecake": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with cheesecake — aged bonded HH against clean custard. Works; BIB structure overshoots the dessert's delicacy.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Chilean Seabass": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's aged 100-proof bonded single-barrel overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon weight needs red meat, not the salmon's already-rich oils. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond belongs on the steak course.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Chocolate Brownie": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with the chocolate brownie — 10-year bonded against cocoa. Works; the aged BIB depth meets the brownie cleanly.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Chocolate Cake": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the bourbon backbone carries the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the toast adds a warmth the dessert can accept.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Clam Chowder": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon body sits with the chowder, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; milestone-edition over-specified.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Cowboy Ribeye": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with the Cowboy Ribeye — aged 100-proof BIB against cap fat. The 10-year bonded depth handles the ribeye with authority; the premium HH BIB for this cut. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Crab Cake": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with crab cake — 10-year 100-proof BIB against delicate crab. Avoid; pour a crisp white wine.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Creamed Spinach": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with creamed spinach — aged bonded HH against dairy. Strong; BIB structure and 10-year depth sit with richness.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Creamy Potato": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the potato soup, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; the Dylan-brand story is wasted on the salad.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Creme Brulee": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the bourbon body sits with the brulee, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; Vermont-brand character doesn't drive.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Escargot": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's bold caramel-spice character finds register with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Faroe Island Salmon": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's aged 100-proof bonded single-barrel overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond belongs on the steak course.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Filet Mignon": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with the filet — Heaven Hill's 10-year bottled-in-bond single-barrel. 100-proof, aged depth, historic brand. A premium aged-BIB alternate to Elijah Craig Single Barrel; the 10-year aging gives the filet a richer Heaven Hill frame. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|French Onion": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the caramel-spice register matches the French onion, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; Marian McLain L.E.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Grilled Caesar": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with the grilled Caesar — aged bonded HH against charred romaine. Strong; the 10-year BIB earns the Caesar with BIB weight and age.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Gumbo": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the brown-spirit warmth threads the gumbo, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; JW Blue is over-specified for the side — save the rare-cask bottle for the protein course.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the bourbon body sits with the honey carrots, and the oak softens the caramelized sugar. Works; AE CS handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|House Wedge": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with the House Wedge — 100-proof 10-year BIB against iceberg and bleu. Works; bonded weight overpowers the salad.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Kansas City": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with the KC — 100-proof 10-year bonded single-barrel against the strip's marbling. The bonded weight and aging carry the cut at the premium HH BIB register. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Loaded Potato": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the bourbon weight handles the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the premium pour is wasted on the salad's simplicity.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Lobster Mac": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the brown-spirit warmth threads the lobster mac, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; light body doesn't overshoot.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Market Fish": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's aged 100-proof bonded single-barrel overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Mocha Creme": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the bourbon weight handles the mocha creme, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; milestone-release covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Mushroom Bisque": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the caramel-spice register matches the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the pour's refinement is underused by the salad.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Mushrooms": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with the mushrooms — bonded 10-year Heaven Hill against earthy umami. The aged depth layers into mushroom character with BIB weight. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with the PB brownie — aged bonded HH against peanut butter and cocoa. Works; the 10-year BIB depth gives the dessert substantial weight.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Porterhouse": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with the porterhouse — 100-proof 10-year BIB across strip and filet. Strong; bonded weight leans strip-side, filet tolerates.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Prime Tartare": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's bold caramel-spice character lifts the tartare's raw beef and brine — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Rainbow Trout": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's aged 100-proof bonded single-barrel flattens the trout's delicate flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond for the steak course.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Roast Half Chicken": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the caramel-spice register matches the roast chicken, and the vanilla softens the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the bourbon body sits with the chickpea soup, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; master-blender doesn't drive.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's aged 100-proof bonded single-barrel overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Save the Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond for the steak course.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the caramel-spice register matches the garlic spinach, and the oak frames the side. Works; the aging is wasted on the salad.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Seafood Tower": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's aged 100-proof bonded single-barrel fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond for the steak course.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Seared Scallops": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against aged bonded HH. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Seasonal Soup": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight sits alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the bourbon depth settles into the seasonal soup, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; the toast notes don't really interplay with the soup but don't clash.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Seasonal Vegetables": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the brown-spirit warmth threads the seasonal vegetables, and the caramel rounds the side. Works; aged premium slightly over-specified.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Shrimp Bisque": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon backbone carries the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; save the bottle for the protein course — a soup is wrong for a $200 pour.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Shrimp Cocktail": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against aged bonded HH. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Swordfish": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's aged 100-proof bonded single-barrel swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond belongs on the steak course.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|The Tomahawk": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with the Tomahawk — 100-proof 10-year BIB against bone-in ribeye. The bonded weight and aging earn the cut where lighter single-barrels fade; the Heaven Hill-side Tomahawk call alongside E.H. Taylor (BT). Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Tomato Basil": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the oak depth lays under the tomato basil, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; gentle composed match.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Truffle Fries": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with truffle fries — 100-proof 10-year BIB against truffle-parmesan. The aged bonded richness gives the side authority few single-barrels match. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's aged 100-proof bonded single-barrel flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond for the steak course.",
  "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the oak depth lays under the curry, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; the pour's assertiveness is a bit much for the soup but doesn't clash.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Asparagus": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony finds neutral with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the elegant Suntory/Nikka register matches the asparagus, and the umami-tinged finish frames the side. Works; BIB slightly over-specified.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the precise Japanese craft body wraps the au gratin, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; retailer-pick wasted on salad.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Beignets": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the elegant Suntory/Nikka register matches the beignets, and the green-fruit edge brightens the dessert. Works; neutral, not elevating.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Bone Marrow": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony -- blended Japanese, harmony, silky. The Japanese whisky balance frames the rich marrow, and the sandalwood-and-honey register softens the starter. Strong; the pairing lands at register without strain against the cut; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Bone-In Filet": "Hibiki Harmony with the bone-in filet — premium refined Japanese blend against tenderloin-with-bone. Excellent; Hibiki's elegant harmony of cask types frames the cut at premium Japanese register.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Broccoli Cheddar": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the Mizunara-influenced register sits with the broccoli cheddar, and the oak threads the cream. Works; blend character covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Broccolini": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony leans against the broccolini's tender green stalks: the Japanese whisky balance frames the broccolini, and the green-fruit edge brightens the side. Works; Sinatra Select handles the richness at Sinatra-tribute register.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Brussels and Belly": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony finds neutral with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the Mizunara-influenced register sits with the pork-belly plate, and the precision rounds the side. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Burrata": "Hibiki Harmony with burrata — refined Japanese blend against fresh dairy. Works; Japanese whisky's delicate category + Hibiki's refinement make it whisky-curious-burrata-possible at premium register.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Butternut Squash": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony leans against the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the elegant Suntory/Nikka register matches the squash bisque, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; save the BTAC bottle for the protein course — the side doesn't deserve the pour.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Carrot Cake": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony leans against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the Japanese whisky balance frames the carrot cake, and the Japanese-craft balance underlines the dessert. Works; OGD 16 handles dessert density at distinctive register.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Cheesecake": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony sits alongside the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the precise Japanese craft body wraps the cheesecake, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; boutique character gives the dessert a craft frame.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Chilean Seabass": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony leans against the seabass' buttery seabass flesh: the Mizunara-influenced register sits with the seabass, and the Japanese-craft balance underlines the plate. Works; high proof over-specified for the soup.",
