  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Seafood Tower": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony finds neutral with the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the precise Japanese craft body wraps the seafood tower, and the precision rounds the starter. Works; curated single-barrel slightly over-specified.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Seared Scallops": "Hibiki Harmony with seared scallops — refined Japanese blend against scallop delicacy. Excellent; Hibiki's elegant harmony frames scallops with premium Japanese-blend distinction — where Toki is gentle, Hibiki is refined.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Seasonal Soup": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony reads alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the restrained whisky body threads the seasonal soup, and the green-fruit edge brightens the bowl. Works; HH 20's aged character meets the glaze at collector register.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Seasonal Vegetables": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony reads alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the precise Japanese craft body wraps the seasonal vegetables, and the Japanese-craft balance underlines the side. Works; boutique character gives the dessert a craft frame.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Shrimp Bisque": "Hibiki Harmony with shrimp bisque — premium Suntory blend against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Hibiki's refined character rides the bisque at premium register.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Shrimp Cocktail": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony sits alongside the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish: the restrained whisky body threads the chilled shrimp, and the green-fruit edge brightens the starter. Works; the 10-year holds without lifting.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Swordfish": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony sits alongside the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak: the Mizunara-influenced register sits with the swordfish, and the green-fruit edge brightens the plate. Works; Parker's Heritage 16th handles the richness at annual-release register.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|The Tomahawk": "Hibiki Harmony with the Tomahawk — refined Japanese blend against 32oz cap-fat. Avoid; Japanese whisky's delicate character is wrong for this cut. Reach for a bourbon or cab.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Tomato Basil": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony leans against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the Japanese whisky balance frames the tomato basil, and the precision rounds the bowl. Works; bonded weight slightly over-specified.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Truffle Fries": "Hibiki Harmony with truffle fries — refined Japanese blend against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Hibiki's elegant harmony meets the earthy-rich at premium register.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony reads alongside the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the elegant Suntory/Nikka register matches the tuna, and the umami-tinged finish frames the plate. Works; private-selection wasted on the salad.",
  "Hibiki Japanese Harmony|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony leans against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the Mizunara-influenced register sits with the curry, and the green-fruit edge brightens the bowl. Works; boutique character doesn't drive.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|1792 Small Batch": "1792 Small Batch's caramel-spice character sits alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the bourbon depth settles into the honey carrots, and the oak frames the caramelized sugar. Works; the distinctive character is underused by the salad's simplicity.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|1792 Sweet Wheat": "1792 Sweet Wheat's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the bourbon depth settles into the honey carrots, and the oak frames the caramelized sugar. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|1881 Napa Valley": "1881 Napa Valley's bold cherry-coffee cassis finds neutral with the carrots' honeyed sweetness — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the coffee meets the caramel. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|2 James Gin": "2 James Gin's crisp char-juniper botanicals reads alongside the carrots' honeyed sweetness — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the botanicals echo the green plate. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|A Midnight's Winter Dram": "A Midnight's Winter Dram's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the scotch backbone matches the honey carrots, and the oak balances the burnt-sugar edge. Works; mid-proof pour is slightly over-specified.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Aberlour 16": "Aberlour 16's double-matured Speyside balance sits alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the Highland register carries the honey carrots, and the oak frames the caramelized sugar. Works; own-plus-sourced covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Adictivo Cristalino": "Adictivo Cristalino's rested-agave body reads alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the aged-agave weight wraps the honey carrots, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; ceremonial depth is composed with the dessert.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Adictivo Reposado": "Adictivo Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register sits alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the barrel-rested body handles the honey carrots, and the oak threads the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Alexander Valley Chardonnay": "Sonoma Chardonnay — ripe apple, pear, warm vanilla oak, smooth balanced texture. The apple-pear plays against carrots' honey-glaze sweetness and the oak-vanilla weight handles the roasted char. Strong accessible Chardonnay for honey-roasted carrots — California oak on the sweet-root classic.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Alexander Valley Cyrus": "Alexander Valley Cyrus's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis sits beside the carrots' honeyed sweetness — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the cocoa deepens the fudge. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Alexander Valley Homestead Red": "Alexander Valley Homestead Red's coffee-mocha tannin plays cleanly against the carrots' honeyed sweetness — the medium-body red frames the green plate, and the coffee meets the caramel. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Amaro Nonino": "Amaro Nonino's crisp orange-peel-grappa sweetness fights the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- aperitivo bitterness and the glaze's sugar refuse each other — bitter wins, dessert reads cloying. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Amaro Nonino lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Ancho Reyes": "Ancho Reyes' sweet liqueur character doubles down on the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- sweet liqueur and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no contrast left. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Ancho Reyes belongs on the steak course.",
