  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Salt-Cured Halibut with the honey carrots -- the halibut's salt-cured flesh meets the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the lighter course hands off to dessert, the meal closes clean. Works; the side reads as a measured plate companion.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Sambuca": "Sambuca's sweet liqueur character clashes with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a digestif. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Sambuca on the steak course instead.",
