  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Scapegrace Fortuna": "Scapegrace Fortuna's NZ craft single malt finds neutral with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the bourbon depth settles into the honey carrots, and the oak frames the caramelized sugar. Works; bonded weight overpowers this dish.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Scavino Barolo": "Piedmont Barolo's tar-and-tannin intensity against caramelized-honey carrots — firm-tannin Nebbiolo is wildly wrong for a sweet-root side. Never pair. Route Scavino to the Tomahawk or Porterhouse; take honey carrots with Pinot Noir, rosé, or Chardonnay.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Schloss Vollrads Riesling": "Honey Roasted Carrots: these honey-roasted carrots' caramelized sweetness and earthy warmth meets this off-dry Riesling's stone-fruit sweetness and mineral backbone. Bright acidity lifts green vegetables; mineral lines up with the clean vegetable bite. Works — coherent. Gold standard; the headline call at the table.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters": "Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters's bold cherry-chocolate cassis finds neutral with the carrots' honeyed sweetness — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the cocoa deepens the fudge. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Seafood Tower": "Seafood Tower and the honey carrots -- acid and sugar share the table, neither course pulls heavy. Works; both items hold their register, no clash.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Seared Scallops": "The scallops and the honey carrots -- the savory course resolves into sugar, the meal closes with contrast. Works; the call holds whether the table sequences them or shares.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Seasonal Soup": "Seasonal Soup and the honey carrots -- the seasonal soup's house seasonal build meets the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: a quiet call, the meal carries without strain. Works; no conflict however the table orders them.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Sesti Brunello di Montalcino": "Sesti Brunello di Montalcino's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity crowds the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- the side needs a crisper register to carry it cleanly. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Sesti Brunello di Montalcino on the steak course instead.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Shafer 1.5": "Shafer 1.5's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth crowds the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- the side needs a crisper register to carry it cleanly. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Save the Shafer 1.5 for the steak course.",
  "Honey Roasted Carrots|Shafer Hillside Select": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power fights the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- red tannin and the glaze's sugar pull against each other — sugar reads cloying, tannin bitter. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Shafer Hillside Select for the steak course.",
