  "Inverroche Gin|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Inverroche Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Inverroche Gin for the steak course.",
  "Inverroche Gin|Porterhouse": "Inverroche Gin's botanical-driven lift underclubs the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character -- gin's light register can't carry the marbled char — the cut deserves a bigger pour. The plate deserves Odette Cabernet Sauvignon, Weller 12 Year, or Domaine du Grand Tinel, not a gin. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Inverroche Gin on another course instead.",
  "Inverroche Gin|Prime Tartare": "Inverroche with the tartare — South African fynbos gin against raw beef. Strong; Inverroche's floral-herbal supports tartare with Cape-terroir character; Monkey 47's 47-botanical complexity is the featured craft-gin-tartare match.",
  "Inverroche Gin|Rainbow Trout": "Inverroche Gin's crisp earth-floral botanicals finds register with the trout's delicate flesh — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
