  "Iron Fish Gin|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Iron Fish Gin's coriander-and-juniper register sits alongside the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the floral edge frames the tuna, and the juniper threads the plate. Strong; Sapphire's softness meets the bleu at accessible register.",
  "Iron Fish Gin|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Iron Fish Gin's cask-strength citrus-earth botanicals sits beside the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the honey balances the spice. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Asparagus": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the bourbon depth settles into the asparagus, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; annual-release complexity over-specified.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet northern MI mezcal-cask. Works; Ironfish Mezcal handles the richness at Michigan-hometown register.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Beignets": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon depth settles into the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Vermont-brand at matched register.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Bone Marrow": "Ironfish Bourbon Mezcal Casks with bone marrow — northern MI farm-to-bottle bourbon finished in mezcal casks against umami fat. Excellent; Ironfish Mezcal's smoky-agave character engages marrow with distinctive finish — the mezcal-smoke + marrow-umami is a featured Michigan-hometown pairing.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Bone-In Filet": "Ironfish Bourbon Mezcal Casks with the bone-in filet — northern MI mezcal-cask against tenderloin-with-bone. Works; Ironfish Mezcal frames the cut at Michigan-hometown register.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Broccoli Cheddar": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the bourbon weight handles the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; boutique-release covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Broccolini": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the broccolini's tender green stalks: the bourbon weight handles the broccolini, and the oak-and-spice register settles the side. Works; pleasant but not a standout.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Brussels and Belly": "Ironfish Bourbon Mezcal Casks with Brussels + Belly — Iron Fish MI mezcal-cask bourbon against maple-glazed pork belly. Excellent; Ironfish Mezcal's smoky character meets the glaze with distinctive mezcal-smoke + maple-sweetness resonance.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Burrata": "Ironfish Bourbon Mezcal Casks with burrata — Iron Fish MI mezcal-cask against fresh dairy. Avoid; bourbon weight wrong for burrata.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Butternut Squash": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bourbon backbone carries the squash bisque, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Carrot Cake": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet northern MI mezcal-cask. Works; Ironfish Mezcal threads the cake at Michigan-hometown register.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Cheesecake": "Ironfish Bourbon Mezcal Casks with cheesecake — Iron Fish MI mezcal-cask against custard. Works; Ironfish Mezcal threads the cheesecake at Michigan-hometown register.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Chilean Seabass": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks belongs on the steak course.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Chocolate Brownie": "Ironfish Bourbon Mezcal Casks with the chocolate brownie — northern MI mezcal-cask bourbon against cocoa. Strong; Ironfish Mezcal's smoke meets cocoa at Michigan-hometown register — smoky-agave + chocolate is distinctive.",
