  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Creme Brulee": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the oak depth lays under the brulee, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; AE Triple Cask's layered character rides the cream at distinctive register.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Escargot": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks's agave-juniper character lifts the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the smoke meets the umami depth. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Faroe Island Salmon": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Filet Mignon": "Ironfish Bourbon Mezcal Casks with the filet — northern MI farm-to-bottle mezcal-cask bourbon against tenderloin. Strong; Ironfish Mezcal's smoky character frames tenderloin at Michigan-hometown register.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|French Onion": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the caramel-spice register matches the French onion, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; premium KO story wasted on salad.",
