  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|House Wedge": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the wedge's iceberg-and-bleu cool crunch: the bourbon backbone carries the wedge, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; Old World complexity wasted on salad simplicity.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Kansas City": "Kansas City: strip marbling meets Iron Fish Distillery (Thompsonville MI, northern Michigan, farm-to-bottle) bourbon finished in mezcal casks, sibling to Iron Fish Gin already on the menu. Ironfish Mezcal Cask's smoky-agave-finish + Michigan-farm-to-bottle character is the featured Michigan-hometown-exotic-finish-KC pairing — mezcal-cask smoke + strip marbling is a distinctive pairing no other bourbon on the menu offers. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Loaded Potato": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; pour's narrative is underused by the salad.",
