  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Market Fish": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks belongs on the steak course.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Mocha Creme": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the mocha creme, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; aging wasted on the salad.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Mushroom Bisque": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the caramel-spice register matches the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; Fortuna handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks|Mushrooms": "Mushrooms: earthy umami meets Iron Fish MI mezcal-cask bourbon. Ironfish Mezcal's smoky-agave character is the featured Michigan-exotic-mushroom pairing — smoke + earth is textbook, and Ironfish delivers it at Michigan-farm-to-bottle register. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
