  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Beignets": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards' silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift jars against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. J Davies Ferrington Vineyards belongs on the steak course.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Bone Marrow": "Anderson Valley Pinot against pure collagen-fat marrow — concentrated Mendocino Pinot still lacks the tannin needed to cut the render. Never pair. Route marrow to Cabs, Bordeaux, Meritage, or structured bold reds; keep J Davies Ferrington for the filet, chicken, or seafood course.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Bone-In Filet": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards's cherry-coffee tannin sits with the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the medium-body red frames the lean cut, and the cassis plays against the grilled char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Broccoli Cheddar": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards' silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the Pinot body brightens the broccoli cheddar, and the cherry-and-earth note frames the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Broccolini": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards's cherry-coffee tannin leans against the broccolini's tender green — the medium-body red frames the green plate, and the cassis underlines the green edge. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Brussels and Belly": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards's cherry-coffee tannin sits alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the coffee meets the caramel. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Burrata": "Anderson Valley Pinot — dark cherry, blackberry, mocha, refined tannin. The medium tannin meets burrata's creamy-delicate center and the mocha plays against basil-tomato. Works as Anderson Valley Pinot for burrata — concentrated Mendocino; whites and rosés peak higher for the delicate starter.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Butternut Squash": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards' silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift reads alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the Pinot body brightens the squash bisque, and the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; the call holds at neutral register.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Carrot Cake": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards' silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. J Davies Ferrington Vineyards lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Cheesecake": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards' silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift jars against the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. J Davies Ferrington Vineyards belongs on the steak course.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Chilean Seabass": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards' silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift jars against the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- tannin on oily fish goes bitter, where a Pinot at the right register would carry it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. J Davies Ferrington Vineyards belongs on the steak course.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Chocolate Brownie": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards' silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift jars against the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. J Davies Ferrington Vineyards lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Chocolate Cake": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards' silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift flattens the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the J Davies Ferrington Vineyards for the steak course.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Clam Chowder": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards's cherry-coffee tannin plays cleanly against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; capable alongside. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Cowboy Ribeye": "Anderson Valley Pinot — dark cherry, blackberry, mocha, refined-firm tannin, medium body. The refined tannin stretches toward ribeye's big marbled build though body falls short of the cut's fat-and-char demand vs. bolder Cabs. Works as concentrated Pinot for ribeye — Mendocino structure for Pinot-preferring guest.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Crab Cake": "Anderson Valley Pinot — dark cherry, blackberry, mocha, refined tannin. The medium tannin meets crab's sweet meat and the mocha plays against romesco. Strong Anderson Valley Pinot for crab cake — concentrated red on the shellfish starter.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Creamed Spinach": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards's cherry-coffee tannin leans against the spinach's dairy-rich cream — the medium-body red frames the green plate, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Creamy Potato": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards's cherry-coffee tannin reads alongside the potato soup's silky body — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
