  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Shrimp Cocktail": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards' silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. J Davies Ferrington Vineyards belongs on the steak course.",
  "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards|Swordfish": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards' silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- tannin against rare-seared crust reads astringent without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the J Davies Ferrington Vineyards on the steak course instead.",
