  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Asparagus": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character crowds the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- the side needs a crisper register to carry it cleanly. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Diamond Mountain Cab — dark fruit, graphite, mineral backbone, firm tannin. The structured body cuts au gratin's cheese-and-cream weight and the graphite plays against the golden crust. Strong mountain Cab for au gratin — volcanic-soil complexity on the decadent side.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Beignets": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character jars against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Bone Marrow": "Diamond Mountain Cab — volcanic dark fruit, graphite, mineral, firm tannin. The structured body meets marrow's rendered-fat richness and the graphite-mineral frames the bone depth. Strong mountain Cab for marrow — Schramsberg estate complexity and firm structure handle the rich starter.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Bone-In Filet": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon -- Davies Estate, Diamond Mountain, mineral. The Diamond-Mountain-Cab body wraps the bone-enhanced filet, and the mineral edge frames the cut. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Broccoli Cheddar": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character clashes with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Broccolini": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character overshadows the broccolini's tender green stalks -- red weight crowds a green side without lifting it — needs crisp register, not tannin. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Brussels and Belly": "J. Davies — Diamond Mountain Cab with dark fruit, graphite, mineral, firm tannin. The structured body handles pork-belly fat and the graphite plays against charred brussels. Strong mountain Cab for Brussels and Belly — volcanic complexity cuts the rich starter with Schramsberg provenance depth.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Burrata": "Diamond Mountain Cab against burrata's creamy-delicate center — firm graphite-mineral body crushes the milk and basil-tomato-pistachio clashes with volcanic dark fruit. Never pair. Route burrata to rosé, Pinot Blanc, or Sancerre and keep J. Davies for the steak course.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Butternut Squash": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character overwhelms the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Carrot Cake": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Cheesecake": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character pulls against the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- the red's dry-fruit register has no bridge to dessert tang or sugar. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon lands on the steak course — not here.",
