  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Cowboy Ribeye": "Diamond Mountain Cab — volcanic soils, dark fruit, graphite, mineral backbone, firm tannin. The structured body handles Cowboy's marbled bone-in richness and the graphite meets rendered fat. Strong mountain Cab for Cowboy — Schramsberg estate complexity, though rounder Cabs like Caymus peak higher for crowd-pleasing ribeye.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Crab Cake": "Diamond Mountain Cab against crab cake's delicate sweet shellfish — firm-tannin graphite-mineral crushes romesco-and-crab. Never pair. Route crab cake to Chablis, Sancerre, or Champagne and keep J. Davies for the steak course where its volcanic mountain character shines.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Creamed Spinach": "J. Davies — Diamond Mountain Cab with dark fruit, graphite, mineral, firm tannin. The structured body cuts creamed spinach's dairy weight and the graphite-mineral plays against the earthy sauce. Peak mountain Cab for creamed spinach — Schramsberg provenance and volcanic-soil complexity on the classic side. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
