  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Escargot": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cherry-juniper cassis holds the line with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the firm tannin cuts the rich starter, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Faroe Island Salmon": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character fights the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the red's tannin and the salmon's rich oils refuse to integrate. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Filet Mignon": "J. Davies — Diamond Mountain Cab from the Schramsberg estate with volcanic-soil intensity, dark fruit, graphite, mineral backbone, firm tannin, real aging potential. The structured body meets butter-tender filet's lean sweetness and the graphite plays against escargot-butter toppers. Peak mountain Cab for filet — Schramsberg provenance hook. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|French Onion": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cherry-juniper cassis holds with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Grilled Caesar": "Diamond Mountain Cab — dark fruit, graphite, mineral, firm tannin. The structured body meets anchovy-parmesan dressing and the graphite-mineral plays against grilled-romaine char. Works as mountain Cab for grilled Caesar — Schramsberg provenance and volcanic complexity on the classic layered salad.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Gumbo": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character overwhelms the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Honey Roasted Carrots": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character fights the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- red tannin and the glaze's sugar pull against each other — sugar reads cloying, tannin bitter. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|House Wedge": "J. Davies — Diamond Mountain Cab, dark fruit, graphite, mineral, firm tannin. The structured body cuts iceberg-and-bacon and the graphite plays against blue cheese dressing. Works as mountain Cab for the wedge — Schramsberg provenance red choice, though whites peak higher for the classic wedge.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Kansas City": "Diamond Mountain Cab — Schramsberg estate, volcanic soils, dark fruit, graphite, mineral, firm tannin. The structured body meets Kansas City's lean-bold marbled strip and the graphite-mineral plays against the beefy char. Peak mountain Cab for Kansas City — Schramsberg provenance story plus high-elevation concentration on the strip. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Loaded Potato": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cherry-juniper cassis sits beside the loaded potato's richness — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the mineral edge cuts the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Lobster Mac": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cherry-juniper cassis holds with the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the opulent body matches the indulgent side, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Market Fish": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the red's structure is wrong for delicate flesh — built for red meat. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Mocha Creme": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character jars against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Mushroom Bisque": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cherry-juniper cassis reads alongside the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the mineral edge cuts the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Mushrooms": "Diamond Mountain Cab — Schramsberg estate, volcanic soils, dark fruit, graphite, mineral. The mineral-graphite meshes with mushroom umami and the firm structure frames the sauté earth. Peak mountain Cab for mushrooms — volcanic-soil complexity lines up directly with earth-on-earth. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Peanut Butter Brownie": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character clashes with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- savory tannin sits awkwardly on cocoa weight without resolving. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Porterhouse": "J. Davies — Diamond Mountain Cab, dark fruit, graphite, mineral, firm tannin. The structured body frames Porterhouse's dual-texture strip-and-filet and the graphite-mineral plays against both lean and fatty sides. Strong mountain Cab for Porterhouse — Schramsberg provenance and volcanic complexity on the dual-cut classic.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Prime Tartare": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cherry-juniper cassis lifts the tartare's raw beef and brine — the firm tannin cuts the rich starter, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Rainbow Trout": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Roast Half Chicken": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cherry-juniper cassis sits beside the chicken's herbed crisp skin — the concentrated body carries the herb-crisped bird, and the mineral edge lifts the dish. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character jars against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Salt-Cured Halibut": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character clashes with the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character crowds the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- the side needs a crisper register to carry it cleanly. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Seafood Tower": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Seared Scallops": "J. Davies Diamond Mountain Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — firm graphite-mineral obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save J. Davies for the steak course where its mountain Schramsberg character peaks.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Seasonal Soup": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character overwhelms the seasonal soup's house seasonal build -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Seasonal Vegetables": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character overshadows the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate -- red weight crowds a green side without lifting it — needs crisp register, not tannin. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Shrimp Bisque": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the Diamond-Mountain-Cab body wraps the shrimp bisque, and the mineral edge frames the bowl. Works; the side call holds at neutral register.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Shrimp Cocktail": "J. Davies Diamond Mountain Cab against chilled sweet-briny shrimp — firm graphite-mineral is the wrong axis for cold shellfish and cocktail sauce. Never layer. Route shrimp cocktail to Champagne, Sancerre, or Chablis and save J. Davies for the steak course where its volcanic character belongs.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Swordfish": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character overshadows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- dark-fruit weight crowds the seared sesame crust — needs a sparkling or crisp white for lift. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|The Tomahawk": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cherry-juniper cassis finds register with the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the opulent body meets the cap-fat, and the mineral edge lifts the dish. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Tomato Basil": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character overwhelms the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Le Garenne Rosé, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Truffle Fries": "J. Davies — Diamond Mountain Cab with volcanic dark fruit, graphite, mineral backbone, firm tannin. The structured body frames truffle-fry earth and the graphite-mineral cuts the crisp oil-and-salt. Peak mountain Cab for truffle fries — Schramsberg estate provenance meets the decadent side. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character overshadows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- dark-fruit weight crowds the seared sesame crust — needs a sparkling or crisp white for lift. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character jars against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Le Garenne Rosé, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Asparagus": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the bourbon weight handles the asparagus, and the oak-and-spice register settles the side. Works; neutral companion.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with the au gratin — aged Tennessee against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; JD 12 handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Beignets": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon backbone carries the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Bone Marrow": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with bone marrow — 12yr aged Tennessee against umami fat. Excellent; JD 12's aged vanilla-caramel is the featured JD-marrow pairing — the aged depth finally cuts marrow where the entry JDs just sit alongside.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Bone-In Filet": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year -- aged Tennessee whiskey, 12yr premium tier, deeper vanilla-caramel depth. The bourbon depth settles into the bone-enhanced filet, and the vanilla softens the cut. Strong; bonded weight at matched premium register.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Broccoli Cheddar": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the oak depth lays under the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the distinctive character is underused by the salad's simplicity.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Broccolini": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the caramel-spice register matches the broccolini, and the oak frames the side. Works; premium KO story wasted on salad.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Brussels and Belly": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with Brussels + Belly — aged charcoal-mellowed Tennessee against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; JD 12's aged vanilla-caramel meets the glaze at premium register.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Burrata": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with burrata — aged Tennessee against fresh dairy. Avoid; Tennessee weight wrong for burrata.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Butternut Squash": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the oak depth lays under the squash bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Carrot Cake": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with carrot cake — 12yr aged Tennessee against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; JD 12's aged depth threads the cake at premium register.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Cheesecake": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the brown-spirit warmth threads the cheesecake, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; novelty maturation at matched register.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Chilean Seabass": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon weight needs red meat, not the salmon's already-rich oils. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Jack Daniel's 12 Year on the steak course instead.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Chocolate Brownie": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight: the bourbon body sits with the brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; AE CS handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Chocolate Cake": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the bourbon depth settles into the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the pour's complexity is underused by the salad.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Clam Chowder": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chowder, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; boutique-craft doesn't drive.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Cowboy Ribeye": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with the cowboy ribeye — 12yr aged Tennessee against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Excellent; JD 12's aged depth handles the ribeye at premium register; JD Bonded's 100-proof is tied here with more backbone approach.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Crab Cake": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with crab cake — aged Tennessee against delicate lump crab. Avoid; Tennessee wrong for seafood. Reach for a vodka or gin.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Creamed Spinach": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with creamed spinach — 12yr aged Tennessee against dairy-rich side. Strong; JD 12's aged depth rides the cream at premium register.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Creamy Potato": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the caramel-spice register matches the potato soup, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; high proof over-specified.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Creme Brulee": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the bourbon backbone carries the brulee, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; collector-bottle depth gives the dessert ultra-premium character.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Escargot": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's bold caramel-char character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon weight grips the savory plate, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Faroe Island Salmon": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Jack Daniel's 12 Year belongs on the steak course.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Filet Mignon": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with the filet — aged Tennessee against tenderloin. Excellent; JD 12's aged depth frames tenderloin at premium Tennessee register.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|French Onion": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the French onion, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Grilled Caesar": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with the grilled Caesar — aged Tennessee against charred romaine and anchovy. Strong; JD 12's aged vanilla-caramel meets the char at premium register.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Gumbo": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the bourbon depth settles into the gumbo, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the brown-spirit warmth threads the honey carrots, and the oak softens the caramelized sugar. Works; aged premium slightly over-specified.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|House Wedge": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with the House Wedge — aged Tennessee against iceberg and bleu. Strong; JD 12's aged character engages the bleu at premium register.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Kansas City": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with the KC — aged Tennessee whiskey, 12yr premium tier, deeper vanilla-caramel depth. Excellent; JD 12's aged depth is the premium JD-KC pairing — where Old No. 7 is iconic-entry and Bonded brings 100-proof backbone, the 12 Year adds aged Tennessee gravitas.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Loaded Potato": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the bourbon depth settles into the loaded potato soup, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the cream. Works; JD Bonded's backbone handles the richness at Bonded register.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Lobster Mac": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon depth settles into the lobster mac, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Market Fish": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Jack Daniel's 12 Year for the steak course.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Mocha Creme": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the caramel-spice register matches the mocha creme, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; Old World complexity wasted on salad simplicity.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Mushroom Bisque": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the pour's delicacy doesn't overpower the soup, but doesn't particularly elevate it either.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Mushrooms": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with mushrooms — aged charcoal-mellowed Tennessee against earthy umami. Excellent; JD 12's aged vanilla-caramel threads mushroom earthiness at premium Tennessee register.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight sits alongside the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the bourbon backbone carries the PB brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; flagship depth gives the dessert premium aged character.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Porterhouse": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with the porterhouse — aged Tennessee against strip-and-filet. Strong; JD 12's aged depth frames the two-cut plate at premium register.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Prime Tartare": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's bold caramel-char character holds the line with the tartare's raw beef and brine — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; the call lands cleanly.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Rainbow Trout": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Jack Daniel's 12 Year lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Roast Half Chicken": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the roast chicken, and the rounded sweetness brightens the plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the chickpea soup, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; bonded weight overpowers this dish.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Jack Daniel's 12 Year on the steak course instead.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the garlic spinach, and the rounded sweetness brightens the side. Works; the Dylan-brand story is wasted on the salad.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Seafood Tower": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Jack Daniel's 12 Year for the steak course.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Seared Scallops": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with seared scallops — 12yr aged Tennessee against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Tennessee overwhelms scallops.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Seasonal Soup": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the bourbon depth settles into the seasonal soup, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; AE CS meets the char at premium wine-finish register.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Seasonal Vegetables": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the bourbon depth settles into the seasonal vegetables, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; boutique-blend depth gives composed dessert character.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Shrimp Bisque": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with shrimp bisque — aged Tennessee against cream-shrimp soup. Works; JD 12's aged depth rides the bisque at premium register.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Shrimp Cocktail": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with shrimp cocktail — 12yr aged Tennessee against cold shrimp. Avoid; Tennessee wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Swordfish": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Jack Daniel's 12 Year lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|The Tomahawk": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's bold caramel-char character sits with the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the whiskey weight settles into the bone-in cut, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Tomato Basil": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the bourbon backbone carries the tomato basil, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Truffle Fries": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with truffle fries — aged Tennessee against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; JD 12's aged depth meets the earthy-rich at premium register.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Jack Daniel's 12 Year for the steak course.",
  "Jack Daniel's 12 Year|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the brown-spirit warmth threads the curry, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; bold character slightly over-specified for the soup.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Asparagus": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the bourbon backbone carries the asparagus, and the caramel rounds the side. Works; annual-release wasted on salad.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet 100-proof Tennessee. Works; JD Bonded's backbone handles the richness at Bonded register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Beignets": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon backbone carries the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; high proof over-specified for the soup.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Bone Marrow": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with bone marrow — Bottled-in-Bond Tennessee against umami fat. Strong; JD Bonded's 100-proof engages marrow at Bonded register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Bone-In Filet": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's bold char-spice character matches the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the bourbon depth supports the lean cut without overpowering, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Broccoli Cheddar": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the caramel-spice register matches the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; HH 20 is over-specified for an app; save the collector bottle for the main.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Broccolini": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the broccolini's tender green stalks: the bourbon body sits with the broccolini, and the oak frames the side. Works; bonded weight pushes past the soup's register slightly.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Brussels and Belly": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with Brussels + Belly — 100-proof Tennessee against maple-glazed pork belly. Excellent; JD Bonded's backbone cuts the glaze harder than Old No. 7 can.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Burrata": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with burrata — 100-proof Tennessee against fresh dairy. Avoid; Tennessee weight wrong for burrata.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Butternut Squash": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bourbon depth settles into the squash bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; narrative-bourbon doesn't drive.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Carrot Cake": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet 100-proof Tennessee. Works; JD Bonded's backbone threads the cake at Bonded register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Cheesecake": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the brown-spirit warmth threads the cheesecake, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; Vermont-brand at matched register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Chilean Seabass": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Jack Daniel's Bonded for the steak course.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Chocolate Brownie": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight: the bourbon depth settles into the brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; JW Black handles the richness at premium-blend register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Chocolate Cake": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the oak depth lays under the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the pour's sweetness meets the dessert without pushing past.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Clam Chowder": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon weight handles the chowder, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Cowboy Ribeye": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with the cowboy ribeye — 100-proof Tennessee against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Excellent; JD Bonded's higher proof is the featured JD-ribeye pairing — the extra backbone handles cap-fat intensity where Old No. 7 feels under-specified.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Crab Cake": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with crab cake — 100-proof Tennessee against delicate lump crab. Avoid; Tennessee is wrong for seafood. Reach for a vodka or gin.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Creamed Spinach": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with creamed spinach — 100-proof Tennessee against dairy-rich side. Strong; JD Bonded's backbone cuts the cream at Bonded-Act register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Creamy Potato": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the bourbon body sits with the potato soup, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the toast adds a warmth the dessert can accept.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Creme Brulee": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth leans against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the bourbon weight handles the brulee, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; Portwood is over-specified for a side — save for main course.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Escargot": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's bold char-spice character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon depth cuts the umami fat, and the spice frames the umami depth. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Faroe Island Salmon": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Jack Daniel's Bonded for the steak course.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Filet Mignon": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with the filet — 100-proof Bottled-in-Bond Tennessee against tenderloin. Excellent; JD Bonded's extra backbone frames tenderloin with Bonded-Act gravitas — where Old No. 7 is iconic-entry, Bonded is premium-robust.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|French Onion": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the bourbon weight handles the French onion, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; distinctive finish over-specified.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Grilled Caesar": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with the grilled Caesar — 100-proof Tennessee against charred romaine and anchovy. Strong; JD Bonded's backbone meets the char at Bonded register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Gumbo": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the bourbon depth settles into the gumbo, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; bonded weight slightly over-specified.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the bourbon weight handles the honey carrots, and the oak underlines the burnt sugar. Works; oak sits beside the dessert gently.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|House Wedge": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with the House Wedge — 100-proof Tennessee against iceberg and bleu. Strong; JD Bonded's backbone engages the bleu at Bonded-Act register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Kansas City": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with the KC — Bottled-in-Bond Jack Daniel's, 100-proof, more robust than Old No. 7. Excellent; JD Bonded's 100-proof backbone is the featured JD-KC upgrade — the extra proof handles strip marbling more structurally than Old No. 7's standard charcoal-mellowed approach.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Loaded Potato": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the caramel-spice register matches the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; EC 18's aged character meets the glaze at aged-HH register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Lobster Mac": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon body sits with the lobster mac, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; curated doesn't drive.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Market Fish": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Jack Daniel's Bonded belongs on the steak course.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Mocha Creme": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the oak depth lays under the mocha creme, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Mushroom Bisque": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; BIB slightly over-specified.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Mushrooms": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with mushrooms — 100-proof Bottled-in-Bond Tennessee against earthy umami. Excellent; JD Bonded's extra proof threads mushroom earthiness with Bonded-Act gravitas.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the bourbon backbone carries the PB brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; AE meets the char at wine-finish register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Porterhouse": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with the porterhouse — 100-proof Bottled-in-Bond against strip-and-filet. Strong; JD Bonded frames the two-cut plate at Bonded-Act register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Prime Tartare": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's bold char-spice character holds steady against the tartare's raw beef and brine — the caramel-oak depth threads the savory plate, and the spice frames the umami depth. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Rainbow Trout": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the trout's delicate flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Jack Daniel's Bonded for the steak course.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Roast Half Chicken": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the bourbon depth settles into the roast chicken, and the vanilla softens the plate. Works; EC 18's aged character meets the glaze at aged-HH register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chickpea soup, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; Fortuna handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Jack Daniel's Bonded for the steak course.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the bourbon weight handles the garlic spinach, and the rounded sweetness brightens the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Seafood Tower": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Jack Daniel's Bonded for the steak course.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Seared Scallops": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with seared scallops — Bonded Tennessee against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Tennessee overwhelms scallops.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Seasonal Soup": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the bourbon backbone carries the seasonal soup, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; the complex character gives the dessert a refined frame.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Seasonal Vegetables": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the bourbon body sits with the seasonal vegetables, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Shrimp Bisque": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with shrimp bisque — 100-proof Bottled-in-Bond Tennessee against cream-shrimp soup. Works; JD Bonded's backbone rides the bisque at Bonded register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Shrimp Cocktail": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with shrimp cocktail — Bottled-in-Bond Tennessee against cold shrimp. Avoid; Tennessee wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Swordfish": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Jack Daniel's Bonded lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|The Tomahawk": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth rests at register with the Tomahawk's theatrical bone-in marbling and smoky char: the bourbon weight handles the 36oz showpiece, and the vanilla rounds the flame-grilled char. Strong; accessible dessert pairing at the entry register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Tomato Basil": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the tomato basil, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; bold proof overshoots delicacy.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Truffle Fries": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with truffle fries — 100-proof Tennessee against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; JD Bonded's extra backbone meets the earthy-rich at Bonded-Act register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Jack Daniel's Bonded for the steak course.",
  "Jack Daniel's Bonded|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Jack Daniel's Bonded's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the curry, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Asparagus": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the bourbon body sits with the asparagus, and the oak frames the side. Works; the distinctive character is underused by the salad's simplicity.",
  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7 with the au gratin — iconic Tennessee against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Old No. 7's vanilla-caramel handles the richness at iconic register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Beignets": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the caramel-spice register matches the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; save the BTAC bottle for the protein course — the side doesn't deserve the pour.",
  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Bone Marrow": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7 with bone marrow — Lincoln County-Process Tennessee against umami fat. Strong; Old No. 7's vanilla-caramel sits alongside marrow at iconic register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder; JD 12 Year's aged depth is the featured JD-marrow match.",
  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Bone-In Filet": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7's crisp caramel-char character sits with the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the bourbon weight grips the lean cut, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Broccoli Cheddar": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the bourbon backbone carries the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Broccolini": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the broccolini's tender green stalks: the bourbon backbone carries the broccolini, and the oak-and-spice register settles the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Brussels and Belly": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7 with Brussels + Belly — charcoal-mellowed Tennessee against maple-glazed pork belly. Excellent; Old No. 7's vanilla-caramel meets the maple glaze with iconic Tennessee resonance — maple-and-charcoal is a featured textbook pairing.",
  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Burrata": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7 with burrata — iconic Tennessee against fresh dairy. Avoid; Tennessee weight wrong for burrata.",
