  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Carrot Cake": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7 with carrot cake — Tennessee whiskey against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; Old No. 7's vanilla-caramel meets the cake at iconic register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Cheesecake": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the caramel-spice register matches the cheesecake, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; boutique-sourced wasted on salad.",
  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Chilean Seabass": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Jack Daniel's Old No. 7 on the steak course instead.",
  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Chocolate Brownie": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the Twin Oak's depth slightly overshoots the dessert's simplicity.",
  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Chocolate Cake": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; craft-blend covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Clam Chowder": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon depth settles into the chowder, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Cowboy Ribeye": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7 with the cowboy ribeye — iconic Tennessee against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Strong; Old No. 7 handles the ribeye with iconic character; JD Bonded's 100-proof and Sinatra Select's richer oak are better for the heavier cut.",
