  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Creme Brulee": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the bourbon body sits with the brulee, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; grain notes don't really engage the soup but don't clash.",
  "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7|Escargot": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7's crisp caramel-char character finds register with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon weight grips the savory plate, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
