  "Jack Daniel's Sinatra Select|Swordfish": "Jack Daniel's Sinatra Select's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Jack Daniel's Sinatra Select for the steak course.",
  "Jack Daniel's Sinatra Select|The Tomahawk": "Jack Daniel's Sinatra Select's bold char-malt character holds steady against the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the whiskey weight settles into the bone-in cut, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Jack Daniel's Sinatra Select|Tomato Basil": "Jack Daniel's Sinatra Select's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the tomato basil, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; doesn't drive.",
