  "Jefferson's Reserve|Truffle Fries": "Jefferson's Reserve with truffle fries — blended elegance against truffle-parmesan. The smooth profile lets truffle lead; distinct from Woodford's fruit-forward take or BT's straight oak — Jefferson's sits in a polished middle. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Jefferson's Reserve|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Jefferson's Reserve's blended honey and vanilla overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Jefferson's Reserve for the steak course.",
