  "Jim Beam Black Label|Escargot": "Jim Beam Black Label's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the bourbon body sits with the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; boutique character cuts the glaze with craft distinctiveness; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Jim Beam Black Label|Faroe Island Salmon": "Jim Beam Black Label's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the salmon's rich oily flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Jim Beam Black Label belongs on the steak course.",
  "Jim Beam Black Label|Filet Mignon": "Jim Beam Black Label with the filet — 86-proof aged Beam against the 10oz cut. Strong; more body than White Label brings, but still underpowered vs. Weller Special Reserve, Maker's Mark, or Buffalo Trace for the filet.",
  "Jim Beam Black Label|French Onion": "Jim Beam Black Label's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the brown-spirit warmth threads the French onion, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; HH 20 handles dessert density at collector register.",
