  "Jim Beam Black Label|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Jim Beam Black Label's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the bourbon weight handles the honey carrots, and the oak frames the caramelized sugar. Works; BIB structure overshoots the dessert's delicacy.",
  "Jim Beam Black Label|House Wedge": "Jim Beam Black Label with the House Wedge — iceberg and bleu against aged Beam. Works; oak slightly over-specified for the salad.",
  "Jim Beam Black Label|Kansas City": "Jim Beam Black Label with the KC — aged Jim Beam, 8 years in the barrel, 86 proof. The aging gives the pour more weight than White Label and enough oak to carry the strip. Distinct from White Label (too light for the strip); the aged Beam for everyday strip orders. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Jim Beam Black Label|Loaded Potato": "Jim Beam Black Label's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the oak depth lays under the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; 10-year depth overshoots delicacy.",
