  "Jim Beam Black Label|Market Fish": "Jim Beam Black Label's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Jim Beam Black Label for the steak course.",
  "Jim Beam Black Label|Mocha Creme": "Jim Beam Black Label's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the bourbon depth settles into the mocha creme, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; CC 43 Year is over-specified for a soup; save the rare bottle.",
