  "Johnnie Walker Black|Market Fish": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character flattens the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a scotch. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Johnnie Walker Black for the steak course.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Mocha Creme": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the Highland register carries the mocha creme, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; gentle match at matched registers.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Mushroom Bisque": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the scotch backbone matches the mushroom bisque, and the oak underlines the umami weight. Works; boutique over-specified.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Mushrooms": "JW Black with mushrooms — 12yr balanced blend against earthy umami. Excellent; JW Black's balanced smoke + aged-malt character threads mushroom earthiness at benchmark premium register — more balanced than JW Red's bold entry approach.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character leans against the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the PB brownie, and the smoke threads the dessert. Works; bold intensity slightly over-specified.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Porterhouse": "JW Black with the porterhouse — iconic 12yr blended against strip-and-filet. Strong; JW Black frames the two-cut plate at benchmark premium register.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Prime Tartare": "Johnnie Walker Black's blended-smoky character frames the tartare's raw beef and brine — the bourbon weight grips the savory plate. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Rainbow Trout": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character swallows the trout's delicate flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a scotch. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Johnnie Walker Black for the steak course.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Roast Half Chicken": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the malt-driven body wraps the roast chicken, and the honey rounds the plate. Works; premium single-barrel wasted on the salad.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the malt-driven body wraps the chickpea soup, and the honey rounds the bowl. Works; the smooth character gives the dessert a composed frame.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character flattens the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Johnnie Walker Black on the steak course instead.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the scotch depth settles into the garlic spinach, and the malt edge frames the side. Works; Old World complexity wasted on salad simplicity.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Seafood Tower": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Johnnie Walker Black belongs on the steak course.",
