  "Johnnie Walker Black|Seasonal Vegetables": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the scotch depth settles into the seasonal vegetables, and the oak-and-smoke underlines the side. Works; private-selection wasted on the salad.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Shrimp Bisque": "JW Black with shrimp bisque — iconic 12yr blended against cream-shrimp soup. Works; JW Black rides the bisque at premium-blend register.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Shrimp Cocktail": "JW Black with shrimp cocktail — 12yr balanced blended against cold shrimp. Avoid; Scotch wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Swordfish": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon's sweet weight crowds the rare crust's clean char. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Johnnie Walker Black for the steak course.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|The Tomahawk": "Johnnie Walker Black's blended-smoky character frames the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the caramel-and-oak weight rises with the cap-fat. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Tomato Basil": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the tomato basil, and the honey rounds the bowl. Works; annual-release complexity over-specified.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Truffle Fries": "JW Black with truffle fries — 12yr balanced JW against truffle-parmesan. Strong; JW Black's balanced smoke + aged-malt meets the earthy-rich at premium-blend register.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Johnnie Walker Black for the steak course.",
  "Johnnie Walker Black|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the curry, and the honey rounds the bowl. Works; boutique character gives the dessert a craft frame.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Asparagus": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character leans against the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the scotch depth settles into the asparagus, and the heather brightens the side. Works; curated single-barrel slightly over-specified.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Au Gratin Potatoes": "JW Blue with the au gratin — hand-selected rare-cask JW against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; the side is not the place for JW Blue — save the bottle for the filet or KC.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Beignets": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the Highland register carries the beignets, and the heather brightens the dessert. Works; save the collector bottle for the protein course.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Bone Marrow": "JW Blue with bone marrow — hand-selected rare-cask JW against umami fat. Works; JW Blue's silky-complex character sits alongside marrow at collector register but doesn't cut it; save the bottle for filet or KC — reach for Fernet Branca if the guest wants the marrow-cutting experience.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Bone-In Filet": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the scotch backbone matches the bone-enhanced filet, and the honey rounds the cut. Works; the 80-proof softness doesn't overshoot the salad the way heavier bourbons do.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Broccoli Cheddar": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the scotch backbone matches the broccoli cheddar, and the oak softens the cream. Works; the story is wasted on the salad.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Broccolini": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the scotch depth settles into the broccolini, and the malt edge frames the side. Works; richer profile overshoots the dessert's delicacy.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Brussels and Belly": "JW Blue with Brussels + Belly — luxury collector JW against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; JW Blue is over-specified for the side — save the rare-cask bottle for the protein course.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Burrata": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character fights the burrata's fresh basil-tomato-cream delicacy -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Il Colle Prosecco Superiore, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Johnnie Walker Blue on the steak course instead.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Butternut Squash": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the malt-driven body wraps the squash bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the spicy-sweet character gives the dessert a Barton frame.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Carrot Cake": "JW Blue with carrot cake — 60+yr rare-cask JW against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; save the bottle for the protein course — Dewar's 15 or Monkey Shoulder is the right Scotch for carrot cake at appropriate register.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Cheesecake": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the Highland register carries the cheesecake, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; a gentle composed match at the premium tier.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Chilean Seabass": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon weight needs red meat, not the salmon's already-rich oils. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Johnnie Walker Blue belongs on the steak course.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Chocolate Brownie": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the brownie, and the honey rounds the dessert. Works; AE Triple Cask meets the char at distinctive register.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Chocolate Cake": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the malt-driven body wraps the chocolate cake, and the smoke threads the dessert. Works; boutique-sourced doesn't drive.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Clam Chowder": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the Highland register carries the chowder, and the oak threads the cream. Works; BTAC story wasted on salad.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Cowboy Ribeye": "JW Blue with the cowboy ribeye — ultra-premium luxury JW against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Strong; JW Blue handles the ribeye with collector-register silkiness, though the bottle is better spent on the filet (the refined cut that matches Blue's silky-smooth character).",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Crab Cake": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character overshadows the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- the spirit weight crowds the delicate shellfish — no acid to clean the brine. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not a scotch. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Johnnie Walker Blue lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Creamed Spinach": "JW Blue with creamed spinach — 60+yr rare-cask JW against dairy-rich side. Works; JW Blue is over-specified for a side — save the bottle for the main course.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Creamy Potato": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the potato soup, and the oak threads the cream. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for the side — save the collector bottle for the protein course.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Creme Brulee": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character leans against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the scotch depth settles into the brulee, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; JW Blue is over-specified for the side — save the rare-cask bottle for the protein course.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Escargot": "Johnnie Walker Blue's blended-luxury-malt character finds register with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Faroe Island Salmon": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a scotch. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Johnnie Walker Blue for the steak course.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Filet Mignon": "JW Blue with the filet — ultra-premium luxury JW, hand-selected rare casks including 60+yr old stocks, ~$200/pour silky-complex collector icon. Excellent; JW Blue earns its pour on tenderloin — the ultra-premium silky-smooth character is one of the three pairings on the menu where the bottle actually gets what it deserves. Reverence, not just dinner.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|French Onion": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the scotch depth settles into the French onion, and the malt edge frames the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Grilled Caesar": "JW Blue with the grilled Caesar — ultra-premium rare-cask JW against charred romaine and anchovy. Strong; JW Blue's luxury silky-smoke meets the char at collector register; JW Black handles this pairing more economically.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Gumbo": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the malt-driven body wraps the gumbo, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the bowl. Works; Voyage 23 frames the cut at ocean-finish register.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the malt-and-oak threads the honey carrots, and the oak balances the burnt-sugar edge. Works; Voyage 23 handles the richness at ocean-finish register.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|House Wedge": "JW Blue with the House Wedge — ultra-premium JW against iceberg and bleu. Works; the wedge is far too casual for JW Blue — save the rare-cask bottle for something worthy of its register.",
  "Johnnie Walker Blue|Kansas City": "JW Blue with the KC — ultra-premium luxury blended Scotch against an 18oz strip. Excellent; JW Blue's hand-selected rare-cask silkiness handles strip marbling at luxury-register — where JW Black is iconic-premium and JW Red is entry-smoke, Blue is the collector experience on the biggest steak cut.",
