  "Jubilation by Colgin|Market Fish": "Jubilation by Colgin's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the red's structure is wrong for delicate flesh — built for red meat. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Jubilation by Colgin for the steak course.",
  "Jubilation by Colgin|Mocha Creme": "Jubilation by Colgin's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Jubilation by Colgin on the steak course instead.",
  "Jubilation by Colgin|Mushroom Bisque": "Jubilation by Colgin's bold char-chocolate cassis stays alongside the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
