  "Jubilation by Colgin|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Jubilation by Colgin's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- savory tannin sits awkwardly on cocoa weight without resolving. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Jubilation by Colgin belongs on the steak course.",
  "Jubilation by Colgin|Porterhouse": "Jubilation — Colgin cult Napa, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violets, espresso, firm tannin. The firm tannin handles Porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet and the dark chocolate plays against both lean-and-fatty sides. Strong cult Napa for Porterhouse — Colgin on the dual-cut classic.",
