  "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye|Creme Brulee": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the rye-and-oak weight handles the brulee, and the oak threads the cream. Works; the distinctive character is underused by the salad's simplicity.",
  "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye|Escargot": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye's pepper-spice character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the spice frames the umami depth. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye|Faroe Island Salmon": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye on the steak course instead.",
  "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye|Filet Mignon": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye with the filet — allocated premium KO against the 10oz cut. The 10-year depth earns the filet at excellent; the allocated KO for guests who want distinctive-brand premium KY rye. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
