  "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye|Shrimp Bisque": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the rye spice cuts the shrimp bisque, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; master-blender doesn't drive.",
  "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye|Shrimp Cocktail": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against premium KO. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye|Swordfish": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye for the steak course.",
  "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye|The Tomahawk": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye with the Tomahawk — Kentucky Owl's allocated 10-year premium rye. Distinctive branding, premium allocation tier; the KO character gives the Tomahawk a unique premium rye frame distinct from WP's Vermont approach or BT's BTAC. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye|Tomato Basil": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character leans against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the high-rye spice register matches the tomato basil, and the rye-grain bite cuts the bowl. Works; boutique-blend wasted on salad.",
  "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye|Truffle Fries": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye with truffle fries — allocated KO against truffle-parmesan. The 10-year premium character gives the side collector-level frame. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the high-rye spice register matches the curry, and the rye-grain bite cuts the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
