  "Knickerbocker Gin|Truffle Fries": "Knickerbocker Gin's bold citrus-juniper botanicals reads alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Knickerbocker Gin|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Knickerbocker Gin's gin lift with floral-and-pepper sits alongside the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the floral edge frames the tuna, and the juniper threads the plate. Strong; Neptunia's briny character engages the bleu with distinctive maritime profile.",
  "Knickerbocker Gin|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Knickerbocker Gin's bold citrus-juniper botanicals plays cleanly against the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus brightens the spice. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Asparagus": "Knob Creek 12 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the bourbon backbone carries the asparagus, and the oak-and-spice register settles the side. Works; accessible gentle match.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Knob Creek 12 Year with au gratin potatoes — 12-year high-rye against cheese-and-cream. Strong; aged Beam matches richness cleanly.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Beignets": "Knob Creek 12 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the brown-spirit warmth threads the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; EHT Full Proof is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Bone Marrow": "Knob Creek 12 Year with bone marrow — aged 100-proof Beam against umami fat. The 12 years of aging meets marrow's intensity where standard Knob Creek is only strong. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Bone-In Filet": "Knob Creek 12 Year's bold juniper-oak character lifts the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the whiskey character holds register with the tenderloin, and the juniper sharpens the char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Broccoli Cheddar": "Knob Creek 12 Year's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the caramel-spice register matches the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; gentle match.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Broccolini": "Knob Creek 12 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the oak depth lays under the broccolini, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Brussels and Belly": "Knob Creek 12 Year with Brussels + Belly — 12-year aged high-rye meets maple-glazed pork belly. The aged nutty-oak cuts the glaze with premium Beam authority. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Burrata": "Knob Creek 12 Year with burrata — fresh dairy against aged Beam. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Butternut Squash": "Knob Creek 12 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bourbon depth settles into the squash bisque, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Carrot Cake": "Knob Creek 12 Year with carrot cake — 12-year aged Beam against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; aged oak-spice slightly over-specified.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Cheesecake": "Knob Creek 12 Year with cheesecake — aged high-rye against clean custard. Works; aged character overshoots delicacy.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Chilean Seabass": "Knob Creek 12 Year's aged 12 years at 100 proof smothers the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Knob Creek 12 Year belongs on the steak course.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Chocolate Brownie": "Knob Creek 12 Year with the chocolate brownie — aged 100-proof against cocoa. Works; the 12-year depth meets the brownie cleanly.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Chocolate Cake": "Knob Creek 12 Year's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the bourbon body sits with the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; save the bottle for the protein course — a soup is wrong for a $200 pour.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Clam Chowder": "Knob Creek 12 Year's aged 12 years at 100 proof leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon depth settles into the chowder, and the rounded sweetness brightens the cream. Works; annual-release complexity over-specified.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Cowboy Ribeye": "Knob Creek 12 Year with the Cowboy Ribeye — aged 100-proof high-rye against cap fat. The 12 years of aging and 100-proof weight earn the ribeye with Beam's signature nutty-oak character at premium depth. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Crab Cake": "Knob Creek 12 Year with crab cake — 12-year aged Beam against delicate crab. Avoid; pour a crisp white wine.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Creamed Spinach": "Knob Creek 12 Year with creamed spinach — aged nutty Beam against dairy. Strong; oak-aged depth sits with richness at premium register.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Creamy Potato": "Knob Creek 12 Year's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the bourbon body sits with the potato soup, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Creme Brulee": "Knob Creek 12 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the brulee, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the 10-year's restraint lets the soup lead.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Escargot": "Knob Creek 12 Year's aged 12 years at 100 proof leans against the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the bourbon depth settles into the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; AE Triple Cask's layered character meets the earthy-rich with distinctive complexity; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Faroe Island Salmon": "Knob Creek 12 Year's aged 12 years at 100 proof overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon weight needs red meat, not the salmon's already-rich oils. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Knob Creek 12 Year for the steak course.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Filet Mignon": "Knob Creek 12 Year with the filet — aged 12 years at 100 proof. Beam's premium Knob Creek expression; the extra aging gives the nutty-oak character more depth than standard Knob Creek brings. A premium aged Beam-side call for filet orders. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|French Onion": "Knob Creek 12 Year's aged 12 years at 100 proof sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the bourbon depth settles into the French onion, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; the pour's assertiveness is a bit much for the soup but doesn't clash.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Grilled Caesar": "Knob Creek 12 Year with the grilled Caesar — aged nutty-oak Beam against charred romaine. Strong; the 12-year depth earns the Caesar with aged character.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Gumbo": "Knob Creek 12 Year's aged 12 years at 100 proof reads alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the bourbon depth settles into the gumbo, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; bonded weight a touch ambitious for the dessert.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Knob Creek 12 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the honey carrots, and the oak threads the caramelized sugar. Works; the toast notes don't really interplay with the soup but don't clash.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|House Wedge": "Knob Creek 12 Year with the House Wedge — premium aged Beam against iceberg and bleu. Works; aging wasted on the salad.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Kansas City": "Knob Creek 12 Year with the KC — 12-year aged high-rye at 100 proof against the strip's marbling. The aging adds oak depth to standard Knob Creek's nutty character; a premium aged-Beam strip pour. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Loaded Potato": "Knob Creek 12 Year's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the caramel-spice register matches the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the light body doesn't overshoot the salad.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Lobster Mac": "Knob Creek 12 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak depth lays under the lobster mac, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Market Fish": "Knob Creek 12 Year's aged 12 years at 100 proof smothers the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Knob Creek 12 Year lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Mocha Creme": "Knob Creek 12 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the oak depth lays under the mocha creme, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the pour's complexity is underused by the salad.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Mushroom Bisque": "Knob Creek 12 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Mushrooms": "Knob Creek 12 Year with the mushrooms — aged nutty Beam against earthy umami. The 12-year depth gives mushroom character more layers than standard Knob Creek. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Peanut Butter Brownie: peanut butter and cocoa meet aged nutty Beam. Works; nutty character finds PB-and-cocoa territory in a way standard Knob Creek hints at and Knob Creek 12 delivers.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Porterhouse": "Knob Creek 12 Year with the porterhouse — aged high-rye across strip and filet. Strong; 12-year depth leans strip-side, filet tolerates.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Prime Tartare": "Knob Creek 12 Year's aged 12 years at 100 proof sits alongside the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami: the bourbon depth settles into the tartare, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; scale pushes past Elmer T's balance — E.H; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Rainbow Trout": "Knob Creek 12 Year's aged 12 years at 100 proof swallows the trout's delicate flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Knob Creek 12 Year for the steak course.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Roast Half Chicken": "Knob Creek 12 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the roast chicken, and the caramel rounds the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Knob Creek 12 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chickpea soup, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Knob Creek 12 Year's aged 12 years at 100 proof overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Knob Creek 12 Year belongs on the steak course.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Knob Creek 12 Year's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the garlic spinach, and the oak-and-spice register settles the side. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Seafood Tower": "Knob Creek 12 Year's aged 12 years at 100 proof crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Knob Creek 12 Year for the steak course.",
