  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Seasonal Vegetables": "Knob Creek 12 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the bourbon body sits with the seasonal vegetables, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; milestone-edition over-specified.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Shrimp Bisque": "Knob Creek 12 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon depth settles into the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Shrimp Cocktail": "Knob Creek 12 Year with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against aged 100-proof. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|Swordfish": "Knob Creek 12 Year's aged 12 years at 100 proof flattens the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Knob Creek 12 Year for the steak course.",
  "Knob Creek 12 Year|The Tomahawk": "Knob Creek 12 Year with the Tomahawk — 12-year 100-proof against bone-in ribeye. Strong; the aged weight handles the cut but Baker's 107-proof or Four Roses Select's 104-proof bring more grip.",
