  "Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye|Faroe Island Salmon": "Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye's rye-spice character smothers the salmon's rich oily flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye|Filet Mignon": "Filet Mignon: the 10oz center-cut meets Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye — a blend of bourbon and rye at 100 proof. Unique within the Beam lineup; spicy-sweet complexity neither pure bourbon nor pure rye delivers. Layered conversation-starter pour. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye|French Onion": "Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the French onion, and the rye-grain bite cuts the bowl. Works; the bourbon-and-side match sits as a balanced companion.",
  "Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye|Grilled Caesar": "Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye with the grilled Caesar — blended bourbon-rye against charred romaine and anchovy. The rye brightness and bourbon depth together earn this Caesar in a way no single-mash bourbon can. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
