  "Komos Anejo Reserva|Chilean Seabass": "Komos Anejo Reserva's aged-agave character clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- agave and oily fish refuse each other — the fish needs acid, not aged spirit. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Komos Anejo Reserva lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Komos Anejo Reserva|Chocolate Brownie": "Chocolate Brownie: warm dark chocolate meets Komos Anejo Reserva. Excellent; the wine-cask-Hungarian-oak character threads chocolate at luxury-reserve register — distinctive cask influence on cocoa.",
  "Komos Anejo Reserva|Chocolate Cake": "Komos Anejo Reserva's aged-agave character sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the rested-agave depth sits with the chocolate cake, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the dessert. Works; distinctive ceremony over-specified for two-cut plate.",
  "Komos Anejo Reserva|Clam Chowder": "Komos Anejo Reserva's rested-agave body leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the oak-aged tequila body threads the chowder, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Komos Anejo Reserva|Cowboy Ribeye": "Komos Anejo Reserva's rested-agave body sits alongside the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness: the barrel-rested body handles the cap-fat ribeye, and the oak threads the cut. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Komos Anejo Reserva|Crab Cake": "Komos Anejo Reserva's aged-agave character overwhelms the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- aged tequila is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Komos Anejo Reserva for the steak course.",
  "Komos Anejo Reserva|Creamed Spinach": "Komos Anejo Reserva's rested-agave body leans against the creamed spinach's rich bechamel-laced greens: the barrel-rested body handles the creamed spinach, and the oak threads the side. Strong; multi-cask complexity sits with richness at collector-craft register.",
