  "Komos Extra Anejo|Swordfish": "Komos Extra Anejo's aged-agave character clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- aged tequila is wrong register for a main fish or poultry course. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Komos Extra Anejo for the steak course.",
  "Komos Extra Anejo|The Tomahawk": "The Tomahawk: dramatic bone-on showpiece meets Komos Extra Anejo. Excellent; the Komos luxury-icon line's extra-añejo expression matches the tomahawk at ceremonial register — save the bottle.",
  "Komos Extra Anejo|Tomato Basil": "Komos Extra Anejo's aged-agave character leans against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the tomato basil, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Komos Extra Anejo|Truffle Fries": "Komos Extra Añejo with truffle fries — Riedel-luxury aged Komos against truffle-parmesan. The aged depth gives the side luxury-brand frame. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Komos Extra Anejo|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Komos Extra Anejo's aged-agave character clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- aged tequila is wrong register for a main fish or poultry course. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Komos Extra Anejo belongs on the steak course.",
  "Komos Extra Anejo|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Komos Extra Anejo's aged-agave character sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the oak-aged tequila body threads the curry, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Asparagus": "Komos Rosa Reposado's rested-agave body finds neutral with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the barrel-rested body handles the asparagus, and the oak threads the side. Works; aged depth is refined but not a standout.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Komos Rosa Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register reads alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the añejo register carries the au gratin, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; the wine-cask character adds interest but isn't a standout.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Beignets": "Komos Rosa Reposado's añejo-pour depth sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the rested-agave depth sits with the beignets, and the soft-spice note softens the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Bone Marrow": "Komos Rosa Reposado with bone marrow — wine-cask pink reposado against umami fat. Strong; the strawberry-cherry character is a distinctive counterpoint to marrow's intensity.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Bone-In Filet": "Komos Rosa Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register reads register-aligned with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the añejo register carries the bone-enhanced filet, and the cooked-agave note underlines the cut. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Broccoli Cheddar": "Komos Rosa Reposado's barrel-aged tequila weight reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the barrel-rested body handles the broccoli cheddar, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Broccolini": "Komos Rosa Reposado's rested-agave body leans against the broccolini's tender green stalks: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the broccolini, and the caramel-agave register brightens the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Brussels and Belly": "Komos Rosa Reposado with Brussels + Belly — rosé-finished reposado against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; the wine-cask notes don't compete with the dish's sweetness effectively.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Burrata": "Komos Rosa Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the burrata's fresh basil-tomato-cream delicacy: the rested-agave depth sits with the burrata, and the caramel-agave register brightens the starter. Works; clean and composed pairing.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Butternut Squash": "Komos Rosa Reposado's rested-agave body finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the barrel-rested body handles the squash bisque, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Carrot Cake": "Komos Rosa Reposado's añejo-pour depth reads alongside the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the rested-agave depth sits with the carrot cake, and the oak threads the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Cheesecake": "Komos Rosa Reposado's rested-agave body reads alongside the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the aged-agave weight wraps the cheesecake, and the caramel-agave register brightens the dessert. Works; clean and refined but not a marquee pairing.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Chilean Seabass": "Komos Rosa Reposado's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the seabass' buttery seabass flesh: the añejo register carries the seabass, and the oak threads the plate. Works; the 70th's clarity is too delicate to drive the pairing.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Chocolate Brownie": "Komos Rosa Reposado's aged-agave character leans against the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight: the añejo register carries the brownie, and the cooked-agave note underlines the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Chocolate Cake": "Komos Rosa Reposado's aged-agave character finds neutral with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the oak-aged tequila body threads the chocolate cake, and the cooked-agave note underlines the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Clam Chowder": "Komos Rosa Reposado's añejo-pour depth leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the aged-agave weight wraps the chowder, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; Ultra over-specified for small plate.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Cowboy Ribeye": "Komos Rosa Reposado with the Cowboy Ribeye — luxury pink reposado against cap fat. Strong; the wine-cask rosé character is slightly out of register for the ribeye's scale.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Crab Cake": "Komos Rosa Reposado with crab cake — wine-cask-finished pink reposado against lump crab. The rosé character and strawberry threads lift the crab with wine-driven elegance; a distinctive seafood pairing. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Creamed Spinach": "Komos Rosa Reposado's añejo-pour depth leans against the creamed spinach's rich bechamel-laced greens: the aged-agave weight wraps the creamed spinach, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; luxury ceremony over-specified for two-cut plate.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Creamy Potato": "Komos Rosa Reposado's barrel-aged tequila weight finds neutral with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the barrel-rested body handles the potato soup, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; maturation depth composed with this dish.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Creme Brulee": "Komos Rosa Reposado's rested-agave body leans against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the rested-agave depth sits with the brulee, and the cooked-agave note underlines the dessert. Works; luxury ceremony over-specified for two-cut plate.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Escargot": "Komos Rosa Reposado's rested-agave body meets at register with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the añejo register carries the buttered escargot, and the oak threads the starter. Strong; extended maturation sits with richness.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Faroe Island Salmon": "Komos Rosa Reposado with the salmon — wine-cask-finished reposado against salmon richness. The pink character and strawberry notes frame the salmon with rosé-wine logic; the rosa-reposado salmon pairing. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Filet Mignon": "Komos Rosa Reposado with the filet — wine-cask-finished reposado against the 10oz cut. The rosé character and strawberry notes give the filet a different frame than standard reposados bring; a luxury distinctive pour. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|French Onion": "Komos Rosa Reposado's añejo-pour depth sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the barrel-rested body handles the French onion, and the caramel-agave register brightens the bowl. Works; Ultra over-specified.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Grilled Caesar": "Komos Rosa Reposado with the grilled Caesar — luxury pink reposado against charred romaine and anchovy. Strong; the wine-cask strawberry notes give the Caesar a different frame than standard reposados.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Gumbo": "Komos Rosa Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register leans against the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the oak-aged tequila body threads the gumbo, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; 5-year Ultra over-specified for two-cut plate.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Komos Rosa Reposado's aged-agave character reads alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the barrel-rested body handles the honey carrots, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the side. Works; clean agave cuts the glaze but isn't a standout.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|House Wedge": "Komos Rosa Reposado with the House Wedge — luxury pink reposado against iceberg and bleu. The wine-cask character and bleu pick each other up in unexpected ways; distinctive. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Kansas City": "Komos Rosa Reposado with the KC — luxury brand, wine-cask-finished (pink hue from French oak + wine cask). Strawberry, cherry, light oak atop the reposado base. Riedel-designed bottle is part of the presentation; a luxury pour that brings theatrics to the strip. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Loaded Potato": "Komos Rosa Reposado's rested-agave body finds neutral with the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the añejo register carries the loaded potato soup, and the caramel-agave register brightens the bowl. Works; the pour is a touch over-specified for the side.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Lobster Mac": "Komos Rosa Reposado's rested-agave body finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the barrel-rested body handles the lobster mac, and the oak threads the side. Works; 1942 aged depth is a touch over-specified for the small plate.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Market Fish": "Komos Rosa Reposado's rested-agave body reads alongside the market fish's clean white-fish flesh: the oak-aged tequila body threads the market fish, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Mocha Creme": "Komos Rosa Reposado's añejo-pour depth reads alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the barrel-rested body handles the mocha creme, and the oak threads the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Mushroom Bisque": "Komos Rosa Reposado's aged-agave character sits alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the rested-agave depth sits with the mushroom bisque, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; ceremonial over-specified.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Mushrooms": "Komos Rosa Reposado with the mushrooms — wine-cask pink reposado against earthy umami. Strong; the strawberry-cherry layers into mushroom depth distinctively.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Komos Rosa Reposado's barrel-aged tequila weight sits alongside the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the rested-agave depth sits with the PB brownie, and the cooked-agave note underlines the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Porterhouse": "Komos Rosa Reposado's crisp agave-floral character holds steady against the porterhouse's two-cut character — the aged-tequila depth grips the marbled cut, and the oak underlines the char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Prime Tartare": "Komos Rosa Reposado with the tartare — wine-cask pink reposado against raw beef. Works; the strawberry-cherry is an unusual but capable counterpoint.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Rainbow Trout": "Komos Rosa Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register reads alongside the trout's delicate flesh: the oak-aged tequila body threads the trout, and the caramel-agave register brightens the plate. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Roast Half Chicken": "Komos Rosa Reposado with the roast half chicken — luxury pink reposado against roasted chicken. Works; the wine-cask character adds interest but isn't a standout.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Komos Rosa Reposado's aged-agave character finds neutral with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the barrel-rested body handles the chickpea soup, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Komos Rosa Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register sits alongside the halibut's salt-cured flesh: the barrel-rested body handles the halibut, and the soft-spice note softens the plate. Works; clean entry match.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Komos Rosa Reposado's aged-agave character finds neutral with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the rested-agave depth sits with the garlic spinach, and the caramel-agave register brightens the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Seafood Tower": "Komos Rosa Reposado's aged-agave character reads alongside the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the añejo register carries the seafood tower, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the starter. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Seared Scallops": "Komos Rosa Reposado with seared scallops — wine-cask rosé against caramelized scallop. The strawberry and cherry in the finish play with the scallop's sear; a wine-cask-reposado standout. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Seasonal Soup": "Komos Rosa Reposado's rested-agave body sits alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the rested-agave depth sits with the seasonal soup, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Seasonal Vegetables": "Komos Rosa Reposado's aged-agave character reads alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the seasonal vegetables, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; clean but not a standout.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Shrimp Bisque": "Komos Rosa Reposado with shrimp bisque — rosé-finished reposado against cream-based seafood. Strong; the wine-cask notes sit with the bisque distinctively.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Shrimp Cocktail": "Komos Rosa Reposado with shrimp cocktail — rosé-finished reposado against cold shrimp. The strawberry and cherry cut through the cocktail sauce in a way straight reposados can't; wine-cask seafood pairing. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Swordfish": "Komos Rosa Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak: the barrel-rested body handles the swordfish, and the caramel-agave register brightens the plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|The Tomahawk": "Komos Rosa Reposado with the Tomahawk — luxury pink reposado against massive cut. Avoid; rosa reposados are cold-seafood and light-cuts territory.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Tomato Basil": "Komos Rosa Reposado's aged-agave character reads alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the rested-agave depth sits with the tomato basil, and the caramel-agave register brightens the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Truffle Fries": "Komos Rosa Reposado with truffle fries — wine-cask rosé against truffle-parmesan. Works; the pink character doesn't quite align with truffle's earth.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Komos Rosa Reposado's añejo-pour depth sits alongside the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the barrel-rested body handles the tuna, and the cooked-agave note underlines the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Komos Rosa Reposado|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Komos Rosa Reposado's aged-agave character reads alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the barrel-rested body handles the curry, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; the smoothness doesn't drive the pairing but the theatrics do.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Asparagus": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character reads alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the Highland register carries the asparagus, and the malt edge frames the side. Works; JD Bonded's backbone handles the richness at Bonded register.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character sits alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the scotch backbone matches the au gratin, and the oak softens the cream. Works; the pour is a touch ambitious for the salad.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Beignets": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the scotch depth settles into the beignets, and the heather brightens the dessert. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Bone Marrow": "* Lagavulin 8 -- Islay peat, younger-bottling, salt. The scotch backbone matches the rich marrow, and the smoke threads the starter. Gold standard; Lagavulin 8's salt-and-smoke is the ceremonial peated-Islay match for the marrow's umami fat — pour without second-guessing.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Bone-In Filet": "Lagavulin 8 -- Islay peat, younger-bottling, salt. The peat-smoke meets the bone-enhanced filet, and the saline edge frames the cut. Strong; the 10-year gives the pour weight the side can accept.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Broccoli Cheddar": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the malt-driven body wraps the broccoli cheddar, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; Parker's Heritage 16th is over-specified for an app; save the collector bottle for the main.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Broccolini": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character reads alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the scotch backbone matches the broccolini, and the honey rounds the side. Works; accessible gentle match.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and crispy pork belly meet Lagavulin 8's vibrant peat in a clean back-and-forth. Brightness over brute force; the maple-sweetness still leads, the 8-year's smoke frames without crushing. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Burrata": "Lagavulin 8 with burrata — fresh dairy delicacy against peat is a hard mismatch. Even Lagavulin's balanced profile overpowers burrata's cream and basil oil. Avoid across all Islays; reach for gin or a light white wine.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Butternut Squash": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the scotch backbone matches the squash bisque, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; HH 20's aged character meets the glaze at collector register.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Carrot Cake": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character leans against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the scotch depth settles into the carrot cake, and the heather brightens the dessert. Works; the pairing is pleasant but not a standout.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Cheesecake": "Lagavulin 8 with cheesecake — cheesecake's clean dairy-custard register isn't built for peat. The 8-year's brightness can't rescue the pairing; the smoke sits wrong against the custard. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Chilean Seabass": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Lagavulin 8 on the steak course instead.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Chocolate Brownie": "Lagavulin 8 with the chocolate brownie — vibrant peat meets cocoa in a classic Islay dessert move. Less intense than Laphroaig's version, less sweet than Bowmore's sherried take; the 8-year's brightness plays beautifully against dark sweetness without burying it. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Chocolate Cake": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character leans against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the scotch backbone matches the chocolate cake, and the honey rounds the dessert. Works; private-selection wasted on the salad.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Clam Chowder": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the scotch depth settles into the chowder, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; annual-release covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Cowboy Ribeye": "Lagavulin 8 alongside the Cowboy Ribeye — sea-spray and smoke meet the ribeye's cap fat. Reaches for the same register as with the Tomahawk; one for guests who want Islay character with a bigger cut but aren't committed to the longest, heaviest dram on the shelf. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Crab Cake": "Lagavulin 8 with the crab cake — sea-spray and peat steamroll the crab's sweetness. The delicate lump meat can't carry the dram's intensity, even the 8-year's. Seafood-wide avoid for all three Islays; pour a gin or a lighter tequila here instead. Avoid; the pairing fights at the table — point the guest elsewhere.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Creamed Spinach": "Creamed Spinach: the dairy-forward side meets Lagavulin 8's balanced peat. The peat sits beside the cream without quite meshing; the 8-year fares better than Laphroaig's medicinal weight here, but this isn't the Islay's strongest register. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Creamy Potato": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the peat-smoke meets the potato soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; AE CS meets the char at premium wine-finish register.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Creme Brulee": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character leans against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the malt-and-oak threads the brulee, and the oak threads the cream. Works; Discovery complexity wasted on salad simplicity.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Escargot": "Lagavulin 8 -- Islay peat, younger-bottling, salt. The heather-and-honey weight sits with the buttered escargot, and the honey rounds the starter. Strong; craft-blend sits with richness; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Faroe Island Salmon": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a scotch. Avoid; the better calls are above. Pour the Lagavulin 8 on the steak course instead.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Filet Mignon": "Filet Mignon: the restraint and clean beef purity of the 10oz center-cut meets Lagavulin 8's vibrant peat. Capable but not ideal — the 8-year still has too much smoke for the filet's subtlety. Pour Bowmore 12 if a guest wants a peated Islay that actually lifts this cut. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Lagavulin 8|French Onion": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character reads alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the Highland register carries the French onion, and the oak-and-smoke underlines the bowl. Works; IW Harper 15 frames the two-cut plate at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Grilled Caesar": "Grilled Caesar: the charred romaine and anchovy-forward dressing meet Lagavulin 8's bright peat and sea-spray brine. The char echoes the smoke, the anchovy picks up the iodine. The lightest Islay of the three — the Caesar pairing for guests who want peat without a medicinal wall. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Gumbo": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character reads alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the gumbo, and the honey rounds the bowl. Works; master-blender doesn't drive.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character finds neutral with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the Highland register carries the honey carrots, and the oak frames the caramelized sugar. Works; HH 20 frames the two-cut plate at collector register.",
  "Lagavulin 8|House Wedge": "Lagavulin 8 with the House Wedge — the peat overpowers the crisp iceberg and bleu dressing more than it lifts them. Capable only; the spirit steamrolls the salad. Pour as an aperitif alongside rather than as a match. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Kansas City": "Kansas City: the strip's firm marbling and savory char meet Lagavulin 8's balanced peat and sea-spray brine. The 8-year carries the strip cleanly; less intense than Laphroaig with the same cut, more assertive than Bowmore. The middle-ground Islay pour for strip orders. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Loaded Potato": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character leans against the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the scotch backbone matches the loaded potato soup, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; Remus 15 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Lobster Mac": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the scotch backbone matches the lobster mac, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the pour is a touch ambitious for the salad.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Market Fish": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a scotch. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Lagavulin 8 for the steak course.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Mocha Creme": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character leans against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the scotch backbone matches the mocha creme, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; concentrated blend slightly over-specified.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Mushroom Bisque": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the scotch depth settles into the mushroom bisque, and the oak depth meets the umami. Works; Old Fitz 9 brings more depth here.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Mushrooms": "Lagavulin 8 with the mushrooms — sea-spray and smoke meet umami depth. The 8-year is more aligned here than Laphroaig (less medicinal interference) but less remarkable than Bowmore's honey-forward take. Strong without being the marquee Islay call for this side.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character reads alongside the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the malt-and-oak threads the PB brownie, and the malt edge frames the dessert. Works; distinctive character doesn't drive.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Porterhouse": "Porterhouse: two cuts in one plate (filet side + strip side) meet Lagavulin 8's balanced Islay peat. The strip side takes the 8-year's smoke beautifully; the filet side tolerates the brightness better than it would Laphroaig. A solid Islay pour for porterhouse tables. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Prime Tartare": "Prime Tartare: the tartare's mineral depth and raw beef purity meet Lagavulin 8's sea-spray and bright phenolics. The 8-year lifts the tartare where Laphroaig would crush it; Bowmore is too gentle to contribute. Lagavulin is the Islay call for tartare tables. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Rainbow Trout": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a scotch. Avoid; the better calls are above. Lagavulin 8 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Roast Half Chicken": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character finds neutral with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the malt-and-oak threads the roast chicken, and the heather brightens the plate. Works; BIB over-specified for side.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character finds neutral with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the malt-and-oak threads the chickpea soup, and the oak-and-smoke underlines the bowl. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for the side — save the collector bottle for the protein course.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Lagavulin 8 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character leans against the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the malt-and-oak threads the garlic spinach, and the malt edge frames the side. Works; Voyage 23 frames the two-cut plate at ocean-finish register.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Seafood Tower": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Lagavulin 8 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Seared Scallops": "Lagavulin 8 with seared scallops — seared seafood's delicate sweetness gets buried by peat. The 8-year isn't as aggressive as Laphroaig but still too much for scallops. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Seasonal Soup": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character leans against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the Highland register carries the seasonal soup, and the heather brightens the bowl. Works; curated single-barrel covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Seasonal Vegetables": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character leans against the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the malt-driven body wraps the seasonal vegetables, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the side. Works; Boss Hog's allocation story is wasted on the salad.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Shrimp Bisque": "Lagavulin 8 with the shrimp bisque — maritime brine in the dram picks up the bisque's sea-driven base; peat adds dimension. The 8-year's vibrancy prevents the heaviness Laphroaig brings. Surprising but coherent. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Shrimp Cocktail": "Lagavulin 8 with shrimp cocktail — cold poached shrimp and cocktail sauce against peated Islay is a miss across the board. The 8-year's brightness doesn't save it. Avoid; reach for gin or a clean vodka.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Swordfish": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character flattens the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Lagavulin 8 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Lagavulin 8|The Tomahawk": "Lagavulin 8 with the Tomahawk — peat smoke in the dram meets grill char on the cut. The 8-year's bright phenolics carry the scale of the bone-in ribeye without feeling heavy. Aggressive, memorable; for guests who want a peated Islay with a max-impact cut but prefer balance over Laphroaig's medicinal wall. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Tomato Basil": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the malt-and-oak threads the tomato basil, and the oak-and-smoke underlines the bowl. Works; HH 20 frames the two-cut plate at collector register.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Truffle Fries": "Lagavulin 8 with truffle fries — citrus-oil brightness against truffle-parmesan fat. The 8-year's lift complements truffle's earthiness better than Laphroaig's medicinal approach; strong, if not quite the refined pour Bowmore brings. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Lagavulin 8 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Lagavulin 8|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the Highland register carries the curry, and the malt edge frames the bowl. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Asparagus": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis holds with the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the cassis underlines the green edge. Works; the match holds without overshooting. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Napa Cab — Lail entry-level, polished blackcurrant, cedar, dark cherry, refined medium tannin. The refined tannin cuts gruyère-cream weight and the cedar plays against the lactic richness. Works as historically-pedigreed Napa Cab for au gratin — Lail family polish on the cheesy side.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Beignets": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Lail Vineyards Blueprint for the steak course.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Bone Marrow": "Napa Cab — Lail entry-level, polished blackcurrant, cedar, dark cherry, refined medium tannin. The refined tannin cuts marrow's collagen fat and the cedar plays against the smoky mineral depth. Peak historically-pedigreed Napa Cab for marrow — Lail family structure on the rich starter. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Bone-In Filet": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis matches the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the concentrated body carries the strip, and the cassis plays against the grilled char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Broccoli Cheddar": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Broccolini": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis holds with the broccolini's tender green — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the cassis underlines the green edge. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Brussels and Belly": "Napa Cab — Lail entry-level, polished blackcurrant, cedar, dark cherry, refined medium tannin. The refined tannin cuts pork-belly fat and the cedar plays against charred brussels. Strong historically-pedigreed Napa Cab for Brussels and Belly — Lail family polish on the rich starter.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Burrata": "Historically-pedigreed Napa Cab against burrata's creamy-delicate center — Blueprint's full-body cedar-blackcurrant structure overwhelms the starter. Never pair. Route burrata to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Prosecco; keep Blueprint for the steak course.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Butternut Squash": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis sits alongside the squash soup's silky sweet — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Carrot Cake": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Lail Vineyards Blueprint for the steak course.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Cheesecake": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Lail Vineyards Blueprint belongs on the steak course.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Chilean Seabass": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- tannin on oily fish goes bitter, where a Pinot at the right register would carry it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Lail Vineyards Blueprint for the steak course.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Chocolate Brownie": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- savory tannin sits awkwardly on cocoa weight without resolving. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Lail Vineyards Blueprint on the steak course instead.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Chocolate Cake": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Lail Vineyards Blueprint on the steak course instead.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Clam Chowder": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Cowboy Ribeye": "Napa Cab — Lail entry-level, polished blackcurrant, cedar, dark cherry, refined medium tannin, full body. The full body handles ribeye's big marbled build and the cedar plays against beefy char. Strong historically-pedigreed Napa Cab for ribeye — Lail family polish on the bold cut.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Crab Cake": "Historically-pedigreed Napa Cab against crab cake's delicate sweet meat — Blueprint's refined medium-tannin structure buries the shellfish. Never pair. Route crab cake to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Blueprint for filet, strip, or the steak course.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Creamed Spinach": "Napa Cab — Lail entry-level, polished blackcurrant, cedar, dark cherry, refined medium tannin. The refined tannin cuts béchamel's dairy weight and the cedar plays against the spinach base. Strong historically-pedigreed Napa Cab for creamed spinach — Lail family polish reframes the rich side.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Creamy Potato": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis stays alongside the potato soup's silky body — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Creme Brulee": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth pulls against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- the red's dry-fruit register has no bridge to dessert tang or sugar. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Lail Vineyards Blueprint on the steak course instead.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Escargot": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the concentrated body grips the savory plate. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Faroe Island Salmon": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth fights the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the red's tannin and the salmon's rich oils refuse to integrate. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Lail Vineyards Blueprint for the steak course.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Filet Mignon": "Napa Cab — Robin Lail (Mondavi/Inglenook family) entry-level bottling, polished blackcurrant, cedar, dark cherry, refined medium tannin, balanced. The refined structure meets butter-tender filet's delicate sweetness and the cedar plays against escargot-butter. Peak historically-pedigreed Napa Cab for filet — Lail family story on the delicate cut. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|French Onion": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis reads alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Grilled Caesar": "Napa Cab — Lail entry-level, polished blackcurrant, cedar, dark cherry, refined medium tannin. The refined tannin cuts anchovy-parmesan dressing and the cedar plays against grilled-romaine char. Works as historically-pedigreed Napa Cab for grilled Caesar — Lail family polish on the layered salad.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Gumbo": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis reads alongside the gumbo's spiced Creole stew — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis plays cleanly against the carrots' honeyed sweetness — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the cassis underlines the green edge. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|House Wedge": "Napa Cab — Lail entry-level, polished blackcurrant, cedar, dark cherry, refined medium tannin. The refined tannin cuts iceberg-and-bacon and the cedar plays against blue cheese dressing. Works as historically-pedigreed Napa Cab for the wedge — Lail family polish reframes the salad; whites peak higher.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Kansas City": "Napa Cab — Lail entry-level, polished blackcurrant, cedar, dark cherry, refined medium tannin. The refined tannin meets Kansas City's lean-bold marbled strip and the cedar plays against beefy char. Peak historically-pedigreed Napa Cab for the strip — Robin Lail's Mondavi-Inglenook pedigree on the American cut. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Loaded Potato": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis reads alongside the loaded potato's richness — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Lobster Mac": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis stays alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the opulent body matches the indulgent side, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Market Fish": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Lail Vineyards Blueprint belongs on the steak course.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Mocha Creme": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth fights the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- the dry red and the chocolate's sugar refuse each other — tannin reads bitter on the finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Lail Vineyards Blueprint for the steak course.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Mushroom Bisque": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis sits beside the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; capable alongside. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Mushrooms": "Napa Cab — Lail entry-level, polished blackcurrant, cedar, dark cherry, refined medium tannin. The cedar-earth echoes roasted-mushroom glutamate and the blackcurrant plays against the earth depth. Peak historically-pedigreed Napa Cab for mushrooms — Lail family refinement on the earthy side. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- savory tannin sits awkwardly on cocoa weight without resolving. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Lail Vineyards Blueprint for the steak course.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Porterhouse": "Napa Cab — Lail entry-level, polished blackcurrant, cedar, dark cherry, refined medium tannin. The refined tannin handles Porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet and the cedar plays against both lean-and-fatty sides. Strong historically-pedigreed Napa Cab for Porterhouse — Lail family polish on the dual-cut classic.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Prime Tartare": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis frames the tartare's raw beef and brine — the concentrated body grips the savory plate. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Rainbow Trout": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Lail Vineyards Blueprint for the steak course.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Roast Half Chicken": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis reads alongside the chicken's herbed crisp skin — the concentrated body carries the herb-crisped bird, and the cassis plays against the grilled char. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis finds neutral with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper warmth — the opulent body overshoots the light soup. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Lail Vineyards Blueprint on the steak course instead.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis stays alongside the garlic-spinach's buttered greens — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Seafood Tower": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Lail Vineyards Blueprint on the steak course instead.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Seared Scallops": "Historically-pedigreed Napa Cab against scallop sweetness — Blueprint's full-body structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Blueprint for the steak course.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Seasonal Soup": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis reads alongside the seasonal soup's house build — the opulent body overshoots the light soup. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Seasonal Vegetables": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis stays alongside the seasonal garden plate — the opulent body overshoots the light side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Shrimp Bisque": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's deep dark-fruit and grippy tannin finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the structured body wraps the shrimp bisque, and the cassis frames the bowl. Works; the side reads as a measured plate companion.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Shrimp Cocktail": "Historically-pedigreed Napa Cab against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — full-body Blueprint and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Blueprint for the steak course.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Swordfish": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- tannin against rare-seared crust reads astringent without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Lail Vineyards Blueprint lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|The Tomahawk": "Napa Cab — Lail entry-level, polished blackcurrant, cedar, dark cherry, refined medium tannin, full body. The full body meets Tomahawk's massive bone-in ribeye though refined medium tannin reads rounder than firm-tannin prestige Cabs on the grand cut. Strong Napa Cab for Tomahawk — Lail pedigree on the grand scale.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Tomato Basil": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis plays cleanly against the tomato basil's bright acid — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the cassis frames the herb butter. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Truffle Fries": "Napa Cab — Lail entry-level, polished blackcurrant, cedar, dark cherry, refined medium tannin. The refined tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the cedar plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak historically-pedigreed Napa Cab for truffle fries — Lail family structure on the umami hit. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- tannin against rare-seared crust reads astringent without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Lail Vineyards Blueprint for the steak course.",
  "Lail Vineyards Blueprint|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's bold cherry cassis finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the opulent body overshoots the light soup. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée|Asparagus": "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée's bold floral-oak cassis reads alongside the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the rounded sweetness softens the green edge. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Lail flagship multi-appellation Napa Cab — dark fruit, cassis, graphite, dried violet, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts gruyère-cream weight and the dried violet plays against the lactic richness. Works as historically-significant Napa Cab for au gratin — Daniel Cuvée structure on the cheesy side.",
  "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée|Beignets": "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- tannin can't pivot to warm pastry sugar — the pour reads dry, the dessert reads heavy. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée belongs on the steak course.",
  "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée|Bone Marrow": "Lail flagship multi-appellation Napa Cab — dark fruit, cassis, graphite, dried violet, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts marrow's collagen fat and the graphite plays against the smoky mineral depth. Peak historically-significant Napa Cab for marrow — Daniel Cuvée pedigree on the rich starter. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée|Bone-In Filet": "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée's dense blackberry-and-cassis tannin sits alongside the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the structured body wraps the bone-enhanced filet, and the cassis frames the cut. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée|Broccoli Cheddar": "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée's bold floral-oak cassis finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cream — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée|Broccolini": "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée's bold floral-oak cassis plays cleanly against the broccolini's tender green — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the rounded sweetness softens the green edge. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée|Brussels and Belly": "Lail flagship multi-appellation Napa Cab — dark fruit, cassis, graphite, dried violet, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts pork-belly fat and the dried violet plays against charred brussels. Strong historically-significant Napa Cab for Brussels and Belly — Daniel Cuvée structure on the rich starter.",
