  "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée|Shrimp Cocktail": "Historically-significant Napa Cab against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — firm-tannin Daniel Cuvée and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Daniel Cuvée for the steak course.",
  "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée|Swordfish": "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée for the steak course.",
  "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée|The Tomahawk": "Lail flagship multi-appellation Napa Cab — Howell/Calistoga/Oakville/Stags Leap, dark fruit, cassis, graphite, dried violet, firm tannin, full body. The firm tannin handles Tomahawk's massive bone-in ribeye and the graphite plays against smoky char. Peak historically-significant Napa Cab for Tomahawk — Daniel Cuvée pedigree on the grand cut. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
