  "Liberator Gin|Truffle Fries": "Liberator Gin's citrus-juniper botanicals sits beside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Liberator Gin|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Liberator Gin's citrus-juniper botanicals plays cleanly against the tuna's seared rare crust — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Liberator Gin|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Liberator Gin's citrus-juniper botanicals finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus brightens the spice. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Licor 43|Asparagus": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character clashes with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- sugar on a clean vegetable side is wrong direction — needs herb-acid lift, not sweetness. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a digestif. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Licor 43 for the steak course.",
  "Licor 43|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- sweet liqueur and dairy-rich side double the indulgence with no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Licor 43 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Licor 43|Beignets": "Beignets: the beignets' light, airy, powdered-sugar sweetness meets this sweet cream liqueur's dessert-adjacent lushness. Sweet liqueur's dessert-adjacent sweetness amplifies the dessert — doubles up on sugar. Strong when the dessert is restrained.",
  "Licor 43|Bone Marrow": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character clashes with the bone marrow's unctuous rendered-marrow richness -- sweet liqueur is dessert energy — wrong place for the table's first course. The plate deserves Fernet Branca, Lagavulin 8, or George T. Stagg, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Licor 43 on the steak course instead.",
  "Licor 43|Bone-In Filet": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character clashes with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- a sweet liqueur belongs after the meal, not during the steak course. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a digestif. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Licor 43 for another course.",
  "Licor 43|Broccoli Cheddar": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- the liqueur's sweetness buries the soup's creamy base instead of supporting it. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Licor 43 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Licor 43|Broccolini": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character clashes with the broccolini's tender green stalks -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a digestif. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Licor 43 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Licor 43|Brussels and Belly": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character clashes with Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Licor 43 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Licor 43|Burrata": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the burrata's fresh basil-tomato-cream delicacy -- sweet liqueur and fresh dairy compound the richness without contrast — heavy too early. The plate deserves Il Colle Prosecco Superiore, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Licor 43 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Licor 43|Butternut Squash": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- the liqueur's sweetness buries the soup's creamy base instead of supporting it. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a digestif. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Licor 43 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Licor 43|Carrot Cake": "Carrot Cake: the carrot cake's warm-spice, cream-cheese indulgence meets this sweet cream liqueur's dessert-adjacent lushness. Sweet liqueur's dessert-adjacent sweetness amplifies the dessert — doubles up on sugar. Strong when the dessert is restrained.",
  "Licor 43|Cheesecake": "Cheesecake: the cheesecake's dense, tangy dairy richness meets this sweet cream liqueur's dessert-adjacent lushness. Sweet liqueur's dessert-adjacent sweetness amplifies the dessert — doubles up on sugar. Strong when the dessert is restrained.",
  "Licor 43|Chilean Seabass": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the liqueur's sugar piles onto the fish's natural oils with no lift. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Licor 43 on the steak course instead.",
  "Licor 43|Chocolate Brownie": "Chocolate Brownie: this dense chocolate dessert's deep cocoa richness meets this sweet cream liqueur's dessert-adjacent lushness. Sweet liqueur's dessert-adjacent sweetness amplifies the dessert — doubles up on sugar. Works as an indulgence.",
  "Licor 43|Chocolate Cake": "Chocolate Cake: this dense chocolate dessert's deep cocoa richness meets this sweet cream liqueur's dessert-adjacent lushness. Sweet liqueur's dessert-adjacent sweetness amplifies the dessert — doubles up on sugar. Works as an indulgence.",
  "Licor 43|Clam Chowder": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the liqueur's sweetness buries the soup's creamy base instead of supporting it. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Licor 43 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Licor 43|Cowboy Ribeye": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character clashes with the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness -- sweet liqueur on the headline cut is dessert-course energy — save it for after the meal. The plate deserves Macallan 18, Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon, or Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Licor 43 for another course.",
  "Licor 43|Crab Cake": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character clashes with the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- sweet liqueur is dessert energy — wrong place for the table's first course. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Licor 43 lands on the steak course — not here.",
