  "Licor 43|Creamy Potato": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character clashes with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Licor 43 on the steak course instead.",
  "Licor 43|Creme Brulee": "Creme Brulee: this delicate custard's creamy, vanilla sweetness meets this sweet cream liqueur's dessert-adjacent lushness. Sweet liqueur's dessert-adjacent sweetness amplifies the dessert — doubles up on sugar. A headliner match — context-driven peak. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Licor 43|Escargot": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character buries the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- sweet liqueur smothers the herb-bright opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a digestif. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Licor 43 for the steak course.",
  "Licor 43|Faroe Island Salmon": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- a sweet liqueur is dessert-course energy — wrong register for any main protein. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Licor 43 belongs on the steak course.",
