  "Loaded Potato|Licor 43": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup -- sugar piled onto cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Licor 43 on the steak course instead.",
  "Loaded Potato|Limoncello": "Limoncello's sweet liqueur character clashes with the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a digestif. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Limoncello for the steak course.",
  "Loaded Potato|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Willamette Pinot — dark cherry, forest floor, refined structure, low tannin. The low-tannin silk lifts the soup's bacon-cheddar weight and the forest-floor earth plays against the loaded toppings. Peaks from the dish's side; on this wine's card it's strong — below peaks with duck, lamb, and mushroom-sauced proteins. Confident pour when a guest anchors on Loaded Potato. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
