  "Loaded Potato|Vesper": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build holds with the loaded potato's richness — the cocktail lift refreshes against the hearty soup, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Loaded Potato|Veuve Clicquot Brut": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's biscuit-apple acidity reads alongside the loaded potato's richness — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the apple notes lift the custard. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Loaded Potato|Vieux Carré": "Sazerac rye, Pierre Ferrand cognac, Contratto, Bénédictine, two bitters. The rye-cognac depth meets the soup's bacon-cheddar weight and Bénédictine's herbal edge plays against scallion. Works as spirit-forward for loaded potato — sophisticated cocktail route; wines peak higher as dedicated pairings.",
  "Loaded Potato|Villon Cognac": "Villon Cognac's modern profile and soft elderflower edge sits alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the brandy depth wraps the loaded potato soup, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Loaded Potato|Vin Santo": "Vin Santo's Tuscan dried-fruit-and-honey sweetness doubles down on the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup -- sweet wine on cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — heavy, no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a dessert wine. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Vin Santo for the steak course.",
