  "Lobster Mac|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels + Belly alongside the lobster mac -- the bourbon-maple glaze reads alongside the lobster-cheese-cream build. Works; both sides hold at neutral register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Buffalo Trace": "Buffalo Trace's rounded vanilla-and-toffee character sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak depth lays under the lobster mac, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lobster Mac|Buffalo Trace Cream": "Buffalo Trace Cream's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- sweet liqueur and dairy-rich side double the indulgence with no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Buffalo Trace Cream for the steak course.",
  "Lobster Mac|Bulleit Bourbon": "Bulleit Bourbon's high-rye spice-forward depth reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the caramel-spice register matches the lobster mac, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; KBS distinctiveness is slightly over-specified for the two-cut plate.",
  "Lobster Mac|Burrata": "The burrata and the lobster mac -- cheese-on-cheese, the meal goes redundant. Avoid; the table reads heavy without payoff. Suggest Il Colle Prosecco Superiore, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc for the burrata, or Cowboy Ribeye, Far Niente Chardonnay, or The Tomahawk for the lobster mac.",
  "Lobster Mac|Butternut Squash": "The butternut squash and the lobster mac on the same meal -- cream-and-sugar build the close, the meal finishes generous. Works; sequence or share, the build holds.",
  "Lobster Mac|Cade Cabernet Sauvignon": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's bold juniper-mineral cassis finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Camarena Tequila": "Camarena Tequila's añejo-pour depth leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the añejo register carries the lobster mac, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lobster Mac|Campari": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- bitter aperitivo on the supporting side reads as wrong register for the course. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Lobster Mac|Canadian Club": "Canadian Club's workhorse Canadian blend leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the rye-blended Canadian body sits with the lobster mac, and the oak threads the cream. Works; boutique character gives the dessert a craft frame.",
  "Lobster Mac|Canadian Club 43 Year": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the blended whisky body wraps the lobster mac, and the oak softens the cream. Works; complexity wasted on salad.",
  "Lobster Mac|Captain Morgan Rum": "Captain Morgan Rum's green-agave-and-cane lift finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the light-rum body cuts the lobster mac, and the unaged-cane note plays against the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Caribou Crossing": "Caribou Crossing's craft profile is wrong for scallops reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the Canadian whisky weight matches the lobster mac, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; CC 43 Year is over-specified for a side — save the rare bottle for the main course.",
  "Lobster Mac|Carrot Cake": "The lobster mac alongside the carrot cake -- the cream rounds into the sweet close, the meal lands rich and full. Works; the contrast holds, neither course overshadows the other.",
  "Lobster Mac|Casa LBV Port": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness doubles down on the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- sweet wine and a dairy side compound the richness — dessert energy on savory plate. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Lobster Mac|Casamigos Mezcal": "Casamigos Mezcal's rustic mezcal weight finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the wood-fire body meets the lobster mac, and the earthy backbone threads the side. Works; the side-salad call holds.",
  "Lobster Mac|Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon": "Napa Rutherford Cab — concentrated black fruit, cocoa, mocha, velvety tannin. The opulent body meets lobster-mac's cream-cheese richness and the cocoa frames the dense pasta. Strong iconic Napa Cab for lobster mac — crowd-pleasing lushness works on the indulgent side, though opulent Chardonnay often peaks higher.",
  "Lobster Mac|Chambord": "Chambord's sweet liqueur character clashes with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; the better calls are above. Chambord belongs on the steak course.",
  "Lobster Mac|Cheesecake": "The lobster mac and the cheesecake -- the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence hands off cleanly to the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: cream-and-sugar build the close, the meal finishes generous. Works; sequence them or share the table, no clash.",
  "Lobster Mac|Chilean Seabass": "Chilean Seabass with the lobster mac -- the seabass' buttery seabass flesh meets the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: cream and protein share the meal, the build reads full. Works; the side reads as a measured plate companion.",
  "Lobster Mac|Chocolate Brownie": "Lobster Mac and the brownie -- cream-and-sugar build the close, the meal finishes generous. Works; the meal closes cleanly from the side.",
  "Lobster Mac|Chocolate Cake": "The lobster mac and the chocolate cake -- the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence hands off cleanly to the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the cream rounds into the sweet close, the meal lands rich and full. Works; sequence them or share the table, no clash.",
  "Lobster Mac|Chopin Vodka": "Chopin Vodka's bold char-cream neutrality leans against the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Christian Bros Brandy": "Christian Brothers with lobster mac — value brandy against pasta-and-lobster richness. Works; Christian Bros is over-specified for the dish vs Hennessy but handles it functionally.",
  "Lobster Mac|Château Batailley": "Château Batailley's bold leather-tobacco cassis plays cleanly against the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Château Beaucastel": "Château Beaucastel's bold earth-leather cassis reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Château Gombaude-Guillot": "Pomerol Merlot-Cab Franc — Château Gombaude-Guillot, biodynamic Pomerol, 2016, dark plum, truffle, mocha, velvety finish. The velvety texture wraps the dairy-rich lobster-cheese-cream build and the mocha plays with the indulgent weight. Peak Pomerol for lobster mac — plush Merlot handles the richest side. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Lobster Mac|Château Haut Segottes": "Château Haut Segottes's cherry-earth tannin sits beside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Château de Rouillac": "Château de Rouillac's leather-tobacco tannin stays alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Clam Chowder": "The chowder alongside the lobster mac -- both bring shellfish as the headline. Avoid; one is enough. Pair the chowder with Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis; pair the lobster mac with Cowboy Ribeye, Far Niente Chardonnay, or The Tomahawk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Clase Azul Anejo": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak-aged tequila body threads the lobster mac, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; Durango presentation slightly over-specified.",
  "Lobster Mac|Clase Azul Durango": "Clase Azul Durango's aged-agave character sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the aged-agave weight wraps the lobster mac, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Clase Azul Gold": "Clase Azul Gold's rested-agave body sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the aged-agave weight wraps the lobster mac, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's espadín-and-smoke register finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the espadín-and-smoke body wraps the lobster mac, and the campfire register frames the side. Works; too light for dessert density at this level.",
  "Lobster Mac|Clase Azul Plata": "Clase Azul Plata's silky Jalisco blanco with ceramic-decanter presentation sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the blanco-tequila body matches the lobster mac, and the bright blanco register underlines the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Clase Azul Reposado": "Clase Azul Reposado's ceramic-icon reposado character sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak-aged tequila body threads the lobster mac, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Lobster Mac|Clase Azul Ultra": "Clase Azul Ultra's aged-agave character finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the rested-agave depth sits with the lobster mac, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; luxury ceremony over-specified for two-cut plate.",
  "Lobster Mac|Clermont Steep": "Clermont Steep's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the brown-spirit warmth threads the lobster mac, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; milestone-release doesn't drive.",
  "Lobster Mac|Clos Petit Ona Grenache": "Clos Petit Ona Grenache's char-earth tannin reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Codigo 1530 Rosa": "Codigo 1530 Rosa's aged-agave character reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the lobster mac, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the side. Works; Durango ceremony over-specified for small plate.",
  "Lobster Mac|Contratto Vermouth": "Contratto Vermouth's vermouth-wine-base sweetness stays alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the bitter herb edge cuts the rich side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Corazon Blanco": "Corazon Blanco's blanco-tequila or blanco-tequila register leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the lobster mac, and the unaged-cane note plays against the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Corazon Reposado": "Corazon Reposado's barrel-aged tequila weight sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak-aged tequila body threads the lobster mac, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the side. Works; Durango presentation slightly over-specified.",
  "Lobster Mac|Corazon Sazerac": "Corazon Sazerac's barrel-aged tequila weight finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the barrel-rested body handles the lobster mac, and the oak threads the side. Works; the agave cuts the glaze but the pairing isn't marquee.",
  "Lobster Mac|Corazon Stagg": "Corazon Stagg's barrel-aged tequila weight sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the barrel-rested body handles the lobster mac, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Corazon Weller": "Corazon Weller's añejo-pour depth leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the añejo register carries the lobster mac, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; boutique agave brightness is an unusual counterpoint.",
  "Lobster Mac|Corazón del Sol Malbec": "Corazón del Sol Malbec's bold floral cassis stays alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Corpse Reviver": "Corpse Reviver's shaken-and-bright cocktail register sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bright build frames the lobster mac, and the citrus cuts the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Courvoisier Cognac": "Courvoisier with lobster mac — Napoleon-era cognac against pasta-and-lobster richness. Strong; Courvoisier's drier oak frames the richness with structural lift.",
  "Lobster Mac|Cowboy Ribeye": "* The cowboy ribeye with the lobster mac -- the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness frames the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence. Gold standard; the side that defines the steak course.",
  "Lobster Mac|Crab Cake": "The crab cake and the lobster mac share shellfish as the primary character. Avoid; the meal doubles down without contrast. Route the crab cake with Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin or the lobster mac with Cowboy Ribeye, Far Niente Chardonnay, or The Tomahawk instead.",
  "Lobster Mac|Cragganmore 12": "Cragganmore 12's complex Speyside character leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the lobster mac, and the oak threads the cream. Works; the Dylan-brand story is wasted on the salad.",
  "Lobster Mac|Creamy Potato": "The potato soup alongside the lobster mac -- cream stacked on cream, the plate reads dense across the meal. Works; the table can build them in order or together.",
  "Lobster Mac|Creme Brulee": "The lobster mac and the brulee -- the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence hands off cleanly to the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: rich dairy yields to dessert weight, the close composes thickly. Works; sequence them or share the table, no clash.",
  "Lobster Mac|Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée": "Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée's cherry-earth tannin sits beside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Crown Royal": "Crown Royal's classic Canadian blend smoothness sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the smooth Canadian register carries the lobster mac, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; the sweetness is a touch much for the salad's simplicity.",
  "Lobster Mac|Cucumber Gimlet": "Cucumber Gimlet: this gin cocktail's citrus brightness and botanical lift meets this rich, creamy side's dairy-driven indulgence. Citrus cocktail against rich, dairy-heavy side — acid cuts fat but brightness overreaches. Works as a contrast pour.",
  "Lobster Mac|Dalmore 12": "Dalmore 12's sherry-finished Highland character leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the malt-driven body wraps the lobster mac, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; the sherry-cask character rides the cream at benchmark register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge": "Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge's crisp earth-mineral tannin stays alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lobster Mac|Darioush Cabernet Franc": "Darioush Cabernet Franc's cherry-floral tannin leans against the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's bold coffee-mocha cassis stays alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Detroit City Gin": "Detroit City Gin's bold char-juniper botanicals sits beside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the juniper carries the shellfish. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Detroit City Vodka": "Detroit City Vodka's hometown craft vodka finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the crystalline body carries the lobster mac, and the bright vodka edge brightens the side. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Dewar's 15": "Dewar's 15's Highland-scotch character leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the lobster mac, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; the pour's delicacy doesn't overpower the soup, but doesn't particularly elevate it either.",
  "Lobster Mac|Dewar's White Label": "Dewar's White Label's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the malt-and-oak threads the lobster mac, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; curated doesn't drive.",
  "Lobster Mac|Disaronno": "Disaronno's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- the liqueur's sugar buries the side's cream instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Disaronno on the steak course instead.",
  "Lobster Mac|Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye": "Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye's rye-spice character leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the dry rye body wraps the lobster mac, and the oak threads the cream. Works; the complex character is wasted on the salad.",
  "Lobster Mac|Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum": "Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum's rich layered-spirit body finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the rich pour wraps the lobster mac, and the deep backbone frames the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lobster Mac|Domaine Serene Grand Cheval": "Willamette flagship Pinot Blend — dark cherry, Bing cherry, toasted spice, forest floor, silky. The acid cuts lobster-mac's cream-cheese richness and the toasted-spice plays against the dense pasta. Works as flagship Willamette Pinot for the lobster mac side — Oregon layering; accessible Chard peaks higher.",
  "Lobster Mac|Domaine Tempier Bandol": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's bold earth-mineral cassis stays alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the smoke meets the umami depth. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé": "Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé's citrus-mineral acidity reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Domaine du Grand Tinel": "Domaine du Grand Tinel's bold earth-herbal cassis sits beside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the opulent body matches the indulgent side, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Don Fulano Anejo": "Don Fulano Anejo's rested-agave body sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak-aged tequila body threads the lobster mac, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Don Fulano Blanco": "Don Fulano Blanco's blanco-tequila or blanco-tequila register sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the lobster mac, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Don Fulano Reposado": "Don Fulano Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the barrel-rested body handles the lobster mac, and the oak threads the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lobster Mac|Don Julio 1942": "Don Julio 1942's icon extra-añejo character sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the rested-agave depth sits with the lobster mac, and the caramel-agave register brightens the side. Works; cedar and maple don't quite align.",
  "Lobster Mac|Don Julio 70th": "Don Julio 70th's aged-agave character finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the lobster mac, and the oak threads the side. Works; the bold agave overpowers the dish's restraint.",
  "Lobster Mac|Don Julio Blanco": "Don Julio Blanco's workhorse blanco with clean agave snap sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the unaged blanco body cuts the lobster mac, and the bright blanco register underlines the side. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Don Julio Reposado": "Don Julio Reposado's rested-agave body sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak-aged tequila body threads the lobster mac, and the oak threads the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Drambuie": "Drambuie's sweet liqueur character clashes with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Drambuie lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Lobster Mac|Dunville's Single Malt": "Dunville's Single Malt's Irish whiskey smoothness sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the approachable Irish character carries the lobster mac, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; JW Blue is over-specified for a side — save the bottle for the main course.",
  "Lobster Mac|E.H. Taylor Full Proof": "E.H. Taylor Full Proof's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the lobster mac, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; bold proof overshoots delicacy.",
  "Lobster Mac|E.H. Taylor Rye": "E.H. Taylor Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the rye spice cuts the lobster mac, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; aging wasted on the salad.",
  "Lobster Mac|E.H. Taylor Small Batch": "E.H. Taylor Small Batch's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the brown-spirit warmth threads the lobster mac, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; own-plus-sourced over-specified.",
  "Lobster Mac|Eagle Rare 10 Year": "Eagle Rare 10 Year's aged-oak elegance sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the caramel-spice register matches the lobster mac, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the premium pour is wasted on the salad's simplicity.",
