  "Lobster Mac|Elijah Craig Straight Rye": "Elijah Craig Straight Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the high-rye spice register matches the lobster mac, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; Voyage 23 frames the two-cut plate at ocean-finish register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Elk Cove Five Mountain": "Elk Cove Five Mountain's cherry-clove tannin sits beside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lobster Mac|Elk Cove Pinot Blanc": "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc: this crisp white's citrus-driven acidity and mineral edge meets this rich, creamy side's dairy-driven indulgence. Crisp white acidity cuts dairy richness — palate-cleansing counterpoint. Strong — the acid refreshes the fat.",
  "Lobster Mac|Elmer T. Lee": "Elmer T. Lee's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the brown-spirit warmth threads the lobster mac, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; mid-proof pour is slightly over-specified.",
  "Lobster Mac|Empress 1908 Gin": "Empress 1908 Gin's bold anise-butter botanicals reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Epoch Ingenuity": "Epoch Ingenuity's bold pepper-smoke cassis plays cleanly against the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the smoke meets the umami depth. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Escargot": "Escargot and the lobster mac -- dairy plays against umami, the table reads layered. Works; both items hold their register, no clash.",
  "Lobster Mac|Espresso Martini": "Espresso Martini's roasted-coffee martini richness doubles down on the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- cocktail whiskey and dairy side meet without contrast — both heavy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a spirit-forward cocktail. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Espresso Martini on the steak course instead.",
  "Lobster Mac|Espresso Old Fashioned": "Buffalo Trace, Buffalo Bourbon Cream, Frangelico, espresso, brown sugar, Angostura. Coffee bitterness fights our truffle roux's nuance; the cocktail's weight buries the lobster. Reserve for the marrow or steak course. Avoid; route the table to a better-matched pour.",
  "Lobster Mac|Evening Land Seven Springs": "Evening Land Seven Springs's cherry-earth tannin stays alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the smoke meets the umami depth. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon": "Lobster Mac: dark-fruit Cab body settles into the cream-rich side; firm tannin cuts the lactic edge and the oak threads the indulgence. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Lobster Mac|Far Niente Chardonnay": "Far Niente Chardonnay -- Napa Chardonnay, tropical fruit, oak. The cool-climate register carries the lobster mac, and the green-apple edge brightens the side. Excellent; a confident headline pairing. Gold standard; the headline call at the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Faroe Island Salmon": "Faroe Island Salmon with the lobster mac -- the salmon's rich oily flesh meets the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: cream meets protein, the meal builds with weight. Works; the side reads as a measured plate companion.",
  "Lobster Mac|Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi": "Super Tuscan — Le Pupille Saffredi Maremma, Cab-Merlot-Petit Verdot, 2021, blackcurrant, tobacco, graphite, Mediterranean herbs, firm-tannin finish. The firm tannin reads heavier than lobster-cheese-cream delicacy demands but Mediterranean herbs play with the indulgent build. Works for lobster mac — Chardonnay fits the dairy cleaner.",
  "Lobster Mac|Faust Napa Valley Cabernet": "Faust Napa Valley Cabernet's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the opulent body matches the indulgent side, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía": "Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía's cherry-earth tannin sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Fernet Branca": "Fernet Branca's nuclear bitter-menthol intensity stays alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the bitter herb edge cuts the rich side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Fernet Menta": "Fernet Menta's crisp mint-menthol edge plays cleanly against the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the bitter herb edge cuts the rich side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Filet Mignon": "The filet alongside the lobster mac -- the filet's lean buttery tenderness frames the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence. Excellent; the pairing earns its featured slot.",
  "Lobster Mac|Fireball Whisky": "Fireball Whisky's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- the liqueur's sugar buries the side's cream instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Fireball Whisky for the steak course.",
  "Lobster Mac|Fisher Unity Pinot Noir": "Sonoma Pinot — cranberry, red cherry, baking spice, silky. The acid cuts lobster-mac's cream-cheese richness and the cherry plays against the dense pasta. Works as by-the-glass Pinot for the lobster mac side — unconventional red pick, accessible Chard peaks higher.",
  "Lobster Mac|Four Roses Small Batch Select": "Four Roses Small Batch Select's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the lobster mac, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; neutral, not elevating.",
  "Lobster Mac|Four Roses Yellow Label": "Four Roses Yellow Label's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon body sits with the lobster mac, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; AE CS handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Fox & Oden": "Fox & Oden's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon depth settles into the lobster mac, and the rounded sweetness brightens the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Fox & Oden Double Oaked": "Fox & Oden Double Oaked's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon depth settles into the lobster mac, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the private select's layered profile underserves the dessert's simplicity.",
  "Lobster Mac|Frangelico": "Frangelico's Piedmont hazelnut depth to mocha at after-dinner register clashes with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Frangelico on the steak course instead.",
  "Lobster Mac|Freemark Abbey Bosché": "Freemark Abbey Bosché's bold juniper-leather cassis holds with the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the opulent body matches the indulgent side, and the juniper carries the shellfish. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|French 75": "French 75's citrus-earth build finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the oak frames the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|French Onion": "The French onion and the lobster mac -- both cheese-forward, the table doubles up on cheese. Avoid; pick one or the other. Pair the French onion with Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée; pair the lobster mac with Cowboy Ribeye, Far Niente Chardonnay, or The Tomahawk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Frias Block 5": "Frias Block 5's bold herbal-umami cassis holds with the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo": "G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo's structured dark-fruit weight sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the structured body wraps the lobster mac, and the cassis frames the side. Works; the two sides share the meal without competing.",
  "Lobster Mac|G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti": "G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti's peach-and-honey frizzante sweetness mis-pairs with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- sparkling is opener territory — the side reads small under its lift. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a sparkling. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Lobster Mac|G4 Blanco": "G4 Blanco's unaged silver-spirit body sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the blanco-tequila body matches the lobster mac, and the unaged-cane note plays against the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lobster Mac|G4 High Proof": "G4 High Proof's cooked-agave-and-oak register leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the añejo register carries the lobster mac, and the oak threads the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Garavogue Irish Whiskey": "Garavogue Irish Whiskey's Irish whiskey smoothness sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the gentle Irish body threads the lobster mac, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; private-selection wasted on the salad.",
  "Lobster Mac|George T. Stagg": "George T. Stagg's cask-strength BTAC bourbon power finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the brown-spirit warmth threads the lobster mac, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Lobster Mac|Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon": "Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cherry-oak cassis sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the opulent body matches the indulgent side, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Ghost Block Zinfandel": "Ghost Block Zinfandel's bold pepper-spice cassis finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lobster Mac|Glenfiddich 12": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the scotch depth settles into the lobster mac, and the oak threads the cream. Works; neutral companion.",
  "Lobster Mac|Glenfiddich 14": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the Highland register carries the lobster mac, and the oak threads the cream. Works; the complex profile is over-specified for this dish.",
  "Lobster Mac|Glenfiddich 18": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the malt-and-oak threads the lobster mac, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; Parker's Heritage 16th handles the richness at annual-release register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the scotch depth settles into the lobster mac, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; Vermont-brand character doesn't drive.",
  "Lobster Mac|Glenglassaugh 12": "Glenglassaugh 12's Highland-scotch character leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the scotch depth settles into the lobster mac, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; gentle match.",
  "Lobster Mac|Glenlivet 12": "Glenlivet 12's entry Speyside character reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the lobster mac, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Glenmorangie 10": "Glenmorangie 10's tallest-stills Highland bourbon-cask character reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the malt-driven body wraps the lobster mac, and the oak threads the cream. Works; the smooth character gives the dessert a composed frame.",
  "Lobster Mac|Glenmorangie 18": "Glenmorangie 18's aged Highland with Oloroso finish finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the malt-driven body wraps the lobster mac, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the toast adds a warmth the dessert can accept.",
  "Lobster Mac|Graham's 10 Year Tawny": "Graham's 10 Year Tawny's dessert-wine sweetness doubles down on the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- sweet wine and a dairy side compound the richness — dessert energy on savory plate. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Graham's 10 Year Tawny lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Lobster Mac|Graham's 20 Year Tawny": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth clashes with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Reserve the Graham's 20 Year Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Lobster Mac|Graham's 2017 Vintage Port": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight doubles down on the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- sweet wine and a dairy side compound the richness — dessert energy on savory plate. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Graham's 2017 Vintage Port belongs on the steak course.",
  "Lobster Mac|Gran Patron Platinum": "Gran Patron Platinum's unaged silver-spirit body leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the silver-spirit register lifts the lobster mac, and the bright blanco register underlines the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Grand Marnier": "Grand Marnier's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- sweet liqueur and dairy-rich side double the indulgence with no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Grand Marnier lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Lobster Mac|Gray Whale Gin": "Gray Whale Gin's bold citrus-herbal botanicals sits beside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Green Chartreuse": "Green Chartreuse's bittersweet rhubarb-and-orange edge reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the herbal cut works the lobster mac, and the amaro backbone frames the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Grey Goose Vodka": "Grey Goose Vodka's neutral vodka register finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the unflavored body sits with the lobster mac, and the crisp profile carries the side. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Grilled Caesar": "The Caesar and the lobster mac -- cheese-on-cheese, the meal goes redundant. Avoid; the table reads heavy without payoff. Suggest Green Chartreuse, Tanqueray Gin, or Scavino Barolo for the Caesar, or Cowboy Ribeye, Far Niente Chardonnay, or The Tomahawk for the lobster mac.",
  "Lobster Mac|Gumbo": "The gumbo alongside the lobster mac -- the spiced course breaks the cream, the table reads balanced. Works; the table can build them in order or together.",
  "Lobster Mac|Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet": "Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet's bold earth-umami cassis holds with the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the opulent body matches the indulgent side, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|HDW 100 Vodka": "HDW 100 Vodka's char-herbal neutrality plays cleanly against the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Lobster Mac|Hakushu 12 Year": "Hakushu 12 with lobster mac — Suntory Forest-Distillery single malt against pasta-and-lobster. Works; Hakushu's subtle peat handles the rich dish at distinctive register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the lobster mac, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; save the bottle for the protein course — a soup is wrong for a $200 pour.",
  "Lobster Mac|Hangar 1 Vodka": "Hangar 1 Vodka's neutral vodka register reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the unflavored body sits with the lobster mac, and the crisp profile carries the side. Works; the glacial-clean finish is a luxury-register Russian-tradition dessert finisher.",
  "Lobster Mac|Head Fake": "Head Fake's sweet citrus-lemon build sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the sweet character sits at digestif register, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Lobster Mac|Heaven Hill 20 Year": "Heaven Hill 20 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the brown-spirit warmth threads the lobster mac, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; CC 43 Year is over-specified for a soup; save the rare bottle.",
  "Lobster Mac|Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond": "Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon body sits with the lobster mac, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the 80-proof softness doesn't overshoot the salad the way heavier bourbons do.",
  "Lobster Mac|Heaven's Door 10 Year": "Heaven's Door 10 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon backbone carries the lobster mac, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; KBS distinctiveness is slightly over-specified for the two-cut plate.",
  "Lobster Mac|Heitz Martha's Vineyard": "Heitz Martha's Vineyard's bold eucalyptus-herbal cassis leans against the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Heitz Trailside Vineyard": "Heitz Trailside Vineyard's bold cherry-mint cassis finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Hendricks Flora Adora": "Hendricks Flora Adora's crisp char-elderflower botanicals sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the honey threads the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lobster Mac|Hendricks Gin": "Hendricks Gin's crisp cucumber-rose botanicals sits beside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the floral edge frames the shellfish. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Lobster Mac|Hendricks Grand Cabaret": "Hendricks Grand Cabaret's bold anise-char botanicals sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the juniper carries the shellfish. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Hendricks Neptunia": "Hendricks Neptunia's crisp anise-brine botanicals sits beside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Hendricks Orbium": "Hendricks Orbium's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Hennessy Cognac": "Hennessy with lobster mac — VS/VSOP benchmark against pasta-and-lobster richness. Strong; Hennessy's oak frames the richness without fighting it.",
  "Lobster Mac|Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the brown-spirit warmth threads the lobster mac, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; light body doesn't overshoot.",
  "Lobster Mac|Hibiki Japanese Harmony": "Hibiki Harmony with lobster mac — refined premium blend against pasta-and-lobster richness. Works; Hibiki's elegant harmony handles the rich dish at premium register.",
  "Lobster Mac|House Wedge": "The wedge and the lobster mac share cheese as the primary character. Avoid; the meal doubles down without contrast. Route the wedge with St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Weller 12 Year, or Le Garenne Rosé or the lobster mac with Cowboy Ribeye, Far Niente Chardonnay, or The Tomahawk instead.",
  "Lobster Mac|I.W. Harper 15 Year": "I.W. Harper 15 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the lobster mac, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; annual-release wasted on salad.",
  "Lobster Mac|Il Colle Prosecco Superiore": "Il Colle Prosecco Superiore's crisp apple-citrus acidity plays cleanly against the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Inhibited": "Tito's, Kahlúa, Bailey's, chocolate liqueur, espresso, chocolate-drizzled glass. Cream-on-cream with the lobster mac's dairy richness; Bailey's softens the cheese weight and espresso cuts through. Strong unconventional pairing when guest wants indulgent cocktail alongside the most indulgent side.",
  "Lobster Mac|Inverroche Gin": "Inverroche Gin's crisp earth-floral botanicals holds with the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Iron Fish Gin": "Iron Fish Gin's cask-strength citrus-earth botanicals plays cleanly against the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the honey threads the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the brown-spirit warmth threads the lobster mac, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Lobster Mac|Isaac Bowman Port Finish": "Isaac Bowman Port Finish's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon weight handles the lobster mac, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|J Davies Ferrington Vineyards": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards's cherry-coffee tannin reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Lobster Mac|J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cherry-juniper cassis holds with the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the opulent body matches the indulgent side, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; the call holds at register.",
