  "Lobster Mac|Johnnie Walker Black": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the Highland register carries the lobster mac, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; a gentle composed match at the premium tier.",
  "Lobster Mac|Johnnie Walker Blue": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the malt-driven body wraps the lobster mac, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; Voyage 23 frames the cut at ocean-finish register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Johnnie Walker Red": "Johnnie Walker Red's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the scotch depth settles into the lobster mac, and the oak threads the cream. Works; the 10-year BIB depth gives the dessert substantial weight.",
  "Lobster Mac|Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon": "Alexander Valley Cab — cassis, plum, cedar, mint, fine tannin. The elegant body meets lobster-mac's cream-cheese richness and the cedar plays against the dense pasta. Strong Jordan for lobster mac — refined balance handles the indulgent side, though opulent Chardonnay often peaks higher.",
  "Lobster Mac|Joseph Mellot Sancerre": "Joseph Mellot Sancerre's crisp citrus-mineral acidity leans against the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Jubilation by Colgin": "Jubilation by Colgin's bold char-chocolate cassis reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the opulent body matches the indulgent side, and the juniper carries the shellfish. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Jung and Wulff Guyana": "Jung and Wulff Guyana's deep-bodied spirit register reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the heavy body handles the lobster mac, and the dense weight underlines the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Jung and Wulff Trinidad": "Jung and Wulff Trinidad's dense-spirit weight finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the rich pour wraps the lobster mac, and the deep backbone frames the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Kahlua": "Kahlua's sweet liqueur character clashes with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Kahlua for the steak course.",
  "Lobster Mac|Kansas City": "Kansas City alongside the lobster mac -- the KC's lean-bold strip with savory grain carries cleanly into the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence. Excellent; the headline side pairing for the KC.",
  "Lobster Mac|Keenan Chardonnay": "Spring Mountain Napa Chardonnay — green apple, lemon curd, subtle oak, bright acidity. The bright acid cuts lobster-mac's cream-cheese richness and the subtle oak adds depth without crushing the lobster's delicate sweetness. Peak balanced Chardonnay for lobster mac — mountain structure meets indulgent side. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
