  "Lobster Mac|Los Vecinos Mezcal": "Los Vecinos Mezcal's rustic mezcal weight leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the wood-fire body meets the lobster mac, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Louis XIII Cognac": "Louis XIII with lobster mac — 1,200-eaux-de-vie cognac against pasta-and-lobster. Works; the rich dish is over-specified for a bottle meant to be savored alone — save the Louis XIII.",
  "Lobster Mac|Lucano Amaro": "Lucano Amaro's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- bitter aperitivo on the supporting side reads as wrong register for the course. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Lucano Amaro for the steak course.",
