  "Lobster Mac|Negroni": "Equal parts gin, Contratto vermouth, Campari. The bitter Campari fights the manchego sweetness and truffle's earthy depth; a structural clash. Keep the Negroni for the tartare course where it peaks. Avoid; route the table to a better-matched pour.",
  "Lobster Mac|Never Say Die Rye": "Never Say Die Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the high-rye spice register matches the lobster mac, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; Old Fitz 9 brings more depth here.",
