  "Lobster Mac|Patron Anejo": "Patron Anejo's barrel-aged tequila weight sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak-aged tequila body threads the lobster mac, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; Ultra's aged depth is over-specified for dessert simplicity.",
  "Lobster Mac|Patron Silver": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the unaged body brightens the lobster mac, and the unaged-cane note plays against the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Patron XO Cafe": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- sweet liqueur and dairy-rich side double the indulgence with no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Patron XO Cafe belongs on the steak course.",
  "Lobster Mac|Paul Bara Grand Rosé Brut": "Paul Bara Grand Cru Pinot Noir rosé — structured grower Champagne with raspberry, red currant, minerality. The body handles lobster-mac's lush cream-cheese weight unconventionally; fine bubbles cut the richness without clashing. Works as unconventional rosé Champagne for the lobster mac side.",
  "Lobster Mac|Peanut Butter Brownie": "The lobster mac and the PB brownie -- the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence hands off cleanly to the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: rich cream gives way to sweet, the close lands generously. Works; sequence them or share the table, no clash.",
  "Lobster Mac|Peju Cabernet Sauvignon": "Peju Cabernet Sauvignon's bold char-cherry cassis leans against the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the opulent body matches the indulgent side, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Pierre Ferrand Cognac": "Pierre Ferrand with lobster mac — artisanal Grande Champagne against pasta-and-lobster richness. Strong; Ferrand's craft character frames the richness with unblended polish.",
  "Lobster Mac|Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut": "2015 Côte des Blancs prestige Champagne — layered citrus, brioche, white flowers, and creamy texture. The creamy texture aligns with lobster-mac's rich cream-cheese build and the brioche adds depth. Works as an unconventional indulgence pour for lobster mac — prestige meets richness side-wise.",
  "Lobster Mac|Pikesville Rye": "Pikesville Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the dry rye body wraps the lobster mac, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; save the BTAC bottle for the protein course — the side doesn't deserve the pour.",
  "Lobster Mac|Pineau des Charentes": "Pineau des Charentes' sweet liqueur character overwhelms the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- the liqueur's sugar buries the side's cream instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Pineau des Charentes for the steak course.",
  "Lobster Mac|Pio Cesare Barbaresco": "Pio Cesare Barbaresco's bold Nebbiolo-cherry cassis plays cleanly against the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Plymouth Gin": "Plymouth Gin's Plymouth-style-rounder botanicals leans against the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Poderi Aldo Conterno Nebbiolo": "Poderi Aldo Conterno Nebbiolo's bold cherry-citrus cassis sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Pommery Cuvée Louise": "2004 Pommery Cuvée Louise — aged 20-year Champagne. Almond, apricot, honey, brioche-rich. The aged complexity and brioche align with lobster-mac's rich cream-cheese weight unconventionally. Works as indulgence-on-indulgence when the occasion calls for it — though younger Champagne suits the side more economically.",
  "Lobster Mac|Porterhouse": "Porterhouse with the lobster mac -- the 40oz dual strip-and-filet meets the shellfish-in-cream indulgence, both courses indulgent, neither outpacing the other. Strong; the side reads steakhouse-classic alongside the cut.",
  "Lobster Mac|Prime Tartare": "Prime Tartare and the lobster mac -- cream and umami share the plate, the build reads dense and clean. Works; both items hold their register, no clash.",
  "Lobster Mac|Quilt Cabernet Sauvignon": "Quilt Cabernet Sauvignon's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis holds with the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the caramel softens the cream. Works; the pairing reads neutral at the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|RAEN Royal St Robert": "RAEN Royal St Robert's cherry-mineral tannin stays alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Rainbow Trout": "The trout into the lobster mac -- the lighter course primes the richer, the meal carries register lift. Works; safe alongside, but not the headline pick.",
  "Lobster Mac|Raventós Cava de NIT Rosé Brut": "Spanish rosé Cava — sparkling, red-fruit character, clean acid. The bubbles cut the truffle-cream roux and the rosé fruit plays against the lobster's sweetness. Fun non-obvious sparkling alternative to Champagne when the table wants something playful. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Redbreast 12 Year": "Redbreast 12 Year's single pot still Irish character reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the Irish whiskey body sits with the lobster mac, and the oak threads the cream. Works; collector-bottle depth gives the dessert ultra-premium character.",
  "Lobster Mac|Redbreast 21 Year": "Redbreast 21 Year's aged single pot still Irish finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the gentle Irish body threads the lobster mac, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Remus 15 Year Gatsby Reserve": "Remus 15 Year Gatsby Reserve's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the brown-spirit warmth threads the lobster mac, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; save the collector bottle for the protein course.",
  "Lobster Mac|Remy VSOP Cognac": "Rémy VSOP with lobster mac — Grande Champagne cognac against pasta-and-lobster. Strong; Rémy's elegance frames the richness with refined polish.",
  "Lobster Mac|Rey Sol Anejo": "Rey Sol Anejo's rested-agave body reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the añejo register carries the lobster mac, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the side. Works; clean and composed pairing.",
  "Lobster Mac|Reyka Vodka": "Reyka Vodka's crisp Icelandic-glacial neutrality finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Rishi's Old Antique": "Rishi's Old Antique's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon weight handles the lobster mac, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Roast Half Chicken": "The chicken alongside the lobster mac -- cream rounds the protein, the plate composes thick. Works; the side sits without pulling focus.",
  "Lobster Mac|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "The chickpea soup and the lobster mac on the same meal -- spice and cream share the table, the contrast settles round. Works; sequence or share, the build holds.",
  "Lobster Mac|Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs — Le Mesnil Grand Cru Chardonnay. Chalk, lemon curd, green apple, no dosage. The austere acidity cuts lobster-mac's cream-cheese richness and the mineral adds dimension. Works as sommelier Champagne for the lobster-mac side — no-dosage precision cuts the richness.",
  "Lobster Mac|Roku Gin": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Ron Zacapa Rum": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the high-proof register matches the lobster mac, and the layered body brightens the side. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Russell's Reserve 10 Year": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon depth settles into the lobster mac, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; retailer-pick wasted on salad.",
  "Lobster Mac|Salt-Cured Halibut": "The halibut into the lobster mac -- the lighter course primes the richer, the meal carries register lift. Works; safe alongside, but not the headline pick.",
  "Lobster Mac|Sambuca": "Sambuca's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- sweet liqueur and dairy-rich side double the indulgence with no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Sambuca on the steak course instead.",
  "Lobster Mac|San Simeon Stormwatch": "San Simeon Stormwatch's bold cherry-coffee cassis leans against the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; safe call, no friction.",
  "Lobster Mac|Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir": "Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir's cherry-earth tannin sits beside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Sauternes Glass": "Sauternes Glass' dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Sauternes Glass belongs on the steak course.",
  "Lobster Mac|Sazerac": "Sazerac's bold anise-cherry build stays alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the whiskey-build weight settles into the rich side, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Sazerac Rye": "Sazerac Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the rye-and-oak weight handles the lobster mac, and the oak softens the cream. Works; accessible gentle match.",
  "Lobster Mac|Scapegrace Fortuna": "Scapegrace Fortuna's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the lobster mac, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Scavino Barolo": "Scavino Barolo: this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight meets this rich, creamy side's dairy-driven indulgence. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. Directional mismatch at this intersection. Avoid; the call reads off-register; recommend an alternative.",
  "Lobster Mac|Schloss Vollrads Riesling": "Schloss Vollrads Riesling's crisp apricot-floral acidity stays alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters": "Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters's bold cherry-chocolate cassis leans against the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Seafood Tower": "The seafood tower alongside the lobster mac -- both bring shellfish as the headline. Avoid; one is enough. Pair the seafood tower with Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut; pair the lobster mac with Cowboy Ribeye, Far Niente Chardonnay, or The Tomahawk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Seared Scallops": "The scallops and the lobster mac -- shellfish-on-shellfish, the meal goes redundant. Avoid; the table reads heavy without payoff. Suggest Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre for the scallops, or Cowboy Ribeye, Far Niente Chardonnay, or The Tomahawk for the lobster mac.",
  "Lobster Mac|Seasonal Soup": "The seasonal soup and the lobster mac -- a clean call, no friction either way. Works; sequence them or share the table, the call holds either way.",
  "Lobster Mac|Sesti Brunello di Montalcino": "Sesti Brunello di Montalcino's bold cherry-earth cassis leans against the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the opulent body matches the indulgent side, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lobster Mac|Shafer 1.5": "Shafer 1.5's bold coffee-juniper cassis stays alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the caramel softens the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Shafer Hillside Select": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the allocated-Cab depth wraps the lobster mac, and the graphite frames the side. Works; the side sits without pulling focus.",
  "Lobster Mac|Shrimp Bisque": "The shrimp bisque and the lobster mac -- both shellfish-forward, the table doubles up on shellfish. Avoid; pick one or the other. Pair the shrimp bisque with Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay; pair the lobster mac with Cowboy Ribeye, Far Niente Chardonnay, or The Tomahawk.",
  "Lobster Mac|Shrimp Cocktail": "The shrimp cocktail and the lobster mac -- shellfish-on-shellfish, the meal goes redundant. Avoid; the table reads heavy without payoff. Suggest Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut for the shrimp cocktail, or Cowboy Ribeye, Far Niente Chardonnay, or The Tomahawk for the lobster mac.",
  "Lobster Mac|Siete Leguas Blanco": "Siete Leguas Blanco's green-agave-and-cane lift finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the blanco-tequila body matches the lobster mac, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; clean additive-free lifts the dish depending on preparation.",
  "Lobster Mac|Siete Leguas Reposado": "Siete Leguas Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the barrel-rested body handles the lobster mac, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon: this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight meets this rich, creamy side's dairy-driven indulgence. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A capable pair; richness aligns if not perfectly. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lobster Mac|Simon Family Estate Reserve": "Simon Family Estate Reserve's bold oak cassis finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the opulent body matches the indulgent side, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; the pairing reads neutral at the table. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
