  "Lobster Mac|Tanq 10 Gin": "Tanq 10 Gin's crisp citrus-floral botanicals sits beside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lobster Mac|Tanqueray Gin": "Tanqueray Gin's bold London-Dry-juniper botanicals stays alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the juniper carries the shellfish. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lobster Mac|Taylor Fladgate Tawny": "Taylor Fladgate Tawny's classic tawny with caramel-nut sweetness doubles down on the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- sweet wine and a dairy side compound the richness — dessert energy on savory plate. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Taylor Fladgate Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Lobster Mac|Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle": "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle for the steak course.",
  "Lobster Mac|Tears of Llorona": "Tears of Llorona's rested-agave body finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the añejo register carries the lobster mac, and the oak threads the side. Works; Ultra's ceremonial depth composed with this dish.",
