  "Lobster Mac|Venge Scout's Honor": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis sits beside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the caramel-spice settles the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Venge Silencieux": "Venge Silencieux's bold cherry-chocolate cassis sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the opulent body matches the indulgent side, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Vesper": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build stays alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Lobster Mac|Veuve Clicquot Brut": "Yellow label Veuve — Reims Champagne, ripe apple, white peach, biscuit, creamy mousse. The creamy body aligns with lobster-mac's rich cream-cheese weight and the lively acidity cuts through. Works as crowd-pleasing Champagne for the lobster mac side — indulgence meets celebration side-by-side.",
  "Lobster Mac|Vieux Carré": "Vieux Carré's bold herbal-spice build stays alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the whiskey-build weight settles into the rich side, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Lobster Mac|Villon Cognac": "Villon with lobster mac — saffron-infused cognac spirit against pasta-and-lobster richness. Strong; Villon's saffron notes have a natural seafood-adjacent affinity the other cognacs can't claim.",
  "Lobster Mac|Vin Santo": "Vin Santo's Tuscan dried-fruit-and-honey sweetness doubles down on the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- sweet wine and a dairy side compound the richness — dessert energy on savory plate. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Pour the Vin Santo on the steak course instead.",
  "Lobster Mac|Weller 107": "Weller 107's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon backbone carries the lobster mac, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; Boss Hog's allocation story is wasted on the salad.",
  "Lobster Mac|Weller 12 Year": "Weller 12 Year's aged wheated honey-vanilla character finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon weight handles the lobster mac, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; stout-barrel story wasted on salad.",
