  "Lobster Mac|WhistlePig Boss Hog X Commandments": "WhistlePig Boss Hog X Commandments' rye-spice character reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the lobster mac, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; premium rye gives the dessert substantial depth.",
  "Lobster Mac|WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year": "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year's rye-spice character reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the rye backbone drives the lobster mac, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the pour's brightness is a gentle counterpoint to the dessert's richness.",
  "Lobster Mac|Willett Pot Still Reserve": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the caramel-spice register matches the lobster mac, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; Caribbean Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Woodford Reserve": "Woodford Reserve's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the caramel-spice register matches the lobster mac, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; Woodford Double Oaked frames the two-cut plate at KY-benchmark register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Woodford Reserve Double Oaked": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the brown-spirit warmth threads the lobster mac, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lobster Mac|Woodford Reserve Rye": "Woodford Reserve Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the rye spice cuts the lobster mac, and the oak softens the cream. Works; 10-year depth overshoots delicacy.",
  "Lobster Mac|Woodinville Rye": "Woodinville Rye's rye-spice character leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the dry rye body wraps the lobster mac, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; the pour's sweetness meets the dessert without pushing past.",
  "Lobster Mac|Yamazaki 12 Year": "Yamazaki 12 with lobster mac — Japan's flagship single malt against pasta-and-lobster. Works; Yamazaki 12's honey-fruit elegance handles the rich dish at flagship register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Yamazaki 18 Year": "Yamazaki 18 with lobster mac — aged Suntory single malt against pasta-and-lobster. Works; Yamazaki 18's aged character handles the rich dish at collector register.",
  "Lobster Mac|Yellow Chartreuse": "Yellow Chartreuse's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- bitter aperitivo on the supporting side reads as wrong register for the course. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Yellow Chartreuse for the steak course.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Asparagus": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the malt-driven body wraps the asparagus, and the honey rounds the side. Works; the pour's toasted warmth threads through the char without overpowering.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with the au gratin — complex 20yr Highland against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Loch Lomond 20's aged character handles the richness at collector register.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Beignets": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the beignets, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the dessert. Works; distinctive finish over-specified.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Bone Marrow": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with bone marrow — 20yr complex Highland against umami fat. Strong; Loch Lomond 20's aged depth sits alongside marrow at collector register; Oban 14 still leads the Highland-marrow pairings.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Bone-In Filet": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the malt-and-oak threads the bone-enhanced filet, and the heather brightens the cut. Works; retailer-pick wasted on salad.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Broccoli Cheddar": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the malt-and-oak threads the broccoli cheddar, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; not revelatory but well-matched registers.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Broccolini": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the broccolini's tender green stalks: the Highland register carries the broccolini, and the malt edge frames the side. Works; AE Triple Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Brussels and Belly": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with Brussels + Belly — 20yr aged varied-still Highland against maple-glazed pork belly. Works; Loch Lomond 20's aged complexity meets the glaze at collector register.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Burrata": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with burrata — 20yr varied-still Highland against fresh dairy. Avoid; Scotch weight wrong for burrata's cream.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Butternut Squash": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character leans against the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the Highland register carries the squash bisque, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; the bonded richness gives the dessert more than lighter pours do.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Carrot Cake": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with carrot cake — 20yr Highland against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; Loch Lomond 20's complex-aged character threads the cake's spice at collector register; Dalmore 12 still leads the Highland-carrot-cake pairing.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Cheesecake": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with cheesecake — 20yr complex Highland against custard. Strong; Loch Lomond 20's aged-depth threads the cheesecake at collector register.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Chilean Seabass": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's complex 20yr aged Highland overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Loch Lomond 20 Year belongs on the steak course.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Chocolate Brownie": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's complex 20yr aged Highland sits alongside the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight: the scotch depth settles into the brownie, and the malt edge frames the dessert. Works; boutique-sourced doesn't drive.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Chocolate Cake": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's complex 20yr aged Highland sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the scotch depth settles into the chocolate cake, and the malt edge frames the dessert. Works; the 100-proof is a touch over-specified for the dessert's register.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Clam Chowder": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the malt-driven body wraps the chowder, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; boutique-sourced doesn't drive.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Cowboy Ribeye": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with the cowboy ribeye — 20yr aged Highland against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Excellent; Loch Lomond 20's aged depth frames the ribeye at collector register; Oban 18's maritime + sherry-finish is the featured Highland-ribeye match.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Crab Cake": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with crab cake — 20yr Highland against delicate crab. Avoid; Scotch wrong for seafood. Reach for a vodka or gin.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Creamed Spinach": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with creamed spinach — complex 20yr aged Highland against dairy-rich side. Strong; Loch Lomond 20's varied-still character rides the cream at collector register.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Creamy Potato": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the Highland register carries the potato soup, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; collector-bottle doesn't drive.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Creme Brulee": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the scotch backbone matches the brulee, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; OGD 16 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Escargot": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's caramel-spice character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Faroe Island Salmon": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's complex 20yr aged Highland swallows the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a scotch. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Loch Lomond 20 Year belongs on the steak course.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Filet Mignon": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with the filet — 20yr Highland single malt, distinctive for varied still types (traditional pot + straight-neck) giving complex aged character. Excellent; Loch Lomond 20's complex-aged profile frames tenderloin with distinctive depth — 20 years of aging gives it gravitas the 12-18yr siblings don't quite reach.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|French Onion": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the scotch backbone matches the French onion, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; extended-aged home-state pour wasted on salad.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Grilled Caesar": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with the grilled Caesar — 20yr aged varied-still Highland against charred romaine and anchovy. Excellent; Loch Lomond 20's complex-aged character meets the char at collector-Highland register.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Gumbo": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the scotch depth settles into the gumbo, and the oak-and-smoke underlines the bowl. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for a side — save the collector bottle for the main.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the malt-driven body wraps the honey carrots, and the oak frames the caramelized sugar. Works; extended-aged home-state pour wasted on salad.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|House Wedge": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with the House Wedge — 20yr aged Highland against iceberg and bleu. Strong; Loch Lomond 20's complex depth engages the bleu at collector register.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Kansas City": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with the KC — 20yr complex-aged Highland against an 18oz strip. Excellent; Loch Lomond 20's 20-year aging and varied-still complexity handle strip marbling at collector register.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Loaded Potato": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the malt-and-oak threads the loaded potato soup, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; premium proof overpowers this dish.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Lobster Mac": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the malt-and-oak threads the lobster mac, and the oak softens the cream. Works; milestone-release doesn't drive.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Market Fish": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's complex 20yr aged Highland smothers the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a scotch. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Loch Lomond 20 Year for the steak course.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Mocha Creme": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the Highland register carries the mocha creme, and the oak softens the cream. Works; IW Harper 15 handles dessert density at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Mushroom Bisque": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's complex 20yr aged Highland sits alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the scotch depth settles into the mushroom bisque, and the oak frames the umami. Works; the pour's toasted warmth threads through the char without overpowering.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Mushrooms": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with mushrooms — complex 20yr Highland against earthy umami. Excellent; Loch Lomond 20's varied-still complexity threads mushroom earthiness at collector-aged register.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character leans against the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the scotch backbone matches the PB brownie, and the honey rounds the dessert. Works; annual-release complexity over-specified.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Porterhouse": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with the porterhouse — 20yr Highland against strip-and-filet. Strong; Loch Lomond 20's complex-aged depth frames the two-cut plate at collector register.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Prime Tartare": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's caramel-spice character holds the line with the tartare's raw beef and brine — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Rainbow Trout": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's complex 20yr aged Highland smothers the trout's delicate flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a scotch. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Loch Lomond 20 Year for the steak course.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Roast Half Chicken": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's complex 20yr aged Highland finds neutral with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the scotch depth settles into the roast chicken, and the malt edge frames the plate. Works; X Commandments story wasted on salad.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the chickpea soup, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; save the BTAC bottle for the protein course — the side doesn't deserve the pour.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's complex 20yr aged Highland flattens the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Loch Lomond 20 Year for the steak course.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the scotch backbone matches the garlic spinach, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the side. Works; Prohibition narrative wasted on salad.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Seafood Tower": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's complex 20yr aged Highland drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Loch Lomond 20 Year for the steak course.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Seared Scallops": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with seared scallops — aged complex Highland against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Seasonal Soup": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character leans against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the malt-driven body wraps the seasonal soup, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; Parker's Heritage 16th is over-specified for an app; save the collector bottle for the main.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Seasonal Vegetables": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character leans against the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the scotch depth settles into the seasonal vegetables, and the heather brightens the side. Works; novelty maturation at matched register.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Shrimp Bisque": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with shrimp bisque — 20yr aged Highland against cream-shrimp soup. Works; Loch Lomond 20 is over-specified for a soup; save the collector-aged Highland for the main course.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Shrimp Cocktail": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's complex 20yr aged Highland fights the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Loch Lomond 20 Year on the steak course instead.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Swordfish": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's complex 20yr aged Highland overwhelms the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Loch Lomond 20 Year for the steak course.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|The Tomahawk": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's caramel-spice character holds steady against the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the caramel-and-oak weight rises with the cap-fat, and the caramel echoes the grilled char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Tomato Basil": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the tomato basil, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; OGD 16 frames the two-cut plate at distinctive register.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Truffle Fries": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with truffle fries — 20yr complex-aged Highland against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Loch Lomond 20's aged depth and varied-still complexity meet the earthy-rich at collector register.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's complex 20yr aged Highland swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Loch Lomond 20 Year belongs on the steak course.",
  "Loch Lomond 20 Year|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the curry, and the smoke threads the bowl. Works; OGD 16 frames the two-cut plate at distinctive register.",
  "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye|Asparagus": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the rye spice cuts the asparagus, and the rye-grain bite cuts the side. Works; the 80-proof softness doesn't overshoot the salad the way heavier bourbons do.",
  "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye's rye-spice character leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the au gratin, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; JW Blue is over-specified for the side — save the rare-cask bottle for the protein course.",
  "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye|Beignets": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the rye spice cuts the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; complex profile overshoots the dessert's delicacy.",
  "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye|Bone Marrow": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye with bone marrow — sourced boutique rye against umami fat. The premium-blended character meets marrow with boutique-brand authority. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye|Bone-In Filet": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye's pepper-spice character holds steady against the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the aged-oak weight frames the lean cut, and the oak underlines the char. Strong; a steady recommendation at the table.",
  "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye|Broccoli Cheddar": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the rye-and-oak weight handles the broccoli cheddar, and the oak threads the cream. Works; no driver pairing.",
  "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye|Broccolini": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye's rye-spice character leans against the broccolini's tender green stalks: the high-rye spice register matches the broccolini, and the dry-spice register brightens the side. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye|Brussels and Belly": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye with Brussels + Belly — sourced boutique rye meets maple-glazed pork belly. The premium-blend character cuts the glaze with boutique distinctiveness. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye|Burrata": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye with burrata — fresh dairy against premium sourced rye. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye|Butternut Squash": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye's rye-spice character leans against the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the rye-and-oak weight handles the squash bisque, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; the aging is wasted on the salad.",
  "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye|Carrot Cake": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye's rye-spice character leans against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the dry rye body wraps the carrot cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; concentrated blend slightly over-specified.",
  "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye|Cheesecake": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the rye spice cuts the cheesecake, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye|Chilean Seabass": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye's rye-spice character swallows the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Lock Stock & Barrel Rye belongs on the steak course.",
