  "Macallan 18|Porterhouse": "Macallan 18 with the porterhouse — 18yr aged Oloroso Speyside against strip-and-filet. Works; Macallan 18's aged depth frames the two-cut plate at premium register.",
  "Macallan 18|Prime Tartare": "Macallan 18's bold sherry-dried-fruit character matches the tartare's raw beef and brine — the caramel-oak depth threads the savory plate. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Macallan 18|Rainbow Trout": "Macallan 18's premium aged 18yr Oloroso Speyside overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a scotch. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Macallan 18 for the steak course.",
  "Macallan 18|Roast Half Chicken": "Macallan 18's premium aged 18yr Oloroso Speyside sits alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the scotch backbone matches the roast chicken, and the smoke threads the plate. Works; the distinctive character is underused by the salad's simplicity.",
  "Macallan 18|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Macallan 18's premium aged 18yr Oloroso Speyside leans against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the aged Oloroso depth wraps the chickpea soup, and the dried-fruit-and-spice softens the bowl. Works; Old World complexity wasted on salad simplicity.",
  "Macallan 18|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Macallan 18's premium aged 18yr Oloroso Speyside swallows the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Macallan 18 for the steak course.",
