  "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye|Clam Chowder": "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye's rye-spice character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the rye spice cuts the chowder, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; the unique maturation story adds interest to a gentle dessert match.",
  "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye|Cowboy Ribeye": "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye with the Cowboy Ribeye — 16-year aged Michigan rye against cap fat. Extended maturation handles the ribeye with distinctive Michigan-distillery authority. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye|Crab Cake": "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye's rye-spice character smothers the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye for the steak course.",
