  "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye's rye-spice character overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye lands on the steak course — not here.",
