  "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye|The Tomahawk": "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye with the Tomahawk — 16-year aged single-barrel from Mammoth Distilling, Michigan. Home-state distillery; the extended 16-year maturation gives the Tomahawk a local-Michigan rye with serious age. Pour with home-state pride for Michigan guests. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye|Tomato Basil": "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye's rye-spice character leans against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the rye spice cuts the tomato basil, and the dry-spice register brightens the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye|Truffle Fries": "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye with truffle fries — 16-year aged Michigan against truffle-parmesan. The extended maturation gives the side distinctive aged-rye character with home-state pride. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye's rye-spice character flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye on the steak course instead.",
  "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the rye backbone drives the curry, and the dry-spice register brightens the bowl. Works; HH 20 frames the two-cut plate at collector register.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Asparagus": "Marc Brédif Chinon's cherry-earth tannin stays alongside the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the medium-body red frames the green plate, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Marc Brédif Chinon's cherry-earth tannin plays cleanly against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Beignets": "Marc Brédif Chinon's herbaceous Cab Franc with red-fruit and bell-pepper flattens the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Marc Brédif Chinon for the steak course.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Bone Marrow": "Marc Brédif Chinon's cherry-earth tannin reads alongside the marrow's umami-fat depth — the medium-body red meets the savory plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Bone-In Filet": "Marc Brédif Chinon's cherry-earth tannin holds the line with the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the medium-body red frames the lean cut, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Strong; the call lands cleanly.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Broccoli Cheddar": "Marc Brédif Chinon's herbaceous Cab Franc with red-fruit and bell-pepper reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the Cab Franc body lifts the broccoli cheddar, and the bell-pepper-and-cherry note frames the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Broccolini": "Marc Brédif Chinon's cherry-earth tannin stays alongside the broccolini's tender green — the medium-body red frames the green plate, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Brussels and Belly": "Marc Brédif Chinon's cherry-earth tannin reads alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the herbs frame the grilled char. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Burrata": "Loire Cab Franc — Chinon light body, raspberry, red cherry, bell pepper, forest floor, supple low tannin, bright high acid. The bright acid handles burrata's creamy-delicate center and the red cherry plays against the fresh cheese. Strong Loire CF for burrata — unusual red for cream-forward starter, food-wine acid reframes the dish.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Butternut Squash": "Marc Brédif Chinon's herbaceous Cab Franc with red-fruit and bell-pepper leans against the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the Cab Franc body lifts the squash bisque, and the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; the side call holds at neutral register.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Carrot Cake": "Marc Brédif Chinon's herbaceous Cab Franc with red-fruit and bell-pepper jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Marc Brédif Chinon on the steak course instead.",
