  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Escargot": "Loire Cab Franc — Chinon light body, raspberry, red cherry, bell pepper, forest floor, supple low tannin, bright high acid. The bright acid cuts escargot's butter-garlic parsley weight and the forest floor plays against the earthy snail. Strong Loire CF for escargot — classic French pairing on the French starter.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Faroe Island Salmon": "Loire Cab Franc — Chinon light body, raspberry, red cherry, bell pepper, forest floor, supple low tannin, bright high acid. The bright acid plays against salmon's rich omega-three oils; preparation changes seasonally — check with kitchen for today's build. Peak food wine for salmon — lighter-than-Bordeaux CF handles fish across seasonal preparations.",
