  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Loire Cab Franc — Chinon light body, raspberry, red cherry, bell pepper, forest floor, supple low tannin, bright high acid. The bright acid cuts garlic-sauté weight and the bell pepper plays against the spinach base. Strong Loire CF for garlic spinach — food-wine acidity on the lighter side.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Seafood Tower": "Marc Brédif Chinon's herbaceous Cab Franc with red-fruit and bell-pepper crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Marc Brédif Chinon for the steak course.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Seared Scallops": "Marc Brédif Chinon's herbaceous Cab Franc with red-fruit and bell-pepper crowds out the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Marc Brédif Chinon for the steak course.",
