  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Shrimp Bisque": "Loire Cab Franc — Chinon light body, raspberry, red cherry, bell pepper, forest floor, supple low tannin, bright high acid. The bright acid cuts shrimp bisque's cream-sherry weight and the red cherry plays against the shellfish base. Works as unusual Loire CF for the bisque — food-wine acidity on the rich soup.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Shrimp Cocktail": "Marc Brédif Chinon's herbaceous Cab Franc with red-fruit and bell-pepper overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Marc Brédif Chinon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Swordfish": "Marc Brédif Chinon's cherry-earth tannin plays cleanly against the swordfish's meaty flesh — the silken tannin frames the fish, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|The Tomahawk": "Light-body Loire Cab Franc against Tomahawk's massive bone-in ribeye — Chinon's raspberry-bell pepper delicacy gets buried by the grand cut. Never pair. Route Tomahawk to Cabernet Sauvignon, Bordeaux, or prestige Napa Cab; keep Chinon for chicken, salmon, mushrooms, or lighter apps where food-wine acidity peaks.",
  "Marc Brédif Chinon|Tomato Basil": "Marc Brédif Chinon's cherry-earth tannin stays alongside the tomato basil's bright acid — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; capable alongside. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
