  "Margarita|Cowboy Ribeye": "Margarita's blanco-and-citrus margarita brightness underclubs the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness -- a light citrus cocktail can't carry the marbled char — needs whiskey or red wine weight. The plate deserves Macallan 18, Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon, or Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon, not a light cocktail. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Margarita for another course.",
  "Margarita|Crab Cake": "Corazon Blanco, lemon, lime, orange, Cointreau — salted rim. The triple-citrus build cuts crab's romesco and the blanco's clean agave profile meets the sweet meat directly; Cointreau smooths the finish. Peak classic cocktail for crab cake when guest wants citrus-forward agave.",
