  "Margarita|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Margarita's crisp agave-brine build sits beside the garlic-spinach's buttered greens — the cocktail lift sits with the light side, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Margarita|Seafood Tower": "Corazon Blanco, lemon, lime, orange, Cointreau. The triple-citrus handles the raw-bar shellfish and the blanco's agave profile adds warmth against oysters and shrimp. Strong tower cocktail when guest wants a classic Margarita rather than Champagne for the full spread.",
  "Margarita|Seared Scallops": "Corazon Blanco, lemon, lime, orange, Cointreau. The triple-citrus structure meets scallops' clean-seared sweetness and the blanco's agave profile cuts without crushing delicacy. Peak Margarita pairing for scallops — bright, clean, and doesn't overwhelm the dish. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
