  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Asparagus": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- bitter aperitivo on the supporting side reads as wrong register for the course. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Mata Hari Absinthe for the steak course.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- amaro bitterness on dairy reads metallic — needs warmth or sweetness to balance. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Mata Hari Absinthe belongs on the steak course.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Beignets": "Beignets: warm sugar-dusted pastry meets Mata Hari. Excellent; the anise-fennel-wormwood character plays with sugar-dust at 60% register — absinthe on warm fried pastry.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Bone Marrow": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bitter-herb aperitivo edge overwhelms the bone marrow's unctuous rendered-marrow richness -- bitter aperitivo flattens the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Fernet Branca, Lagavulin 8, or George T. Stagg, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Mata Hari Absinthe for the steak course.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Bone-In Filet": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bitter-herb aperitivo edge mis-pairs with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- bitter botanicals on the cut fight the savory char without payoff. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Mata Hari Absinthe lands on another course — not here.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Broccoli Cheddar": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Mata Hari Absinthe on the steak course instead.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Broccolini": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bitter-herb aperitivo edge doubles down on the broccolini's tender green stalks -- bitter herbs and a green vegetable side compound the same register — no contrast. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Mata Hari Absinthe for the steak course.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Brussels and Belly": "Mata Hari Absinthe's sweet wormwood-anise character finds register with the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the sweet character sits at digestif register, and the anise frames the char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Burrata": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bitter-herb aperitivo edge fights the burrata's fresh basil-tomato-cream delicacy -- bitter herbs and fresh dairy refuse each other — the milky plate reads sour back. The plate deserves Il Colle Prosecco Superiore, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Mata Hari Absinthe for the steak course.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Butternut Squash": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- amaro bitterness on dairy cream reads metallic — no bridge from herbal sharp to soft fat. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Mata Hari Absinthe for the steak course.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Carrot Cake": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Mata Hari Absinthe. Works; the anise-fennel character adds herbal dimension to the cake's spice at 60% register.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Cheesecake": "Mata Hari Absinthe: Bohemian-style absinthe from Austria, 60% ABV, wormwood-anise-fennel, traditional louche. Excellent on cheesecake; the wormwood-anise clarity cuts cheesecake cream at absinthe-classic register — high-proof herbal cleaver.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Chilean Seabass": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bitter aperitivo is for before or after the meal — not on a main protein. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Mata Hari Absinthe for the steak course.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Chocolate Brownie": "Chocolate Brownie: warm dark chocolate meets Mata Hari. Excellent; the wormwood-anise profile cuts chocolate at Bohemian-absinthe register — high-proof anise on cocoa.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Chocolate Cake": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bittersweet rhubarb-and-orange edge sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the herbal cut works the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Clam Chowder": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the better calls are above. Mata Hari Absinthe lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Cowboy Ribeye": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness -- bitter aperitivo belongs before or after the meal, not alongside the steak. The plate deserves Macallan 18, Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon, or Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Mata Hari Absinthe for another course.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Crab Cake": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bitter-herb aperitivo edge overwhelms the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- bitter aperitivo flattens the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Mata Hari Absinthe on the steak course instead.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Creamed Spinach": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the creamed spinach's rich bechamel-laced greens -- amaro bitterness on dairy reads metallic — needs warmth or sweetness to balance. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Weller 12 Year, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Mata Hari Absinthe for the steak course.",
