  "Mata Hari Absinthe|House Wedge": "Mata Hari Absinthe's sweet wormwood-anise character holds the line with the wedge's iceberg, bacon, and bleu — the sweet character sits at digestif register, and the anise threads the herb edge. Strong; a steady recommendation at the table.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Kansas City": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bitter-herb aperitivo edge sits alongside the KC's lean-bold strip with savory grain: the amaro-bitter register cuts the strip steak, and the amaro backbone frames the cut. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Mata Hari Absinthe|Loaded Potato": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bitter-herb aperitivo edge fights the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup -- bitter herbs cut the bisque's round cream without lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Mata Hari Absinthe lands on the steak course — not here.",
