  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Lobster Mac": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon weight handles the lobster mac, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the light body doesn't overshoot the salad.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Market Fish": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Michter's 10 Year Bourbon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Mocha Creme": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the brown-spirit warmth threads the mocha creme, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Mushroom Bisque": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the bourbon body sits with the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the pour's sweetness meets the dessert without pushing past.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Mushrooms": "Michter's 10 Bourbon with mushrooms — Michter's single-barrel 10yr against earthy umami. Excellent; Michter's 10's 10yr character threads mushroom earthiness at prestigious-independent register.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Peanut Butter Brownie: peanut butter and cocoa meet Michter's flagship 10yr. Works; Michter's 10 handles dessert density at prestigious-independent register.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Porterhouse": "Michter's 10 Bourbon with the porterhouse — Michter's allocated 10yr against strip-and-filet. Works; Michter's 10 frames the two-cut plate at prestigious-independent register.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Prime Tartare": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's caramel-juniper character sits with the tartare's raw beef and brine — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Rainbow Trout": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Michter's 10 Year Bourbon for the steak course.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Roast Half Chicken": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the oak depth lays under the roast chicken, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the bourbon depth settles into the chickpea soup, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; narrative-bourbon doesn't drive.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Save the Michter's 10 Year Bourbon for the steak course.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the oak depth lays under the garlic spinach, and the oak frames the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Seafood Tower": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit weight crowds the delicate shellfish — no acid to clean the brine. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Michter's 10 Year Bourbon for the steak course.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Seared Scallops": "Michter's 10 Bourbon with seared scallops — Michter's allocated 10yr against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Seasonal Soup": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the bourbon body sits with the seasonal soup, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; not revelatory but well-matched registers.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Seasonal Vegetables": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the seasonal vegetables, and the oak-and-spice register settles the side. Works; AE Triple Cask meets the char at distinctive register.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Shrimp Bisque": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the brown-spirit warmth threads the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; Voyage 23 frames the cut at ocean-finish register.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Shrimp Cocktail": "Michter's 10 Bourbon with shrimp cocktail — Michter's allocated 10yr against cold shrimp. Avoid; bourbon wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Swordfish": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Michter's 10 Year Bourbon lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|The Tomahawk": "Michter's 10 Bourbon with the Tomahawk — Michter's flagship 10yr against 32oz cap-fat. Works; Michter's 10's aged character is under-specified for Tomahawk intensity; reach for a barrel-proof bourbon.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Tomato Basil": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the caramel-spice register matches the tomato basil, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Truffle Fries": "Michter's 10 Bourbon with truffle fries — Michter's allocated 10yr against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Michter's 10's single-barrel depth meets the earthy-rich at prestigious-independent register.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon's sweet weight crowds the rare crust's clean char. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Michter's 10 Year Bourbon for the steak course.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the caramel-spice register matches the curry, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Rye|Asparagus": "Michter's 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the high-rye spice register matches the asparagus, and the rye-pepper note underlines the side. Works; pleasant but not a standout.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Rye|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Michter's 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the rye spice cuts the au gratin, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; annual-release wasted on salad.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Rye|Beignets": "Michter's 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Michter's 10 Year Rye|Bone Marrow": "Michter's 10 Year Rye with bone marrow — premium aged Michter's against umami fat. The 10-year polished character meets marrow with small-batch aged authority. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
