  "Milagro Anejo|Chilean Seabass": "Milagro Anejo's aged-agave character clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- agave and oily fish refuse each other — the fish needs acid, not aged spirit. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Milagro Anejo for the steak course.",
