  "Milagro Anejo|Clam Chowder": "Milagro Anejo's rested-agave body reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the añejo register carries the chowder, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Milagro Anejo|Cowboy Ribeye": "Milagro Anejo's crisp agave-vanilla character sits with the ribeye's cap fat and char — the aged-tequila depth grips the marbled cut, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Milagro Anejo|Crab Cake": "Milagro Anejo's aged-agave character smothers the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- aged-agave register crowds the delicate shellfish frame. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Milagro Anejo lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Milagro Anejo|Creamed Spinach": "Milagro Anejo's crisp agave-vanilla character holds steady against the spinach's dairy-rich cream — the añejo weight overshoots the light side, and the rounded sweetness brightens the cream. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
