  "Milagro Anejo|Faroe Island Salmon": "Milagro Anejo's aged-agave character clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- agave and oily fish refuse each other — the fish needs acid, not aged spirit. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Milagro Anejo for the steak course.",
