  "Milagro Anejo|Kansas City": "Milagro Anejo: Highland Jalisco 100% Blue Weber, triple-distilled, 14+ months French oak — softer and cleaner than Patron. Excellent on KC strip; the French-oak-aged refined character frames the lean cut at accessible-craft register — Milagro is the softer-finishing accessible craft answer to Patron.",
  "Milagro Anejo|Loaded Potato": "Milagro Anejo's barrel-aged tequila weight reads alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the aged-agave weight wraps the loaded potato soup, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Milagro Anejo|Lobster Mac": "Milagro Anejo's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the aged-agave weight wraps the lobster mac, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Milagro Anejo|Market Fish": "Milagro Anejo's aged-agave character clashes with the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- aged tequila is wrong register for a main fish or poultry course. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Milagro Anejo lands on the steak course — not here.",
