  "Milagro Reposado|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Milagro Reposado's rested-agave body finds neutral with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the añejo register carries the tuna, and the caramel-agave register brightens the plate. Works; Riedel-luxury over-specified.",
  "Milagro Reposado|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Milagro Reposado's añejo-pour depth sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the añejo register carries the curry, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Asparagus": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the bourbon backbone carries the asparagus, and the rounded sweetness brightens the side. Works; complexity wasted on salad.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet Mister Sam Bronfman tribute. Mister Sam's aged-blended character handles the richness at collector register. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Beignets": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon weight handles the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; a composed but not remarkable match.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Bone Marrow": "Mister Sam with bone marrow — Sazerac Seagram's-tribute blend against umami fat. Excellent; Mister Sam's complex blended character engages marrow at Seagram's-tribute register.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Bone-In Filet": "Mister Sam with the bone-in filet — Sazerac Seagram's-tribute blended whiskey against tenderloin-with-bone. Excellent; Mister Sam's blended-heritage character frames the cut at Seagram's-tribute register.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Broccoli Cheddar": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the oak depth lays under the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Broccolini": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the bourbon depth settles into the broccolini, and the oak frames the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet Mister Sam Bronfman tribute. Works; Mister Sam's blended character meets the glaze at tribute register.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Burrata": "Mister Sam with burrata — Sazerac blended tribute against fresh dairy. Avoid; whiskey weight wrong for burrata.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Butternut Squash": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bourbon body sits with the squash bisque, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; save the BTAC bottle for the protein course — the side doesn't deserve the pour.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Carrot Cake": "Mister Sam with carrot cake — Seagram's-era tribute blend against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; Mister Sam's blended-heritage character threads the cake at collector register.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Cheesecake": "Mister Sam with cheesecake — Sazerac tribute blend against custard. Works; Mister Sam's blended character threads the cheesecake at Seagram's-tribute register.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Chilean Seabass": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey belongs on the steak course.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Chocolate Brownie": "Mister Sam with the chocolate brownie — Sazerac Bronfman tribute blend against cocoa. Strong; Mister Sam's aged-blended character meets cocoa at Seagram's-tribute register.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Chocolate Cake": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the caramel-spice register matches the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Sinatra Select handles the richness at Sinatra-tribute register.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Clam Chowder": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the chowder, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Cowboy Ribeye": "Mister Sam with the cowboy ribeye — Sazerac tribute blended whiskey against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Strong; Mister Sam frames the ribeye at Seagram's-tribute register.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Crab Cake": "Mister Sam with crab cake — Sazerac Seagram's-tribute against delicate lump crab. Avoid; blended whiskey wrong for seafood. Reach for a vodka or gin.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Creamed Spinach": "Mister Sam with creamed spinach — Mister Sam tribute against dairy-rich side. Strong; Mister Sam's blended character rides the cream at Seagram's-tribute register.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Creamy Potato": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the bourbon depth settles into the potato soup, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Creme Brulee": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the brulee, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; BIB structure overshoots the dessert's delicacy.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Escargot": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's bold leather character frames the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the bourbon weight grips the savory plate. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Faroe Island Salmon": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey for the steak course.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Filet Mignon": "Mister Sam with the filet — Sazerac's Mister Sam Bronfman tribute, blended American whiskey including Seagram's-era stocks, limited-release premium blend. Excellent; Mister Sam's blended-Seagram's-era character frames tenderloin with collector-register Seagram's nostalgia — where Beam family brings Beam aged, Mister Sam brings Seagram's heritage preserved in blend form.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|French Onion": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the bourbon backbone carries the French onion, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Grilled Caesar": "Grilled Caesar: charred romaine and anchovy meet Mister Sam Bronfman tribute. Works; Mister Sam is over-specified for an app; save the tribute bottle for the main.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Gumbo": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the caramel-spice register matches the gumbo, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; the toast adds a warmth the dessert can accept.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the honey carrots, and the oak softens the caramelized sugar. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|House Wedge": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the wedge's iceberg-and-bleu cool crunch: the caramel-spice register matches the wedge, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; Marian McLain L.E.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Kansas City": "Mister Sam with the KC — Mister Sam Bronfman tribute against an 18oz strip. Strong; Mister Sam handles the strip at Seagram's-tribute register.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Loaded Potato": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the oak depth lays under the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the bourbon-with-dessert pairing holds at neutral.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Lobster Mac": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the caramel-spice register matches the lobster mac, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; aging wasted on the salad.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Market Fish": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Mocha Creme": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the bourbon depth settles into the mocha creme, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; Voyage 23 frames the two-cut plate at ocean-finish register.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Mushroom Bisque": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the bourbon depth settles into the mushroom bisque, and the caramel-spice settles the cream. Works; retailer-pick wasted on salad.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Mushrooms": "Mister Sam with mushrooms — Sazerac Bronfman-tribute blended against earthy umami. Excellent; Mister Sam's complex aged-blended character threads mushroom earthiness at Seagram's-tribute register.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Peanut Butter Brownie: peanut butter and cocoa meet Sazerac blended whiskey. Works; Mister Sam handles dessert density at Seagram's-tribute register.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Porterhouse": "Mister Sam with the porterhouse — Sazerac Mister Sam tribute against strip-and-filet. Works; Mister Sam frames the two-cut plate at Seagram's-tribute register.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Prime Tartare": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami: the caramel-spice register matches the tartare, and the oak depth meets the umami. Strong; Remus 15 handles the richness at Gatsby-tribute register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Rainbow Trout": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the trout's delicate flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey for the steak course.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Roast Half Chicken": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the brown-spirit warmth threads the roast chicken, and the caramel rounds the plate. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the bourbon backbone carries the chickpea soup, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; the private select's layered profile underserves the dessert's simplicity.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the brown-spirit warmth threads the garlic spinach, and the caramel rounds the side. Works; distinctive character is worth mentioning tableside, even if the pairing isn't marquee.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Seafood Tower": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit weight crowds the delicate shellfish — no acid to clean the brine. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey belongs on the steak course.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Seared Scallops": "Mister Sam with seared scallops — Mister Sam tribute blend against scallop delicacy. Avoid; whiskey overwhelms scallops.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Seasonal Soup": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the bourbon weight handles the seasonal soup, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Seasonal Vegetables": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the caramel-spice register matches the seasonal vegetables, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Shrimp Bisque": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon body sits with the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; flagship depth gives the dessert premium aged character.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Shrimp Cocktail": "Mister Sam with shrimp cocktail — Sazerac Bronfman tribute against cold shrimp. Avoid; whiskey wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Swordfish": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey on the steak course instead.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|The Tomahawk": "Mister Sam with the Tomahawk — Sazerac tribute blended whiskey against 32oz cap-fat. Works; Mister Sam's aged-blended character is under-specified for Tomahawk intensity; reach for a barrel-proof bourbon.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Tomato Basil": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the bourbon weight handles the tomato basil, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; JD Bonded's backbone handles the richness at Bonded register.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Truffle Fries": "Mister Sam with truffle fries — Sazerac tribute blended whiskey against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Mister Sam's aged-blended depth meets the earthy-rich at Seagram's-tribute register.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon's sweet weight crowds the rare crust's clean char. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the bourbon weight handles the curry, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; the toast adds a warmth the dessert can accept.",
  "Mocha Creme|1792 Small Batch": "1792 Small Batch's caramel-spice character reads alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the caramel-spice register matches the mocha creme, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; extended maturation gives the dessert home-state aged character.",
  "Mocha Creme|1792 Sweet Wheat": "1792 Sweet Wheat's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the bourbon body sits with the mocha creme, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; IW Harper 15 handles dessert density at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Mocha Creme|1881 Napa Valley": "1881 Napa Valley's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the 1881 Napa Valley for the steak course.",
  "Mocha Creme|2 James Gin": "2 James Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not a gin. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the 2 James Gin for the steak course.",
  "Mocha Creme|A Midnight's Winter Dram": "A Midnight's Winter Dram's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the scotch depth settles into the mocha creme, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; premium proof overpowers this dish.",
  "Mocha Creme|Aberlour 16": "Aberlour 16 with mocha creme — double-matured Speyside against coffee-chocolate dessert. Works; Aberlour 16's sherry-side threads the mocha; Balvenie 21 Portwood is the featured mocha match.",
  "Mocha Creme|Adictivo Cristalino": "Adictivo Cristalino's aged-agave character clashes with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- aged-agave register fights chocolate sweetness without bridging. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Adictivo Cristalino for the steak course.",
  "Mocha Creme|Adictivo Reposado": "Adictivo Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register reads alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the aged-agave weight wraps the mocha creme, and the caramel-agave register brightens the dessert. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Mocha Creme|Alexander Valley Chardonnay": "Alexander Valley Chardonnay's crisp white-wine character falls short of the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- dry white can't carry chocolate's weight — needs a tawny or sweet wine for the close. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not a white wine. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Alexander Valley Chardonnay for the steak course.",
  "Mocha Creme|Alexander Valley Cyrus": "Alexander Valley Cyrus' red-fruit-and-spice elegance jars against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Alexander Valley Cyrus belongs on the steak course.",
  "Mocha Creme|Alexander Valley Homestead Red": "Alexander Valley Homestead Red's red-fruit-and-spice elegance flattens the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Alexander Valley Homestead Red lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Mocha Creme|Amaro Nonino": "Amaro Nonino's crisp orange-peel-grappa sweetness holds steady against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate dessert — the bitter herb edge cuts dessert sweetness, and the orange peel echoes the chocolate. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Mocha Creme|Ancho Reyes": "Ancho Reyes's ancho-chile-smoke sweetness holds steady against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate dessert — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar, and the smoke crosses the cocoa. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Mocha Creme|Angel's Envy": "Angel's Envy with mocha creme — flagship AE port-finish against coffee-chocolate dessert. Works; AE's port-derived jammy-fruit threads mocha at wine-finish register.",
  "Mocha Creme|Angel's Envy Cask Strength": "AE Cask Strength with mocha creme — cask-strength port-finish against coffee-chocolate dessert. Works; AE CS's port-derived jammy-fruit threads mocha at premium register.",
  "Mocha Creme|Angel's Envy Triple Cask": "AE Triple Cask with mocha creme — AE triple-cask finish against coffee-chocolate dessert. Excellent; AE Triple Cask's layered-cask character is the featured AE-mocha pairing — additional cask complexity threads coffee-and-cocoa distinctively.",
  "Mocha Creme|Aperol": "Aperol's crisp bitter-orange-aperitivo edge holds steady against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate dessert — the bitter herb edge cuts dessert sweetness, and the orange peel echoes the chocolate. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Mocha Creme|Asparagus": "Asparagus and the mocha creme -- acid plays against sweetness, the close stays unburdened. Works; the meal closes cleanly from the side.",
  "Mocha Creme|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Au Gratin Potatoes and the mocha creme -- rich cream gives way to sweet, the close lands generously. Works; clean transition or together if the table wants.",
  "Mocha Creme|Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon": "Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- savory tannin sits awkwardly on cocoa weight without resolving. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Mocha Creme|Averna Amaro": "Averna Amaro's caramel-orange sweetness holds steady against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate dessert — the bitter herb edge cuts dessert sweetness, and the caramel pairs into the cream. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Mocha Creme|Aviation": "Aviation's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift clashes with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- light cocktail citrus is wrong direction for the dessert's richness. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not a light cocktail. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Save the Aviation for the steak course.",
  "Mocha Creme|Aviation Gin": "Aviation Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- gin botanicals jar against the chocolate's sweetness with no bridge. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not a gin. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Aviation Gin belongs on the steak course.",
  "Mocha Creme|Avion 44": "Avion 44 with mocha creme — 44-month aged Avion against coffee-chocolate. Works; extended maturation finds mocha at premium register.",
  "Mocha Creme|Avion Silver": "Avion Silver's unaged blanco-tequila lift with agave-citrus snap falls short of the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- light spirit can't carry chocolate's weight — needs a richer pour like an aged rum or tawny. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not a light spirit. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Avion Silver for the steak course.",
  "Mocha Creme|Bacardi Rum": "Bacardi Rum's crisp workhorse-clean character leans against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the crisp body lifts the mocha creme, and the clean profile carries the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Mocha Creme|Baileys Irish Cream": "Mocha Creme: coffee-chocolate dessert meets Baileys. Excellent; Baileys and coffee is the textbook pairing — the Irish-whiskey-cream meets mocha at iconic register.",
  "Mocha Creme|Baker's": "Baker's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the mocha creme, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; annual-release story wasted on salad.",
  "Mocha Creme|Balvenie 12 American Oak": "Balvenie 12 American Oak's bourbon-cask Speyside softness sits alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the Highland register carries the mocha creme, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; Marian McLain L.E.",
  "Mocha Creme|Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask": "Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask with mocha creme — rum-cask-finished Speyside against coffee-chocolate dessert. Works; Caribbean Cask's vanilla-caramel threads the mocha; Balvenie 21 Portwood's port-cask is the featured mocha match.",
  "Mocha Creme|Balvenie 16 Single Barrel": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the mocha creme, and the oak threads the cream. Works; collector-bottle depth gives ultra-premium character.",
  "Mocha Creme|Balvenie 21 Portwood": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with mocha creme — 21yr port-finished Speyside against coffee-chocolate dessert. Excellent; port's red-berry-fruit marries coffee and chocolate with collector-register depth — the featured Sherried Speyside-mocha pairing in the cluster.",
  "Mocha Creme|Bardstown Château Laboude": "Bardstown Château Laboude with mocha creme — Bardstown Bourbon Co. French-wine finish against coffee-chocolate dessert. Works; Bardstown Château Laboude's French-wine-fruit threads mocha at contemporary-craft register.",
  "Mocha Creme|Bardstown Discovery #6": "Bardstown Discovery #6's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the brown-spirit warmth threads the mocha creme, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Mocha Creme|Bardstown Founders KBS": "Bardstown Founders KBS's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the bourbon depth settles into the mocha creme, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; accessible gentle match.",
  "Mocha Creme|Bardstown Foursquare": "Bardstown Foursquare's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the brown-spirit warmth threads the mocha creme, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; 100-proof complexity sits beside the soup.",
  "Mocha Creme|Bardstown Fusion #7": "Bardstown Fusion #7's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth leans against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the bourbon depth settles into the mocha creme, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Mocha Creme|Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel": "Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the bourbon weight handles the mocha creme, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; OGD 16 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Mocha Creme|Basil Hayden's": "Basil Hayden's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the oak depth lays under the mocha creme, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; craft-blender complexity over-specified.",
  "Mocha Creme|Basil Hayden's 10 Year": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the caramel-spice register matches the mocha creme, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; allocated character doesn't drive.",
  "Mocha Creme|Basil Hayden's Malted Rye": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character leans against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the rye-and-oak weight handles the mocha creme, and the oak softens the cream. Works; BH Red Wine Cask's softer-proof character rides the cream at distinctive register.",
  "Mocha Creme|Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with mocha creme — BH red-wine finish against coffee-chocolate dessert. Works; BH Red Wine Cask's red-wine-fruit + rye-spice threads mocha at distinctive register.",
