  "Mocha Creme|Evening Land Seven Springs": "Evening Land Seven Springs' red-fruit-and-spice elegance fights the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- the dry red and the chocolate's sugar refuse each other — tannin reads bitter on the finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Evening Land Seven Springs belongs on the steak course.",
