  "Mocha Creme|Glenmorangie 10": "Glenmorangie 10's tallest-stills Highland bourbon-cask character reads alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the scotch backbone matches the mocha creme, and the oak softens the cream. Works; KBS distinctiveness is slightly over-specified for the two-cut plate.",
  "Mocha Creme|Glenmorangie 18": "Glenmorangie 18's aged Highland with Oloroso finish finds neutral with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the mocha creme, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Mocha Creme|Graham's 10 Year Tawny": "10-year oak-cask oxidative Tawny — Graham's entry-point, dried apricot, walnut, toffee, gentle spice. The toffee plays with espresso-yolk custard depth and the walnut echoes coffee-roast bitterness. Strong Tawny for mocha creme — Vintage Port's chocolate intensity edges higher on the espresso pour.",
  "Mocha Creme|Graham's 20 Year Tawny": "20-year oak-cask oxidative Tawny — Graham's step-up, concentrated dried fruit, roasted hazelnut, orange peel, silky long finish. The roasted hazelnut echoes espresso-roast directly and the orange peel lifts yolk-cream custard. Strong step-up Tawny for mocha creme — Vintage Port's intensity edges higher on espresso.",
  "Mocha Creme|Graham's 2017 Vintage Port": "2017 declared-vintage Port — Graham's bottle-aged, dense inky, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, powerful structured. The dark chocolate echoes espresso-cocoa depth and the powerful structure handles yolk-cream custard. Peak Vintage Port for mocha creme — espresso-meets-chocolate with bottle-aged intensity. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
