  "Mount Gay Rum|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Mount Gay Rum's green-agave-and-cane lift sits alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the unaged body brightens the garlic spinach, and the unaged-cane register underlines the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Mount Gay Rum|Seafood Tower": "Mount Gay Rum's Caribbean-rum register with bright sugarcane leans against the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the unaged body brightens the seafood tower, and the rum-and-lime thread softens the starter. Strong; the premium-craft blanco frames the fish at the Maestra-Tequilera register.",
  "Mount Gay Rum|Seared Scallops": "Seared Scallops: scallop delicacy meets Mount Gay. Excellent; the Barbados-tradition character frames scallops at heritage register — the character-forward option vs. Bacardi's clean-neutral.",
  "Mount Gay Rum|Seasonal Soup": "Mount Gay Rum's green-agave-and-cane lift leans against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the unaged body brightens the seasonal soup, and the unaged-cane note plays against the bowl. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Mount Gay Rum|Seasonal Vegetables": "Mount Gay Rum's unaged Caribbean-rum body reads alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the cane-and-citrus body lifts the seasonal vegetables, and the cane register underlines the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Mount Gay Rum|Shrimp Bisque": "Mount Gay Rum's crisp Barbados-molasses character matches the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the crisp body sits with the plate. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Mount Gay Rum|Shrimp Cocktail": "Mount Gay Rum: world's oldest continuously-operating rum distillery, Barbados since 1703. Excellent on shrimp cocktail; the traditional-craft character with its subtle molasses hint adds tradition-weight to the classic light-rum-on-shellfish move — where Bacardi is the workhorse, Mount Gay is the heritage reach.",
  "Mount Gay Rum|Swordfish": "Mount Gay Rum's Caribbean-rum body sits alongside the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak: the unaged body brightens the swordfish, and the Caribbean register brightens the plate. Strong; the refined character frames the fish at the premium register.",
  "Mount Gay Rum|The Tomahawk": "Mount Gay Rum's light-rum register with cane and citrus lift underclubs the Tomahawk's theatrical bone-in marbling and smoky char -- light spirit can't stand up to the marbled char — needs a Cab, bourbon, or añejo. The plate deserves Corazon Stagg, Opus One, or George T. Stagg, not a light spirit. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Mount Gay Rum belongs on another course.",
  "Mount Gay Rum|Tomato Basil": "Mount Gay Rum's silver-rum body reads alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the Caribbean-rum body wraps the tomato basil, and the rum-and-lime thread softens the bowl. Works; refined craft composes cleanly.",
  "Mount Gay Rum|Truffle Fries": "Mount Gay Rum's unaged silver-rum body sits alongside the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the silver-rum body cuts the truffle fries, and the unaged-cane note plays against the side. Works; refined character is slightly over-specified for the dish.",
  "Mount Gay Rum|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Mount Gay Rum's cane-and-citrus register leans against the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the unaged body brightens the tuna, and the Caribbean register brightens the plate. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Mount Gay Rum|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Mount Gay Rum's silver-rum body leans against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the light-rum body cuts the curry, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the bowl. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Muga Reserva|Asparagus": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin sits alongside the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the medium-body red frames the green plate, and the rounded sweetness softens the green edge. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Muga Reserva|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Rioja Alta Reserva Tempranillo-blend — Muga, American-French oak, strawberry, dried cherry, vanilla, leather. The vanilla-oak wraps around gruyere-cream and the medium body handles dairy weight. Works for au gratin — a Chardonnay's cream-on-cream lifts higher.",
  "Muga Reserva|Beignets": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- tannin can't pivot to warm pastry sugar — the pour reads dry, the dessert reads heavy. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Muga Reserva for the steak course.",
  "Muga Reserva|Bone Marrow": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin reads alongside the marrow's umami-fat depth — the medium-body red meets the savory plate, and the oak frames the cream. Strong; the match carries without overshooting.",
  "Muga Reserva|Bone-In Filet": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin reads alongside the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the medium-body red frames the lean cut, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Muga Reserva|Broccoli Cheddar": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin sits beside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the oak frames the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Muga Reserva|Broccolini": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin sits alongside the broccolini's tender green — the medium-body red frames the green plate, and the rounded sweetness softens the green edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Muga Reserva|Brussels and Belly": "Rioja Alta Reserva Tempranillo-blend — Muga, American-French oak, strawberry, dried cherry, vanilla, leather, savory-earthy. The leather plays with pork-belly fat and the vanilla-oak matches brussels-char bitterness. Strong Rioja for brussels-and-belly — traditional-oak polish on fat-and-char.",
  "Muga Reserva|Burrata": "Never pair Muga with burrata — oak-vanilla and leather clash with fresh cream and the savory-earthy finish buries tomato-basil brightness. Lead with Santa Margherita Pinot Grigio's clean lift or a Rosé's strawberry-to-tomato-sweetness bridge.",
  "Muga Reserva|Butternut Squash": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin sits beside the squash soup's silky sweet — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the oak frames the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Muga Reserva|Carrot Cake": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Muga Reserva on the steak course instead.",
  "Muga Reserva|Cheesecake": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth jars against the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Muga Reserva lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Muga Reserva|Chilean Seabass": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Muga Reserva lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Muga Reserva|Chocolate Brownie": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth flattens the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Muga Reserva for the steak course.",
  "Muga Reserva|Chocolate Cake": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth jars against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Muga Reserva belongs on the steak course.",
  "Muga Reserva|Clam Chowder": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the caramel-spice settles the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Muga Reserva|Cowboy Ribeye": "Rioja Alta Reserva Tempranillo-blend — Muga, American-French oak, strawberry, dried cherry, vanilla, leather, medium body. The medium body is slightly light for Cowboy's marbled 26oz bone-in, but the vanilla-oak handles grilled char. Strong Rioja for ribeye — a refined mid-weight match.",
  "Muga Reserva|Crab Cake": "Never pair Muga with crab cake — oak-driven vanilla and leather bury delicate lump crab and the savory finish fights the romesco. Lead with Heitz Sauvignon Blanc's citrus lift or Reverdy Sancerre's mineral edge for shellfish clarity.",
  "Muga Reserva|Creamed Spinach": "Rioja Alta Reserva Tempranillo-blend — Muga, American-French oak, strawberry, dried cherry, vanilla, leather, medium body. The vanilla-oak wraps around dairy-heavy cream and the medium body handles spinach-iron. Strong Rioja for creamed spinach — a gentle traditional pairing.",
  "Muga Reserva|Creamy Potato": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin finds neutral with the potato soup's silky body — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the oak frames the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Muga Reserva|Creme Brulee": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth jars against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Muga Reserva for the steak course.",
  "Muga Reserva|Escargot": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth sits at register with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the Rioja American-oak register matches the buttered escargot, and the vanilla-leather edge frames the starter. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Muga Reserva|Faroe Island Salmon": "Rioja Alta Reserva Tempranillo-blend — Muga, American-French oak, strawberry, dried cherry, vanilla, leather. The medium body handles salmon's oil-richness, though the oak-vanilla is slightly heavy for flesh-sweetness. Works for salmon — preparation changes seasonally, check with kitchen for today's build.",
  "Muga Reserva|Filet Mignon": "Rioja Alta Reserva Tempranillo-blend — Muga, American-French oak, strawberry, dried cherry, vanilla, leather, medium body. The medium body matches butter-tender filet's delicate weight and the vanilla-oak plays against escargot-butter. Strong Rioja for filet — approachable traditional-house pairing.",
  "Muga Reserva|French Onion": "Rioja Alta Reserva Tempranillo-blend — American-French oak, strawberry, dried cherry, vanilla, leather. The vanilla-oak meets French Onion's gruyère-crust richness and the dried cherry plays against the caramelized onion. Strong Rioja for French Onion — Spanish earth on the French classic.",
  "Muga Reserva|Grilled Caesar": "Grilled Caesar: the Grilled Caesar's charred romaine, anchovy umami, and bold creamy dressing meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. Tannin and char, umami and dark fruit — the bold red and the Caesar punch at the same level. A confident Caesar pour. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Muga Reserva|Gumbo": "Rioja Alta Reserva Tempranillo-blend — American-French oak, strawberry, dried cherry, vanilla, leather. The leather-vanilla meshes with gumbo's dark-roux depth and the dried cherry plays against andouille's spice. Peak Rioja for gumbo — Spanish oak on the Cajun classic. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Muga Reserva|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin stays alongside the carrots' honeyed sweetness — the medium-body red frames the green plate, and the vanilla amplifies the dessert sugar. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Muga Reserva|House Wedge": "Rioja Alta Reserva Tempranillo-blend — Muga, American-French oak, strawberry, dried cherry, vanilla, leather. The leather matches blue-cheese funk and the vanilla-oak plays with bacon-fat char. Works for wedge — cold iceberg mutes Muga's oak complexity, so a lighter Chianti reads cleaner.",
  "Muga Reserva|Kansas City": "Rioja Alta Reserva Tempranillo-blend — Muga, American-French oak, strawberry, dried cherry, vanilla, leather, savory-earthy. The vanilla-oak wraps around Kansas City's lean-bold strip char and the leather echoes grilled-beef depth. Peak Rioja for the strip — oak-driven Tempranillo match. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Muga Reserva|Loaded Potato": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin plays cleanly against the loaded potato's richness — the medium-body red frames the hearty soup, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Muga Reserva|Lobster Mac": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin reads alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Muga Reserva|Market Fish": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth clashes with the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Muga Reserva for the steak course.",
  "Muga Reserva|Mocha Creme": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth flattens the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Muga Reserva for the steak course.",
  "Muga Reserva|Mushroom Bisque": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin sits beside the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the medium-body red frames the hearty soup, and the caramel softens the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Muga Reserva|Mushrooms": "Rioja Alta Reserva Tempranillo-blend — Muga, American-French oak, strawberry, dried cherry, vanilla, leather, savory-earthy. The savory-earthy finish echoes roasted-mushroom glutamate and the vanilla-oak plays with butter. Peak Rioja for mushrooms — traditional-oak plus earth harmony. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Muga Reserva|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth fights the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- the dry red and the chocolate's sugar refuse each other — tannin reads bitter on the finish. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Muga Reserva belongs on the steak course.",
  "Muga Reserva|Porterhouse": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin matches the porterhouse's two-cut character — the medium-body red meets the cap-fat at lighter register, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; the match carries without overshooting.",
  "Muga Reserva|Prime Tartare": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth reads register-aligned with the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami: the Rioja American-oak register matches the tartare, and the Tempranillo tannin grips the starter. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Muga Reserva|Rainbow Trout": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Muga Reserva belongs on the steak course.",
  "Muga Reserva|Roast Half Chicken": "Rioja Alta Reserva Tempranillo-blend — Muga traditional house, American-and-French oak, strawberry, dried cherry, vanilla, leather, savory-earthy finish. The vanilla-oak plays against chicken-skin char and the leather matches herb-jus depth. Peak Rioja for the bird — preparation changes seasonally, check with kitchen for today's build. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Muga Reserva|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Rioja Alta Reserva Tempranillo-blend — American-French oak, strawberry, dried cherry, vanilla, leather. The leather-vanilla meshes with the soup's smoky chickpea base and the dried cherry plays against roasted-pepper sweetness. Works tier on this wine's card — solid fit for Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea but below the wine's peaks with the Tomahawk, Porterhouse, and Bone-In Filet.",
  "Muga Reserva|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth clashes with the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Muga Reserva for the steak course.",
  "Muga Reserva|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin sits beside the garlic-spinach's buttered greens — the medium-body red frames the green plate, and the caramel softens the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Muga Reserva|Seafood Tower": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Muga Reserva on the steak course instead.",
  "Muga Reserva|Seared Scallops": "Never pair Muga with seared scallops — vanilla-oak and leather overwhelm delicate sweet shellfish and the savory finish clashes with browned-butter. Lead with Clos de la Chapelle Chardonnay or Rombauer's creamy richness for sear-seared harmony.",
  "Muga Reserva|Seasonal Soup": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin plays cleanly against the seasonal soup's house build — the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Muga Reserva|Seasonal Vegetables": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin finds neutral with the seasonal garden plate — the medium-body red frames the green plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Muga Reserva|Shrimp Bisque": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin leans against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the medium-body red frames the hearty soup, and the oak frames the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Muga Reserva|Shrimp Cocktail": "Never pair Muga with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp plus cocktail-sauce horseradish gets crushed by oak-vanilla and leather, and the savory depth has nowhere to land. Lead with Laurent Perrier Brut Champagne's bubble-driven palate reset.",
  "Muga Reserva|Swordfish": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- tannin against rare-seared crust reads astringent without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Muga Reserva on the steak course instead.",
  "Muga Reserva|The Tomahawk": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin holds steady against the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the medium-body red meets the cap-fat at lighter register, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Muga Reserva|Tomato Basil": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin sits beside the tomato basil's bright acid — the medium-body red meets the light soup, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Muga Reserva|Truffle Fries": "Rioja Alta Reserva Tempranillo-blend — Muga, American-French oak, strawberry, dried cherry, vanilla, leather, savory-earthy. The savory-earthy finish echoes truffle-oil mushroom depth and the vanilla wraps around parm. Peak Rioja for truffle fries — oak-and-earth match. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Muga Reserva|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Muga Reserva's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- tannin against rare-seared crust reads astringent without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Muga Reserva lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Muga Reserva|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin sits beside the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|1792 Small Batch": "1792 Small Batch's caramel-spice character leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the bourbon depth settles into the mushroom bisque, and the caramel softens the cream. Works; craft-blend over-specified.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|1792 Sweet Wheat": "1792 Sweet Wheat's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the bourbon weight handles the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; annual-release wasted on salad.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|1881 Napa Valley": "1881 Napa Valley's bold cherry-coffee cassis holds with the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; capable alongside. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|2 James Gin": "2 James Gin's crisp char-juniper botanicals reads alongside the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|A Midnight's Winter Dram": "A Midnight's Winter Dram's Highland-scotch character reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the scotch backbone matches the mushroom bisque, and the oak frames the umami. Works; IW Harper 15 frames the two-cut plate at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Aberlour 16": "Aberlour 16's double-matured Speyside balance sits alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the malt-and-oak threads the mushroom bisque, and the oak depth meets the umami. Works; single-barrel depth gives the dessert more than Small Batch.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Adictivo Cristalino": "Adictivo Cristalino's añejo-pour depth leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the aged-agave weight wraps the mushroom bisque, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Adictivo Reposado": "Adictivo Reposado's rested-agave body sits alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the añejo register carries the mushroom bisque, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Alexander Valley Chardonnay": "Sonoma Chardonnay — ripe apple, pear, warm vanilla oak, smooth balanced texture. The oak-vanilla weight aligns with the bisque's cream-mushroom richness and the apple-pear lifts the umami base. Strong accessible Chardonnay for the bisque — California oak on the earthy classic.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Alexander Valley Cyrus": "Alexander Valley Cyrus's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis reads alongside the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Alexander Valley Homestead Red": "Alexander Valley Homestead Red's coffee-mocha tannin sits alongside the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the medium-body red frames the hearty soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Amaro Nonino": "Amaro Nonino's crisp orange-peel-grappa sweetness clashes with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream -- amaro bitterness on dairy cream reads metallic — no bridge from herbal sharp to soft fat. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Amaro Nonino on the steak course instead.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Ancho Reyes": "Ancho Reyes' sweet liqueur character overwhelms the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream -- the liqueur's sweetness buries the soup's creamy base instead of supporting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Ancho Reyes belongs on the steak course.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Angel's Envy": "Angel's Envy's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the bourbon depth settles into the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Angel's Envy Cask Strength": "Angel's Envy Cask Strength's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the brown-spirit warmth threads the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Angel's Envy Triple Cask": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the bourbon depth settles into the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Aperol": "Aperol's crisp bitter-orange-aperitivo edge fights the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream -- bitter herbs cut the bisque's round cream without lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Aperol lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Asparagus": "Mushroom Bisque and the asparagus -- the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream meets the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: acid breaks the umami stack, the table earns the brighter note. Works; no conflict however the table orders them.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Au Gratin Potatoes": "The mushroom bisque and the au gratin -- dairy plays against umami, the table reads layered. Works; sequence them or share the table, the call holds either way.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon": "Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cherry-coffee cassis leans against the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Averna Amaro": "Averna Amaro's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Averna Amaro for the steak course.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Aviation": "Aviation's crisp almond-cherry build holds with the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the cocktail lift refreshes against the hearty soup, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Aviation Gin": "Aviation Gin's floral-juniper botanicals stays alongside the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Avion 44": "Avion 44's rested-agave body reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the aged-agave weight wraps the mushroom bisque, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Avion Silver": "Avion Silver's silver-spirit lift with agave-citrus edge reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the blanco-tequila body matches the mushroom bisque, and the unaged-cane note plays against the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
