  "Mushroom Bisque|Les Pallières Raciné": "Les Pallières Raciné's concentrated dark-fruit and tannin leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the structured body wraps the mushroom bisque, and the cassis frames the bowl. Works; the close composes without strain.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Liberator Gin": "Liberator Gin's citrus-juniper botanicals finds neutral with the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Licor 43": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream -- the liqueur's sweetness buries the soup's creamy base instead of supporting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Licor 43 on the steak course instead.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Limoncello": "Limoncello's sweet liqueur character clashes with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Limoncello for the steak course.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Willamette Pinot — dark cherry, forest floor, refined structure, low tannin. The forest-floor earth meshes directly with mushroom umami and the silky body lifts the cream base. Peak Oregon Pinot for the bisque — earth-on-earth pairing, refined Willamette character on the umami classic. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Little Book": "Little Book's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the caramel-spice register matches the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; blend character covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Lobster Mac": "The mushroom bisque and the lobster mac -- cream meets umami, the table goes deep. Works; sequence them or share the table, the call holds either way.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Loch Lomond 20 Year": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's complex 20yr aged Highland sits alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the scotch depth settles into the mushroom bisque, and the oak frames the umami. Works; the pour's toasted warmth threads through the char without overpowering.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Lock Stock & Barrel Rye": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the rye backbone drives the mushroom bisque, and the oak threads the umami plate. Works; the 10-year BIB depth gives the dessert substantial weight.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Long Road Gin": "Long Road Gin's crisp citrus-juniper botanicals reads alongside the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Los Vecinos Mezcal": "Los Vecinos Mezcal's smoky agave character reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the espadín-and-smoke body wraps the mushroom bisque, and the green-agave edge brightens the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Louis XIII Cognac": "Louis XIII Cognac's luxury-icon cognac depth mis-pairs with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream -- an icon cognac on a soup-salad course is wrong moment — its register demands the close, not the open. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an icon cognac. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Louis XIII Cognac belongs on the steak course.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Lucano Amaro": "Lucano Amaro's bitter-herb aperitivo edge fights the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream -- bitter herbs cut the bisque's round cream without lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Lucano Amaro for the steak course.",
  "Mushroom Bisque|Lunaria Coste di Moro": "Lunaria Coste di Moro's spice-driven red elegance leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the silky body carries the mushroom bisque, and the cherry-pepper note frames the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
