  "Mushrooms|Bowman Brothers Small Batch": "Bowman Brothers Small Batch with the mushrooms — Virginia-aged small-batch against earthy umami. The smooth character layers into mushroom depth at the approachable register. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Mushrooms|Bowmore 12": "Mushrooms: the earthy, umami-forward side meets Bowmore 12's honey, orchard fruit, and sherry-softened peat. The pairing opens the dish up instead of covering it — distinct from Lagavulin 8 or Laphroaig 10 with the same side. Pour when a guest wants peated Islay but the rest of the table skews lighter. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Mushrooms|Braida Montebruna Barbera": "Piedmont Monferrato Barbera d'Asti — Braida benchmark, juicy dark cherry, blackberry, high acid, low tannin, medium body. The high acid cuts through roasted-mushroom glutamate and the blackberry plays against the earth depth. Peak benchmark Barbera for mushrooms — food-wine acidity on the earthy side. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Mushrooms|Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon": "Mushrooms: the structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit anchors the mushroom's umami weight; firm tannin and oak hold their register. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Mushrooms|Broccoli Cheddar": "The broccoli cheddar and the mushrooms -- cream rounds the savory, the meal earns its depth. Works; sequence them or share the table, the call holds either way.",
  "Mushrooms|Bruichladdich": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets this earthy, umami-packed side's mushroom-and-truffle depth. Whiskey's oak and sweetness mirror the side's dairy and umami depth. A headliner match — context-driven peak. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
