  "Mushrooms|Frias Block 5": "Mushrooms: the side's mushroom richness pulls the bold red's body; tannin and oak settle into the umami without overshooting. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the pairing reads at register.",
  "Mushrooms|G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo": "Piedmont Barolo DOCG Nebbiolo — G.D. Vajra Albe La Morra, tar, rose petal, dried cherry, firm tannic backbone, full body, high acid. The tar echoes roasted-mushroom glutamate and the dried cherry plays against the earth depth. Peak classic Barolo for mushrooms — earth-on-earth Barolo match. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Mushrooms|G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti": "Piedmont sweet sparkling — peach, honey, floral. Sweetness fights every umami aspect of the mushrooms; the earthy depth gets fought by every note in the wine. Route Moscato to dessert. Avoid; the call reads off-register; recommend an alternative.",
  "Mushrooms|G4 Blanco": "G4 Blanco's clean silver register leans against the mushrooms' earthy umami weight: the blanco-tequila body matches the mushrooms, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Mushrooms|G4 High Proof": "G4 High Proof with the mushrooms — 104-proof concentrated reposado against earthy umami. Strong; the bold agave layers into mushroom depth distinctively.",
  "Mushrooms|Garavogue Irish Whiskey": "Garavogue with mushrooms — western Ireland craft Irish against earthy umami. Excellent; Garavogue's small-batch character threads mushrooms with distinctive regional-Irish depth.",
  "Mushrooms|George T. Stagg": "GTS with mushrooms — BTAC 15+yr cask-strength against earthy umami. Strong; GTS threads mushrooms at collector-BTAC register.",
  "Mushrooms|Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon": "Oakville Cab — blackcurrant, dark cherry, graphite, toasted oak, firm tannin. The graphite-oak meshes with mushroom umami and the dense structure frames the sauté earth. Strong Oakville Cab for mushrooms — Napa's golden-strip complexity on the earthy side.",
  "Mushrooms|Ghost Block Zinfandel": "Napa Oakville Zinfandel — Ghost Block, ripe jammy fruit, blackberry preserves, cracked pepper, full body, medium tannin. The cracked pepper plays with roasted-mushroom butter-depth, though the jammy fruit reads heavy for earth-glutamate. Strong California-Zin for mushrooms — an old-world Grenache fits earthier.",
