  "Mushrooms|Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir": "Mushrooms: this earthy, umami-packed side's mushroom-and-truffle depth meets this elegant red's cherry-bright, silky-tannin frame. The elegant red's acidity cuts the dairy fat while its cherry lifts the earthy umami. Strong — the wine refreshes the side's richness.",
  "Mushrooms|Sauternes Glass": "Sauternes Glass' dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the mushrooms' earthy umami weight -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Los Vecinos Mezcal, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Sauternes Glass for the steak course.",
  "Mushrooms|Sazerac": "Sazerac rye, Peychaud's, sugar, absinthe-rinsed glass. The rye's spice cuts mushroom-side butter-sauté richness and the absinthe-edge adds aromatic lift against earth. Strong pairing — the Sazerac's structure and nose handles mushroom depth well.",
