  "Mushrooms|Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon": "Silver Oak — Alexander Valley Cab with American-oak vanilla, coconut, dill, ripe cassis, plum. The lush body meshes with mushroom umami and the vanilla-dill frames the sauté. Strong recognizable Cab for mushrooms — American-oak signature works, though savory Cabs like Gundlach peak higher on earth-on-earth match.",
  "Mushrooms|Simon Family Estate Reserve": "Boutique Napa family estate Cab — dark plum, cassis, toasted oak, long refined finish, firm tannin. The toasted oak echoes roasted-mushroom glutamate and the dark plum plays against the earth depth. Strong boutique Napa Cab for mushrooms — Simon Family estate structure on the earthy side.",
  "Mushrooms|Spottswoode Lyndenhurst": "St. Helena Napa Cab — Spottswoode organic family estate, plum, dark cherry, violet, silky medium tannin. The silky structure echoes roasted-mushroom glutamate and the plum plays against the earth depth. Peak organic Napa Cab for mushrooms — Spottswoode family story on the earthy side. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Mushrooms|St Supéry Cabernet Sauvignon": "Napa Rutherford Cab — blackberry, cassis, mocha, full body. The earth-mocha profile meshes directly with mushroom umami and the firm tannin frames the sauté without overwhelming. Peak by-the-glass Cab for mushrooms — classic Napa character, natural earth-on-earth pairing. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Mushrooms|St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc": "St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc's citrus-lemon acidity plays cleanly against the mushrooms' earthy umami — the crisp acidity sits with the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Mushrooms|St Supéry Élu Meritage": "Napa Dollarhide Meritage — blackcurrant, black cherry, espresso, toasty oak, firm tannin. The espresso-earth echoes roasted-mushroom glutamate and the toasty oak plays against the earth depth. Peak estate Meritage for mushrooms — Napa Bordeaux-style on the earthy side. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Mushrooms|Stagg Jr. Batch #15": "Stagg Jr. Batch #15 with mushrooms — BT non-age-statement cask-strength against earthy umami. Strong; Stagg Jr.'s cask-strength threads mushrooms at barrel-proof register.",
  "Mushrooms|Stoli Elit Vodka": "Stoli Elit Vodka's crisp ultra-filtered-luxury neutrality leans against the mushrooms' earthy umami — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; capable alongside. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Mushrooms|Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc": "Marlborough Sauvignon Blanc — grassy, green, light-bodied. Wrong weight class entirely for mushroom umami; the wine vanishes underneath the earthy depth. Keep Stoneleigh for the wedge salad or shrimp cocktail where it has a defined job to do. Avoid; the pairing fights at the table — point the guest elsewhere.",
  "Mushrooms|Swordfish": "The swordfish alongside the mushrooms -- the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak meets the mushrooms' earthy umami weight cleanly. Strong; the call reads at register without overshooting against the main.",
  "Mushrooms|Tanq 10 Gin": "Tanq 10 Gin's crisp citrus-floral botanicals leans against the mushrooms' earthy umami — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; the match holds without overshooting. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Mushrooms|Tanqueray Gin": "Tanqueray Gin's bold London-Dry-juniper botanicals plays cleanly against the mushrooms' earthy umami — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Mushrooms|Taylor Fladgate Tawny": "Taylor Fladgate Tawny's classic tawny with caramel-nut sweetness clashes with the mushrooms' earthy umami weight -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Los Vecinos Mezcal, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a dessert wine. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Taylor Fladgate Tawny on the steak course instead.",
  "Mushrooms|Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle": "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the mushrooms' earthy umami weight -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Los Vecinos Mezcal, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle for the steak course.",
  "Mushrooms|Tears of Llorona": "Tears of Llorona with the mushrooms — multi-cask aged against earthy umami. The Scotch/sherry/cognac cask layers create mushroom-pairing complexity no single-cask aged tequila reaches. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Mushrooms|Teeter Totter Cabernet Sauvignon": "Teeter Totter — Napa Cab, rich dark fruit, mocha, smooth finish. The polished body meshes with mushroom umami and the mocha frames the sauté earth. Peak mid-tier Napa Cab for mushrooms — crowd-pleaser concentration on the earthy side without prestige-bottle commitment. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Mushrooms|Tenuta di Arceno Chianti Classico": "Mushrooms: Cab tannin frames the earthy mushroom-and-truffle depth; dark fruit lifts the umami into the wine's body. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Mushrooms|The BG": "The BG's crisp citrus-earth build sits beside the mushrooms' earthy umami — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Mushrooms|The Happy Wife": "The Happy Wife's crisp citrus-ginger build stays alongside the mushrooms' earthy umami — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the spice frames the umami depth. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Mushrooms|The Manhattan": "Maker's Mark private barrel with Contratto, vanilla syrup, Angostura. The vanilla-sweet bourbon wraps around mushroom's earthy depth; classic cocktail on a classic side. Heavier cocktail route for committed spirit guests. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Mushrooms|The Prisoner Red Blend": "Napa Red Blend — The Prisoner, Zin-Cab-Petite Sirah-Syrah-Charbono, layered dark fruit, smooth integrated tannin, full body, lush finish. The layered dark fruit plays with roasted-mushroom butter-depth and the full body handles glutamate-weight. Peak Prisoner for mushrooms — Napa lush on the earthy side. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Mushrooms|The Tomahawk": "The Tomahawk with the mushrooms -- umami plays against the protein, the table earns its depth. Works; the side carries cleanly with the cut.",
