  "Mushrooms|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "The tuna into the mushrooms -- the delicate course primes the savory, the table builds register. Works; safe alongside, but not the headline pick.",
  "Mushrooms|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "The curry opens the meal, the mushrooms with the entree -- the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth sets up cleanly for the mushrooms' earthy umami weight. Strong; the build reads thoughtful across the courses.",
  "Mushrooms|Venge Family Reserve": "Mushrooms: the mushroom's umami depth meets the bold red's structured tannin; dark fruit threads the truffle-and-earth without crowding. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the pairing reads at register.",
  "Mushrooms|Venge Scout's Honor": "Napa Zin-led blend — Kirk Venge's Scout's Honor, blackberry, boysenberry, black pepper, vanilla, full body, generous finish. Vanilla plays with garlic-butter glaze and black pepper lifts umami earthiness. Works for mushroom side — Zin-led fruit bridges funky richness; Scavino or Caymus fits harder.",
  "Mushrooms|Venge Silencieux": "Kirk Venge single-vineyard Napa — dark cherry, cassis, chocolate, floral violet, silky soft tannin. The chocolate echoes roasted-mushroom glutamate and the violet plays against the earth depth. Peak winemaker's Napa Cab for mushrooms — Venge precision on the earthy side. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Mushrooms|Vesper": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build sits alongside the mushrooms' earthy umami — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Mushrooms|Veuve Clicquot Brut": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's classic yellow-label Champagne body reads alongside the mushrooms' earthy umami weight: the pinot-driven lift brightens the mushrooms, and the toast-and-citrus edge frames the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Mushrooms|Vieux Carré": "Sazerac rye, Pierre Ferrand cognac, Contratto, Bénédictine, two bitters. The Bénédictine's herbal complexity meets the mushroom side's earth directly and the rye-cognac split handles the butter-sauté richness. Strong pairing — a nuanced cocktail for a nuanced side.",
  "Mushrooms|Villon Cognac": "Villon with mushrooms — cocktail-ready cognac spirit against earthy umami. Strong; Villon's infusion threads the mushrooms at contemporary register.",
  "Mushrooms|Vin Santo": "Vin Santo's Tuscan dried-fruit-and-honey sweetness clashes with the mushrooms' earthy umami weight -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Los Vecinos Mezcal, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Vin Santo belongs on the steak course.",
  "Mushrooms|Weller 107": "Weller 107 with the mushrooms — the extra proof gives the pour weight against umami. Bolder than Weller Special Reserve here; the Weller for a guest who wants wheat character but doesn't want the pour to recede. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Mushrooms|Weller 12 Year": "Weller 12 Year with the mushrooms — aged honey and oak meet earthy umami. The 12-year's complexity gives the side layers; less approachable than Weller Special Reserve with mushrooms, more polished than Weller 107. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Mushrooms|Weller Millennium": "Weller Millennium with the mushrooms — the Millennium's layered oak meets mushroom umami in a sophisticated interplay. The depth earns the pairing beyond 'just wheated and earth'; this is the premium Weller for this side. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Mushrooms|Weller Special Reserve": "Weller Special Reserve with the mushrooms — approachable wheated honey meets earthy umami. The 90-proof softness lets the mushrooms lead; a gentle but aligned side pairing. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
