  "Myers's Rum|Chilean Seabass": "Myers's Rum's aged-rum register with molasses and oak depth overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- heavy spirit weight buries the main protein — needs a wine or lighter spirit. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Myers's Rum for the steak course.",
  "Myers's Rum|Chocolate Brownie": "Myers's Rum: Jamaican dark rum, Diageo-owned, molasses-heavy workhorse. Excellent on brownie; the molasses-forward profile threads chocolate at cocktail-staple register — this is the dark-rum-on-dessert classic without the Zacapa luxury or Doctor Bird funk.",
