  "Myers's Rum|Crab Cake": "Myers's Rum's aged-rum register with molasses and oak depth overwhelms the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- the spirit's weight is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; the better calls are above. Myers's Rum lands on the steak course — not here.",
