  "Myers's Rum|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Myers's Rum's aged-rum register with molasses and oak depth overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- heavy spirit weight buries the main protein — needs a wine or lighter spirit. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Myers's Rum for the steak course.",
