  "Myers's Rum|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Myers's Rum's aged-rum register with molasses and oak depth overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- heavy spirit weight buries the main protein — needs a wine or lighter spirit. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Myers's Rum for the steak course.",
