  "Not a Paper Plane|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build finds neutral with the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Beignets": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build plays cleanly against the beignet's warm sugar-dusted pastry — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Bone Marrow": "Bulleit bourbon, Nonino Quintessential, Aperol, Angostura. The bourbon cuts marrow's rendered fat and Nonino's herbal-bitter backbone adds complexity against savory bone; Aperol softens the edges. Peak spirit-forward cocktail for marrow when guest wants amaro-driven over pure bourbon.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Bone-In Filet": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build sits beside the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the cocktail is outweighed by the cut, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Broccoli Cheddar": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build leans against the broccoli cheddar's cream — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Broccolini": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build reads alongside the broccolini's tender green — the cocktail lift sits with the light side, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Brussels and Belly": "Bulleit bourbon, Nonino amaro, Aperol, Angostura. The bourbon meets belly's rendered fat and Nonino's herbal bitterness cuts against the belly's sweet glaze; Aperol plays with brussels char. Works — though Bowdie's Old Fashioned and Espresso OF peak higher for this build.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Burrata": "Bulleit bourbon, Nonino amaro, Aperol, Angostura. Spirit-forward amaro-bourbon cocktail crushes burrata's creamy-delicate profile; the cocktail has no hook into basil-tomato-cheese. Never pair — burrata belongs with Prosecco, French 75, or light gin cocktails.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Butternut Squash": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build plays cleanly against the squash soup's silky sweet — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Carrot Cake": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build stays alongside the carrot cake's spiced cream cheese — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Cheesecake": "Not a Paper Plane's stirred whiskey-led build finds neutral with the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the bold-mix depth handles the cheesecake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Chilean Seabass": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build matches the seabass's buttery flesh — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Chocolate Brownie": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build plays cleanly against the brownie's warm cocoa depth — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Chocolate Cake": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build sits alongside the cake's layered chocolate — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Clam Chowder": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build stays alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Cowboy Ribeye": "Cowboy Ribeye: this marbled ribeye's fatty richness, smoky crust, and bold beef expression meets this bold whiskey-forward cocktail's oak, spice, and spirit depth. Whiskey depth, oak, and sweetness carry beef weight — the drink scrubs fat and echoes char. Strong — steakhouse classic.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Crab Cake": "Bulleit bourbon, Nonino Quintessential, Aperol, Angostura. Spirit-forward bourbon-and-amaro weight overwhelms crab's sweet-delicate meat; the cocktail has no hook into the light romesco. Never pair — crab cake belongs with Sauv Blanc, French 75, or gin cocktails.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Creamed Spinach": "Bulleit bourbon, Nonino amaro, Aperol, Angostura. The bourbon-and-amaro depth sits alongside creamed spinach's dairy weight; Nonino's bitterness cuts the cream and Aperol brightens against parmesan. Strong pairing — a sophisticated cocktail for a classic side.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Creamy Potato": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build leans against the potato soup's silky body — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Creme Brulee": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Escargot": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build reads alongside the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the cocktail lift refreshes the starter, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the match holds without overshooting. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Faroe Island Salmon": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build lifts the salmon's rich oily flesh — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Filet Mignon": "Bulleit bourbon, Nonino amaro, Aperol, Angostura — stirred, spirit-forward. The bourbon depth meets butter-tender filet and Nonino's clean herbal bitterness cuts the beef's richness; Aperol's orange edge adds aromatic lift. Peak amaro-forward cocktail for filet — rewards attention.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|French Onion": "Not a Paper Plane's spirit-forward cocktail register reads alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the bold-mix depth handles the French onion, and the bitters edge frames the bowl. Works; the opener sits without competing.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Grilled Caesar": "Bulleit bourbon, Nonino amaro, Aperol, Angostura — stirred. The bourbon-and-amaro handles anchovy-parmesan dressing directly and Aperol's bitter orange plays against grilled-romaine char. Peak bitter cocktail for the salad — the Nonino-and-Aperol herbal structure matches the layered flavors.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Gumbo": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build stays alongside the gumbo's spiced Creole stew — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus brightens the spice. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build leans against the carrots' honeyed sweetness — the cocktail lift sits with the light side, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|House Wedge": "Bulleit bourbon, Nonino Quintessential, Aperol, Angostura — stirred. The bourbon-and-amaro structure can handle iceberg-and-blue-cheese weight and Aperol's bitter orange plays against the dressing. Works as an amaro-forward opener — heavier than most wedge cocktails but holds up.",
  "Not a Paper Plane|Kansas City": "Kansas City: this bold, beefy strip's firm texture and savory char meets this bold whiskey-forward cocktail's oak, spice, and spirit depth. Whiskey depth, oak, and sweetness carry beef weight — the drink scrubs fat and echoes char. A headliner steakhouse cocktail. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
