  "Old Elk Cigar Cut|Truffle Fries": "Old Elk Cigar Cut with truffle fries — Old Elk Colorado craft against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Old Elk Cigar Cut's cigar-companion character meets the earthy-rich at distinctive register.",
  "Old Elk Cigar Cut|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Old Elk Cigar Cut's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Old Elk Cigar Cut on the steak course instead.",
  "Old Elk Cigar Cut|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Old Elk Cigar Cut's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the bourbon body sits with the curry, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; Voyage 23 frames the two-cut plate at ocean-finish register.",
  "Old Emmer|Asparagus": "Old Emmer's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the bourbon depth settles into the asparagus, and the oak frames the side. Works; the story is wasted on the salad.",
