  "Old Emmer|Filet Mignon": "Filet Mignon: tenderloin meets emmer-wheat wheated bourbon. Old Emmer's ancient-grain wheated character frames tenderloin with distinctive craft-bourbon register — parallel to Weller 12 and Basil Hayden's approaches, but using an ancient wheat variant. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Old Emmer|French Onion": "Old Emmer's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the oak depth lays under the French onion, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; Remus 15 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
