  "Old Emmer|House Wedge": "House Wedge: iceberg and bleu meet emmer-wheat wheated bourbon. Works; Old Emmer's wheated character threads the wedge at craft register.",
  "Old Emmer|Kansas City": "Old Emmer with the KC — wheated bourbon made from emmer wheat (ancient grain), reclassified from American Single Malt / Tennessee (it's a wheated bourbon, not a single malt). Excellent; Old Emmer's emmer-wheat-derived softness is the distinctive wheated-bourbon-KC pairing — where Weller and Maker's use modern soft red winter wheat, Old Emmer uses the ancient-grain variant for distinctive craft character.",
  "Old Emmer|Loaded Potato": "Old Emmer's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; GTS is over-specified for a side — save the collector bottle.",
  "Old Emmer|Lobster Mac": "Old Emmer's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon weight handles the lobster mac, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; extended-aged home-state pour wasted on salad.",
  "Old Emmer|Market Fish": "Old Emmer's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Old Emmer for the steak course.",
  "Old Emmer|Mocha Creme": "Old Emmer's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the bourbon backbone carries the mocha creme, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; IW Harper 15 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Old Emmer|Mushroom Bisque": "Old Emmer's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the oak depth lays under the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
