  "Old Emmer|Seafood Tower": "Old Emmer's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Old Emmer for the steak course.",
