  "Old Emmer|Seasonal Vegetables": "Old Emmer's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the bourbon weight handles the seasonal vegetables, and the rounded sweetness brightens the side. Works; regional craft at matched register.",
  "Old Emmer|Shrimp Bisque": "Old Emmer's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the brown-spirit warmth threads the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; EC 18's aged character meets the glaze at aged-HH register.",
  "Old Emmer|Shrimp Cocktail": "Old Emmer's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overshadows the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the spirit weight crowds the delicate shellfish — no acid to clean the brine. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Old Emmer for the steak course.",
  "Old Emmer|Swordfish": "Old Emmer's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon's sweet weight crowds the rare crust's clean char. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Old Emmer on the steak course instead.",
  "Old Emmer|The Tomahawk": "Old Emmer's crisp char-earth character holds the line with the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the aged-oak weight carries the flame-grilled char, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Old Emmer|Tomato Basil": "Old Emmer's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the caramel-spice register matches the tomato basil, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; light body doesn't overshoot.",
  "Old Emmer|Truffle Fries": "Old Emmer with truffle fries — emmer-wheat wheated bourbon against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Old Emmer's craft-wheated character meets the earthy-rich at distinctive register.",
  "Old Emmer|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Old Emmer's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Old Emmer for the steak course.",
  "Old Emmer|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Old Emmer's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the caramel-spice register matches the curry, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; richer profile is over-specified for this dish.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Asparagus": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight sits alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the oak depth lays under the asparagus, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; Caribbean Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with au gratin potatoes — 100-proof wheated against cheese-and-cream. Strong; the bonded wheat honey sits with richness cleanly.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Beignets": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the caramel-spice register matches the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Bone Marrow": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with bone marrow — 100-proof wheated BIB against umami fat. The bonded wheat gives the starter a different frame than Wellers' 90-proof softness or Heaven Hill BIB's non-wheated structure. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Bone-In Filet": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's caramel-honey character holds steady against the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the bourbon weight grips the lean cut, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Broccoli Cheddar": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's Heaven Hill's wheated heritage bond reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the bourbon depth settles into the broccoli cheddar, and the rounded sweetness brightens the cream. Works; collector-bottle depth gives the dessert ultra-premium character.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Broccolini": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the bourbon backbone carries the broccolini, and the oak-and-spice register settles the side. Works; single-barrel depth gives the dessert more than Small Batch.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Brussels and Belly": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with Brussels + Belly — wheated BIB meets maple-glazed pork belly. The bonded weight and wheat honey handle the dish's sweetness with more structure than standard wheated pours. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Burrata": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with burrata — fresh dairy against wheated BIB. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Butternut Squash": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's Heaven Hill's wheated heritage bond reads alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bourbon depth settles into the squash bisque, and the caramel-spice settles the cream. Works; the pour's complexity is underused by the salad.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Carrot Cake": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with carrot cake — wheated BIB's honey against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; the bonded weight adds dimension the 90-proof wheated pours don't bring.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Cheesecake": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with cheesecake — 100-proof wheated against custard. Works; bonded weight a touch ambitious for the dessert.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Chilean Seabass": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's Heaven Hill's wheated heritage bond overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Old Fitzgerald 7 Year lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Chocolate Brownie": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with the chocolate brownie — wheated BIB against cocoa. Works; for cocoa interplay, Weller 107 or Basil Hayden's Toast are better calls.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Chocolate Cake": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the bourbon weight handles the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; boutique-blend wasted on salad.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Clam Chowder": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the oak depth lays under the chowder, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; the toast adds a warmth the dessert can accept.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Cowboy Ribeye": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with the Cowboy Ribeye — 100-proof wheated bond against cap fat. The bonded proof earns the ribeye where 90-proof wheated pours fade; the wheated BIB answer to this cut. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Crab Cake": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with crab cake — wheated BIB against delicate crab. Avoid; pour a white wine.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Creamed Spinach": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with creamed spinach — bonded wheat against dairy. Strong; the wheat honey threads through cream with BIB's structural backbone.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Creamy Potato": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the bourbon backbone carries the potato soup, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; EC 18 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Creme Brulee": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's Heaven Hill's wheated heritage bond sits alongside the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the bourbon depth settles into the brulee, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; distinctive character doesn't drive.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Escargot": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character sits at register with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the bourbon backbone carries the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; distinctive character sits with richness at novelty register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Faroe Island Salmon": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's Heaven Hill's wheated heritage bond clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Old Fitzgerald 7 Year for the steak course.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Filet Mignon": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with the filet — Heaven Hill's wheated heritage bond. 100-proof BIB, 7 years aged, wheated mash. Distinct from Larceny's 92-proof wheated and from Wellers' similar wheated profile — more bonded weight. The wheated BIB for filet orders. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|French Onion": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the bourbon depth settles into the French onion, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; master-blender doesn't drive.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Grilled Caesar": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with the grilled Caesar — charred romaine against wheated bond. Works; Old Fitz 9 brings more depth here.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Gumbo": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the bourbon weight handles the gumbo, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; multi-distillery complexity doesn't drive.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's Heaven Hill's wheated heritage bond sits alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the bourbon depth settles into the honey carrots, and the oak frames the caramelized sugar. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|House Wedge": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with the House Wedge — iceberg and bleu against wheated BIB. Works; pour slightly over-specified for the salad.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Kansas City": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with the KC — 100-proof wheated bond against the strip's marbling. The bonded weight from Heaven Hill's wheated heritage carries the cut cleanly; distinct from Heaven Hill BIB (non-wheated) — honey-softer, still 100-proof. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Loaded Potato": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the brown-spirit warmth threads the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Lobster Mac": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the lobster mac, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; the 10-year's restraint lets the soup lead.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Market Fish": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's Heaven Hill's wheated heritage bond flattens the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Old Fitzgerald 7 Year belongs on the steak course.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Mocha Creme": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the bourbon backbone carries the mocha creme, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Mushroom Bisque": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the bourbon depth settles into the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; bonded weight pushes past the soup's register slightly.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Mushrooms": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with the mushrooms — 100-proof wheated against earthy umami. The bonded wheat honey plays with mushroom depth distinctively. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the caramel-spice register matches the PB brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; pour is a touch over-specified for the dessert.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Porterhouse": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with the porterhouse — wheated BIB across strip and filet. Strong; bonded weight leans strip-side, filet tolerates; Old Fitz 9 brings more age for this plate.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Prime Tartare": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's caramel-honey character sits with the tartare's raw beef and brine — the caramel-oak depth threads the savory plate, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Rainbow Trout": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's Heaven Hill's wheated heritage bond flattens the trout's delicate flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Old Fitzgerald 7 Year for the steak course.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Roast Half Chicken": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the bourbon depth settles into the roast chicken, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the plate. Works; X Commandments story wasted on salad.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's Heaven Hill's wheated heritage bond reads alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the bourbon depth settles into the chickpea soup, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's Heaven Hill's wheated heritage bond overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Old Fitzgerald 7 Year belongs on the steak course.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the bourbon depth settles into the garlic spinach, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; the 10-year holds without lifting.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Seafood Tower": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's Heaven Hill's wheated heritage bond fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Old Fitzgerald 7 Year on the steak course instead.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Seared Scallops": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 100-proof. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Seasonal Soup": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the caramel-spice register matches the seasonal soup, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; save the collector bottle for the protein course.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Seasonal Vegetables": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the bourbon weight handles the seasonal vegetables, and the oak-and-spice register settles the side. Works; bonded weight pushes slightly past the soup.",
  "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year|Shrimp Bisque": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood against wheated BIB. Works; bonded weight pushes slightly past the soup.",
