  "Paloma|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Paloma's crisp agave-citrus build finds register with the tuna's seared rare crust — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Paloma|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Paloma's crisp agave-citrus build reads alongside the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus brightens the spice. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Asparagus": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character finds neutral with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the asparagus, and the rye edge frames the side. Works; BH Red Wine Cask meets the char at distinctive register.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the allocated rye depth threads the au gratin, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; no driver pairing.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Beignets": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the high-rye spice register matches the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; HH 20 is over-specified for an app; save the collector bottle for the main.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Bone Marrow": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with bone marrow — unicorn Pappy against umami fat. The Van Winkle legacy intensity meets marrow with allocation-story authority; a once-a-table pairing. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Bone-In Filet": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye -- allocated, aged rye, caramel-spice. The dry rye body wraps the bone-enhanced filet, and the spice-and-vanilla thread softens the cut. Strong; Vermont-brand character cuts the glaze with distinctive rye voice.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Broccoli Cheddar": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character leans against the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the allocated rye depth threads the broccoli cheddar, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the richer pour finds more with the dessert than Original brings.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Broccolini": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character leans against the broccolini's tender green stalks: the dry rye body wraps the broccolini, and the rye-pepper note underlines the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Brussels and Belly": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with Brussels + Belly — Van Winkle Family Reserve meets maple-glazed pork belly. The 13-year Pappy depth cuts the glaze with unicorn Van Winkle authority. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Burrata": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with burrata — fresh dairy against Van Winkle Family Reserve. Avoid; unicorn rye deserves better.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Butternut Squash": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the allocated rye depth threads the squash bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the pour's assertiveness is a bit much for the soup but doesn't clash.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Carrot Cake": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character leans against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the carrot cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; wine-cask over-specified.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Cheesecake": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character sits alongside the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the high-rye spice register matches the cheesecake, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; OGD 16 handles dessert density at distinctive register.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Chilean Seabass": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon weight needs red meat, not the salmon's already-rich oils. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye for the steak course.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Chocolate Brownie": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with the chocolate brownie — unicorn Pappy Rye against cocoa. Works; Van Winkle legacy meets the brownie at allocation register.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Chocolate Cake": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character reads alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the rye backbone drives the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the richer pour finds more with the dessert than Original brings.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Clam Chowder": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the rye-and-oak weight handles the chowder, and the oak softens the cream. Works; JW Black handles the richness at premium-blend register.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Cowboy Ribeye": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with the Cowboy Ribeye — unicorn Van Winkle rye against cap fat. The 13-year Pappy depth gives the ribeye Van Winkle-legacy intensity; collector-pour with serious scarcity. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Crab Cake": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character crowds out the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye belongs on the steak course.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Creamed Spinach": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with creamed spinach — Pappy Rye against dairy. Strong; Van Winkle legacy sits with richness at unicorn register.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Creamy Potato": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the rye backbone drives the potato soup, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; BIB structure is a touch over-specified for this dish.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Creme Brulee": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the high-rye spice register matches the brulee, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; craft-blend over-specified.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Escargot": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's bold allocated-caramel character frames the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; the call lands cleanly.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Faroe Island Salmon": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye belongs on the steak course.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Filet Mignon": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with the filet — unicorn Van Winkle against the 10oz cut. The 13-year Pappy Rye earns the filet at excellent; the Van Winkle-legacy rye for filet orders — extreme scarcity means this is once-a-table territory. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|French Onion": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character leans against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the high-rye spice register matches the French onion, and the rye edge frames the bowl. Works; the pour's sweetness meets the dessert without pushing past.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Grilled Caesar": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with the grilled Caesar — 13-year Pappy against charred romaine. Works; Van Winkle legacy doesn't drive the Caesar.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Gumbo": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character sits alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the rye backbone drives the gumbo, and the rye-pepper note underlines the bowl. Works; IW Harper 15 frames the two-cut plate at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character reads alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the honey carrots, and the oak balances the burnt-sugar edge. Works; Voyage 23 handles the richness at ocean-finish register.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|House Wedge": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with the House Wedge — Van Winkle unicorn against iceberg and bleu. Works; Pappy's allocation story is wasted on salad.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Kansas City": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with the KC — Van Winkle Family Reserve against the strip. The 13-year unicorn gives the strip Pappy-legacy depth; the absolute top-shelf rye for strip when it's the table's special occasion. Gold standard; the headline call at the table.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Loaded Potato": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character leans against the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the rye backbone drives the loaded potato soup, and the oak softens the cream. Works; CC 43 Year is over-specified for a side; save the rare bottle for the main.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Lobster Mac": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the rye backbone drives the lobster mac, and the oak softens the cream. Works; milestone-release covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Market Fish": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye for the steak course.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Mocha Creme": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character finds neutral with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the rye spice cuts the mocha creme, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; Parker's Heritage 16th is over-specified for an app; save the collector bottle for the main.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Mushroom Bisque": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the mushroom bisque, and the oak balances the umami register. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Mushrooms": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with the mushrooms — unicorn Pappy against earthy umami. Strong; Van Winkle legacy layers into mushroom depth at allocation register.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with the PB brownie — Van Winkle Family Reserve against peanut butter and cocoa. Works; unicorn depth gives the dessert Pappy-legacy character.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Porterhouse": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with the porterhouse — Van Winkle Family Reserve across strip and filet. Strong; unicorn Pappy leans strip-side on this plate.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Prime Tartare": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with the tartare — unicorn Pappy against raw beef. Strong; Van Winkle legacy is a collector-register counterpoint to tartare; save Pappy for tables that know what they ordered.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Rainbow Trout": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character smothers the trout's delicate flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Roast Half Chicken": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character reads alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the rye-and-oak weight handles the roast chicken, and the spice-and-vanilla thread softens the plate. Works; HH rye interesting but doesn't drive.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character reads alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the rye-and-oak weight handles the chickpea soup, and the rye edge frames the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character swallows the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye on the steak course instead.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character sits alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the high-rye spice register matches the garlic spinach, and the rye edge frames the side. Works; the unique maturation story adds interest to a gentle dessert match.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Seafood Tower": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye for the steak course.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Seared Scallops": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character smothers the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye for the steak course.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Seasonal Soup": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character reads alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the rye-and-oak weight handles the seasonal soup, and the rye edge frames the bowl. Works; GTS is over-specified for a side — save the collector bottle.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Seasonal Vegetables": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character sits alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the dry rye body wraps the seasonal vegetables, and the rye-pepper note underlines the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Shrimp Bisque": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the rye backbone drives the shrimp bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; high proof over-specified for the soup.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Shrimp Cocktail": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against unicorn Pappy. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Swordfish": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character overwhelms the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye on the steak course instead.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|The Tomahawk": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with the Tomahawk — the Van Winkle Family Reserve Rye, 13 years, 95.6 proof, Buffalo Trace-produced. Unicorn allocation; one of the rarest ryes on any menu. The Tomahawk meets its unicorn rye counterpart — a pairing that only happens when the table specifically asks for Pappy Rye. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Tomato Basil": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the rye-and-oak weight handles the tomato basil, and the rye edge frames the bowl. Works; novelty maturation at matched register.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Truffle Fries": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with truffle fries — Pappy Rye against truffle-parmesan. The Van Winkle unicorn gives the side legacy-level ceremony. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye for the steak course.",
  "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the rye-and-oak weight handles the curry, and the spice-and-vanilla thread softens the bowl. Works; Old Fitz 9 brings more depth here.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Asparagus": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth clashes with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- the bourbon's register is wrong for a clean vegetable side — needs crisp white instead. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition for the steak course.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with the au gratin — HH collector cask-strength against cheese-and-cream potatoes. Works; Parker's Heritage 16th handles the richness at annual-release register.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Beignets": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon body sits with the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; collector-bottle doesn't drive.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Bone Marrow": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with bone marrow — HH collector cask-strength against umami fat. Excellent; Parker's Heritage 16th cuts marrow at annual-release register — its cask-strength weight actually matches marrow.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Bone-In Filet": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads register-aligned with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the bone-enhanced filet, and the oak-and-spice register settles the cut. Strong; wine-cask complexity sits with richness.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Broccoli Cheddar": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the brown-spirit warmth threads the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; bold proof overshoots delicacy.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Broccolini": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth crowds the broccolini's tender green stalks -- the spirit needs the cut, not the supporting side. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Brussels and Belly": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with Brussels + Belly — HH annual cask-strength against maple-glazed pork belly. Excellent; Parker's Heritage 16th meets the glaze with collector-register intensity.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Burrata": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with burrata — HH annual cask-strength against fresh dairy. Avoid; barrel-proof obliterates burrata.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Butternut Squash": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the squash bisque, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Carrot Cake": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with carrot cake — HH collector against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; Parker's Heritage 16th meets the cake at annual-release register.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Cheesecake": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with cheesecake — HH annual cask-strength against custard. Avoid; barrel-proof intensity is wrong for custard's delicate character.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Chilean Seabass": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon weight needs red meat, not the salmon's already-rich oils. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition on the steak course instead.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Chocolate Brownie": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with the chocolate brownie — Heaven Hill collector cask-strength against cocoa. Excellent; Parker's Heritage 16th's annual-release intensity meets cocoa at collector register.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Chocolate Cake": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the bourbon backbone carries the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; curated doesn't drive.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Clam Chowder": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon depth settles into the chowder, and the oak frames the cream. Works; boutique-sourced wasted on salad.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Cowboy Ribeye": "Cowboy Ribeye: 26oz bone-in cap-fat meets Heaven Hill annual limited release, 16th Edition in the Parker's Heritage tribute series, collector-register cask-strength. Parker's Heritage brings HH's heritage collector-register craft to 26oz cap-fat — the annual-release provenance makes every pour a conversation about which edition you're serving. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Crab Cake": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with crab cake — HH collector cask-strength against delicate lump crab. Avoid; barrel-proof obliterates crab. Reach for a vodka or gin.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Creamed Spinach": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with creamed spinach — Heaven Hill annual against dairy-rich side. Strong; Parker's Heritage 16th's cask-strength cuts the cream at collector register.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Creamy Potato": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the potato soup, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for a side — save the collector bottle for the main.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Creme Brulee": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the bourbon depth settles into the brulee, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; IW Harper 15 handles dessert density at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Escargot": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads register-aligned with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the brown-spirit warmth threads the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Faroe Island Salmon": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with the salmon — HH cask-strength against oily salmon. Avoid; barrel-proof bourbon too intense for fish.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Filet Mignon": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with the filet — HH annual limited cask-strength against tenderloin. Works; Parker's Heritage 16th is over-specified for filet — save the collector bottle for the ribeye/Tomahawk.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|French Onion": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth leans against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the bourbon body sits with the French onion, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; EHT Full Proof handles the richness at historic Kentucky register.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Grilled Caesar": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with the grilled Caesar — HH annual against charred romaine and anchovy. Works; Parker's Heritage 16th is over-specified for an app; save the collector bottle for the main.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Gumbo": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the brown-spirit warmth threads the gumbo, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- the side reads small under oak-and-vanilla density. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition belongs on the steak course.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|House Wedge": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's soft-oak bourbon body leans against the wedge's iceberg-and-bleu cool crunch: the brown-spirit warmth threads the wedge, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; Marian McLain L.E.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Kansas City": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with the KC — Heaven Hill collector annual against an 18oz strip. Excellent; Parker's Heritage 16th's cask-strength handles strip marbling at HH-annual-release register.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Loaded Potato": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the bourbon depth settles into the loaded potato soup, and the caramel-spice settles the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Lobster Mac": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the brown-spirit warmth threads the lobster mac, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Market Fish": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition for the steak course.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Mocha Creme": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the mocha creme, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; Marian McLain L.E.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Mushroom Bisque": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the oak depth lays under the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Mushrooms": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with mushrooms — Heaven Hill collector against earthy umami. Strong; Parker's Heritage 16th's cask-strength character threads mushrooms at annual-release register.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with the PB brownie — HH collector against peanut butter and cocoa. Strong; Parker's Heritage 16th's cask-strength handles dessert density at annual-release register.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Porterhouse": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with the porterhouse — HH annual collector bourbon against strip-and-filet. Strong; Parker's Heritage 16th frames the two-cut plate at collector cask-strength register.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Prime Tartare": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's rounded-oak bourbon character sits at register with the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami: the bourbon backbone carries the tartare, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; the 10-year oak gives the side backbone distinct from wheated approaches; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Rainbow Trout": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Roast Half Chicken": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with the chicken — HH collector cask-strength against roasted poultry. Avoid; barrel-proof is over-specified for chicken — save the collector bottle.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the caramel-spice register matches the chickpea soup, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; collector-bottle doesn't drive.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition for the steak course.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth crowds the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- the spirit needs the cut, not the supporting side. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition for the steak course.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Seafood Tower": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition for the steak course.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Seared Scallops": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with seared scallops — collector cask-strength against scallop delicacy. Avoid; barrel-proof wrong for scallops.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Seasonal Soup": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth leans against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the bourbon depth settles into the seasonal soup, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; JW Blue is over-specified for a side — save the bottle for the main course.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Seasonal Vegetables": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth crowds the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate -- the spirit needs the cut, not the supporting side. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition for the steak course.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Shrimp Bisque": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon weight handles the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; save the bottle for the protein course — a soup is wrong for a $200 pour.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Shrimp Cocktail": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with shrimp cocktail — HH collector cask-strength against cold shrimp. Avoid; barrel-proof wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Swordfish": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|The Tomahawk": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with the Tomahawk — HH annual collector bourbon against 32oz bone-in cap-fat. Excellent; Parker's Heritage 16th's collector cask-strength character handles Tomahawk intensity with HH-annual-release gravitas.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Tomato Basil": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the bourbon depth settles into the tomato basil, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Truffle Fries": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with truffle fries — HH annual cask-strength against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Parker's Heritage 16th meets the earthy-rich at collector register.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition for the steak course.",
  "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the bourbon depth settles into the curry, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; the Millennium's register overshoots the dessert's.",
  "Patron Anejo|Asparagus": "Patron Anejo's rested-agave body sits alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the barrel-rested body handles the asparagus, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Patron Anejo|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet Patron Anejo. Works; vanilla-caramel handles richness at workhorse register.",
  "Patron Anejo|Beignets": "Patron Anejo's barrel-aged tequila weight finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the barrel-rested body handles the beignets, and the cooked-agave note underlines the dessert. Works; luxury over-specified for small plate.",
  "Patron Anejo|Bone Marrow": "Patron Anejo's crisp oak-agave character sits with the marrow's umami-fat depth — the añejo depth cuts the umami fat, and the oak underlines the char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Patron Anejo|Bone-In Filet": "Patron Anejo's aged-agave character sits alongside the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the añejo register carries the bone-enhanced filet, and the cooked-agave note underlines the cut. Strong; the boutique character gives dimension but the starter earns a heavier pour.",
  "Patron Anejo|Broccoli Cheddar": "Patron Anejo's cooked-agave-and-oak register leans against the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the añejo register carries the broccoli cheddar, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Patron Anejo|Broccolini": "Patron Anejo's rested-agave body sits alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the añejo register carries the broccolini, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; the wine-cask notes don't compete with the dish's sweetness effectively.",
  "Patron Anejo|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed meets Patron Anejo. Excellent; vanilla-caramel rides the maple glaze at accessible register — sugar on sugar through American-oak.",
  "Patron Anejo|Burrata": "Patron Anejo's aged-agave character fights the burrata's fresh basil-tomato-cream delicacy -- agave and fresh dairy refuse each other texturally. The plate deserves Il Colle Prosecco Superiore, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Patron Anejo on the steak course instead.",
  "Patron Anejo|Butternut Squash": "Patron Anejo's barrel-aged tequila weight finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the barrel-rested body handles the squash bisque, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Patron Anejo|Carrot Cake": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Patron Anejo. Strong; American-oak vanilla-caramel amplifies cake spice at accessible-premium register.",
  "Patron Anejo|Cheesecake": "Patron Anejo's barrel-aged tequila weight finds neutral with the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the rested-agave depth sits with the cheesecake, and the cooked-agave note underlines the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Patron Anejo|Chilean Seabass": "Patron Anejo's aged-agave character clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- agave and oily fish refuse each other — the fish needs acid, not aged spirit. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Patron Anejo belongs on the steak course.",
  "Patron Anejo|Chocolate Brownie": "Chocolate Brownie: warm dark chocolate meets Patron Anejo. Excellent; American-oak vanilla-caramel threads chocolate at premium-gateway añejo register.",
  "Patron Anejo|Chocolate Cake": "Patron Anejo's rested-agave body sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the chocolate cake, and the oak threads the dessert. Works; extended maturation over-specified.",
  "Patron Anejo|Clam Chowder": "Patron Anejo's aged-agave character leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the aged-agave weight wraps the chowder, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; Durango ceremony over-specified for small plate.",
  "Patron Anejo|Cowboy Ribeye": "Patron Anejo's añejo-pour depth sits alongside the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness: the barrel-rested body handles the cap-fat ribeye, and the oak threads the cut. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Patron Anejo|Crab Cake": "Patron Anejo's aged-agave character overwhelms the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- aged tequila is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Patron Anejo for the steak course.",
  "Patron Anejo|Creamed Spinach": "Patron Anejo's crisp oak-agave character lifts the spinach's dairy-rich cream — the añejo weight overshoots the light side, and the oak rounds the cream. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Patron Anejo|Creamy Potato": "Patron Anejo's rested-agave body finds neutral with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the oak-aged tequila body threads the potato soup, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; wheated-soft character handles richness at gentler-Expresiones register.",
  "Patron Anejo|Creme Brulee": "Patron Anejo's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the rested-agave depth sits with the brulee, and the caramel-agave register brightens the dessert. Works; clean and composed pairing.",
  "Patron Anejo|Escargot": "Patron Anejo's cooked-agave-and-oak register sits alongside the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the barrel-rested body handles the buttered escargot, and the oak threads the starter. Strong; accessible agave cuts the dairy at the entry register.",
  "Patron Anejo|Faroe Island Salmon": "Patron Anejo's aged-agave character clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- aged tequila is wrong register for a main fish or poultry course. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Patron Anejo for the steak course.",
  "Patron Anejo|Filet Mignon": "Filet Mignon: tender lean cut meets Patron Anejo. Excellent; the American-oak vanilla-caramel profile frames filet at accessible-premium register — Patron is the universal-recognition añejo on the most refined cut.",
  "Patron Anejo|French Onion": "Patron Anejo's aged-agave character leans against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the barrel-rested body handles the French onion, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; craft character doesn't drive the pairing.",
  "Patron Anejo|Grilled Caesar": "Patron Anejo's añejo-pour depth sits alongside the Caesar's charred-romaine and anchovy edge: the añejo register carries the grilled Caesar, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Patron Anejo|Gumbo": "Patron Anejo's rested-agave body reads alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the oak-aged tequila body threads the gumbo, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Patron Anejo|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Patron Anejo's aged-agave character finds neutral with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the aged-agave weight wraps the honey carrots, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Patron Anejo|House Wedge": "Patron Anejo's rested-agave body sits alongside the wedge's iceberg-and-bleu cool crunch: the oak-aged tequila body threads the wedge, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; the earthy craft character doesn't quite lift the truffle the way polished reposados suggest they might.",
  "Patron Anejo|Kansas City": "Patron Anejo: Jalisco 100% Blue Weber, 12+ months American oak — the most-distributed premium añejo globally, the accessible gateway to aged tequila. Excellent on KC strip; vanilla-caramel-cooked-agave frames the lean cut at premium-workhorse register — the iconic-bottle pour on the steak guest every room knows.",
  "Patron Anejo|Loaded Potato": "Patron Anejo's rested-agave body reads alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the añejo register carries the loaded potato soup, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; refined but not a standout.",
  "Patron Anejo|Lobster Mac": "Patron Anejo's barrel-aged tequila weight sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the oak-aged tequila body threads the lobster mac, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; Ultra's aged depth is over-specified for dessert simplicity.",
  "Patron Anejo|Market Fish": "Patron Anejo's aged-agave character overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- aged-agave weight buries the delicate flesh — agave register is wrong for fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Patron Anejo lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Patron Anejo|Mocha Creme": "Patron Anejo's aged-agave character leans against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the añejo register carries the mocha creme, and the soft-spice note softens the dessert. Works; bold agave is a distinctive counterpoint but slightly overpowering.",
  "Patron Anejo|Mushroom Bisque": "Patron Anejo's añejo-pour depth sits alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the rested-agave depth sits with the mushroom bisque, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; clean and composed pairing.",
  "Patron Anejo|Mushrooms": "Mushrooms: earthy umami meets Patron Anejo. Excellent; the American-oak-aged agave threads mushroom-earth at gateway-añejo register.",
  "Patron Anejo|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Patron Anejo's rested-agave body leans against the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the rested-agave depth sits with the PB brownie, and the oak threads the dessert. Works; accessible aged composed with dessert.",
  "Patron Anejo|Porterhouse": "Patron Anejo's crisp oak-agave character finds register with the porterhouse's two-cut character — the aged-tequila depth grips the marbled cut, and the oak underlines the char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Patron Anejo|Prime Tartare": "Patron Anejo's crisp oak-agave character holds steady against the tartare's raw beef and brine — the añejo depth cuts the umami fat, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Patron Anejo|Rainbow Trout": "Patron Anejo's aged-agave character overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- aged-agave weight buries the delicate flesh — agave register is wrong for fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; the better calls are above. Patron Anejo belongs on the steak course.",
  "Patron Anejo|Roast Half Chicken": "Patron Anejo's cooked-agave-and-oak register leans against the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the rested-agave depth sits with the roast chicken, and the cooked-agave note underlines the plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Patron Anejo|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Patron Anejo's añejo-pour depth leans against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the rested-agave depth sits with the chickpea soup, and the caramel-agave register brightens the bowl. Works; single-estate character handles richness at craft register.",
  "Patron Anejo|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Patron Anejo's aged-agave character clashes with the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- aged tequila is wrong register for a main fish or poultry course. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Patron Anejo for the steak course.",
  "Patron Anejo|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Patron Anejo's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the barrel-rested body handles the garlic spinach, and the oak threads the side. Works; clean and refined but not a marquee pairing.",
  "Patron Anejo|Seafood Tower": "Patron Anejo's aged-agave character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- aged tequila is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Patron Anejo on the steak course instead.",
  "Patron Anejo|Seared Scallops": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Patron Anejo. Avoid; aged-agave heavy for scallops. Reach for a blanco, light rum, or vodka.",
  "Patron Anejo|Seasonal Soup": "Patron Anejo's añejo-pour depth finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the rested-agave depth sits with the seasonal soup, and the caramel-agave register brightens the bowl. Works; the cedar is novel but the dish doesn't call for distinctive-wood character.",
  "Patron Anejo|Seasonal Vegetables": "Patron Anejo's añejo-pour depth sits alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the seasonal vegetables, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; extended maturation composed with this dish.",
  "Patron Anejo|Shrimp Bisque": "Patron Anejo's cooked-agave-and-oak register leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the oak-aged tequila body threads the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; clean character doesn't drive the pairing.",
  "Patron Anejo|Shrimp Cocktail": "Patron Anejo's aged-agave character overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- aged tequila is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Patron Anejo lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Patron Anejo|Swordfish": "Patron Anejo's aged-agave character fights the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the cask-aged agave register pulls against the savory sear. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Patron Anejo on the steak course instead.",
  "Patron Anejo|The Tomahawk": "Patron Anejo's crisp oak-agave character lifts the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the añejo weight matches the cap-fat, and the oak underlines the char. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Patron Anejo|Tomato Basil": "Patron Anejo's rested-agave body finds neutral with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the rested-agave depth sits with the tomato basil, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; cedar and maple don't quite align.",
  "Patron Anejo|Truffle Fries": "Truffle Fries: Parmesan-and-truffle meets Patron Anejo. Excellent; the cooked-agave-vanilla character handles truffle-salt-fat at premium register — crowd-pleasing añejo answer.",
  "Patron Anejo|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Patron Anejo's aged-agave character clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- aged tequila is wrong register for a main fish or poultry course. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Patron Anejo on the steak course instead.",
  "Patron Anejo|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Patron Anejo's añejo-pour depth finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the barrel-rested body handles the curry, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; clean and refined but not a marquee pairing.",
  "Patron Silver|Asparagus": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift sits alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the unaged body brightens the asparagus, and the bright blanco register underlines the side. Works; the ceremony overshoots the dish.",
  "Patron Silver|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the blanco-tequila body matches the au gratin, and the agave-citrus thread frames the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Patron Silver|Beignets": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift falls short of the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- light spirit reads thin against dessert sweetness. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a light spirit. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Patron Silver belongs on the steak course.",
  "Patron Silver|Bone Marrow": "Patron Silver with bone marrow — iconic blanco against umami fat. Avoid; marrow overwhelms clean blanco.",
  "Patron Silver|Bone-In Filet": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift sits alongside the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the unaged body brightens the bone-enhanced filet, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the cut. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Patron Silver|Broccoli Cheddar": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift leans against the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the broccoli cheddar, and the green-agave edge brightens the bowl. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Patron Silver|Broccolini": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift finds neutral with the broccolini's tender green stalks: the unaged body brightens the broccolini, and the bright blanco register underlines the side. Works; clean composes cleanly.",
  "Patron Silver|Brussels and Belly": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift sits alongside Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts: the silver-spirit register lifts the pork-belly plate, and the unaged-cane note plays against the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Patron Silver|Burrata": "Patron Silver with burrata — Patron's clean profile against fresh dairy. The citrus lifts the cream cleanly; an accessible everyday blanco-burrata pairing. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Patron Silver|Butternut Squash": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the squash bisque, and the green-agave edge brightens the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Patron Silver|Carrot Cake": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift falls short of the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- light spirit reads thin against dessert sweetness. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a light spirit. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Patron Silver on the steak course instead.",
  "Patron Silver|Cheesecake": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift falls short of the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- light spirit reads thin against dessert sweetness. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not a light spirit. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Patron Silver for the steak course.",
  "Patron Silver|Chilean Seabass": "Patron Silver -- polished silver tequila, restaurant call, agave-forward. The silver-tequila body brightens the seabass, and the polished agave note threads the plate. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Patron Silver|Chocolate Brownie": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift falls short of the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- light spirit reads thin against dessert sweetness. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not a light spirit. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Patron Silver for the steak course.",
  "Patron Silver|Chocolate Cake": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift falls short of the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- light spirit can't carry chocolate's weight — needs a richer pour like an aged rum or tawny. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not a light spirit. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Patron Silver belongs on the steak course.",
  "Patron Silver|Clam Chowder": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the chowder, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Patron Silver|Cowboy Ribeye": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift underclubs the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness -- light spirit lands short of any prime cut. The plate deserves Macallan 18, Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon, or Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon, not a light spirit. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Patron Silver for another course.",
  "Patron Silver|Crab Cake": "Patron Silver with crab cake — 80-proof iconic blanco, globally the most recognized brand. Clean citrus-forward agave against lump crab; less distinctive than Don Julio Blanco's benchmark character, more globally familiar. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Patron Silver|Creamed Spinach": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift finds neutral with the creamed spinach's rich bechamel-laced greens: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the creamed spinach, and the bright blanco register underlines the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Patron Silver|Creamy Potato": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the silver-spirit register lifts the potato soup, and the green-agave edge brightens the bowl. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Patron Silver|Creme Brulee": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift mis-pairs with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- the spirit reads thin against the custard's richness. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not a light spirit. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Patron Silver belongs on the steak course.",
  "Patron Silver|Escargot": "Patron Silver with escargot — 80-proof Patron against garlic-butter snails. The clean citrus cuts the garlic-butter at the accessible register. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Patron Silver|Faroe Island Salmon": "Patron Silver with the salmon — iconic blanco against salmon's richness. The citrus-forward character frames the salmon at the everyday accessible tier. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Patron Silver|Filet Mignon": "Patron Silver with the filet — 80-proof iconic Patron against the 10oz cut. Works; blanco isn't the natural filet call.",
  "Patron Silver|French Onion": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the blanco-tequila body matches the French onion, and the green-agave edge brightens the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Patron Silver|Grilled Caesar": "Patron Silver with the grilled Caesar — Patron against charred romaine. Strong; the citrus and anchovy find each other at the everyday globally-familiar register.",
  "Patron Silver|Gumbo": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift leans against the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the gumbo, and the green-agave edge brightens the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Patron Silver|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift finds neutral with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the silver-spirit register lifts the honey carrots, and the agave-citrus thread frames the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Patron Silver|House Wedge": "Patron Silver with the House Wedge — globally-marketed blanco against iceberg and bleu. The clean citrus cuts the bleu at the everyday accessible register. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Patron Silver|Kansas City": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift reads alongside the KC's lean-bold strip with savory grain: the blanco-tequila body matches the strip steak, and the agave-citrus thread frames the cut. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Patron Silver|Loaded Potato": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift leans against the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the loaded potato soup, and the agave-citrus thread frames the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Patron Silver|Lobster Mac": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the unaged body brightens the lobster mac, and the unaged-cane note plays against the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Patron Silver|Market Fish": "Patron Silver with the market fish — Patron against catch of the day. Works; clean blanco lifts the fish at the accessible register.",
  "Patron Silver|Mocha Creme": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift falls short of the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- light spirit reads thin against dessert sweetness. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not a light spirit. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Patron Silver for the steak course.",
  "Patron Silver|Mushroom Bisque": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the blanco-tequila body matches the mushroom bisque, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the bowl. Works; clean composes cleanly.",
  "Patron Silver|Mushrooms": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift finds neutral with the mushrooms' earthy umami weight: the blanco-tequila body matches the mushrooms, and the agave-citrus thread frames the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Patron Silver|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift falls short of the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- light spirit reads thin against dessert sweetness. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not a light spirit. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Patron Silver for the steak course.",
  "Patron Silver|Porterhouse": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift reads alongside the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character: the silver-spirit register lifts the dual-cut steak, and the agave-citrus thread frames the cut. Works; refined character is slightly over-specified for the dish.",
  "Patron Silver|Prime Tartare": "Patron Silver with the tartare — iconic Patron against raw beef. The clean citrus-forward agave is a bright counterpoint at the globally-familiar register. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Patron Silver|Rainbow Trout": "Patron Silver -- polished silver tequila, restaurant call, agave-forward. The silver-tequila body brightens the trout, and the polished agave note threads the plate. Strong; the clean family-heritage character provides a craft through-line.",
  "Patron Silver|Roast Half Chicken": "Patron Silver with the roast half chicken — iconic blanco against roasted chicken. Works; citrus-forward composes cleanly.",
  "Patron Silver|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift sits alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the chickpea soup, and the agave-citrus thread frames the bowl. Works; refined craft composes cleanly.",
  "Patron Silver|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Patron Silver's crisp agave-pepper character holds the line with the halibut's salt-cured flesh — the crisp body frames the fish cleanly, and the agave anchors the savory plate. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Patron Silver|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift leans against the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the silver-tequila register lifts the garlic spinach, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Patron Silver|Seafood Tower": "Patron Silver with the seafood tower — iconic blanco against raw oysters, shrimp, lobster. The clean citrus-forward character provides the through-line at the everyday register. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Patron Silver|Seared Scallops": "Patron Silver with seared scallops — Patron's iconic silver against caramelized scallop. The clean citrus-forward profile meets the sear at the approachable everyday register; the globally-familiar blanco-seafood pour. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Patron Silver|Seasonal Soup": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift sits alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the silver-tequila body brightens the seasonal soup, and the polished agave note threads the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Patron Silver|Seasonal Vegetables": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift sits alongside the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the blanco-tequila body matches the seasonal vegetables, and the bright blanco register underlines the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Patron Silver|Shrimp Bisque": "Patron Silver with shrimp bisque — Patron against cream-based seafood. The citrus cuts the dairy at the globally-familiar tier. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Patron Silver|Shrimp Cocktail": "Patron Silver with shrimp cocktail — iconic 80-proof Patron against cold shrimp. The citrus-forward clean agave threads through cocktail sauce at the everyday Patron register. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Patron Silver|Swordfish": "Patron Silver -- polished silver tequila, restaurant call, agave-forward. The blanco-tequila body matches the swordfish, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the plate. Strong; the refined craft character provides a premium through-line.",
  "Patron Silver|The Tomahawk": "Patron Silver with the Tomahawk — 80-proof blanco against bone-in ribeye. Avoid; bourbon or scotch territory.",
  "Patron Silver|Tomato Basil": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift leans against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the unaged blanco body cuts the tomato basil, and the green-agave edge brightens the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Patron Silver|Truffle Fries": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift reads alongside the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the blanco-tequila body matches the truffle fries, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Patron Silver|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Patron Silver's crisp agave-pepper character holds the line with the tuna's seared rare crust — the crisp body frames the fish cleanly, and the agave-pepper carries the char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Patron Silver|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the silver-spirit register lifts the curry, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the bowl. Works; ceremonial pairing depends on preparation.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Asparagus": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- sugar on a clean vegetable side is wrong direction — needs herb-acid lift, not sweetness. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a digestif. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Patron XO Cafe for the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Patron XO Cafe for the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Beignets": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet coffee-tequila-base depth holds steady against the beignet's warm sugar-dusted pastry — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Bone Marrow": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character flattens the bone marrow's unctuous rendered-marrow richness -- sugar dulls the savory edge of a rich meat opener instead of complementing it. The plate deserves Fernet Branca, Lagavulin 8, or George T. Stagg, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Patron XO Cafe belongs on the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Bone-In Filet": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- sweet liqueur is post-meal territory — wrong register for any steak course. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Patron XO Cafe lands on another course — not here.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Broccoli Cheddar": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- the liqueur's sweetness buries the soup's creamy base instead of supporting it. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Patron XO Cafe on the steak course instead.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Broccolini": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the broccolini's tender green stalks -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Patron XO Cafe belongs on the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Brussels and Belly": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character doubles down on Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts -- sweet liqueur and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no contrast left. The plate deserves Corazon Weller, Angel's Envy, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Patron XO Cafe lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Burrata": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the burrata's fresh basil-tomato-cream delicacy -- sweet liqueur is dessert energy — wrong place for the table's first course. The plate deserves Il Colle Prosecco Superiore, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, not a digestif. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Patron XO Cafe belongs on the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Butternut Squash": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- the liqueur's sweetness buries the soup's creamy base instead of supporting it. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Patron XO Cafe for the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Carrot Cake": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Patron XO Cafe. Works; the drier-tequila-coffee profile plays cake spice at spirit-forward register.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Cheesecake": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet coffee-tequila-base depth sits with the cheesecake's custard cream — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar, and the coffee threads the cream. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Chilean Seabass": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- a sweet liqueur is dessert-course energy — wrong register for any main protein. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Patron XO Cafe for the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Chocolate Brownie": "Chocolate Brownie: warm dark chocolate meets Patron XO Cafe. Excellent; one of the strong calls on the list.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Chocolate Cake": "Chocolate Cake: layered chocolate dessert meets Patron XO Cafe. Excellent; the Jalisco-tequila-Arabica profile frames chocolate layers at spirit-forward register — the dark-bitter coffee-liqueur move.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Clam Chowder": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the liqueur's sweetness buries the soup's creamy base instead of supporting it. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Patron XO Cafe on the steak course instead.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Cowboy Ribeye": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness -- sweet liqueur is post-meal territory — wrong register for any steak course. The plate deserves Macallan 18, Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon, or Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Patron XO Cafe lands on another course — not here.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Crab Cake": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- sweet liqueur on cold shellfish is wrong-course energy — too forward for a clean opener. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Patron XO Cafe for the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Creamed Spinach": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the creamed spinach's rich bechamel-laced greens -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Weller 12 Year, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Patron XO Cafe on the steak course instead.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Creamy Potato": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- sugar piled onto cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Patron XO Cafe lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Creme Brulee": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet coffee-tequila-base depth holds steady against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar, and the coffee threads the cream. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Escargot": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight -- sweet liqueur is dessert energy — wrong place for the table's first course. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Mata Hari Absinthe, or Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Patron XO Cafe belongs on the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Faroe Island Salmon": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- a sweet liqueur is dessert-course energy — wrong register for any main protein. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Patron XO Cafe on the steak course instead.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Filet Mignon": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the filet's lean buttery tenderness -- the liqueur's sugar buries the lean cut's buttery delicacy. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Maker's Mark Cellar Aged, or Yamazaki 18 Year, not a digestif. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Patron XO Cafe for another course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|French Onion": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth -- sweet liqueur on savory broth jars — sugar pulls one way, the salt-and-spice broth pulls the other. The plate deserves Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a digestif. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Patron XO Cafe for the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Grilled Caesar": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character jars against the Caesar's charred-romaine and anchovy edge -- sugar on cold lettuce reads like dressing gone wrong — needs acid, not sweetness. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Tanqueray Gin, or Scavino Barolo, not a digestif. Avoid; the better calls are above. Patron XO Cafe lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Gumbo": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- sweet liqueur on savory broth jars — sugar pulls one way, the salt-and-spice broth pulls the other. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not a digestif. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Patron XO Cafe for the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Patron XO Cafe belongs on the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|House Wedge": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character jars against the wedge's iceberg-and-bleu cool crunch -- sugar on cold lettuce reads like dressing gone wrong — needs acid, not sweetness. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Weller 12 Year, or Le Garenne Rosé, not a digestif. Avoid; the better calls are above. Pour the Patron XO Cafe on the steak course instead.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Kansas City": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the KC's lean-bold strip with savory grain -- sweet liqueur is post-meal territory — wrong register for any steak course. The plate deserves Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, Pio Cesare Barbaresco, or Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Patron XO Cafe on another course instead.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Loaded Potato": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a digestif. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Patron XO Cafe for the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Lobster Mac": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence -- sweet liqueur and dairy-rich side double the indulgence with no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Patron XO Cafe belongs on the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Market Fish": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- a sweet liqueur is dessert-course energy — wrong register for any main protein. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Patron XO Cafe lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Mocha Creme": "Patron XO Cafe: 100% Patron Silver tequila + Arabica coffee extract at 35% ABV — drier, more spirit-forward than Kahlua. Excellent on mocha creme; the tequila-base-Arabica profile brings spirit-forward-coffee register to coffee-chocolate — less sweet, more assertive than the Kahlua approach. Gold standard; the headline call at the table.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Mushroom Bisque": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a digestif. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Patron XO Cafe for the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Mushrooms": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character fights the mushrooms' earthy umami weight -- the liqueur's sweet register pulls against the mushroom's umami without bridge. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Los Vecinos Mezcal, or Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, not a digestif. Avoid; the better calls are above. Patron XO Cafe belongs on the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Peanut Butter Brownie: peanut-chocolate stack meets Patron XO Cafe. Excellent; the tequila-Arabica character wraps peanut-chocolate at spirit-forward register — less sweet than Kahlua, more tequila-coffee presence.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Porterhouse": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character -- sweet liqueur on the headline cut is dessert-course energy — save it for after the meal. The plate deserves Odette Cabernet Sauvignon, Weller 12 Year, or Domaine du Grand Tinel, not a digestif. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Patron XO Cafe on another course instead.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Prime Tartare": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami -- sweet liqueur is dessert energy — wrong place for the table's first course. The plate deserves Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Belvedere Vodka, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Patron XO Cafe on the steak course instead.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Rainbow Trout": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character smothers the trout's delicate flesh -- the liqueur's sweet register buries the gentle flesh's lift. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Patron XO Cafe belongs on the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Roast Half Chicken": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast -- a sweet liqueur is dessert-course energy — wrong register for any main protein. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Patron XO Cafe lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth -- sweet liqueur on savory broth jars — sugar pulls one way, the salt-and-spice broth pulls the other. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a digestif. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Patron XO Cafe for the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- sugar on delicate fish is wrong direction — the plate needs acid, not sweetness. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; one of those is the move. Patron XO Cafe lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- sugar on a clean vegetable side is wrong direction — needs herb-acid lift, not sweetness. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Patron XO Cafe on the steak course instead.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Seafood Tower": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet liqueur on cold shellfish is wrong-course energy — too forward for a clean opener. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Patron XO Cafe for the steak course.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Seared Scallops": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Patron XO Cafe. Avoid; coffee-liqueur wrong for scallops. Reach for a light rum, vodka, or gin.",
  "Patron XO Cafe|Seasonal Soup": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Patron XO Cafe lands on the steak course — not here.",
