  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Château Beaucastel": "Château Beaucastel's old-world Châteauneuf-du-Pape gravitas jars against the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Château Beaucastel belongs on the steak course.",
