  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Detroit City Vodka": "Detroit City Vodka's hometown craft vodka falls short of the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- vodka brings no flavor to bridge the chocolate's weight — neutral but wrong for the close. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not a vodka. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Detroit City Vodka lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Dewar's 15": "Dewar's 15's Highland-scotch character leans against the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the scotch depth settles into the PB brownie, and the heather brightens the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Dewar's White Label": "Dewar's White Label's Highland-scotch character finds neutral with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the malt-driven body wraps the PB brownie, and the honey rounds the dessert. Works; boutique-sourced wasted on salad.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Disaronno": "★ Disaronno's sweet almond-marzipan character rises to meet the PB brownie's peanut-cocoa stack — the sweet character mirrors the dessert sugar, and the nut character carries the chocolate. Gold standard; pour without second-guessing.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye": "Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the PB brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the Dylan-brand story is wasted on the salad.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum": "Peanut Butter Brownie: peanut-chocolate meets Doctor Bird. Excellent; the high-ester Jamaican funk wraps peanut-chocolate in tropical-fruit intensity — bold pairing, rewards the guest who wants character.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Domaine Serene Grand Cheval": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift fights the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- the dry red and the chocolate's sugar refuse each other — tannin reads bitter on the finish. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval for the steak course.",
