  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Domaine du Grand Tinel": "Domaine du Grand Tinel's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register clashes with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- savory tannin sits awkwardly on cocoa weight without resolving. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Domaine du Grand Tinel on the steak course instead.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Don Fulano Anejo": "Don Fulano Anejo's añejo-pour depth reads alongside the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the aged-agave weight wraps the PB brownie, and the caramel-agave register brightens the dessert. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Don Fulano Blanco": "Don Fulano Blanco's unaged blanco-tequila lift with agave-citrus snap falls short of the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- light spirit can't carry chocolate's weight — needs a richer pour like an aged rum or tawny. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not a light spirit. Avoid; the better calls are above. Don Fulano Blanco lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Don Fulano Reposado": "Don Fulano Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the rested-agave depth sits with the PB brownie, and the oak threads the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Don Julio 1942": "Don Julio 1942 with the PB brownie — 1942 benchmark against peanut butter and cocoa. Works; iconic extra añejo is composed with the dessert.",
