  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Sambuca": "Sambuca's after-dinner liqueur weight leans against the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the sweet-liqueur register carries the PB brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Strong; the pairing carries its register cleanly against the cut.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|San Simeon Stormwatch": "San Simeon Stormwatch's red-fruit-and-spice elegance fights the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- the dry red and the chocolate's sugar refuse each other — tannin reads bitter on the finish. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. San Simeon Stormwatch belongs on the steak course.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir": "Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift flattens the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Sauteed Garlic Spinach and the PB brownie -- acid and sugar share the table, neither course pulls heavy. Works; the meal closes cleanly from the side.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Sauternes Glass": "Sauternes — Sémillon-Sauvignon Blanc with noble rot (botrytis cinerea), apricot, honey, orange marmalade, luscious unctuous, bright acid. The apricot lifts peanut-butter-frosting density and the bright acid cuts fudge-brownie richness. Strong Sauternes for peanut butter brownie — Vintage Port's chocolate-depth fits brownies harder.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Sazerac": "Sazerac rye, Peychaud's, sugar, absinthe-rinsed glass. The anise-rye profile clashes with peanut butter on every axis; spirit-forward classic has no job with dessert. Never pair — save Sazerac for tartare, marrow, or pre-dinner service.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Sazerac Rye": "Sazerac Rye's rye-spice character leans against the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the rye spice cuts the PB brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Scapegrace Fortuna": "Scapegrace Fortuna's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the caramel-spice register matches the PB brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Scavino Barolo": "Piedmont Nebbiolo — tar, dried rose, firm tannin. Barolo's structure fights dessert completely; tannin against peanut butter frosting is incoherent. Never pair — Barolo belongs with the Tomahawk or Porterhouse steaks.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Schloss Vollrads Riesling": "Schloss Vollrads Riesling's crisp apricot-floral acidity holds with the PB brownie's peanut-cocoa stack — the dry white underclubs the dessert sugar, and the mineral edge lifts the dish. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters": "Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters' red-fruit-and-spice elegance jars against the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters on the steak course instead.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Seafood Tower": "Seafood Tower and the PB brownie -- the bright register lifts the sweet, the meal closes clean. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Seared Scallops": "The scallops and the PB brownie -- the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness bookends with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Seasonal Soup": "Seasonal Soup and the PB brownie -- the courses share the meal without conflict. Works; sequence them as opener and close or share the table, no clash.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Seasonal Vegetables": "The seasonal vegetables and the PB brownie -- the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate hands off cleanly to the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: a quiet call, the meal carries without strain. Works; sequence them or share the table, no clash.",
