  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Siete Leguas Blanco": "Siete Leguas Blanco's unaged blanco-tequila lift with agave-citrus snap falls short of the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- light spirit can't carry chocolate's weight — needs a richer pour like an aged rum or tawny. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not a light spirit. Avoid; the better calls are above. Pour the Siete Leguas Blanco on the steak course instead.",
