  "Peanut Butter Brownie|St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc": "St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc's crisp white-wine character falls short of the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- dry white can't carry chocolate's weight — needs a tawny or sweet wine for the close. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not a white wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc for the steak course.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|St Supéry Élu Meritage": "St Supéry Élu Meritage's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit flattens the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the St Supéry Élu Meritage on the steak course instead.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Stagg Jr. Batch #15": "Stagg Jr. Batch #15 with the PB brownie — BT cask-strength against peanut butter and cocoa. Strong; Stagg Jr.'s intensity handles dessert density at barrel-proof register.",
