  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc": "Marlborough Sauvignon Blanc — grassy, green, light. Wrong category entirely — green-herbal white against peanut butter and fudge is incoherent. Never pair. Stoneleigh belongs with the wedge salad or shrimp cocktail.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Swordfish": "After the swordfish, the PB brownie -- the meaty grilled fish gives way to peanut-and-chocolate fudge, vanilla ice cream over the top. Works; the dense dessert outweighs the cleaner main, but the close holds without strain.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Tanq 10 Gin": "Tanq 10 Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- gin botanicals jar against the chocolate's sweetness with no bridge. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Tanq 10 Gin on the steak course instead.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Tanqueray Gin": "Tanqueray Gin's botanical-driven lift fights the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- juniper and cocoa refuse each other — botanical bitterness reads metallic against chocolate. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Tanqueray Gin for the steak course.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Taylor Fladgate Tawny": "Classic Douro Tawny — Taylor Fladgate (founded 1692), smooth balanced, dried fruit, almond, warm clean finish. The almond echoes peanut-butter-frosting nuttiness and the dried fruit bridges fudge-brownie brown-sugar depth. Strong heritage-Tawny for peanut butter brownie — Graham's 10 Year's toffee fits richer.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle": "Flagship Vintage Port — Taylor Fladgate bottle, extraordinarily rich, dark fruit, chocolate, tobacco, minutes-long evolving finish. The chocolate bridges peanut-butter-frosting richness and the tobacco plays with dense fudge-brownie base. Peak flagship-Vintage for peanut butter brownie — celebrated bottle on the dense bake. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Tears of Llorona": "Tears of Llorona with the PB brownie — triple-cask aged against peanut butter and cocoa. Works; multi-cask complexity composed with dessert at distinctive register.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Teeter Totter Cabernet Sauvignon": "Teeter Totter Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth fights the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- the dry red and the chocolate's sugar refuse each other — tannin reads bitter on the finish. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Teeter Totter Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Tenuta di Arceno Chianti Classico": "Tenuta di Arceno Chianti Classico's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity jars against the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Tenuta di Arceno Chianti Classico for the steak course.",
