  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Veuve Clicquot Brut": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's classic yellow-label Champagne body clashes with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- brut bubbles and chocolate weight refuse each other — needs sweetness, not crisp acid. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not a sparkling. Avoid; the better calls are above. Veuve Clicquot Brut belongs on the steak course.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Vieux Carré": "Vieux Carré's bold herbal-spice build stays alongside the PB brownie's peanut-cocoa stack — the whiskey-build sweetness threads the dessert, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Villon Cognac": "Villon with the PB brownie — modern cognac spirit against peanut butter and cocoa. Excellent; Villon's approachable sweetness meets the dessert density at contemporary register.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Vin Santo": "Tuscan Vin Santo — Trebbiano-Malvasia straw-dried, sealed-barrel years, amber, honey, dried apricot, walnut, nutty oxidative. The walnut echoes peanut-butter-frosting nuttiness and the dried apricot lifts fudge-brownie brown-sugar depth. Peak Vin Santo for peanut butter brownie — nut-on-nut-plus-honey complexity. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Peanut Butter Brownie|Weller 107": "Weller 107's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the bourbon depth settles into the PB brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; flagship depth gives the dessert premium aged character.",
