  "Rainbow Trout|Alexander Valley Cyrus": "Alexander Valley Cyrus' red-fruit-and-spice elegance clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Alexander Valley Cyrus for the steak course.",
  "Rainbow Trout|Alexander Valley Homestead Red": "Alexander Valley Homestead Red's red-fruit-and-spice elegance clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Alexander Valley Homestead Red for the steak course.",
  "Rainbow Trout|Amaro Nonino": "Amaro Nonino's crisp orange-peel-grappa sweetness clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- aperitivo bitterness fights gentle flesh without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Amaro Nonino lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Rainbow Trout|Ancho Reyes": "Ancho Reyes' sweet liqueur character clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- a sweet liqueur is dessert-course energy — wrong register for any main protein. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a digestif. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Ancho Reyes for the steak course.",
  "Rainbow Trout|Angel's Envy": "Angel's Envy's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the trout's delicate flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Angel's Envy lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Rainbow Trout|Angel's Envy Cask Strength": "Angel's Envy Cask Strength's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Angel's Envy Cask Strength lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Rainbow Trout|Angel's Envy Triple Cask": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Angel's Envy Triple Cask for the steak course.",
  "Rainbow Trout|Aperol": "Aperol's crisp bitter-orange-aperitivo edge overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bitter herbs flatten delicate fish — the protein can't lift the amaro's register. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Aperol for the steak course.",
  "Rainbow Trout|Asparagus": "The trout and the asparagus on the plate -- the trout body matches the bright green side, and the mineral edge lifts the fish. Strong; the side holds the trout's weight without competing.",
  "Rainbow Trout|Au Gratin Potatoes": "The trout alongside the au gratin -- the delicate plate yields to rich, the meal builds. Works; the side sits without pulling focus.",
  "Rainbow Trout|Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon": "Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Pour the Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
