  "Rainbow Trout|Aviation": "Aviation's gin-or-tequila cocktail lift meets at register with the trout's delicate flesh: the bright build frames the trout, and the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly. Strong; the match stays in its register against the cut.",
  "Rainbow Trout|Aviation Gin": "Aviation Gin's floral-juniper botanicals holds steady against the trout's delicate flesh — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Rainbow Trout|Avion 44": "Avion 44's rested-agave body reads alongside the trout's delicate flesh: the añejo register carries the trout, and the cooked-agave note underlines the plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Rainbow Trout|Avion Silver": "Avion Silver's crisp agave character holds steady against the trout's delicate flesh — the crisp body frames the fish cleanly. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Rainbow Trout|Bacardi Rum": "Bacardi Rum -- Carta Blanca, workhorse light rum, clean. The crisp body lifts the trout, and the clean profile carries the plate. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Rainbow Trout|Baileys Irish Cream": "Baileys Irish Cream's sweet liqueur character smothers the trout's delicate flesh -- the liqueur's sweet register buries the gentle flesh's lift. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a digestif. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Baileys Irish Cream belongs on the steak course.",
