  "Rainbow Trout|Basil Hayden's": "Basil Hayden's light high-rye and cocoa swallows the trout's delicate flesh -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Basil Hayden's for the steak course.",
  "Rainbow Trout|Basil Hayden's 10 Year": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's aged oak and rye spice overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Basil Hayden's 10 Year for the steak course.",
  "Rainbow Trout|Basil Hayden's Malted Rye": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Basil Hayden's Malted Rye for the steak course.",
