  "Rainbow Trout|Canadian Club 43 Year": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character flattens the trout's delicate flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Canadian Club 43 Year lands on the steak course — not here.",
