  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Creme Brulee": "Rémy VSOP with creme brulee — Fine Champagne elegance against vanilla custard and caramelized sugar. Excellent; Rémy's refined profile is the featured cognac-brulee match — floral notes find the caramel with grace Courvoisier can't replicate.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Escargot": "Remy VSOP Cognac's cognac-fruit character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the barrel-aged depth cuts the umami fat, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Faroe Island Salmon": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- cognac and oily fish double up the richness with no foil. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a cognac. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Remy VSOP Cognac for the steak course.",
