  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac clashes with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- cognac on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a cognac. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Remy VSOP Cognac for the steak course.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|House Wedge": "Rémy VSOP with the House Wedge — premium cognac against iceberg and bleu. Works; Rémy's refinement is over-specified for the wedge.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Kansas City": "Rémy VSOP with the KC — Fine Champagne cognac against an 18oz strip. Strong; Rémy's elegance handles the strip at refined register, though Courvoisier's drier oak is the featured cognac-KC match.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Loaded Potato": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac leans against the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the cognac register matches the loaded potato soup, and the oak-and-vanilla edge brightens the bowl. Works; Rémy's elegance handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Lobster Mac": "Rémy VSOP with lobster mac — Grande Champagne cognac against pasta-and-lobster. Strong; Rémy's elegance frames the richness with refined polish.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Market Fish": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac clashes with the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- cognac is post-meal energy — wrong register for a main protein. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a cognac. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Remy VSOP Cognac for the steak course.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Mocha Creme": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac sits alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the cognac register matches the mocha creme, and the caramel rounds the dessert. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Mushroom Bisque": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the Limousin-oak weight handles the mushroom bisque, and the caramel threads the umami register. Works; composed but not a standout.",
