  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Peanut Butter Brownie: peanut butter and cocoa meet elegant cognac. Strong; Rémy's refinement handles the dessert density at premium register.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Porterhouse": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac finds neutral with the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character: the brandy depth wraps the dual-cut steak, and the caramel rounds the cut. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Prime Tartare": "Remy VSOP Cognac's cognac-fruit character holds the line with the tartare's raw beef and brine — the barrel-aged depth cuts the umami fat, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Strong; the match carries without overshooting.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Rainbow Trout": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- cognac's aged-grape weight buries delicate fish — digestif belongs after the meal. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a cognac. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Remy VSOP Cognac for the steak course.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Roast Half Chicken": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac reads alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the eau-de-vie body carries the roast chicken, and the caramel rounds the plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac sits alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the aged-grape brandy body sits with the chickpea soup, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- cognac's aged-grape weight buries delicate fish — digestif belongs after the meal. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a cognac. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Remy VSOP Cognac lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac clashes with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- cognac on a green vegetable side is wrong direction — needs crisp white instead. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not a cognac. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Remy VSOP Cognac belongs on the steak course.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Seafood Tower": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac clashes with the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- cognac is wrong-course energy for the table's opener. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a cognac. Avoid; one of those is the move. Remy VSOP Cognac belongs on the steak course.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Seared Scallops": "Rémy VSOP with seared scallops — premium cognac against scallop delicacy. Avoid; cognac overwhelms scallops.",
