  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Seasonal Vegetables": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac clashes with the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate -- cognac on a green vegetable side is wrong direction — needs crisp white instead. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, not a cognac. Avoid; the better calls are above. Remy VSOP Cognac belongs on the steak course.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Shrimp Bisque": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the cognac register matches the shrimp bisque, and the orchard-fruit thread frames the bowl. Works; Rémy's elegance handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Shrimp Cocktail": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- cognac weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs sparkling or a crisp white. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a cognac. Avoid; the better calls are above. Remy VSOP Cognac lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Swordfish": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- cognac is post-meal energy — wrong register for a main protein. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a cognac. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Remy VSOP Cognac belongs on the steak course.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|The Tomahawk": "Remy VSOP Cognac's cognac-fruit character frames the Tomahawk's char-and-fat — the barrel-aged depth meets the cap-fat, and the cassis plays against the grilled char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Tomato Basil": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the brandy depth wraps the tomato basil, and the dried-fruit note underlines the bowl. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Truffle Fries": "Rémy VSOP with truffle fries — Grande Champagne cognac against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Rémy's elegance meets the earthy-rich with refined polish — the most luxurious working-cognac truffle pairing in the batch.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac fights the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- cognac's aged register pulls against the savory sear without resolving. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a cognac. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Remy VSOP Cognac on the steak course instead.",
  "Remy VSOP Cognac|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac leans against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the cognac register matches the curry, and the orchard-fruit thread frames the bowl. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Rey Sol Anejo|Asparagus": "Rey Sol Anejo's aged-agave character finds neutral with the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the rested-agave depth sits with the asparagus, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; bold agave is a distinctive counterpoint but slightly overpowering.",
