  "Roast Half Chicken|Aviation Gin": "Aviation with the chicken — Portland American dry gin against roasted poultry. Strong; Aviation's soft juniper supports chicken cleanly at crowd-pleasing register.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Avion 44": "Avion 44's cooked-agave-and-oak register leans against the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the rested-agave depth sits with the roast chicken, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Avion Silver": "Avion Silver with the roast half chicken — filtered highland against roasted chicken. Works; clean composes cleanly.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Bacardi Rum": "Bacardi Rum's crisp workhorse-clean character leans against the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the crisp body lifts the roast chicken, and the clean profile carries the plate. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Baileys Irish Cream": "Baileys Irish Cream's sweet liqueur character clashes with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast -- a sweet liqueur is dessert-course energy — wrong register for any main protein. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; one of those is the move. Baileys Irish Cream belongs on the steak course.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Baker's": "Baker's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the oak depth lays under the roast chicken, and the oak frames the plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Balvenie 12 American Oak": "Balvenie 12 American Oak's bourbon-cask Speyside softness finds neutral with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the roast chicken, and the smoke threads the plate. Works; JW Blue is over-specified for the side — save the rare-cask bottle for the protein course.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask": "Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask's rum-finished Speyside character sits alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the scotch backbone matches the roast chicken, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the plate. Works; the pour's delicacy doesn't overpower the soup, but doesn't particularly elevate it either.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Balvenie 16 Single Barrel": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's Highland-scotch character leans against the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the malt-and-oak threads the roast chicken, and the malt edge frames the plate. Works; the pour's brightness is a gentle counterpoint to the dessert's richness.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Balvenie 21 Portwood": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside reads alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the scotch depth settles into the roast chicken, and the heather brightens the plate. Works; the spicy-sweet character gives the dessert a Barton frame.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Bardstown Château Laboude": "Bardstown Château Laboude's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the brown-spirit warmth threads the roast chicken, and the oak-and-spice register settles the plate. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Bardstown Discovery #6": "Bardstown Discovery #6's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the bourbon depth settles into the roast chicken, and the oak frames the plate. Works; Remus 15 frames the two-cut plate at Gatsby-tribute register.",
