  "Roast Half Chicken|Bowdie's Old Fashioned": "Bowdie's Old Fashioned: this bold whiskey-forward cocktail's oak, spice, and spirit depth meets this roasted chicken's savory, rich poultry-skin flavor. Bold whiskey against roasted chicken — the drink outweighs but oak and savory can mesh. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark": "Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the bourbon depth settles into the roast chicken, and the vanilla softens the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Bowman Brothers Small Batch": "Bowman Brothers Small Batch's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the bourbon backbone carries the roast chicken, and the rounded sweetness brightens the plate. Works; the 10-year holds without lifting.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Bowmore 12": "Bowmore 12's lighter-Islay peat character leans against the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the roast chicken, and the smoke threads the plate. Works; Discovery complexity wasted on salad simplicity.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Braida Montebruna Barbera": "Piedmont Monferrato Barbera d'Asti — Braida benchmark, juicy dark cherry, blackberry, high acid, low tannin, medium body. The high acid and light tannin play against roasted chicken's skin-and-jus build; preparation changes seasonally — check with kitchen for today's build. Peak Italian-food-wine for chicken across most seasonal preparations. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon's bold earth cassis holds with the chicken's herbed crisp skin — the concentrated body carries the herb-crisped bird, and the cassis plays against the grilled char. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Broccoli Cheddar": "Roast Half Chicken after the broccoli cheddar -- the cheddar-and-broccoli cream opens with rich-savory weight, the chicken following with herbed crisp-skin roast the cream primed without crowding. Strong; cream into roast reads classic.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Broccolini": "Roast Half Chicken with the broccolini -- the herb-butter chicken matches the garlic-and-broccolini side. Strong; reliable side for the chicken.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Bruichladdich": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets this roasted chicken's savory, rich poultry-skin flavor. Bold whiskey against roasted chicken — the drink outweighs but oak and savory can mesh. Strong — aligned depth.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Brussels and Belly": "Roast Half Chicken with Brussels + Belly -- the roast bird matches the glazed pork starter. Strong; reliable side for the chicken.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Buffalo Trace": "Buffalo Trace's rounded vanilla-and-toffee character leans against the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the vanilla settles into the roast chicken, and the oak threads the plate. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Buffalo Trace Cream": "Buffalo Trace Cream's sweet liqueur character buries the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast -- sugar smothers the chicken's savory frame — wait for dessert. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Buffalo Trace Cream for the steak course.",
