  "Roast Half Chicken|Campari": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast -- bitter aperitivo is for before or after the meal — not on a main protein. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Campari on the steak course instead.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Canadian Club": "Canadian Club with the chicken — traditional Canadian blend, 1858-founded Hiram Walker, grain-forward easy-drinking heritage brand. Excellent; Canadian Club's grain-forward heritage character frames chicken with traditional Canadian distinction — where Crown Royal is smooth-iconic, CC is grain-forward-heritage.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Canadian Club 43 Year": "CC 43 Year with the chicken — ultra-premium aged Canadian against roasted poultry. Excellent; CC 43 Year's aged depth frames chicken at collector register — Crown Royal handles this pairing at crowd-pleasing register, the CC 43 elevates it.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Captain Morgan Rum": "Captain Morgan Rum's green-agave-and-cane lift leans against the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the unaged body brightens the roast chicken, and the cane-and-citrus thread frames the plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Caribou Crossing": "Caribou Crossing with the chicken — Sazerac-owned single-barrel Canadian against roasted poultry. Excellent; Caribou Crossing's distinctive craft character frames chicken at single-barrel register.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Carrot Cake": "The chicken into the carrot cake -- the herb-butter bird hands off to spiced cake and cream-cheese frosting, walnut crunch on the close. Strong; the savory-herb main and the spiced cake share register cleanly across the meal.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Casa LBV Port": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast -- dessert wine on a main protein is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; one of those is the move. Casa LBV Port lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Casamigos Mezcal": "Casamigos Mezcal's espadín-and-smoke register leans against the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the smoky agave register handles the roast chicken, and the campfire register frames the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
