  "Roast Half Chicken|Creme Brulee": "After the chicken, the brulee -- the jus-finished bird yields to vanilla-bean custard and torched-sugar crust, berries lifting the close. Strong; the steakhouse-classic close on the lighter main.",
  "Roast Half Chicken|Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée": "Eola-Amity Willamette Pinot — cherry, raspberry, forest floor, mineral backbone. The high acid plays against roasted chicken's skin-and-jus structure; preparation changes seasonally — check with kitchen for today's build. Peak benchmark Oregon Pinot for chicken across most seasonal builds. Gold standard; pour without second-guessing.",
