  "Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea|Espresso Martini": "Espresso Martini's roasted-coffee martini richness clashes with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth -- soup-salad course needs lift — bitters-and-whiskey brings weight instead. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a spirit-forward cocktail. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Espresso Martini for the steak course.",
