  "Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea|Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle": "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth -- honeyed sugar on savory broth jars — wrong direction for the course. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle for the steak course.",
