  "Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea|Teeter Totter Cabernet Sauvignon": "Teeter Totter Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overwhelms the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Teeter Totter Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea|Tenuta di Arceno Chianti Classico": "Tuscany Chianti Classico DOCG Sangiovese — vibrant cherry, dried herbs, tomato leaf, savory earth, medium body, medium tannin, high acid. The tomato-leaf meets the soup's tomato-pepper base directly and the high acid lifts the chickpea earth. Works tier on this wine's card — solid fit for Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea but below the wine's peaks with the Tomahawk, Porterhouse, and Bone-In Filet.",
