  "Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea|Yellow Chartreuse": "Yellow Chartreuse's bitter-herb aperitivo edge jars against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth -- bitter botanicals on savory broth pull against the salt-and-spice frame without resolving. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Yellow Chartreuse for the steak course.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Asparagus": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs's crisp apple-char acidity stays alongside the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the lively bubbles sit with the light side, and the mineral edge frames the green plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
