  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Beignets": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs — Le Mesnil Grand Cru Chardonnay. Chalk, lemon curd, green apple, no dosage. The austere acidity cuts beignets' fried-dough weight and the precision plays against powdered sugar. Works as sommelier Champagne for dessert — though this bottle shines more with savory courses.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Bone Marrow": "Le Mesnil Grand Cru blanc de blancs against marrow's rendered-fat richness — austere precision is overwhelmed by bone depth. Never pair. Route marrow to big Cab, Manhattan, or Bowdie's Old Fashioned; keep Moncuit for tartare, seafood tower, scallops, or filet course.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Bone-In Filet": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs' bright sparkling effervescence underclubs the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- sparkling sits short of the prime cut's weight. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a sparkling. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs on another course instead.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Broccoli Cheddar": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs's crisp apple-char acidity sits beside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the mousse refreshes against the broth, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Broccolini": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs's crisp apple-char acidity sits alongside the broccolini's tender green — the lively bubbles sit with the light side, and the mineral edge frames the green plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Brussels and Belly": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs's crisp apple-char acidity sits alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; safe call, no friction. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Burrata": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs — Le Mesnil Grand Cru blanc de blancs with chalky minerality, lemon curd, green apple, no dosage. The austere acidity cuts burrata's cream and the chalk plays against basil-tomato-pistachio cleanly. Peak sommelier Champagne for burrata — technical elegance. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Butternut Squash": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs's crisp apple-char acidity sits beside the squash soup's silky sweet — the mousse refreshes against the broth, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Carrot Cake": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs' bright sparkling effervescence clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- a dry sparkling belongs with the opener, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a sparkling. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs belongs on the steak course.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Cheesecake": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs' bright sparkling effervescence jars against the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- sparkling acid cuts through custard wrong — leaves the dessert reading sharp. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not a sparkling. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs belongs on the steak course.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Chilean Seabass": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs's crisp apple-char acidity sits with the seabass's buttery flesh — the bright acidity frames the fish without weight, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Chocolate Brownie": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs' bright sparkling effervescence clashes with the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- a dry sparkling belongs with the opener, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not a sparkling. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs on the steak course instead.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Chocolate Cake": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs' bright sparkling effervescence clashes with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- a dry sparkling belongs with the opener, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not a sparkling. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs on the steak course instead.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Clam Chowder": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs's crisp apple-char acidity holds with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the mousse refreshes against the broth, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Cowboy Ribeye": "Robert Moncuit austere Champagne against the Cowboy's marbled bone-in ribeye — blanc de blancs precision crumples under rendered fat. Never pair. Route Cowboy to Silver Oak, Caymus, or bold bourbon; keep Moncuit for starters, seafood tower, or filet course where it shines.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Crab Cake": "Le Mesnil Grand Cru Chardonnay Champagne — chalky minerality, lemon curd, green apple, almost no dosage. The pure austere structure cuts romesco and the lemon curd plays against crab's sweet meat directly. Peak sommelier's Champagne for crab cake — precision-on-precision pairing. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
