  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Mocha Creme": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs' bright sparkling effervescence clashes with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- brut bubbles and chocolate weight refuse each other — needs sweetness, not crisp acid. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not a sparkling. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs for the steak course.",
