  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Porterhouse": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs' bright sparkling effervescence underclubs the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character -- sparkling reads light against the marbled char — the cut deserves a structured red. The plate deserves Odette Cabernet Sauvignon, Weller 12 Year, or Domaine du Grand Tinel, not a sparkling. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs on another course instead.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Prime Tartare": "Prime Tartare: this rich, umami-forward starter's bold fat and concentrated savory depth meets this versatile sparkling's bright acidity, toasty lees character, and cleansing bubbles. Sparkling's bubbles and acid scrub the starter's fat while the bright frame lifts the plate. Strong — palate-cleansing start.",
