  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs's crisp apple-char acidity holds steady against the halibut's salt-cured flesh — the bright acidity frames the fish without weight, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs's crisp apple-char acidity sits beside the garlic-spinach's buttered greens — the lively bubbles sit with the light side, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Seafood Tower": "Le Mesnil Grand Cru Chardonnay — sommelier's Champagne with chalky minerality, lemon curd, green apple, and almost no dosage. The pure austere precision elevates the tower's mixed shellfish and the chalk-saline character echoes oyster brine. Peak technical Champagne for the seafood tower. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Seared Scallops": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs — Le Mesnil Grand Cru blanc de blancs with chalky minerality, lemon curd, green apple, and no dosage. The austere precision frames scallops' clean-seared sweetness and the chalk adds dimension against the pan-sear. Peak sommelier Champagne for scallops. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Seasonal Soup": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs's crisp apple-char acidity finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house build — the mousse refreshes against the broth. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Seasonal Vegetables": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs's crisp apple-char acidity sits beside the seasonal garden plate — the lively bubbles sit with the light side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Shrimp Bisque": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs' bright sparkling effervescence reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the fine bubbles lift the shrimp bisque, and the citrus frames the bowl. Works; too light for dessert density at this level.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Shrimp Cocktail": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs — Le Mesnil Grand Cru blanc de blancs. Chalky minerality, lemon curd, green apple, no dosage. The no-dosage austerity cuts chilled shrimp's sweet brine precisely and the lemon curd plays against cocktail-sauce. Peak sommelier Champagne for shrimp cocktail. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Swordfish": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs's crisp apple-char acidity holds steady against the swordfish's meaty flesh — the bright acidity frames the fish without weight, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|The Tomahawk": "Le Mesnil Grand Cru blanc de blancs against the biggest marbled steak on the menu — austere no-dosage precision has no weight to meet Tomahawk fat and char. Never pair. Route Tomahawk to Caymus, Opus, or Barolo; save Moncuit for tartare, seafood tower, or filet course.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Tomato Basil": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs' bright sparkling effervescence sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the fine bubbles lift the tomato basil, and the citrus frames the bowl. Works; a measured close to the meal.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Truffle Fries": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs's crisp apple-char acidity plays cleanly against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs's crisp apple-char acidity holds steady against the tuna's seared rare crust — the bright acidity frames the fish without weight, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs's crisp apple-char acidity stays alongside the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the mousse refreshes against the broth, and the citrus brightens the spice. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Roku Gin|Asparagus": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals leans against the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Roku Gin|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals plays cleanly against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Roku Gin|Beignets": "Roku Gin's botanical-driven lift fights the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- gin's herbal edge has no foil against warm pastry sugar — sharp meets sweet, neither wins. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not a gin. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Roku Gin lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Roku Gin|Bone Marrow": "Roku with bone marrow — Suntory sakura-yuzu-sansho gin against umami fat. Avoid; gin can't cut marrow. Reach for Fernet Branca.",
  "Roku Gin|Bone-In Filet": "Roku Gin's botanical-driven lift underclubs the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- gin reads light against the prime cut's weight — needs a red or whiskey. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a gin. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Roku Gin for another course.",
  "Roku Gin|Broccoli Cheddar": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals sits beside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Roku Gin|Broccolini": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals sits beside the broccolini's tender green — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Roku Gin|Brussels and Belly": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals stays alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Roku Gin|Burrata": "Roku with burrata — 6-Japanese-botanical gin (sakura flower + leaf) against fresh dairy. Excellent; one of the strong calls on the list.",
  "Roku Gin|Butternut Squash": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals sits beside the squash soup's silky sweet — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Roku Gin|Carrot Cake": "Roku Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- gin's botanical-citrus register fights dessert sweetness without a bridge. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Roku Gin for the steak course.",
  "Roku Gin|Cheesecake": "Roku Gin's botanical-driven lift jars against the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- sharp botanicals cut through dairy custard without resolving — the dessert reads broken. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not a gin. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Roku Gin for the steak course.",
  "Roku Gin|Chilean Seabass": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals finds register with the seabass's buttery flesh — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Strong; a steady recommendation at the table.",
  "Roku Gin|Chocolate Brownie": "Roku Gin's botanical-driven lift fights the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- juniper and cocoa refuse each other — botanical bitterness reads metallic against chocolate. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not a gin. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Roku Gin for the steak course.",
  "Roku Gin|Chocolate Cake": "Roku Gin's botanical-driven lift fights the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- juniper and cocoa refuse each other — botanical bitterness reads metallic against chocolate. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not a gin. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Roku Gin for the steak course.",
  "Roku Gin|Clam Chowder": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals lift the shellfish. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Roku Gin|Cowboy Ribeye": "Roku Gin's botanical-driven lift underclubs the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness -- gin's light register can't carry the marbled char — the cut deserves a bigger pour. The plate deserves Macallan 18, Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon, or Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon, not a gin. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Roku Gin for another course.",
  "Roku Gin|Crab Cake": "Roku with crab cake — Japanese Suntory gin with sakura + yuzu + sansho against delicate lump crab. Excellent; Roku's sansho-pepper lift and yuzu-citrus frame crab with Japanese-seafood-precision — parallel to Inverroche's fynbos-floral and Botanist's Islay-foraged approaches as terroir-distinctive craft gin for seafood.",
  "Roku Gin|Creamed Spinach": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals sits beside the spinach's dairy-rich cream — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Roku Gin|Creamy Potato": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals finds neutral with the potato soup's silky body — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Roku Gin|Creme Brulee": "Roku Gin's botanical-driven lift jars against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- sharp botanicals cut through dairy custard without resolving — the dessert reads broken. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not a gin. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Roku Gin for the steak course.",
  "Roku Gin|Escargot": "Roku with escargot — sansho-pepper Suntory Japanese gin against garlic-butter snails. Strong; Roku's sansho adds distinctive Japanese-pepper lift to the butter; Mahón's Mediterranean juniper still cuts butter hardest.",
  "Roku Gin|Faroe Island Salmon": "Roku with the salmon — Japanese gin with yuzu + sakura + sansho against oily salmon. Excellent; Roku's yuzu-and-sakura profile is classic sashimi territory — the thematic-perfect Japanese-gin-salmon pairing, where yuzu lifts fish like the Japanese classics teach.",
  "Roku Gin|Filet Mignon": "Roku with the filet — Suntory Japanese gin against tenderloin. Works; gin over-specified for steak.",
  "Roku Gin|French Onion": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals cut the cheese richness. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Roku Gin|Grilled Caesar": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals stays alongside the Caesar's char-and-anchovy — the botanical lift matches the leaf-and-acid plate, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Roku Gin|Gumbo": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals sits beside the gumbo's spiced Creole stew — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the pepper amplifies the spice. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Roku Gin|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals plays cleanly against the carrots' honeyed sweetness — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the herbs echo the green plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Roku Gin|House Wedge": "Roku with the House Wedge — Japanese sakura-yuzu-tea-sansho gin against iceberg and bleu. Strong; Roku's sansho-pepper engages the bleu with distinctive Japanese character.",
  "Roku Gin|Kansas City": "Roku Gin's botanical-driven lift mis-pairs with the KC's lean-bold strip with savory grain -- gin's clean lift reads thin against the cut's weight. The plate deserves Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, Pio Cesare Barbaresco, or Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye, not a gin. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Roku Gin on another course instead.",
  "Roku Gin|Loaded Potato": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals leans against the loaded potato's richness — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Roku Gin|Lobster Mac": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Roku Gin|Market Fish": "Roku with the market fish — Japanese Suntory gin against featured fish. Works; Roku's yuzu-sakura profile handles most fish preparations with Japanese-precision character.",
  "Roku Gin|Mocha Creme": "Roku Gin's botanical-driven lift fights the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- juniper and cocoa refuse each other — botanical bitterness reads metallic against chocolate. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not a gin. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Roku Gin on the steak course instead.",
  "Roku Gin|Mushroom Bisque": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals leans against the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Roku Gin|Mushrooms": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals leans against the mushrooms' earthy umami — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Roku Gin|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Roku Gin's botanical-driven lift clashes with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- gin botanicals jar against the chocolate's sweetness with no bridge. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not a gin. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Roku Gin for the steak course.",
  "Roku Gin|Porterhouse": "Roku Gin's botanical-driven lift falls short of the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character -- botanical-citrus can't stand up to 26+ ounces — a Cab or bourbon earns it. The plate deserves Odette Cabernet Sauvignon, Weller 12 Year, or Domaine du Grand Tinel, not a gin. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Roku Gin on another course instead.",
  "Roku Gin|Prime Tartare": "Roku with the tartare — Suntory Japanese gin against raw beef. Strong; Roku's sansho-pepper lifts tartare's minerality with distinctive Japanese-pepper character; Monkey 47's 47-botanical and Orbium's quinine-wormwood are still the featured craft-gin-tartare matches.",
  "Roku Gin|Rainbow Trout": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals finds register with the trout's delicate flesh — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Roku Gin|Roast Half Chicken": "Roku with the chicken — sakura-yuzu-tea-sansho Japanese gin against roasted poultry. Works; Roku's Japanese-botanical profile supports chicken at distinctive register.",
  "Roku Gin|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals sits alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper warmth — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the pepper amplifies the spice. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Roku Gin|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals holds steady against the halibut's salt-cured flesh — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Roku Gin|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals leans against the garlic-spinach's buttered greens — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Roku Gin|Seafood Tower": "Roku with the seafood tower — 6-Japanese-botanical Suntory gin against the raw bar. Strong; Roku's yuzu-sansho profile lifts the tower with Japanese-terroir distinction; Gray Whale's California ocean-botanicals and Botanist's Islay-foraged are the featured craft-tower matches, with Roku as the Japanese-story alternative.",
  "Roku Gin|Seared Scallops": "Roku with seared scallops — Suntory Japanese gin, 6 Japanese botanicals (sakura flower, sakura leaf, yuzu peel, sencha tea, gyokuro tea, sansho pepper). Excellent; Roku's yuzu-and-sansho profile is the featured Japanese-gin-scallop pairing — yuzu lifts scallop sweetness like the classic sashimi move, and sansho pepper adds distinctive finish no Western gin replicates.",
  "Roku Gin|Seasonal Soup": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals stays alongside the seasonal soup's house build — the gin botanicals sit with the plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Roku Gin|Seasonal Vegetables": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals stays alongside the seasonal garden plate — the botanical edge sits with the light side. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Roku Gin|Shrimp Bisque": "Roku with shrimp bisque — yuzu-sakura Japanese gin against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Roku's yuzu-citrus cuts the bisque with Japanese-precision lift.",
  "Roku Gin|Shrimp Cocktail": "Roku with shrimp cocktail — Suntory yuzu-sakura-sansho Japanese gin against cold shrimp. Excellent; Roku's yuzu profile is textbook Japanese citrus-and-seafood — elevates the classic cold app with sashimi-adjacent distinction.",
  "Roku Gin|Swordfish": "Roku Gin's botanical-driven lift leans against the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak: the floral edge frames the swordfish, and the juniper threads the plate. Strong; Neptunia's briny character engages the bleu with distinctive maritime profile.",
  "Roku Gin|The Tomahawk": "Roku with the Tomahawk — Japanese gin against 32oz cap-fat. Avoid; gin has no answer. Reach for a bourbon or cab.",
  "Roku Gin|Tomato Basil": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals plays cleanly against the tomato basil's bright acid — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Roku Gin|Truffle Fries": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals stays alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Roku Gin|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals sits with the tuna's seared rare crust — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the juniper sharpens the char. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Roku Gin|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals stays alongside the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the pepper amplifies the spice. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Asparagus": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum reads alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the layered spirit body sits with the asparagus, and the heavy-pour register grips the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum sits alongside the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the rich pour wraps the au gratin, and the heavy-pour register grips the side. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Beignets": "Ron Zacapa Rum -- Solera 23, Guatemalan, honey-vanilla-caramel. The Solera honey wraps the beignets, and the caramel rounds the dessert. Excellent; the herbal-bitter-complex digestif cuts through sugar-and-fried-dough at 55% register — textbook green-digestif move. Gold standard; the recommendation that earns the regular.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Bone Marrow": "Bone Marrow: umami fat meets Ron Zacapa. Excellent; the aged-solera character with its depth meets the marrow at luxury register — one of the few rums that earns its place against bourbon on this plate. Gold standard; pour without second-guessing.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Bone-In Filet": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey character sits with the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the light body is outweighed by the cut, and the honey rounds the grilled char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Broccoli Cheddar": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum leans against the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the dense-spirit weight carries the broccoli cheddar, and the layered body brightens the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Broccolini": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum finds neutral with the broccolini's tender green stalks: the heavy body handles the broccolini, and the dense weight underlines the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Brussels and Belly": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey character matches the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the crisp body sits with the plate, and the honey rounds the grilled char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Burrata": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum overwhelms the burrata's fresh basil-tomato-cream delicacy -- the spirit's weight is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Il Colle Prosecco Superiore, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Ron Zacapa Rum for the steak course.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Butternut Squash": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum reads alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the dense-spirit weight carries the squash bisque, and the layered body brightens the bowl. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Carrot Cake": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon spice meet Ron Zacapa. Excellent; the Solera-23 caramel and tropical-spice threads run directly into the carrot-cake warmth at luxury register.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Cheesecake": "Cheesecake: custard-dairy dessert meets Ron Zacapa. Excellent; the honey-vanilla-solera character threads the cheesecake's creamy register beautifully — premium-sipping-rum-meets-dessert textbook.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Chilean Seabass": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- heavy spirit weight buries the main protein — needs a wine or lighter spirit. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Ron Zacapa Rum lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Chocolate Brownie": "Ron Zacapa Rum: Guatemalan Solera 23, high-altitude Andean aging, premium-sipping rum with honey-vanilla-caramel register. Excellent on brownie; the solera's honey-caramel thread meets warm chocolate at luxury register — this is the sipping-rum-on-dessert move.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Chocolate Cake": "Ron Zacapa Rum -- Solera 23, Guatemalan, honey-vanilla-caramel. The rich pour wraps the chocolate cake, and the dense weight underlines the dessert. Strong; a steady recommendation at the table.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Clam Chowder": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the heavy body handles the chowder, and the deep backbone frames the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Cowboy Ribeye": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey character frames the ribeye's cap fat and char — the light body is outweighed by the cap-fat, and the honey rounds the grilled char. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Crab Cake": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum overwhelms the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- the spirit's weight is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; the better calls are above. Ron Zacapa Rum belongs on the steak course.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Creamed Spinach": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum sits alongside the creamed spinach's rich bechamel-laced greens: the high-proof register matches the creamed spinach, and the heavy-pour register grips the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Creamy Potato": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the dense-spirit weight carries the potato soup, and the rich character softens the bowl. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Creme Brulee": "Ron Zacapa Rum -- Solera 23, Guatemalan, honey-vanilla-caramel. The Solera honey wraps the brulee, and the caramel rounds the dessert. Excellent; the herbal-complex digestif contrasts burnt-sugar-cream with bracing 55% clarity — one of the greatest dessert-pairings on the menu. Gold standard; the headline call at the table.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Escargot": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey character holds steady against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the light body is outpaced by the savory plate, and the rounded sweetness meets the herb butter. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Faroe Island Salmon": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- heavy spirit weight buries the main protein — needs a wine or lighter spirit. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Ron Zacapa Rum for the steak course.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Filet Mignon": "Ron Zacapa Rum -- Solera 23, Guatemalan, honey-vanilla-caramel. The dense-spirit weight carries the lean buttery filet, and the heavy-pour register grips the cut. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|French Onion": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum reads alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the layered spirit body sits with the French onion, and the layered body brightens the bowl. Works; a measured close to the meal.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Grilled Caesar": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum reads alongside the Caesar's charred-romaine and anchovy edge: the high-proof register matches the grilled Caesar, and the dense weight underlines the bowl. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Gumbo": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum reads alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the rich pour wraps the gumbo, and the dense weight underlines the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum leans against the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the dense-spirit weight carries the honey carrots, and the heavy-pour register grips the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|House Wedge": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum finds neutral with the wedge's iceberg-and-bleu cool crunch: the heavy body handles the wedge, and the rich character softens the bowl. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Kansas City": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey character sits with the strip's lean char — the light body is outweighed by the cut, and the honey rounds the grilled char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Loaded Potato": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum sits alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the layered spirit body sits with the loaded potato soup, and the dense weight underlines the bowl. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Lobster Mac": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum leans against the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the high-proof register matches the lobster mac, and the layered body brightens the side. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Market Fish": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- heavy spirit weight buries the main protein — needs a wine or lighter spirit. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Ron Zacapa Rum on the steak course instead.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Mocha Creme": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey character sits with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate dessert — the crisp body underclubs the dessert, and the honey threads the cream. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
