  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Roast Half Chicken": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum reads alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the rich pour wraps the roast chicken, and the layered body brightens the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum sits alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the rich pour wraps the chickpea soup, and the heavy-pour register grips the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- heavy spirit weight buries the main protein — needs a wine or lighter spirit. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Ron Zacapa Rum on the steak course instead.",
