  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Seasonal Vegetables": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum leans against the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the layered spirit body sits with the seasonal vegetables, and the layered body brightens the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Shrimp Bisque": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the rich pour wraps the shrimp bisque, and the deep backbone frames the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Shrimp Cocktail": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the spirit's weight is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Ron Zacapa Rum on the steak course instead.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Swordfish": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum overwhelms the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- heavy spirit weight buries the main protein — needs a wine or lighter spirit. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Ron Zacapa Rum for the steak course.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|The Tomahawk": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum finds neutral with the Tomahawk's theatrical bone-in marbling and smoky char: the layered spirit body sits with the 36oz showpiece, and the dense weight underlines the cut. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Tomato Basil": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum reads alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the layered spirit body sits with the tomato basil, and the layered body brightens the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Truffle Fries": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey character matches the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the crisp body sits with the plate. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- heavy spirit weight buries the main protein — needs a wine or lighter spirit. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Ron Zacapa Rum for the steak course.",
  "Ron Zacapa Rum|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the heavy body handles the curry, and the deep backbone frames the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Asparagus": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the asparagus, and the oak-and-spice register settles the side. Works; private-selection wasted on the salad.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with au gratin potatoes — aged Wild Turkey against cheese-and-cream. Strong; sophisticated Kentucky non-wheated match.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Beignets": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon backbone carries the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Bone Marrow": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with bone marrow — aged Wild Turkey against umami fat. The 90-proof and 10 years of oak give the pour the structure to meet the starter cleanly; a classic Kentucky approach to the marrow. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Bone-In Filet": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's caramel-honey character holds the line with the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the bourbon weight grips the lean cut, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Broccoli Cheddar": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the oak depth lays under the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; the complex character gives the dessert a refined frame.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Broccolini": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's soft-oak bourbon body finds neutral with the broccolini's tender green stalks: the caramel-spice register matches the broccolini, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; craft-blender complexity over-specified.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Brussels and Belly": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with Brussels + Belly — aged Kentucky bourbon meets maple-glazed pork belly. The 10-year oak depth handles the sweetness without over-matching. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Burrata": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with burrata — fresh dairy against aged bourbon. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Butternut Squash": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the oak depth lays under the squash bisque, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; master-blender doesn't drive.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Carrot Cake": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with carrot cake — aged caramel-vanilla against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Cheesecake": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with cheesecake — aged caramel against clean custard. Works; gentle composed match.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Chilean Seabass": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's aged Wild Turkey oak overwhelms the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Russell's Reserve 10 Year for the steak course.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Chocolate Brownie": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with the chocolate brownie — aged Wild Turkey against cocoa. Works; for cocoa interplay, Weller 107 or Weller Millennium. Russell's is the sipping-bourbon answer here.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Chocolate Cake": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's aged Wild Turkey oak leans against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the bourbon depth settles into the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; BIB structure is a touch over-specified for the dessert.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Clam Chowder": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's aged Wild Turkey oak finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon depth settles into the chowder, and the rounded sweetness brightens the cream. Works; regional craft at matched register.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Cowboy Ribeye": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with the Cowboy Ribeye — aged 90-proof Wild Turkey against cap fat and char. The age gives the pour enough body for the ribeye; a non-wheated alternate to Weller 12 or Eagle Rare 10. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Crab Cake": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with crab cake — aged bourbon against delicate crab. Avoid; pour a crisp white wine.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Creamed Spinach": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with creamed spinach — aged bourbon depth against dairy. Strong; the 10-year oak gives the side backbone distinct from wheated approaches.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Creamy Potato": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the caramel-spice register matches the potato soup, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Creme Brulee": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the bourbon backbone carries the brulee, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; stout-barrel story wasted on salad.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Escargot": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's caramel-honey character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Faroe Island Salmon": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's aged Wild Turkey oak clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Russell's Reserve 10 Year on the steak course instead.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Filet Mignon": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with the filet — Wild Turkey's aged sipping bourbon. 90 proof, 10 years old, classic Kentucky caramel-vanilla-oak profile. Distinct from BT's flagship cleanliness — more Wild Turkey character, more oak richness from aging. A non-wheated premium alternate for filet. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|French Onion": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's aged Wild Turkey oak sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the bourbon depth settles into the French onion, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; GTS is over-specified for an app; save the collector bottle for the main course.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Grilled Caesar": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with the grilled Caesar — charred romaine and anchovy against aged bourbon. Works; the 10-year earns a bit more of the Caesar than younger non-wheated pours bring.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Gumbo": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register leans against the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the bourbon depth settles into the gumbo, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; craft-blender complexity over-specified.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's aged Wild Turkey oak reads alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the bourbon depth settles into the honey carrots, and the oak frames the caramelized sugar. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|House Wedge": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with the House Wedge — iceberg and bleu against aged bourbon. Works; the Wild Turkey depth is underused by the salad.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Kansas City": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with the KC — Wild Turkey's 10-year aged profile against the strip's marbling. The age gives the pour enough oak depth to carry the char cleanly; distinct from Eagle Rare 10's Buffalo Trace-style elegance — more classic Kentucky vocabulary. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Loaded Potato": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the oak depth lays under the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Lobster Mac": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the bourbon depth settles into the lobster mac, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; retailer-pick wasted on salad.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Market Fish": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's aged Wild Turkey oak overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Russell's Reserve 10 Year for the steak course.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Mocha Creme": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the caramel-spice register matches the mocha creme, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; Old Fitz 9 brings more depth here.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Mushroom Bisque": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; KBS distinctiveness is slightly over-specified for the two-cut plate.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Mushrooms": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with the mushrooms — aged bourbon oak against earthy umami. Wild Turkey's 10-year gives the side layers; distinct from BT's cleaner approach. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the bourbon backbone carries the PB brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; OGD 16 frames the two-cut plate at distinctive register.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Porterhouse": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with the porterhouse — aged Wild Turkey across strip and filet. Strong; the classic Kentucky profile covers both sides cleanly but Eagle Rare 10 is the firmer call for max-strip-impact.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Prime Tartare": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's aged Wild Turkey oak sits alongside the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami: the bourbon depth settles into the tartare, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; BIB structure sits with the richness; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Rainbow Trout": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's aged Wild Turkey oak overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Russell's Reserve 10 Year for the steak course.",
