  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the chickpea soup, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; AE Triple Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's aged Wild Turkey oak overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Russell's Reserve 10 Year lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the bourbon weight handles the garlic spinach, and the caramel rounds the side. Works; EC 18's aged character meets the glaze at aged-HH register.",
  "Russell's Reserve 10 Year|Seafood Tower": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year's aged Wild Turkey oak crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Russell's Reserve 10 Year for the steak course.",
