  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Bowmore 12": "Bowmore 12's lighter-Islay peat character flattens the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Bowmore 12 for the steak course.",
  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Braida Montebruna Barbera": "Braida Montebruna Barbera's cherry-earth tannin sits alongside the halibut's salt-cured flesh — the silken tannin frames the fish, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Broccoli Cheddar": "Salt-Cured Halibut after the broccoli cheddar -- the cheddar-and-broccoli cream opens with rich-savory weight, the halibut following with firm cured flesh the cream gave room for. Strong; cream cleans for the cured main.",
  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Broccolini": "Salt-Cured Halibut with the broccolini -- the salt-cured flesh anchors against the lemon-pepper broccolini. Strong; reliable side for the halibut.",
