  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon": "Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon's estate-Cab Napa character clashes with the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Far Niente Chardonnay": "Salt-Cured Halibut: this delicate seafood's mild, flaky flesh meets this rich, oak-aged Chardonnay's butter, stone fruit, and full-bodied weight. Oaky Chardonnay's butter and stone fruit lock into rich fish — texture matching texture. A headliner white pour for rich fish. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi": "Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the red's structure is wrong for delicate flesh — built for red meat. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi for the steak course.",
  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Faust Napa Valley Cabernet": "Faust Napa Valley Cabernet's structured Napa Cab with cassis depth clashes with the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Save the Faust Napa Valley Cabernet for the steak course.",
  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía": "Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth clashes with the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía belongs on the steak course.",
  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Fernet Branca": "Fernet Branca's nuclear bitter-menthol intensity plays cleanly against the halibut's salt-cured flesh — the bitter herb edge cleans the fish, and the bitter cuts the fat. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
