  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Johnnie Walker Black": "Johnnie Walker Black's Highland-scotch character flattens the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Johnnie Walker Black on the steak course instead.",
