  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Komos Anejo Reserva": "Komos Anejo Reserva's aged-agave character overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- aged-agave weight buries the delicate flesh — agave register is wrong for fish. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Komos Anejo Reserva belongs on the steak course.",
