  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Lalo Silver": "Lalo Silver's clean silver register sits alongside the halibut's salt-cured flesh: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the halibut, and the agave-citrus thread frames the plate. Strong; the pairing reads cleanly.",
  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Laphroaig 10": "Laphroaig 10's classic Islay peat overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a scotch. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Laphroaig 10 for the steak course.",
