  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé": "Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé's fine-bubble Champagne register leans against the halibut's salt-cured flesh: the fine bubbles lift the halibut, and the citrus frames the plate. Strong; reliable opener for the cut.",
  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut": "Tours-sur-Marne Chardonnay-blend Champagne — precise green apple, lemon zest, whisper of brioche, vibrant acidity. The high-acid finish cuts through the sweet soy glaze and the brioche plays against cured halibut. Strong Champagne for salt-cured halibut — bubbles reset the palate between bites.",
  "Salt-Cured Halibut|Le Garenne Rosé": "Salt-Cured Halibut: this delicate seafood's mild, flaky flesh meets this dry Provence-style rosé's red-fruit freshness and light weight. Crisp acidity and mineral edge mirror fish's own brininess — clean, classic alignment. Works cleanly.",
