  "Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir's cherry-earth tannin stays alongside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the herbs cut the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir|Beignets": "Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift jars against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir for the steak course.",
