  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|2 James Gin": "2 James Gin's crisp char-juniper botanicals sits alongside the garlic-spinach's buttered greens — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the botanicals echo the green plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|A Midnight's Winter Dram": "A Midnight's Winter Dram's Highland-scotch character leans against the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the scotch depth settles into the garlic spinach, and the malt edge frames the side. Works; GTS is over-specified for an app; save the collector bottle for the main course.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Aberlour 16": "Aberlour 16's double-matured Speyside balance sits alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the malt-and-oak threads the garlic spinach, and the malt edge frames the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Adictivo Cristalino": "Adictivo Cristalino's rested-agave body finds neutral with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the rested-agave depth sits with the garlic spinach, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; accessible aged composed with this dish.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Adictivo Reposado": "Adictivo Reposado's aged-agave character finds neutral with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the añejo register carries the garlic spinach, and the caramel-agave register brightens the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Alexander Valley Chardonnay": "Alexander Valley Chardonnay — ripe apple, pear, warm vanilla oak. The oak-vanilla weight cuts the sauté butter and the apple-pear fruit plays against garlic without clashing with the spinach's earth. Works as accessible California Chardonnay for the sauté side — oak rounds the pairing.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Alexander Valley Cyrus": "Alexander Valley Cyrus's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis finds neutral with the garlic-spinach's buttered greens — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Alexander Valley Homestead Red": "Alexander Valley Homestead Red's coffee-mocha tannin finds neutral with the garlic-spinach's buttered greens — the medium-body red frames the green plate, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Amaro Nonino": "Amaro Nonino's crisp orange-peel-grappa sweetness doubles down on the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- bitter herbs and a green vegetable side compound the same register — no contrast. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Amaro Nonino for the steak course.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Ancho Reyes": "Ancho Reyes' sweet liqueur character clashes with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Reserve the Ancho Reyes for the steak course.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Angel's Envy": "Angel's Envy's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the bourbon depth settles into the garlic spinach, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; gentle composed match.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Angel's Envy Cask Strength": "Angel's Envy Cask Strength's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth clashes with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- the bourbon's register is wrong for a clean vegetable side — needs crisp white instead. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Angel's Envy Cask Strength lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Angel's Envy Triple Cask": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth reads alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the bourbon depth settles into the garlic spinach, and the oak frames the side. Works; narrative-bourbon doesn't drive.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Aperol": "Aperol's crisp bitter-orange-aperitivo edge clashes with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- bitter aperitivo on the supporting side reads as wrong register for the course. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; one of those is the move. Aperol belongs on the steak course.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon": "Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth crowds the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- the side needs a crisper register to carry it cleanly. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Averna Amaro": "Averna Amaro's bitter-herb aperitivo edge doubles down on the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- bitter herbs and a green vegetable side compound the same register — no contrast. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Averna Amaro for the steak course.",
