  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Booker's": "Booker's cask-strength bourbon depth smothers the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- the side reads small under oak-and-vanilla density. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Booker's for the steak course.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Botanist Gin": "Botanist Gin's crisp Islay-gentle-botanical botanicals sits beside the garlic-spinach's buttered greens — the botanical edge sits with the light side, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Bowdie's Old Fashioned": "Buffalo Trace muddled with our rum-soaked cherries, orange, and Angostura. Bourbon's caramel weight buries the light spinach and dominates the escargot butter's garlic-shallot character. Reserve for beef sides or the marrow course. Avoid; the pairing fights at the table — point the guest elsewhere.",
