  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon": "Alexander Valley Cabernet — soft tannin. Works if the guest is committed to red through the main and side, but the Sauvignon Blancs and Pinots peak higher against the lighter spinach. Acceptable not-peak option.",
  "Sauteed Garlic Spinach|Joseph Mellot Sancerre": "Joseph Mellot Sancerre — Loire Sauv Blanc with grapefruit, chalk, fresh herbs. The mineral and herb profile plays against the sauté butter-garlic and echoes spinach's earth cleanly. Works as Sancerre for the sauté side — Loire precision on a simple but well-made sauce.",
