  "Seafood Tower|Bardstown Founders KBS": "Bardstown Founders KBS's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Bardstown Founders KBS for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Bardstown Foursquare": "Bardstown Foursquare's rum-cask + cocoa is textbook — tropical-rum + chocolate fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Bardstown Foursquare for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Bardstown Fusion #7": "Bardstown Fusion #7's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Bardstown Fusion #7 for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel": "Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Basil Hayden's": "Basil Hayden's light high-rye and cocoa smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Basil Hayden's on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Basil Hayden's 10 Year": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's aged oak and rye spice drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Basil Hayden's 10 Year belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Basil Hayden's Malted Rye": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Basil Hayden's Malted Rye for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Basil Hayden's Toast": "Basil Hayden's Toast's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Basil Hayden's Toast for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Bee's Knees": "Empress Indigo gin with lemon and honey lavender syrup. Honey sweetness against brine works; the Indigo's butterfly-pea color-change adds visual interest next to the tower. Cocktail route for guests who don't want sparkling. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Seafood Tower|Beefeater Gin": "Beefeater with the seafood tower — classic London Dry against the raw bar. Excellent; Beefeater is the approachable tower-gin pairing when Tanq feels too heavy and Plymouth too soft.",
  "Seafood Tower|Beignets": "Seafood Tower and the beignets -- bright meets sweet, the contrast stays light. Works; the bookends compose neutrally.",
  "Seafood Tower|Belvedere Vodka": "Belvedere with the seafood tower — single-estate rye against the raw bar. Strong; Belvedere's character is distinctive but Goose's softness is the flagship tower choice.",
  "Seafood Tower|Blade & Bow": "Blade & Bow's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Blade & Bow lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Blanton's Gold": "Blanton's Gold's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Blanton's Gold belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Blanton's Original": "Blanton's Original's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Blanton's Original for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Blanton's Straight from the Barrel": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Blanton's Straight from the Barrel lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Blood Oath Pact 10": "Blood Oath Pact 10's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Blood Oath Pact 10 for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Blood Oath Pact 8": "Blood Oath Pact 8's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Blood Oath Pact 8 on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Blood Oath Pact 9": "Blood Oath Pact 9's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Blood Oath Pact 9 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Bluecoat Gin": "Bluecoat with the seafood tower — Philadelphia citrus-forward craft against the raw bar. Strong; Bluecoat's 4-citrus profile lifts the tower at American-artisan register; Gray Whale's ocean-botanicals is still the featured craft-tower match.",
  "Seafood Tower|Bodega Noemia A Lisa": "Bodega Noemia A Lisa's plush Malbec with plum-and-violet weight crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Bodega Noemia A Lisa on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Bombay Dry Gin": "Bombay Dry with the seafood tower — juniper-assertive London Dry against the raw bar. Excellent; Bombay Dry's traditional character delivers the raw bar classic-gin experience.",
  "Seafood Tower|Bombay Sapphire Gin": "Bombay Sapphire with the seafood tower — vapor-infused 10-botanical against the raw bar. Excellent; Sapphire's softer floral character is the accessible luxury pairing — where Tanq is serious and Plymouth is English-traditional, Sapphire is approachable.",
  "Seafood Tower|Bone-In Filet": "The bone-in filet after the seafood tower -- the iced shellfish cleans the palate, the 14oz cut following with bone-marrow depth the opener leaves room for. Strong; the contrast in temperature and weight reads composed.",
  "Seafood Tower|Booker's": "Booker's cask-strength bourbon depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Booker's lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Botanist Gin": "Botanist with the seafood tower — Bruichladdich Islay craft gin, 22 foraged Islay botanicals + 9 classic. Excellent; Botanist's wildcrafted Islay-herb character frames the raw bar with a coastal-Scotland story no other gin on the menu can claim — same island that makes Islay Scotch, but in gin form. The most thematically right tower gin.",
  "Seafood Tower|Bowdie's Old Fashioned": "Buffalo Trace muddled with our rum-soaked cherries, orange, and Angostura. Bourbon and cold shellfish don't meet well — the caramel weight buries the brine and delicate textures. Reserve for the steak course. Avoid; the call reads off-register; recommend an alternative.",
  "Seafood Tower|Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark": "Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Bowman Brothers Small Batch": "Bowman Brothers Small Batch's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Bowman Brothers Small Batch lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Bowmore 12": "Bowmore 12's lighter-Islay peat character drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Bowmore 12 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Braida Montebruna Barbera": "Braida Montebruna Barbera's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Braida Montebruna Barbera on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Broccoli Cheddar": "The seafood tower with the broccoli cheddar -- the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup meets the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the bright cuts the rich cleanly. Works; both opening courses earn their place.",
  "Seafood Tower|Broccolini": "Seafood Tower alongside the broccolini -- the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup meets the broccolini's tender green stalks: both crisp and clean, the table reads light from open to handoff. Works; no conflict, the meal builds.",
  "Seafood Tower|Bruichladdich": "Seafood Tower: this delicate seafood starter's briny-fresh sweetness meets this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight. Whiskey's oak and caramel are only going to land if the starter can carry weight — check the plate. Works as a parallel pour.",
  "Seafood Tower|Buffalo Trace": "Buffalo Trace's rounded vanilla-and-toffee character smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Buffalo Trace lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Buffalo Trace Cream": "Buffalo Trace Cream's sweet liqueur character clashes with the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet liqueur is dessert energy — wrong place for the table's first course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Buffalo Trace Cream on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Bulleit Bourbon": "Bulleit Bourbon's high-rye spice-forward depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Bulleit Bourbon lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Butternut Squash": "The seafood tower with the butternut squash -- the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup meets the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: acid plays against sweetness, the close stays unburdened. Works; both opening courses earn their place.",
  "Seafood Tower|Cade Cabernet Sauvignon": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Camarena Tequila": "Camarena Tequila's añejo-pour depth sits alongside the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the añejo register carries the seafood tower, and the oak threads the starter. Works; brightness can cut the glaze but wheated bourbons sit better with this dish.",
  "Seafood Tower|Campari": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bitter aperitivo flattens the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Canadian Club": "Canadian Club's workhorse Canadian blend crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Canadian Club for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Canadian Club 43 Year": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Canadian Club 43 Year lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Captain Morgan Rum": "Captain Morgan Rum's light-rum register with cane and citrus lift mis-pairs with the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- this light spirit's register is wrong for the starter — try a different pour. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a light spirit. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Captain Morgan Rum on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Caribou Crossing": "Caribou Crossing's craft profile is wrong for scallops overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit weight crowds the delicate shellfish — no acid to clean the brine. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Caribou Crossing for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Carrot Cake": "The seafood tower and the carrot cake -- the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup bookends with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Seafood Tower|Casa LBV Port": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- dessert sugar on cold shellfish is wrong direction — needs sparkling or Sancerre. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Casa LBV Port belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Casamigos Mezcal": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- mezcal smoke obliterates delicate shellfish — needs sparkling or sancerre. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a mezcal. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Casamigos Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon": "Caymus's cocoa, mocha, and velvety tannins — a full Napa Cab with no business near cold oysters and lobster. The structural mismatch is extreme. Save the bottle for the main course, steer Cab-only guests to Champagne here. Avoid; the call reads off-register; recommend an alternative.",
  "Seafood Tower|Chambord": "Chambord's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet liqueur on cold shellfish is wrong-course energy — too forward for a clean opener. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Chambord for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Cheesecake": "Seafood Tower and the cheesecake -- acid and sugar share the table, neither course pulls heavy. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Seafood Tower|Chilean Seabass": "Chilean Seabass with the seafood tower as the lead-in -- the pan-finished seabass threads the iced shellfish tower. Strong; the starter sets the table for the seabass.",
  "Seafood Tower|Chocolate Brownie": "The seafood tower alongside the brownie -- the bright register lifts the sweet, the meal closes clean. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Seafood Tower|Chocolate Cake": "The seafood tower alongside the chocolate cake -- the bright register lifts the sweet, the meal closes clean. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Seafood Tower|Chopin Vodka": "Chopin with the seafood tower — Polish potato vodka against the raw bar. Strong; Chopin frames the tower with creamy character, though Goose's wheat silkiness is the flagship luxury pairing.",
  "Seafood Tower|Christian Bros Brandy": "Christian Bros Brandy's barrel-aged cognac character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- cognac weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs sparkling or a crisp white. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a cognac. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Christian Bros Brandy for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Château Batailley": "Château Batailley's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Château Batailley on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Château Beaucastel": "Château Beaucastel's old-world Châteauneuf-du-Pape gravitas overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Pour the Château Beaucastel on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Château Gombaude-Guillot": "Château Gombaude-Guillot's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Château Gombaude-Guillot belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Château Haut Segottes": "Château Haut Segottes' Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Château Haut Segottes for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Château de Rouillac": "Château de Rouillac's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Château de Rouillac belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Clam Chowder": "The seafood tower alongside the chowder -- both bring shellfish as the headline. Avoid; one is enough. Pair the seafood tower with Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut; pair the chowder with Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis.",
  "Seafood Tower|Clase Azul Anejo": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- aged tequila is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Clase Azul Anejo for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Clase Azul Durango": "Clase Azul Durango's añejo-pour depth leans against the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the rested-agave depth sits with the seafood tower, and the soft-spice note softens the starter. Works; ceremony over-specified.",
  "Seafood Tower|Clase Azul Gold": "Clase Azul Gold's joven blend with mezcal accent overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- aged tequila is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; the better calls are above. Clase Azul Gold lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- mezcal smoke is too forward for the table's opener. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a mezcal. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Clase Azul Plata": "Clase Azul Plata with the seafood tower — ceramic-bottle luxury blanco across raw oysters, shrimp, and lobster. The premium presentation elevates the whole tower; pour when the table wants the full experience. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Seafood Tower|Clase Azul Reposado": "Clase Azul Reposado's ceramic-icon reposado character sits alongside the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the seafood tower, and the caramel-agave register brightens the starter. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Seafood Tower|Clase Azul Ultra": "Clase Azul Ultra's aged-agave character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- añejo weight has no foil against cold shellfish — needs sparkling or crisp white. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Clase Azul Ultra lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Clermont Steep": "Clermont Steep's Jim Beam's wheated expression overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit weight crowds the delicate shellfish — no acid to clean the brine. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Clermont Steep for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Clos Petit Ona Grenache": "Clos Petit Ona Grenache's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Clos Petit Ona Grenache on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Codigo 1530 Rosa": "Codigo 1530 Rosa's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the oak-aged tequila body threads the seafood tower, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the starter. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Seafood Tower|Contratto Vermouth": "Contratto Vermouth's vermouth-wine-base sweetness finds neutral with the tower's chilled shellfish — the bitter herb edge overpowers the shellfish. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Seafood Tower|Corazon Blanco": "Corazon Blanco with the seafood tower — single-estate highland across raw oysters, shrimp, lobster. Strong; the Sazerac-family character provides a distinctive through-line.",
  "Seafood Tower|Corazon Reposado": "Corazon Reposado's rested-agave body reads alongside the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the seafood tower, and the caramel-agave register brightens the starter. Works; the 70th's smoothness is an unusual but interesting counterpoint.",
  "Seafood Tower|Corazon Sazerac": "Corazon Sazerac's aged-agave character reads alongside the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the añejo register carries the seafood tower, and the soft-spice note softens the starter. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Seafood Tower|Corazon Stagg": "Corazon Stagg's añejo tequila finished in ex-George-T reads alongside the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the barrel-rested body handles the seafood tower, and the oak threads the starter. Works; distinctive ceremony over-specified.",
  "Seafood Tower|Corazon Weller": "Corazon Weller's rested-agave body reads alongside the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the añejo register carries the seafood tower, and the soft-spice note softens the starter. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Seafood Tower|Corazón del Sol Malbec": "Corazón del Sol Malbec's plush Malbec with plum-and-violet weight overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Corazón del Sol Malbec for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Corpse Reviver": "Warner's gin, Lillet, Pierre Ferrand cognac, lemon, absinthe rinse. The citrus-and-botanical structure handles the raw-bar spread and the anise-edge adds aromatic depth. Strong tower cocktail — though Champagne and French 75 peak slightly higher for raw shellfish.",
  "Seafood Tower|Courvoisier Cognac": "Courvoisier Cognac's classic VS cognac overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- cognac weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs sparkling or a crisp white. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a cognac. Avoid; the better calls are above. Courvoisier Cognac belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Cowboy Ribeye": "Cowboy Ribeye after the seafood tower -- the iced shellfish opens with bright cold-brine, the 26oz marbled char-and-fat following with rendered richness that the cold opener primed the palate to receive. Strong; the contrast carries the table.",
  "Seafood Tower|Cragganmore 12": "Cragganmore 12's complex Speyside character drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Cragganmore 12 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Creamed Spinach": "Seafood Tower and the creamed spinach -- acid plays against richness, the contrast holds across the courses. Works; both items hold their register, no clash.",
  "Seafood Tower|Creamy Potato": "Seafood Tower alongside the potato soup -- acid lifts the richness, the meal gets the contrast it needs. Works; the openers share the table cleanly, sequence or share.",
  "Seafood Tower|Creme Brulee": "Seafood Tower and the brulee -- acid and sugar share the table, neither course pulls heavy. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Seafood Tower|Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée": "Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée's Willamette Pinot elegance overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Crown Royal": "Crown Royal's classic Canadian blend smoothness fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Crown Royal for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Cucumber Gimlet": "Hendrick's muddled with cucumber, lime, ginger syrup, soda top. The cocktail's garden-fresh profile handles the raw-bar spread — oysters, shrimp, crab legs — well; soda adds lift. Strong tower pairing when guest wants a non-bubbly option alongside the shellfish.",
  "Seafood Tower|Dalmore 12": "Dalmore 12's sherry-finished Highland character fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Dalmore 12 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge": "Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge's Loire Valley Pinot Noir crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Darioush Cabernet Franc": "Darioush Cabernet Franc's herbaceous Cab Franc with red-fruit and bell-pepper crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Darioush Cabernet Franc for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Detroit City Gin": "Detroit City Gin with the seafood tower — Detroit craft gin against the raw bar. Strong; Detroit City is the Detroit-pride tower pairing.",
  "Seafood Tower|Detroit City Vodka": "Detroit City Vodka's crisp grain-juniper neutrality plays cleanly against the tower's chilled shellfish — the neutral profile carries the shellfish without weight. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Seafood Tower|Dewar's 15": "Dewar's 15's 15yr aged Highland blend overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit weight crowds the delicate shellfish — no acid to clean the brine. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Dewar's 15 on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Dewar's White Label": "Dewar's White Label's Highland blend with Aberfeldy-malt core crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; the better calls are above. Pour the Dewar's White Label on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Disaronno": "Disaronno's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet liqueur on cold shellfish is wrong-course energy — too forward for a clean opener. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; one of those is the move. Disaronno belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye": "Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye's rye-spice character crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum": "Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum's aged-rum register with molasses and oak depth overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit's weight is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Domaine Serene Grand Cheval": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Domaine Tempier Bandol": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Domaine Tempier Bandol lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé": "Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé's citrus-mineral acidity plays cleanly against the tower's chilled shellfish — the crisp acidity lifts the shellfish without weight, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Seafood Tower|Domaine du Grand Tinel": "Domaine du Grand Tinel's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Domaine du Grand Tinel for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Don Fulano Anejo": "Don Fulano Anejo's aged-agave character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- aged tequila is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Don Fulano Anejo on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Don Fulano Blanco": "Don Fulano Blanco with the seafood tower — highland craft across raw oysters, shrimp, lobster. Strong; the refined craft character provides a premium through-line.",
  "Seafood Tower|Don Fulano Reposado": "Don Fulano Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the seafood tower, and the oak threads the starter. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Seafood Tower|Don Julio 1942": "Don Julio 1942's icon extra-añejo character finds neutral with the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the rested-agave depth sits with the seafood tower, and the soft-spice note softens the starter. Works; accessible aged sits with richness.",
  "Seafood Tower|Don Julio 70th": "Don Julio 70th's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the oak-aged tequila body threads the seafood tower, and the oak threads the starter. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Seafood Tower|Don Julio Blanco": "Don Julio Blanco with the seafood tower — benchmark blanco across raw oysters, shrimp, and lobster. The clean agave and citrus provide the through-line for the whole tower; an everyday-premium pairing. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Seafood Tower|Don Julio Reposado": "Don Julio Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register leans against the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the seafood tower, and the oak threads the starter. Works; single-estate character handles richness at craft register.",
  "Seafood Tower|Drambuie": "Drambuie's sweet liqueur character smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sugar buries the delicate shellfish without any acid to balance. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Drambuie lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Dunville's Single Malt": "Dunville's Single Malt's Irish whiskey smoothness smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Dunville's Single Malt for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|E.H. Taylor Full Proof": "E.H. Taylor Full Proof's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the E.H. Taylor Full Proof for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|E.H. Taylor Rye": "E.H. Taylor Rye's rye-spice character crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the E.H. Taylor Rye for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|E.H. Taylor Small Batch": "E.H. Taylor Small Batch's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the E.H. Taylor Small Batch for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Eagle Rare 10 Year": "Eagle Rare 10 Year's aged-oak elegance drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Eagle Rare 10 Year for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Eastern Kille Dry Gin": "Eastern Kille with the seafood tower — small-batch GR family craft against the raw bar. Strong; Eastern Kille is a Grand Rapids-proud tower pairing.",
  "Seafood Tower|El Cabo": "El Cabo's cooked-agave-and-oak register reads alongside the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the aged-agave weight wraps the seafood tower, and the cooked-agave note underlines the starter. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Seafood Tower|El Mayor Extra Anejo": "El Mayor Extra Anejo's aged-agave character smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- aged-agave register crowds the delicate shellfish frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. El Mayor Extra Anejo belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|El Mayor Reposado": "El Mayor Reposado's aged-agave character leans against the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the barrel-rested body handles the seafood tower, and the caramel-agave register brightens the starter. Works; the agave cuts the glaze but the pairing isn't marquee.",
  "Seafood Tower|Elephant Gin": "Elephant Gin with the seafood tower — conservation-charity craft gin against the raw bar. Excellent; Elephant is the story-driven tower pairing — baobab/buchu/lion's tail profile distinctive enough to make the raw bar memorable.",
  "Seafood Tower|Elijah Craig 18 Year": "Elijah Craig 18 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Elijah Craig 18 Year belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Elijah Craig Private Barrel": "Elijah Craig Private Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Elijah Craig Private Barrel on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Elijah Craig Single Barrel": "Elijah Craig Single Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Elijah Craig Single Barrel for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Elijah Craig Small Batch": "Elijah Craig Small Batch's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Elijah Craig Small Batch on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Elijah Craig Straight Rye": "Elijah Craig Straight Rye's rye-spice character fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Elijah Craig Straight Rye on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Elk Cove Five Mountain": "Elk Cove Five Mountain's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Elk Cove Five Mountain for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Elk Cove Pinot Blanc": "Willamette Oregon Pinot Blanc — soft pear, white peach, floral, refreshing acidity. The medium-body freshness resets palate between oysters, shrimp, and crab and the fruit plays against brine across the platter. Strong unoaked white for the seafood tower — more character than Sauv Blanc.",
  "Seafood Tower|Elmer T. Lee": "Elmer T. Lee's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Elmer T. Lee for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Empress 1908 Gin": "Empress 1908 with the seafood tower — BC color-changing gin against the raw bar. Strong; Empress's floral-citrus profile lifts the tower with visual-distinctive character; Gray Whale's California ocean-botanicals is still the featured craft-tower match.",
  "Seafood Tower|Epoch Ingenuity": "Epoch Ingenuity's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Epoch Ingenuity for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Espresso Martini": "Tito's, espresso, Grind Espresso Liqueur, Averna amaro, vanilla syrup, Angostura. Coffee-forward cocktail against raw shellfish spread is incoherent on every axis. Never pair — the tower demands Champagne, French 75, or light gin cocktails, never an espresso-based dessert cocktail.",
  "Seafood Tower|Espresso Old Fashioned": "Buffalo Trace, bourbon cream, Frangelico, espresso, brown sugar, Angostura. Raw shellfish-and-oyster display against a dessert-weight coffee cocktail is incoherent on every axis. Never pair — the tower demands Champagne, crisp whites, or oyster-friendly bubbles, never a heavy coffee-bourbon pour.",
  "Seafood Tower|Evening Land Seven Springs": "Evening Land Seven Springs' red-fruit-and-spice elegance overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Evening Land Seven Springs for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon": "Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon's estate-Cab Napa character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Far Niente Chardonnay": "Far Niente Chardonnay's bold butter-char acidity finds register with the tower's chilled shellfish — the crisp acidity lifts the shellfish without weight, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Seafood Tower|Faroe Island Salmon": "Faroe Island Salmon preceded by the seafood tower -- the pan-finished salmon meets the chilled shellfish lineup. Strong; reliable opener for the main.",
  "Seafood Tower|Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi": "Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Faust Napa Valley Cabernet": "Faust Napa Valley Cabernet's structured Napa Cab with cassis depth overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Faust Napa Valley Cabernet belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía": "Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Fernet Branca": "Fernet Branca's nuclear bitter-menthol intensity plays cleanly against the tower's chilled shellfish — the bitter herb edge overpowers the shellfish. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Seafood Tower|Fernet Menta": "Fernet Menta's crisp mint-menthol edge plays cleanly against the tower's chilled shellfish — the bitter herb edge overpowers the shellfish. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Seafood Tower|Filet Mignon": "Filet Mignon after the seafood tower -- the iced shellfish lineup cleans the palate, the 10oz lean cut following with quiet beef butter. Strong; the cold opener resets the table for the cut.",
  "Seafood Tower|Fireball Whisky": "Fireball Whisky's sweet liqueur character clashes with the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet liqueur is dessert energy — wrong place for the table's first course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Fireball Whisky for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Fisher Unity Pinot Noir": "Fisher Unity Pinot Noir's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Fisher Unity Pinot Noir for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Four Roses Small Batch Select": "Four Roses Small Batch Select's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Four Roses Small Batch Select belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Four Roses Yellow Label": "Four Roses Yellow Label's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit weight crowds the delicate shellfish — no acid to clean the brine. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Four Roses Yellow Label on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Fox & Oden": "Fox & Oden's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit weight crowds the delicate shellfish — no acid to clean the brine. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Fox & Oden belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Fox & Oden Double Oaked": "Fox & Oden Double Oaked's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Fox & Oden Double Oaked for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Frangelico": "Frangelico's Piedmont hazelnut depth to mocha at after-dinner register overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet liqueur on cold shellfish is wrong-course energy — too forward for a clean opener. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Frangelico on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Freemark Abbey Bosché": "Freemark Abbey Bosché's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Freemark Abbey Bosché belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|French 75": "Inverroche gin, lemon, vanilla syrup, Prosecco top. The Prosecco's bubbles and citrus-led gin are built for raw shellfish — oysters, shrimp, crab legs. Vanilla syrup softens what would be a sharper build. Peak cocktail for the tower's celebratory, raw-bar-centric indulgence.",
  "Seafood Tower|French Onion": "The seafood tower with the French onion -- the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup meets the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: acid breaks the umami stack, the table earns the brighter note. Works; both opening courses earn their place.",
  "Seafood Tower|Frias Block 5": "Frias Block 5's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Frias Block 5 for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo": "G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo's high-acid Nebbiolo with rose-and-tar grip overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti": "G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti's peach-and-honey frizzante sweetness mis-pairs with the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- this specific sparkling fights the starter — a different brut or rosé would carry it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a sparkling. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|G4 Blanco": "G4 Blanco with the seafood tower — craft 80-proof across raw oysters, shrimp, lobster. Strong; Camarena-family craft provides a distinctive through-line.",
  "Seafood Tower|G4 High Proof": "G4 High Proof's rested-agave body reads alongside the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the barrel-rested body handles the seafood tower, and the oak threads the starter. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Seafood Tower|Garavogue Irish Whiskey": "Garavogue Irish Whiskey's Irish whiskey smoothness drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Garavogue Irish Whiskey for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|George T. Stagg": "George T. Stagg's cask-strength BTAC bourbon power drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the George T. Stagg for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon": "Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Ghost Block Zinfandel": "Ghost Block Zinfandel's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Ghost Block Zinfandel for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Glenfiddich 12": "Glenfiddich 12's entry Speyside benchmark fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Glenfiddich 12 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Glenfiddich 14": "Glenfiddich 14's Highland-scotch character crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Glenfiddich 14 on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Glenfiddich 18": "Glenfiddich 18's aged Speyside with sherry finish smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Glenfiddich 18 for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23's Cuvée-finished 23-year Speyside luxury smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Glenglassaugh 12": "Glenglassaugh 12's Highland-scotch character overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit weight crowds the delicate shellfish — no acid to clean the brine. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Glenglassaugh 12 for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Glenlivet 12": "Glenlivet 12's entry Speyside character fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Glenlivet 12 for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Glenmorangie 10": "Glenmorangie 10's tallest-stills Highland bourbon-cask character drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Glenmorangie 10 on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Glenmorangie 18": "Glenmorangie 18's aged Highland with Oloroso finish crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Glenmorangie 18 for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Graham's 10 Year Tawny": "Graham's 10 Year Tawny's dessert-wine sweetness overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- dessert sugar on cold shellfish is wrong direction — needs sparkling or Sancerre. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Graham's 10 Year Tawny belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Graham's 20 Year Tawny": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth clashes with the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Graham's 20 Year Tawny lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Graham's 2017 Vintage Port": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Gran Patron Platinum": "Gran Patron Platinum with the seafood tower — ultra-premium Patron across raw oysters, shrimp, and lobster. The triple-distilled smoothness provides a refined through-line for the whole tower. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Seafood Tower|Grand Marnier": "Grand Marnier's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet liqueur on cold shellfish is wrong-course energy — too forward for a clean opener. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Grand Marnier for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Gray Whale Gin": "Gray Whale with the seafood tower — California ocean-botanical gin with Mendocino kombu against the raw bar. Excellent; Gray Whale is the featured Smooth/Citrus Craft Gin-tower pairing — the kombu-and-California-botanical profile is the most thematically right craft gin for the raw bar, parallel to Botanist's Islay approach for Botanical-Forward.",
  "Seafood Tower|Green Chartreuse": "Green Chartreuse's bitter-herb aperitivo edge overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- amaro bitterness on cold shellfish flattens the delicate brine — needs sparkling instead. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Green Chartreuse lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Grey Goose Vodka": "Grey Goose with the seafood tower — French winter wheat from Picardie, Cognac-region pedigree. Excellent; Goose's soft silky elegance is the luxury default when a table orders the tower and wants a call vodka that matches the occasion.",
  "Seafood Tower|Grilled Caesar": "The seafood tower with the Caesar -- the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup meets the Caesar's charred-romaine and anchovy edge: acid breaks the umami stack, the table earns the brighter note. Works; both opening courses earn their place.",
  "Seafood Tower|Gumbo": "Seafood Tower and the gumbo together -- acid breaks the heat, the meal earns relief from the spice. Works; the table opens with both, no clash either way.",
  "Seafood Tower|Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet": "Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|HDW 100 Vodka": "HDW 100 Vodka's char-herbal neutrality holds steady against the tower's chilled shellfish — the neutral profile carries the shellfish without weight, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Seafood Tower|Hakushu 12 Year": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character finds neutral with the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the Mizunara-influenced register sits with the seafood tower, and the Japanese-craft balance underlines the starter. Works; premium proof overshoots delicacy.",
  "Seafood Tower|Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Hangar 1 Vodka": "Hangar 1 Vodka: clean craft vodka from Alameda, CA. Excellent on seafood tower; neutral-clean profile frames shellfish at California-craft register.",
  "Seafood Tower|Head Fake": "Wheatley vodka, limoncello, triple sec, lemon, simple syrup. The citrus-forward profile handles the raw-bar spread and Wheatley's clean finish doesn't crush oysters or shrimp. Strong tower cocktail when guest wants sweet-and-bright rather than Champagne or French 75.",
  "Seafood Tower|Heaven Hill 20 Year": "Heaven Hill 20 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Heaven Hill 20 Year lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond": "Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Heaven's Door 10 Year": "Heaven's Door 10 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Heaven's Door 10 Year for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Heitz Martha's Vineyard": "Heitz Martha's Vineyard's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Heitz Martha's Vineyard for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Heitz Trailside Vineyard": "Heitz Trailside Vineyard's Napa-icon Cab character overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Heitz Trailside Vineyard for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Hendricks Flora Adora": "Flora Adora with the seafood tower — Spring-release floral Hendrick's against the raw bar. Excellent; Flora Adora's lavish-garden profile elevates the tower with distinctive floral character; Neptunia's coastal profile is the Hendrick's tower pick for thematic seafood match.",
  "Seafood Tower|Hendricks Gin": "Hendricks with the seafood tower — flagship Scottish gin against the raw bar. Excellent; Hendrick's cucumber-rose profile is the crowd-pleasing Hendrick's-tower pairing; Neptunia's coastal-maritime expression is the more thematic Hendrick's tower choice.",
  "Seafood Tower|Hendricks Grand Cabaret": "Grand Cabaret with the seafood tower — fruit-forward Hendrick's against the raw bar. Excellent; Grand Cabaret's black-currant character brings distinctive cocktail-culture lift to the tower.",
  "Seafood Tower|Hendricks Neptunia": "Neptunia with the seafood tower — Hendrick's coastal release, bladderwrack seaweed + Ayrshire coast thyme + coastal flowers. Excellent; Neptunia's briny-maritime character is the featured Hendrick's Family-seafood-tower pairing — the Scottish-sea-botanical gin meets the raw bar with terroir-echoing thematic precision.",
  "Seafood Tower|Hendricks Orbium": "Orbium with the seafood tower — bitter-tonic Hendrick's against the raw bar. Excellent; Orbium's quinine-wormwood profile is a cocktail-culture tower choice — perpetual G&T character meets the raw bar.",
  "Seafood Tower|Hennessy Cognac": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- cognac weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs sparkling or a crisp white. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a cognac. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hennessy Cognac lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond": "Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond's aged 100-proof bonded single-barrel fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Hibiki Japanese Harmony": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony finds neutral with the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the precise Japanese craft body wraps the seafood tower, and the precision rounds the starter. Works; curated single-barrel slightly over-specified.",
  "Seafood Tower|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Seafood Tower and the honey carrots -- acid and sugar share the table, neither course pulls heavy. Works; both items hold their register, no clash.",
  "Seafood Tower|House Wedge": "Seafood Tower and the wedge together -- acid lifts the umami, the meal carries lift without losing depth. Works; the table opens with both, no clash either way.",
  "Seafood Tower|I.W. Harper 15 Year": "I.W. Harper 15 Year's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. I.W. Harper 15 Year belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Il Colle Prosecco Superiore": "Glera Prosecco from Veneto — bright floral with white peach, green apple, clean citrus finish. The light crisp bubbles meet the tower's mixed shellfish and bright brine cleanly, refreshing between oysters, shrimp, and crab. Strong approachable seafood tower pour — value-forward without sacrificing freshness.",
  "Seafood Tower|Inhibited": "Tito's, Kahlúa, Bailey's, chocolate liqueur, espresso, chocolate-drizzled glass. Dessert coffee-cream cocktail against raw shellfish spread is incoherent on every axis. Never pair — the tower demands Champagne, French 75, or light gin cocktails, never a chocolate martini.",
  "Seafood Tower|Inverroche Gin": "Inverroche with the seafood tower — South African fynbos gin against the raw bar. Excellent; Inverroche's Cape-floral character gives the tower a distinctive terroir-story pairing — the fynbos bloom-profile lifts the raw bar with elegance.",
  "Seafood Tower|Iron Fish Gin": "Iron Fish with the seafood tower — northern-Michigan farm gin against the raw bar. Strong; Iron Fish's farm-to-bottle character is a story-driven tower pairing for guests who want Michigan-geography depth.",
  "Seafood Tower|Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks": "Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit weight crowds the delicate shellfish — no acid to clean the brine. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Isaac Bowman Port Finish": "Isaac Bowman Port Finish's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Isaac Bowman Port Finish lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|J Davies Ferrington Vineyards": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards' silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the J Davies Ferrington Vineyards for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon": "J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon's Diamond Mountain Cab character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
