  "Seafood Tower|Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir": "Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis": "Burgundy Chablis — unoaked Chard with flint, chalk, lemon, green apple, lean precise. The clean mineral acidity meshes with brine across the tower and resets palate between oysters, shrimp, and crab. Strong classical Chablis for the seafood tower — textbook unoaked Chardonnay pairing.",
