  "Seafood Tower|Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon": "Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon's classical-Napa Cab elegance overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Joseph Mellot Sancerre": "Loire Sancerre — benchmark Sauv Blanc with grapefruit, chalk, herbs, tension finish. The tension-filled mineral meshes with brine across oysters, shrimp, crab, and lobster and resets palate between tower elements. Strong benchmark Sauv Blanc for the tower — Loire precision for the whole shellfish platter.",
  "Seafood Tower|Jubilation by Colgin": "Jubilation by Colgin's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Jubilation by Colgin on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Jung and Wulff Guyana": "Jung and Wulff Guyana's aged-rum register with molasses and oak depth overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit's weight is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Jung and Wulff Guyana for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Jung and Wulff Trinidad": "Jung and Wulff Trinidad's aged-rum register with molasses and oak depth overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit's weight is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Jung and Wulff Trinidad on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Kahlua": "Kahlua's sweet liqueur character smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sugar buries the delicate shellfish without any acid to balance. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Kahlua lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Kansas City": "Kansas City after the seafood tower -- the iced shellfish opens with cold-brine refresh, the 18oz strip following with clean savory grain that the tower's cool primed without crowding. Strong; the contrast in register reads composed.",
  "Seafood Tower|Keenan Chardonnay": "Keenan Chardonnay's bold apple-butter acidity holds steady against the tower's chilled shellfish — the crisp acidity lifts the shellfish without weight, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Seafood Tower|Keenan Mernet": "Keenan Mernet's herbaceous Cab Franc with red-fruit and bell-pepper overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Keenan Mernet lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye for the steak course.",
