  "Seafood Tower|Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye": "Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye's rye-spice character fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Knob Creek Rye": "Knob Creek Rye's rye-spice character crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Knob Creek Rye for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Komos Anejo Reserva": "Komos Anejo Reserva's aged-agave character smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- aged-agave register crowds the delicate shellfish frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Komos Anejo Reserva for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Komos Crystallino Anejo": "Komos Crystallino Anejo's crisp char-floral character holds steady against the tower's chilled shellfish — the añejo weight overshoots the delicate plate, and the floral edge frames the shellfish. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Seafood Tower|Komos Extra Anejo": "Komos Extra Anejo's aged-agave character smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- aged-agave register crowds the delicate shellfish frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Komos Extra Anejo belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Komos Rosa Reposado": "Komos Rosa Reposado's aged-agave character reads alongside the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the añejo register carries the seafood tower, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the starter. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Seafood Tower|Lagavulin 8": "Lagavulin 8's younger-Islay peat character drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Lagavulin 8 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Lail Vineyards Blueprint": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Lail Vineyards Blueprint on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée": "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Lalo Silver": "Lalo Silver with the seafood tower — additive-free craft across raw oysters, shrimp, lobster. Strong; the clean family-heritage character provides a craft through-line.",
  "Seafood Tower|Laphroaig 10": "Laphroaig 10's classic Islay peat crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Laphroaig 10 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seafood Tower|Larceny Small Batch": "Larceny Small Batch's Heaven Hill wheated caramel fights the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Larceny Small Batch for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé": "Pinot Noir Champagne rosé — silky structured mousse with strawberry, raspberry, and fresh cherry. The fine bubbles and red-berry complexity reset the palate between oysters, shrimp, and crab and elevate the whole shellfish platter. Peak sophisticated rosé Champagne for the seafood tower. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Seafood Tower|Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut": "Tours-sur-Marne Chardonnay-blend Champagne — precise and refined with green apple, lemon zest, whisper of brioche, and clean long finish. The vibrant acidity resets the palate between oysters, shrimp, crab, and lobster — sommelier's choice for the whole platter. Peak seafood tower Champagne. Gold standard; the recommendation that earns the regular.",
  "Seafood Tower|Le Garenne Rosé": "Loire rosé — Pinot Noir with strawberry, watermelon, floral, crisp dry. The fresh-fruit acid resets palate between oysters, shrimp, crab, and lobster and the berry-floral plays against brine across the platter. Strong summer rosé for the seafood tower — seasonal lightness for mixed shellfish.",
  "Seafood Tower|Le Ragnaie Brunello": "Le Ragnaie Brunello's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Le Ragnaie Brunello for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Le Volte dell'Ornellaia": "Le Volte dell'Ornellaia's Sangiovese-driven Tuscan acidity crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Le Volte dell'Ornellaia belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Lemon Lavender Gin Martini": "Plymouth gin, lemon, honey lavender syrup, Prosecco float. The floral-bright profile handles raw-bar spread and Prosecco's lift matches the tower's celebratory mood. Strong cocktail alternative to Champagne for the tower — especially for gin-curious guests.",
  "Seafood Tower|Les Pallières Raciné": "Les Pallières Raciné's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register overshadows the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Les Pallières Raciné belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Liberator Gin": "Liberator with the seafood tower — Ferndale Valentine craft against the raw bar. Strong; Liberator is a Michigan-pride tower pairing; Gray Whale's California ocean-botanicals is still the featured craft-tower match.",
  "Seafood Tower|Licor 43": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet liqueur on cold shellfish is wrong-course energy — too forward for a clean opener. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Licor 43 on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Limoncello": "Seafood Tower: this delicate seafood starter's briny-fresh sweetness meets this sweet cream liqueur's dessert-adjacent lushness. Liqueur sweetness or herbal complexity against a starter — wrong register typically. Works as a digestif move.",
  "Seafood Tower|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir's Willamette layered Pinot character crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Little Book": "Little Book's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Little Book for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Loaded Potato": "The seafood tower preceded by the loaded potato -- the bright register cleaves the heavy course, the table breathes. Works; safe opening pair, the meal builds without strain.",
  "Seafood Tower|Lobster Mac": "The seafood tower alongside the lobster mac -- both bring shellfish as the headline. Avoid; one is enough. Pair the seafood tower with Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut; pair the lobster mac with Cowboy Ribeye, Far Niente Chardonnay, or The Tomahawk.",
  "Seafood Tower|Loch Lomond 20 Year": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's complex 20yr aged Highland drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Loch Lomond 20 Year for the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Lock Stock & Barrel Rye": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye's rye-spice character drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Lock Stock & Barrel Rye on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Long Road Gin": "Long Road with the seafood tower — ultra-local Grand Rapids gin against the raw bar. Strong; Long Road is a GR-pride story-driven tower pairing.",
  "Seafood Tower|Los Vecinos Mezcal": "Los Vecinos Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- mezcal smoke is too forward for the table's opener. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a mezcal. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Los Vecinos Mezcal on the steak course instead.",
  "Seafood Tower|Louis XIII Cognac": "Louis XIII Cognac's luxury-icon cognac depth mis-pairs with the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- a luxury cognac is wrong moment for the opener — save it for after the meal. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an icon cognac. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Louis XIII Cognac belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Lucano Amaro": "Lucano Amaro's bitter-herb aperitivo edge overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- bitter aperitivo flattens the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; one of those is the move. Lucano Amaro belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seafood Tower|Lunaria Coste di Moro": "Lunaria Coste di Moro's red-fruit-and-spice elegance crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Lunaria Coste di Moro belongs on the steak course.",
