  "Seared Scallops|Eagle Rare 10 Year": "Eagle Rare 10 Year with seared scallops — the 10-year's oak buries scallop delicacy. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Eastern Kille Dry Gin": "Eastern Kille with seared scallops — juniper-forward Grand Rapids gin against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Eastern Kille's classic London Dry style lifts scallops with local-family-craft character.",
  "Seared Scallops|El Cabo": "El Cabo with seared scallops — craft reposado against caramelized scallop. The agave-forward character meets the sear with small-batch distinctiveness. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Seared Scallops|El Mayor Extra Anejo": "El Mayor Extra Anejo with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against aged El Mayor. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|El Mayor Reposado": "El Mayor Reposado with seared scallops — accessible reposado against caramelized scallop. The agave brightness picks up the scallop's sear cleanly. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Seared Scallops|Elephant Gin": "Elephant Gin with seared scallops — African-botanical craft gin against scallop sweetness. Excellent; baobab and buchu bring a savanna-herbal lift to scallops that no classic London Dry replicates.",
  "Seared Scallops|Elijah Craig 18 Year": "Elijah Craig 18 with seared scallops — aged HH against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Elijah Craig Private Barrel": "Elijah Craig Private Barrel with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against private-barrel single-barrel. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Elijah Craig Single Barrel": "Elijah Craig Single Barrel with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 94-proof single-barrel. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Seared Scallops|Elijah Craig Small Batch": "Elijah Craig Small Batch with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against small-batch. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Seared Scallops|Elijah Craig Straight Rye": "Elijah Craig Straight Rye with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 94-proof rye. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Elk Cove Five Mountain": "Chehalem Mountains Willamette Pinot — cherry, violet, clove, medium tannin. The medium tannin leaves room for scallop sweetness and the violet-clove plays against caramelized-exterior char. Strong step-up Pinot for scallops — structured Willamette on the delicate shellfish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Elk Cove Pinot Blanc": "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc — Willamette Oregon, soft pear, white peach, floral, refreshing acidity. The refreshing acid frames scallops' clean-seared sweetness and the pear-peach fruit adds lift against the pan-sear without overpowering. Peak medium-body white for scallops — sophisticated alternative to Chard.",
  "Seared Scallops|Elmer T. Lee": "Elmer T. Lee with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against namesake single-barrel. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Seared Scallops|Empress 1908 Gin": "Empress 1908 with seared scallops — BC butterfly-pea-flower gin against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Empress's floral-citrus profile mirrors scallop sweetness with distinctive BC-craft character.",
  "Seared Scallops|Epoch Ingenuity": "Never pair Epoch with seared scallops — smoked meat and crushed pepper overwhelm delicate sweet shellfish and the full body fights browned-butter. Lead with Clos de la Chapelle Chardonnay or Rombauer's creamy richness for sear-seared harmony.",
  "Seared Scallops|Escargot": "Escargot with the scallops -- the garlic-herb butter meets the caramelized scallop. Strong; reliable match across the courses.",
  "Seared Scallops|Espresso Martini": "Tito's, espresso, Grind Espresso Liqueur, Averna amaro, vanilla syrup, Angostura. Coffee-and-amaro weight annihilates scallops' delicate sweet-seared profile on every axis. Never pair — scallops demand crisp whites, French 75, or Vesper, not an espresso-based dessert cocktail.",
  "Seared Scallops|Espresso Old Fashioned": "Buffalo Trace, bourbon cream, Frangelico, espresso, brown sugar, Angostura. Dessert-weight cocktail annihilates the scallops' delicate sweetness; coffee and hazelnut have no hook into the clean seared profile. Never pair — scallops demand bright whites, not heavy coffee cocktails.",
  "Seared Scallops|Evening Land Seven Springs": "Eola-Amity Willamette Pinot — black cherry, smoked meat, dried rose, crushed stone, medium tannin. The smoked-meat plays against scallop sweetness and the crushed-stone frames caramelized-exterior char. Peak savory Pinot for scallops — Willamette depth on the delicate shellfish. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Seared Scallops|Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon": "Luxurious Oakville Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — opulent chocolate-espresso obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save Far Niente for the steak course where its best-cuts character peaks.",
  "Seared Scallops|Far Niente Chardonnay": "Napa Oakville Chardonnay — buttered citrus, toasted hazelnut, crème brûlée, velvety texture. The lush oak-butter echoes the scallops' pan-butter directly and the hazelnut adds depth against the pan-sear. Peak special-occasion Chardonnay for scallops — indulgence meets precision. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Seared Scallops|Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi": "Never pair Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi with seared scallops — Super Tuscan firm tannin and tobacco crush clean-seared shellfish and the graphite fights scallop sweetness. Lead with Raventós Cava, Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé. Route Saffredi to ribeye.",
  "Seared Scallops|Faust Napa Valley Cabernet": "Faust Napa Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — brooding tobacco-chocolate obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save Faust for the steak course where its value Napa structure peaks.",
  "Seared Scallops|Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía": "Never pair Fento Mencía with seared scallops — fresh red cherry and high acid still fight the delicate sweet shellfish and browned-butter richness. Lead with Clos de la Chapelle Chardonnay or Rombauer's creamy richness for sear-seared harmony.",
  "Seared Scallops|Fernet Branca": "Fernet Branca with seared scallops — saffron-menthol against scallop delicacy. Avoid; the power level is wrong.",
  "Seared Scallops|Fernet Menta": "Fernet Menta with seared scallops — mint bitter against scallop delicacy. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Fireball Whisky": "Fireball Whisky's sweet liqueur character smothers the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- sugar buries the delicate shellfish without any acid to balance. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a digestif. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Fireball Whisky lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seared Scallops|Fisher Unity Pinot Noir": "Sonoma Pinot — cranberry, red cherry, baking spice, silky. The soft tannin leaves room for scallop sweetness and the cherry-spice plays against caramelized-exterior char. Strong by-the-glass Pinot for scallops — California silk handles the delicate shellfish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Four Roses Small Batch Select": "Four Roses Small Batch Select with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 104-proof. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Four Roses Yellow Label": "Four Roses Yellow Label with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 80-proof bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Fox & Oden": "Fox & Oden with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against craft bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Fox & Oden Double Oaked": "Fox & Oden Double Oaked with seared scallops — Detroit-brand Double Oaked against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Frangelico": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Frangelico. Avoid; hazelnut-liqueur wrong for scallops. Reach for a light rum, vodka, or gin.",
  "Seared Scallops|Freemark Abbey Bosché": "Rutherford Bosché Cab against scallop sweetness — firm-tannin blackcurrant-graphite structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Freemark Abbey Bosché for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|French 75": "Inverroche gin, lemon, vanilla syrup, Prosecco top. The citrus-and-Prosecco profile meets scallops' clean sweet-seared character directly and the vanilla-softened gin doesn't crush the delicacy. Peak cocktail alternative to Champagne for scallops — shares the bubbles axis. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Seared Scallops|French Onion": "The scallops with the French onion -- the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness meets the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: umami plays against the protein, the table earns its depth. Works; both opening courses earn their place.",
  "Seared Scallops|Frias Block 5": "Frias Block 5 Spring Mountain Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — firm iron-herbal obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save Frias for the steak course where its single-block character peaks.",
  "Seared Scallops|G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo": "Classic Piedmont Barolo against scallop sweetness — Vajra's firm-tannin tar-rose structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Vajra for aged beef where the classic Barolo character earns the bottle.",
  "Seared Scallops|G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti": "The Maillard crust on a scallop produces caramelized, slightly sweet compounds that echo the Moscato's stone fruit character, while the wine's acidity keeps the natural oceanic brine from turning cloying. Together they read as a single continuous sweetness — one savory, one fruity — with a clean, bright finish. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Seared Scallops|G4 Blanco": "G4 Blanco with seared scallops — Felipe Camarena's craft blanco against caramelized scallop. The agave-forward character meets the sear with G4 distillery distinctiveness. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Seared Scallops|G4 High Proof": "G4 High Proof with seared scallops — bold agave against caramelized scallop. Strong; the 104-proof pushes against scallop sweetness; reach for Don Julio 70th for the refined scallop-reposado pairing.",
  "Seared Scallops|Garavogue Irish Whiskey": "Garavogue with seared scallops — Sligo-river craft Irish against scallop delicacy. Works; Garavogue's small-batch character sits alongside scallops at craft-Irish register.",
  "Seared Scallops|George T. Stagg": "George T. Stagg's cask-strength BTAC bourbon power smothers the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the George T. Stagg for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon": "Ghost Block Oakville Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — firm graphite-oak obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save Ghost Block for the steak course where its Oakville character peaks.",
  "Seared Scallops|Ghost Block Zinfandel": "Never pair Ghost Block with seared scallops — cracked pepper and jammy fruit overwhelm delicate sweet shellfish and the full body fights browned-butter. Lead with Clos de la Chapelle Chardonnay or Rombauer's creamy richness for sear-seared harmony.",
  "Seared Scallops|Glenfiddich 12": "Glenfiddich 12 with seared scallops — apple/pear Speyside against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Glenfiddich 14": "Glenfiddich 14 with seared scallops — Bourbon Barrel Reserve against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Glenfiddich 18": "Glenfiddich 18 with seared scallops — Oloroso + bourbon cask against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with seared scallops — Cuvée-cask Speyside against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Glenglassaugh 12": "Glenglassaugh 12 with seared scallops — coastal-tropical Highland against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Glenlivet 12": "Glenlivet 12 with seared scallops — honey-floral Speyside against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Glenmorangie 10": "Glenmorangie 10 with seared scallops — honey-floral Highland against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Glenmorangie 18": "Glenmorangie 18 with seared scallops — 18yr Highland against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Graham's 10 Year Tawny": "Graham's 10 Year Tawny's dessert-wine sweetness overwhelms the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- dessert sugar on cold shellfish is wrong direction — needs sparkling or Sancerre. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a dessert wine. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Graham's 10 Year Tawny belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Graham's 20 Year Tawny": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth clashes with the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Graham's 20 Year Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Graham's 2017 Vintage Port": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Gran Patron Platinum": "Gran Patron Platinum with seared scallops — triple-distilled premium Patron against caramelized scallop. The smooth concentrated agave frames the sear at the ultra-premium register. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Seared Scallops|Grand Marnier": "Grand Marnier's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- sweet liqueur on cold shellfish is wrong-course energy — too forward for a clean opener. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Grand Marnier for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Gray Whale Gin": "Gray Whale with seared scallops — California ocean-conservation gin against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Gray Whale's Mendocino-kombu-and-Big-Sur-juniper frames scallops with Pacific-coast-specific terroir.",
  "Seared Scallops|Green Chartreuse": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Green Chartreuse. Avoid; herbal-complex digestif wrong for scallops. Reach for a light rum, vodka, or gin.",
  "Seared Scallops|Grey Goose Vodka": "Grey Goose with seared scallops — soft French wheat vodka against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Goose's silkiness mirrors scallop richness at luxury register — where Tito's is round, Goose is silk.",
  "Seared Scallops|Grilled Caesar": "The scallops with the Caesar -- the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness meets the Caesar's charred-romaine and anchovy edge. Strong; the opening courses share the table at full register.",
  "Seared Scallops|Gumbo": "Seared Scallops and the gumbo together -- heat lifts the rich course, the table earns the warmer note. Works; the table opens with both, no clash either way.",
  "Seared Scallops|Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet": "Sonoma Rhinefarm Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — savory cedar-herb obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save Gundlach Bundschu for the steak course where its savory Sonoma character peaks.",
  "Seared Scallops|HDW 100 Vodka": "HDW 100 with seared scallops — 100-proof craft vodka against scallop sweetness. Excellent; HDW 100's extra backbone frames scallops with more lift than the 80-proof siblings — distinctive higher-proof craft character.",
  "Seared Scallops|Hakushu 12 Year": "Hakushu 12 with seared scallops — Japanese Alps lightly-peated single malt against scallop delicacy. Excellent; Hakushu's crisp-green + subtle peat is delicate enough to sit with scallops where most peated whiskies can't — Forest-Distillery lightness is the category advantage here.",
  "Seared Scallops|Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 88.9-proof BT single-barrel. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Seared Scallops|Hangar 1 Vodka": "Seared Scallops: scallop sweetness meets California craft from Alameda, blended grain + Viognier-grape distillate with distinctive floral lift. Hangar 1's grape-component floral character is the featured craft-vodka-scallop pairing — where Detroit City sits with and HDW 100 lifts, Hangar 1 floralizes the pairing with a register no other Craft Vodka touches. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Seared Scallops|Head Fake": "Wheatley vodka, limoncello, triple sec, lemon, simple syrup. The lemon-and-citrus profile meets scallops' clean-seared sweetness and Wheatley's wheat-based clean finish doesn't crush the delicacy. Peak bright-and-sweet cocktail for scallops when guest wants citrus over martini.",
  "Seared Scallops|Heaven Hill 20 Year": "Heaven Hill 20 Year with seared scallops — HH 20yr aged against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond": "Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against bonded weight. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Heaven's Door 10 Year": "Heaven's Door 10 Year with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against aged premium. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Heitz Martha's Vineyard": "Iconic Napa Cab against seared scallops' clean caramelized shellfish — Heitz's bold menthol-cedar signature obliterates the delicate sweet sear. Never pair. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc; save Martha's Vineyard for the Tomahawk or Porterhouse.",
  "Seared Scallops|Heitz Trailside Vineyard": "Heitz Trailside Rutherford Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — refined mint-cedar obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save Heitz Trailside for the steak course where its historic-house Rutherford character peaks.",
  "Seared Scallops|Hendricks Flora Adora": "Flora Adora with seared scallops — Spring-release floral Hendrick's against scallop sweetness. Strong; Flora Adora's lavish-floral mirrors scallop sweetness with distinctive garden character.",
  "Seared Scallops|Hendricks Gin": "Hendricks with seared scallops — flagship cucumber-rose gin against scallop sweetness. Strong; Hendrick's perfumed signature frames scallops at crowd-pleasing register.",
  "Seared Scallops|Hendricks Grand Cabaret": "Grand Cabaret with seared scallops — cocktail-culture fruit Hendrick's against scallop sweetness. Strong; Grand Cabaret's black-currant-and-rhubarb mirrors scallop sweetness at distinctive register.",
  "Seared Scallops|Hendricks Neptunia": "Neptunia with seared scallops — briny Hendrick's coastal release against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Neptunia's bladderwrack-seaweed profile mirrors scallop's marine origin distinctively.",
  "Seared Scallops|Hendricks Orbium": "Orbium with seared scallops — bitter-tonic Hendrick's against scallop sweetness. Strong; Orbium's quinine-wormwood cuts scallop sweetness with distinctive bitter-contrast.",
  "Seared Scallops|Hennessy Cognac": "Hennessy with seared scallops — VS/VSOP against scallop delicacy. Avoid; cognac oak-depth overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against aged bonded HH. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Hibiki Japanese Harmony": "Hibiki Harmony with seared scallops — refined Japanese blend against scallop delicacy. Excellent; Hibiki's elegant harmony frames scallops with premium Japanese-blend distinction — where Toki is gentle, Hibiki is refined.",
  "Seared Scallops|Honey Roasted Carrots": "The scallops and the honey carrots -- the savory course resolves into sugar, the meal closes with contrast. Works; the call holds whether the table sequences them or shares.",
  "Seared Scallops|House Wedge": "Seared Scallops alongside the wedge -- the caramelized sear plays against the cool wedge plate. Strong; the openers compose cleanly together.",
  "Seared Scallops|I.W. Harper 15 Year": "I.W. Harper 15 with seared scallops — BT-distilled 15yr against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Il Colle Prosecco Superiore": "Veneto Glera — floral Prosecco with white peach, green apple, crisp bubbles, and clean citrus finish. The light-bodied effervescence meets scallops' clean-seared sweetness without overpowering. Strong starter pour for scallops — though Champagne and high-acid whites peak higher on this pairing.",
  "Seared Scallops|Inhibited": "Tito's, Kahlúa, Bailey's, chocolate liqueur, espresso, chocolate-drizzled glass. Dessert cocktail crushes scallops' delicate sweet-seared profile; chocolate and coffee have no hook into clean seafood. Never pair — scallops demand crisp whites or French 75, not rich coffee cocktails.",
  "Seared Scallops|Inverroche Gin": "Inverroche with seared scallops — Western Cape fynbos-botanical gin against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Inverroche's floral lift mirrors scallop sweetness with South African-terroir distinction.",
  "Seared Scallops|Iron Fish Gin": "Iron Fish with seared scallops — northern-Michigan farm-to-bottle gin against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Iron Fish's Michigan-honey-and-estate-botanical profile frames scallops with distinctive farm-forward character.",
  "Seared Scallops|Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks": "Ironfish Bourbon Mezcal Casks with seared scallops — northern MI mezcal-cask against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Isaac Bowman Port Finish": "Isaac Bowman Port Finish with seared scallops — Sazerac-owned port-finish against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|J Davies Ferrington Vineyards": "Anderson Valley Pinot — dark cherry, blackberry, mocha, refined tannin. The refined tannin leaves room for scallop sweetness and the mocha plays against caramelized-exterior char. Strong Anderson Valley Pinot for scallops — concentrated Mendocino on the delicate shellfish.",
  "Seared Scallops|J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon": "J. Davies Diamond Mountain Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — firm graphite-mineral obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save J. Davies for the steak course where its mountain Schramsberg character peaks.",
  "Seared Scallops|Jack Daniel's 12 Year": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with seared scallops — 12yr aged Tennessee against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Tennessee overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Jack Daniel's Bonded": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with seared scallops — Bonded Tennessee against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Tennessee overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Jack Daniel's Old No. 7": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7 with seared scallops — Tennessee whiskey against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Tennessee overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Jack Daniel's Sinatra Select": "JD Sinatra Select with seared scallops — Sinatra Barrels Tennessee against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Tennessee overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Jameson Irish Whiskey": "Jameson with seared scallops — iconic entry Irish against scallop delicacy. Works; Jameson's smooth triple-distilled character is gentle enough to sit alongside scallops where heavier whiskies can't; not featured but the softest whisky option.",
  "Seared Scallops|Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir": "Russian River Pinot — red cherry, pomegranate, subtle earth, smooth, low tannin. The soft tannin leaves room for scallop sweetness and the subtle earth plays against caramelized-exterior char. Strong food-friendly Pinot for scallops — reliable pairing on the delicate shellfish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis": "Burgundy unoaked Chardonnay — flinty, chalky minerality with bright lemon and green apple. Lean and precise. The flint-chalk frames scallops' clean-seared sweetness and the lemon cuts the browned edge. Peak textbook Chablis for scallops — unoaked precision on the French classic. Gold standard; the headline call at the table.",
  "Seared Scallops|Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E.": "Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E. with seared scallops — master-blender tribute against scallop delicacy. Avoid; save the collector bottle.",
  "Seared Scallops|Jefferson's Ocean Voyage 23": "Jefferson's Ocean Voyage 23 with seared scallops — Voyage #23 against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops even with ocean-finish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Jefferson's Reserve": "Jefferson's Reserve with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against blended oak. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Jefferson's Reserve VR Twin Oak": "Jefferson's Reserve VR Twin Oak with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against double-barrel oak. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Jim Beam Black Label": "Jim Beam Black Label with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against aged Beam. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Jim Beam White Label": "Jim Beam White Label with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 80-proof. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Seared Scallops|Johnnie Walker Black": "JW Black with seared scallops — 12yr balanced JW against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Johnnie Walker Blue": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character crowds out the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- bourbon depth is wrong for the table's opening course. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a scotch. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Johnnie Walker Blue for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Johnnie Walker Red": "JW Red with seared scallops — peat-influenced JW against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon": "Elegant Sonoma Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — fine-tannin cedar-mint obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save Jordan for the steak course where its refined Alexander Valley balance peaks.",
  "Seared Scallops|Joseph Mellot Sancerre": "Loire Sancerre — benchmark Sauv Blanc, crisp and refined with white grapefruit, chalk, fresh herbs, tension-filled finish. The tension-filled mineral backbone frames scallops' clean-seared sweetness and the herbs play against the pan-sear. Peak Sancerre for scallops — textbook French-on-French pairing. Gold standard; the recommendation that earns the regular.",
  "Seared Scallops|Jubilation by Colgin": "Cult Napa Cab blend against scallop sweetness — Jubilation's firm-tannin Colgin structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Jubilation for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Jung and Wulff Guyana": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Jung and Wulff Guyana. Avoid; wooden-still weight wrong for scallops. Reach for a light rum, vodka, or gin.",
  "Seared Scallops|Jung and Wulff Trinidad": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Jung and Wulff Trinidad. Avoid; aged-rum weight wrong for scallops. Reach for a light rum, vodka, or gin.",
  "Seared Scallops|Kahlua": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Kahlua. Avoid; coffee-liqueur weight wrong for scallops. Reach for a light rum, vodka, or gin.",
  "Seared Scallops|Keenan Chardonnay": "Napa Chardonnay with apple and lemon, softer oak presence than Far Niente. Same function, lighter footprint — less oak means the scallop's caramelized exterior gets room. Pitch when the guest wants Napa Chard but not the fullest version. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Seared Scallops|Keenan Mernet": "Spring Mountain Napa Mernet against scallop sweetness — mountain-grown Merlot-Cab structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Keenan Mernet for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 10-year KO. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Seared Scallops|Kentucky Owl Confiscated": "Kentucky Owl Confiscated with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against KO Confiscated. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's": "Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's with seared scallops — luxury American-Irish crossover against scallop delicacy. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for scallops — save the collector bottle.",
  "Seared Scallops|Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône": "Never pair Kermit Lynch Rhône with seared scallops — pepper and garrigue overwhelm delicate sweet shellfish and the medium body clashes with browned-butter. Lead with Clos de la Chapelle Chardonnay or Rombauer's creamy richness for sear-seared harmony.",
  "Seared Scallops|Ketel One Vodka": "Ketel One with seared scallops — clean Nolet-family wheat against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Ketel's crispness frames the scallop cleanly — neither rounded nor silky, just precise.",
  "Seared Scallops|Knickerbocker Gin": "Knickerbocker with seared scallops — hop-forward Holland MI gin against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Knickerbocker's brewer's-heritage bitter-hop notes frame scallops with distinctive contemporary character.",
  "Seared Scallops|Knob Creek": "Knob Creek with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 100-proof bourbon. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Knob Creek 12 Year": "Knob Creek 12 Year with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against aged 100-proof. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Seared Scallops|Knob Creek 15 Year": "Knob Creek 15 with seared scallops — aged Beam KC against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Knob Creek 18 Year": "Knob Creek 18 with seared scallops — 18yr Beam KC against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye": "Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against blended depth. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Knob Creek Rye": "Knob Creek Rye with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 100-proof rye. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Komos Anejo Reserva": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Komos Anejo Reserva. Avoid; wine-cask-finished añejo too heavy for scallops. Save the bottle — reach for a blanco, light rum, or vodka.",
  "Seared Scallops|Komos Crystallino Anejo": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Komos Crystallino. Avoid; crystallino-filtered añejo complexity wrong for scallops. Save the bottle — reach for a blanco, light rum, or vodka.",
  "Seared Scallops|Komos Extra Anejo": "Komos Extra Añejo with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against aged Komos. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Komos Rosa Reposado": "Komos Rosa Reposado with seared scallops — wine-cask rosé against caramelized scallop. The strawberry and cherry in the finish play with the scallop's sear; a wine-cask-reposado standout. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Seared Scallops|Lagavulin 8": "Lagavulin 8 with seared scallops — seared seafood's delicate sweetness gets buried by peat. The 8-year isn't as aggressive as Laphroaig but still too much for scallops. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Lail Vineyards Blueprint": "Historically-pedigreed Napa Cab against scallop sweetness — Blueprint's full-body structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Blueprint for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée": "Historically-significant Napa Cab against scallop sweetness — Daniel Cuvée's firm-tannin graphite-cassis structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Daniel Cuvée for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Lalo Silver": "Lalo Silver with seared scallops — Lalo González's additive-free craft against caramelized scallop. The clean family-heritage blanco frames the sear at the craft register. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Seared Scallops|Laphroaig 10": "Laphroaig 10 with scallops — seared seafood's clean caramelized sweetness cannot survive Laphroaig's phenolic wall. Absolute miss; avoid. Avoid; pair this elsewhere on the menu.",
  "Seared Scallops|Larceny Small Batch": "Larceny Small Batch with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against wheated. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé": "Tours-sur-Marne Pinot Noir rosé Champagne — benchmark rosé, silky mousse, red berry notes, long elegant finish. The strawberry-raspberry complexity frames scallops' clean-seared sweetness and the fine bubbles refresh the browned edge. Peak rosé Champagne for scallops — elegance-on-elegance pairing. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Seared Scallops|Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut": "Tours-sur-Marne Chardonnay-blend Champagne — precise green apple and lemon zest, whisper of brioche, clean long finish. The vibrant acidity frames scallops' sweet-seared profile and the mineral precision cuts the browned edge. Peak Champagne for scallops — elegance-on-elegance pairing. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Seared Scallops|Le Garenne Rosé": "Le Garenne Rosé — Loire Pinot Noir with strawberry, watermelon, light floral, crisp dry. The fresh-fruit acid frames scallops' clean-seared sweetness and the delicate berry adds lift against the pan-sear. Peak summer rosé for scallops — seasonal lightness meets sweet shellfish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Le Ragnaie Brunello": "Italy's-most-prestigious Brunello against scallop sweetness — Le Ragnaie's firm-tannin tobacco-leather structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Le Ragnaie for Bone-In Filet, Tomahawk, or Porterhouse.",
  "Seared Scallops|Le Volte dell'Ornellaia": "Tuscan Merlot-driven blend against seared scallops' clean sweet sear — Le Volte's dark-fruit and Italian tannin are wrong-footed against delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc; save Le Volte for the steak course or hearty pasta.",
  "Seared Scallops|Lemon Lavender Gin Martini": "Plymouth gin, lemon, honey lavender syrup, Prosecco float. The cocktail's floral-bright profile meets scallops' clean-seared sweetness directly; honey softens and Prosecco adds lift. Peak floral-martini pairing for scallops — sophistication with approachability.",
  "Seared Scallops|Les Pallières Raciné": "Never pair Raciné with seared scallops — garrigue, iron, and earthy mineral overwhelm delicate sweet shellfish and the medium tannin fights browned-butter. Lead with Clos de la Chapelle Chardonnay or Rombauer's creamy richness for sear-seared harmony.",
  "Seared Scallops|Liberator Gin": "Liberator with seared scallops — 100% Michigan-grain craft gin against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Liberator's smooth hometown profile frames scallops at Michigan-pride register.",
  "Seared Scallops|Licor 43": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character smothers the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- sugar buries the delicate shellfish without any acid to balance. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Licor 43 on the steak course instead.",
  "Seared Scallops|Limoncello": "Seared Scallops: this delicate seafood starter's briny-fresh sweetness meets this sweet cream liqueur's dessert-adjacent lushness. Liqueur sweetness or herbal complexity against a starter — wrong register typically. Works as a digestif move.",
  "Seared Scallops|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Willamette Pinot — dark cherry, forest floor, spice, medium body, low tannin. The soft tannin leaves room for scallop sweetness and the cherry-spice plays against caramelized-exterior char. Peak by-the-glass Pinot for scallops — textbook delicate-red-with-sweet-shellfish pairing. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Seared Scallops|Little Book": "Little Book with seared scallops — Beam blended cask-strength against scallop delicacy. Avoid; barrel-proof wrong for scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Loaded Potato": "The scallops preceded by the loaded potato -- cream meets protein, the meal builds with weight. Works; safe opening pair, the meal builds without strain.",
  "Seared Scallops|Lobster Mac": "The scallops and the lobster mac -- shellfish-on-shellfish, the meal goes redundant. Avoid; the table reads heavy without payoff. Suggest Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre for the scallops, or Cowboy Ribeye, Far Niente Chardonnay, or The Tomahawk for the lobster mac.",
  "Seared Scallops|Loch Lomond 20 Year": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with seared scallops — aged complex Highland against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Lock Stock & Barrel Rye": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against sourced rye. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Long Road Gin": "Long Road with seared scallops — Grand Rapids estate gin against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Long Road's Michigan-botanical profile frames scallops at hometown register.",
  "Seared Scallops|Los Vecinos Mezcal": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Los Vecinos. Avoid; traditional smoke wrong for scallops. Reach for a vodka or gin.",
  "Seared Scallops|Louis XIII Cognac": "Louis XIII Cognac's luxury-icon cognac depth mis-pairs with the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- a luxury cognac is wrong moment for the opener — save it for after the meal. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not an icon cognac. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Louis XIII Cognac for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Lucano Amaro": "Lucano with seared scallops — floral-anise amaro against scallop delicacy. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Lunaria Coste di Moro": "Rustic Abruzzo Montepulciano against scallop sweetness — Lunaria's earthy grip buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Lunaria for the steak course or rustic Italian pairings.",
  "Seared Scallops|Macallan 12 Sherry": "Macallan 12 Sherry with seared scallops — Oloroso-cask Speyside against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Macallan 18": "Macallan 18 with seared scallops — 18yr Oloroso-cask Speyside against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Macallan Estate": "Macallan Estate with seared scallops — Estate-grown-oak Macallan against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Macauley Petite Syrah": "Never pair Macauley with seared scallops — dense tannin and black pepper overwhelm delicate sweet shellfish and the full body fights browned-butter sweetness. Lead with Clos de la Chapelle Chardonnay or Rombauer's creamy richness for sear-seared harmony.",
  "Seared Scallops|Macauley Pinot Noir": "Sonoma Pinot — bright strawberry, red cherry, light floral, soft tannins, light body. The soft tannin leaves room for scallop sweetness and the red cherry plays against caramelized-exterior char. Strong accessible Pinot for scallops — Macauley on the delicate shellfish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Macauley Stagecoach Vineyard": "Macauley Stagecoach Atlas Peak Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — powerful iron-espresso obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save Macauley for the steak course where its Stagecoach character peaks.",
  "Seared Scallops|Mahon Gin": "Mahón with seared scallops — Menorcan PDO juniper-heavy Mediterranean gin against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Mahón's Spanish-island terroir frames scallops with Mediterranean sharpness.",
  "Seared Scallops|Maker's Mark": "Maker's Mark with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against iconic wheated. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Maker's Mark Cellar Aged": "Maker's Mark Cellar Aged with seared scallops — aged oak against scallop caramelized sweetness is a mismatch. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Seared Scallops|Malibu Rum": "Malibu Rum's light-rum register with cane and citrus lift mis-pairs with the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- this light spirit's register is wrong for the starter — try a different pour. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a light spirit. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Malibu Rum belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye": "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 16-year Michigan. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Seared Scallops|Marc Brédif Chinon": "Marc Brédif Chinon's herbaceous Cab Franc with red-fruit and bell-pepper crowds out the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Marc Brédif Chinon for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Margarita": "Corazon Blanco, lemon, lime, orange, Cointreau. The triple-citrus structure meets scallops' clean-seared sweetness and the blanco's agave profile cuts without crushing delicacy. Peak Margarita pairing for scallops — bright, clean, and doesn't overwhelm the dish. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Seared Scallops|Marimar Estate Christina": "Russian River Green Valley Pinot — ripe strawberry, cherry compote, warm spice, silky. The soft tannin leaves room for scallop sweetness and the warm-spice plays against caramelized-exterior char. Strong plush Pinot for scallops — Russian River silk on the delicate shellfish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Mata Hari Absinthe": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Mata Hari Absinthe. Avoid; wormwood-absinthe wrong for scallops. Reach for a light rum, vodka, or gin.",
  "Seared Scallops|Michter's 10 Year Bourbon": "Michter's 10 Bourbon with seared scallops — Michter's allocated 10yr against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Michter's 10 Year Rye": "Michter's 10 Year Rye with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 10-year premium. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Michter's US*1 Rye": "Michter's US*1 Rye with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 84.8-proof rye. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Seared Scallops|Mijenta Blanco": "Mijenta Blanco with seared scallops — additive-free craft blanco against caramelized scallop. The clean highland agave frames the sear with premium craft integrity. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Seared Scallops|Milagro Anejo": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Milagro Anejo. Avoid; aged-agave heavy for scallops. Reach for a blanco, light rum, or vodka.",
  "Seared Scallops|Milagro Reposado": "Milagro Reposado with seared scallops — modern clean reposado against caramelized scallop. The triple-distilled clarity frames the scallop cleanly. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Seared Scallops|Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey": "Mister Sam with seared scallops — Mister Sam tribute blend against scallop delicacy. Avoid; whiskey overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Mocha Creme": "The scallops alongside the mocha creme -- the entree yields to the dessert, the meal arc reads on-key. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Seared Scallops|Monkey 47 Gin": "Monkey 47 with seared scallops — Black Forest craft gin against scallop sweetness. Excellent; the 47-botanical complexity frames scallops with Schwarzwald layered character.",
  "Seared Scallops|Monkey Shoulder": "Monkey Shoulder with seared scallops — triple-Speyside-malt blend against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Montenegro Amaro": "Montenegro with seared scallops — amaro against scallop delicacy. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Mount Gay Rum": "Seared Scallops: scallop delicacy meets Mount Gay. Excellent; the Barbados-tradition character frames scallops at heritage register — the character-forward option vs. Bacardi's clean-neutral.",
  "Seared Scallops|Muga Reserva": "Never pair Muga with seared scallops — vanilla-oak and leather overwhelm delicate sweet shellfish and the savory finish clashes with browned-butter. Lead with Clos de la Chapelle Chardonnay or Rombauer's creamy richness for sear-seared harmony.",
  "Seared Scallops|Mushroom Bisque": "Seared Scallops alongside the mushroom bisque -- protein and umami share the plate, the build reads weighty and clean. Works; the openers share the table cleanly, sequence or share.",
  "Seared Scallops|Mushrooms": "The scallops opens the meal, the mushrooms with the entree -- the rare-center scallop plays against the mushrooms. Strong; both items.",
  "Seared Scallops|Myers's Rum": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Myers's. Avoid; dark-rum weight overwhelms scallops. Reach for a light rum, vodka, or gin.",
  "Seared Scallops|Negroni": "Gin, Contratto, Campari. The bitter-orange and herbal weight obliterates the scallops' delicate sweet-seared profile; Campari has no hook into clean seafood. Never pair — scallops demand crisp whites, French 75, or Vesper, not bitter structure.",
  "Seared Scallops|Never Say Die Rye": "Never Say Die Rye with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against UK-aged rye. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Seared Scallops|Never Say Die Small Batch": "Never Say Die Small Batch with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against UK-aged. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Seared Scallops|New Holland Beer Barrel Bourbon": "New Holland Beer Barrel Bourbon with seared scallops — Holland MI beer-barrel against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|New York Sour": "Jameson, lemon, simple, egg white, Daou Cab float. The Cab float's tannic red-wine character crushes the scallops' delicate sweetness despite the lemon brightness; the cocktail wasn't built for fine seafood. Never pair — scallops demand whites or Champagne, not a red-wine-topped sour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Nickel & Nickel Cabernet": "Nickel & Nickel Oakville Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — concentrated graphite-cassis obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save Nickel & Nickel for the steak course where its prestige Oakville character peaks.",
  "Seared Scallops|Nolets Dry Gin": "Nolet's with seared scallops — Turkish rose/peach/raspberry Dutch gin against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Nolet's fruit-forward floral profile mirrors scallop sweetness distinctively — the contemporary-gin pairing no British London Dry replicates.",
  "Seared Scallops|Not a Paper Plane": "Bulleit bourbon, Nonino amaro, Aperol, Angostura — stirred. Spirit-forward amaro-bourbon obliterates scallops' delicate sweet-seared profile; Nonino's bitterness has no hook into clean seafood. Never pair — scallops demand crisp whites, French 75, or Vesper.",
  "Seared Scallops|Oban 14": "Oban 14 with seared scallops — coastal Highland against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Oban 18": "Oban 18 with seared scallops — aged maritime Highland against scallop delicacy. Avoid; Scotch overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Ocho Anejo": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Ocho Anejo. Avoid; aged-agave heavy for scallops. Reach for a blanco, light rum, or vodka.",
  "Seared Scallops|Odette Cabernet Sauvignon": "Odette Stags Leap Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — velvet-glove sage-cedar obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save Odette for the steak course where its refined Stags Leap character peaks.",
  "Seared Scallops|Old Elk Cigar Cut": "Old Elk Cigar Cut with seared scallops — Old Elk cigar-paired against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Old Emmer": "Old Emmer with seared scallops — wheated bourbon against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Old Fitzgerald 7 Year": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 100-proof. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Seared Scallops|Old Fitzgerald 9 Year": "Old Fitzgerald 9 Year with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 9-year wheated. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Seared Scallops|Old Grand-Dad 16 Year": "OGD 16 with seared scallops — aged high-rye OGD against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Opus One": "Collector Napa Cab blend against scallop sweetness — Opus One's firm-tannin Bordeaux blend buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Opus One for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Our Lady of Guadalupe Acolytes": "Willamette Trappist Monastery Chardonnay — rich ripe pear, butterscotch, toasted oak. The rich butterscotch-oak aligns with scallops' pan-sear and the pear frames the sweet shellfish. Peak Oregon Chardonnay for scallops — provenance hook plus opulent match on the classic. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Seared Scallops|Pablo Sour": "Reposado tequila, lemon, vanilla syrup, egg white. The foam carries vanilla-and-lemon aromatics on every sip and meets scallops' clean-seared sweetness without crushing delicacy. Peak textural cocktail for scallops — both dishes lead with silky, clean profiles.",
  "Seared Scallops|Paloma": "Seared Scallops: this delicate seafood starter's briny-fresh sweetness meets this bright tequila cocktail's citrus lift and agave backbone. Light cocktail and delicate starter share the same register — fresh opener. A headliner match — context-driven peak. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Seared Scallops|Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character smothers the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with seared scallops — collector cask-strength against scallop delicacy. Avoid; barrel-proof wrong for scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Patron Anejo": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Patron Anejo. Avoid; aged-agave heavy for scallops. Reach for a blanco, light rum, or vodka.",
  "Seared Scallops|Patron Silver": "Patron Silver with seared scallops — Patron's iconic silver against caramelized scallop. The clean citrus-forward profile meets the sear at the approachable everyday register; the globally-familiar blanco-seafood pour. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Seared Scallops|Patron XO Cafe": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Patron XO Cafe. Avoid; coffee-liqueur wrong for scallops. Reach for a light rum, vodka, or gin.",
  "Seared Scallops|Paul Bara Grand Rosé Brut": "Bouzy Grand Cru grower Champagne — structured Pinot Noir rosé with ripe raspberry, red currant, and mineral finish. The Burgundian weight frames scallops' clean-seared sweetness and the red-fruit depth elevates the pan-sear. Peak serious rosé Champagne for scallops — depth meets precision. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Seared Scallops|Peanut Butter Brownie": "The scallops and the PB brownie -- the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness bookends with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Seared Scallops|Peju Cabernet Sauvignon": "Peju Rutherford Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — elegant dusty-cocoa obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save Peju for the steak course where its refined Rutherford character peaks.",
  "Seared Scallops|Pierre Ferrand Cognac": "Pierre Ferrand with seared scallops — Grande Champagne 1er Cru against scallop delicacy. Avoid; cognac overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut": "Pierre Gimonnet Special Club — 2015 Côte des Blancs Chardonnay. Layered citrus zest, toasted brioche, white flowers, creamy texture. The vintage depth frames scallops' clean-seared sweetness and the creamy mouthfeel echoes the pan-butter. Peak prestige Champagne for scallops. Gold standard; pour without second-guessing.",
  "Seared Scallops|Pikesville Rye": "Pikesville Rye with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 110-proof. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Pineau des Charentes": "Cognac-region fortified — Pineau des Charentes in aperitif mode, grape juice plus young Cognac oak-aged, white grape, honey, warm nutty Cognac. The honey plays with browned-butter sweet sear and the white grape lifts delicate shellfish. Strong Pineau for seared scallops — aperitif mode on the delicate cut.",
  "Seared Scallops|Pio Cesare Barbaresco": "Approachable-Barolo-sibling Barbaresco against scallop sweetness — Pio Cesare's firm-tannin tar structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Pio Cesare for aged beef where Barbaresco elegance earns the bottle.",
  "Seared Scallops|Plymouth Gin": "Plymouth with seared scallops — softer English gin against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Plymouth's earthier juniper and sweet notes mirror scallop richness — less aggressive than Tanq, more textural than Beefeater.",
  "Seared Scallops|Poderi Aldo Conterno Nebbiolo": "Serious-Barolo Aldo Conterno against scallop sweetness — decade-built firm tannin and tar structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Aldo Conterno for Tomahawk, Porterhouse, or Bone-In Filet where prestige earns the bottle.",
  "Seared Scallops|Pommery Cuvée Louise": "2004 Pommery Cuvée Louise — 20-year vintage Champagne. Toasted almond, dried apricot, honey, brioche-rich palate. The aged complexity frames scallops' clean-seared sweetness and the almond-honey echoes the pan-butter. Peak occasion Champagne for scallops — vintage-on-vintage moment, treat it accordingly. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Seared Scallops|Porterhouse": "The porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character overwhelms the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness: the bold beefy character obliterates the scallops, and the dual strip-and-filet drowns out the seared-rare scallop plate. Avoid; the courses can't share a meal cleanly. Pair the scallops with Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre on a different visit; pour Odette Cabernet Sauvignon, Weller 12 Year, or Domaine du Grand Tinel alongside the porterhouse.",
  "Seared Scallops|Prime Tartare": "Prime Tartare with the scallops -- the caper-and-shallot edge holds with the sweet scallop plate. Strong; reliable match across the courses.",
  "Seared Scallops|Quilt Cabernet Sauvignon": "Quilt Napa Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — lush chocolate-vanilla obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save Quilt for the steak course where its polished Napa character peaks.",
  "Seared Scallops|RAEN Royal St Robert": "Fort Ross-Seaview Sonoma Coast Pinot — sea-influenced, red cherry, cranberry, wild strawberry, crushed rock, silky. The sea-bred minerality echoes scallop sweetness and the crushed-rock frames caramelized-exterior char. Peak Burgundian California Pinot for scallops — sea-influenced Pinot for sea-sourced shellfish. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Seared Scallops|Raventós Cava de NIT Rosé Brut": "Catalan Cava rosé — dry blend with wild strawberry, raspberry, mineral spine, saline finish. The saline cuts scallops' clean-seared edge and the berry frames the sweet pan-sear. Strong Cava-with-scallops pairing — food-friendly sophistication at accessible price point.",
  "Seared Scallops|Redbreast 12 Year": "Redbreast 12 with seared scallops — single pot still Irish against scallop delicacy. Works; Redbreast 12's pot still richness is heavier for scallops than Jameson's smoothness, but still lighter than most whiskies.",
  "Seared Scallops|Redbreast 21 Year": "Redbreast 21 with seared scallops — 21yr aged pot still Irish against scallop delicacy. Works; Redbreast 21's aged pot still is heavy for scallops — save the collector bottle.",
  "Seared Scallops|Remus 15 Year Gatsby Reserve": "Remus 15 Gatsby with seared scallops — high-rye MGP 15yr against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Remy VSOP Cognac": "Rémy VSOP with seared scallops — premium cognac against scallop delicacy. Avoid; cognac overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Rey Sol Anejo": "Rey Sol Anejo with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against sun-bottle aged. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Reyka Vodka": "Reyka with seared scallops — Icelandic vodka, lava-filtered glacial water, wheat-and-barley. Excellent; Reyka's mineral character is the distinctive match for scallops — the oceanic pairing where the glacial profile echoes the fish's origin. Gold standard; the recommendation that earns the regular.",
  "Seared Scallops|Rishi's Old Antique": "Rishi's Old Antique with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against retailer-label. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Seared Scallops alongside the chickpea soup -- the seared scallops plays against the chickpea soup, and the baking spice plays against the grilled char. Strong; the openers compose cleanly together.",
  "Seared Scallops|Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs — Le Mesnil Grand Cru blanc de blancs with chalky minerality, lemon curd, green apple, and no dosage. The austere precision frames scallops' clean-seared sweetness and the chalk adds dimension against the pan-sear. Peak sommelier Champagne for scallops. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Seared Scallops|Roku Gin": "Roku with seared scallops — Suntory Japanese gin, 6 Japanese botanicals (sakura flower, sakura leaf, yuzu peel, sencha tea, gyokuro tea, sansho pepper). Excellent; Roku's yuzu-and-sansho profile is the featured Japanese-gin-scallop pairing — yuzu lifts scallop sweetness like the classic sashimi move, and sansho pepper adds distinctive finish no Western gin replicates.",
  "Seared Scallops|Ron Zacapa Rum": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Ron Zacapa. Avoid; dark-rum weight overwhelms scallops. Reach for a light rum, vodka, or gin.",
  "Seared Scallops|Russell's Reserve 10 Year": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against aged Wild Turkey. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Sambuca": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Sambuca. Avoid; anise liqueur wrong for scallops. Reach for a light rum, vodka, or gin.",
  "Seared Scallops|San Simeon Stormwatch": "Paso Cab-dominant Bordeaux blend against scallop sweetness — full-body mocha-cherry structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Stormwatch for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir": "Sta. Rita Hills Santa Barbara Pinot — rich, layered, dark cherry, earth, dried herbs, medium tannin. The medium tannin leaves room for scallop sweetness and the dark cherry plays against caramelized-exterior char. Peak legendary-vineyard Pinot for scallops — Santa Barbara finesse on delicate shellfish. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Seared Scallops|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "The scallops and the garlic spinach on different courses -- the starter opens, the side rides with the entrée. Strong; the meal builds cleanly.",
  "Seared Scallops|Sauternes Glass": "Sauternes Glass' dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Sauternes Glass lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Seared Scallops|Sazerac": "Sazerac rye, Peychaud's, sugar, absinthe-rinsed glass. Spirit-forward weight obliterates the scallops' delicate sweetness and the anise edge clashes with clean seared seafood. Never pair — scallops demand crisp whites or Champagne, not classic rye cocktails.",
  "Seared Scallops|Sazerac Rye": "Sazerac Rye with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 90-proof rye. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Scapegrace Fortuna": "Scapegrace Fortuna with seared scallops — New Zealand single malt against scallop delicacy. Avoid; single malt overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Scavino Barolo": "King-of-Italian Barolo against scallop sweetness — Scavino's powerful firm-tannin tar-leather structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Scavino for Bone-In Filet or Tomahawk where the prestige earns the bottle.",
  "Seared Scallops|Schloss Vollrads Riesling": "Rheingau Riesling — apricot, white peach, petrol, lively acid, off-dry. The off-dry acidity frames scallops' clean-seared sweetness and the apricot-peach fruit adds complexity against the pan-sear. Peak German Riesling for scallops — 700-year estate provenance, fruit-and-acid precision. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Seared Scallops|Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters": "By-the-glass California Cab against scallop sweetness — full-body cassis-chocolate structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Lost Chapters for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Seafood Tower": "The seafood tower and the scallops -- shellfish-on-shellfish, the meal goes redundant. Avoid; the table reads heavy without payoff. Suggest Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut for the seafood tower, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre for the scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Seasonal Soup": "Seared Scallops and the seasonal soup together -- the seared scallops threads the house bowl. Strong; both openers earn their place on the meal.",
  "Seared Scallops|Seasonal Vegetables": "The scallops opens the meal, the seasonal vegetables with the entree -- the rare-center scallop wraps the rotating-vegetable side. Strong; the meal builds cleanly.",
  "Seared Scallops|Sesti Brunello di Montalcino": "Never pair Sesti with seared scallops — firm tannin and sandalwood earth overwhelm the delicate sweet shellfish and the high acid fights the browned-butter. Lead with Clos de la Chapelle Chardonnay or Rombauer's creamy richness for sear-seared harmony.",
  "Seared Scallops|Shafer 1.5": "Stags Leap Shafer Cab against scallop sweetness — 1.5's opulent blackberry-mocha structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Shafer 1.5 for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Shafer Hillside Select": "Stags Leap collector's Cab against scallop sweetness — Hillside Select's firm-tannin dense structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Hillside Select for the steak course where the 32-month oak and graphite earn the bottle.",
  "Seared Scallops|Shrimp Bisque": "The scallops and the shrimp bisque -- both shellfish-forward, the table doubles up on shellfish. Avoid; pick one or the other. Pair the scallops with Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre; pair the shrimp bisque with Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay.",
  "Seared Scallops|Shrimp Cocktail": "The scallops and the shrimp cocktail -- shellfish-on-shellfish, the meal goes redundant. Avoid; the table reads heavy without payoff. Suggest Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre for the scallops, or Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut for the shrimp cocktail.",
  "Seared Scallops|Siete Leguas Blanco": "Siete Leguas Blanco with seared scallops — tahona-crushed traditional against caramelized scallop. The rustic agave meets the sear in a distinct register from polished blancos. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Seared Scallops|Siete Leguas Reposado": "Siete Leguas Reposado with seared scallops — rustic agave against caramelized scallop. The traditional craft character meets the sear in a different register than filtered or balanced reposados. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Seared Scallops|Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon": "American-oak Alexander Valley Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — lush vanilla-dill obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save Silver Oak for the steak course where its American-oak signature peaks.",
  "Seared Scallops|Simon Family Estate Reserve": "Boutique Napa estate Cab against scallop sweetness — Estate Reserve's firm-tannin plum-cassis structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Estate Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Spottswoode Lyndenhurst": "Organic Napa Cab against scallop sweetness — Lyndenhurst's full-body plum-violet structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Lyndenhurst for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|St Supéry Cabernet Sauvignon": "St Supéry Napa Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — full-body mocha-tannin obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, Pinot Blanc, or rosé and save St Supéry for the steak course where the Rutherford Cab character peaks.",
  "Seared Scallops|St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc": "Napa Dollarhide Sauvignon Blanc — lemon, grapefruit, gooseberry, clean lively finish. The lively acid frames scallops' clean-seared sweetness and the lemon-grapefruit lifts the pan-sear. Peak Napa Sauv Blanc for scallops — rounder than NZ, brighter than Chardonnay, bridges both worlds. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Seared Scallops|St Supéry Élu Meritage": "Napa Meritage against scallop sweetness — firm-tannin five-varietal structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Élu for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Stagg Jr. Batch #15": "Stagg Jr. Batch #15 with seared scallops — BT cask-strength against scallop delicacy. Avoid; barrel-proof wrong for scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Stoli Elit Vodka": "Stoli Elit with seared scallops — ultra-premium Russian wheat against scallop sweetness. Excellent; the crystalline cleanness frames scallops with top-shelf precision — no textural softness, just pure lift.",
  "Seared Scallops|Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc": "Marlborough Sauvignon Blanc — passionfruit, grapefruit, fresh-cut grass, zesty acidity. The zesty acid frames scallops' clean-seared sweetness and the tropical-citrus adds lift against the pan-sear. Peak approachable NZ Sauv Blanc for scallops — bright by-the-glass pour for the classic pairing. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Seared Scallops|Tanq 10 Gin": "Tanq 10 with seared scallops — Tanqueray No. Ten, small-batch premium, whole-citrus-distilled (grapefruit, orange, lime) + chamomile. Excellent; Tanq 10's fresh-citrus lift is the distinctive gin-scallop pairing — where Tanq flagship leads with juniper proof, Tanq 10 leads with bright citrus that mirrors scallop sweetness.",
  "Seared Scallops|Tanqueray Gin": "Tanqueray with seared scallops — juniper icon against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Tanq's 47.3% proof and angelica-coriander-licorice botanical spine cut scallop richness where Plymouth's softer character just accompanies.",
  "Seared Scallops|Taylor Fladgate Tawny": "Taylor Fladgate Tawny's classic tawny with caramel-nut sweetness clashes with the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Taylor Fladgate Tawny belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle": "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a dessert wine. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Tears of Llorona": "Tears of Llorona's aged-agave character overwhelms the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- añejo weight has no foil against cold shellfish — needs sparkling or crisp white. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Tears of Llorona for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Teeter Totter Cabernet Sauvignon": "Teeter Totter Napa Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — polished mocha obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save Teeter Totter for the steak course where its crowd-pleaser character peaks.",
  "Seared Scallops|Tenuta di Arceno Chianti Classico": "Tuscan Chianti Classico against scallop sweetness — Arceno's medium-tannin cherry-earth structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Arceno for red meat, pasta, or Italian table service.",
  "Seared Scallops|The BG": "Traveller whiskey, honey lavender, grapefruit, black walnut bitters, ginger beer. The whiskey base crushes scallops' delicate sweet-seared profile; black walnut bitters have no hook into clean seafood. Never pair — scallops demand crisp whites, French 75, or Vesper.",
  "Seared Scallops|The Happy Wife": "Tito's, orange juice, ginger syrup. The orange-and-ginger meets scallops' clean-seared sweetness without crushing; Tito's clean vodka keeps the pairing light. Strong approachable cocktail for scallops when guest wants simple over sophisticated — delivers on both ends.",
  "Seared Scallops|The Manhattan": "Maker's Mark private barrel, Contratto vermouth, vanilla syrup, Angostura. The spirit-forward Manhattan obliterates the scallops' delicate sweetness and the vanilla depth muddies the clean sear. Never pair — scallops demand crisp whites or bubbles, not a classic whiskey cocktail.",
  "Seared Scallops|The Prisoner Red Blend": "Never pair Prisoner with seared scallops — layered dark fruit and full body overwhelm delicate sweet shellfish and the smooth tannin fights browned-butter sweetness. Lead with Clos de la Chapelle Chardonnay or Rombauer's creamy richness for sear-seared harmony.",
  "Seared Scallops|The Tomahawk": "The Tomahawk's theatrical bone-in marbling and smoky char overwhelms the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness: the smoky bone-in weight obliterates the scallops, and the marbled char crowds out the seared-rare scallop plate. Avoid; the courses can't share a meal cleanly. Pair the scallops with Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre on a different visit; pour Opus One, Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon, or George T. Stagg alongside the Tomahawk.",
  "Seared Scallops|Thomas H. Handy Sazerac Rye": "Thomas H. Handy Sazerac Rye with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against BTAC uncut. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Seared Scallops|Thomas S. Moore Chardonnay Cask": "Thomas S. Moore Chardonnay Cask with seared scallops — Barton chardonnay-cask against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops even at white-wine-finish register.",
  "Seared Scallops|Titos Vodka": "Tito's with seared scallops — round corn-based vodka against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Tito's roundness mirrors scallop's natural sweetness — softer approach than Belvedere's pepper.",
  "Seared Scallops|Toki Suntory Japanese Whisky": "Toki Suntory with seared scallops — entry Japanese blend against scallop delicacy. Excellent; Toki's delicate-light character is gentle enough for scallops — Japanese whisky's category-advantage softness makes scallops approachable where most whiskies can't go.",
  "Seared Scallops|Tomato Basil": "Seared Scallops and the tomato basil together -- the butter-finished scallop carries into the bright soup. Strong; both openers earn their place on the meal.",
  "Seared Scallops|Transfusion": "Hangar 1, muddled black grapes, lime, ginger beer top. The fruit-forward profile meets scallops' clean-seared sweetness and the ginger beer's dry finish cleans the pairing. Strong refreshing cocktail for scallops — lighter than classic martinis while still pairing well.",
  "Seared Scallops|Trombo Cedano Reposado": "Trombo Cedano Reposado with seared scallops — cedar-wood notes against caramelized scallop. Strong; the cedar is distinctive but slightly overshadows the scallop — Don Julio 70th is the refined scallop-reposado call.",
  "Seared Scallops|Truffle Fries": "The scallops and the truffle fries -- protein meets umami, the table builds substance. Works; sequence them or share the table, no concern either way.",
  "Seared Scallops|Tullamore D.E.W.": "Tullamore D.E.W. with seared scallops — drier Irish blend against scallop delicacy. Works; Tullamore's heritage character is gentle enough for scallops but not featured.",
  "Seared Scallops|Venge Family Reserve": "Oakville flagship Napa Cab against scallop sweetness — Family Reserve's full-body structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Family Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Venge Scout's Honor": "Never pair Venge Scout's Honor with seared scallops — full-bodied Zin-led jammy blend crushes clean-seared shellfish and the black pepper fights scallop sweetness. Lead with Raventós Cava, Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé. Route the Scout's Honor to ribeye.",
  "Seared Scallops|Venge Silencieux": "Winemaker's Napa Cab against scallop sweetness — Silencieux's full-body cassis-chocolate structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Silencieux for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Vesper": "Nolet's gin, Ketel One, Lillet — equal parts, stirred cold. Nolet's rose-and-peach softness meets scallops' clean-seared sweetness directly; Lillet's citrus-bitter edge cuts without crushing. Peak martini pairing for the cleanest seafood on the menu.",
  "Seared Scallops|Veuve Clicquot Brut": "Yellow label Veuve — Pinot Noir-dominant Reims Champagne with ripe apple, white peach, biscuit, creamy mousse, lively acidity. The balanced structure frames scallops' clean-seared sweetness and the biscuit echoes the pan-butter. Peak recognizable Champagne for scallops — reliable celebration pour. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Seared Scallops|Vieux Carré": "Sazerac rye, Pierre Ferrand cognac, Contratto, Bénédictine, two bitters. The cocktail's full spirit weight obliterates the scallops' delicate sweetness; rye spice and cognac richness have no hook into the clean seared profile. Never pair — scallops demand crisp whites.",
  "Seared Scallops|Villon Cognac": "Villon with seared scallops — Courvoisier-sibling spirit against scallop delicacy. Avoid; cognac overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Vin Santo": "Vin Santo's Tuscan dried-fruit-and-honey sweetness overwhelms the scallops' caramelized sear-and-sweet richness -- dessert sugar on cold shellfish is wrong direction — needs sparkling or Sancerre. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre, not a dessert wine. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Vin Santo for the steak course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Weller 107": "Weller 107 with seared scallops — bigger-body wheated buries scallop sweetness. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Weller 12 Year": "Weller 12 Year with seared scallops — aged oak and scallop delicacy don't bridge. Avoid; the seafood can't carry the bourbon's weight. Choose a restrained white wine instead.",
  "Seared Scallops|Weller Millennium": "Weller Millennium with seared scallops — the Millennium's depth buries scallop delicacy. Avoid; pour a white wine or a clean cocktail.",
  "Seared Scallops|Weller Special Reserve": "Weller Special Reserve with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against wheated bourbon. Avoid; even entry Weller overshoots the seafood's register.",
  "Seared Scallops|Wheatley Vodka": "Wheatley with seared scallops — Buffalo Trace wheat vodka against scallop sweetness. Excellent; Wheatley's clean wheat frames scallops at value-premium register — a smart pick without Goose's price tag.",
  "Seared Scallops|WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel Rye": "WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against aged WP. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|WhistlePig 12 Year Old World": "WhistlePig 12 Year Old World with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against multi-cask WP. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Seared Scallops|WhistlePig 15 Year": "WhistlePig 15 Year with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 15-year premium. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Seared Scallops|WhistlePig Boss Hog IX 17 Year": "WhistlePig Boss Hog IX with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against unicorn WP. Avoid; save the Boss Hog.",
  "Seared Scallops|WhistlePig Boss Hog X Commandments": "WhistlePig Boss Hog X with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against X Commandments. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Seared Scallops|WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year": "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 100-proof WP. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Seared Scallops|Willett Pot Still Reserve": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against craft high-rye. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Seared Scallops|Woodford Reserve": "Woodford Reserve with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against small-batch oak. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Woodford Reserve Double Oaked": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked with seared scallops — Brown-Forman Double Oaked against scallop delicacy. Avoid; bourbon overwhelms scallops.",
  "Seared Scallops|Woodford Reserve Rye": "Woodford Reserve Rye with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against 90.4-proof rye. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Seared Scallops|Woodinville Rye": "Woodinville Rye with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against PNW craft rye. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Seared Scallops|Yamazaki 12 Year": "Yamazaki 12 with seared scallops — flagship Japanese single malt against scallop delicacy. Strong; Yamazaki 12's honey-fruit elegance frames scallops at distinguished register; Hakushu's peat is Japanese whisky's more distinctive scallop lift.",
  "Seared Scallops|Yamazaki 18 Year": "Yamazaki 18 with seared scallops — aged Suntory single malt against scallop delicacy. Strong; Yamazaki 18's aged character is heavier for scallops than the 12 — save the collector bottle for the main course.",
  "Seared Scallops|Yellow Chartreuse": "Seared Scallops: scallops meet Yellow Chartreuse. Avoid; honey-herbal liqueur wrong for scallops. Reach for a light rum, vodka, or gin.",
  "Seasonal Soup|1792 Small Batch": "1792 Small Batch's caramel-spice character reads alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the bourbon depth settles into the seasonal soup, and the rounded sweetness softens the bowl. Works; the bourbon's character is distinctive but the pairing isn't a standout.",
  "Seasonal Soup|1792 Sweet Wheat": "1792 Sweet Wheat's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the brown-spirit warmth threads the seasonal soup, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; sweet character distinctive but not driving.",
  "Seasonal Soup|1881 Napa Valley": "1881 Napa Valley's bold cherry-coffee cassis holds with the seasonal soup's house build — the opulent body overshoots the light soup. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Seasonal Soup|2 James Gin": "2 James Gin's crisp char-juniper botanicals leans against the seasonal soup's house build — the gin botanicals sit with the plate. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Seasonal Soup|A Midnight's Winter Dram": "A Midnight's Winter Dram's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the heather-and-honey weight sits with the seasonal soup, and the malt-driven sweetness softens the bowl. Works; annual-release covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Seasonal Soup|Aberlour 16": "Aberlour 16's double-matured Speyside balance finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the Highland register carries the seasonal soup, and the malt edge frames the bowl. Works; boutique at matched register.",
  "Seasonal Soup|Adictivo Cristalino": "Adictivo Cristalino's rested-agave body reads alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the barrel-rested body handles the seasonal soup, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; clean and composed pairing.",
  "Seasonal Soup|Adictivo Reposado": "Adictivo Reposado's añejo-pour depth leans against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the oak-aged tequila body threads the seasonal soup, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; ceremonial over-specified.",
  "Seasonal Soup|Alexander Valley Chardonnay": "Alexander Valley Chardonnay's apple-butter acidity sits alongside the seasonal soup's house build — the crisp acidity sits with the plate. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Seasonal Soup|Alexander Valley Cyrus": "Alexander Valley Cyrus's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis plays cleanly against the seasonal soup's house build — the opulent body overshoots the light soup. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Seasonal Soup|Alexander Valley Homestead Red": "Alexander Valley Homestead Red's coffee-mocha tannin sits beside the seasonal soup's house build — the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Seasonal Soup|Amaro Nonino": "Amaro Nonino's crisp orange-peel-grappa sweetness jars against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build -- bitter botanicals on savory broth pull against the salt-and-spice frame without resolving. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Amaro Nonino for the steak course.",
  "Seasonal Soup|Ancho Reyes": "Ancho Reyes' sweet liqueur character clashes with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Ancho Reyes on the steak course instead.",
  "Seasonal Soup|Angel's Envy": "Angel's Envy's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the caramel-spice register matches the seasonal soup, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Seasonal Soup|Angel's Envy Cask Strength": "Angel's Envy Cask Strength's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the bourbon weight handles the seasonal soup, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; aging wasted on the salad.",
  "Seasonal Soup|Angel's Envy Triple Cask": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the caramel-spice register matches the seasonal soup, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; bonded weight a touch ambitious for the dessert.",
  "Seasonal Soup|Aperol": "Aperol's crisp bitter-orange-aperitivo edge clashes with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Aperol belongs on the steak course.",
  "Seasonal Soup|Asparagus": "The seasonal soup and the asparagus on the same meal -- neither course pulls focus, the table reads even. Works; sequence or share, the build holds.",
  "Seasonal Soup|Au Gratin Potatoes": "The seasonal soup and the au gratin on the same meal -- neither course pulls focus, the table reads even. Works; sequence or share, the build holds.",
  "Seasonal Soup|Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon": "Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overwhelms the seasonal soup's house seasonal build -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
