  "Shafer 1.5|Shrimp Cocktail": "Stags Leap Shafer Cab against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — opulent 1.5 and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Shafer 1.5 for the steak course.",
  "Shafer 1.5|Swordfish": "Shafer 1.5's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overshadows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- dark-fruit weight crowds the seared sesame crust — needs a sparkling or crisp white for lift. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Shafer 1.5 on the steak course instead.",
  "Shafer 1.5|The Tomahawk": "Stags Leap Shafer 1.5 — entry-level, opulent blackberry, mocha, vanilla, plush soft tannin, full body. The full body meets Tomahawk's massive bone-in ribeye though plush soft tannin reads rounder than firm-tannin prestige Cabs on the grand cut. Strong Stags Leap Cab for Tomahawk — Shafer opulence on the grand scale.",
  "Shafer 1.5|Tomato Basil": "Shafer 1.5's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Le Garenne Rosé, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Shafer 1.5 for the steak course.",
  "Shafer 1.5|Truffle Fries": "Truffle Fries: the mushroom's umami depth meets the bold red's structured tannin; dark fruit threads the truffle-and-earth without crowding. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Shafer 1.5|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Shafer 1.5's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Shafer 1.5 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Shafer 1.5|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Shafer 1.5's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Le Garenne Rosé, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Shafer 1.5 for the steak course.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Asparagus": "Stags Leap collector's Cab against asparagus — dense Hillside Select structure against sulfur-forward vegetable is wildly wrong. Never pair. Route Shafer to the best steak cuts; take asparagus with Sauvignon Blanc, Sancerre, or Chablis.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Stags Leap collector's Cab — Hillside Select 32-month French oak, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, graphite, dense yet silky, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts gruyère-cream weight and the dark chocolate plays against the lactic richness. Works as collector's Napa Cab for au gratin — Hillside Select pairs better with the main cut.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Beignets": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power flattens the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Shafer Hillside Select for the steak course.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Bone Marrow": "Stags Leap collector's Cab — Hillside Select 32-month French oak, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, graphite, dense yet silky, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts marrow's collagen fat and the graphite plays against the smoky mineral depth. Peak collector's Napa Cab for marrow — Hillside Select dense-yet-silky structure on the rich starter. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Bone-In Filet": "Shafer Hillside Select -- Stags Leap allocated icon, cassis, graphite. The allocated-Cab depth wraps the bone-enhanced filet, and the graphite frames the cut. Strong; reliable match across the courses.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Broccoli Cheddar": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power clashes with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Shafer Hillside Select on the steak course instead.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Broccolini": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power crowds the broccolini's tender green stalks -- the side needs a crisper register to carry it cleanly. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Shafer Hillside Select for the steak course.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Burrata": "Stags Leap collector's Cab against burrata's creamy-delicate center — Hillside Select's firm-tannin dense graphite structure overwhelms the starter. Never pair. Route burrata to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Prosecco; keep Hillside Select for the steak course — this bottle deserves the main cut.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Butternut Squash": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power clashes with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Shafer Hillside Select for the steak course.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Carrot Cake": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Shafer Hillside Select on the steak course instead.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Cheesecake": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power pulls against the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- the red's dry-fruit register has no bridge to dessert tang or sugar. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Save the Shafer Hillside Select for the steak course.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Chilean Seabass": "Stags Leap collector's Cab against buttery Chilean seabass — dense Hillside Select structure overwhelms the delicate fish. Never pair. Route Shafer to the best steak cuts; take seabass with Chardonnay, Pinot Noir, or Chablis.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Chocolate Brownie": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power flattens the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Shafer Hillside Select for the steak course.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Chocolate Cake": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power flattens the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Shafer Hillside Select belongs on the steak course.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Clam Chowder": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power overwhelms the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Shafer Hillside Select for the steak course.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Cowboy Ribeye": "Stags Leap collector's Cab — Hillside Select 32-month French oak, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, graphite, dense yet silky, firm tannin. The dense silky structure handles ribeye's big marbled build and the dark chocolate plays against beefy char. Peak collector's Napa Cab for ribeye — Hillside Select extraordinary length on the bold cut. Gold standard; the headline call at the table.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Crab Cake": "Stag's Leap flagship Cabernet — structured, powerful, built for beef. Tannin plus delicate crab equals mismatch; the wine eats the dish. Reserve the bottle for the Tomahawk or Porterhouse where it can actually meet real weight. Avoid; the pairing fights at the table — point the guest elsewhere.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Creamed Spinach": "Stags Leap collector's Cab — Hillside Select 32-month French oak, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, graphite, dense yet silky, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts béchamel's dairy weight and the violet plays against the spinach base. Strong collector's Napa Cab for creamed spinach — Hillside Select poise reframes the rich side.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Creamy Potato": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power flattens the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- the wine's structure sits on top of the bisque's cream instead of integrating. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Shafer Hillside Select for the steak course.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Creme Brulee": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power flattens the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Shafer Hillside Select lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Escargot": "Shafer Hillside Select's bold cassis-tobacco tannin plays cleanly against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the Cab structure meets the savory depth, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Faroe Island Salmon": "Shafer Hillside Select: this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight meets this rich, fatty seafood's buttery flesh and delicate-yet-substantial texture. The bold red's tannin shreds the fish's delicate flake, and the dark fruit clashes with briny sweetness. Textbook avoid — this is the classic red-meat-only territory. Avoid; the pairing fights at the table — point the guest elsewhere.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Filet Mignon": "Stags Leap collector's Cab — Hillside Select 32-month French oak, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, graphite, dense yet silky, firm tannin, full body. The silky structure meets butter-tender filet's delicate sweetness and the violet plays against escargot-butter. Strong collector's Napa Cab for filet — Hillside Select poise on the delicate cut.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|French Onion": "Shafer Hillside Select's bold cassis-tobacco tannin reads alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Grilled Caesar": "Shafer Hillside Select's bold cassis-tobacco tannin sits alongside the Caesar's char-and-anchovy — the opulent body overshoots the leaf-and-acid plate, and the cassis plays against the grilled char. Works; reliable companion, low risk. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Gumbo": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power jars against the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Shafer Hillside Select lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power fights the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- red tannin and the glaze's sugar pull against each other — sugar reads cloying, tannin bitter. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Shafer Hillside Select for the steak course.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|House Wedge": "Stags Leap collector's Cab — Hillside Select 32-month French oak, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, graphite, dense yet silky, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts iceberg-and-bacon and the violet plays against blue cheese dressing. Works as collector's Napa Cab for the wedge — Hillside Select reframes the classic salad, but this bottle deserves the steak course.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Kansas City": "Stags Leap collector's Cab — Hillside Select 32-month French oak, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, graphite, dense yet silky, firm tannin. The firm tannin meets Kansas City's lean-bold marbled strip and the graphite plays against beefy char. Strong collector's Napa Cab for the strip — Hillside Select on the American cut.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Loaded Potato": "Shafer Hillside Select's bold cassis-tobacco tannin leans against the loaded potato's richness — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cassis cuts the cheese richness. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Lobster Mac": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the allocated-Cab depth wraps the lobster mac, and the graphite frames the side. Works; the side sits without pulling focus.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Market Fish": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power clashes with the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Shafer Hillside Select belongs on the steak course.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Mocha Creme": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power flattens the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Shafer Hillside Select on the steak course instead.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Mushroom Bisque": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the allocated-Cab depth wraps the mushroom bisque, and the graphite frames the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Mushrooms": "Stags Leap collector's Cab — Hillside Select 32-month French oak, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, graphite, dense yet silky, firm tannin. The graphite echoes roasted-mushroom glutamate and the violet plays against the earth depth. Strong collector's Napa Cab for mushrooms — Hillside Select extraordinary length on the earthy side.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power flattens the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Shafer Hillside Select on the steak course instead.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Porterhouse": "Stags Leap collector's Cab — Hillside Select 32-month French oak, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, graphite, dense yet silky, firm tannin. The firm tannin handles Porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet and the graphite plays against both lean-and-fatty sides. Strong collector's Napa Cab for Porterhouse — Hillside Select on the dual-cut classic.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Prime Tartare": "Stags Leap collector's Cab against raw Prime Tartare — Hillside Select's firm-tannin graphite-blackcurrant structure overwhelms the delicate raw beef with capers, shallot, and quail yolk. Never pair. Route tartare to Champagne, Pinot Noir, or lighter Cab; keep Hillside Select for the Tomahawk, Cowboy, or Bone-In Filet course.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Rainbow Trout": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Shafer Hillside Select for the steak course.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Roast Half Chicken": "Stag's Leap flagship — structured, powerful, built for beef. Chicken can't stand up to it; the wine gets wasted on a main that doesn't demand it. Reserve for the Tomahawk or Porterhouse. Avoid; the call reads off-register; recommend an alternative.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Stags Leap collector's Cab against a smoky vegetable soup — dense Hillside Select structure is wildly overkill for the Mediterranean classic. Never pair. Route Shafer to the best steak cuts; take the soup with Pinot Noir, rosé, or Rioja.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the red's structure is wrong for delicate flesh — built for red meat. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Shafer Hillside Select lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power clashes with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- tannin on raw green vegetable reads astringent without payoff. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Shafer Hillside Select for the steak course.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Seafood Tower": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Shafer Hillside Select lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Seared Scallops": "Stags Leap collector's Cab against scallop sweetness — Hillside Select's firm-tannin dense structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Hillside Select for the steak course where the 32-month oak and graphite earn the bottle.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Seasonal Soup": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power jars against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Shafer Hillside Select for the steak course.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Seasonal Vegetables": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power overshadows the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate -- red weight crowds a green side without lifting it — needs crisp register, not tannin. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Shafer Hillside Select for the steak course.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Shrimp Bisque": "Shafer Hillside Select's bold cassis-tobacco tannin plays cleanly against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cassis frames the herb butter. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Shrimp Cocktail": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power crowds out the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Shafer Hillside Select on the steak course instead.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Swordfish": "Shafer Hillside Select: this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight meets this meaty, firm swordfish's substantial, grilled character. The bold red's tannin shreds the fish's delicate flake, and the dark fruit clashes with briny sweetness. Textbook avoid — this is the classic red-meat-only territory. Avoid; the call reads off-register; recommend an alternative.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|The Tomahawk": "Stags Leap collector's Cab — Hillside Select 32-month French oak, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, graphite, dense yet silky, firm tannin, full body. The firm tannin handles Tomahawk's massive bone-in ribeye and the graphite plays against smoky char. Peak collector's Napa Cab for Tomahawk — one of Napa's most coveted on the grand cut. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Tomato Basil": "Shafer Hillside Select's Stags Leap allocated Cab power jars against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Le Garenne Rosé, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Shafer Hillside Select on the steak course instead.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Truffle Fries": "Stags Leap collector's Cab — Hillside Select 32-month French oak, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, graphite, dense yet silky, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the graphite plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak collector's Napa Cab for truffle fries — one of the great bottles on the umami hit. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Stags Leap collector's Cab against rare-seared yellowfin tuna — dense Hillside Select structure overwhelms the delicate fish. Never pair. Route Shafer to the best steak cuts; take tuxedo tuna with Pinot Noir, Pinot Blanc, or Chablis.",
  "Shafer Hillside Select|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Stags Leap collector's Cab against a coconut-milk vegetable curry — dense Hillside Select structure overwhelms the spiced classic. Never pair. Route Shafer to the best steak cuts; take the curry with Riesling, rosé, or Pinot Noir.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|1792 Small Batch": "1792 Small Batch's caramel-spice character sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon body sits with the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; Parker's Heritage 16th is over-specified for an app; save the collector bottle for the main.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|1792 Sweet Wheat": "1792 Sweet Wheat with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood against sweet-wheat. Works; sweet character distinctive but not driving.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|1881 Napa Valley": "1881 Napa Valley's bold cherry-coffee cassis plays cleanly against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|2 James Gin": "2 James with shrimp bisque — Detroit local gin against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; 2 James cuts the bisque with American-craft character.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|A Midnight's Winter Dram": "A Midnight's Winter Dram's Highland-scotch character sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the malt-and-oak threads the shrimp bisque, and the oak threads the cream. Works; BH Red Wine Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Aberlour 16": "Aberlour 16's double-matured Speyside balance leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon-plus-sherry depth wraps the shrimp bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the intensity overpowers this dish.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Adictivo Cristalino": "Adictivo Cristalino with shrimp bisque — filtered cristalino against cream-based seafood. Strong; aged-but-clear character sits with the bisque with distinctive craft depth.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Adictivo Reposado": "Adictivo Reposado with shrimp bisque — extended-aged reposado against cream-based seafood. Strong; the aged depth sits with the soup's richness.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Alexander Valley Chardonnay": "Sonoma Chardonnay — ripe apple, pear, warm vanilla oak, smooth balanced. The oak-vanilla texture aligns with the bisque's cream-shellfish richness and the apple-pear fruit lifts the butter-roux weight. Peak approachable Chardonnay for bisque — California oak on California-style soup. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Alexander Valley Cyrus": "Alexander Valley Cyrus's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis holds with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cassis frames the herb butter. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Alexander Valley Homestead Red": "Alexander Valley Homestead Red's coffee-mocha tannin sits alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the medium-body red frames the hearty soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Amaro Nonino": "Amaro Nonino's crisp orange-peel-grappa sweetness clashes with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Amaro Nonino on the steak course instead.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Ancho Reyes": "Ancho Reyes's ancho-chile-smoke sweetness sits with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the sweet character sits at digestif register, and the smoke wraps the briny shellfish. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Angel's Envy": "Angel's Envy with shrimp bisque — port-finished bourbon against cream-shrimp soup. Avoid; port-fruit clashes with seafood soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Angel's Envy Cask Strength": "AE Cask Strength with shrimp bisque — cask-strength port-finish against cream-shrimp soup. Avoid; port-fruit clashes with seafood soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Angel's Envy Triple Cask": "AE Triple Cask with shrimp bisque — multi-cask AE against cream-shrimp soup. Avoid; wine-fruit clashes with seafood soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Aperol": "Aperol's crisp bitter-orange-aperitivo edge clashes with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- amaro bitterness on dairy cream reads metallic — no bridge from herbal sharp to soft fat. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Aperol for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Asparagus": "Shrimp Bisque and the asparagus -- the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup meets the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: bright-acid breaks the weight, the plate finds its lift. Works; no conflict however the table orders them.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Au Gratin Potatoes": "The shrimp bisque and the au gratin -- the meal doubles the cream, neither course gets to play off the other. Works; sequence them or share the table, the call holds either way.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon": "Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cherry-coffee cassis sits beside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Averna Amaro": "Averna Amaro's bitter-herb aperitivo edge fights the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- bitter herbs cut the bisque's round cream without lifting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Averna Amaro for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Aviation": "Aviation gin, Luxardo maraschino, crème de violette, ginger syrup. The cocktail's floral lightness and ginger warmth cut the bisque's cream-shellfish richness without crushing. Strong pairing — the Aviation's visual appeal adds table interest alongside the bisque.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Aviation Gin": "Aviation with shrimp bisque — smooth Oregon craft against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Aviation rides the bisque at crowd-pleasing register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Avion 44": "Avion 44's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the oak-aged tequila body threads the shrimp bisque, and the caramel-agave register brightens the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Avion Silver": "Avion Silver with shrimp bisque — Jalisco-highlands against cream-based seafood. Strong; filtered agave cuts the dairy cleanly.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bacardi Rum": "* Bacardi Rum -- Carta Blanca, workhorse light rum, clean. The unaged-cane register matches the shrimp bisque, and the cane-and-citrus thread frames the bowl. The premium presentation elevates the whole tower; pour when the table wants the full experience. Gold standard; the headline call at the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Baileys Irish Cream": "Baileys Irish Cream's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- the liqueur's sweetness buries the soup's creamy base instead of supporting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Baileys Irish Cream belongs on the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Baker's": "Baker's' oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon weight handles the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; Vermont-brand at matched register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Balvenie 12 American Oak": "Balvenie 12 Am Oak with shrimp bisque — vanilla-forward Speyside against cream-shrimp soup. Works; Balvenie rides the bisque at handcrafted register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask": "Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask's rum-finished Speyside character sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the malt-and-oak threads the shrimp bisque, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Balvenie 16 Single Barrel": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel with shrimp bisque — First Fill American Oak against cream-shrimp soup. Works; Balvenie 16 rides the bisque at collector register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Balvenie 21 Portwood": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the port-cask depth wraps the shrimp bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; BIB over-specified for side.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bardstown Château Laboude": "Bardstown Château Laboude with shrimp bisque — French-wine-cask Bardstown against cream-shrimp soup. Avoid; wine-fruit clashes with seafood soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bardstown Discovery #6": "Bardstown Discovery #6's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon depth settles into the shrimp bisque, and the caramel-spice settles the cream. Works; light body doesn't overshoot.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bardstown Founders KBS": "Bardstown Founders KBS's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon body sits with the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bardstown Foursquare": "Bardstown Foursquare with shrimp bisque — rum-cask Bardstown against cream-shrimp soup. Avoid; tropical-rum-fruit clashes with seafood soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bardstown Fusion #7": "Bardstown Fusion #7's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon body sits with the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel": "Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon backbone carries the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; JD 12 handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Basil Hayden's": "Basil Hayden's with shrimp bisque — light high-rye against cream-based seafood. Works; the pour's delicacy doesn't overpower the soup, but doesn't particularly elevate it either.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Basil Hayden's 10 Year": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with shrimp bisque — aged light high-rye against cream-based seafood. Works; the 10-year's restraint lets the soup lead.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Basil Hayden's Malted Rye": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with shrimp bisque — malted character against cream-based seafood. Works; grain notes don't really engage the soup but don't clash.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with shrimp bisque — Beam BH red-wine finish against cream-shrimp soup. Avoid; red-wine-fruit clashes with seafood soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Basil Hayden's Toast": "Basil Hayden's Toast with shrimp bisque — toasted caramel against cream-based seafood. Works; the toast notes don't really interplay with the soup but don't clash.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bee's Knees": "Empress Indigo gin, lemon, honey lavender syrup. The honey softens against cream-shellfish soup and lemon brightens shrimp sweetness; lavender adds aromatic complexity. Works as a light starter pairing — though Sauv Blanc and Champagne peak higher for bisque.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Beefeater Gin": "Beefeater with shrimp bisque — balanced London Dry against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Beefeater cuts the bisque without Tanq's aggression.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Beignets": "Shrimp Bisque and the beignets -- rich cream gives way to sweet, the close lands generously. Works; either timing holds, the table builds either way.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Belvedere Vodka": "Belvedere with shrimp bisque — aromatic Polish rye against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; the pepper cuts the bisque's richness where wheat vodkas ride it.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Blade & Bow": "Blade & Bow with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood against blended bourbon. Works neutrally.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Blanton's Gold": "Blanton's Gold's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon body sits with the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; EC 18's aged character meets the glaze at aged-HH register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Blanton's Original": "Blanton's Original's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon backbone carries the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; annual-release complexity over-specified.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Blanton's Straight from the Barrel": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon weight handles the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Blood Oath Pact 10": "Blood Oath Pact 10's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon backbone carries the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the 10-year's restraint lets the soup lead.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Blood Oath Pact 8": "Blood Oath Pact 8's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon depth settles into the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; curated single-barrel slightly over-specified.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Blood Oath Pact 9": "Blood Oath Pact 9's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon weight handles the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; Remus 15 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bluecoat Gin": "Bluecoat with shrimp bisque — Philadelphia citrus-forward craft against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Bluecoat's 4-citrus profile cuts the bisque's richness with American-artisan lift.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bodega Noemia A Lisa": "Bodega Noemia A Lisa's bold earth-floral cassis sits alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the floral edge frames the shellfish. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bombay Dry Gin": "Bombay Dry with shrimp bisque — juniper-assertive London Dry against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Bombay Dry's pine notes cut the bisque with angular precision.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bombay Sapphire Gin": "Bombay Sapphire with shrimp bisque — 10-botanical softer London Dry against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Sapphire's floral notes ride the bisque softer than angular Bombay Dry would cut it.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bone Marrow": "Bone Marrow alongside the shrimp bisque -- cream meets protein, the meal builds with weight. Works; the openers share the table cleanly, sequence or share.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bone-In Filet": "Bone-In Filet into the shrimp bisque -- the buttery beef meets the shrimp bisque. Strong; reliable opener for the cut.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Booker's": "Booker's' cask-strength bourbon depth sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the cask-strength power drives the shrimp bisque, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the cream. Works; extended maturation gives the dessert home-state aged character.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Botanist Gin": "Botanist with shrimp bisque — Islay wildcrafted craft gin against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Botanist's foraged-herbal character cuts the bisque with Hebridean terroir.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bowdie's Old Fashioned": "Buffalo Trace muddled with our rum-soaked cherries, orange, and Angostura over a large cube. The cocktail's weight overwhelms the delicate seafood cream base and buries the smoked paprika finish. Reserve this cocktail for the beef course instead. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark": "Bowdie's Private Select Maker's Mark with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood meets house-pick caramel. Works; neutral companion.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bowman Brothers Small Batch": "Bowman Brothers Small Batch's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the oak depth lays under the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; HH 20 handles dessert density at collector register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bowmore 12": "Bowmore 12 with the shrimp bisque — honeyed peat and orchard-fruit notes meet the bisque's sea-driven cream. The sherry touch lifts the soup's sweetness; softer peat doesn't flatten the seafood depth. Strong — the most refined Islay-bisque pour.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Braida Montebruna Barbera": "Braida Montebruna Barbera's cherry-earth tannin holds with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the medium-body red frames the hearty soup, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon's bold earth cassis sits alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cassis frames the herb butter. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Broccolini": "The shrimp bisque and the broccolini on the same meal -- bright-acid breaks the weight, the plate finds its lift. Works; sequence or share, the build holds.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bruichladdich": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets this rich, creamy seafood soup's sweet-briny depth over dairy-rich base. Cocktail against a creamy seafood soup — acidity and lift cut the dairy base while the spirit carries its own weight. Strong — bright cuts rich.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Brussels and Belly": "The shrimp bisque and Brussels + Belly -- cream rounds the protein, the plate composes thick. Works; sequence them or share the table, the call holds either way.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Buffalo Trace": "Buffalo Trace with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood against flagship bourbon. Works neutrally.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Buffalo Trace Cream": "Buffalo Trace Cream's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- sugar piled onto cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Buffalo Trace Cream for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Bulleit Bourbon": "Bulleit Bourbon with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood against high-rye. Works; rye spice doesn't particularly elevate the soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Burrata": "The burrata with the shrimp bisque -- the burrata's fresh basil-tomato-cream delicacy meets the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the lighter course primes the richer, the meal carries register lift. Works; both opening courses earn their place.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Cade Cabernet Sauvignon": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's bold juniper-mineral cassis leans against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Camarena Tequila": "Camarena Tequila with shrimp bisque — value reposado against cream-based seafood. Strong; accessible agave cuts the dairy at the entry register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Campari": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- amaro bitterness on dairy cream reads metallic — no bridge from herbal sharp to soft fat. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; one of those is the move. Campari belongs on the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Canadian Club": "Canadian Club with shrimp bisque — heritage Canadian against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Canadian Club's grain-forward character rides the bisque at traditional register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Canadian Club 43 Year": "CC 43 Year with shrimp bisque — 43yr aged Canadian against cream-shrimp soup. Works; CC 43 Year is over-specified for a soup; save the rare bottle.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Captain Morgan Rum": "Captain Morgan Rum's clean silver register sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the light-rum body cuts the shrimp bisque, and the unaged-cane note plays against the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Caribou Crossing": "Caribou Crossing with shrimp bisque — Sazerac-owned Canadian against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Caribou Crossing's hand-selected character rides the bisque at craft register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Carrot Cake": "The shrimp bisque alongside the carrot cake -- rich cream gives way to sweet, the close lands generously. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Casa LBV Port": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness doubles down on the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- sweet wine on cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — heavy, no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Casa LBV Port for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Casamigos Mezcal": "Casamigos Mezcal's bold agave-soft-smoke character holds steady against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the agave smoke threads the broth, and the smoke wraps the briny shellfish. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon": "Caymus — Napa Cab with concentrated black fruit, cocoa, mocha, velvety tannin. The opulent body can meet the bisque's cream-shellfish richness but the cocoa-mocha profile is the wrong axis for shellfish soup. Works as iconic Napa Cab for bisque — Chardonnay, Champagne, or Riesling peak higher on cream-soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Chambord": "Chambord's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- the liqueur's sweetness buries the soup's creamy base instead of supporting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Chambord belongs on the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Cheesecake": "The shrimp bisque and the cheesecake -- the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup bookends with the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Chilean Seabass": "The seabass after the shrimp bisque -- the buttery flesh sits with the cream-finished bisque. Works; the opener sits without competing.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Chocolate Brownie": "The shrimp bisque alongside the brownie -- cream-and-sugar build the close, the meal finishes generous. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Chocolate Cake": "Shrimp Bisque and the chocolate cake -- rich dairy yields to dessert weight, the close composes thickly. Works; sequence them as opener and close or share the table, no clash.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Chopin Vodka": "Chopin with shrimp bisque — creamy potato vodka against cream-shrimp soup. Excellent; the pairing earns its featured slot.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Christian Bros Brandy": "Christian Bros Brandy's rancio-edged cognac weight reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the eau-de-vie body carries the shrimp bisque, and the dried-fruit note underlines the bowl. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Château Batailley": "Château Batailley's bold leather-tobacco cassis holds with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cassis frames the herb butter. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Château Beaucastel": "Château Beaucastel's bold earth-leather cassis reads alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Château Gombaude-Guillot": "Pomerol Merlot-Cab Franc — Château Gombaude-Guillot, biodynamic Pomerol, 2016, dark plum, truffle, mocha, velvety finish. The velvety Merlot bridges tomato-cream bisque weight and the mocha plays with shellfish depth. Strong Pomerol for bisque — plush Bordeaux handles the rich soup unconventionally.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Château Haut Segottes": "Château Haut Segottes' Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the Bordeaux body wraps the shrimp bisque, and the cassis-and-tobacco edge frames the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Château de Rouillac": "Château de Rouillac's leather-tobacco tannin sits beside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the medium-body red frames the hearty soup. Works; capable alongside. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Clase Azul Anejo": "Clase Azul Anejo's barrel-aged tequila weight reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the shrimp bisque, and the caramel-agave register brightens the bowl. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Clase Azul Durango": "Clase Azul Durango's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the barrel-rested body handles the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; accessible aged composes with the plate.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Clase Azul Gold": "Clase Azul Gold's rested-agave body sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the rested-agave depth sits with the shrimp bisque, and the caramel-agave register brightens the bowl. Works; luxury over-specified for small plate.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's rustic mezcal weight sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the wood-fire body meets the shrimp bisque, and the earthy backbone threads the bowl. Strong; a steady recommendation at the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Clase Azul Plata": "Clase Azul Plata with shrimp bisque — luxury blanco against cream-based seafood. Strong; the smooth agave sits with the bisque's richness at premium register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Clase Azul Reposado": "Clase Azul Reposado with shrimp bisque — premium reposado against cream-based seafood. Strong; smoothness sits with the bisque's richness gracefully.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Clase Azul Ultra": "Clase Azul Ultra's barrel-aged tequila weight finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the barrel-rested body handles the shrimp bisque, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Clermont Steep": "Clermont Steep with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood against Beam wheated. Works neutrally.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Clos Petit Ona Grenache": "Roussillon Southern France Grenache — Clos Petit Ona, wild raspberry, kirsch, garrigue, warm spice, medium body. The medium body handles tomato-cream and the wild raspberry lifts shellfish-sweetness. Strong Southern-French for bisque — Mediterranean red-on-shellfish bridge.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Codigo 1530 Rosa": "Codigo 1530 Rosa with shrimp bisque — Cabernet-cask reposado against cream-based seafood. Strong; the wine notes sit with the bisque in wine-country register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Contratto Vermouth": "Contratto Vermouth's vermouth-wine-base sweetness holds the line with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the bitter herb edge frames the hearty soup. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Corazon Blanco": "Corazon Blanco with shrimp bisque — highland agave against cream-based seafood. Strong; single-estate sits with the bisque at craft register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Corazon Reposado": "Corazon Reposado with shrimp bisque — highland agave against cream-based seafood. Strong; the brightness cuts the dairy cleanly.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Corazon Sazerac": "Corazon Sazerac's aged-agave character leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; distinctive composed with this dish.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Corazon Stagg": "Corazon Stagg's cooked-agave-and-oak register sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the barrel-rested body handles the shrimp bisque, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Corazon Weller": "Corazon Weller's rested-agave body reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the oak-aged tequila body threads the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Corazón del Sol Malbec": "Mendoza Argentina Malbec — Corazón del Sol, dark plum, blackberry jam, violet, velvety tannin, full body. The full body handles tomato-cream weight, but the jam-forward fruit reads heavy against shellfish-sweetness. Works for bisque — a Rosé's bridge or Chardonnay's cream fit better.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Corpse Reviver": "Warner's gin, Lillet, Pierre Ferrand cognac, lemon, absinthe rinse. The cocktail's lemon cuts bisque's cream-shellfish richness and cognac adds warmth against the soup's weight. Works well — though French 75 or Champagne peak slightly higher for bisque.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Courvoisier Cognac": "Courvoisier Cognac's classic VS cognac reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the cognac register matches the shrimp bisque, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; Courvoisier's backbone handles the richness.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Cowboy Ribeye": "The cowboy ribeye after the shrimp bisque -- the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup sets the table for the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness: two rich courses on the same plate, the table earns its substance. Works; the opener carries before the cut.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Crab Cake": "The crab cake alongside the shrimp bisque -- both bring shellfish as the headline. Avoid; one is enough. Pair the crab cake with Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin; pair the shrimp bisque with Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Cragganmore 12": "Cragganmore 12 with shrimp bisque — Classic Malt Speyside against cream-shrimp soup. Works; Cragganmore's subtle smoke cuts the bisque at distinctive register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Creamed Spinach": "The shrimp bisque alongside the creamed spinach -- the meal doubles the cream, neither course gets to play off the other. Works; the table can build them in order or together.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Creme Brulee": "Shrimp Bisque and the brulee -- the cream rounds into the sweet close, the meal lands rich and full. Works; sequence them as opener and close or share the table, no clash.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée": "Eola-Amity Willamette Pinot — cherry, raspberry, forest floor, mineral, high acid. The acid cuts bisque's cream weight and the forest-floor plays against shellfish umami and sherry. Strong Oregon Pinot for shrimp bisque — benchmark red against the rich shellfish soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Crown Royal": "Crown Royal with shrimp bisque — smooth Canadian against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Crown Royal's vanilla-honey rides the bisque at crowd-pleasing register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Cucumber Gimlet": "Hendrick's muddled with cucumber, lime, ginger syrup, soda top. The lime-and-ginger structure cuts the bisque's cream-shellfish richness and cucumber adds freshness against the soup's weight. Strong pairing when guest wants cocktail rather than white wine alongside bisque.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Dalmore 12": "Dalmore 12 with shrimp bisque — Matusalem-cask Highland against cream-shrimp soup. Works; Dalmore's sherry-finish rides the bisque at luxury register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge": "Sancerre Rouge — Loire red Pinot, raspberry, chalk, dried herbs, high acid. The chalk-acid cuts bisque's cream weight and the dried-herbs play against shellfish umami and sherry. Strong Loire red for shrimp bisque — hidden-gem French Pinot against the rich soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Darioush Cabernet Franc": "Darioush Cabernet Franc's cherry-floral tannin finds neutral with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the medium-body red frames the hearty soup, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon": "Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon's bold coffee-mocha cassis holds with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Detroit City Gin": "Detroit City Gin with shrimp bisque — urban craft juniper against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Detroit City cuts the bisque with hometown character.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Detroit City Vodka": "Detroit City with shrimp bisque — Detroit-distilled vodka against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Detroit City rides the bisque at hometown register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Dewar's 15": "Dewar's 15 with shrimp bisque — 15yr Highland blend against cream-shrimp soup. Works; Dewar's 15 rides the bisque at premium-blend register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Dewar's White Label": "Dewar's White Label with shrimp bisque — Aberfeldy-malt blend against cream-shrimp soup. Works; Dewar's White rides the bisque at entry register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Disaronno": "Disaronno's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- sugar piled onto cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; one of those is the move. Disaronno lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye": "Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye with shrimp bisque — craft blended rye against cream-based seafood. Works; boutique character doesn't drive.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum": "Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum's high-proof pour register leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the rich pour wraps the shrimp bisque, and the deep backbone frames the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Domaine Serene Grand Cheval": "Willamette flagship Pinot Blend — dark cherry, Bing cherry, toasted spice, forest floor, silky. The acid cuts bisque's cream weight and the forest-floor plays against shellfish umami and sherry. Strong flagship Willamette Pinot for shrimp bisque — layered Oregon against the rich soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Domaine Tempier Bandol": "Domaine Tempier Bandol's bold earth-mineral cassis reads alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the smoke wraps the briny shellfish. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé": "Pouilly-Fumé — Loire Sauv Blanc, gun-flint minerality, grapefruit, lime zest, fuller body than NZ. The smoky mineral cuts the bisque's cream-shellfish richness and the citrus lifts the butter-roux weight. Peak serious Sauv Blanc for bisque — flint meets cream in a classical match. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Domaine du Grand Tinel": "Domaine du Grand Tinel's bold earth-herbal cassis plays cleanly against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Don Fulano Anejo": "Don Fulano Anejo's cooked-agave-and-oak register leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the añejo register carries the shrimp bisque, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Don Fulano Blanco": "Don Fulano Blanco with shrimp bisque — premium highland against cream-based seafood. Strong; refined craft sits with the bisque's richness at premium register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Don Fulano Reposado": "Don Fulano Reposado with shrimp bisque — highland reposado against cream-based seafood. Strong; vanilla-honey sits with the bisque's richness elegantly.",
