  "Shrimp Bisque|Elk Cove Five Mountain": "Chehalem Mountains Willamette Pinot — cherry, violet, clove, structured. The acid cuts bisque's cream weight and the clove-spice plays against shellfish umami and sherry. Strong step-up Pinot for shrimp bisque — structured Willamette against the rich soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Elk Cove Pinot Blanc": "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc — Willamette with soft pear, white peach, floral lift, refreshing acidity. The refreshing acid cuts the bisque's cream-shellfish richness and the pear-peach fruit adds lift against butter-roux weight. Peak medium-body white for bisque — lighter cut than Chard, more fruit than Chablis.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Elmer T. Lee": "Elmer T. Lee's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon backbone carries the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; CC 43 Year is over-specified for a side; save the rare bottle for the main.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Empress 1908 Gin": "Empress 1908 with shrimp bisque — color-changing BC craft against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Empress's floral-citrus rides the bisque at distinctive register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Epoch Ingenuity": "Epoch Ingenuity's bold pepper-smoke cassis plays cleanly against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the smoke wraps the briny shellfish. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Escargot": "Escargot alongside the shrimp bisque -- cream and umami share the plate, the build reads dense and clean. Works; the openers share the table cleanly, sequence or share.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Espresso Martini": "Espresso Martini's roasted-coffee martini richness flattens the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- whiskey-cocktail register buries the soup's cream instead of carrying it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a spirit-forward cocktail. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Espresso Martini for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Espresso Old Fashioned": "Buffalo Trace, bourbon cream, Frangelico, espresso, brown sugar, Angostura. Coffee-hazelnut profile against cream-shellfish soup is unusual but not clashing; the bourbon cream softens the contrast. Works for cocktail-first guests — though white wine or Champagne peaks higher for bisque.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Evening Land Seven Springs": "Eola-Amity Willamette Pinot — black cherry, smoked meat, dried rose, crushed stone. The crushed-stone minerality cuts bisque's cream weight and the smoked-meat plays against shellfish umami and sherry. Peak savory Pinot for shrimp bisque — Willamette complexity against the rich soup. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon": "Far Niente — Oakville Cab, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, espresso, violet, smooth powerful. The opulent body can meet the bisque's cream-shellfish richness but Cab-with-shellfish-soup stretches the axis. Works as Far Niente for bisque — Chardonnay, Champagne, or Riesling peak higher on cream-soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Far Niente Chardonnay": "Far Niente Chardonnay -- Napa Chardonnay, tropical fruit, oak. The crisp white-wine body matches the shrimp bisque, and the stone-fruit note underlines the bowl. Excellent; a textbook match that delivers. Gold standard; the pairing that defines the moment.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Faroe Island Salmon": "Faroe Island Salmon with the shrimp bisque alongside -- the Atlantic salmon plate reads beside the silky shrimp cream. Works; the side-salad call holds before the main.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi": "Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi's dense blackberry-and-cassis tannin leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the structured body wraps the shrimp bisque, and the cassis frames the bowl. Works; the close holds, neither soars nor fights.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Faust Napa Valley Cabernet": "Faust Napa Valley Cabernet's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis plays cleanly against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía": "Galicia Ribeira Sacra Mencía — Fento, fresh red cherry, slate minerality, light body, high acid. The high acid cuts tomato-cream and the slate plays with shellfish-coastal notes. Works for bisque — a red-on-shellfish needs careful sell, but Mencía's lightness threads the needle.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Fernet Branca": "Fernet Branca's nuclear bitter-menthol intensity holds with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the bitter herb edge frames the hearty soup, and the bitter cuts the cream richness. Works; capable alongside. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Fernet Menta": "Fernet Menta's crisp mint-menthol edge leans against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the bitter herb edge frames the hearty soup. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Filet Mignon": "Filet Mignon after the shrimp bisque -- the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup primes the palate for the filet's lean buttery tenderness. Strong; the soup-or-salad sets the table without crowding the cut.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Fireball Whisky": "Fireball Whisky's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- the liqueur's sweetness buries the soup's creamy base instead of supporting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Fireball Whisky for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Fisher Unity Pinot Noir": "Sonoma Pinot — cranberry, red cherry, baking spice, silky. The acid cuts bisque's cream weight and the cherry-spice plays against shellfish umami and sherry. Strong by-the-glass Pinot for shrimp bisque — California silk against the rich soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Four Roses Small Batch Select": "Four Roses Small Batch Select's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon depth settles into the shrimp bisque, and the caramel softens the cream. Works; bonded weight pushes past the soup's register slightly.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Four Roses Yellow Label": "Four Roses Yellow Label with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood against entry bourbon. Works neutrally; light body sits with the soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Fox & Oden": "Fox & Oden's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon backbone carries the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; narrative-bourbon doesn't drive.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Fox & Oden Double Oaked": "Fox & Oden Double Oaked with shrimp bisque — Detroit Double Oaked against cream-shrimp soup. Avoid; Double-Oaked caramel clashes with seafood soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Frangelico": "Frangelico's Piedmont hazelnut depth to mocha at after-dinner register clashes with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Frangelico lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Freemark Abbey Bosché": "Freemark Abbey Bosché's bold juniper-leather cassis leans against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the juniper carries the shellfish. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|French 75": "Inverroche gin, lemon, vanilla syrup, Prosecco top. The bubbles-and-citrus cut the bisque's cream-and-shellfish richness and fynbos gin adds aromatic lift. Works as a bright opener alongside the bisque — though Sauvignon Blanc or Champagne peak slightly higher.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Frias Block 5": "Frias Block 5's bold herbal-umami cassis holds with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo": "G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo's sweet char-cherry tannin finds neutral with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the sweet character sits at digestif register, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti": "G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti's peach-and-honey frizzante sweetness mis-pairs with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- this sparkling's acidity is wrong direction for the soup-salad course. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a sparkling. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti on the steak course instead.",
