  "Shrimp Bisque|Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon": "Alexander Valley Cab — cassis, plum, cedar, mint, fine tannin. The elegant body can meet the bisque's cream-shellfish richness but Cab-with-shellfish-soup stretches the pairing axis. Strong Jordan for bisque — Chardonnay, Champagne, or Riesling peak higher on cream-soup, though Jordan's balance handles it.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Joseph Mellot Sancerre": "Loire Sancerre — crisp refined Sauv Blanc, grapefruit, chalk, fresh herbs, tension finish. The tension-filled acid cuts the bisque's cream-shellfish richness and the herbs play against butter-roux. Strong benchmark Sauv Blanc for bisque — Loire precision meets French cream-soup tradition.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Jubilation by Colgin": "Jubilation by Colgin's bold char-chocolate cassis sits alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the juniper carries the shellfish. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Jung and Wulff Guyana": "Jung and Wulff Guyana's heavy aged-spirit weight reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the dense-spirit weight carries the shrimp bisque, and the heavy-pour register grips the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Jung and Wulff Trinidad": "Jung and Wulff Trinidad's high-proof pour register leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the heavy body handles the shrimp bisque, and the deep backbone frames the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Kahlua": "Kahlua's sweet liqueur character clashes with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- the soup-salad course needs lift or acid — sweet liqueur brings neither. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Kahlua for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Kansas City": "The KC after the shrimp bisque -- the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup sets the table for the KC's lean-bold strip with savory grain: cream rounds the protein, the plate composes thick. Works; the opener carries before the cut.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Keenan Chardonnay": "Keenan Chardonnay — Spring Mountain Napa, green apple, lemon curd, subtle oak, bright acid. The bright acid cuts the bisque's cream-shellfish richness and the subtle oak complements the butter-roux without adding too much weight. Peak mountain Chardonnay for bisque — balance meets cream-soup classic. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Keenan Mernet": "Keenan Mernet's bold cherry-earth cassis sits alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the rye spice cuts the shrimp bisque, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; master-blender doesn't drive.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Kentucky Owl Confiscated": "Kentucky Owl Confiscated's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon weight handles the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; master-blender doesn't drive.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's": "Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's with shrimp bisque — luxury crossover Irish against cream-shrimp soup. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for a soup — save the collector bottle for the main course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône": "Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône's cherry-earth tannin stays alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the medium-body red frames the hearty soup, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Ketel One Vodka": "Ketel One with shrimp bisque — clean Dutch wheat against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Ketel's citrus cuts the bisque's richness rather than riding it.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Knickerbocker Gin": "Knickerbocker with shrimp bisque — hop-influenced Holland MI gin against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Knickerbocker's hop-bitter notes cut the bisque with distinctive character.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Knob Creek": "Knob Creek with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood against 100-proof high-rye. Works; the boldness pushes slightly past what the soup asks for.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Knob Creek 12 Year": "Knob Creek 12 Year's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon depth settles into the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Knob Creek 15 Year": "Knob Creek 15 Year's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon backbone carries the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Knob Creek 18 Year": "Knob Creek 18 Year's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the oak depth lays under the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; BH Red Wine Cask's softer-proof character rides the cream at distinctive register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye": "Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood against blended bourbon-rye. Works; 100-proof complexity sits beside the soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Knob Creek Rye": "Knob Creek Rye with shrimp bisque — 100-proof rye against cream-based seafood. Works; bold character slightly over-specified for the soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Komos Anejo Reserva": "Komos Anejo Reserva's rested-agave body finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the aged-agave weight wraps the shrimp bisque, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Komos Crystallino Anejo": "Komos Crystallino Anejo's rested-agave body reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the barrel-rested body handles the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; benchmark extra añejo is slightly ambitious for the two-cut plate.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Komos Extra Anejo": "Komos Extra Anejo's rested-agave body finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the barrel-rested body handles the shrimp bisque, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Komos Rosa Reposado": "Komos Rosa Reposado with shrimp bisque — rosé-finished reposado against cream-based seafood. Strong; the wine-cask notes sit with the bisque distinctively.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Lagavulin 8": "Lagavulin 8 with the shrimp bisque — maritime brine in the dram picks up the bisque's sea-driven base; peat adds dimension. The 8-year's vibrancy prevents the heaviness Laphroaig brings. Surprising but coherent. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Lail Vineyards Blueprint": "Lail Vineyards Blueprint's deep dark-fruit and grippy tannin finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the structured body wraps the shrimp bisque, and the cassis frames the bowl. Works; the side reads as a measured plate companion.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée": "Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée's bold floral-oak cassis leans against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Lalo Silver": "Lalo Silver with shrimp bisque — Lalo González craft against cream-based seafood. Strong; clean additive-free sits with the bisque at craft register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Laphroaig 10": "Shrimp Bisque: the cream-base bisque meets Laphroaig 10's medicinal iodine. Too much; the dram's intensity flattens the soup's nuance. Capable only. For Islay-bisque pairings, Lagavulin 8 is balanced, Bowmore 12 is refined. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Larceny Small Batch": "Larceny Small Batch with shrimp bisque — wheated honey against cream-based seafood. Works neutrally; doesn't drive.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé": "Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé's crisp berry-cherry acidity stays alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut": "Chardonnay-blend Champagne — green apple, lemon zest, whisper of brioche, vibrant acidity. The high-acid precision cuts the bisque's cream-shellfish richness and the brioche note complements butter-roux weight. Peak Champagne pairing for shrimp bisque — cleanliness meets indulgence course-perfectly. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Le Garenne Rosé": "Provence rosé — strawberry, citrus, clean. Works against the bisque but doesn't peak; the Chardonnays and Chablis do more against the coconut milk and the smoked paprika finish. Fine default pour when the guest isn't moving off rosé.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Le Ragnaie Brunello": "Le Ragnaie Brunello's bold cherry-earth cassis leans against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the juniper carries the shellfish. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Le Volte dell'Ornellaia": "Le Volte dell'Ornellaia's cherry-coffee tannin leans against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the medium-body red frames the hearty soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Lemon Lavender Gin Martini": "Plymouth gin, lemon, honey lavender syrup, Prosecco float. The lemon-and-lavender cuts the bisque's cream-shellfish richness and Prosecco adds effervescence against the soup's weight. Strong pairing — floral martini handles bisque where heavier cocktails would fight.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Les Pallières Raciné": "Les Pallières Raciné's bold earth-mineral cassis sits beside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Liberator Gin": "Liberator with shrimp bisque — 100% Michigan-grain craft against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Liberator's smooth profile rides the bisque at hometown register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Licor 43": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- the liqueur's sweetness buries the soup's creamy base instead of supporting it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Licor 43 for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Limoncello": "Limoncello's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- sugar piled onto cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Limoncello for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Willamette Pinot — dark cherry, forest floor, spice, refined structure. The acid cuts bisque's cream weight and the forest-floor earth plays against shellfish umami and sherry. Peak by-the-glass Oregon Pinot for shrimp bisque — elegant red against the rich shellfish soup. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Little Book": "Little Book's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the brown-spirit warmth threads the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; JD 12 handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Lobster Mac": "The shrimp bisque and the lobster mac -- both shellfish-forward, the table doubles up on shellfish. Avoid; pick one or the other. Pair the shrimp bisque with Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay; pair the lobster mac with Cowboy Ribeye, Far Niente Chardonnay, or The Tomahawk.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Loch Lomond 20 Year": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with shrimp bisque — 20yr aged Highland against cream-shrimp soup. Works; Loch Lomond 20 is over-specified for a soup; save the collector-aged Highland for the main course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Lock Stock & Barrel Rye": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the rye-and-oak weight handles the shrimp bisque, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; bold intensity slightly over-specified.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Long Road Gin": "Long Road with shrimp bisque — Grand Rapids estate-pride gin against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Long Road's Michigan-botanical character rides the bisque at hometown register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Los Vecinos Mezcal": "Los Vecinos Mezcal's espadín-and-smoke register leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the smoky agave register handles the shrimp bisque, and the green-agave edge brightens the bowl. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Louis XIII Cognac": "Louis XIII Cognac's luxury-icon cognac depth mis-pairs with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- an icon cognac on a soup-salad course is wrong moment — its register demands the close, not the open. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an icon cognac. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Louis XIII Cognac on the steak course instead.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Lucano Amaro": "Lucano Amaro's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- amaro bitterness on dairy cream reads metallic — no bridge from herbal sharp to soft fat. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Lucano Amaro belongs on the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Lunaria Coste di Moro": "Lunaria Coste di Moro's char-cherry tannin holds with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the medium-body red frames the hearty soup, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Macallan 12 Sherry": "Macallan 12 Sherry's classic Sherry-Cask Speyside character leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the scotch backbone matches the shrimp bisque, and the oak softens the cream. Works; the pour's delicacy doesn't overpower the soup, but doesn't particularly elevate it either.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Macallan 18": "Macallan 18's premium aged 18yr Oloroso Speyside sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the Highland register carries the shrimp bisque, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; complexity wasted on salad.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Macallan Estate": "Macallan Estate's estate Speyside character finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the estate depth wraps the shrimp bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the smooth character gives the dessert a composed frame.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Macauley Petite Syrah": "Macauley Petite Syrah's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis holds with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cassis frames the herb butter. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Macauley Pinot Noir": "Sonoma Pinot — bright strawberry, red cherry, light floral, soft tannins. The light acid cuts bisque's cream weight and the strawberry plays against shellfish umami and sherry. Works as accessible Pinot for shrimp bisque — mid-tier Macauley against the rich soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Macauley Stagecoach Vineyard": "Macauley Stagecoach Vineyard's bold coffee cassis holds with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Mahon Gin": "Mahón with shrimp bisque — PDO Menorcan gin against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Mahón's Mediterranean juniper cuts the bisque with Spanish distinction.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Maker's Mark": "Maker's Mark with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood meets 90-proof wheated. Works neutrally; pour doesn't drive.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Maker's Mark Cellar Aged": "Maker's Mark Cellar Aged with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood meets cellar-aged caramel. Works; neutral companion.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Malibu Rum": "Malibu Rum's clean silver register reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the unaged body brightens the shrimp bisque, and the Caribbean register brightens the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye": "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the rye spice cuts the shrimp bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; rye's brightness is a gentle counterpoint.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Marc Brédif Chinon": "Loire Cab Franc — Chinon light body, raspberry, red cherry, bell pepper, forest floor, supple low tannin, bright high acid. The bright acid cuts shrimp bisque's cream-sherry weight and the red cherry plays against the shellfish base. Works as unusual Loire CF for the bisque — food-wine acidity on the rich soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Margarita": "Corazon Blanco, lemon, lime, orange, Cointreau. The triple-citrus cuts the bisque's cream-shellfish richness and the salted rim adds savory contrast against the soup's sweetness. Strong cocktail pairing — Margarita handles bisque where many classic cocktails would fight.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Marimar Estate Christina": "Russian River Green Valley Pinot — ripe strawberry, cherry compote, warm spice, silky. The acid cuts bisque's cream weight and the cherry-compote plays against shellfish umami and sherry. Strong plush Pinot for shrimp bisque — Russian River opulence against the rich soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Market Fish": "Market Fish with the shrimp bisque alongside -- the white-fish body sits with the cream-finished bisque. Works; the side-salad call holds before the main.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Mata Hari Absinthe": "Mata Hari Absinthe's sweet wormwood-anise character finds register with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the sweet character sits at digestif register, and the anise threads the herb edge. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Michter's 10 Year Bourbon": "Michter's 10 Year Bourbon's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the brown-spirit warmth threads the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; Voyage 23 frames the cut at ocean-finish register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Michter's 10 Year Rye": "Michter's 10 Year Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the dry rye body wraps the shrimp bisque, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; HH 20 frames the two-cut plate at collector register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Michter's US*1 Rye": "Michter's US*1 Rye with shrimp bisque — smooth pot-still rye against cream-based seafood. Works; the Michter's polish is interesting but doesn't drive.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Mijenta Blanco": "Mijenta Blanco with shrimp bisque — additive-free craft against cream-based seafood. Strong; clean highland sits with the bisque at premium-craft register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Milagro Anejo": "Milagro Anejo's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the aged-agave weight wraps the shrimp bisque, and the caramel-agave register brightens the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Milagro Reposado": "Milagro Reposado with shrimp bisque — modern clean reposado against cream-based seafood. Strong; the triple-distillation clarity sits with the bisque cleanly.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey": "Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon body sits with the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; flagship depth gives the dessert premium aged character.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Mocha Creme": "The shrimp bisque alongside the mocha creme -- cream-and-sugar build the close, the meal finishes generous. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Monkey 47 Gin": "Monkey 47 with shrimp bisque — lingonberry-forest craft gin against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Monkey 47's complexity cuts the bisque with Schwarzwald character.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Monkey Shoulder": "Monkey Shoulder with shrimp bisque — Speyside-malt blend against cream-shrimp soup. Works; Monkey Shoulder rides the bisque at distinctive register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Montenegro Amaro": "Montenegro Amaro's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Montenegro Amaro belongs on the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Mount Gay Rum": "Mount Gay Rum's crisp Barbados-molasses character matches the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the crisp body sits with the plate. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Muga Reserva": "Muga Reserva's cherry-earth tannin leans against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the medium-body red frames the hearty soup, and the oak frames the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Mushrooms": "The shrimp bisque and the mushrooms -- dairy plays against umami, the table reads layered. Works; sequence them or share the table, the call holds either way.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Myers's Rum": "Myers's Rum's high-proof pour register sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the high-proof register matches the shrimp bisque, and the dense weight underlines the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Negroni": "Negroni's citrus-herbal build sits alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the cocktail lift refreshes against the hearty soup, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Never Say Die Rye": "Never Say Die Rye with shrimp bisque — UK-aged rye against cream-based seafood. Works; distinctive character doesn't drive.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Never Say Die Small Batch": "Never Say Die Small Batch with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood against UK-matured bourbon. Works; distinctive character doesn't drive but adds interest.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|New Holland Beer Barrel Bourbon": "New Holland Beer Barrel Bourbon with shrimp bisque — MI beer-barrel against cream-shrimp soup. Avoid; hop-bitter clashes with seafood soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|New York Sour": "Jameson, lemon, simple, egg white, Daou Cab float. The lemon-sour cuts the bisque's cream-and-shellfish richness beautifully and the egg-white foam echoes the soup's texture. Strong unconventional pairing — the sour profile handles bisque where heavier cocktails would fight it.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Nickel & Nickel Cabernet": "Nickel & Nickel Cabernet's bold oak cassis holds with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the match holds without overshooting. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Nolets Dry Gin": "Nolet's with shrimp bisque — Turkish rose/peach/raspberry against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Nolet's fruit-floral rides the bisque at contemporary register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Not a Paper Plane": "Not a Paper Plane's citrus-herbal build holds with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the cocktail lift refreshes against the hearty soup, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Oban 14": "Oban 14 with shrimp bisque — coastal Highland against cream-shrimp soup. Works; Oban's maritime profile cuts the bisque with coastal-terroir resonance — the most thematic bisque pairing in the Highland cluster despite being Works tier due to whisky-meets-soup challenge.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Oban 18": "Oban 18 with shrimp bisque — premium maritime Highland against cream-shrimp soup. Works; Oban 18's aged coastal character cuts the bisque with thematic maritime resonance, though over-specified for a soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Ocho Anejo": "Ocho Anejo's aged-agave character reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the rested-agave depth sits with the shrimp bisque, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; the wine-cask notes don't compete with the dish's sweetness effectively.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Odette Cabernet Sauvignon": "Odette Cabernet Sauvignon's bold sage cassis leans against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Old Elk Cigar Cut": "Old Elk Cigar Cut with shrimp bisque — cigar-paired bourbon against cream-shrimp soup. Avoid; cigar-bourbon character clashes with seafood soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Old Emmer": "Old Emmer's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the brown-spirit warmth threads the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; EC 18's aged character meets the glaze at aged-HH register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Old Fitzgerald 7 Year": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood against wheated BIB. Works; bonded weight pushes slightly past the soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Old Fitzgerald 9 Year": "Old Fitzgerald 9 Year with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood against aged wheated. Works neutrally.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Old Grand-Dad 16 Year": "Old Grand-Dad 16 Year's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; PNW character doesn't drive.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Opus One": "Opus One: this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight meets this rich, creamy seafood soup's sweet-briny depth over dairy-rich base. Bold red meets rich, caramelized depth — the wine's dark fruit threads through the savory base. Not a clean fit — the soup's register clashes. Avoid; pair this elsewhere on the menu.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Our Lady of Guadalupe Acolytes": "Our Lady of Guadalupe Acolytes — Willamette Trappist Chardonnay with ripe pear, butterscotch, toasted oak, rich layered. The rich oak weight aligns with the bisque's cream-shellfish richness and the butterscotch plays against the butter-roux. Peak provenance-forward Chardonnay for bisque — worth mentioning the monastery story. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Pablo Sour": "Reposado tequila, lemon, vanilla syrup, egg white. The silky foam echoes the bisque's cream-and-shellfish texture and lemon cuts the soup's richness. Peak pairing — the cocktail's foam-on-foam play with bisque is a memorable service moment. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Paloma": "Reposado tequila, grapefruit, vanilla syrup. The grapefruit cuts the bisque's cream-shellfish richness and vanilla smooths against the soup's weight. Strong pairing — though Sauvignon Blanc and Champagne peak slightly higher for bisque, the Paloma handles it cleanly.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye's allocated-icon Pappy rye character sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the rye backbone drives the shrimp bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; high proof over-specified for the soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition": "Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the bourbon weight handles the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; save the bottle for the protein course — a soup is wrong for a $200 pour.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Patron Anejo": "Patron Anejo's cooked-agave-and-oak register leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the oak-aged tequila body threads the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; clean character doesn't drive the pairing.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Patron Silver": "Patron Silver with shrimp bisque — Patron against cream-based seafood. The citrus cuts the dairy at the globally-familiar tier. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Patron XO Cafe": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character doubles down on the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- sugar piled onto cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Patron XO Cafe for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Paul Bara Grand Rosé Brut": "Paul Bara Grand Rosé Brut's crisp mineral-raspberry acidity sits beside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Peanut Butter Brownie": "The shrimp bisque and the PB brownie -- the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup bookends with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Peju Cabernet Sauvignon": "Peju Cabernet Sauvignon's bold char-cherry cassis stays alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Pierre Ferrand Cognac": "Pierre Ferrand Cognac's artisan cognac with orange peel leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the brandy depth wraps the shrimp bisque, and the rancio register softens the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut": "Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut's char-citrus acidity reads alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Pikesville Rye": "Pikesville Rye with shrimp bisque — 110-proof bold rye against cream-based seafood. Works; high proof over-specified for the soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Pineau des Charentes": "Cognac-region fortified — Pineau des Charentes in aperitif mode, grape juice plus young Cognac oak-aged, white grape, honey, warm nutty Cognac. The honey plays with tomato-cream sweetness and the warm nutty Cognac bridges shellfish-coastal depth. Works for bisque — a Chardonnay's cream fits richer.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Pio Cesare Barbaresco": "Pio Cesare Barbaresco's bold Nebbiolo-cherry cassis stays alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Plymouth Gin": "Plymouth with shrimp bisque — softer Plymouth-style against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Plymouth rides the bisque at softer register than Tanq cuts it.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Poderi Aldo Conterno Nebbiolo": "Poderi Aldo Conterno Nebbiolo's bold cherry-citrus cassis sits alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Pommery Cuvée Louise": "Pommery Cuvée Louise's mineral-prestige acidity plays cleanly against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Porterhouse": "Porterhouse into the shrimp bisque -- the meal layers rich on rich, the table carries weight cleanly when the registers match. Works; safe opener, the meal builds without crowding.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Prime Tartare": "The tartare with the shrimp bisque -- the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami meets the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: cream rounds the savory, the meal earns its depth. Works; both opening courses earn their place.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Quilt Cabernet Sauvignon": "Quilt Cabernet Sauvignon's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis leans against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the caramel softens the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|RAEN Royal St Robert": "Fort Ross-Seaview Sonoma Coast Pinot — sea-influenced, red cherry, cranberry, wild strawberry, crushed rock, high acid. The high acid cuts bisque's cream weight and the sea-bred minerality plays against shellfish umami and sherry. Strong Burgundian Pinot for shrimp bisque — elegant against the rich soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Rainbow Trout": "Rainbow Trout with the shrimp bisque alongside -- the herb-finished trout holds against the cream-finished bisque. Works; the side-salad call holds before the main.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Raventós Cava de NIT Rosé Brut": "Raventós Cava de NIT Rosé Brut: this sparkling rosé's strawberry-and-brioche charm with crisp acidity meets this rich, creamy seafood soup's sweet-briny depth over dairy-rich base. Bubbles and acid cut the soup's creamy weight. Strong — brightness-on-richness.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Redbreast 12 Year": "Redbreast 12 with shrimp bisque — pot still Irish against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Redbreast 12's rich-oily character rides the bisque at premium-Irish register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Redbreast 21 Year": "Redbreast 21 with shrimp bisque — 21-year aged pot still Irish against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Redbreast 21 rides the bisque at collector register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Remus 15 Year Gatsby Reserve": "Remus 15 Year Gatsby Reserve's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the brown-spirit warmth threads the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; JD 12 handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Remy VSOP Cognac": "Remy VSOP Cognac's VSOP fine-champagne cognac leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the cognac register matches the shrimp bisque, and the orchard-fruit thread frames the bowl. Works; Rémy's elegance handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Rey Sol Anejo": "Rey Sol Anejo's rested-agave body sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the shrimp bisque, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; aged-but-clear character composes with the dish.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Reyka Vodka": "Reyka with shrimp bisque — Icelandic glacial vodka against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Reyka's mineral cuts the bisque's richness where Chopin's creamy vodka rides it.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Rishi's Old Antique": "Rishi's Old Antique's grain-and-oak bourbon register finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for a soup — save the collector bottle for the main course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Roast Half Chicken": "Roast Half Chicken with the shrimp bisque alongside -- the roast bird holds against the rich shellfish soup. Works; the side-salad call holds before the main.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs' bright sparkling effervescence reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the fine bubbles lift the shrimp bisque, and the citrus frames the bowl. Works; too light for dessert density at this level.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Roku Gin": "Roku with shrimp bisque — yuzu-sakura Japanese gin against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Roku's yuzu-citrus cuts the bisque with Japanese-precision lift.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Ron Zacapa Rum": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey premium-sipping rum leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the rich pour wraps the shrimp bisque, and the deep backbone frames the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Russell's Reserve 10 Year": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood against aged bourbon. Works neutrally.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Salt-Cured Halibut preceded by the shrimp bisque -- the firm-flesh fish reads alongside the silky shrimp cream. Works; the call holds at neutral register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Sambuca": "Sambuca's after-dinner liqueur weight sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the digestif body mirrors the shrimp bisque, and the honey threads the cream. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|San Simeon Stormwatch": "San Simeon Stormwatch's structured dark-fruit weight sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the structured body wraps the shrimp bisque, and the cassis frames the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir": "Sta. Rita Hills Santa Barbara Pinot — rich, layered, dark cherry, earth, dried herbs. The acid cuts bisque's cream weight and the earth-and-herbs play against shellfish umami and sherry. Strong legendary-vineyard Pinot for shrimp bisque — layered Santa Barbara against the rich soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "The shrimp bisque and the garlic spinach on the same meal -- acid plays against richness, the contrast holds across the courses. Works; sequence or share, the build holds.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Sauternes Glass": "Sauternes — Sémillon-Sauvignon Blanc with noble rot (botrytis cinerea), apricot, honey, orange marmalade, luscious unctuous, bright acid. The honey plays with tomato-cream-sweetness and the bright acid cuts shellfish-cream weight. Strong Sauternes for bisque — noble-rot sweetness bridges the rich shellfish soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Sazerac": "Sazerac rye, Peychaud's bitters, sugar, absinthe-rinsed glass. Rye's spice against cream-shellfish soup is bold; the anise-edge is unusual with bisque but not clashing. Works for cocktail-first guests — though white wine peaks higher for bisque.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Sazerac Rye": "Sazerac Rye with shrimp bisque — iconic rye against cream-based seafood. Works; the rye spice is interesting against the bisque but doesn't drive.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Scapegrace Fortuna": "Scapegrace Fortuna with shrimp bisque — NZ craft single malt against cream-shrimp soup. Works; Fortuna rides the bisque at distinctive register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Scavino Barolo": "Piedmont Barolo DOCG Nebbiolo — Scavino Castiglione Falletto, tar, dried rose, cherry, leather, powerful firm tannin, high acid. The high acid cuts shrimp bisque's cream-sherry weight and the tar plays against the shellfish base. Works as King-of-Italian for the bisque — Scavino's food-demanding acid on the rich soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Schloss Vollrads Riesling": "Rheingau Germany Riesling — apricot, white peach, petrol, lively acid backbone, off-dry. The off-dry fruit-acid play cuts the bisque's cream-shellfish richness and the apricot-peach plays against the butter-roux. Peak German Riesling for bisque — 700-year estate provenance adds a teaching moment. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters": "Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters's bold cherry-chocolate cassis holds with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Seafood Tower": "The seafood tower and the shrimp bisque -- both shellfish-forward, the table doubles up on shellfish. Avoid; pick one or the other. Pair the seafood tower with Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut; pair the shrimp bisque with Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Seared Scallops": "The scallops and the shrimp bisque -- both shellfish-forward, the table doubles up on shellfish. Avoid; pick one or the other. Pair the scallops with Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, or Joseph Mellot Sancerre; pair the shrimp bisque with Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Seasonal Vegetables": "Shrimp Bisque and the seasonal vegetables -- the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup meets the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: a clean call, no friction either way. Works; no conflict however the table orders them.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Sesti Brunello di Montalcino": "Sesti Brunello di Montalcino's bold cherry-earth cassis sits alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Shafer 1.5": "Shafer 1.5's bold coffee-juniper cassis finds neutral with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the caramel-spice settles the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Shafer Hillside Select": "Shafer Hillside Select's bold cassis-tobacco tannin plays cleanly against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cassis frames the herb butter. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Shrimp Cocktail": "The shrimp cocktail and the shrimp bisque -- shellfish-on-shellfish, the meal goes redundant. Avoid; the table reads heavy without payoff. Suggest Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut for the shrimp cocktail, or Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay for the shrimp bisque.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Siete Leguas Blanco": "Siete Leguas Blanco with shrimp bisque — tahona-crushed against cream-based seafood. Strong; the traditional craft character sits with the soup in a distinctive register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Siete Leguas Reposado": "Siete Leguas Reposado with shrimp bisque — rustic agave against cream-based seafood. Strong; the craft traditional character sits with the soup in a distinctive register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon": "Alexander Valley Cab — American-oak vanilla, coconut, dill, ripe cassis, plum, soft tannin. The lush body can meet the bisque's cream-shellfish richness but Cab-with-shellfish-soup stretches the axis. Works as Silver Oak for bisque — Chardonnay, Champagne, or Riesling peak higher on cream-soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Simon Family Estate Reserve": "Simon Family Estate Reserve's bold oak cassis reads alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Spottswoode Lyndenhurst": "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst's bold cherry-floral cassis holds with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|St Supéry Cabernet Sauvignon": "St Supéry Cabernet Sauvignon's bold char-coffee cassis finds neutral with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc": "St Supéry — Napa Sauv Blanc with lemon, grapefruit, gooseberry, lively finish. The lively acid cuts the bisque's cream-shellfish richness; the lemon-gooseberry plays against butter-roux. Works as Napa Sauv Blanc for bisque — rounder body handles the cream, though Chardonnay peaks higher for this course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|St Supéry Élu Meritage": "St Supéry Élu Meritage's bold cherry-coffee cassis holds with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Stagg Jr. Batch #15": "Stagg Jr. Batch #15's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the shrimp bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; Remus 15 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Stoli Elit Vodka": "Stoli Elit with shrimp bisque — ultra-premium Russian wheat against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Elit's clarity rides the bisque at luxury register without adding texture.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc": "Stoneleigh — Marlborough Sauv Blanc, passionfruit, grapefruit, grass, zesty. The zesty acid cuts the bisque's cream-shellfish richness; the tropical-citrus plays against butter-roux. Works as bright NZ Sauv Blanc for bisque — though richer Chardonnay peaks higher for this cream-soup course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Swordfish": "Swordfish into the shrimp bisque -- the dense fish steak reads beside the shrimp bisque. Works; safe opener, but not the headline pick.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Tanq 10 Gin": "Tanq 10 with shrimp bisque — premium citrus-Tanq against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Tanq 10's citrus brightens the bisque at refined register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Tanqueray Gin": "Tanqueray with shrimp bisque — high-proof London Dry against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Tanq's juniper cuts the bisque's richness sharply.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Taylor Fladgate Tawny": "Taylor Fladgate Tawny's classic tawny with caramel-nut sweetness clashes with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Taylor Fladgate Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle": "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle's dessert-wine sweetness doubles down on the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- sweet wine on cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — heavy, no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle on the steak course instead.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Tears of Llorona": "Tears of Llorona's aged-agave character sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the añejo register carries the shrimp bisque, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; clean and refined but not a marquee pairing.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Teeter Totter Cabernet Sauvignon": "Teeter Totter Cabernet Sauvignon's bold coffee-mocha cassis finds neutral with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the coffee threads the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Tenuta di Arceno Chianti Classico": "Tenuta di Arceno Chianti Classico's cherry-earth tannin plays cleanly against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the medium-body red frames the hearty soup, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|The BG": "Shrimp Bisque: this rich, creamy seafood soup's sweet-briny depth over dairy-rich base meets this bold whiskey-forward cocktail's oak, spice, and spirit depth. Cocktail against a creamy seafood soup — acidity and lift cut the dairy base while the spirit carries its own weight. Strong — bright cuts rich.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|The Happy Wife": "Tito's, orange juice, ginger syrup. The orange juice cuts the bisque's cream-shellfish richness and ginger's subtle warmth plays against the soup's weight. Strong straightforward pairing — the Happy Wife's simplicity handles the bisque well.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|The Manhattan": "The Manhattan's bold oak-vanilla build finds neutral with the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the whiskey-build depth matches the hearty soup, and the caramel-spice settles the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|The Prisoner Red Blend": "The Prisoner Red Blend's bold char cassis reads alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|The Tomahawk": "The Tomahawk after the shrimp bisque -- the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup sets the table for the Tomahawk's theatrical bone-in marbling and smoky char: cream meets protein, the meal builds with weight. Works; the opener carries before the cut.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Thomas H. Handy Sazerac Rye": "Thomas H. Handy Sazerac Rye's rye-spice character leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the shrimp bisque, and the oak softens the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Thomas S. Moore Chardonnay Cask": "Thomas S. Moore Chardonnay Cask with shrimp bisque — white-wine-finished Barton bourbon against cream-shrimp soup. Avoid; chardonnay-and-shrimp is great on paper but bourbon weight breaks the bisque.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Titos Vodka": "Tito's with shrimp bisque — American vodka against rich cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Tito's roundness rides the bisque's richness without cutting or deepening it.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Toki Suntory Japanese Whisky": "Toki Suntory with shrimp bisque — entry Suntory blend against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Toki's delicate character rides the bisque at crowd-pleasing register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Transfusion": "Hangar 1 vodka, muddled black grapes, lime, ginger beer top. The lime and ginger cut the bisque's cream-shellfish richness and the grape adds fruit complexity. Strong sessionable pairing for bisque when guest wants something tall rather than a classic martini.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Trombo Cedano Reposado": "Trombo Cedano Reposado with shrimp bisque — cedar-wood notes against cream-based seafood. Strong; cedar is distinctive but doesn't drive this pairing.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Truffle Fries": "Shrimp Bisque and the truffle fries -- the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup meets the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: dairy plays against umami, the table reads layered. Works; no conflict however the table orders them.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Tullamore D.E.W.": "Tullamore D.E.W. with shrimp bisque — drier Irish blend against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Tullamore's drier character cuts the bisque with heritage-Irish distinction.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "The tuna after the shrimp bisque -- the sesame crust sits with the shrimp bisque. Works; the opener sits without competing.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Shrimp Bisque and the curry together -- soup-and-salad open the meal. Works; both courses share the opening without crowding.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Venge Family Reserve": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis leans against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the caramel-spice settles the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Venge Scout's Honor": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis leans against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the rounded sweetness brightens the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Venge Silencieux": "Venge Silencieux's bold cherry-chocolate cassis sits beside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cherry-fruit rounds the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Vesper": "Nolet's gin, Ketel One vodka, Lillet. The cocktail's clean-structured profile meets cream-shellfish soup without fighting; Lillet's citrus-bitter cuts the cream weight. Strong martini alternative when guest wants cocktail rather than white wine with bisque.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Veuve Clicquot Brut": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's biscuit-apple acidity sits alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the apple notes lift the custard. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Vieux Carré": "Vieux Carré's bold herbal-spice build stays alongside the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the whiskey-build depth matches the hearty soup, and the herbs play the buttery edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Villon Cognac": "Villon Cognac's rancio-edged cognac weight sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the aged-grape brandy body sits with the shrimp bisque, and the dried-fruit note underlines the bowl. Works; Rémy's elegance handles the richness at premium register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Vin Santo": "Vin Santo's Tuscan dried-fruit-and-honey sweetness doubles down on the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup -- sweet wine on cream is dessert-course energy on a savory plate — heavy, no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Bacardi Rum, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Vin Santo for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Weller 107": "Weller 107 with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood meets higher-proof wheat. Works; the pour's assertiveness is a bit much for the soup but doesn't clash.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Weller 12 Year": "Weller 12 Year with the shrimp bisque — aged wheated sweetness against cream-based seafood. The 12-year holds its own but doesn't particularly elevate the soup; it's a neutral companion. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Weller Millennium": "Weller Millennium with the shrimp bisque — sea-driven cream meets aged wheated honey. Works without elevating either; the Millennium's scarcity suggests saving for a better pairing.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Weller Special Reserve": "Weller Special Reserve with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood meets gateway wheated sweetness. Neutral match; the Weller holds its own but doesn't drive the pairing. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Wheatley Vodka": "Wheatley with shrimp bisque — Buffalo Trace wheat vodka against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Wheatley's cleanness rides the bisque's richness without adding character.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel Rye": "WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the dry rye body wraps the shrimp bisque, and the oak threads the cream. Works; Old World complexity wasted on salad simplicity.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|WhistlePig 12 Year Old World": "WhistlePig 12 Year Old World's rye-spice character finds neutral with the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the high-rye spice register matches the shrimp bisque, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; X Commandments story wasted on salad.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|WhistlePig 15 Year": "WhistlePig 15 Year's rye-spice character leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the rye-and-oak weight handles the shrimp bisque, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; the rye spice is interesting against the bisque but doesn't drive.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|WhistlePig Boss Hog IX 17 Year": "WhistlePig Boss Hog IX 17 Year's rye-spice character leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the rye-and-oak weight handles the shrimp bisque, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; blend character covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|WhistlePig Boss Hog X Commandments": "WhistlePig Boss Hog X Commandments' rye-spice character leans against the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the high-rye spice register matches the shrimp bisque, and the oak depth lays under the cream. Works; IW Harper 15 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year": "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year with shrimp bisque — 100-proof WP against cream-based seafood. Works; Vermont-brand character doesn't drive.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Willett Pot Still Reserve": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood against craft high-rye. Works; oak spice sits beside the soup without driving.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Woodford Reserve": "Woodford Reserve with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood against small-batch. Works neutrally; Woodford holds.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Woodford Reserve Double Oaked": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked with shrimp bisque — iconic Double-Oaked against cream-shrimp soup. Avoid; Double-Oaked caramel clashes with seafood soup.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Woodford Reserve Rye": "Woodford Reserve Rye with shrimp bisque — small-batch rye against cream-based seafood. Works; fruit-forward interesting but doesn't drive.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Woodinville Rye": "Woodinville Rye with shrimp bisque — Washington State craft against cream-based seafood. Works; PNW character doesn't drive.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Yamazaki 12 Year": "Yamazaki 12 with shrimp bisque — flagship Japanese single malt against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Yamazaki 12's Mizunara-oak elegance rides the bisque at flagship register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Yamazaki 18 Year": "Yamazaki 18 with shrimp bisque — aged Yamazaki against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Yamazaki 18's Mizunara-oak depth rides the bisque at collector register.",
  "Shrimp Bisque|Yellow Chartreuse": "Yellow Chartreuse's gentian-driven cut sits alongside the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup: the herbal cut works the shrimp bisque, and the amaro backbone frames the bowl. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|1792 Small Batch": "1792 Small Batch with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against 93.7-proof Barton. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|1792 Sweet Wheat": "1792 Sweet Wheat with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against sweet-wheat. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|1881 Napa Valley": "1881 Napa Cab against chilled sweet-briny shrimp — mocha-tannin body is the wrong axis for cold shellfish and cocktail sauce. Never layer. Route shrimp cocktail to Champagne, Sancerre, or Chablis and save 1881 for the steak course where its entry Napa character belongs.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|2 James Gin": "2 James with shrimp cocktail — Detroit-distilled local gin against cold shrimp. Excellent; 2 James delivers the classic pairing with local-pride distinction — the answer when a guest asks for something Michigan.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|A Midnight's Winter Dram": "A Midnight's Winter Dram with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against rare craft release. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Aberlour 16": "Aberlour 16 with shrimp cocktail — double-matured Speyside against cold shrimp. Avoid; Scotch wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Adictivo Cristalino": "Adictivo Cristalino with shrimp cocktail — filtered cristalino against cold shrimp. The distinctive aged-but-clear character threads through cocktail sauce with craft-theatrical presentation. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Adictivo Reposado": "Adictivo Reposado with shrimp cocktail — long-aged reposado against cold shrimp. The aged character gives the cocktail a weightier counterpoint than standard reposados bring. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Alexander Valley Chardonnay": "Alexander Valley Chardonnay's apple-butter acidity finds register with the shrimp's chilled sweetness — the crisp acidity lifts the shellfish without weight, and the juniper carries the shellfish. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Alexander Valley Cyrus": "Sonoma Meritage against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — full-body red and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Cyrus for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Alexander Valley Homestead Red": "Sonoma Bordeaux blend against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — red wine and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Homestead Red for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Amaro Nonino": "Amaro Nonino's crisp orange-peel-grappa sweetness overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- amaro bitterness on cold shellfish flattens the delicate brine — needs sparkling instead. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Amaro Nonino on the steak course instead.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Ancho Reyes": "Ancho Reyes' sweet liqueur character clashes with the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- sweet liqueur is dessert energy — wrong place for the table's first course. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Ancho Reyes for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Angel's Envy": "Angel's Envy with shrimp cocktail — port-finished Louisville against cold shrimp. Avoid; bourbon wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Angel's Envy Cask Strength": "AE Cask Strength with shrimp cocktail — 117+ proof AE against cold shrimp. Avoid; bourbon wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Angel's Envy Triple Cask": "AE Triple Cask with shrimp cocktail — multi-cask AE against cold shrimp. Avoid; bourbon wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Aperol": "Aperol's crisp bitter-orange-aperitivo edge overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- bitter aperitivo flattens the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Aperol belongs on the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Asparagus": "The shrimp cocktail and the asparagus -- two bright registers, the table reads fresh across the courses. Works; sequence them or share the table, no concern either way.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Shrimp Cocktail alongside the au gratin -- the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish meets the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: bright-acid breaks the weight, the plate finds its lift. Works; no conflict, the meal builds.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon": "Austin Hope Paso Cab against chilled sweet-briny shrimp — plush warm-spice is the wrong axis for cold shellfish and cocktail sauce. Never layer. Route shrimp cocktail to Champagne, Sancerre, or Chablis and save Austin Hope for steak where its Paso warmth belongs.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Averna Amaro": "Averna Amaro's bitter-herb aperitivo edge overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- amaro bitterness on cold shellfish flattens the delicate brine — needs sparkling instead. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Averna Amaro for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Aviation": "Aviation gin, Luxardo, crème de violette, ginger syrup — pale purple, shaken. The cocktail's floral-and-cherry profile lifts chilled shrimp's brine and ginger plays against cocktail-sauce horseradish. Peak visually-driven pairing for shrimp cocktail — both light and elegant.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Aviation Gin": "Aviation with shrimp cocktail — soft-juniper Portland craft gin against cold shrimp. Excellent; Aviation's balanced lavender-orange-peel profile delivers the classic cold app with crowd-pleasing character.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Avion 44": "Avion 44 with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against aged Avion. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Avion Silver": "Avion Silver with shrimp cocktail — 80-proof Avion against cold shrimp. The filtered clean agave threads through cocktail sauce at the everyday accessible tier. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bacardi Rum": "* Bacardi Rum -- Carta Blanca, workhorse light rum, clean. The unaged body brightens the chilled shrimp, and the light-rum lift plays against the starter. Excellent on shrimp cocktail; Bacardi's neutral-clean profile is the textbook light-rum move on cold shellfish — the workhorse answer when guest wants something light with seafood. Gold standard; the headline call at the table.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Baileys Irish Cream": "Baileys Irish Cream's sweet liqueur character clashes with the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- sweet liqueur is dessert energy — wrong place for the table's first course. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Baileys Irish Cream for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Baker's": "Baker's with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against 107-proof Beam. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Balvenie 12 American Oak": "Balvenie 12 Am Oak with shrimp cocktail — bourbon-cask Speyside against cold shrimp. Avoid; Scotch wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask": "Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask with shrimp cocktail — Caribbean-rum-cask Speyside against cold shrimp. Avoid; Scotch wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Balvenie 16 Single Barrel": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel with shrimp cocktail — First Fill American Oak against cold shrimp. Avoid; Scotch wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Balvenie 21 Portwood": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with shrimp cocktail — 21yr port-finished Speyside against cold shrimp. Avoid; Scotch wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bardstown Château Laboude": "Bardstown Château Laboude with shrimp cocktail — Bardstown French-wine finish against cold shrimp. Avoid; bourbon wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bardstown Discovery #6": "Bardstown Discovery #6 with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against craft-blender. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bardstown Founders KBS": "Bardstown Founders KBS with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against KBS-finished. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bardstown Foursquare": "Bardstown Foursquare with shrimp cocktail — Foursquare rum-cask against cold shrimp. Avoid; bourbon wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bardstown Fusion #7": "Bardstown Fusion #7 with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against Fusion blend. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel": "Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against Rishi's-picked. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Basil Hayden's": "Basil Hayden's with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against high-rye. Avoid; separate courses.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Basil Hayden's 10 Year": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp and aged bourbon don't bridge. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Basil Hayden's Malted Rye": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against malted rye. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with shrimp cocktail — Beam BH against cold shrimp. Avoid; bourbon wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Basil Hayden's Toast": "Basil Hayden's Toast with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against toasted bourbon. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bee's Knees": "Empress Indigo gin with lemon and honey lavender syrup. Honey against brine works and the Indigo's color-change is a conversation starter. Not the peak — the sparkling options do more — but a valid cocktail-route choice. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Beefeater Gin": "Beefeater with shrimp cocktail — classic 40% London Dry against cold shrimp. Excellent; Beefeater's balance is the textbook gin-shrimp pairing — the English institution delivering on expectation.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Beignets": "Shrimp Cocktail and the beignets -- bright meets sweet, the contrast stays light. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Belvedere Vodka": "Belvedere with shrimp cocktail — single-estate rye vodka against cold shrimp. Excellent; aromatic rye character brings brightness the wheat vodkas don't match.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Blade & Bow": "Blade & Bow with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against blended bourbon. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Blanton's Gold": "Blanton's Gold with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against richer Blanton's. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Blanton's Original": "Blanton's Original with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against iconic single-barrel. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Blanton's Straight from the Barrel": "Blanton's SfB with shrimp cocktail — cask-strength Blanton's against cold shrimp. Avoid; barrel-proof wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Blood Oath Pact 10": "Blood Oath Pact 10 with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against milestone-release. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Blood Oath Pact 8": "Blood Oath Pact 8 with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against annual-release. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Blood Oath Pact 9": "Blood Oath Pact 9 with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against annual-release. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bluecoat Gin": "Bluecoat with shrimp cocktail — 4-citrus Philly organic craft against cold shrimp. Excellent; Bluecoat's American citrus-forward profile elevates the classic cold app with patriotic-artisan lift.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bodega Noemia A Lisa": "Never pair Noemia with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp plus cocktail-sauce horseradish gets crushed by full body, blackberry, and graphite, and the silky elegance has nowhere to land. Lead with Laurent Perrier Brut Champagne's bubble-driven palate reset.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bombay Dry Gin": "Bombay Dry with shrimp cocktail — original-recipe juniper against cold shrimp. Excellent; Bombay Dry's assertiveness makes the pairing feel distinctive rather than default.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bombay Sapphire Gin": "Bombay Sapphire with shrimp cocktail — 10-botanical softer floral against cold shrimp. Excellent; Sapphire's accessibility makes this the approachable gin-shrimp pairing — the blue-bottle icon delivering the expected.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bone-In Filet": "The bone-in filet after the shrimp cocktail -- the chilled shrimp's citrus-horseradish snap refreshes the palate, the 14oz bone-deepened cut following with marrow-touched butter. Strong; the opener resets for the cut's richness.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Booker's": "Booker's with shrimp cocktail — Beam cask-strength against cold shrimp. Avoid; barrel-proof wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Botanist Gin": "Botanist with shrimp cocktail — Islay-foraged craft against cold shrimp. Strong; Botanist's Hebridean botanicals elevate the classic cold app with oceanic-island character.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bowdie's Old Fashioned": "Buffalo Trace muddled with our rum-soaked cherries, orange, and Angostura. Bourbon's caramel weight buries cold shrimp; the cocktail-sauce heat gets swallowed too. Reserve this cocktail for the beef course where it earns its spot. Avoid; pair this elsewhere on the menu.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark": "Bowdie's Private Select Maker's Mark with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against house-pick oak. Avoid; separate pours.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bowman Brothers Small Batch": "Bowman Brothers Small Batch with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against Virginia small-batch. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bowmore 12": "Bowmore 12 with shrimp cocktail — cold poached shrimp and Islay peat don't bridge regardless of how gentle the peat is. Bowmore 12's honey doesn't rescue it. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Braida Montebruna Barbera": "Italian food-wine Barbera against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — Braida's juicy cherry-blackberry and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Braida for red meat.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brandlin Mount Veeder Cab against chilled sweet-briny shrimp — firm graphite-earth is the wrong axis for cold shellfish and cocktail sauce. Never layer. Route shrimp cocktail to Champagne, Sancerre, or Chablis and save Brandlin for steak where its Mount Veeder character belongs.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Broccoli Cheddar": "Shrimp Cocktail and the broccoli cheddar together -- bright-acid breaks the weight, the plate finds its lift. Works; the table opens with both, no clash either way.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Broccolini": "The shrimp cocktail and the broccolini -- both crisp and clean, the table reads light from open to handoff. Works; the call holds whether the table sequences them or shares.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bruichladdich": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets this delicate seafood starter's briny-fresh sweetness. Whiskey's oak and caramel are only going to land if the starter can carry weight — check the plate. Strong for rich-umami starters.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Buffalo Trace": "Buffalo Trace with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against BT flagship. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Buffalo Trace Cream": "Buffalo Trace Cream's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- sweet liqueur on cold shellfish is wrong-course energy — too forward for a clean opener. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Buffalo Trace Cream for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Bulleit Bourbon": "Bulleit Bourbon with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against high-rye. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Butternut Squash": "Shrimp Cocktail alongside the butternut squash -- acid and sugar share the table, neither course pulls heavy. Works; the openers share the table cleanly, sequence or share.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Cade Cabernet Sauvignon": "Cade Howell Mountain Cab against chilled sweet-briny shrimp — firm iron-mineral is the wrong axis for cold shellfish and cocktail sauce. Never layer. Route shrimp cocktail to Champagne, Sancerre, or Chablis and save Cade for steak where its LEED-estate Howell character belongs.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Camarena Tequila": "Camarena Tequila with shrimp cocktail — value reposado against cold shrimp. The entry-tier agave threads through the cocktail sauce cleanly. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Campari": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- amaro bitterness on cold shellfish flattens the delicate brine — needs sparkling instead. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Campari on the steak course instead.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Canadian Club": "Canadian Club's workhorse Canadian blend drowns out the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Canadian Club on the steak course instead.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Canadian Club 43 Year": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character smothers the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Canadian Club 43 Year on the steak course instead.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Captain Morgan Rum": "Captain Morgan Rum's spiced-vanilla character finds register with the shrimp's chilled sweetness — the crisp body lifts the shellfish without overwhelming, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Caribou Crossing": "Caribou Crossing's craft profile is wrong for scallops smothers the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- bourbon warmth has no foil against cold, clean shellfish. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Reserve the Caribou Crossing for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Carrot Cake": "The shrimp cocktail and the carrot cake -- the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish bookends with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Casa LBV Port": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- dessert wine is wrong-course energy for the opener. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a dessert wine. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Casa LBV Port belongs on the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Casamigos Mezcal": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- mezcal smoke obliterates delicate shellfish — needs sparkling or sancerre. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a mezcal. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Casamigos Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon": "Caymus Napa Cab against chilled sweet-briny shrimp — opulent cocoa-mocha is the wrong axis for cold shellfish and cocktail sauce. Never layer. Route shrimp cocktail to Champagne, Sancerre, or Chablis and save the iconic Napa name for steak.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Chambord": "Chambord's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- sweet liqueur on cold shellfish is wrong-course energy — too forward for a clean opener. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Save the Chambord for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Cheesecake": "Shrimp Cocktail and the cheesecake -- acid plays against sweetness, the close stays unburdened. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Chilean Seabass": "Chilean Seabass with the shrimp cocktail as the lead-in -- the buttery flesh threads the cocktail-citrus plate. Strong; the starter sets the table for the seabass.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Chocolate Brownie": "The shrimp cocktail alongside the brownie -- bright meets sweet, the contrast stays light. Works; the bookends compose neutrally.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Chocolate Cake": "The shrimp cocktail and the chocolate cake -- the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish bookends with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body. Works; no flavor conflict across the meal, either as opener-close or together.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Chopin Vodka": "Chopin with shrimp cocktail — potato vodka against cold shrimp. Excellent; Chopin's creaminess is a distinctive frame for the classic cold app — softer than Belvedere's rye sibling.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Christian Bros Brandy": "Christian Bros Brandy's barrel-aged cognac character clashes with the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- cognac is wrong-course energy for the table's opener. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a cognac. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Christian Bros Brandy for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Château Batailley": "Classified Pauillac Bordeaux against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — firm-tannin red and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Batailley for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Château Beaucastel": "Never pair Beaucastel with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp plus cocktail-sauce horseradish gets crushed by full body, leather, and truffle, and the bucket-list complexity has nowhere to land. Lead with Laurent Perrier Brut Champagne's bubble-driven palate reset.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Château Gombaude-Guillot": "Never pair Château Gombaude-Guillot with shrimp cocktail — plush Pomerol Merlot's velvety weight overshadows cold poached shrimp and cocktail-sauce horseradish. Lead with Veuve Clicquot, Raventós Cava, or French 75. Gombaude-Guillot lives on the red-meat course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Château Haut Segottes": "Right-bank Bordeaux against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — Merlot-led red and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Haut Segottes for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Château de Rouillac": "Left-bank Bordeaux against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — firm-tannin red and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Château de Rouillac for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Clam Chowder": "The shrimp cocktail and the chowder -- shellfish-on-shellfish, the meal goes redundant. Avoid; the table reads heavy without payoff. Suggest Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut for the shrimp cocktail, or Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis for the chowder.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Clase Azul Anejo": "Clase Azul Anejo's aged-agave character overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- añejo weight has no foil against cold shellfish — needs sparkling or crisp white. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Clase Azul Anejo for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Clase Azul Durango": "Clase Azul Durango with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against Durango ceremony. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Clase Azul Gold": "Clase Azul Gold with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against golden-ceramic. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- mezcal smoke obliterates delicate shellfish — needs sparkling or sancerre. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a mezcal. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal on the steak course instead.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Clase Azul Plata": "Clase Azul Plata with shrimp cocktail — ultra-premium blanco against cold shrimp. The luxury smooth agave threads through cocktail sauce with ceremony. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Clase Azul Reposado": "Clase Azul Reposado with shrimp cocktail — luxury reposado against cold shrimp. Smooth agave and cocktail sauce find each other cleanly; a premium cold-seafood ceremony. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Clase Azul Ultra": "Clase Azul Ultra with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against top-tier ceremonial. Avoid; save the Ultra.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Clermont Steep": "Clermont Steep with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against Beam wheated. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Clos Petit Ona Grenache": "Never pair Clos Petit Ona with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp plus cocktail-sauce horseradish gets crushed by kirsch and garrigue, and the warm spice has nowhere to land. Lead with Laurent Perrier Brut Champagne's bubble-driven palate reset.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Codigo 1530 Rosa": "Codigo 1530 Rosa with shrimp cocktail — Napa Cab-cask rosé against cold shrimp. The wine fruit cuts the cocktail sauce with distinctive character. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Contratto Vermouth": "Contratto Vermouth's vermouth-wine-base sweetness holds with the shrimp's chilled sweetness — the bitter herb edge overpowers the shellfish. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Corazon Blanco": "Corazon Blanco with shrimp cocktail — single-estate highland blanco against cold shrimp. The agave-forward character threads through cocktail sauce with Sazerac-family distinctiveness. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Corazon Reposado": "Corazon Reposado with shrimp cocktail — highland agave brightness against cold shrimp and cocktail sauce. The single-estate character threads through the horseradish cleanly. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Corazon Sazerac": "Corazon Sazerac's aged-agave character smothers the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- aged-agave register crowds the delicate shellfish frame. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Corazon Sazerac belongs on the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Corazon Stagg": "Corazon Stagg's añejo tequila finished in ex-George-T overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- aged tequila is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Corazon Stagg lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Corazon Weller": "Corazon Weller's aged-agave character overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- aged tequila is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Corazon Weller lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Corazón del Sol Malbec": "Never pair Corazón Malbec with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp plus cocktail-sauce horseradish gets crushed by jam-forward full body, and the velvety tannin has nowhere to land. Lead with Laurent Perrier Brut Champagne's bubble-driven palate reset.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Corpse Reviver": "Warner's gin, Lillet, Pierre Ferrand cognac, lemon, absinthe rinse. The lemon cuts chilled shrimp's sweet brine and the absinthe-edge adds aromatic complexity against cocktail-sauce bite. Peak classical cocktail for a classical starter — sophistication in both glasses.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Courvoisier Cognac": "Courvoisier Cognac's classic VS cognac overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- cognac weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs sparkling or a crisp white. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a cognac. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Courvoisier Cognac belongs on the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Cowboy Ribeye": "Cowboy Ribeye after the shrimp cocktail -- the chilled shrimp's citrus-horseradish snap cleans the palate, the 26oz cap-and-fat cut following with rendered char-and-fat richness. Strong; the bright opener primes the indulgent cut.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Cragganmore 12": "Cragganmore 12 with shrimp cocktail — distinctive Speyside against cold shrimp. Avoid; Scotch wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Creamed Spinach": "The shrimp cocktail and the creamed spinach -- the bright register cleaves the heavy course, the table breathes. Works; sequence them or share the table, no concern either way.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Creamy Potato": "The shrimp cocktail preceded by the potato soup -- acid plays against richness, the contrast holds across the courses. Works; safe opening pair, the meal builds without strain.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Creme Brulee": "The shrimp cocktail alongside the brulee -- acid and sugar share the table, neither course pulls heavy. Works; both bookends earn their place, the meal arc holds.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée": "Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée's Willamette Pinot elegance overshadows the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée on the steak course instead.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Crown Royal": "Crown Royal's classic Canadian blend smoothness drowns out the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; one of those is the move. Crown Royal belongs on the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Cucumber Gimlet": "Hendrick's gin, cucumber, lime, ginger syrup, soda top. Fresh cucumber and lime cut chilled shrimp's brine and the ginger syrup softens cocktail-sauce horseradish bite. Peak starter pairing — cocktail's garden-fresh structure meets the shrimp's clean sweetness. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Dalmore 12": "Dalmore 12's sherry-finished Highland character overshadows the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the spirit weight crowds the delicate shellfish — no acid to clean the brine. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Dalmore 12 belongs on the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge": "Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge's Loire Valley Pinot Noir crowds out the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Darioush Cabernet Franc": "Rare Napa CF against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — medium-tannin Darioush and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Darioush for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon": "Darioush Silverado Trail Cab against chilled sweet-briny shrimp — plush mocha-spice is the wrong axis for cold shellfish and cocktail sauce. Never layer. Route shrimp cocktail to Champagne, Sancerre, or Chablis and save Darioush for steak where its Persian-inspired plush character belongs.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Detroit City Gin": "Detroit City Gin with shrimp cocktail — Detroit City Distillery against cold shrimp. Excellent; urban craft character delivers the classic cold-app pairing with Detroit-pride distinction.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Detroit City Vodka": "Detroit City with shrimp cocktail — Detroit-distilled craft vodka against cold shrimp. Excellent; hometown craft character delivers the classic cold-app pairing with Michigan-pride distinction.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Dewar's 15": "Dewar's 15 with shrimp cocktail — 15yr Dewar's against cold shrimp. Avoid; Scotch wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Dewar's White Label": "Dewar's White Label with shrimp cocktail — entry blended Scotch against cold shrimp. Avoid; Scotch wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Disaronno": "Disaronno's sweet liqueur character smothers the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- sugar buries the delicate shellfish without any acid to balance. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Disaronno on the steak course instead.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye": "Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against craft rye. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum": "Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum's aged-rum register with molasses and oak depth overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the spirit's weight is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Domaine Serene Grand Cheval": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift crowds out the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Domaine Serene Grand Cheval for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Domaine Tempier Bandol": "Never pair Tempier with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp plus cocktail-sauce horseradish gets crushed by game, olive, and firm tannin, and the cult-producer complexity has nowhere to land. Lead with Laurent Perrier Brut Champagne's bubble-driven palate reset.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé": "Loire Pouilly-Fumé — Sauv Blanc with gun-flint smoky minerality, grapefruit, lime zest. The serious-bodied flinty structure cuts chilled shrimp's sweet brine and the citrus plays against cocktail-sauce bite. Strong Sauv Blanc for shrimp cocktail — more depth than NZ, more serious than Sancerre.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Domaine du Grand Tinel": "Never pair Grand Tinel with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp plus cocktail-sauce horseradish gets crushed by full body, black pepper, and garrigue, and the herbal earth has nowhere to land. Lead with Laurent Perrier Brut Champagne's bubble-driven palate reset.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Don Fulano Anejo": "Don Fulano Anejo's aged-agave character smothers the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- aged-agave register crowds the delicate shellfish frame. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Don Fulano Anejo for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Don Fulano Blanco": "Don Fulano Blanco with shrimp cocktail — refined highland blanco against cold shrimp. The craft agave cuts through cocktail sauce at the premium craft register. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Don Fulano Reposado": "Don Fulano Reposado with shrimp cocktail — highland reposado against cold shrimp. The vanilla-honey cuts the cocktail sauce cleanly; refined cold-seafood pairing. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Don Julio 1942": "Don Julio 1942 with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against iconic 1942. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Don Julio 70th": "Don Julio 70th with shrimp cocktail — filtered clarity against cold shrimp. The 70th is the most refined reposado pairing with cold seafood; it's closer to a premium blanco in character here. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Don Julio Blanco": "Don Julio Blanco with shrimp cocktail — benchmark blanco against cold shrimp and cocktail sauce. The citrus and clean agave cut through the horseradish with industry-standard precision. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Don Julio Reposado": "Shrimp Cocktail: cold shrimp and cocktail sauce meet Don Julio Reposado's citrus-forward agave. Brightness threads through the cocktail sauce's horseradish. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Drambuie": "Drambuie's sweet liqueur character clashes with the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- sweet liqueur is dessert energy — wrong place for the table's first course. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Drambuie lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Dunville's Single Malt": "Dunville's Single Malt's Irish whiskey smoothness overshadows the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the spirit weight crowds the delicate shellfish — no acid to clean the brine. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; the better calls are above. Pour the Dunville's Single Malt on the steak course instead.",
