  "Shrimp Cocktail|Elijah Craig Straight Rye": "Elijah Craig Straight Rye with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against HH rye. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Elk Cove Five Mountain": "Elk Cove Five Mountain's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift overshadows the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Elk Cove Five Mountain on the steak course instead.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Elk Cove Pinot Blanc": "Willamette Pinot Blanc — soft pear, white peach, delicate floral, refreshing acidity. The refreshing acid cuts chilled shrimp's sweet brine and the pear-peach fruit plays against cocktail-sauce bite. Peak medium-body white for shrimp cocktail — lighter than Chard, rounder than Sauv Blanc.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Elmer T. Lee": "Elmer T. Lee with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against namesake single-barrel. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Empress 1908 Gin": "Empress 1908 with shrimp cocktail — color-changing floral-citrus gin against cold shrimp. Excellent; Empress's rose-and-citrus profile elevates the classic cold app with visual-distinctive character the other Smooth/Citrus siblings don't offer.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Epoch Ingenuity": "Never pair Epoch with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp plus cocktail-sauce horseradish gets crushed by smoked meat, olive, and full body, and the crushed pepper has nowhere to land. Lead with Laurent Perrier Brut Champagne's bubble-driven palate reset.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Espresso Martini": "Espresso Martini's roasted-coffee martini richness overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- whiskey-cocktail weight is wrong for cold shellfish — the opener needs lift, not bitters. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a spirit-forward cocktail. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Espresso Martini for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Espresso Old Fashioned": "Espresso Old Fashioned's spirit-forward cocktail register overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the cocktail's weight is forward for the table's first course. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a spirit-forward cocktail. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Espresso Old Fashioned for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Evening Land Seven Springs": "Evening Land Seven Springs' red-fruit-and-spice elegance overshadows the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Evening Land Seven Springs for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon": "Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon's estate-Cab Napa character crowds out the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Far Niente Chardonnay": "Far Niente Chardonnay's bold butter-char acidity frames the shrimp's chilled sweetness — the crisp acidity lifts the shellfish without weight, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Faroe Island Salmon": "The salmon after the shrimp cocktail -- the oil-rich fish plays against the classic shrimp cocktail. Strong; the starter composes cleanly before the main.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi": "Never pair Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi with shrimp cocktail — Super Tuscan firm-tannin overshadows cold poached shrimp and tobacco-graphite clashes with cocktail-sauce horseradish. Lead with Veuve Clicquot, Raventós Cava, or French 75. Saffredi lives on the red-meat course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Faust Napa Valley Cabernet": "Faust Napa Cab against chilled sweet-briny shrimp — brooding tobacco-chocolate is the wrong axis for cold shellfish and cocktail sauce. Never layer. Route shrimp cocktail to Champagne, Sancerre, or Chablis and save Faust for the steak course where its brooding Napa character belongs.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía": "Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía's Tempranillo with vanilla-and-leather depth crowds out the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Fernet Branca": "Fernet Branca's nuclear bitter-menthol intensity sits beside the shrimp's chilled sweetness — the bitter herb edge overpowers the shellfish. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Fernet Menta": "Fernet Menta's crisp mint-menthol edge plays cleanly against the shrimp's chilled sweetness — the bitter herb edge overpowers the shellfish. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Filet Mignon": "Filet Mignon after the shrimp cocktail -- the chilled shrimp and citrus-horseradish bite refreshes the palate, the 10oz tenderloin following with clean grilled butter. Strong; the bright opener primes the lean cut.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Fireball Whisky": "Fireball Whisky's sweet liqueur character clashes with the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- sweet liqueur is dessert energy — wrong place for the table's first course. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; the better calls are above. Fireball Whisky lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Fisher Unity Pinot Noir": "Fisher Unity Pinot Noir's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift overshadows the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the elegant red is built for the entrée, not the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Fisher Unity Pinot Noir on the steak course instead.",
