  "Shrimp Cocktail|Gray Whale Gin": "Gray Whale with shrimp cocktail — ocean-botanical California gin against cold shrimp. Excellent; Gray Whale's 6-California-botanical profile elevates the classic cold app with ocean-conservation-mission distinction.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Green Chartreuse": "Green Chartreuse's bitter-herb aperitivo edge overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- bitter aperitivo flattens the opener's lighter register. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Green Chartreuse on the steak course instead.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Grey Goose Vodka": "Grey Goose with shrimp cocktail — luxury French wheat against cold shrimp. Excellent; Goose's silky finish elevates the classic cold app to a tasting pairing. Gold standard; the headline call at the table.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Grilled Caesar": "Shrimp Cocktail alongside the Caesar -- acid breaks the umami stack, the table earns the brighter note. Works; the openers share the table cleanly, sequence or share.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Gumbo": "The shrimp cocktail with the gumbo -- the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish meets the gumbo's spiced creole stew: bright-acid lifts the spiced course, the contrast settles the table. Works; both opening courses earn their place.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet": "Gundlach Bundschu Sonoma Cab against chilled sweet-briny shrimp — savory cedar-herb is the wrong axis for cold shellfish and cocktail sauce. Never layer. Route shrimp cocktail to Champagne, Sancerre, or Chablis and save the Rhinefarm Cab for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|HDW 100 Vodka": "HDW 100 with shrimp cocktail — 100-proof craft against cold shrimp. Excellent; HDW 100's herbal lift elevates the classic cold app at higher-proof register.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Hakushu 12 Year": "Hakushu 12 Year's lightly-peated Hakushu character finds neutral with the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish: the restrained whisky body threads the chilled shrimp, and the sandalwood-and-honey register softens the starter. Works; Remus 15 frames the two-cut plate at Gatsby-tribute register.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against BT single-barrel. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Hangar 1 Vodka": "Hangar 1 with shrimp cocktail — Alameda California craft against cold shrimp. Excellent; Hangar 1's floral lift elevates the classic cold app with California-blended distinctive character.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Head Fake": "Wheatley vodka, limoncello, triple sec, lemon, simple syrup — sugar rim. The Italian-citrus limoncello rounds the lemon and cuts chilled shrimp's sweet brine; the sugar rim plays against cocktail-sauce. Peak bright-citrus starter cocktail for shrimp cocktail — approachable lemon drop done right.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Heaven Hill 20 Year": "Heaven Hill 20 Year with shrimp cocktail — HH 20yr against cold shrimp. Avoid; bourbon wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond": "Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against 100-proof bond. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Heaven's Door 10 Year": "Heaven's Door 10 Year with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against aged Dylan bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Heitz Martha's Vineyard": "Iconic Napa Cab against chilled sweet-briny shrimp — Martha's Vineyard's concentrated dark fruit and cedar are wildly wrong for a cold shellfish classic. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Champagne, Sancerre, or Chablis; save the legendary Heitz for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Heitz Trailside Vineyard": "Heitz Trailside Rutherford Cab against chilled sweet-briny shrimp — refined mint-cedar is the wrong axis for cold shellfish and cocktail sauce. Never layer. Route shrimp cocktail to Champagne, Sancerre, or Chablis and save Heitz Trailside for steak where its historic-house character belongs.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Hendricks Flora Adora": "Flora Adora with shrimp cocktail — Hendrick's floral-garden Spring release against cold shrimp. Excellent; Flora Adora's lavish-floral profile elevates the classic cold app with distinctive spring-garden character.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Hendricks Gin": "Hendricks with shrimp cocktail — flagship cucumber-rose gin against cold shrimp. Excellent; Hendrick's perfumed signature elevates the classic cold app with distinctive low-juniper character.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Hendricks Grand Cabaret": "Grand Cabaret with shrimp cocktail — cocktail-culture Hendrick's fruit-release against cold shrimp. Excellent; Grand Cabaret's black-currant brightens the classic cold app with distinctive stage-show character.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Hendricks Neptunia": "Neptunia with shrimp cocktail — coastal-release Hendrick's against cold shrimp. Excellent; Neptunia's maritime character elevates the classic cold app with Scottish-sea terroir distinction.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Hendricks Orbium": "Orbium with shrimp cocktail — quinine-forward Hendrick's against cold shrimp. Excellent; Orbium's bitter-tonic character elevates the classic cold app with distinctive G-and-T-style lift.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Hennessy Cognac": "Hennessy Cognac's classic dried-fruit-and-vanilla cognac clashes with the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- cognac is wrong-course energy for the table's opener. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a cognac. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Hennessy Cognac for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against aged bonded HH. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Hibiki Japanese Harmony": "Hibiki Japanese Harmony's blended Japanese harmony sits alongside the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish: the restrained whisky body threads the chilled shrimp, and the green-fruit edge brightens the starter. Works; the 10-year holds without lifting.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Shrimp Cocktail and the honey carrots -- acid and sugar share the table, neither course pulls heavy. Works; both items hold their register, no clash.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|House Wedge": "The shrimp cocktail with the wedge -- the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish meets the wedge's iceberg-and-bleu cool crunch: the bright register pulls against the savory, the contrast lands. Works; both opening courses earn their place.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|I.W. Harper 15 Year": "I.W. Harper 15 with shrimp cocktail — historic-Kentucky 15yr against cold shrimp. Avoid; bourbon wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Il Colle Prosecco Superiore": "Glera from Veneto — bright and floral with white peach, green apple, and a clean citrus finish. The crisp bubbles cut chilled shrimp's sweet brine and play cleanly against cocktail-sauce horseradish bite. Peak starter pour — Prosecco-and-shrimp classic done right. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Inhibited": "Inhibited's chocolate-cocoa build sits with the shrimp's chilled sweetness — the cocktail lift carries the shellfish without weight. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Inverroche Gin": "Inverroche with shrimp cocktail — fynbos-floral South African gin against cold shrimp. Excellent; Inverroche's terroir-specific floral lift elevates the classic cold app with Cape-distinct character.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Iron Fish Gin": "Iron Fish with shrimp cocktail — Benzie County estate-gin against cold shrimp. Excellent; Iron Fish's Michigan-honey notes elevate the classic cold app with farm-to-bottle character.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks": "Ironfish Bourbon Mezcal Casks with shrimp cocktail — northern MI mezcal-cask against cold shrimp. Avoid; bourbon wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Isaac Bowman Port Finish": "Isaac Bowman Port Finish with shrimp cocktail — Virginia port-finish against cold shrimp. Avoid; bourbon wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|J Davies Ferrington Vineyards": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards' silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. J Davies Ferrington Vineyards belongs on the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon": "J. Davies Diamond Mountain Cab against chilled sweet-briny shrimp — firm graphite-mineral is the wrong axis for cold shellfish and cocktail sauce. Never layer. Route shrimp cocktail to Champagne, Sancerre, or Chablis and save J. Davies for the steak course where its volcanic character belongs.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Jack Daniel's 12 Year": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with shrimp cocktail — 12yr aged Tennessee against cold shrimp. Avoid; Tennessee wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Jack Daniel's Bonded": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with shrimp cocktail — Bottled-in-Bond Tennessee against cold shrimp. Avoid; Tennessee wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Jack Daniel's Old No. 7": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7 with shrimp cocktail — charcoal-mellowed Tennessee against cold shrimp. Avoid; Tennessee wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Jack Daniel's Sinatra Select": "JD Sinatra Select with shrimp cocktail — Sinatra Barrels Tennessee against cold shrimp. Avoid; Tennessee wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Jameson Irish Whiskey": "Jameson Irish Whiskey's classic Irish blend smoothness overshadows the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the spirit weight crowds the delicate shellfish — no acid to clean the brine. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Jameson Irish Whiskey on the steak course instead.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir": "Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Reserve the Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis": "Burgundy Chablis — unoaked Chard with flint, chalk, lemon, green apple. The lean precise acid cuts chilled shrimp's sweet brine and the flint-chalk plays against cocktail-sauce bite. Strong classical unoaked white for shrimp cocktail — French precision on the classic starter.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E.": "Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E. with shrimp cocktail — sea-aged L.E. against cold shrimp. Avoid; save the collector bottle.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Jefferson's Ocean Voyage 23": "Jefferson's Ocean Voyage 23 with shrimp cocktail — ship-aged bourbon against cold shrimp. Avoid; bourbon wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Jefferson's Reserve": "Jefferson's Reserve with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against blended honey-vanilla. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Jefferson's Reserve VR Twin Oak": "Jefferson's Reserve VR Twin Oak with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against double-barrel. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Jim Beam Black Label": "Jim Beam Black Label with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against aged Beam. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Jim Beam White Label": "Jim Beam White Label with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against entry bourbon. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Johnnie Walker Black": "JW Black with shrimp cocktail — 12yr balanced blended against cold shrimp. Avoid; Scotch wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Johnnie Walker Blue": "Johnnie Walker Blue's Highland-scotch character fights the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Johnnie Walker Blue for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Johnnie Walker Red": "JW Red with shrimp cocktail — bold-smoke entry JW against cold shrimp. Avoid; Scotch wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon": "Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon's classical-Napa Cab elegance overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Joseph Mellot Sancerre": "Loire Sancerre — crisp refined Sauv Blanc, white grapefruit, chalk, fresh herbs, tension finish. The tension-filled structure cuts chilled shrimp's sweet brine and the grapefruit-herb plays against cocktail-sauce bite. Peak benchmark Sauv Blanc for shrimp cocktail — precision pairing, sense-of-place wine. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Jubilation by Colgin": "Cult Napa Cab blend against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — firm-tannin Colgin structure and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Jubilation for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Jung and Wulff Guyana": "Jung and Wulff Guyana's aged-rum register with molasses and oak depth overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the spirit's weight is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Jung and Wulff Guyana lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Jung and Wulff Trinidad": "Jung and Wulff Trinidad's aged-rum register with molasses and oak depth overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the spirit's weight is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Jung and Wulff Trinidad for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Kahlua": "Kahlua's sweet liqueur character overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- sweet liqueur on cold shellfish is wrong-course energy — too forward for a clean opener. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Reserve the Kahlua for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Kansas City": "Kansas City after the shrimp cocktail -- the chilled shrimp's citrus-horseradish bite cleans the palate, the 18oz strip's clean savory grain following with restrained char. Strong; the bright opener primes the strip's middle register.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Keenan Chardonnay": "Keenan Chardonnay's bold apple-butter acidity finds register with the shrimp's chilled sweetness — the crisp acidity lifts the shellfish without weight, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Keenan Mernet": "Spring Mountain Napa Mernet against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — mountain-grown Merlot-Cab and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Keenan Mernet for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against premium KO. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Kentucky Owl Confiscated": "Kentucky Owl Confiscated with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against KO Confiscated. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's": "Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's Irish whiskey smoothness fights the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône": "Never pair Kermit Lynch Rhône with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp plus cocktail-sauce horseradish gets crushed by pepper and garrigue, and the red-fruit has nowhere to land. Lead with Laurent Perrier Brut Champagne's bubble-driven palate reset.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Ketel One Vodka": "Ketel One with shrimp cocktail — Dutch wheat from the Nolet family distillery. Excellent; Ketel's clean citrus-floral finish lifts cold shrimp with Dutch-bar precision — where Tito's rounds and Goose softens, Ketel crisps.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Knickerbocker Gin": "Knickerbocker with shrimp cocktail — New Holland hop-influenced gin against cold shrimp. Excellent; Knickerbocker's distinctive hop-herbal character elevates the classic cold app with brewer's-heritage distinction.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Knob Creek": "Knob Creek with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against bold high-rye. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Knob Creek 12 Year": "Knob Creek 12 Year with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against aged 100-proof. Avoid; reach for a wine that fits the plate.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Knob Creek 15 Year": "Knob Creek 15 with shrimp cocktail — aged Beam KC against cold shrimp. Avoid; bourbon wrong for cold seafood.",
