  "Shrimp Cocktail|Komos Anejo Reserva": "Komos Anejo Reserva's aged-agave character overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- aged tequila is too forward for the opening course. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Komos Anejo Reserva on the steak course instead.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Komos Crystallino Anejo": "Komos Crystallino Anejo's aged-agave character smothers the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- aged-agave register crowds the delicate shellfish frame. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an añejo tequila. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Komos Crystallino Anejo lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Komos Extra Anejo": "Komos Extra Añejo with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against Riedel-luxury aged. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Komos Rosa Reposado": "Komos Rosa Reposado with shrimp cocktail — rosé-finished reposado against cold shrimp. The strawberry and cherry cut through the cocktail sauce in a way straight reposados can't; wine-cask seafood pairing. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Lagavulin 8": "Lagavulin 8 with shrimp cocktail — cold poached shrimp and cocktail sauce against peated Islay is a miss across the board. The 8-year's brightness doesn't save it. Avoid; reach for gin or a clean vodka.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Lail Vineyards Blueprint": "Historically-pedigreed Napa Cab against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — full-body Blueprint and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Blueprint for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée": "Historically-significant Napa Cab against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — firm-tannin Daniel Cuvée and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Daniel Cuvée for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Lalo Silver": "Lalo Silver with shrimp cocktail — additive-free craft blanco against cold shrimp. The clean heritage-craft agave threads through cocktail sauce with family-lineage distinctiveness. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Laphroaig 10": "Laphroaig 10 with shrimp cocktail — iodine-on-iodine isn't the echo it sounds like; it's just too much. The shrimp gets erased. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Larceny Small Batch": "Larceny Small Batch with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against wheated honey. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé": "Pinot Noir Champagne rosé from Tours-sur-Marne — silky mousse with strawberry, raspberry, and cherry. The red-berry profile cuts chilled shrimp's sweet brine and the long elegant finish plays against cocktail-sauce bite. Peak rosé Champagne for shrimp cocktail — benchmark starter pairing. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut": "Chardonnay-blend Champagne — green apple, lemon zest, whisper of brioche, vibrant acidity. The high-acid structure cuts chilled shrimp's sweet brine and plays precisely against cocktail-sauce bite. Peak Champagne for shrimp cocktail — classical pairing at benchmark quality. Gold standard; pour without second-guessing.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Le Garenne Rosé": "Loire Pinot Noir rosé — pale salmon, strawberry, watermelon, floral, crisp dry. The fresh-fruit finish cuts chilled shrimp's sweet brine and the berry-floral plays against cocktail-sauce bite. Peak summer rosé for shrimp cocktail — seasonal lightness on the classic chilled starter.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Le Ragnaie Brunello": "Italy's-most-prestigious Brunello against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — firm-tannin Le Ragnaie and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Le Ragnaie for aged beef.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Le Volte dell'Ornellaia": "Tuscan Merlot-driven blend against chilled sweet-briny shrimp — Le Volte's medium-full red structure is the wrong axis for cold shellfish. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Champagne, Sancerre, or Chablis; save Le Volte for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Lemon Lavender Gin Martini": "Plymouth gin, lemon, honey lavender syrup, Prosecco float. The lemon-and-honey cuts chilled shrimp's brine and lavender adds aromatic complexity against cocktail-sauce. Peak cocktail pairing for shrimp cocktail — shares the bright, light profile with the starter.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Les Pallières Raciné": "Never pair Raciné with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp plus cocktail-sauce horseradish gets crushed by garrigue, iron, and full body, and the old-vine complexity has nowhere to land. Lead with Laurent Perrier Brut Champagne's bubble-driven palate reset.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Liberator Gin": "Liberator with shrimp cocktail — Valentine Distilling Michigan craft against cold shrimp. Excellent; Liberator delivers the classic cold app with Ferndale-hometown-craft character.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Licor 43": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character smothers the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- sugar buries the delicate shellfish without any acid to balance. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a digestif. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Licor 43 for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Limoncello": "Shrimp Cocktail: this delicate seafood starter's briny-fresh sweetness meets this sweet cream liqueur's dessert-adjacent lushness. Liqueur sweetness or herbal complexity against a starter — wrong register typically. Works as a digestif move.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir: this elegant red's cherry-bright, silky-tannin frame meets this delicate seafood starter's briny-fresh sweetness. Elegant red's cherry and silk mirror the starter's register — light-on-light or bright-on-rich depending on the plate. Works cleanly.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Little Book": "Little Book with shrimp cocktail — Fred Noe annual against cold shrimp. Avoid; barrel-proof wrong for cold seafood.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Loaded Potato": "Shrimp Cocktail and the loaded potato together -- acid plays against richness, the contrast holds across the courses. Works; the table opens with both, no clash either way.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Lobster Mac": "The shrimp cocktail and the lobster mac -- shellfish-on-shellfish, the meal goes redundant. Avoid; the table reads heavy without payoff. Suggest Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut for the shrimp cocktail, or Cowboy Ribeye, Far Niente Chardonnay, or The Tomahawk for the lobster mac.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Loch Lomond 20 Year": "Loch Lomond 20 Year's complex 20yr aged Highland fights the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a scotch. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Loch Lomond 20 Year on the steak course instead.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Lock Stock & Barrel Rye": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against premium sourced. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Long Road Gin": "Long Road with shrimp cocktail — GR craft Michigan-botanical gin against cold shrimp. Excellent; Long Road delivers the classic cold app with Grand Rapids-pride hometown character.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Los Vecinos Mezcal": "Los Vecinos Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- mezcal smoke obliterates delicate shellfish — needs sparkling or sancerre. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a mezcal. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Los Vecinos Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Louis XIII Cognac": "Louis XIII Cognac's luxury-icon cognac depth mis-pairs with the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- a luxury cognac is wrong moment for the opener — save it for after the meal. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an icon cognac. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Louis XIII Cognac lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Shrimp Cocktail|Lucano Amaro": "Lucano Amaro's bitter-herb aperitivo edge overwhelms the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- amaro bitterness on cold shellfish flattens the delicate brine — needs sparkling instead. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Lucano Amaro for the steak course.",
