  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Chocolate Cake": "Siete Leguas Reposado's rested-agave body sits alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the aged-agave weight wraps the chocolate cake, and the caramel-agave register brightens the dessert. Works; the wine-cask character adds dimension but not standout.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Clam Chowder": "Siete Leguas Reposado's rested-agave body finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the barrel-rested body handles the chowder, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Cowboy Ribeye": "Siete Leguas Reposado with the Cowboy Ribeye — tahona-crushed reposado against cap fat. Strong; the rustic craft character is more at home than polished reposados here, though G4 High Proof brings more grip.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Crab Cake": "Siete Leguas Reposado with crab cake — traditional agave's earthier character against lump crab. The tahona-crushed craft gives the pairing more texture than Don Julio's balance brings; distinctive. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Creamed Spinach": "Siete Leguas Reposado's aged-agave character finds neutral with the creamed spinach's rich bechamel-laced greens: the añejo register carries the creamed spinach, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; ceremonial over-specified.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Creamy Potato": "Siete Leguas Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the rested-agave depth sits with the potato soup, and the cooked-agave note underlines the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Creme Brulee": "Siete Leguas Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the brulee, and the caramel-agave register brightens the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Escargot": "Siete Leguas Reposado's crisp agave-earth character matches the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the añejo depth cuts the umami fat, and the mineral edge mirrors the briny meat. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Faroe Island Salmon": "Siete Leguas Reposado with the salmon — traditional agave against salmon richness. Strong; the craft character is distinctive but not as refined a salmon match as Don Fulano or Don Julio 70th.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Filet Mignon": "Siete Leguas Reposado with the filet — tahona-crushed traditional character against the 10oz cut. The rustic agave gives the filet a different vocabulary than polished reposados; a craft-forward call for the cut. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|French Onion": "Siete Leguas Reposado's añejo-pour depth finds neutral with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the French onion, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Grilled Caesar": "Siete Leguas Reposado with the grilled Caesar — tahona-crushed traditional against charred romaine and anchovy. Strong; the earthy agave matches the Caesar's weight.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Gumbo": "Siete Leguas Reposado's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the barrel-rested body handles the gumbo, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; accessible aged composes with the plate.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Siete Leguas Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register leans against the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the añejo register carries the honey carrots, and the caramel-agave register brightens the side. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|House Wedge": "Siete Leguas Reposado with the House Wedge — tahona-crushed traditional against iceberg and bleu. The earthier agave cuts the bleu distinctly; craft reposado for salad orders. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Kansas City": "Siete Leguas Reposado with the KC — traditional tahona-crushed agave, family-distillery craft. Rustic, earthier character than Don Julio's polished benchmark; the strip's marbling meets the traditional agave with real grip. Old-school tequila for guests who want character. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Loaded Potato": "Siete Leguas Reposado's aged-agave character finds neutral with the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the barrel-rested body handles the loaded potato soup, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; approachable agave cuts the glaze but not marquee.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Lobster Mac": "Siete Leguas Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the barrel-rested body handles the lobster mac, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Market Fish": "Siete Leguas Reposado's aged-agave character leans against the market fish's clean white-fish flesh: the barrel-rested body handles the market fish, and the oak threads the plate. Works; distinctive craft character lifts the fish depending on preparation.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Mocha Creme": "Siete Leguas Reposado's añejo-pour depth leans against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the rested-agave depth sits with the mocha creme, and the soft-spice note softens the dessert. Works; Riedel-luxury over-specified.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Mushroom Bisque": "Siete Leguas Reposado's aged-agave character finds neutral with the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the mushroom bisque, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; Ultra over-specified for small plate.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Mushrooms": "Siete Leguas Reposado with the mushrooms — tahona-crushed traditional against earthy umami. Strong; the rustic agave finds mushroom earth cleanly.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Siete Leguas Reposado's aged-agave character reads alongside the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the oak-aged tequila body threads the PB brownie, and the oak threads the dessert. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Porterhouse": "Siete Leguas Reposado's crisp agave-earth character sits with the porterhouse's two-cut character — the añejo weight matches the cap-fat, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Prime Tartare": "Siete Leguas Reposado with the tartare — tahona-crushed against raw beef. Works; traditional agave is a distinctive counterpoint to tartare's mineral depth.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Rainbow Trout": "Siete Leguas Reposado's aged-agave character finds neutral with the trout's delicate flesh: the barrel-rested body handles the trout, and the oak threads the plate. Works; the 70th's clarity gets overwhelmed by the dish's density.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Roast Half Chicken": "Siete Leguas Reposado with the roast half chicken — rustic reposado against roasted chicken. Works; clean but not a standout.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Siete Leguas Reposado's añejo-pour depth sits alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the oak-aged tequila body threads the chickpea soup, and the soft-spice note softens the bowl. Works; refined but not a standout.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Siete Leguas Reposado's aged-agave character finds neutral with the halibut's salt-cured flesh: the añejo register carries the halibut, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Siete Leguas Reposado's barrel-aged tequila weight sits alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the añejo register carries the garlic spinach, and the cooked-agave note underlines the side. Works; aged-but-clear character composes with the dish.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Seafood Tower": "Siete Leguas Reposado's añejo-pour depth leans against the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the barrel-rested body handles the seafood tower, and the cooked-agave note underlines the starter. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Seared Scallops": "Siete Leguas Reposado with seared scallops — rustic agave against caramelized scallop. The traditional craft character meets the sear in a different register than filtered or balanced reposados. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Seasonal Soup": "Siete Leguas Reposado's añejo-pour depth finds neutral with the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the seasonal soup, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Seasonal Vegetables": "Siete Leguas Reposado's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the aged-agave weight wraps the seasonal vegetables, and the oak threads the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Shrimp Bisque": "Siete Leguas Reposado with shrimp bisque — rustic agave against cream-based seafood. Strong; the craft traditional character sits with the soup in a distinctive register.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Shrimp Cocktail": "Siete Leguas Reposado with shrimp cocktail — traditional agave against cold shrimp and cocktail sauce. The rustic character threads through the horseradish with grip polished reposados lack. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Swordfish": "Siete Leguas Reposado's aged-agave character sits alongside the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak: the añejo register carries the swordfish, and the oak threads the plate. Works; iconic extra añejo is composed with the dessert.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|The Tomahawk": "Siete Leguas Reposado with the Tomahawk — traditional reposado against massive cut. Avoid; bourbon or scotch territory.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Tomato Basil": "Siete Leguas Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register reads alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the barrel-rested body handles the tomato basil, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Truffle Fries": "Siete Leguas Reposado with truffle fries — traditional agave against truffle-parmesan. Works; the earthy craft character doesn't quite lift the truffle the way polished reposados suggest they might.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Siete Leguas Reposado's aged-agave character sits alongside the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the oak-aged tequila body threads the tuna, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Siete Leguas Reposado|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Siete Leguas Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register reads alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the añejo register carries the curry, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; clean accessible match.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Asparagus": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character crowds the asparagus' green-vegetal edge -- the side needs a crisper register to carry it cleanly. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Joseph Mellot Sancerre, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Silver Oak — Alexander Valley Cab with American-oak vanilla, coconut, dill, ripe cassis, plum. The lush body cuts au gratin's cheese-and-cream weight and the vanilla-dill plays against the golden crust. Works as recognizable Cab for au gratin — American-oak signature on the decadent side.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Beignets": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character jars against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Bone Marrow": "Silver Oak — Alexander Valley Cab, American-oak vanilla, coconut, dill, ripe cassis, plum. The lush body meets marrow's rendered-fat richness and the vanilla-dill frames the bone depth distinctively. Strong recognizable Cab for marrow — American-oak signature, though firmer Cabs like Frias or Ghost Block peak higher for the starter.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Bone-In Filet": "American-oak vanilla, coconut, and dill against the bone-in filet's richer marble. The oak's sweetness has more surface to meet here than on the standard filet. Soft tannin keeps it approachable — a familiar label for first-time steakhouse guests. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Broccoli Cheddar": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character clashes with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Broccolini": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character crowds the broccolini's tender green stalks -- the side needs a crisper register to carry it cleanly. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Brussels and Belly": "Alexander Valley Cab — American-oak vanilla, coconut, dill, ripe cassis, plum. The lush body handles pork-belly fat and the vanilla-dill plays against charred brussels. Strong recognizable Cab for Brussels and Belly — Silver Oak's American-oak signature cuts the rich starter with distinctive lushness.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Burrata": "Silver Oak American-oak Cab against burrata's creamy-delicate center — lush vanilla-dill crushes the milk and basil-tomato-pistachio clashes with ripe cassis-plum. Never pair. Route burrata to rosé, Pinot Blanc, or Sancerre and keep Silver Oak for the steak course.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Butternut Squash": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character overwhelms the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Carrot Cake": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Cheesecake": "Silver Oak — Alexander Valley Cab, American-oak vanilla, coconut, dill, ripe cassis. The lush body meets cheesecake's dense cream and the vanilla plays against the tangy richness. Works as recognizable Cab for cheesecake — American-oak signature plus cream pairing, though dessert wines peak higher.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Chilean Seabass": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Chocolate Brownie": "Alexander Valley Cab — American-oak vanilla, coconut, dill, ripe cassis, plum. The lush body meets chocolate-brownie fudge and the vanilla-dill plays against the rich dessert distinctively. Works as Silver Oak for brownie — American-oak signature Cab-on-chocolate, name-recognition sells the moment.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Chocolate Cake": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character jars against the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Clam Chowder": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character flattens the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- the wine's structure sits on top of the bisque's cream instead of integrating. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Cowboy Ribeye": "Silver Oak — Alexander Valley Sonoma Cab aged exclusively in American oak, giving distinctive vanilla, coconut, dill alongside ripe cassis, plum, soft polished tannin. The American-oak lushness handles Cowboy's marbled bone-in richness directly. Peak recognizable Cab for Cowboy — guests who know Cabernet know Silver Oak. Gold standard; pour without second-guessing.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Crab Cake": "Silver Oak Alexander Valley Cab against crab cake's delicate sweet shellfish — American-oak vanilla-dill crushes romesco-and-crab. Never pair. Route crab cake to Chablis, Sancerre, or Champagne and keep Silver Oak for the steak course where its recognizable American-oak signature shines.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Creamed Spinach": "Silver Oak — Alexander Valley Cab, American-oak vanilla, coconut, dill, ripe cassis, plum. The lush body cuts creamed spinach's dairy weight and the vanilla-dill plays against the earthy sauce. Peak recognizable Cab for creamed spinach — American-oak signature on the classic steakhouse side. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Creamy Potato": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character overwhelms the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Creme Brulee": "Alexander Valley Cab — American-oak vanilla, coconut, dill, ripe cassis. The lush body can handle crème brûlée's custard-and-burnt-sugar, though Cab-with-custard stretches the pairing axis. Works as Silver Oak for crème brûlée — American-oak signature, though dessert wines peak higher for the custard.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Escargot": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cassis-oak tannin holds the line with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the firm tannin cuts the rich starter, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Faroe Island Salmon": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character fights the salmon's rich oily flesh -- the red's tannin and the salmon's rich oils refuse to integrate. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Filet Mignon": "Silver Oak — Alexander Valley Cab with American-oak vanilla, coconut, dill, ripe cassis, plum, soft tannin. The lush body meets butter-tender filet's lean sweetness and the vanilla-dill echoes escargot-butter toppers. Strong recognizable Cab for filet — American-oak lushness, though leaner Cabs peak higher on the delicate cut.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|French Onion": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cassis-oak tannin holds with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Grilled Caesar": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cassis-oak tannin sits alongside the Caesar's char-and-anchovy — the opulent body overshoots the leaf-and-acid plate, and the cassis plays against the grilled char. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Gumbo": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character jars against the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character fights the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- red tannin and the glaze's sugar pull against each other — sugar reads cloying, tannin bitter. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|House Wedge": "Silver Oak — Alexander Valley Cab, American-oak vanilla, coconut, dill. The lush body cuts iceberg-and-bacon and the vanilla plays against blue cheese dressing. Works as recognizable Cab for the wedge — American-oak signature red, though whites or rosés peak higher for the classic wedge.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Kansas City": "Alexander Valley Cab — American-oak vanilla, coconut, dill, ripe cassis, plum, soft tannin. The lush American-oak body meets Kansas City's lean-bold marbled strip and the vanilla-dill plays against the beefy char. Peak recognizable Cab for Kansas City — Silver Oak's distinctive American-oak signature on the classic strip. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Loaded Potato": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cassis-oak tannin sits alongside the loaded potato's richness — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Lobster Mac": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon: this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight meets this rich, creamy side's dairy-driven indulgence. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A capable pair; richness aligns if not perfectly. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Market Fish": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character clashes with the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Mocha Creme": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character fights the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- the dry red and the chocolate's sugar refuse each other — tannin reads bitter on the finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Mushroom Bisque": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cassis-oak tannin finds neutral with the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; capable alongside.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Mushrooms": "Silver Oak — Alexander Valley Cab with American-oak vanilla, coconut, dill, ripe cassis, plum. The lush body meshes with mushroom umami and the vanilla-dill frames the sauté. Strong recognizable Cab for mushrooms — American-oak signature works, though savory Cabs like Gundlach peak higher on earth-on-earth match.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character flattens the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Porterhouse": "Alexander Valley Cab — American-oak vanilla, coconut, dill, ripe cassis, plum, soft tannin. The lush body frames Porterhouse's dual-texture strip-and-filet and the vanilla-dill plays against both lean and fatty sides. Peak recognizable Cab for Porterhouse — Silver Oak's American-oak signature on the dual-cut classic. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Prime Tartare": "Silver Oak American-oak Cab against prime tartare's raw-iron richness — lush vanilla-dill crushes the delicate seasoned beef. Never pair. Route tartare to Champagne, Sancerre, or Chablis and save Silver Oak for the steak course where its American-oak signature peaks.",
