  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Roast Half Chicken": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's bold cassis-oak tannin sits beside the chicken's herbed crisp skin — the concentrated body carries the herb-crisped bird, and the cassis plays against the grilled char. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character jars against the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon belongs on the steak course.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character clashes with the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character clashes with the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens -- tannin on raw green vegetable reads astringent without payoff. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Evening Land Seven Springs, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Seafood Tower": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Seared Scallops": "American-oak Alexander Valley Cab against seared scallops' clean pan-sear — lush vanilla-dill obliterates delicate shellfish sweetness. Never layer. Route scallops to Chablis, Sancerre, or Pinot Blanc and save Silver Oak for the steak course where its American-oak signature peaks.",
  "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon|Seasonal Soup": "Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon's American-oak Cab character jars against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
