  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Burrata": "Organic Napa Cab against burrata's creamy-delicate center — Lyndenhurst's full-body plum-violet structure overwhelms the starter. Never pair. Route burrata to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Prosecco; keep Lyndenhurst for the steak course.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Butternut Squash": "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst's Napa estate Cab with structured cassis overwhelms the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream -- the red is built for protein weight, not a light soup or salad base. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Spottswoode Lyndenhurst belongs on the steak course.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Carrot Cake": "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst's Napa estate Cab with structured cassis flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Spottswoode Lyndenhurst lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Cheesecake": "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst's Napa estate Cab with structured cassis pulls against the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- the red's dry-fruit register has no bridge to dessert tang or sugar. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not an elegant red. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Spottswoode Lyndenhurst lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Chilean Seabass": "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst's Napa estate Cab with structured cassis fights the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the red's tannin and the salmon's rich oils refuse to integrate. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Spottswoode Lyndenhurst for the steak course.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Chocolate Brownie": "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst's Napa estate Cab with structured cassis jars against the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Spottswoode Lyndenhurst for the steak course.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Chocolate Cake": "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst's Napa estate Cab with structured cassis clashes with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- savory tannin sits awkwardly on cocoa weight without resolving. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Spottswoode Lyndenhurst for the steak course.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Clam Chowder": "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst's Napa estate Cab with structured cassis clashes with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Spottswoode Lyndenhurst lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Cowboy Ribeye": "St. Helena Napa Cab — Spottswoode organic family estate, plum, dark cherry, violet, silky medium tannin, full body. The full body handles ribeye's big marbled build and the violet plays against beefy char. Strong organic Napa Cab for ribeye — Spottswoode family story on the bold cut.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Crab Cake": "Organic Napa Cab against crab cake's delicate sweet meat — Lyndenhurst's full-body plum-violet structure buries the shellfish. Never pair. Route crab cake to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Lyndenhurst for filet, strip, or the steak course.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Creamed Spinach": "St. Helena Napa Cab — Spottswoode organic family estate, plum, dark cherry, violet, silky medium tannin. The silky tannin cuts béchamel's dairy weight and the violet plays against the spinach base. Peak organic Napa Cab for creamed spinach — Spottswoode estate polish reframes the rich side. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Creamy Potato": "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst's Napa estate Cab with structured cassis clashes with the potato soup's silky-bodied cream -- red tannin on a cream-based course reads astringent — no acid to bridge dairy and structure. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Spottswoode Lyndenhurst on the steak course instead.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Creme Brulee": "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst's Napa estate Cab with structured cassis jars against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the Spottswoode Lyndenhurst on the steak course instead.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Escargot": "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst's bold cherry-floral cassis finds register with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the Cab structure meets the savory depth, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Faroe Island Salmon": "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst's Napa estate Cab with structured cassis clashes with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Spottswoode Lyndenhurst for the steak course.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Filet Mignon": "St. Helena Napa Cab — Spottswoode certified-organic family estate second label, plum, dark cherry, violet, silky medium tannin, full body. The silky structure meets butter-tender filet's delicate sweetness and the violet plays against escargot-butter. Peak organic Napa Cab for filet — estate story on the delicate cut. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|French Onion": "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst's Napa estate Cab with structured cassis leans against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the structured-Cab depth wraps the French onion, and the cassis frames the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Grilled Caesar": "St. Helena Napa Cab — Spottswoode organic family estate, plum, dark cherry, violet, silky medium tannin. The silky tannin cuts anchovy-parmesan dressing and the violet plays against grilled-romaine char. Works as organic Napa Cab for grilled Caesar — Spottswoode family story on the layered salad.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Gumbo": "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst's Napa estate Cab with structured cassis jars against the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- the dry-fruit register fights warm broth without resolving — needs crisp white or aperitivo. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Spottswoode Lyndenhurst for the steak course.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst's Napa estate Cab with structured cassis fights the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- red tannin and the glaze's sugar pull against each other — sugar reads cloying, tannin bitter. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Spottswoode Lyndenhurst for the steak course.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|House Wedge": "St. Helena Napa Cab — Spottswoode organic family estate, plum, dark cherry, violet, silky medium tannin. The silky tannin cuts iceberg-and-bacon and the plum plays against blue cheese dressing. Works as organic Napa Cab for the wedge — Spottswoode polish reframes the classic salad; whites peak higher.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Kansas City": "St. Helena Napa Cab — Spottswoode organic family estate, plum, dark cherry, violet, silky medium tannin. The silky tannin meets Kansas City's lean-bold marbled strip and the violet plays against beefy char. Peak organic Napa Cab for the strip — Spottswoode family story on the American cut. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst|Loaded Potato": "Spottswoode Lyndenhurst's bold cherry-floral cassis plays cleanly against the loaded potato's richness — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
