  "Swordfish|The Happy Wife": "The Happy Wife's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift mis-pairs with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- light cocktail register is wrong for a main protein. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a light cocktail. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve The Happy Wife for the steak course.",
  "Swordfish|The Manhattan": "The Manhattan's classic Manhattan with rye-and-vermouth depth clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- a whiskey-forward cocktail is built for the cut, not the fish or chicken course. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a spirit-forward cocktail. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. The Manhattan lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Swordfish|The Prisoner Red Blend": "The Prisoner Red Blend's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- tannin against rare-seared crust reads astringent without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. The Prisoner Red Blend belongs on the steak course.",
  "Swordfish|Thomas H. Handy Sazerac Rye": "Thomas H. Handy Sazerac Rye's rye-spice character clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon's sweet weight crowds the rare crust's clean char. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Thomas H. Handy Sazerac Rye for the steak course.",
  "Swordfish|Thomas S. Moore Chardonnay Cask": "Thomas S. Moore Chardonnay Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Thomas S. Moore Chardonnay Cask for the steak course.",
  "Swordfish|Titos Vodka": "Titos Vodka's Texas-corn-workhorse neutrality holds steady against the swordfish's meaty flesh — the neutral profile frames the fish cleanly, and the clean profile carries the herb butter. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Swordfish|Toki Suntory Japanese Whisky": "Toki Suntory Japanese Whisky's entry Suntory Toki character finds neutral with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak: the entry Suntory body sits with the swordfish, and the citrus lifts the plate. Works; BIB structure is a touch over-specified for this dish.",
  "Swordfish|Tomato Basil": "Swordfish after the tomato basil -- the bright tomato-basil acid cleans the palate, the swordfish following with meaty pan-finished steak the acid sharpened the palate for. Strong; acid into the dense fish reads classic.",
  "Swordfish|Transfusion": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build holds steady against the swordfish's meaty flesh — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Swordfish|Trombo Cedano Reposado": "Trombo Cedano Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register sits alongside the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the swordfish, and the oak threads the plate. Works; approachable agave is a gentle counterpoint.",
  "Swordfish|Truffle Fries": "Swordfish alongside the truffle fries -- the savory course rounds the protein, the meal reads layered. Works; the side carries cleanly with the swordfish.",
  "Swordfish|Tullamore D.E.W.": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Tullamore D.E.W. for the steak course.",
  "Swordfish|Venge Family Reserve": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- tannin against rare-seared crust reads astringent without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Venge Family Reserve lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Swordfish|Venge Scout's Honor": "Venge Scout's Honor's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift overshadows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- dark-fruit weight crowds the seared sesame crust — needs a sparkling or crisp white for lift. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Hold the Venge Scout's Honor for the steak course.",
  "Swordfish|Venge Silencieux": "Venge Silencieux's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- tannin against rare-seared crust reads astringent without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Venge Silencieux for the steak course.",
  "Swordfish|Vesper": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build reads alongside the swordfish's meaty flesh — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Swordfish|Veuve Clicquot Brut": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's biscuit-apple acidity sits with the swordfish's meaty flesh — the bright acidity frames the fish without weight, and the brioche notes meet the herb butter. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Swordfish|Vieux Carré": "Vieux Carré's spirit-forward cocktail register fights the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- cocktail bitterness pulls against the savory sear without resolving. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a spirit-forward cocktail. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Vieux Carré for the steak course.",
  "Swordfish|Villon Cognac": "Villon Cognac's modern profile and soft elderflower edge fights the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- cognac's aged register pulls against the savory sear without resolving. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a cognac. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Villon Cognac for the steak course.",
  "Swordfish|Vin Santo": "Vin Santo's Tuscan dried-fruit-and-honey sweetness flattens the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- sweet wine dulls the sear's clean char — savory main deserves a dry pour. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Vin Santo for the steak course.",
  "Swordfish|Weller 107": "Weller 107's bigger-body wheated buries scallop sweetness overwhelms the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Weller 107 on the steak course instead.",
  "Swordfish|Weller 12 Year": "Weller 12 Year's aged wheated honey-vanilla character swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Weller 12 Year for the steak course.",
  "Swordfish|Weller Millennium": "Weller Millennium's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Weller Millennium on the steak course instead.",
  "Swordfish|Weller Special Reserve": "Weller Special Reserve's wheated soft-vanilla character swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Weller Special Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Swordfish|Wheatley Vodka": "Wheatley Vodka's crisp cream neutrality holds steady against the swordfish's meaty flesh — the neutral profile frames the fish cleanly. Strong; a steady recommendation at the table.",
  "Swordfish|WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel Rye": "WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel Rye's rye-spice character clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon's sweet weight crowds the rare crust's clean char. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel Rye belongs on the steak course.",
