  "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle|Grilled Caesar": "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the Caesar's charred-romaine and anchovy edge -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Green Chartreuse, Tanqueray Gin, or Scavino Barolo, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle on the steak course instead.",
  "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle|Gumbo": "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the gumbo's spiced creole stew -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi, or Muga Reserva, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle's dessert-wine sweetness doubles down on the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness -- sweet wine and a sweet glaze double the sugar register — no foil. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, not a dessert wine. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle|House Wedge": "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle's dessert-wine sweetness jars against the wedge's iceberg-and-bleu cool crunch -- sweet wine on cold lettuce refuses the salad's clean register. The plate deserves St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Weller 12 Year, or Le Garenne Rosé, not a dessert wine. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle on the steak course instead.",
  "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle|Kansas City": "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the KC's lean-bold strip with savory grain -- dessert wine belongs after the meal, not alongside the steak. The plate deserves Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, Pio Cesare Barbaresco, or Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye, not a dessert wine. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Save the Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle for another course.",
  "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle|Loaded Potato": "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup -- the soup-salad course needs acid, not dessert sugar. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Save the Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle for the steak course.",
