  "The BG|Cheesecake": "The BG's crisp citrus-earth build finds neutral with the cheesecake's custard cream — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the honey threads the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "The BG|Chilean Seabass": "The BG's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- cocktail sweetness fights the rich fish's natural oils. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a light cocktail. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour The BG on the steak course instead.",
  "The BG|Chocolate Brownie": "The BG's crisp citrus-earth build sits alongside the brownie's warm cocoa depth — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the honey threads the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "The BG|Chocolate Cake": "The BG's crisp citrus-earth build holds with the cake's layered chocolate — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; capable alongside. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "The BG|Clam Chowder": "The BG's crisp citrus-earth build stays alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the honey threads the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "The BG|Cowboy Ribeye": "Cowboy Ribeye: this marbled ribeye's fatty richness, smoky crust, and bold beef expression meets this bold whiskey-forward cocktail's oak, spice, and spirit depth. The whiskey's barrel depth and the steak's flame-grilled fat run at the same intensity — a classic steakhouse move. A headliner steakhouse cocktail. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "The BG|Crab Cake": "The BG's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift mis-pairs with the crab cake's delicate sweet crab in a crisp crust -- this cocktail's register doesn't lift the opener — try a sparkling or crisp white. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, or Tanqueray Gin, not a light cocktail. Avoid; the better calls are above. The BG belongs on the steak course.",
