  "The BG|Escargot": "The BG's crisp citrus-earth build reads alongside the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the cocktail lift refreshes the starter, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; the match carries without overshooting.",
  "The BG|Faroe Island Salmon": "The BG's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift mis-pairs with the salmon's rich oily flesh -- light cocktail register is wrong for a main protein. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a light cocktail. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. The BG lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "The BG|Filet Mignon": "Filet Mignon: the filet's lean, buttery tenderness and delicate mineral edge meets this bold whiskey-forward cocktail's oak, spice, and spirit depth. The whiskey's barrel depth and the steak's flame-grilled fat run at the same intensity — a classic steakhouse move. Works — cocktail-on-steak coherence.",
