  "Tomato Basil|Buffalo Trace Cream": "Buffalo Trace Cream's sweet liqueur character clashes with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid -- sweet liqueur on savory broth jars — sugar pulls one way, the salt-and-spice broth pulls the other. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Le Garenne Rosé, not a digestif. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Buffalo Trace Cream belongs on the steak course.",
  "Tomato Basil|Bulleit Bourbon": "Bulleit Bourbon's high-rye spice-forward depth finds neutral with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the tomato basil, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; the 100-proof is a touch over-specified for this dish's register.",
  "Tomato Basil|Burrata": "The burrata alongside the tomato basil -- both bring tomato as the headline. Avoid; one is enough. Pair the burrata with Il Colle Prosecco Superiore, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc; pair the tomato basil with Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Le Garenne Rosé.",
