  "Tomato Basil|WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year": "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year's rye-spice character leans against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the rye-and-oak weight handles the tomato basil, and the dry-spice register brightens the bowl. Works; bonded weight a touch ambitious for the dessert.",
  "Tomato Basil|Willett Pot Still Reserve": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the tomato basil, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; premium proof overpowers this dish.",
  "Tomato Basil|Woodford Reserve": "Woodford Reserve's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the bourbon weight handles the tomato basil, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; Fortuna's NZ terroir meets the glaze at distinctive register.",
  "Tomato Basil|Woodford Reserve Double Oaked": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the bourbon depth settles into the tomato basil, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; annual-release wasted on salad.",
  "Tomato Basil|Woodford Reserve Rye": "Woodford Reserve Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the rye-and-oak weight handles the tomato basil, and the rye-pepper note underlines the bowl. Works; the 10-year's restraint lets the soup lead.",
  "Tomato Basil|Woodinville Rye": "Woodinville Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the high-rye spice register matches the tomato basil, and the rye edge frames the bowl. Works; a composed but not remarkable match.",
  "Tomato Basil|Yamazaki 12 Year": "Yamazaki 12 Year's Suntory Japanese flagship character finds neutral with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the Japanese-whisky precision frames the tomato basil, and the silky body rounds the bowl. Works; Sinatra Select handles the richness at Sinatra-tribute register.",
  "Tomato Basil|Yamazaki 18 Year": "Yamazaki 18 Year's aged Suntory mizunara character sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the precise Japanese craft body wraps the tomato basil, and the precision rounds the bowl. Works; curated single-barrel slightly over-specified.",
  "Tomato Basil|Yellow Chartreuse": "Yellow Chartreuse's bitter-herb aperitivo edge jars against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid -- bitter botanicals on savory broth pull against the salt-and-spice frame without resolving. The plate deserves Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Le Garenne Rosé, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Yellow Chartreuse for the steak course.",
  "Transfusion|Asparagus": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build sits alongside the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the cocktail lift sits with the light side, and the botanicals echo the green plate. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Transfusion|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build plays cleanly against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Transfusion|Beignets": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build plays cleanly against the beignet's warm sugar-dusted pastry — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Transfusion|Bone Marrow": "Hangar 1, muddled black grapes, lime, ginger beer top. The cocktail's sessionable fruit profile has no structural match for marrow's rendered-fat richness — lime and grape don't cut bone depth. Never pair — keep the Transfusion for starters and raw bar.",
  "Transfusion|Bone-In Filet": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build sits alongside the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the cocktail is outweighed by the cut, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Transfusion|Broccoli Cheddar": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build plays cleanly against the broccoli cheddar's cream — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Transfusion|Broccolini": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build leans against the broccolini's tender green — the cocktail lift sits with the light side, and the botanicals echo the green plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Transfusion|Brussels and Belly": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build sits alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the citrus cuts the rich char. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Transfusion|Burrata": "Hangar 1, muddled black grapes, lime, ginger beer top. The grape's slight tannin adds complexity against burrata's cream and lime cuts through without crushing basil-tomato delicacy. Peak refreshing cocktail for burrata — fruit on the cocktail side meets fruit on the plate.",
  "Transfusion|Butternut Squash": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build sits beside the squash soup's silky sweet — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Transfusion|Carrot Cake": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build finds neutral with the carrot cake's spiced cream cheese — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Transfusion|Cheesecake": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build leans against the cheesecake's custard cream — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Transfusion|Chilean Seabass": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build reads alongside the seabass's buttery flesh — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; the call lands cleanly.",
  "Transfusion|Chocolate Brownie": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build holds with the brownie's warm cocoa depth — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Transfusion|Chocolate Cake": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build holds with the cake's layered chocolate — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Transfusion|Clam Chowder": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build sits alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Transfusion|Cowboy Ribeye": "Transfusion's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift underclubs the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness -- a light citrus cocktail can't carry the marbled char — needs whiskey or red wine weight. The plate deserves Macallan 18, Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon, or Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon, not a light cocktail. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Transfusion lands on another course — not here.",
  "Transfusion|Crab Cake": "Hangar 1 vodka, muddled black grapes, lime, ginger beer. The grape-and-lime profile cuts crab's romesco and ginger beer's dry effervescence lifts the pairing. Peak refreshing cocktail for crab cake — more complex than it looks, matches the crab's delicate sweetness.",
  "Transfusion|Creamed Spinach": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build stays alongside the spinach's dairy-rich cream — the cocktail lift sits with the light side, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Transfusion|Creamy Potato": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build stays alongside the potato soup's silky body — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Transfusion|Creme Brulee": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build stays alongside the brulee's burnt-sugar custard — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Transfusion|Escargot": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build reads alongside the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the cocktail lift refreshes the starter, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Transfusion|Faroe Island Salmon": "Hangar 1 vodka muddled with black grapes and lime, topped with ginger beer. Grape fruit and ginger-beer effervescence keep the drink light enough for Faroe salmon; the fruit adds dimension without competing. Strong; the pairing reads at register.",
  "Transfusion|Filet Mignon": "Hangar 1 vodka, muddled black grapes, lime, ginger beer top. The cocktail's fruit-led sessionable profile is wrong for any steak — ginger beer has no hook into grilled beef. Works only if guest stays on the cocktail; route filet to Cab, Pinot, or Manhattan.",
  "Transfusion|French Onion": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the cocktail lift refreshes against the hearty soup, and the botanicals cut the cheese richness. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Transfusion|Grilled Caesar": "Hangar 1, muddled black grapes, lime, ginger beer. The tart grape and lime balance anchovy-parmesan dressing and ginger beer's dry finish cleans against grilled-romaine char. Strong pairing — the Transfusion's fruit-led refreshment holds up to the salad's layered profile.",
