  "Trombo Cedano Reposado|Seafood Tower": "Trombo Cedano Reposado's rested-agave body sits alongside the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup: the rested-agave depth sits with the seafood tower, and the oak threads the starter. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Trombo Cedano Reposado|Seared Scallops": "Trombo Cedano Reposado with seared scallops — cedar-wood notes against caramelized scallop. Strong; the cedar is distinctive but slightly overshadows the scallop — Don Julio 70th is the refined scallop-reposado call.",
  "Trombo Cedano Reposado|Seasonal Soup": "Trombo Cedano Reposado's añejo-pour depth leans against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the añejo register carries the seasonal soup, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; multi-cask complexity over-specified.",
  "Trombo Cedano Reposado|Seasonal Vegetables": "Trombo Cedano Reposado's añejo-pour depth finds neutral with the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the rested-agave depth sits with the seasonal vegetables, and the caramel-agave register brightens the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Trombo Cedano Reposado|Shrimp Bisque": "Trombo Cedano Reposado with shrimp bisque — cedar-wood notes against cream-based seafood. Strong; cedar is distinctive but doesn't drive this pairing.",
  "Trombo Cedano Reposado|Shrimp Cocktail": "Trombo Cedano Reposado with shrimp cocktail — cedar-aged reposado against cold shrimp. Strong; the cedar character is novel but competes with the cocktail sauce.",
  "Trombo Cedano Reposado|Swordfish": "Trombo Cedano Reposado's cooked-agave-and-oak register sits alongside the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the swordfish, and the oak threads the plate. Works; approachable agave is a gentle counterpoint.",
  "Trombo Cedano Reposado|The Tomahawk": "Trombo Cedano Reposado with the Tomahawk — cedar-wood reposado against massive cut. Avoid; the cut is bourbon-or-scotch territory.",
  "Trombo Cedano Reposado|Tomato Basil": "Trombo Cedano Reposado's aged-agave character reads alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the oak-aged tequila body threads the tomato basil, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the bowl. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Trombo Cedano Reposado|Truffle Fries": "Trombo Cedano Reposado with truffle fries — cedar-aged reposado against truffle-parmesan. The cedar and truffle meet in forest-floor territory; a distinctive cedar-truffle resonance. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Trombo Cedano Reposado|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Trombo Cedano Reposado's rested-agave body leans against the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the cooked-agave-and-oak body matches the tuna, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the plate. Works; the ceremony earns the dish a different register than standard reposado brings.",
  "Trombo Cedano Reposado|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Trombo Cedano Reposado's rested-agave body leans against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the oak-aged tequila body threads the curry, and the oak threads the bowl. Works; multi-cask over-specified for small plate.",
  "Truffle Fries|1792 Small Batch": "1792 Small Batch with truffle fries — 1792's spicy-sweet against truffle-parmesan. The high-rye character gives the side a different frame than BT or Beam bring. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|1792 Sweet Wheat": "1792 Sweet Wheat with truffle fries — sweet-wheat against truffle-parmesan. The distinctive wheat-sweetness finds truffle's earth in a way the cleaner Weller-style wheated does differently. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|1881 Napa Valley": "1881 — entry Napa Cab with dark cherry, blackcurrant, mocha, smooth tannin. The approachable body frames truffle-fry earth and the mocha cuts the crisp oil-and-salt. Peak entry Napa Cab for truffle fries — step-up from glass that pairs confidently with the decadent side. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|2 James Gin": "2 James Gin's crisp char-juniper botanicals plays cleanly against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Truffle Fries|A Midnight's Winter Dram": "A Midnight's Winter Dram with truffle fries — rare craft release against truffle-parmesan. The literary-brand character gives the side a boutique-release frame. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Aberlour 16": "Aberlour 16 with truffle fries — ex-bourbon + Oloroso sherry Speyside against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Aberlour 16's double-matured character meets the earthy-rich with balanced depth.",
  "Truffle Fries|Adictivo Cristalino": "Adictivo Cristalino's rested-agave body reads alongside the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the barrel-rested body handles the truffle fries, and the soft-spice note softens the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Truffle Fries|Adictivo Reposado": "Adictivo Reposado with truffle fries — long-aged reposado against truffle-parmesan. Works; the extended maturation gives the side more than standard reposados bring, though not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|Alexander Valley Chardonnay": "Alexander Valley Chardonnay's apple-butter acidity stays alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the oak frames the umami. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|Alexander Valley Cyrus": "Truffle Fries: the mushroom's umami depth meets the bold red's structured tannin; dark fruit threads the truffle-and-earth without crowding. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Alexander Valley Homestead Red": "Alexander Valley Sonoma Bordeaux blend — plum, blackberry, mocha, soft tannin, smooth. The soft tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the mocha plays against the truffle-oil umami. Strong crowd-pleaser Bordeaux blend for truffle fries — Sonoma softness on the umami hit.",
  "Truffle Fries|Amaro Nonino": "Amaro Nonino with truffle fries — elegant amaro against truffle-parmesan. Works; grappa-based botanicals are a gentle counterpoint to the side.",
  "Truffle Fries|Ancho Reyes": "Ancho Reyes' sweet liqueur character flattens the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- sugar on starch is dessert territory — wrong course for the supporting plate. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; the better calls are above. Hold the Ancho Reyes for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Angel's Envy": "Angel's Envy with truffle fries — port-finished Louisville bourbon against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; AE's softer-oak + port-fruit meets the earthy-rich with wine-finish distinction.",
  "Truffle Fries|Angel's Envy Cask Strength": "AE Cask Strength with truffle fries — cask-strength AE against truffle-parmesan. Strong; AE CS's port-finish at cask-strength meets the earthy-rich at premium register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Angel's Envy Triple Cask": "AE Triple Cask with truffle fries — multi-cask AE against truffle-parmesan. Strong; AE Triple Cask's layered character meets the earthy-rich with distinctive complexity.",
  "Truffle Fries|Aperol": "Aperol with truffle fries — soft aperitivo bitter against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; the gentle orange-rhubarb brightens the earthy side without overwhelming it the way Branca would.",
  "Truffle Fries|Au Gratin Potatoes": "The au gratin and the truffle fries share potato as the primary character. Avoid; the meal doubles down without contrast. Route the au gratin with Bone-In Filet, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Keenan Chardonnay or the truffle fries with The Tomahawk, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Belvedere Vodka instead.",
  "Truffle Fries|Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon": "Truffle Fries: the mushroom's umami depth meets the bold red's structured tannin; dark fruit threads the truffle-and-earth without crowding. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Averna Amaro": "Averna with truffle fries — fuller-body amaro against truffle-parmesan. Works; caramel-orange is a gentle counterpoint.",
  "Truffle Fries|Aviation": "Aviation's shaken-and-bright cocktail register reads alongside the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the bright build frames the truffle fries, and the citrus cuts the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Aviation Gin": "Aviation Gin's floral-juniper botanicals sits alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the spice frames the umami depth. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|Avion 44": "Truffle Fries: earthy truffle-parmesan meets 44-month aged Avion. Extended maturation gives premium Avion character. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Avion Silver": "Avion Silver's blanco-tequila or blanco-tequila register leans against the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the unaged body brightens the truffle fries, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bacardi Rum": "Bacardi Rum's crisp workhorse-clean character leans against the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the bright cane-and-citrus weight carries the truffle fries, and the cane register underlines the side. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Truffle Fries|Baileys Irish Cream": "Baileys Irish Cream's sweet liqueur character clashes with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Baileys Irish Cream for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Baker's": "Baker's with truffle fries — 107-proof small-batch against truffle-parmesan. The bold proof gives the side real grip with Beam premium character. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Balvenie 12 American Oak": "Balvenie 12 Am Oak with truffle fries — handcrafted American Oak Speyside against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Balvenie's sweet-oak vanilla meets the earthy-rich with more depth than Fiddich's lighter bourbon-cask profile.",
  "Truffle Fries|Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask": "Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask with truffle fries — Caribbean-rum-cask Speyside against truffle-parmesan. Works; Caribbean Cask's tropical-sweetness meets the earthy-rich at distinctive register; Macallan or Aberlour's sherry-forward profile is more traditional.",
  "Truffle Fries|Balvenie 16 Single Barrel": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel with truffle fries — single-barrel American Oak Speyside against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; the deeper vanilla and first-fill character meet the earthy-rich at collector register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Balvenie 21 Portwood": "Balvenie 21 Portwood with truffle fries — 21yr port-cask Speyside against truffle-parmesan. Works; Portwood is over-specified for fries — save the collector-bottle for the protein course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bardstown Château Laboude": "Bardstown Château Laboude with truffle fries — Bardstown French-wine-cask against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Bardstown Château Laboude's French-wine-fruit meets the earthy-rich with contemporary-craft distinction.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bardstown Discovery #6": "Bardstown Discovery #6 with truffle fries — sourced Discovery blend against truffle-parmesan. The complex craft-blender character gives the side layered dimension. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bardstown Founders KBS": "Bardstown Founders KBS with truffle fries — stout-barrel bourbon against truffle-parmesan. The coffee-chocolate-stout notes give the side a genuinely distinctive beer-barrel frame. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bardstown Foursquare": "Bardstown Foursquare with truffle fries — Bardstown Foursquare rum-cask against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; the tropical rum-cask character meets the earthy-rich at Caribbean-finish register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bardstown Fusion #7": "Bardstown Fusion #7 with truffle fries — 7th Fusion against truffle-parmesan. The own-plus-sourced character gives the side layered dimension with Bardstown distillery contribution. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel": "Bardstown Rishi's Single Barrel with truffle fries — retailer-pick Bardstown against truffle-parmesan. The curated single-barrel gives the side a specific-selection craft frame. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Basil Hayden's": "Basil Hayden's with truffle fries — rye pepper against truffle-parmesan fat. The 80-proof delicacy lets the truffle lead; the spice notes give the side a lift the Wellers' wheated sweetness can't. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Basil Hayden's 10 Year": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year with truffle fries — aged oak and rye spice against truffle-parmesan. The 10-year brings more vocabulary than standard Basil Hayden's; a sophisticated light-bourbon pairing for this side. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Basil Hayden's Malted Rye": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye with truffle fries — bready malted grain against truffle-parmesan. The malted character finds the truffle's earthiness in a way no other Basil Hayden's does; distinctive, layered. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask with truffle fries — Beam high-rye red-wine finish against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; BH Red Wine Cask's rye-spice + red-wine-fruit meets the earthy-rich with distinctive dimension.",
  "Truffle Fries|Basil Hayden's Toast": "Basil Hayden's Toast with truffle fries — toasted caramel notes against truffle-parmesan fat. The toast finish lifts the side with a different vocabulary than straight Basil Hayden's; a more layered light-bourbon pairing for this side. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bee's Knees": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build plays cleanly against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Beefeater Gin": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals sits alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|Beignets": "Truffle Fries and the beignets -- sugar plays against the savory weight, the table earns its lift. Works; clean transition or together if the table wants.",
  "Truffle Fries|Belvedere Vodka": "Belvedere Vodka: Polish rye-based vodka, premium clean-slightly-sweet profile. Excellent on truffle fries; clean vodka frames truffle-salt-fat at Polish-rye register. Gold standard; the recommendation that earns the regular.",
  "Truffle Fries|Blade & Bow": "Blade & Bow with truffle fries — heritage-blend honey against truffle-parmesan. The storytelling pour gives the side a narrative beyond flavor; a conversation-starter everyday premium pairing. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Blanton's Gold": "Blanton's Gold with truffle fries — 103-proof single-barrel against truffle-parmesan. The richer caramel-vanilla gives the side more grip than Original's balance brings. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Blanton's Original": "Blanton's Original with truffle fries — iconic single-barrel against truffle-parmesan fat. The benchmark caramel-vanilla gives the side a refined frame; the premium single-barrel truffle-fries pairing. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Blanton's Straight from the Barrel": "Blanton's SfB with truffle fries — export cask-strength Blanton's against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Blanton's SfB meets the earthy-rich at barrel-proof register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Blood Oath Pact 10": "Blood Oath Pact 10 with truffle fries — decennial Pact 10 against truffle-parmesan. The milestone-edition character gives the side collector-level frame. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Blood Oath Pact 8": "Blood Oath Pact 8 with truffle fries — Pact 8 against truffle-parmesan. The Mizunara component layers Japanese oak character over the bourbon blend; distinctive side pairing. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Blood Oath Pact 9": "Blood Oath Pact 9 with truffle fries — Pact 9 wine-cask blend against truffle-parmesan. The fruit-finish character gives the side layered annual-release dimension. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bluecoat Gin": "Bluecoat Gin's char-citrus botanicals sits beside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bodega Noemia A Lisa": "Truffle Fries: Cab tannin frames the earthy mushroom-and-truffle depth; dark fruit lifts the umami into the wine's body. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bombay Dry Gin": "Bombay Dry Gin's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals reads alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; the pairing reads neutral at the table. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bombay Sapphire Gin": "Bombay Sapphire Gin's crisp London-Dry-citrus botanicals reads alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate. Works; the pairing reads neutral at the table. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bone Marrow": "The bone marrow opens the meal, the truffle fries with the entree -- the unctuous marrow matches the parsley-finished fries. Strong; both items.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bone-In Filet": "The bone-in filet into the truffle fries -- the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness meets the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight. Excellent; reliable headline side for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Booker's": "Booker's with truffle fries — uncut Beam cask-strength against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Booker's intensity meets the earthy-rich at barrel-proof register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Botanist Gin": "Botanist Gin's crisp Islay-gentle-botanical botanicals stays alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bowdie's Old Fashioned": "Buffalo Trace, rum-infused cherries, orange, bitters. The cocktail's vanilla-caramel plays against truffle oil's earthy richness; brûléed-orange nose lifts the parmesan-truffle aroma. Strong cocktail-side pairing when the fries anchor the table — holds up to the side's full flavor weight.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark": "Bowdie's Private Select Maker's Mark with truffle fries — house-pick depth against truffle-parmesan fat. The stave selection earns this side beyond what standard Maker's reaches; a signature-menu pairing. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bowman Brothers Small Batch": "Bowman Brothers Small Batch with truffle fries — 90-proof Virginia small-batch against truffle-parmesan. The smooth Bowman character gives the side a Sazerac-family frame distinct from BT. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bowmore 12": "Bowmore 12 with truffle fries — honey and sherry notes against truffle-parmesan fat. The softer peat lets truffle's earthiness lead. Strong; cleaner than Lagavulin 8, beautifully lighter than Laphroaig's medicinal approach.",
  "Truffle Fries|Braida Montebruna Barbera": "Piedmont Monferrato Barbera d'Asti — Braida benchmark, juicy dark cherry, blackberry, high acid, low tannin. The high acid cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the blackberry plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak benchmark Barbera for truffle fries — Italian food-wine on the umami hit. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon": "Truffle Fries: the structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit anchors the mushroom's umami weight; firm tannin and oak hold their register. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Broccoli Cheddar": "The broccoli cheddar and the truffle fries share cheese as the primary character. Avoid; the meal doubles down without contrast. Route the broccoli cheddar with Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Alexander Valley Chardonnay or the truffle fries with The Tomahawk, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Belvedere Vodka instead.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bruichladdich": "Bruichladdich: this Islay Scotch's intense peat smoke, medicinal phenol, and bold weight meets this earthy, umami-packed side's mushroom-and-truffle depth. Whiskey's oak and sweetness mirror the side's dairy and umami depth. A headliner match — context-driven peak. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly with the truffle fries on the plate -- the maple-glazed belly sits with the parsley-finished fries. Works; the call composes without crowding.",
  "Truffle Fries|Buffalo Trace": "Buffalo Trace with truffle fries — BT's oak against truffle-parmesan. The flagship's cleanness lets truffle lead; distinct from wheated takes — less honey, more structure. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Buffalo Trace Cream": "Buffalo Trace Cream's sweet liqueur character flattens the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- sugar on starch is dessert territory — wrong course for the supporting plate. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Buffalo Trace Cream lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Truffle Fries|Bulleit Bourbon": "Bulleit Bourbon with truffle fries — high-rye spice against truffle-parmesan. The rye-forward character gives the side a different dimension than wheated caramel; a distinctive approachable-high-rye pairing. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Burrata": "The burrata and the truffle fries -- cheese-on-cheese, the meal goes redundant. Avoid; the table reads heavy without payoff. Suggest Il Colle Prosecco Superiore, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc for the burrata, or The Tomahawk, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Belvedere Vodka for the truffle fries.",
  "Truffle Fries|Butternut Squash": "The butternut squash and the truffle fries -- sugar and umami share the table, the contrast carries the meal. Works; sequence them or share the table, the call holds either way.",
  "Truffle Fries|Cade Cabernet Sauvignon": "Truffle Fries: the mushroom's umami depth meets the bold red's structured tannin; dark fruit threads the truffle-and-earth without crowding. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Camarena Tequila": "Camarena Tequila with truffle fries — value reposado against truffle-parmesan. Works; accessible character doesn't drive.",
  "Truffle Fries|Campari": "Campari with truffle fries — ruby bitter against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; aperitivo bitterness against earthy-rich fries is Italian bar logic — this outperforms on a side where other amari just coexist.",
  "Truffle Fries|Canadian Club": "Canadian Club with truffle fries — 1858 Hiram Walker Canadian against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Canadian Club's grain-forward character meets the earthy-rich at heritage register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Canadian Club 43 Year": "CC 43 Year with truffle fries — 43yr aged Canadian against truffle-parmesan. Strong; CC 43 Year's aged depth meets the earthy-rich at collector register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Captain Morgan Rum": "Captain Morgan Rum's clean silver register finds neutral with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the unaged-cane body sits with the truffle fries, and the light-rum lift plays against the side. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Truffle Fries|Caribou Crossing": "Caribou Crossing with truffle fries — single-barrel Canadian against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Caribou Crossing's craft character meets the earthy-rich at single-barrel register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Carrot Cake": "The truffle fries alongside the carrot cake -- sugar plays against the savory weight, the table earns its lift. Works; the contrast holds, neither course overshadows the other.",
  "Truffle Fries|Casa LBV Port": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness flattens the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- dessert sugar on starch is wrong-course energy for the supporting plate. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Casa LBV Port on the steak course instead.",
  "Truffle Fries|Casamigos Mezcal": "Casamigos Mezcal's bold agave-soft-smoke character lifts the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the agave smoke layers into the rich side, and the smoke meets the umami depth. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Truffle Fries|Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon": "Napa Rutherford Cab — concentrated black fruit, cocoa, mocha, velvety tannin. The opulent body frames truffle-fry earth and the cocoa-mocha cuts the crisp oil-and-salt. Peak iconic Napa Cab for truffle fries — Caymus lushness meets the decadent side with the recognizability of a crowd-pleasing label. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Chambord": "Chambord's sweet liqueur character clashes with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Chambord lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Truffle Fries|Cheesecake": "The truffle fries and the cheesecake -- the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight hands off cleanly to the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: sweet contrast lifts the savory. Works; sequence them or share the table, no clash.",
  "Truffle Fries|Chilean Seabass": "The seabass alongside the truffle fries -- the savory course rounds the protein, the meal reads layered. Works; the side sits without pulling focus.",
  "Truffle Fries|Chocolate Brownie": "Truffle Fries and the brownie -- sugar and umami share the table, the contrast carries the meal. Works; clean transition or together if the table wants.",
  "Truffle Fries|Chocolate Cake": "Truffle Fries and the chocolate cake -- the sweet register lifts the umami, the contrast holds without crowding. Works; the meal closes cleanly from the side.",
  "Truffle Fries|Chopin Vodka": "Chopin Vodka's bold char-cream neutrality plays cleanly against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the caramel meets the nut character. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Truffle Fries|Christian Bros Brandy": "Christian Brothers with truffle fries — American brandy against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Christian Bros's sweetness meets the earthy-rich at value register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Château Batailley": "Pauillac 5ème Cru Classé Bordeaux — blackcurrant, tobacco, cedar, graphite, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the graphite-cedar plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak classified Bordeaux for truffle fries — French earth layers with the truffle hit. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Château Beaucastel": "Truffle Fries: the bold red's cassis grip carries the mushroom-and-truffle depth — structured weight on the earthy side. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Truffle Fries|Château Gombaude-Guillot": "Pomerol Merlot-Cab Franc — Château Gombaude-Guillot, biodynamic Pomerol, 2016, dark plum, truffle, mocha, velvety finish. The truffle in the wine meets the truffle-oil fries directly and velvety Merlot plays with parmesan weight. Strong Pomerol for truffle fries — truffle-on-truffle alignment, French Bordeaux on the side.",
  "Truffle Fries|Château Haut Segottes": "Truffle Fries: the mushroom's umami depth meets the bold red's structured tannin; dark fruit threads the truffle-and-earth without crowding. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Château de Rouillac": "Pessac-Léognan left-bank Bordeaux — blackcurrant, cedar, graphite, tobacco, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the graphite plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak left-bank Bordeaux for truffle fries — French earth doubles the fries' earthy hit. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Clam Chowder": "The chowder and the truffle fries share potato as the primary character. Avoid; the meal doubles down without contrast. Route the chowder with Keenan Chardonnay, Far Niente Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis or the truffle fries with The Tomahawk, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Belvedere Vodka instead.",
  "Truffle Fries|Clase Azul Anejo": "Truffle Fries: Parmesan-and-truffle meets Clase Azul Anejo. Excellent; the luxury-craftsmanship character with sherry-butt-finish complexity handles truffle-salt-fat at ceremonial register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Clase Azul Durango": "Clase Azul Durango with truffle fries — Durango ceremonial against truffle-parmesan. The hand-painted ceramic ceremony gives the side luxury-register frame. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Clase Azul Gold": "Clase Azul Gold with truffle fries — golden-ceremonial blend against truffle-parmesan. The mezcal-touch and blend complexity find truffle earth distinctively at ceremonial register. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal": "Clase Azul Guerrero Mezcal's bold agave-fruit-smoke character matches the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the agave smoke layers into the rich side, and the smoke meets the umami depth. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Clase Azul Plata": "Clase Azul Plata's silky Jalisco blanco with ceramic-decanter presentation sits alongside the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the blanco-tequila body matches the truffle fries, and the agave-citrus thread frames the side. Works; the ceremony overshoots the dish.",
  "Truffle Fries|Clase Azul Reposado": "Clase Azul Reposado with truffle fries — ceramic-bottle reposado against truffle-parmesan. Works; the pairing is less about match and more about experience.",
  "Truffle Fries|Clase Azul Ultra": "Clase Azul Ultra with truffle fries — top-tier ceremonial against truffle-parmesan. The 5-year Ultra gives the side collector-grade luxury frame. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Clermont Steep": "Clermont Steep with truffle fries — Beam wheated against truffle-parmesan. The 90-proof caramel-vanilla wheat gives the side a different character than non-wheated Beam expressions. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Clos Petit Ona Grenache": "Clos Petit Ona Grenache's char-earth tannin reads alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice frames the umami depth. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Truffle Fries|Codigo 1530 Rosa": "Codigo 1530 Rosa with truffle fries — Cabernet-cask rosé against truffle-parmesan. Works; the wine influence is unusual here but doesn't quite drive.",
  "Truffle Fries|Contratto Vermouth": "Contratto Vermouth's vermouth-wine-base sweetness holds with the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the bitter herb edge cuts the rich side. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Corazon Blanco": "Corazon Blanco's unaged silver-spirit body leans against the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the blanco-tequila body matches the truffle fries, and the unaged-cane note plays against the side. Works; refined craft composes cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Corazon Reposado": "Corazon Reposado with truffle fries — single-estate reposado against truffle-parmesan. Works; agave brightness doesn't quite lift the truffle's earth the way bourbon oak does.",
  "Truffle Fries|Corazon Sazerac": "Truffle Fries: Parmesan-and-truffle meets Corazon Sazerac. Excellent; the rye-spice-agave character handles truffle-salt-fat at crossover register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Corazon Stagg": "Truffle Fries: Parmesan-and-truffle meets Corazon Stagg. Excellent; the heavy-caramel-oak-GTS character handles truffle-salt-fat at intense-Expresiones register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Corazon Weller": "Truffle Fries: Parmesan-and-truffle meets Corazon Weller. Excellent; ex-wheated-barrel soft character handles truffle-salt-fat at softer-Expresiones register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Corazón del Sol Malbec": "Truffle Fries: the structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit anchors the mushroom's umami weight; firm tannin and oak hold their register. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Corpse Reviver": "Corpse Reviver's anise-citrus build leans against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; the match holds without overshooting. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Truffle Fries|Courvoisier Cognac": "Courvoisier with truffle fries — drier oak-forward cognac against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Courvoisier's structural backbone frames the earthy-rich side with more cut than Hennessy's rounder approach.",
  "Truffle Fries|Cowboy Ribeye": "Cowboy Ribeye alongside the truffle fries -- the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness meets the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: protein and umami share the plate, the build reads weighty and clean. Works; the side reads as a measured plate companion.",
  "Truffle Fries|Crab Cake": "Crab Cake and the truffle fries -- restrained gives way to umami, the meal earns its weight. Works; both items hold their register, no clash.",
  "Truffle Fries|Cragganmore 12": "Cragganmore 12 with truffle fries — Diageo Classic Malt against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Cragganmore's layered complexity and smoke-hint meet the earthy-rich with distinctive depth.",
  "Truffle Fries|Creamy Potato": "The potato soup and the truffle fries share potato as the primary character. Avoid; the meal doubles down without contrast. Route the potato soup with Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis or the truffle fries with The Tomahawk, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Belvedere Vodka instead.",
  "Truffle Fries|Creme Brulee": "Truffle Fries and the brulee -- the sweet register lifts the umami, the contrast holds without crowding. Works; clean transition or together if the table wants.",
  "Truffle Fries|Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée": "Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée's cherry-earth tannin stays alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice frames the umami depth. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|Crown Royal": "Crown Royal with truffle fries — iconic Canadian blend against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Crown Royal's smooth character meets the earthy-rich at crowd-pleasing register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Cucumber Gimlet": "Cucumber Gimlet's crisp citrus-ginger build holds with the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Truffle Fries|Dalmore 12": "Dalmore 12 with truffle fries — Matusalem-cask Highland luxury against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Dalmore's slightly-oily sherry-finish character meets the earthy-rich with luxurious depth.",
  "Truffle Fries|Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge": "Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge's crisp earth-mineral tannin sits beside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|Darioush Cabernet Franc": "Mount Veeder Napa Cab Franc (rare) — Darioush elegant aromatic, violet, dark cherry, dried rose, savory herb, medium tannin. The medium tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the savory herb plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak rare-Napa CF for truffle fries — Darioush aromatic story on the umami hit. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Darioush Cabernet Sauvignon": "Darioush — Silverado Trail Cab with blackcurrant, dark plum, mocha, spice. The opulent body frames truffle-fry earth and the mocha-spice cuts the crisp oil-and-salt. Peak opulent Napa Cab for truffle fries — Persian-inspired estate story meets the decadent side with plush concentration. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Detroit City Gin": "Detroit City Gin's bold char-juniper botanicals leans against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the spice frames the umami depth. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Truffle Fries|Detroit City Vodka": "Detroit City Vodka's crisp grain-juniper neutrality reads alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Dewar's 15": "Dewar's 15 with truffle fries — sherry-finish Highland blend against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Dewar's 15's aged character meets the earthy-rich at premium register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Dewar's White Label": "Dewar's White Label with truffle fries — Aberfeldy-core blend against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Dewar's White meets the earthy-rich at benchmark register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Disaronno": "Disaronno's sweet liqueur character clashes with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Disaronno for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye": "Doc Swinson's Alter Ego Rye with truffle fries — craft sourced against truffle-parmesan. The blended craft character gives the side a boutique frame. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum": "Doctor Bird Jamaica Rum's bold Jamaican-funk character holds steady against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the whiskey depth meets the indulgent side. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Domaine Serene Grand Cheval": "Domaine Serene Grand Cheval's char-cherry tannin sits beside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice frames the umami depth. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|Domaine Tempier Bandol": "Truffle Fries: the mushroom's umami depth meets the bold red's structured tannin; dark fruit threads the truffle-and-earth without crowding. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé": "Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé's cool-climate white acidity leans against the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the bright acid lifts the truffle fries, and the citrus cuts the side. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Truffle Fries|Domaine du Grand Tinel": "Truffle Fries: the bold red's cassis grip carries the mushroom-and-truffle depth — structured weight on the earthy side. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Don Fulano Anejo": "Truffle Fries: Parmesan-and-truffle meets Don Fulano. Excellent; the 3-year French-oak complexity handles truffle-salt-fat at extended-aged terroir register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Don Fulano Blanco": "Don Fulano Blanco's unaged silver-spirit body leans against the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the silver-spirit register lifts the truffle fries, and the unaged-cane note plays against the side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Truffle Fries|Don Fulano Reposado": "Don Fulano Reposado with truffle fries — highland refinement against truffle-parmesan. Works; vanilla and honey don't quite drive the pairing the way oak-forward spirits do.",
  "Truffle Fries|Don Julio 1942": "Don Julio 1942 with truffle fries — 1942 benchmark against truffle-parmesan. The aged oak and vanilla give the side iconic extra-añejo authority. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Don Julio 70th": "Don Julio 70th with truffle fries — filtered reposado against truffle-parmesan. Works; the 70th's clarity is too delicate to drive the pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Don Julio Blanco": "Don Julio Blanco's workhorse blanco with clean agave snap leans against the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the truffle fries, and the agave-citrus thread frames the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Don Julio Reposado": "Don Julio Reposado with truffle fries — reposado against truffle-parmesan. Works; the oak sits beside the truffle's earth, but this isn't the reposado's strongest match.",
  "Truffle Fries|Drambuie": "Drambuie's sweet liqueur character clashes with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Drambuie for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Dunville's Single Malt": "Dunville's Single Malt with truffle fries — Belfast Irish single malt against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Dunville's meets the earthy-rich at distinctive register.",
  "Truffle Fries|E.H. Taylor Full Proof": "E.H. Taylor Full Proof with truffle fries — BT BiB against truffle-parmesan. Strong; EHT Full Proof meets the earthy-rich at historic Kentucky register.",
  "Truffle Fries|E.H. Taylor Rye": "E.H. Taylor Rye with truffle fries — 100-proof BIB rye against truffle-parmesan. The bonded weight gives the side real grip at premium BT register. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|E.H. Taylor Small Batch": "E.H. Taylor Small Batch with truffle fries — 100-proof BIB against truffle-parmesan. The rich caramel and oak give the side more grip than 90-proof BT pours bring. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Eagle Rare 10 Year": "Eagle Rare 10 Year with truffle fries — Buffalo Trace's aged elegance against truffle-parmesan earthiness. The 10-year's oak gives truffle the frame it needs; clean, not sweet the way wheated bourbons are here. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Eastern Kille Dry Gin": "Eastern Kille Dry Gin's crisp char-citrus botanicals plays cleanly against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Truffle Fries|El Cabo": "El Cabo with truffle fries — boutique reposado against truffle-parmesan. Works; craft character doesn't drive the pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|El Mayor Extra Anejo": "El Mayor Extra Anejo with truffle fries — aged El Mayor against truffle-parmesan. The accessible aged character gives the side value-adjacent premium frame. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|El Mayor Reposado": "El Mayor Reposado with truffle fries — value reposado against truffle-parmesan. Works; light oak doesn't particularly elevate the truffle.",
  "Truffle Fries|Elephant Gin": "Elephant Gin's crisp char-herbal botanicals stays alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the oak frames the umami. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Truffle Fries|Elijah Craig 18 Year": "Elijah Craig 18 with truffle fries — 18yr HH single-barrel against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; EC 18's aged character meets the earthy-rich at aged-single-barrel register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Elijah Craig Private Barrel": "Elijah Craig Private Barrel with truffle fries — house-picked single-barrel against truffle-parmesan. The private-selection character gives the side a curated frame. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Elijah Craig Single Barrel": "Elijah Craig Single Barrel with truffle fries — 94-proof single-barrel against truffle-parmesan. The concentrated oak-spice gives the side grip at the premium Heaven Hill single-barrel register. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Elijah Craig Small Batch": "Elijah Craig Small Batch with truffle fries — spicy-sweet small-batch against truffle-parmesan. The oak spice gives the side a different vocabulary than Heaven Hill BIB's straight bond-structure brings. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Elijah Craig Straight Rye": "Elijah Craig Straight Rye with truffle fries — 94-proof HH rye against truffle-parmesan. The rye spice cuts the richness with HH authority. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Elk Cove Five Mountain": "Elk Cove Five Mountain's cherry-clove tannin leans against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice frames the umami depth. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Truffle Fries|Elk Cove Pinot Blanc": "Elk Cove Pinot Blanc's apple-char acidity plays cleanly against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the crisp acidity sits with the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Truffle Fries|Elmer T. Lee": "Elmer T. Lee with truffle fries — namesake single-barrel against truffle-parmesan. The smooth character gives the side a refined frame at the premium single-barrel register. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Empress 1908 Gin": "Empress 1908 Gin's herbal-botanical edge finds neutral with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the floral edge frames the truffle fries, and the juniper threads the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Epoch Ingenuity": "Truffle Fries: the side's mushroom richness pulls the bold red's body; tannin and oak settle into the umami without overshooting. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Escargot": "The escargot and the truffle fries -- savory-on-savory, the table reads dense and earnest. Works; sequence them or share the table, no concern either way.",
  "Truffle Fries|Espresso Martini": "Tito's, espresso, Grind Espresso Liqueur, Averna amaro, vanilla syrup, Angostura. The coffee meets truffle oil's earth directly and Averna's bitter backbone cuts parmesan weight. Strong cocktail-side pairing when the fries carry a heavier cocktail program.",
  "Truffle Fries|Espresso Old Fashioned": "Buffalo Trace, Buffalo Bourbon Cream, Frangelico, espresso, brown sugar, Angostura. The coffee bitterness and Frangelico's nuttiness meet truffle's earthiness well; heavier dessert-adjacent cocktail route when the guest's already committed to a big-weight pairing. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Evening Land Seven Springs": "Evening Land Seven Springs: this elegant red's cherry-bright, silky-tannin frame meets this earthy, umami-packed side's mushroom-and-truffle depth. The elegant red's acidity cuts the dairy fat while its cherry lifts the earthy umami. Works — clean if not dominant.",
  "Truffle Fries|Far Niente Cabernet Sauvignon": "Oakville luxurious Cab — blackcurrant, dark chocolate, espresso, violet, smooth powerful. The opulent body frames truffle-fry earth and the chocolate-espresso cuts the crisp oil-and-salt. Peak luxurious Oakville Cab for truffle fries — Far Niente's long finish meets the decadent side with extraordinary depth. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Far Niente Chardonnay": "Far Niente Chardonnay's bold butter-char acidity reads alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the oak frames the umami. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Faroe Island Salmon": "Faroe Island Salmon alongside the truffle fries -- protein meets umami, the table builds substance. Works; the side carries cleanly with the salmon.",
  "Truffle Fries|Fattoria Le Pupille Saffredi": "Super Tuscan — Le Pupille Saffredi Maremma, Cab-Merlot-Petit Verdot, 2021, blackcurrant, tobacco, graphite, Mediterranean herbs, firm-tannin finish. The graphite plays with truffle-oil earth and the tobacco cuts parmesan weight. Works for truffle fries — Saffredi's firm tannin reads heavy; Scavino or Caymus fits lighter.",
  "Truffle Fries|Faust Napa Valley Cabernet": "Truffle Fries: the bold red's cassis grip carries the mushroom-and-truffle depth — structured weight on the earthy side. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía": "Fento Ollo de Sapo Mencía's cherry-earth tannin stays alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|Fernet Branca": "Fernet Branca with truffle fries — menthol-saffron against truffle-parmesan. Works; Branca's savory lean makes this a functional side pairing, not a featured match.",
  "Truffle Fries|Fernet Menta": "Fernet Menta with truffle fries — cooling mint against truffle-parmesan. Works; mint is a refreshing counterpoint to the earthy side.",
  "Truffle Fries|Filet Mignon": "The filet into the truffle fries -- the filet's lean buttery tenderness meets the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight. Excellent; reliable headline side for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Fireball Whisky": "Fireball Whisky's sweet liqueur character clashes with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Fireball Whisky lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Truffle Fries|Fisher Unity Pinot Noir": "Fisher Unity Pinot Noir's cherry-earth tannin reads alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice frames the umami depth. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Four Roses Small Batch Select": "Four Roses Small Batch Select with truffle fries — premium 104-proof against truffle-parmesan. The extra proof and recipe-select complexity give the side real grip. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Four Roses Yellow Label": "Four Roses Yellow Label with truffle fries — the 10-recipe blend at entry level. 80 proof floral-and-honey meets truffle-parmesan. The light-body lets truffle lead; entry-level but cleanly matched for this side. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Fox & Oden": "Fox & Oden with truffle fries — boutique small-batch against truffle-parmesan. The craft character gives the side a regional-distillery frame. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Fox & Oden Double Oaked": "Fox & Oden Double Oaked with truffle fries — Fox & Oden Detroit Double Oaked against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Fox & Oden's Double Oaked caramel-oak meets the earthy-rich at distinctive register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Frangelico": "Frangelico's Piedmont hazelnut depth to mocha at after-dinner register flattens the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- sugar on starch is dessert territory — wrong course for the supporting plate. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; the better calls are above. Frangelico lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Truffle Fries|Freemark Abbey Bosché": "Truffle Fries: the bold red's cassis grip carries the mushroom-and-truffle depth — structured weight on the earthy side. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|French 75": "Inverroche gin shaken with lemon and vanilla syrup, topped with Prosecco. Bubbles and lemon against truffle earth feels wrong; the cocktail's brightness fights the fry sauce. Keep for shellfish starters. Avoid; the pairing fights at the table — point the guest elsewhere.",
  "Truffle Fries|French Onion": "The French onion and the truffle fries -- cheese-on-cheese, the meal goes redundant. Avoid; the table reads heavy without payoff. Suggest Daniel Chotard Sancerre Rouge, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée for the French onion, or The Tomahawk, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Belvedere Vodka for the truffle fries.",
  "Truffle Fries|Frias Block 5": "Truffle Fries: the mushroom's umami depth meets the bold red's structured tannin; dark fruit threads the truffle-and-earth without crowding. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|G.D. Vajra Albe Nebbiolo": "Piedmont Barolo DOCG Nebbiolo — G.D. Vajra Albe La Morra, tar, rose petal, dried cherry, firm tannic backbone, high acid. The firm tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the tar plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak classic Barolo for truffle fries — tar-truffle echo on the umami hit. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti": "Piedmont sweet sparkling — peach, honey, floral. Sweet wine against truffle and garlic-Dijon fry sauce is wrong on every axis. Route Moscato to dessert; it has no business on fries. Avoid; the call reads off-register; recommend an alternative.",
  "Truffle Fries|G4 Blanco": "G4 Blanco's silver-spirit lift with agave-citrus edge leans against the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the truffle fries, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|G4 High Proof": "G4 High Proof with truffle fries — concentrated reposado against truffle-parmesan. Works; the pour is a touch over-specified for the side.",
  "Truffle Fries|Garavogue Irish Whiskey": "Garavogue with truffle fries — Sligo-river craft Irish against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Garavogue's craft character meets the earthy-rich at distinctive register.",
  "Truffle Fries|George T. Stagg": "GTS with truffle fries — BTAC ultra-premium against truffle-parmesan. Strong; GTS meets the earthy-rich at collector register; consider whether the side deserves a BTAC pour.",
  "Truffle Fries|Ghost Block Cabernet Sauvignon": "Ghost Block — Oakville Cab with dense blackcurrant, dark cherry, graphite, toasted oak. The structured body frames truffle-fry earth and the graphite-oak cuts the crisp oil-and-salt. Peak Oakville Cab for truffle fries — Napa's golden-strip structure meets the decadent side. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Ghost Block Zinfandel": "Napa Oakville Zinfandel — Ghost Block, ripe jammy fruit, blackberry preserves, cracked pepper, full body, medium tannin. The cracked pepper cuts parm-richness and the full body handles truffle-oil weight. Strong California-Zin for truffle fries — jammy-Zin polish on the cut.",
  "Truffle Fries|Glenfiddich 12": "Glenfiddich 12 with truffle fries — bourbon-cask apple/pear Speyside against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Fiddich's light vanilla and green-fruit character is the approachable Speyside-truffle pairing — where Balvenie 12 adds vanilla depth, Fiddich keeps it gateway-fresh.",
  "Truffle Fries|Glenfiddich 14": "Glenfiddich 14 with truffle fries — Bourbon Barrel Reserve against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; the charred-oak finish meets the earthy-rich with richer vanilla than Fiddich 12 offers.",
  "Truffle Fries|Glenfiddich 18": "Glenfiddich 18 with truffle fries — Small Batch Reserve against truffle-parmesan. Strong; the sherry-cask dried-fruit meets the earthy-rich with premium aged gravitas.",
  "Truffle Fries|Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23": "Glenfiddich Gran Cru 23 with truffle fries — 23yr Cuvée-cask Speyside against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Gran Cru's refined brioche-pastry character meets the earthy-rich with champagne-style polish at rare-release register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Glenglassaugh 12": "Glenglassaugh 12 with truffle fries — recently-reopened Sandend-coast Highland against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Glenglassaugh 12's tropical-fruit meets the earthy-rich with distinctive coastal-Highland character.",
  "Truffle Fries|Glenlivet 12": "Glenlivet 12 with truffle fries — \"The Glenlivet house style\" against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Glenlivet's honey-floral frames the earthy-rich with benchmark elegance.",
  "Truffle Fries|Glenmorangie 10": "Glenmorangie 10 with truffle fries — tallest-stills Highland bourbon-cask against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Glenmorangie 10's honeysuckle-peach-vanilla profile is the featured Highland-truffle pairing — the bourbon-cask vanilla marries truffle-parmesan earthiness cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Glenmorangie 18": "Glenmorangie 18 with truffle fries — 18yr Glenmorangie against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Glenmorangie 18's aged bourbon-plus-sherry depth meets the earthy-rich at premium register; the 10's lighter approach is entry-level, the 18 closes the deal.",
  "Truffle Fries|Graham's 10 Year Tawny": "Graham's 10 Year Tawny's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Pour the Graham's 10 Year Tawny on the steak course instead.",
  "Truffle Fries|Graham's 20 Year Tawny": "Graham's 20 Year Tawny's aged tawny with nutty-caramel depth flattens the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- dessert sugar on starch is wrong-course energy for the supporting plate. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Graham's 20 Year Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Graham's 2017 Vintage Port": "Graham's 2017 Vintage Port's structured vintage port with dark-fruit weight clashes with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Graham's 2017 Vintage Port for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Gran Patron Platinum": "Gran Patron Platinum's blanco-tequila or blanco-tequila register finds neutral with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the bright agave-citrus weight carries the truffle fries, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|Grand Marnier": "Grand Marnier's sweet liqueur character flattens the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- sugar on starch is dessert territory — wrong course for the supporting plate. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Grand Marnier for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Gray Whale Gin": "Gray Whale Gin's bold citrus-herbal botanicals leans against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|Green Chartreuse": "Green Chartreuse's cask-strength herbal-high-proof sweetness finds neutral with the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the sweet character sits at digestif register. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Grey Goose Vodka": "Grey Goose Vodka's crisp French-wheat-soft neutrality leans against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Grilled Caesar": "The Caesar alongside the truffle fries -- both bring cheese as the headline. Avoid; one is enough. Pair the Caesar with Green Chartreuse, Tanqueray Gin, or Scavino Barolo; pair the truffle fries with The Tomahawk, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Belvedere Vodka.",
  "Truffle Fries|Gumbo": "The gumbo and the truffle fries on the same meal -- separate registers share the plate, the contrast settles the build. Works; sequence or share, the build holds.",
  "Truffle Fries|Gundlach Bundschu Cabernet": "Truffle Fries: the bold red's cassis grip carries the mushroom-and-truffle depth — structured weight on the earthy side. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|HDW 100 Vodka": "HDW 100 Vodka's char-herbal neutrality holds with the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|Hakushu 12 Year": "Hakushu 12 with truffle fries — \"Forest Distillery\" single malt against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Hakushu's pine-forest + subtle peat meets the earthy-rich with Forest-Distillery distinction.",
  "Truffle Fries|Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel": "Hancock's Reserve Single Barrel with truffle fries — Blanton's-mash BT single-barrel against truffle-parmesan. The complex profile gives the side a BT single-barrel frame distinct from the everyday bourbons. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Hangar 1 Vodka": "Hangar 1 Vodka's crisp char-floral neutrality stays alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Head Fake": "Wheatley vodka, limoncello, triple sec, lemon, simple syrup, sugar rim — a lemon drop, essentially. Sweet citrus against truffle fries with garlic-Dijon fry sauce is a bad axis; never pair. Route to dessert. Avoid; the call reads off-register; recommend an alternative.",
  "Truffle Fries|Heaven Hill 20 Year": "Heaven Hill 20 Year with truffle fries — HH 20yr aged against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; HH 20's 20-year depth meets the earthy-rich at collector register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond": "Heaven Hill Bottled in Bond with truffle fries — 100-proof traditional against truffle-parmesan. The BIB's straight oak and caramel give the side a clean, sturdy frame; no pretense, just classic Kentucky. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Heaven's Door 10 Year": "Heaven's Door 10 Year with truffle fries — 100-proof 10-year against truffle-parmesan. The aging depth gives the side grip; a storytelling premium pairing. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Heitz Martha's Vineyard": "Truffle Fries: the structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit anchors the mushroom's umami weight; firm tannin and oak hold their register. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Heitz Trailside Vineyard": "Truffle Fries: Cab tannin frames the earthy mushroom-and-truffle depth; dark fruit lifts the umami into the wine's body. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Hendricks Flora Adora": "Hendricks Flora Adora's crisp char-elderflower botanicals stays alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; reliable companion, low risk. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Hendricks Gin": "Hendricks Gin's crisp cucumber-rose botanicals leans against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|Hendricks Grand Cabaret": "Hendricks Grand Cabaret's bold anise-char botanicals reads alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Truffle Fries|Hendricks Neptunia": "Hendricks Neptunia's crisp anise-brine botanicals sits alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Hendricks Orbium": "Hendricks Orbium's crisp botanical-juniper botanicals sits beside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the oak frames the umami. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Hennessy Cognac": "Hennessy with truffle fries — VS/VSOP against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; the oak-and-vanilla frames the earthy-rich side with the classic after-dinner-bite approach.",
  "Truffle Fries|Henry McKenna 10 Year Bottled in Bond": "Henry McKenna 10 Year BIB with truffle fries — 100-proof 10-year BIB against truffle-parmesan. The aged bonded richness gives the side authority few single-barrels match. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Hibiki Japanese Harmony": "Hibiki Harmony with truffle fries — refined Japanese blend against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Hibiki's elegant harmony meets the earthy-rich at premium register.",
  "Truffle Fries|House Wedge": "The wedge and the truffle fries -- both cheese-forward, the table doubles up on cheese. Avoid; pick one or the other. Pair the wedge with St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, Weller 12 Year, or Le Garenne Rosé; pair the truffle fries with The Tomahawk, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Belvedere Vodka.",
  "Truffle Fries|I.W. Harper 15 Year": "I.W. Harper 15 with truffle fries — historic-KY 15yr against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; IW Harper 15's cherry-oak depth meets the earthy-rich at aged-KY-heritage register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Il Colle Prosecco Superiore": "Il Colle Prosecco Superiore's crisp apple-citrus acidity sits alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|Inhibited": "Truffle Fries: this earthy, umami-packed side's mushroom-and-truffle depth meets this coffee-driven cocktail's bitter roast, rich texture, and dessert-adjacent sweetness. Coffee cocktail against a savory plate — wrong register entirely. Strong — the interaction lands despite the axis challenge.",
  "Truffle Fries|Inverroche Gin": "Inverroche Gin's crisp earth-floral botanicals reads alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Truffle Fries|Iron Fish Gin": "Iron Fish Gin's cask-strength citrus-earth botanicals plays cleanly against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the oak frames the umami. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Truffle Fries|Ironfish Bourbon in Mezcal Casks": "Ironfish Bourbon Mezcal Casks with truffle fries — northern MI mezcal-cask finish against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Ironfish Mezcal's smoky character meets the earthy-rich with distinctive Michigan-farm-mezcal resonance.",
  "Truffle Fries|Isaac Bowman Port Finish": "Isaac Bowman Port Finish with truffle fries — Virginia port-finished bourbon against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Isaac Bowman's port-fruit meets the earthy-rich at Virginia-heritage register.",
  "Truffle Fries|J Davies Ferrington Vineyards": "J Davies Ferrington Vineyards's cherry-coffee tannin sits beside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|J. Davies Cabernet Sauvignon": "J. Davies — Diamond Mountain Cab with volcanic dark fruit, graphite, mineral backbone, firm tannin. The structured body frames truffle-fry earth and the graphite-mineral cuts the crisp oil-and-salt. Peak mountain Cab for truffle fries — Schramsberg estate provenance meets the decadent side. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Jack Daniel's 12 Year": "Jack Daniel's 12 Year with truffle fries — aged Tennessee against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; JD 12's aged depth meets the earthy-rich at premium register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Jack Daniel's Bonded": "Jack Daniel's Bonded with truffle fries — 100-proof Tennessee against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; JD Bonded's extra backbone meets the earthy-rich at Bonded-Act register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Jack Daniel's Old No. 7": "Jack Daniel's Old No. 7 with truffle fries — iconic Tennessee against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Old No. 7's vanilla-caramel meets the earthy-rich at iconic Tennessee register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Jack Daniel's Sinatra Select": "JD Sinatra Select with truffle fries — Sinatra Barrels Tennessee against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Sinatra Select's extra-oak character meets the earthy-rich with Sinatra-tribute distinction.",
  "Truffle Fries|Jameson Irish Whiskey": "Jameson with truffle fries — triple-distilled Irish against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Jameson's smooth character meets the earthy-rich at crowd-pleasing register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir": "Jax Calesa Vineyard Pinot Noir's cherry-earth tannin plays cleanly against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis": "Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis's crisp apple-char acidity plays cleanly against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the oak frames the umami. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E.": "Jefferson's Ocean Marian McLain L.E. with truffle fries — master-blender-tribute sea-aged against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Marian McLain L.E.'s limited-edition character meets the earthy-rich at collector register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Jefferson's Ocean Voyage 23": "Jefferson's Ocean Voyage 23 with truffle fries — Voyage #23 sea-aged against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Voyage 23's salt-tinged character meets the earthy-rich with distinctive ocean-finish resonance.",
  "Truffle Fries|Jefferson's Reserve": "Jefferson's Reserve with truffle fries — blended elegance against truffle-parmesan. The smooth profile lets truffle lead; distinct from Woodford's fruit-forward take or BT's straight oak — Jefferson's sits in a polished middle. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Jefferson's Reserve VR Twin Oak": "Jefferson's Reserve VR Twin Oak with truffle fries — complex oak-finished bourbon against truffle-parmesan. The Twin Oak depth echoes the truffle's gravitas; a refined premium side pairing. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Jim Beam Black Label": "Jim Beam Black Label with truffle fries — 86-proof aged Beam against truffle-parmesan. The oak depth gives the side more body than White Label brings; an accessible aged-bourbon side. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Jim Beam White Label": "Jim Beam White Label with truffle fries — 80-proof entry Beam against truffle-parmesan. The approachable lightness lets truffle lead; this is the entry-level mixing bourbon at its best with a side. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Johnnie Walker Black": "JW Black with truffle fries — 12yr balanced JW against truffle-parmesan. Strong; JW Black's balanced smoke + aged-malt meets the earthy-rich at premium-blend register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Johnnie Walker Blue": "JW Blue with truffle fries — luxury JW against truffle-parmesan. Strong; JW Blue's silky-complex character meets the earthy-rich at collector register; consider whether the side deserves a $200 pour or if Blue is better spent on the main.",
  "Truffle Fries|Johnnie Walker Red": "JW Red with truffle fries — peat-influenced entry JW against truffle-parmesan. Strong; JW Red's smoke meets the earthy-rich with distinctive Islay-malt character.",
  "Truffle Fries|Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon": "Sonoma Cab — cassis, plum, cedar, mint, fine tannin, impeccable balance. The elegant body frames truffle-fry earth and the cedar cuts the crisp oil-and-salt. Peak elegant Cab for truffle fries — Jordan's refined character meets the decadent side with balance. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Joseph Mellot Sancerre": "Joseph Mellot Sancerre's crisp citrus-mineral acidity stays alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the crisp acidity sits with the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Truffle Fries|Jubilation by Colgin": "Jubilation — Colgin cult Napa, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violets, espresso, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the espresso plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak cult Napa for truffle fries — Pritchard Hill structure on the umami hit. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Jung and Wulff Guyana": "Jung and Wulff Guyana's bold char-earth character sits with the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the whiskey depth meets the indulgent side, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Jung and Wulff Trinidad": "Jung and Wulff Trinidad's rich layered-spirit body leans against the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the layered spirit body sits with the truffle fries, and the rich character softens the side. Strong; a steady recommendation at the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Kahlua": "Kahlua's sweet liqueur character clashes with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Kahlua for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Kansas City": "Kansas City with the truffle fries -- the 18oz lean-bold strip's savory grain meets the parmesan-and-truffle fry weight, classic steakhouse plate, both sides hold their weight. Strong; a confident order, no second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Keenan Chardonnay": "Keenan Chardonnay's bold apple-butter acidity holds with the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the oak frames the umami. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Truffle Fries|Keenan Mernet": "Truffle Fries: the structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit anchors the mushroom's umami weight; firm tannin and oak hold their register. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye": "Kentucky Owl 10 Year Rye with truffle fries — allocated KO against truffle-parmesan. The 10-year premium character gives the side collector-level frame. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Kentucky Owl Confiscated": "Kentucky Owl Confiscated with truffle fries — KO Confiscated against truffle-parmesan. The narrative-bourbon gives the side a KO storytelling frame. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's": "Kentucky Owl St. Patrick's with truffle fries — Kentucky Owl luxury Irish against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Kentucky Owl's distinctive bourbon-cask Irish character meets the earthy-rich at collector register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône": "Kermit Lynch Côtes du Rhône's cherry-earth tannin reads alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice frames the umami depth. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|Ketel One Vodka": "Ketel One Vodka's Dutch-wheat-crisp neutrality plays cleanly against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|Knickerbocker Gin": "Knickerbocker Gin's bold citrus-juniper botanicals reads alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Truffle Fries|Knob Creek": "Knob Creek with truffle fries — nutty oak and high-rye spice against truffle-parmesan. Knob's character gives the side more grip than wheated pours bring; a bolder everyday-premium side pairing. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Knob Creek 12 Year": "Knob Creek 12 Year with truffle fries — aged 12-year Beam against truffle-parmesan. The aging brings more oak-driven grip to the side than standard Knob Creek delivers. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Knob Creek 15 Year": "Knob Creek 15 with truffle fries — 15yr Beam KC against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; KC 15's aged depth meets the earthy-rich at aged-Beam register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Knob Creek 18 Year": "Knob Creek 18 with truffle fries — 18yr Beam KC against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; KC 18's aged depth meets the earthy-rich at collector register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye": "Knob Creek Bourbon/Rye with truffle fries — the blend's spicy-sweet against truffle-parmesan. A distinctive side pairing that shows what the bourbon-rye blend does with earth. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Knob Creek Rye": "Knob Creek Rye with truffle fries — 100-proof Beam rye against truffle-parmesan. The bold rye cuts through the richness with Beam authority. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Komos Anejo Reserva": "Truffle Fries: Parmesan-and-truffle meets Komos Anejo Reserva. Excellent; the multi-cask finish (French + Hungarian + wine) handles truffle-salt-fat at luxury-reserve register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Komos Crystallino Anejo": "Truffle Fries: Parmesan-and-truffle meets Komos Crystallino. Excellent; the crystallino-filtered complexity handles truffle-salt-fat at trendy-luxury register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Komos Extra Anejo": "Komos Extra Añejo with truffle fries — Riedel-luxury aged Komos against truffle-parmesan. The aged depth gives the side luxury-brand frame. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Komos Rosa Reposado": "Komos Rosa Reposado with truffle fries — wine-cask rosé against truffle-parmesan. Works; the pink character doesn't quite align with truffle's earth.",
  "Truffle Fries|Lagavulin 8": "Lagavulin 8 with truffle fries — citrus-oil brightness against truffle-parmesan fat. The 8-year's lift complements truffle's earthiness better than Laphroaig's medicinal approach; strong, if not quite the refined pour Bowmore brings. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Truffle Fries|Lail Vineyards Blueprint": "Napa Cab — Lail entry-level, polished blackcurrant, cedar, dark cherry, refined medium tannin. The refined tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the cedar plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak historically-pedigreed Napa Cab for truffle fries — Lail family structure on the umami hit. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Lail Vineyards Daniel Cuvée": "Lail flagship multi-appellation Napa Cab — dark fruit, cassis, graphite, dried violet, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the graphite plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak historically-significant Napa Cab for truffle fries — Lail family structure on the umami hit. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Lalo Silver": "Lalo Silver's blanco-tequila or blanco-tequila register leans against the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the silver-spirit register lifts the truffle fries, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Laphroaig 10": "Laphroaig 10 with truffle fries — medicinal peat against truffle-parmesan fat. Capable, but Laphroaig's intensity competes with the truffle rather than complementing it. Lagavulin 8 or Bowmore 12 are better Islay calls for this side. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Larceny Small Batch": "Larceny Small Batch with truffle fries — wheated caramel-honey against truffle-parmesan. The 92-proof body gives the fries more pour-weight than Maker's Mark brings; a clean, balanced side pairing. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé": "Laurent Perrier Brut Rosé's crisp berry-cherry acidity plays cleanly against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut": "Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut: this versatile sparkling's bright acidity, toasty lees character, and cleansing bubbles meets this earthy, umami-packed side's mushroom-and-truffle depth. Acid and bubbles scrub the side's fat while brightness keeps the palate clear. Avoid; redirect the order to a more aligned pour.",
  "Truffle Fries|Le Garenne Rosé": "Le Garenne Rosé's crisp floral-rose acidity reads alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Truffle Fries|Le Ragnaie Brunello": "Truffle Fries: the side's mushroom richness pulls the bold red's body; tannin and oak settle into the umami without overshooting. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Truffle Fries|Le Volte dell'Ornellaia": "Truffle Fries: the mushroom's umami depth meets the bold red's structured tannin; dark fruit threads the truffle-and-earth without crowding. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Lemon Lavender Gin Martini": "Lemon Lavender Gin Martini's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift finds neutral with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the bright build frames the truffle fries, and the citrus cuts the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|Les Pallières Raciné": "Truffle Fries: the bold red's cassis grip carries the mushroom-and-truffle depth — structured weight on the earthy side. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Liberator Gin": "Liberator Gin's citrus-juniper botanicals sits beside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Truffle Fries|Licor 43": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character flattens the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- sugar on starch is dessert territory — wrong course for the supporting plate. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Licor 43 on the steak course instead.",
  "Truffle Fries|Limoncello": "Limoncello's sweet liqueur character flattens the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- sugar on starch is dessert territory — wrong course for the supporting plate. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Limoncello for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir: this elegant red's cherry-bright, silky-tannin frame meets this earthy, umami-packed side's mushroom-and-truffle depth. The elegant red's acidity cuts the dairy fat while its cherry lifts the earthy umami. Works — clean if not dominant.",
  "Truffle Fries|Little Book": "Little Book with truffle fries — Beam blended cask-strength against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Little Book meets the earthy-rich at chapter-series register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Loaded Potato": "The loaded potato and the truffle fries -- potato-on-potato, the meal goes redundant. Avoid; the table reads heavy without payoff. Suggest Far Niente Chardonnay, Keenan Chardonnay, or Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir for the loaded potato, or The Tomahawk, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Belvedere Vodka for the truffle fries.",
  "Truffle Fries|Loch Lomond 20 Year": "Loch Lomond 20 Year with truffle fries — 20yr complex-aged Highland against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Loch Lomond 20's aged depth and varied-still complexity meet the earthy-rich at collector register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Lock Stock & Barrel Rye": "Lock Stock & Barrel Rye with truffle fries — premium sourced against truffle-parmesan. The boutique-blend character gives the side a premium-sourced frame. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Long Road Gin": "Long Road Gin's crisp citrus-juniper botanicals stays alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|Los Vecinos Mezcal": "Los Vecinos Mezcal's agave-pit-smoke character holds the line with the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the agave smoke layers into the rich side, and the smoke meets the umami depth. Strong; the call lands cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Louis XIII Cognac": "Louis XIII with truffle fries — 1,200-eaux-de-vie Baccarat-decanter cognac against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; earthy truffle depth is tier-appropriate for a bottle that demands earthy reverence — the only side on the menu that can share the table with Louis XIII without feeling casual by comparison.",
  "Truffle Fries|Lucano Amaro": "Lucano with truffle fries — Basilicata amaro against truffle-parmesan. Works; floral-anise is a distinctive counterpoint.",
  "Truffle Fries|Lunaria Coste di Moro": "Abruzzo Montepulciano d'Abruzzo — Lunaria earthy grippy, dark cherry, dried herbs, rustic medium body, medium tannin. The medium tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the dried herbs play against the truffle-oil umami. Peak Italian-approachable red for truffle fries — rustic Italian character on the umami hit. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Macallan 12 Sherry": "Macallan 12 Sherry with truffle fries — benchmark sherried-Speyside against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Macallan 12's Oloroso dried-fruit meets the earthy-rich with sherry-cask complexity.",
  "Truffle Fries|Macallan 18": "Macallan 18 with truffle fries — 18yr aged sherried Speyside against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Macallan 18's aged-sherry character meets the earthy-rich at premium register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Macallan Estate": "Macallan Estate with truffle fries — Estate-oak premium Macallan against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Macallan Estate's distinctive oak character meets the earthy-rich with distillery-estate-terroir resonance.",
  "Truffle Fries|Macauley Petite Syrah": "Napa Petite Sirah — Macauley, inky color, dense powerful tannin (not Syrah), blackberry, blueberry, dark chocolate, black pepper, full body. The black pepper cuts parm-richness and the dense tannin handles truffle-oil weight. Strong Petite-Sirah for truffle fries — powerful Napa on the cut.",
  "Truffle Fries|Macauley Pinot Noir": "Macauley Pinot Noir's crisp cherry-floral tannin leans against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Macauley Stagecoach Vineyard": "Truffle Fries: the bold red's cassis grip carries the mushroom-and-truffle depth — structured weight on the earthy side. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Mahon Gin": "Mahon Gin's bold herbal-juniper botanicals stays alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the oak frames the umami. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|Maker's Mark": "Maker's Mark with truffle fries — the iconic red-wax wheated against truffle-parmesan. The 90-proof softness lets truffle lead; a guest-friendly pairing that doesn't make demands. Gold standard; the recommendation that earns the regular.",
  "Truffle Fries|Maker's Mark Cellar Aged": "Maker's Mark Cellar Aged with truffle fries — deeper caramel and vanilla meet truffle earth. The extended maturation gives the pour the richness to echo the truffle; standard Maker's is just sweet here, Cellar Aged is resonant. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Malibu Rum": "Malibu Rum's clean silver register finds neutral with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the light-rum body cuts the truffle fries, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye": "Mammoth 16 Year Single Barrel Rye with truffle fries — 16-year aged Michigan against truffle-parmesan. The extended maturation gives the side distinctive aged-rye character with home-state pride. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Marc Brédif Chinon": "Marc Brédif Chinon's cherry-earth tannin sits beside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|Margarita": "Margarita's crisp agave-brine build stays alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the agave anchors the savory plate. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Truffle Fries|Marimar Estate Christina": "Marimar Estate Christina's cherry-earth tannin sits alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the spice frames the umami depth. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|Market Fish": "The market fish into the truffle fries -- delicate yields to savory weight cleanly. Works; safe alongside, but not the headline pick.",
  "Truffle Fries|Mata Hari Absinthe": "Mata Hari Absinthe's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- bitter aperitivo on the supporting side reads as wrong register for the course. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Reserve the Mata Hari Absinthe for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Michter's 10 Year Bourbon": "Michter's 10 Bourbon with truffle fries — Michter's allocated 10yr against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Michter's 10's single-barrel depth meets the earthy-rich at prestigious-independent register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Michter's 10 Year Rye": "Michter's 10 Year Rye with truffle fries — aged premium Michter's against truffle-parmesan. The polished 10-year depth gives the side a refined small-batch frame. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Michter's US*1 Rye": "Michter's US*1 Rye with truffle fries — smooth small-batch rye against truffle-parmesan. The Michter's polish gives the side a refined frame. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Mijenta Blanco": "Mijenta Blanco's green-agave-and-cane lift sits alongside the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the unaged body brightens the truffle fries, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the side. Works; the ceremony overshoots the dish.",
  "Truffle Fries|Milagro Anejo": "Truffle Fries: Parmesan-and-truffle meets Milagro Anejo. Excellent; the softer-refined character handles truffle-salt-fat at French-oak register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Milagro Reposado": "Milagro Reposado with truffle fries — modern reposado against truffle-parmesan. Works; clean character doesn't drive the pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Mister Sam Tribute Whiskey": "Mister Sam with truffle fries — Sazerac tribute blended whiskey against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Mister Sam's aged-blended depth meets the earthy-rich at Seagram's-tribute register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Mocha Creme": "The truffle fries alongside the mocha creme -- the sweet register lifts the umami, the contrast holds without crowding. Works; the contrast holds, neither course overshadows the other.",
  "Truffle Fries|Monkey 47 Gin": "Monkey 47 Gin's crisp Black-Forest-botanical botanicals leans against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Truffle Fries|Monkey Shoulder": "Monkey Shoulder with truffle fries — Glenfiddich-Balvenie-Kininvie blend against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Monkey Shoulder's Speyside-malt rich-fruit-and-vanilla meets the earthy-rich with distinctive blended-malt character.",
  "Truffle Fries|Montenegro Amaro": "Montenegro with truffle fries — Bologna amaro against truffle-parmesan. Works; vanilla-orange is a gentle counterpoint.",
  "Truffle Fries|Mount Gay Rum": "Mount Gay Rum's unaged silver-rum body sits alongside the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the silver-rum body cuts the truffle fries, and the unaged-cane note plays against the side. Works; refined character is slightly over-specified for the dish.",
  "Truffle Fries|Muga Reserva": "Rioja Alta Reserva Tempranillo-blend — Muga, American-French oak, strawberry, dried cherry, vanilla, leather, savory-earthy. The savory-earthy finish echoes truffle-oil mushroom depth and the vanilla wraps around parm. Peak Rioja for truffle fries — oak-and-earth match. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Mushroom Bisque": "Mushroom Bisque and the truffle fries -- the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream meets the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: both build on umami, the plate carries weight without contrast. Works; no conflict however the table orders them.",
  "Truffle Fries|Mushrooms": "Mushrooms and the truffle fries together -- the garlic-butter mushroom plays against the parmesan-and-truffle side. Strong; the two sides hold the plate at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Myers's Rum": "Myers's Rum's bold molasses-Jamaican character finds register with the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the whiskey depth meets the indulgent side. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Negroni": "Gin, Contratto, Campari — stirred, orange peel. The bitter-orange backbone plays against truffle oil's earthy richness and the herbal vermouth adds depth against parmesan. Works as a bitter cocktail-side pairing when guest leads with the Negroni.",
  "Truffle Fries|Never Say Die Rye": "Never Say Die Rye with truffle fries — Yorkshire-aged rye against truffle-parmesan. The novelty cask character gives the side a distinctive story-driven frame. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Never Say Die Small Batch": "Never Say Die Small Batch with truffle fries — UK-aged Kentucky bourbon against truffle-parmesan. The Yorkshire cask influence gives the side a different dimension than any domestic-aged bourbon brings. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|New Holland Beer Barrel Bourbon": "New Holland Beer Barrel Bourbon with truffle fries — Michigan beer-barrel finish against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; NH Beer Barrel's hop-character meets the earthy-rich with distinctive Michigan-hometown register.",
  "Truffle Fries|New York Sour": "Jameson, lemon, simple, egg white, Daou Cab float. The lemon-sour cuts truffle oil's earth and the egg-white foam adds textural contrast against the crispy fries. Works as an unconventional spirit-forward pairing — though heavier whiskey cocktails peak higher for the truffle depth.",
  "Truffle Fries|Nickel & Nickel Cabernet": "Truffle Fries: the structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit anchors the mushroom's umami weight; firm tannin and oak hold their register. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Nolets Dry Gin": "Nolets Dry Gin's bold char-floral botanicals sits beside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Not a Paper Plane": "Bulleit, Nonino amaro, Aperol, Angostura — stirred down, spirit-forward, bittersweet. The Nonino's herbal bitterness and Aperol's orange depth echo truffle's complexity. Grappa-based amaro character rewards attention on this non-obvious cocktail pairing. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Oban 14": "Oban 14 with truffle fries — West Highland coastal single malt against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Oban's subtle smoke and sea-salt meet the earthy-rich with distinctive maritime-Highland character.",
  "Truffle Fries|Oban 18": "Oban 18 with truffle fries — 18yr West Highland against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Oban 18's aged maritime + sherry-finish meets the earthy-rich at premium register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Ocho Anejo": "Truffle Fries: Parmesan-and-truffle meets Ocho Anejo. Excellent; mineral-driven highland character with whiskey-cask depth handles truffle-salt-fat at craft register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Odette Cabernet Sauvignon": "Truffle Fries: the side's mushroom richness pulls the bold red's body; tannin and oak settle into the umami without overshooting. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Old Elk Cigar Cut": "Old Elk Cigar Cut with truffle fries — Old Elk Colorado craft against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Old Elk Cigar Cut's cigar-companion character meets the earthy-rich at distinctive register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Old Emmer": "Old Emmer with truffle fries — emmer-wheat wheated bourbon against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Old Emmer's craft-wheated character meets the earthy-rich at distinctive register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Old Fitzgerald 7 Year": "Old Fitzgerald 7 Year with truffle fries — wheated BIB against truffle-parmesan. The bonded wheat weight and heritage character give the side distinctive dimension. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Old Fitzgerald 9 Year": "Old Fitzgerald 9 Year with truffle fries — aged wheated BIB against truffle-parmesan. The mature honey gives the side a distinctive sophisticated frame. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Old Grand-Dad 16 Year": "OGD 16 with truffle fries — 16yr OGD rye-forward against truffle-parmesan. Strong; OGD 16's aged rye-spice meets the earthy-rich at distinctive register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Opus One": "Opus One — Oakville Bordeaux blend, dark fruit, mocha, cedar, dried violet, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the cedar-mocha plays against truffle-oil umami. Peak collector Napa Cab blend for truffle fries — prestige wine layered with the truffle hit. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Our Lady of Guadalupe Acolytes": "Our Lady of Guadalupe Acolytes's bold butter-char acidity holds with the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the crisp acidity sits with the plate, and the oak frames the umami. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|Pablo Sour": "Pablo Sour's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift crowds the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- a light cocktail belongs with the opener or aperitif, not a savory side. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a light cocktail. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pablo Sour lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Truffle Fries|Paloma": "Paloma's crisp agave-citrus build sits beside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the oak frames the umami. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Truffle Fries|Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye": "Pappy Van Winkle 13 Year Rye with truffle fries — Pappy Rye against truffle-parmesan. The Van Winkle unicorn gives the side legacy-level ceremony. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Parker's Heritage Collection 16th Edition": "Parker's Heritage 16th Ed with truffle fries — HH annual cask-strength against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Parker's Heritage 16th meets the earthy-rich at collector register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Patron Anejo": "Truffle Fries: Parmesan-and-truffle meets Patron Anejo. Excellent; the cooked-agave-vanilla character handles truffle-salt-fat at premium register — crowd-pleasing añejo answer.",
  "Truffle Fries|Patron Silver": "Patron Silver's polished silver tequila with agave-forward lift reads alongside the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the blanco-tequila body matches the truffle fries, and the lime-and-pepper thread softens the side. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|Patron XO Cafe": "Patron XO Cafe's sweet liqueur character clashes with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Patron XO Cafe for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Paul Bara Grand Rosé Brut": "Paul Bara Grand Rosé Brut's crisp mineral-raspberry acidity sits beside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Truffle Fries and the PB brownie -- the sweet register lifts the umami, the contrast holds without crowding. Works; clean transition or together if the table wants.",
  "Truffle Fries|Peju Cabernet Sauvignon": "Peju — Rutherford Cab with dark cherry, cassis, dusty cocoa, refined tannin. The elegant body frames truffle-fry earth and the Rutherford-dust cuts the crisp oil-and-salt with complexity. Peak elegant Napa Cab for truffle fries — family-estate character meets the decadent side. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Pierre Ferrand Cognac": "Pierre Ferrand with truffle fries — Angeac-Champagne artisanal cognac against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Ferrand's traditional craft character meets the earthy-rich with unblended dimension Hennessy's eaux-de-vie blend doesn't bring.",
  "Truffle Fries|Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut": "Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut's char-citrus acidity sits alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|Pikesville Rye": "Pikesville Rye with truffle fries — 110-proof bold rye against truffle-parmesan. The high proof cuts through richness with Maryland-style intensity. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Pineau des Charentes": "Pineau des Charentes' sweet liqueur character clashes with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- a sweet liqueur on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Pineau des Charentes for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Pio Cesare Barbaresco": "Truffle Fries: the structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit anchors the mushroom's umami weight; firm tannin and oak hold their register. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Plymouth Gin": "Plymouth Gin's Plymouth-style-rounder botanicals sits alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|Poderi Aldo Conterno Nebbiolo": "Truffle Fries: the bold red's cassis grip carries the mushroom-and-truffle depth — structured weight on the earthy side. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the call sits without strain.",
  "Truffle Fries|Pommery Cuvée Louise": "* Pommery Cuvée Louise -- prestige Champagne, brioche, fine mousse. The bright effervescence carries the truffle fries, and the bright acidity cuts the side. Peak seafood tower Champagne. Gold standard; a confident headline pour.",
  "Truffle Fries|Porterhouse": "Porterhouse alongside the truffle fries -- the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character carries cleanly into the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight. Excellent; the headline side pairing for the porterhouse.",
  "Truffle Fries|Prime Tartare": "The tartare and the truffle fries -- both build on umami, the plate carries weight without contrast. Works; sequence them or share the table, no concern either way.",
  "Truffle Fries|Quilt Cabernet Sauvignon": "Quilt — polished Napa Cab with blackberry, dark chocolate, toasted vanilla. The lush chocolate-vanilla frames truffle-fry earth and the ripe fruit cuts the crisp oil-and-salt. Peak indulgent Napa Cab for truffle fries — lush body meets the decadent side without overpowering. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|RAEN Royal St Robert": "RAEN Royal St Robert's cherry-mineral tannin sits beside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Rainbow Trout": "Rainbow Trout with the truffle fries -- the trout's delicate flesh meets the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the lighter plate hands off to the savory, the table arcs clean. Works; the side reads as a measured plate companion.",
  "Truffle Fries|Raventós Cava de NIT Rosé Brut": "Raventós Cava de NIT Rosé Brut's crisp brine-mineral acidity leans against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Redbreast 12 Year": "Redbreast 12 with truffle fries — single pot still premium Irish against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Redbreast 12's pot still oiliness meets the earthy-rich at premium register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Redbreast 21 Year": "Redbreast 21 with truffle fries — aged pot still Irish against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Redbreast 21's aged pot still oiliness meets the earthy-rich at collector register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Remus 15 Year Gatsby Reserve": "Remus 15 Gatsby with truffle fries — MGP 15yr high-rye against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Remus 15's aged rye-spice meets the earthy-rich at Gatsby-tribute register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Remy VSOP Cognac": "Rémy VSOP with truffle fries — Grande Champagne cognac against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Rémy's elegance meets the earthy-rich with refined polish — the most luxurious working-cognac truffle pairing in the batch.",
  "Truffle Fries|Rey Sol Anejo": "Rey Sol Anejo with truffle fries — Moorish-inspired bottle against truffle-parmesan. The distinctive packaging gives the side ceremonial-frame. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Reyka Vodka": "Reyka Vodka's crisp Icelandic-glacial neutrality sits beside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Rishi's Old Antique": "Rishi's Old Antique with truffle fries — retailer-label aged against truffle-parmesan. The boutique-sourced character gives the side a retailer-label frame. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Roast Half Chicken": "Roast Half Chicken with the truffle fries -- the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast meets the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: protein and umami share the plate, the build reads weighty and clean. Works; the side reads as a measured plate companion.",
  "Truffle Fries|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "The chickpea soup and the truffle fries on the same meal -- the courses pull from different keys but share the table cleanly. Works; sequence or share, the build holds.",
  "Truffle Fries|Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs": "Robert Moncuit Les Grand Blancs's crisp apple-char acidity plays cleanly against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Truffle Fries|Roku Gin": "Roku Gin's crisp floral-juniper botanicals stays alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Ron Zacapa Rum": "Ron Zacapa Rum's Solera-honey character matches the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the crisp body sits with the plate. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Russell's Reserve 10 Year": "Russell's Reserve 10 Year with truffle fries — aged Wild Turkey oak against truffle-parmesan. The classic Kentucky depth frames the truffle without the Wellers' wheat-sweet doubling; a sophisticated non-wheated pairing. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Salt-Cured Halibut alongside the truffle fries -- the delicate course primes the savory, the table builds register. Works; the side carries cleanly with the halibut.",
  "Truffle Fries|Sambuca": "Sambuca's sweet liqueur character flattens the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- sugar on starch is dessert territory — wrong course for the supporting plate. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Sambuca for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|San Simeon Stormwatch": "Paso Robles Cab-dominant Bordeaux blend — dark cherry, blackcurrant, mocha, medium tannin. The medium tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the mocha plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak Paso value Bordeaux blend for truffle fries — solid full-body on the umami hit. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir": "Sanford & Benedict Pinot Noir's cherry-earth tannin stays alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the medium-body red sits with the rich side, and the cherry-fruit frames the umami depth. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Sauternes Glass": "Sauternes Glass' dessert-wine sweetness flattens the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- dessert sugar on starch is wrong-course energy for the supporting plate. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Sauternes Glass for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Sazerac": "Sazerac rye, Peychaud's, sugar, absinthe-rinsed glass. The anise-edge nose plays against truffle oil's earth and the rye's spice meets the parmesan-truffle crust. Peak classic pairing when the fries anchor a spirit-forward cocktail program. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Sazerac Rye": "Sazerac Rye with truffle fries — 90-proof iconic rye against truffle-parmesan fat. The rye's spice cuts through the richness with benchmark precision. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Scapegrace Fortuna": "Scapegrace Fortuna with truffle fries — New Zealand craft single malt against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Fortuna's NZ terroir meets the earthy-rich with distinctive southern-hemisphere character.",
  "Truffle Fries|Scavino Barolo": "Piedmont Barolo DOCG Nebbiolo — Scavino Castiglione Falletto, tar, dried rose, cherry, leather, powerful firm tannin, high acid. The firm tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the tar plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak King-of-Italian for truffle fries — tar-truffle echo, Scavino prestige on the umami hit. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Schloss Vollrads Riesling": "Schloss Vollrads Riesling's off-dry Rheingau Riesling with lime-petrol edge finds neutral with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the off-dry body brightens the truffle fries, and the lime-petrol note threads the side. Works; the two desserts share the close without crowding.",
  "Truffle Fries|Scotto Cellars The Lost Chapters": "California Cab by-the-glass — black cherry, cassis, dark chocolate, integrated medium tannin. The medium tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the dark chocolate plays against the truffle-oil umami. Strong by-the-glass Cab for truffle fries — accessible California value on the umami hit.",
  "Truffle Fries|Seafood Tower": "The seafood tower and the truffle fries -- acid breaks the umami stack, the table earns the brighter note. Works; the call holds whether the table sequences them or shares.",
  "Truffle Fries|Seared Scallops": "The scallops and the truffle fries -- protein meets umami, the table builds substance. Works; sequence them or share the table, no concern either way.",
  "Truffle Fries|Seasonal Soup": "The seasonal soup and the truffle fries -- a clean call, no friction either way. Works; sequence them or share the table, the call holds either way.",
  "Truffle Fries|Sesti Brunello di Montalcino": "Tuscany Brunello DOCG Sangiovese Grosso — Sesti biodynamic, cherry, dried rose, sandalwood, firm tannin. The earthy sandalwood echoes truffle-oil mushroom depth and the firm tannin cuts through parm-richness. Peak biodynamic-Brunello for truffle fries — Sesti's earth-on-earth Tuscan match. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Shafer 1.5": "Truffle Fries: the mushroom's umami depth meets the bold red's structured tannin; dark fruit threads the truffle-and-earth without crowding. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Shafer Hillside Select": "Stags Leap collector's Cab — Hillside Select 32-month French oak, blackcurrant, dark chocolate, violet, graphite, dense yet silky, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the graphite plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak collector's Napa Cab for truffle fries — one of the great bottles on the umami hit. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Shrimp Bisque": "Shrimp Bisque and the truffle fries -- the shrimp bisque's creamy shellfish soup meets the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: dairy plays against umami, the table reads layered. Works; no conflict however the table orders them.",
  "Truffle Fries|Shrimp Cocktail": "Shrimp Cocktail alongside the truffle fries -- the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish meets the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: acid lifts the umami, the meal carries lift without losing depth. Works; no conflict, the meal builds.",
  "Truffle Fries|Siete Leguas Blanco": "Siete Leguas Blanco's clean silver register sits alongside the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the unaged body brightens the truffle fries, and the green-agave edge brightens the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Siete Leguas Reposado": "Siete Leguas Reposado with truffle fries — traditional agave against truffle-parmesan. Works; the earthy craft character doesn't quite lift the truffle the way polished reposados suggest they might.",
  "Truffle Fries|Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon": "Alexander Valley Cab — American-oak vanilla, coconut, dill, ripe cassis, plum. The lush body frames truffle-fry earth and the vanilla-dill cuts the crisp oil-and-salt. Peak recognizable Cab for truffle fries — Silver Oak's distinctive American-oak signature meets the decadent side. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Simon Family Estate Reserve": "Boutique Napa family estate Cab — dark plum, cassis, toasted oak, long refined finish, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the toasted oak plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak boutique Napa Cab for truffle fries — Simon Family reserve-level structure on the umami hit. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Spottswoode Lyndenhurst": "St. Helena Napa Cab — Spottswoode organic family estate, plum, dark cherry, violet, silky medium tannin. The silky tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the violet plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak organic Napa Cab for truffle fries — Spottswoode family story on the umami hit. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|St Supéry Cabernet Sauvignon": "St Supéry — Napa Cab with blackberry, cassis, mocha, firm tannin. The mocha-tannin frames truffle-fry earth and the cassis fruit cuts the crisp oil-and-salt. Peak by-the-glass Cab for truffle fries — Rutherford Cab character at a price that fits the side-order moment. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc": "St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc's citrus-lemon acidity reads alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the crisp acidity sits with the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|St Supéry Élu Meritage": "Napa Dollarhide Meritage — blackcurrant, black cherry, espresso, toasty oak, firm tannin. The firm tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the espresso-oak plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak estate Meritage for truffle fries — age-integrated Napa structure on the umami hit. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Stagg Jr. Batch #15": "Stagg Jr. Batch #15 with truffle fries — BT cask-strength against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Stagg Jr. meets the earthy-rich at barrel-proof register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Stoli Elit Vodka": "Stoli Elit Vodka's crisp ultra-filtered-luxury neutrality leans against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Truffle Fries|Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc": "Marlborough Sauvignon Blanc — grassy, green, light. Wrong weight class for truffle fries entirely; the wine disappears under truffle and fry sauce. Keep Stoneleigh for the wedge or the shrimp cocktail. Avoid; the pairing fights at the table — point the guest elsewhere.",
  "Truffle Fries|Swordfish": "Swordfish alongside the truffle fries -- the savory course rounds the protein, the meal reads layered. Works; the side carries cleanly with the swordfish.",
  "Truffle Fries|Tanq 10 Gin": "Tanq 10 Gin's crisp citrus-floral botanicals stays alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|Tanqueray Gin": "Tanqueray Gin's bold London-Dry-juniper botanicals sits alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the gin botanicals sit with the plate, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Truffle Fries|Taylor Fladgate Tawny": "Taylor Fladgate Tawny's classic tawny with caramel-nut sweetness flattens the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- dessert sugar on starch is wrong-course energy for the supporting plate. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Taylor Fladgate Tawny for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle": "Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle's dessert-wine sweetness clashes with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- sweet wine on a savory side is wrong-course energy. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle belongs on the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Tears of Llorona": "Tears of Llorona with truffle fries — triple-cask Scotch/sherry/cognac against truffle-parmesan. The cask-influence layers create a frame for the earthy side that no other extra añejo replicates. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Teeter Totter Cabernet Sauvignon": "Truffle Fries: the mushroom's umami depth meets the bold red's structured tannin; dark fruit threads the truffle-and-earth without crowding. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Tenuta di Arceno Chianti Classico": "Truffle Fries: the side's mushroom richness pulls the bold red's body; tannin and oak settle into the umami without overshooting. A headliner pair — pour confidently. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|The BG": "Traveller whiskey, honey lavender syrup, whole grapefruit squeeze, black walnut bitters, ginger beer. The grapefruit brightens truffle oil's earth and the whiskey adds depth; ginger beer keeps the cocktail sessionable alongside the side. Works as a refreshing cocktail pairing for truffle fries.",
  "Truffle Fries|The Happy Wife": "The Happy Wife's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift finds neutral with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the bright build frames the truffle fries, and the citrus cuts the side. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|The Manhattan": "Maker's Mark private barrel, Contratto vermouth, vanilla syrup, Angostura. The bourbon's oak-vanilla-caramel depth meets truffle oil's earth directly and the Italian vermouth's herbal complexity plays against parmesan. Peak cocktail-side pairing when the fries carry the table's flavor weight. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|The Prisoner Red Blend": "Napa Red Blend — The Prisoner, Zin-Cab-Petite Sirah-Syrah-Charbono, layered dark fruit, smooth integrated tannin, full body, lush finish. The layered fruit plays with truffle-oil mushroom depth and the integrated tannin cuts parm-richness. Peak Prisoner for truffle fries — recognized-label lush on the cut. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|The Tomahawk": "* The Tomahawk alongside the truffle fries -- the Tomahawk's theatrical bone-in marbling and smoky char carries cleanly into the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight. Gold standard; a confident headline pour.",
  "Truffle Fries|Thomas H. Handy Sazerac Rye": "Thomas H. Handy Sazerac Rye with truffle fries — BTAC allocated against truffle-parmesan. The uncut Sazerac intensity gives the side collector-level frame. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Thomas S. Moore Chardonnay Cask": "Thomas S. Moore Chardonnay Cask with truffle fries — chardonnay-cask bourbon against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; TSM Chardonnay Cask's chardonnay-butter meets the earthy-rich with distinctive white-wine-finish character.",
  "Truffle Fries|Titos Vodka": "Titos Vodka's Texas-corn-workhorse neutrality plays cleanly against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Truffle Fries|Toki Suntory Japanese Whisky": "Toki Suntory with truffle fries — light-floral Japanese blend against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Toki's delicate character meets the earthy-rich at crowd-pleasing register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Tomato Basil": "The tomato basil and the truffle fries on the same meal -- the bright register pulls against the savory, the contrast lands. Works; sequence or share, the build holds.",
  "Truffle Fries|Transfusion": "Transfusion's crisp citrus-ginger build finds neutral with the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|Trombo Cedano Reposado": "Trombo Cedano Reposado with truffle fries — cedar-aged reposado against truffle-parmesan. The cedar and truffle meet in forest-floor territory; a distinctive cedar-truffle resonance. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Tullamore D.E.W.": "Tullamore D.E.W. with truffle fries — traditional heritage Irish against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Tullamore's drier heritage meets the earthy-rich at traditional register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "The tuna into the truffle fries -- restrained gives way to umami, the meal earns its weight. Works; safe alongside, but not the headline pick.",
  "Truffle Fries|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas and the truffle fries -- the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth meets the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight: the courses pull from different keys but share the table cleanly. Works; no conflict however the table orders them.",
  "Truffle Fries|Venge Family Reserve": "Kirk Venge flagship Oakville Cab — concentrated blackcurrant, dark chocolate, vanilla, seamless polished finish, soft tannin. The soft tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the dark chocolate plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak Oakville flagship for truffle fries — Venge craftsman opulence on the umami hit. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Venge Scout's Honor": "Napa Zin-led blend — Kirk Venge's Scout's Honor, blackberry, boysenberry, black pepper, vanilla, full body, generous finish. The vanilla meets truffle-oil earth directly and the black pepper cuts parmesan weight. Peak Zin-led for truffle fries — jammy fruit handles the indulgent side. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Venge Silencieux": "Kirk Venge single-vineyard Napa — dark cherry, cassis, chocolate, floral violet, silky soft tannin. The silky tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the chocolate-violet plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak winemaker's Napa Cab for truffle fries — Venge precision on the umami hit. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Vesper": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build plays cleanly against the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the botanicals frame the umami depth. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|Veuve Clicquot Brut": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's biscuit-apple acidity reads alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Truffle Fries|Vieux Carré": "Sazerac rye, Pierre Ferrand cognac, Contratto, Bénédictine, two bitters. The cocktail's herbal complexity from Bénédictine meets truffle oil's earth directly and the rye-cognac depth handles parmesan weight. Peak sophisticated pairing when the fries anchor the table. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Villon Cognac": "Villon with truffle fries — modern cognac against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Villon's saffron-elderflower infusion meets the earthy-rich with distinctive contemporary character.",
  "Truffle Fries|Vin Santo": "Vin Santo's Tuscan dried-fruit-and-honey sweetness flattens the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- dessert sugar on starch is wrong-course energy for the supporting plate. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a dessert wine. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Vin Santo for the steak course.",
  "Truffle Fries|Weller 107": "Weller 107 with truffle fries — bolder wheated against truffle-parmesan fat. The higher proof doesn't overpower the truffle; it matches its earthiness with more heft than Weller Special Reserve. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Weller 12 Year": "Weller 12 Year with truffle fries — twelve years of oak and vanilla against truffle-parmesan fat. The aged wheated sweetness lifts the truffle's earthiness rather than competing with it. A refined pairing; Maker's Mark Cellar Aged is the alternate premium wheated call here. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Weller Millennium": "Weller Millennium with truffle fries — deep honeyed wheat against truffle-parmesan fat. The Millennium brings more gravitas than Weller 12 here; a pairing that feels like it belongs on a special-occasion menu. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Weller Special Reserve": "Weller Special Reserve with truffle fries — caramel-vanilla wheat against truffle-parmesan fat. The entry Weller meets the truffle's earthiness without overreaching; a crowd-pleasing pairing. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Wheatley Vodka": "Wheatley Vodka's crisp cream neutrality stays alongside the truffle fries' Parmesan-and-truffle salt — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Truffle Fries|WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel Rye": "WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel with truffle fries — 10-year WP single-barrel against truffle-parmesan. The aged depth gives the side real grip at the WP-core premium register. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|WhistlePig 12 Year Old World": "WhistlePig 12 Year Old World with truffle fries — multi-cask 12-year against truffle-parmesan. The Old World complexity gives the side layered fruit-and-earth dimension. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|WhistlePig 15 Year": "WhistlePig 15 Year with truffle fries — 15-year premium WP against truffle-parmesan. The extended maturation gives the side a flagship-premium frame. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|WhistlePig Boss Hog IX 17 Year": "WhistlePig Boss Hog IX with truffle fries — allocated barrel-proof WP against truffle-parmesan. The Boss Hog intensity gives the side unicorn-level frame; if the table ordered Boss Hog, the fries elevate to ceremony. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|WhistlePig Boss Hog X Commandments": "WhistlePig Boss Hog X with truffle fries — X Commandments allocated WP against truffle-parmesan. The 10th-edition gives the side collector-level frame; ceremony pairing. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Truffle Fries|WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year": "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year with truffle fries — accessible WP 100-proof against truffle-parmesan. The Canadian-sourced character cuts the richness with Vermont-brand distinctiveness. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Willett Pot Still Reserve": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with truffle fries — high-rye oak spice against truffle-parmesan. The craft character gives the side more vocabulary than the everyday bourbons bring; a sophisticated side pairing. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Woodford Reserve": "Woodford Reserve with truffle fries — fruit-forward small-batch against truffle-parmesan. The floral complexity meets truffle's earth with more vocabulary than BT or the Wellers bring; a refined side pairing. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Woodford Reserve Double Oaked": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked with truffle fries — Brown-Forman KY Double Oaked against truffle-parmesan. Excellent; Woodford Double Oaked's caramel-oak meets the earthy-rich at KY-benchmark register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Woodford Reserve Rye": "Woodford Reserve Rye with truffle fries — elegant rye against truffle-parmesan. The fruit-forward character gives the side a refined small-batch frame. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Truffle Fries|Woodinville Rye": "Woodinville Rye with truffle fries — Washington craft rye against truffle-parmesan. The local-grain character gives the side a non-Kentucky regional frame. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Truffle Fries|Yamazaki 12 Year": "Yamazaki 12 with truffle fries — Suntory flagship single malt against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Yamazaki 12's Mizunara-oak sandalwood-hint meets the earthy-rich at flagship register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Yamazaki 18 Year": "Yamazaki 18 with truffle fries — aged Suntory single malt against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Yamazaki 18's deeper Mizunara-oak meets the earthy-rich at collector register.",
  "Truffle Fries|Yellow Chartreuse": "Yellow Chartreuse's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the truffle fries' parmesan-and-truffle fry weight -- bitter aperitivo on the supporting side reads as wrong register for the course. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Belvedere Vodka, or Maker's Mark, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Yellow Chartreuse lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Asparagus": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend leans against the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the Irish whiskey body sits with the asparagus, and the triple-distilled smoothness brightens the side. Works; Voyage 23 frames the two-cut plate at ocean-finish register.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend leans against the au gratin's cheese-and-cream golden crust: the malt-grain blend handles the au gratin, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; BIB structure overshoots the dessert's delicacy.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Beignets": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend reads alongside the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the Irish whiskey body sits with the beignets, and the orchard-fruit edge underlines the dessert. Works; bold character slightly over-specified for the soup.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Bone Marrow": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s crisp grain-malt character holds steady against the marrow's umami-fat depth — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the rounded sweetness brightens the cream. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Bone-In Filet": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend sits alongside the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the smooth triple-distilled register matches the bone-enhanced filet, and the orchard-fruit edge underlines the cut. Works; pour is a touch over-specified for this dish.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Broccoli Cheddar": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend sits alongside the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the gentle Irish body sits with the broccoli cheddar, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; pour's narrative is underused by the salad.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Broccolini": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend leans against the broccolini's tender green stalks: the smooth triple-distilled register matches the broccolini, and the grain register softens the side. Works; the complex character gives the dessert a refined frame.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Brussels and Belly": "Tullamore D.E.W. with Brussels + Belly — heritage Irish blend against maple-glazed pork belly. Strong; Tullamore's drier character cuts the glaze at traditional register.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Burrata": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend clashes with the burrata's fresh basil-tomato-cream delicacy -- bourbon weight buries the milky cheese plate's delicate frame. The plate deserves Il Colle Prosecco Superiore, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Tullamore D.E.W. belongs on the steak course.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Butternut Squash": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend finds neutral with the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the approachable Irish character carries the squash bisque, and the oak threads the cream. Works; Voyage 23 handles the richness at ocean-finish register.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Carrot Cake": "Tullamore D.E.W. with carrot cake — drier traditional Irish against cream cheese and cinnamon. Works; Tullamore's heritage character threads the cake at drier register.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Cheesecake": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend leans against the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the Irish whiskey body sits with the cheesecake, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Chilean Seabass": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Tullamore D.E.W. belongs on the steak course.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Chocolate Brownie": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend leans against the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight: the approachable Irish character carries the brownie, and the soft malt rounds the dessert. Works; private-selection wasted on the salad.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Chocolate Cake": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend reads alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the smooth triple-distilled register matches the chocolate cake, and the soft malt rounds the dessert. Works; namesake pour is wasted on the salad.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Clam Chowder": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the soft malt-and-grain weight wraps the chowder, and the oak threads the cream. Works; boutique covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Cowboy Ribeye": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend sits alongside the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness: the Irish whiskey body sits with the cap-fat ribeye, and the triple-distilled smoothness brightens the cut. Works; richer profile overshoots the dessert's delicacy.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Crab Cake": "Tullamore D.E.W. with crab cake — traditional triple-distilled Irish against delicate lump crab. Works; Tullamore's heritage character sits alongside crab at traditional-Irish register; vodka or gin still lead for the featured crab pairing.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Creamed Spinach": "Tullamore D.E.W. with creamed spinach — heritage Irish against dairy-rich side. Works; Tullamore's drier character rides the cream at traditional register.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Creamy Potato": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the malt-grain blend handles the potato soup, and the oak threads the cream. Works; boutique-release covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Creme Brulee": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend leans against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the Irish whiskey body sits with the brulee, and the oak rounds the cream. Works; Parker's Heritage 16th handles the richness at annual-release register.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Escargot": "Tullamore D.E.W. -- Irish blend, triple-distilled, gentle. The gentle Irish body sits with the buttered escargot, and the soft malt rounds the starter. Strong; Tullamore's drier character engages the bleu at traditional register; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Faroe Island Salmon": "Tullamore D.E.W. with the salmon — traditional heritage triple-distilled Irish against oily salmon. Excellent; Tullamore's drier character frames the fish with heritage-Irish distinction.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Filet Mignon": "Tullamore D.E.W. with the filet — traditional heritage Irish against tenderloin. Excellent; Tullamore's drier triple-distilled character frames tenderloin at heritage-Irish register.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|French Onion": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend finds neutral with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the Irish whiskey body sits with the French onion, and the gentle barley note frames the bowl. Works; HH 20's aged character meets the glaze at collector register.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Grilled Caesar": "Grilled Caesar: charred romaine and anchovy meet slightly drier Irish blend. Tullamore's drier-classic character is the featured entry-Irish-Caesar pairing — where Jameson's smoothness rounds the char, Tullamore's drier character cuts it more sharply at heritage register. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Gumbo": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend finds neutral with the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the approachable Irish character carries the gumbo, and the grain register softens the bowl. Works; collector-bottle depth gives the dessert ultra-premium character.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend finds neutral with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the gentle Irish body threads the honey carrots, and the oak underlines the burnt sugar. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|House Wedge": "Tullamore D.E.W. with the House Wedge — heritage triple-distilled Irish against iceberg and bleu. Strong; Tullamore's drier character engages the bleu at traditional register.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Kansas City": "Tullamore D.E.W. with the KC — drier traditional Irish blend against an 18oz strip. Excellent; Tullamore's drier heritage handles the strip — slightly more structural than Jameson's smoother approach.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Loaded Potato": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend reads alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the smooth triple-distilled register matches the loaded potato soup, and the oak softens the cream. Works; GTS is over-specified for an app; save the collector bottle for the main course.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Lobster Mac": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the malt-grain blend handles the lobster mac, and the oak softens the cream. Works; a gentle, everyday match.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Market Fish": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; one of those is the move. Tullamore D.E.W. belongs on the steak course.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Mocha Creme": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend leans against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the approachable Irish character carries the mocha creme, and the oak frames the rich cream. Works; Sinatra Select handles the richness at Sinatra-tribute register.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Mushroom Bisque": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the gentle Irish body threads the mushroom bisque, and the oak underlines the umami weight. Works; milestone-release doesn't drive.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Mushrooms": "Tullamore D.E.W. with mushrooms — drier traditional Irish against earthy umami. Strong; Tullamore's heritage-Irish character threads mushrooms at drier register.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend reads alongside the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the gentle Irish body sits with the PB brownie, and the soft malt rounds the dessert. Works; boutique character doesn't drive.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Porterhouse": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend sits alongside the porterhouse's dual strip-and-filet character: the malt-grain blend handles the dual-cut steak, and the triple-distilled smoothness brightens the cut. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Prime Tartare": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s crisp grain-malt character finds register with the tartare's raw beef and brine — the bourbon depth cuts the umami fat, and the oak frames the umami. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Rainbow Trout": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend overwhelms the trout's delicate flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Tullamore D.E.W. lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Roast Half Chicken": "Roast Half Chicken: roasted poultry meets traditional heritage Irish blend (Daniel E. Williams), triple-distilled pot still + malt + grain, slightly drier than Jameson. Tullamore's drier heritage character frames chicken at traditional register — where Jameson brings smooth-approachable, Tullamore brings drier-classic Irish. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend sits alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the Irish whiskey body sits with the chickpea soup, and the grain register softens the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Tullamore D.E.W. for the steak course.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend reads alongside the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the Irish whiskey body sits with the garlic spinach, and the triple-distilled smoothness brightens the side. Works; bonded weight slightly over-specified.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Seafood Tower": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; the better calls are above. Reserve the Tullamore D.E.W. for the steak course.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Seared Scallops": "Tullamore D.E.W. with seared scallops — drier Irish blend against scallop delicacy. Works; Tullamore's heritage character is gentle enough for scallops but not featured.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Seasonal Soup": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend leans against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the gentle Irish body threads the seasonal soup, and the grain register softens the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Seasonal Vegetables": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend finds neutral with the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the approachable Irish character carries the seasonal vegetables, and the triple-distilled smoothness brightens the side. Works; richer profile is over-specified for this dish.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Shrimp Bisque": "Tullamore D.E.W. with shrimp bisque — drier Irish blend against cream-shrimp soup. Strong; Tullamore's drier character cuts the bisque with heritage-Irish distinction.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Shrimp Cocktail": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend fights the shrimp cocktail's cool brine-and-citrus shellfish -- the spirit register reads heavy on a starter's lighter frame. The plate deserves Bacardi Rum, Grey Goose Vodka, or Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Tullamore D.E.W. on the steak course instead.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Swordfish": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend swallows the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Tullamore D.E.W. for the steak course.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|The Tomahawk": "Tullamore D.E.W. with the Tomahawk — heritage Irish against 32oz cap-fat. Avoid; Irish whiskey is too light for this cut. Reach for a bourbon or cab.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Tomato Basil": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend reads alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the soft malt-and-grain weight wraps the tomato basil, and the gentle barley note frames the bowl. Works; the bonded richness gives the dessert more than lighter pours do.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Truffle Fries": "Tullamore D.E.W. with truffle fries — traditional heritage Irish against truffle-parmesan. Strong; Tullamore's drier heritage meets the earthy-rich at traditional register.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an Irish whiskey. Avoid; the better calls are above. Tullamore D.E.W. belongs on the steak course.",
  "Tullamore D.E.W.|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Tullamore D.E.W.'s gentle Irish blend sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the gentle Irish body threads the curry, and the soft malt rounds the bowl. Works; Boss Hog's allocation story is wasted on the salad.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|1792 Small Batch": "1792 Small Batch's caramel-spice character swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. 1792 Small Batch lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|1792 Sweet Wheat": "1792 Sweet Wheat's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. 1792 Sweet Wheat belongs on the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|1881 Napa Valley": "1881 Napa Valley's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overshadows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- dark-fruit weight crowds the seared sesame crust — needs a sparkling or crisp white for lift. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the 1881 Napa Valley for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|2 James Gin": "2 James Gin's crisp char-juniper botanicals finds register with the tuna's seared rare crust — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|A Midnight's Winter Dram": "A Midnight's Winter Dram's Highland-scotch character overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the A Midnight's Winter Dram on the steak course instead.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Aberlour 16": "Aberlour 16's double-matured Speyside balance swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Aberlour 16 for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Adictivo Cristalino": "Adictivo Cristalino's rested-agave body leans against the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the rested-agave depth sits with the tuna, and the cooked-agave note underlines the plate. Strong; modern cleanness is capable but the starter earns a more character-forward reposado.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Adictivo Reposado": "Adictivo Reposado's rested-agave body sits alongside the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the oak-aged tequila body threads the tuna, and the caramel-agave register brightens the plate. Works; distinctive-bottle over-specified.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Alexander Valley Chardonnay": "Alexander Valley Chardonnay -- Sonoma with ripe apple, pear, warm vanilla oak, smooth texture. The bright acid lifts the tuna, and the citrus cuts the plate. Strong; the side composes cleanly with the cut.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Alexander Valley Cyrus": "Alexander Valley Cyrus' red-fruit-and-spice elegance clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Alexander Valley Cyrus lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Alexander Valley Homestead Red": "Alexander Valley Homestead Red's red-fruit-and-spice elegance clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Alexander Valley Homestead Red for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Amaro Nonino": "Amaro Nonino's crisp orange-peel-grappa sweetness clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bitter aperitivo is for before or after the meal — not on a main protein. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Amaro Nonino lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Ancho Reyes": "Ancho Reyes' sweet liqueur character clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- a sweet liqueur is dessert-course energy — wrong register for any main protein. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a digestif. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the Ancho Reyes for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Angel's Envy": "Angel's Envy's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; the better calls are above. Pour the Angel's Envy on the steak course instead.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Angel's Envy Cask Strength": "Angel's Envy Cask Strength's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Angel's Envy Cask Strength belongs on the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Angel's Envy Triple Cask": "Angel's Envy Triple Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Angel's Envy Triple Cask on the steak course instead.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Aperol": "Aperol's crisp bitter-orange-aperitivo edge clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bitter botanicals fight the savory sear — bitter against char without resolution. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Aperol for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Asparagus": "The tuna and the asparagus on the plate -- the seared-rare yellowfin anchors against the vegetal asparagus side, and the mineral edge lifts the fish. Strong; the side holds the tuna's weight without competing.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Au Gratin Potatoes": "The tuna alongside the au gratin -- delicate gives way to rich, the table earns its weight. Works; the side sits without pulling focus.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon": "Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Austin Hope Cabernet Sauvignon for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Averna Amaro": "Averna Amaro's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bitter aperitivo is for before or after the meal — not on a main protein. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Averna Amaro for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Aviation": "Aviation's crisp almond-cherry build matches the tuna's seared rare crust — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; consistent recommendation worth pouring.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Aviation Gin": "Aviation Gin's floral-juniper botanicals lifts the tuna's seared rare crust — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the juniper sharpens the char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Avion 44": "Avion 44's barrel-aged tequila weight leans against the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the rested-agave depth sits with the tuna, and the vanilla-and-pepper edge frames the plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Avion Silver": "Avion Silver's crisp agave character finds register with the tuna's seared rare crust — the crisp body frames the fish cleanly, and the agave-pepper carries the char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Bacardi Rum": "Bacardi Rum's crisp workhorse-clean character sits with the tuna's seared rare crust — the crisp body frames the fish cleanly. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Baileys Irish Cream": "Baileys Irish Cream's sweet liqueur character fights the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- sweet liqueur jars against the savory sear — no bridge between dessert sugar and a seared main. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Baileys Irish Cream for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Baker's": "Baker's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Baker's belongs on the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Balvenie 12 American Oak": "Balvenie 12 American Oak's bourbon-cask Speyside softness swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Balvenie 12 American Oak lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask": "Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask's rum-finished Speyside character clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon's sweet weight crowds the rare crust's clean char. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Pour the Balvenie 14 Caribbean Cask on the steak course instead.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Balvenie 16 Single Barrel": "Balvenie 16 Single Barrel's First Fill American Oak overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Balvenie 16 Single Barrel for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Balvenie 21 Portwood": "Balvenie 21 Portwood's aged Port-finished Speyside overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Balvenie 21 Portwood belongs on the steak course.",
