  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Basil Hayden's": "Basil Hayden's light high-rye and cocoa flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Basil Hayden's lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Basil Hayden's 10 Year": "Basil Hayden's 10 Year's aged oak and rye spice swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Save the Basil Hayden's 10 Year for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Basil Hayden's Malted Rye": "Basil Hayden's Malted Rye's rye-spice character overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Basil Hayden's Malted Rye belongs on the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask": "Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Basil Hayden's Red Wine Cask belongs on the steak course.",
