  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Bee's Knees": "Bee's Knees's crisp butter-citrus build sits with the tuna's seared rare crust — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the honey rounds the grilled char. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Beefeater Gin": "Beefeater Gin's London-Dry-juniper botanicals lifts the tuna's seared rare crust — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the juniper sharpens the char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Beignets": "After the tuna, the beignets -- the seared-rare yellowfin yields to warm choux and powdered sugar, the dipping sauce closing light. Strong; the cleaner main and the lighter close share register across the courses.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Belvedere Vodka": "Belvedere Vodka -- Polish rye-based vodka, premium clean-slightly-sweet profile. The unflavored body sits with the tuna, and the crisp profile carries the plate. Strong; the silkiness sits with butter; Belvedere's pepper still cuts the dish harder.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Blade & Bow": "Blade & Bow's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Save the Blade & Bow for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Blanton's Gold": "Blanton's Gold's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Blanton's Gold for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Blanton's Original": "Blanton's Original's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Blanton's Original on the steak course instead.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Blanton's Straight from the Barrel": "Blanton's Straight from the Barrel's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Pour the Blanton's Straight from the Barrel on the steak course instead.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Blood Oath Pact 10": "Blood Oath Pact 10's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Blood Oath Pact 10 lands on the steak course — not here.",
