  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Blood Oath Pact 9": "Blood Oath Pact 9's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Hold the Blood Oath Pact 9 for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Bluecoat Gin": "Bluecoat Gin's char-citrus botanicals reads alongside the tuna's seared rare crust — the botanical lift frames the fish cleanly, and the smoke meets the char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Bodega Noemia A Lisa": "Bodega Noemia A Lisa's plush Malbec with plum-and-violet weight clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- tannin against rare-seared crust reads astringent without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Hold the Bodega Noemia A Lisa for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Bombay Dry Gin": "Bombay Dry Gin's juniper-and-citrus lift leans against the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the floral edge frames the tuna, and the juniper threads the plate. Strong; Sapphire's softness meets the bleu at accessible register.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Bombay Sapphire Gin": "Bombay Sapphire Gin's botanical-driven lift sits alongside the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the floral edge frames the tuna, and the juniper threads the plate. Strong; Bombay Dry's pine cuts the char at traditional register.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Bone Marrow": "The tuna and the bone marrow across courses -- the sesame crust anchors against the bone-enhanced richness. Strong; the opener carries its register before the main.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Booker's": "Booker's cask-strength bourbon depth swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Hold the Booker's for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Botanist Gin": "Botanist Gin's juniper-and-citrus lift leans against the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the floral edge frames the tuna, and the juniper threads the plate. Strong; Botanist's Hebridean botanicals elevate the classic cold app with oceanic-island character.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Bowdie's Old Fashioned": "Buffalo Trace Old Fashioned against rare-seared yellowfin tuna — bourbon vanilla-caramel has no hook into sesame-crust and honey-sambal brightness. Never layer. Route the cocktail to fatted steaks or marrow; take tuxedo tuna with Pinot Noir, Pinot Blanc, or Chablis.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark": "Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Bowdie's Private Select — Maker's Mark belongs on the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Bowman Brothers Small Batch": "Bowman Brothers Small Batch's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Reserve the Bowman Brothers Small Batch for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Bowmore 12": "Bowmore 12's lighter-Islay peat character clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon's sweet weight crowds the rare crust's clean char. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Pour the Bowmore 12 on the steak course instead.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Braida Montebruna Barbera": "Braida Montebruna Barbera's cherry-earth tannin stays alongside the tuna's seared rare crust — the silken tannin frames the fish, and the cassis plays against the grilled char. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon": "Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overshadows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- dark-fruit weight crowds the seared sesame crust — needs a sparkling or crisp white for lift. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Brandlin Estate Cabernet Sauvignon lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Broccoli Cheddar": "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna after the broccoli cheddar -- the cheddar-and-broccoli cream opens with rich-savory weight, the tuna following with seared-rare flesh and sesame crust the cream primed cleanly. Strong; cream cleans for the seared-rare main.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Broccolini": "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna with the broccolini -- the seared-rare flesh meets the broccolini. Strong; reliable side for the tuna.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Bruichladdich": "Bruichladdich's progressive unpeated Islay flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a scotch. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Bruichladdich for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Brussels and Belly": "The tuna alongside Brussels + Belly -- the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust meets Brussels + Belly's maple-pork-belly glaze over charred sprouts cleanly. Strong; the pairing lands at register without strain against the main.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Buffalo Trace": "Buffalo Trace's rounded vanilla-and-toffee character flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the seared crust without lifting it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Buffalo Trace on the steak course instead.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Buffalo Trace Cream": "Buffalo Trace Cream's sweet liqueur character flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- sugar dulls the crust's clean char instead of carrying it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Buffalo Trace Cream belongs on the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Bulleit Bourbon": "Bulleit Bourbon's high-rye spice-forward depth swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Reserve the Bulleit Bourbon for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Burrata": "The tuna and the burrata across courses -- the seared-rare yellowfin holds with the basil-tomato burrata. Strong; the opener carries its register before the main.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Butternut Squash": "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna after the butternut squash -- the silky sweet squash cream opens with autumnal warmth, the tuna following with seared-rare flesh and sesame crust the squash's sweetness primes cleanly. Strong; sweet cream sets up the seared-rare main.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Cade Cabernet Sauvignon": "Cade Cabernet Sauvignon's Howell Mountain Cab character overshadows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- dark-fruit weight crowds the seared sesame crust — needs a sparkling or crisp white for lift. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Cade Cabernet Sauvignon on the steak course instead.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Camarena Tequila": "Camarena Tequila's aged-agave character reads alongside the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust: the barrel-rested body handles the tuna, and the soft-spice note softens the plate. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Campari": "Campari's aperitivo at its most textbook clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bitter botanicals fight the savory sear — bitter against char without resolution. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Campari for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Canadian Club": "Canadian Club's workhorse Canadian blend swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory sear without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Canadian Club lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Canadian Club 43 Year": "Canadian Club 43 Year's Canadian whisky character clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon's sweet weight crowds the rare crust's clean char. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Canadian Club 43 Year lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Captain Morgan Rum": "Captain Morgan Rum's light-rum register with cane and citrus lift mis-pairs with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- light spirit reads thin against a main protein — needs a fuller pour. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a light spirit. Avoid; one of those is the move. Captain Morgan Rum lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Caribou Crossing": "Caribou Crossing's craft profile is wrong for scallops overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a Canadian whisky. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Caribou Crossing for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Carrot Cake": "The tuna into the carrot cake -- the seared-rare flesh and sesame crust hand off to spiced cake and cream-cheese frosting, walnut crunch on the close. Works; the cleaner main and the spiced dessert share the meal at separate registers.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Casa LBV Port": "Casa LBV Port's dessert-wine sweetness flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- sweet wine dulls the sear's clean char — savory main deserves a dry pour. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a dessert wine. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Casa LBV Port belongs on the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Casamigos Mezcal": "Casamigos Mezcal's smoky agave character overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- mezcal smoke is wrong register for the main fish course. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a mezcal. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Reserve the Casamigos Mezcal for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon": "Napa Rutherford Cab against rare-seared yellowfin tuna with sesame crust and honey sambal — concentrated cocoa-mocha body crushes the delicate fish. Never pair. Route Caymus to the steak course and take tuxedo tuna with Pinot Noir, Pinot Blanc, or Chablis.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Chambord": "Chambord's sweet liqueur character flattens the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- sugar dulls the crust's clean char instead of carrying it. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a digestif. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Chambord for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Cheesecake": "The tuna closes with the cheesecake -- the sesame-crusted yellowfin hands off to dense dairy custard, graham crust and berry compote framing the close. Works; the dairy weight outsizes the lighter main, but it lands cleanly.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Chocolate Brownie": "The tuna closes with the warm fudge brownie -- the sesame-crusted seared-rare flesh gives way to dense cocoa fudge, warm vanilla over the top. Works; the lighter ocean-clean main into the dense close, the meal builds.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Chocolate Cake": "After the tuna, the chocolate cake -- the seared-rare yellowfin yields to layered cocoa-and-ganache, the vanilla scoop closing the meal. Works; the lighter main hands off to the substantial close, the table builds toward sweetness.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Chopin Vodka": "Chopin Vodka's bold char-cream neutrality holds steady against the tuna's seared rare crust — the neutral profile frames the fish cleanly, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Christian Bros Brandy": "Christian Bros Brandy's barrel-aged cognac character fights the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- cognac's aged register pulls against the savory sear without resolving. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a cognac. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Christian Bros Brandy for the steak course.",
