  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Château Gombaude-Guillot": "Château Gombaude-Guillot's Merlot-led Bordeaux blend with plush dark-fruit clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- tannin against rare-seared crust reads astringent without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Château Gombaude-Guillot belongs on the steak course.",
