  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Clos Petit Ona Grenache": "Clos Petit Ona Grenache's spice-and-dark-fruit Rhone register clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Save the Clos Petit Ona Grenache for the steak course.",
