  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Elk Cove Five Mountain": "Elk Cove Five Mountain's silky Pinot Noir with cherry-and-forest-floor lift clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Elk Cove Five Mountain for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Elk Cove Pinot Blanc": "Willamette Pinot Blanc — delicate Oregon white, stone-fruit, crisp. The crisp acid cuts sesame-crust weight and the stone-fruit plays against honey sambal's sweet-spicy lift. Peak Pinot Blanc for tuxedo tuna — Oregon white on the crusted rare-seared classic. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
