  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Espresso Old Fashioned": "Espresso Old Fashioned's spirit-forward cocktail register clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- a whiskey-forward cocktail is built for the cut, not the fish or chicken course. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a spirit-forward cocktail. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Espresso Old Fashioned for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Evening Land Seven Springs": "Willamette Pinot — savory Eola-Amity Pinot, medium tannin, elegant delicate. The savory edge plays against tuna's rare-seared meatiness and the medium tannin handles honey sambal's sweet-spicy edge. Strong Oregon Pinot for tuxedo tuna — Evening Land elegance on the crusted classic.",
