  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Joseph Mellot Sancerre": "Loire Sancerre — refined tension-filled mineral, citrus, flint. The flinty citrus lifts tuna's lean flesh and the mineral plays against sesame-crust. Works as Sancerre for tuxedo tuna — Loire precision on the crusted classic; Pinot Noir peaks higher on the sesame-honey combo.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Jubilation by Colgin": "Jubilation by Colgin's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overshadows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- dark-fruit weight crowds the seared sesame crust — needs a sparkling or crisp white for lift. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Reserve the Jubilation by Colgin for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Jung and Wulff Guyana": "Jung and Wulff Guyana's aged-rum register with molasses and oak depth overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- heavy spirit weight buries the main protein — needs a wine or lighter spirit. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Jung and Wulff Guyana on the steak course instead.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Jung and Wulff Trinidad": "Jung and Wulff Trinidad's aged-rum register with molasses and oak depth overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- heavy spirit weight buries the main protein — needs a wine or lighter spirit. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a heavy spirit. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Jung and Wulff Trinidad lands on the steak course — not here.",
