  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Michter's US*1 Rye": "Michter's US*1 Rye's rye-spice character swallows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- the sweet-spirit register fights the savory main without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Michter's US*1 Rye for the steak course.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Mijenta Blanco": "Mijenta Blanco's crisp agave-cream character holds the line with the tuna's seared rare crust — the crisp body frames the fish cleanly, and the agave-pepper carries the char. Strong; the call lands cleanly.",
