  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut": "Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut -- blanc de blancs, grand cru Chardonnay, fine bead. The chalk-and-citrus body lifts the tuna, and the fine bead frames the plate. Strong; reliable opener for the cut.",
  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Pikesville Rye": "Pikesville Rye's rye-spice character overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pikesville Rye belongs on the steak course.",
