  "Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna|Pio Cesare Barbaresco": "Pio Cesare Barbaresco's firm-tannin tar structure buries the delicate shellfish clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- tannin against rare-seared crust reads astringent without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Pio Cesare Barbaresco on the steak course instead.",
