  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|Licor 43": "Licor 43's sweet liqueur character clashes with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth -- sweet liqueur on savory broth jars — sugar pulls one way, the salt-and-spice broth pulls the other. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Le Garenne Rosé, not a digestif. Avoid; the better calls are above. Licor 43 lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|Limoncello": "Limoncello's sweet liqueur character clashes with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth -- sweet liqueur on savory broth jars — sugar pulls one way, the salt-and-spice broth pulls the other. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Le Garenne Rosé, not a digestif. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Save the Limoncello for the steak course.",
  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir": "Willamette Pinot — dark cherry, forest floor, refined structure, low tannin. The low-tannin silk lifts the curry's coconut-milk weight and the forest-floor earth plays against chickpea depth. Peaks from the dish's side; on this wine's card it's strong — below peaks with duck, lamb, and mushroom-sauced proteins. Confident pour when a guest anchors on Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
