  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|Wheatley Vodka": "Wheatley Vodka's crisp cream neutrality plays cleanly against the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the vodka neutrality sits with the plate. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel Rye": "WhistlePig 10 Year Single Barrel Rye's rye-spice character sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the rye-pepper edge sharpens the curry, and the dry-spice register brightens the bowl. Works; the pour's toasted warmth threads through the char without overpowering.",
  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|WhistlePig 12 Year Old World": "WhistlePig 12 Year Old World's rye-spice character sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the rye spice cuts the curry, and the spice-and-vanilla thread softens the bowl. Works; extended maturation gives the dessert home-state aged character.",
  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|WhistlePig 15 Year": "WhistlePig 15 Year's rye-spice character sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the dry rye body wraps the curry, and the rye-pepper note underlines the bowl. Works; JD Bonded's backbone handles the richness at Bonded register.",
  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|WhistlePig Boss Hog IX 17 Year": "WhistlePig Boss Hog IX 17 Year's rye-spice character leans against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the rye spice cuts the curry, and the dry-spice register brightens the bowl. Works; EC 18 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|WhistlePig Boss Hog X Commandments": "WhistlePig Boss Hog X Commandments' rye-spice character sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the rye backbone drives the curry, and the rye-pepper note underlines the bowl. Works; the spicy-sweet character gives the dessert a Barton frame.",
  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year": "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year's rye-spice character finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the rye-and-oak weight handles the curry, and the rye-grain bite cuts the bowl. Works; Boss Hog's allocation story is wasted on the salad.",
  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|Willett Pot Still Reserve": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the bourbon weight handles the curry, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; the pour's refinement is underused by the salad.",
  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|Woodford Reserve": "Woodford Reserve's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the bourbon weight handles the curry, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; OGD 16 frames the two-cut plate at distinctive register.",
  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|Woodford Reserve Double Oaked": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the bourbon depth settles into the curry, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the bowl. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|Woodford Reserve Rye": "Woodford Reserve Rye's rye-spice character reads alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the high-rye spice register matches the curry, and the rye edge frames the bowl. Works; aging wasted on the salad.",
  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|Woodinville Rye": "Woodinville Rye's rye-spice character finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the high-rye spice register matches the curry, and the spice-and-vanilla thread softens the bowl. Works; milestone-collector wasted on salad.",
  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|Yamazaki 12 Year": "Yamazaki 12 Year's Suntory Japanese flagship character finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the elegant Suntory/Nikka register matches the curry, and the green-fruit edge brightens the bowl. Works; boutique-blend depth gives composed dessert character.",
  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|Yamazaki 18 Year": "Yamazaki 18 Year's aged Suntory mizunara character sits alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the elegant Suntory/Nikka register matches the curry, and the umami-tinged finish frames the bowl. Works; Vermont-brand at matched register.",
  "Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas|Yellow Chartreuse": "Yellow Chartreuse's bitter-herb aperitivo edge clashes with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth -- bitter aperitivo crowds the soup-salad course without complement. The plate deserves Schloss Vollrads Riesling, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Le Garenne Rosé, not a bitter aperitivo. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Yellow Chartreuse belongs on the steak course.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Asparagus": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis finds neutral with the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the rounded sweetness softens the green edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Kirk Venge flagship Oakville Cab — concentrated blackcurrant, dark chocolate, vanilla, seamless polished finish, soft tannin. The soft tannin cuts gruyère-cream weight and the vanilla plays against the lactic richness. Works as Oakville flagship for au gratin — Venge opulence on the cheesy side.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Beignets": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Venge Family Reserve lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Bone Marrow": "Kirk Venge flagship Oakville Cab — concentrated blackcurrant, dark chocolate, vanilla, seamless polished finish, soft tannin. The soft tannin cuts marrow's collagen fat and the dark chocolate plays against the smoky mineral depth. Peak Oakville flagship for marrow — Venge craftsman precision on the rich starter. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Bone-In Filet": "Venge Family Reserve's concentrated dark-fruit and tannin matches register with the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness: the powerful body carries the bone-enhanced filet, and the iron-mineral plays against the cut. Strong; reliable opener for the cut.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Broccoli Cheddar": "Venge Family Reserve's structured dark-fruit weight finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the structured body wraps the broccoli cheddar, and the cassis frames the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Broccolini": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis plays cleanly against the broccolini's tender green — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the rounded sweetness softens the green edge. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; reliable across the meal.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Burrata": "Oakville flagship Napa Cab against burrata's creamy-delicate center — Family Reserve's full-body blackcurrant-chocolate weight overwhelms the starter. Never pair. Route burrata to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Prosecco; keep Family Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Butternut Squash": "Venge Family Reserve's powerful blackcurrant body sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the structured body wraps the squash bisque, and the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Carrot Cake": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Hold the Venge Family Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Cheesecake": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Venge Family Reserve belongs on the steak course.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Chilean Seabass": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Save the Venge Family Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Chocolate Brownie": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth fights the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- the dry red and the chocolate's sugar refuse each other — tannin reads bitter on the finish. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Venge Family Reserve belongs on the steak course.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Chocolate Cake": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth fights the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- the dry red and the chocolate's sugar refuse each other — tannin reads bitter on the finish. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Venge Family Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Clam Chowder": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis holds with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Cowboy Ribeye": "Kirk Venge flagship Oakville Cab — concentrated blackcurrant, dark chocolate, vanilla, seamless polished finish, soft tannin, full body. The full body handles ribeye's big marbled build and the vanilla-chocolate plays against beefy char. Peak Oakville flagship for ribeye — step above Silencieux in power and presence. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Crab Cake": "Oakville flagship Napa Cab against crab cake's delicate sweet meat — Family Reserve's full-body blackcurrant-chocolate structure buries the shellfish. Never pair. Route crab cake to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Family Reserve for filet, strip, or the steak course.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Creamed Spinach": "Kirk Venge flagship Oakville Cab — concentrated blackcurrant, dark chocolate, vanilla, seamless polished finish, soft tannin. The soft tannin cuts béchamel's dairy weight and the dark chocolate plays against the spinach base. Strong Oakville flagship for creamed spinach — Venge opulence reframes the rich side.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Creamy Potato": "Venge Family Reserve's structured dark-fruit weight leans against the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the structured body wraps the potato soup, and the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; the side call holds at neutral register.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Creme Brulee": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth pulls against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- the red's dry-fruit register has no bridge to dessert tang or sugar. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not an elegant red. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Venge Family Reserve belongs on the steak course.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Escargot": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis sits with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the opulent body settles into the umami plate, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Faroe Island Salmon": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth jars against the salmon's rich oily flesh -- tannin on oily fish goes bitter, where a Pinot at the right register would carry it. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Save the Venge Family Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Filet Mignon": "Kirk Venge flagship Oakville Cab — concentrated blackcurrant, dark chocolate, vanilla, seamless polished finish, soft tannin, full body. The soft tannin meets butter-tender filet's delicate sweetness and the vanilla-chocolate plays against escargot-butter. Strong Oakville flagship for filet — Venge craftsman opulence on the delicate cut.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|French Onion": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis leans against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the cocoa deepens the fudge. Works; capable alongside. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Grilled Caesar": "Kirk Venge flagship Oakville Cab — concentrated blackcurrant, dark chocolate, vanilla, seamless polished finish, soft tannin. The soft tannin cuts anchovy-parmesan dressing and the dark chocolate plays against grilled-romaine char. Works as Oakville flagship for grilled Caesar — Venge opulence on the layered salad.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Gumbo": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis leans against the gumbo's spiced Creole stew — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis holds with the carrots' honeyed sweetness — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the cocoa deepens the fudge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|House Wedge": "Kirk Venge flagship Oakville Cab — concentrated blackcurrant, dark chocolate, vanilla, seamless polished finish, soft tannin. The soft tannin cuts iceberg-and-bacon and the dark chocolate plays against blue cheese dressing. Works as Oakville flagship for the wedge — Venge opulence reframes the classic salad; whites peak higher.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Kansas City": "Kirk Venge flagship Oakville Cab — concentrated blackcurrant, dark chocolate, vanilla, seamless polished finish, soft tannin, full body. The polished structure meets Kansas City's lean-bold marbled strip and the dark chocolate plays against beefy char. Peak Oakville flagship for the strip — Venge craftsman pedigree on the American cut. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Loaded Potato": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis stays alongside the loaded potato's richness — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the caramel softens the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Lobster Mac": "Venge Family Reserve's concentrated dark-fruit and tannin finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the structured body wraps the lobster mac, and the cassis frames the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Market Fish": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Venge Family Reserve lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Mocha Creme": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth flattens the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Venge Family Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Mushroom Bisque": "Venge Family Reserve's firm cassis-and-cocoa tannin reads alongside the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the structured body wraps the mushroom bisque, and the cassis frames the bowl. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Mushrooms": "Mushrooms: the mushroom's umami depth meets the bold red's structured tannin; dark fruit threads the truffle-and-earth without crowding. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; the pairing reads at register.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth fights the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- the dry red and the chocolate's sugar refuse each other — tannin reads bitter on the finish. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; the better calls are above. Venge Family Reserve belongs on the steak course.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Porterhouse": "Porterhouse: the Cab's oak-driven weight matches the strip's char-and-fat; firm tannin clears the rendered edge. A confident choice — steakhouse symmetry. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Prime Tartare": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis holds steady against the tartare's raw beef and brine — the Cab structure meets the savory depth, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Rainbow Trout": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the fish's natural fats. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Venge Family Reserve lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Roast Half Chicken": "Venge Family Reserve's deep dark-fruit and grippy tannin leans against the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the structured body wraps the roast chicken, and the cassis frames the plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis finds neutral with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper warmth — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the caramel rounds the earthy plate. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Venge Family Reserve lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis stays alongside the garlic-spinach's buttered greens — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Seafood Tower": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth crowds out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- the wine's weight has no business on cold shellfish — needs acid, not structure. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the Venge Family Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Seared Scallops": "Oakville flagship Napa Cab against scallop sweetness — Family Reserve's full-body structure buries the delicate shellfish. Never pair. Route scallops to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, or Rosé; keep Family Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Seasonal Soup": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis stays alongside the seasonal soup's house build — the opulent body overshoots the light soup. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Seasonal Vegetables": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis plays cleanly against the seasonal garden plate — the opulent body overshoots the light side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Shrimp Bisque": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis leans against the bisque's creamy shellfish soup — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the caramel-spice settles the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Shrimp Cocktail": "Oakville flagship Napa Cab against cold raw shrimp with horseradish — full-body Family Reserve and chilled shellfish with cocktail sauce is textbook clash. Never pair. Route shrimp cocktail to Chardonnay, Sauvignon Blanc, Rosé, or Champagne; keep Family Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Swordfish": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- tannin against rare-seared crust reads astringent without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Venge Family Reserve lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|The Tomahawk": "Kirk Venge flagship Oakville Cab — step above Silencieux, concentrated blackcurrant, dark chocolate, vanilla, seamless polished finish, soft tannin, full body. The full body meets Tomahawk's massive bone-in ribeye and the dark chocolate plays against smoky char. Peak Oakville flagship for Tomahawk — Venge craftsman pedigree on the grand cut. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Tomato Basil": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis stays alongside the tomato basil's bright acid — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Truffle Fries": "Kirk Venge flagship Oakville Cab — concentrated blackcurrant, dark chocolate, vanilla, seamless polished finish, soft tannin. The soft tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the dark chocolate plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak Oakville flagship for truffle fries — Venge craftsman opulence on the umami hit. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Venge Family Reserve's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- tannin against rare-seared crust reads astringent without a bridge. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Reserve the Venge Family Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Venge Family Reserve|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Venge Family Reserve's bold chocolate-cocoa cassis reads alongside the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the opulent body overshoots the light soup. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Asparagus": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis sits beside the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the rounded sweetness softens the green edge. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Napa Zin-led blend — Kirk Venge's Scout's Honor, blackberry, boysenberry, black pepper, vanilla, full body, generous. The vanilla plays with manchego-cream richness and the black pepper cuts gratin weight. Works for au gratin — Cabernet peaks higher on the dense dairy side.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Beignets": "Venge Scout's Honor's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift flattens the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Kahlua, Ron Zacapa Rum, or G.D. Vajra Moscato d'Asti, not an elegant red. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Pour the Venge Scout's Honor on the steak course instead.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Bone Marrow": "Napa Zin-led blend — Kirk Venge's Scout's Honor, blackberry, boysenberry, black pepper, vanilla, full body, generous finish. Black pepper cuts roasted-marrow unctuousness and full body handles beefy-bone depth. Strong Zin-led for marrow — Californian fruit wraps the rendered richness.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Bone-In Filet": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis sits with the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the concentrated body carries the strip, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Broccoli Cheddar": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cream — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the caramel-spice settles the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Broccolini": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis plays cleanly against the broccolini's tender green — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the rounded sweetness softens the green edge. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly: the Brussels and Belly's smoky, sweet pork richness over bitter-char sprouts meets this structured red's cassis-and-dark-fruit frame, firm tannin, and oak-driven weight. The bold red's dark-fruit weight locks into the side's fat and umami; tannin cleans the dairy. A strong, texturally cohesive match. Strong; consistent recommendation across the table.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Burrata": "Never pair Venge Scout's Honor with burrata — Napa Zin-led full-body fruit obliterates basil-tomato-fresh-cheese delicacy and generous alcohol flattens milky texture. Lead with Il Colle Prosecco, Paul Bara Grand Rosé, or Stoneleigh Sauvignon Blanc. Scout's Honor is a steak wine.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Butternut Squash": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis finds neutral with the squash soup's silky sweet — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the caramel-spice settles the cream. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Carrot Cake": "Venge Scout's Honor's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift flattens the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Venge Scout's Honor lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Cheesecake": "Venge Scout's Honor's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift jars against the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- tannin reads astringent next to dairy custard, the custard reads sour back. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not an elegant red. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Reserve the Venge Scout's Honor for the steak course.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Chilean Seabass": "Venge Scout's Honor's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift jars against the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- tannin on oily fish goes bitter, where a Pinot at the right register would carry it. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Pour the Venge Scout's Honor on the steak course instead.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Chocolate Brownie": "Venge Scout's Honor's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift flattens the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Reserve the Venge Scout's Honor for the steak course.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Chocolate Cake": "Venge Scout's Honor's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift flattens the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Venge Scout's Honor belongs on the steak course.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Clam Chowder": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Cowboy Ribeye": "Napa Zin-led blend — Kirk Venge's Scout's Honor, blackberry, boysenberry, black pepper, vanilla, full body, generous finish. The black pepper matches marbled-ribeye char and the ripe Zin fruit wraps around grilled-beef fat. Peak for the 26oz bone-in — bold Californian fruit handles ribeye intensity. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Crab Cake": "Never pair Venge Scout's Honor with crab cake — the Napa Zin-led blend's full body and ripe blackberry fruit bulldoze lump-crab delicacy and romesco cream. Lead with Laurent Perrier Brut, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or French 75 cocktail. Scout's Honor belongs on the red-meat course.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Creamed Spinach": "Napa Zin-led blend — Kirk Venge's Scout's Honor, blackberry, boysenberry, black pepper, vanilla, full body, generous. The vanilla plays with béchamel cream and the black pepper cuts garlic-dairy weight. Strong Zin-led for creamed spinach — full body handles the indulgent side without clashing.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Creamy Potato": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis plays cleanly against the potato soup's silky body — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the caramel softens the cream. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Creme Brulee": "Venge Scout's Honor's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift flattens the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- the structured red has nothing to bridge into a dessert finish. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not an elegant red. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Pour the Venge Scout's Honor on the steak course instead.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Escargot": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis plays cleanly against the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the opulent body settles into the umami plate, and the cassis grips the umami plate. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Faroe Island Salmon": "Never pair Venge Scout's Honor with salmon — preparation changes seasonally, check with kitchen for today's build. Full-bodied Zin-led Napa red crushes salmon fat and black-pepper weight fights delicate flesh. Lead with Lingua Franca Pinot or Domaine Serene. Scout's Honor is a steak wine.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Filet Mignon": "Napa Zin-led blend — Kirk Venge's Scout's Honor, blackberry, boysenberry, black pepper, vanilla, full body, generous. The ripe fruit and full body read heavier than lean-tender filet demands — the butter-tender cut calls for Caymus or Pinot. Works if guest is already on the Zin blend — route filet-specific pairing elsewhere.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|French Onion": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis plays cleanly against the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the vanilla amplifies the dessert sugar. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Grilled Caesar": "Napa Zin-led blend — Kirk Venge's Scout's Honor, blackberry, boysenberry, black pepper, vanilla, full body, generous. The full body reads heavy against anchovy-lemon dressing, though black pepper meets parm-char bite. Works for grilled caesar — Chablis or Sancerre fits the salad cleaner.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Gumbo": "Napa Zin-led blend — Kirk Venge's Scout's Honor, blackberry, boysenberry, black pepper, vanilla, full body, generous. The black pepper meets gumbo's Cajun spice directly and the full body handles the dark-roux weight. Strong Zin-blend for gumbo — pepper-on-spice pairing on the stew classic.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis sits beside the carrots' honeyed sweetness — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the vanilla amplifies the dessert sugar. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|House Wedge": "Napa Zin-led blend — Kirk Venge's Scout's Honor, blackberry, boysenberry, black pepper, vanilla, full body, generous finish. The full body overshadows iceberg-and-blue-cheese simplicity, though black pepper meets the dressing's bite. Works for wedge — Le Garenne Rosé or Sauv Blanc reads cleaner on the salad.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Kansas City": "Napa Zin-led blend — Kirk Venge's Scout's Honor, blackberry, boysenberry, black pepper, vanilla, full body, generous finish. The ripe Zin fruit plays with lean-bold strip beef and black pepper cuts firm-savory grain. Strong Zin-led for KC — Californian fruit-forward weight handles the well-marbled cut.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Loaded Potato": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis plays cleanly against the loaded potato's richness — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the caramel-spice settles the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Lobster Mac": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis sits beside the lobster mac's shellfish cream — the concentrated body settles into the rich side, and the caramel-spice settles the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Market Fish": "Venge Scout's Honor's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- the red's structure is wrong for delicate flesh — built for red meat. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not an elegant red. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Pour the Venge Scout's Honor on the steak course instead.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Mocha Creme": "Venge Scout's Honor's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift jars against the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness -- savory tannin meets dessert sugar with no bridge between them. The plate deserves Kahlua, Patron XO Cafe, or Frangelico, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Venge Scout's Honor lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Mushroom Bisque": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis reads alongside the mushroom bisque's earthy cream — the concentrated body matches the heavy soup, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Mushrooms": "Napa Zin-led blend — Kirk Venge's Scout's Honor, blackberry, boysenberry, black pepper, vanilla, full body, generous finish. Vanilla plays with garlic-butter glaze and black pepper lifts umami earthiness. Works for mushroom side — Zin-led fruit bridges funky richness; Scavino or Caymus fits harder.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Venge Scout's Honor's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift clashes with the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge -- savory tannin sits awkwardly on cocoa weight without resolving. The plate deserves Frangelico, Disaronno, or Graham's 20 Year Tawny, not an elegant red. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Venge Scout's Honor belongs on the steak course.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Porterhouse": "Napa Zin-led blend — Kirk Venge's Scout's Honor, blackberry, boysenberry, black pepper, vanilla, full body, generous finish. Black pepper plays with dual-texture strip-and-tender and ripe fruit handles the mixed profile. Strong Zin-led for Porterhouse — fruit-forward weight bridges both cuts.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Prime Tartare": "Venge Scout's Honor's powerful blackcurrant body leans against the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami: the structured body wraps the tartare, and the cassis frames the starter. Strong; the pairing lands at register without strain.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Rainbow Trout": "Venge Scout's Honor's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift clashes with the trout's delicate flesh -- tannin reads metallic against the delicate fish — a crisp white cleans where red sits heavy. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Hold the Venge Scout's Honor for the steak course.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Roast Half Chicken": "Venge Scout's Honor's deep dark-fruit and grippy tannin reads alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the structured body wraps the roast chicken, and the cassis frames the plate. Works; the opener sits without competing.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis holds with the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper warmth — the opulent body overshoots the light soup, and the pepper amplifies the spice. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Venge Scout's Honor's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- the red's structure is wrong for delicate flesh — built for red meat. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Venge Scout's Honor lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis sits alongside the garlic-spinach's buttered greens — the opulent body overshoots the light side, and the oak frames the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Seafood Tower": "Venge Scout's Honor's jammy Zinfandel with bramble-and-pepper lift overwhelms the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- tannin obliterates the delicate shellfish flavor — a crisp white or sparkling carries it cleanly. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not an elegant red. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Pour the Venge Scout's Honor on the steak course instead.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Seared Scallops": "Never pair Venge Scout's Honor with seared scallops — full-bodied Zin-led jammy blend crushes clean-seared shellfish and the black pepper fights scallop sweetness. Lead with Raventós Cava, Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé. Route the Scout's Honor to ribeye.",
  "Venge Scout's Honor|Seasonal Soup": "Venge Scout's Honor's bold pepper-vanilla cassis plays cleanly against the seasonal soup's house build — the opulent body overshoots the light soup. Works; the call holds at register.",
