  "Venge Silencieux|Swordfish": "Venge Silencieux's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- tannin against rare-seared crust reads astringent without a bridge. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not an elegant red. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Save the Venge Silencieux for the steak course.",
  "Venge Silencieux|The Tomahawk": "Kirk Venge single-vineyard Napa — dark cherry, cassis, chocolate, floral violet, silky soft tannin, full body. The full body meets Tomahawk's massive bone-in ribeye though silky soft tannin reads rounder than firm-tannin Cabs on the grand cut. Strong winemaker's Napa Cab for Tomahawk — Venge refinement on the grand scale.",
  "Venge Silencieux|Tomato Basil": "Venge Silencieux's structured dark-fruit weight sits alongside the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the structured body wraps the tomato basil, and the medium-body red meets the light soup. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Venge Silencieux|Truffle Fries": "Kirk Venge single-vineyard Napa — dark cherry, cassis, chocolate, floral violet, silky soft tannin. The silky tannin cuts truffle-fry potato fat and the chocolate-violet plays against the truffle-oil umami. Peak winemaker's Napa Cab for truffle fries — Venge precision on the umami hit. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Venge Silencieux|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Venge Silencieux's structured Cabernet with cassis-and-cedar depth overshadows the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- dark-fruit weight crowds the seared sesame crust — needs a sparkling or crisp white for lift. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not an elegant red. Avoid; one of those is the move. Venge Silencieux lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Venge Silencieux|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Venge Silencieux's concentrated dark-fruit and tannin leans against the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the structured body wraps the curry, and the cassis frames the bowl. Works; the dessert sits cleanly against the meal's register.",
  "Vesper|Asparagus": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build reads alongside the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the cocktail lift sits with the light side, and the botanicals echo the green plate. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Vesper|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build sits beside the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the cocktail lift cleans the rich side, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Vesper|Beignets": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build sits alongside the beignet's warm sugar-dusted pastry — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Vesper|Bone Marrow": "Nolet's, Ketel One, Lillet. The martini's clean dryness has no structural match for marrow's rendered-fat richness — Lillet's citrus can't cut that deep. Never pair — keep the Vesper for raw bar and starters, route marrow to whiskey cocktails.",
  "Vesper|Bone-In Filet": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build sits alongside the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the cocktail is outweighed by the cut, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Vesper|Broccoli Cheddar": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build plays cleanly against the broccoli cheddar's cream — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
