  "Vesper|Cheesecake": "Vesper's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift reads alongside the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard: the bright build frames the cheesecake, and the citrus cuts the dessert. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Vesper|Chilean Seabass": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build finds register with the seabass's buttery flesh — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Vesper|Chocolate Brownie": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build finds neutral with the brownie's warm cocoa depth — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; a safe alongside, no friction.",
  "Vesper|Chocolate Cake": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build sits alongside the cake's layered chocolate — the cocktail acidity underclubs the dessert, and the citrus brightens the cream. Works; safe call, no friction. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Vesper|Clam Chowder": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build sits beside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Vesper|Cowboy Ribeye": "Vesper's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift underclubs the cowboy ribeye's marbled char-and-fat richness -- a light citrus cocktail can't carry the marbled char — needs whiskey or red wine weight. The plate deserves Macallan 18, Caymus Cabernet Sauvignon, or Silver Oak Cabernet Sauvignon, not a light cocktail. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Hold the Vesper for another course.",
  "Vesper|Crab Cake": "Nolet's, Ketel One, Lillet — stirred. The Lillet's slight citrus bitterness lifts crab's romesco and Nolet's rose-peach profile adds aromatic depth against the delicate meat. Peak martini pairing for crab cake — elegance meets elegance.",
  "Vesper|Creamed Spinach": "Vesper's citrus-and-bright cocktail lift reads alongside the creamed spinach's rich bechamel-laced greens: the bright build frames the creamed spinach, and the citrus cuts the side. Works; the call holds at register.",
