  "Vesper|Escargot": "Nolet's, Ketel One, Lillet. The martini's cool dryness cuts garlic-butter escargot cleanly and Lillet adds citrus brightness against the snails' earthy profile. Strong opener cocktail — classical elegance on both sides of the pairing.",
  "Vesper|Faroe Island Salmon": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build holds steady against the salmon's rich oily flesh — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Vesper|Filet Mignon": "Nolet's, Ketel One, Lillet — equal parts, stirred. The martini's elegance is wrong for any steak — clean cocktail structure has no hook into grilled beef. Works if guest stays on the martini; route filet pairing to Cab, Pinot, or Manhattan.",
  "Vesper|French Onion": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build sits beside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the cocktail lift refreshes against the hearty soup, and the botanicals cut the cheese richness. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Vesper|Grilled Caesar": "Nolet's gin, Ketel One vodka, Lillet. The martini's clean dryness cuts anchovy-parmesan dressing and Lillet's citrus plays against grilled-romaine char. Works as unconventional pairing — cocktail handles salad's layered profile without overwhelming.",
