  "Vesper|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build reads alongside the halibut's salt-cured flesh — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; the call lands cleanly.",
  "Vesper|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build reads alongside the garlic-spinach's buttered greens — the cocktail lift sits with the light side, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Vesper|Seafood Tower": "Nolet's gin, Ketel One vodka, Lillet — stirred cold. The classic martini structure with Nolet's softer botanical profile handles the full raw-bar spread; Lillet's citrus cleans each bite. Peak martini pairing for the tower's chilled-shellfish showcase.",
  "Vesper|Seared Scallops": "Nolet's gin, Ketel One, Lillet — equal parts, stirred cold. Nolet's rose-and-peach softness meets scallops' clean-seared sweetness directly; Lillet's citrus-bitter edge cuts without crushing. Peak martini pairing for the cleanest seafood on the menu.",
  "Vesper|Seasonal Soup": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build leans against the seasonal soup's house build — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup. Works; the pairing reads neutral at the table. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Vesper|Seasonal Vegetables": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build stays alongside the seasonal garden plate — the cocktail lift sits with the light side. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Vesper|Shrimp Bisque": "Nolet's gin, Ketel One vodka, Lillet. The cocktail's clean-structured profile meets cream-shellfish soup without fighting; Lillet's citrus-bitter cuts the cream weight. Strong martini alternative when guest wants cocktail rather than white wine with bisque.",
  "Vesper|Shrimp Cocktail": "Nolet's, Ketel One, Lillet. The vodka-gin split with Lillet's citrus-bitter handles chilled shrimp's clean sweetness and the cocktail sauce's horseradish bite. Peak martini pairing — Bond-classic cocktail with a classic shellfish opener. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Vesper|Swordfish": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build reads alongside the swordfish's meaty flesh — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Vesper|The Tomahawk": "Elegant martini against the biggest steak on the menu — complete structural mismatch. The Vesper's clean-dry profile is obliterated by marbled Tomahawk weight. Never pair — route Tomahawk to Cab, Barolo, or spirit-forward whiskey cocktails.",
  "Vesper|Tomato Basil": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build holds with the tomato basil's bright acid — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus lifts the herbs. Works; the call holds at register.",
