  "Vesper|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build reads alongside the tuna's seared rare crust — the cocktail lift frames the fish cleanly, and the citrus sharpens the briny edge. Strong; a confident match across the table.",
  "Vesper|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Vesper's crisp citrus-juniper build sits beside the curry's spiced chickpea warmth — the cocktail lift sits with the light soup, and the citrus brightens the spice. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Asparagus": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's biscuit-apple acidity stays alongside the asparagus's green-vegetal edge — the lively bubbles sit with the light side, and the mineral edge frames the green plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's biscuit-apple acidity leans against the gratin's cheese-and-cream — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the apple notes lift the custard. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Beignets": "Veuve Clicquot Brut — yellow label Champagne. Ripe apple, white peach, biscuit, creamy mousse, lively acidity. The biscuit complements beignets' fried-dough pastry directly and the peach plays against berry jam. Strong celebration Champagne for beignets — everyone's favorite meets dessert course.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Bone Marrow": "Yellow label Veuve against marrow's rendered-fat richness — even the iconic Reims Champagne is overwhelmed by bone depth. Never pair. Route marrow to big Cab, Manhattan, or Bowdie's Old Fashioned; keep Veuve for tartare, seafood tower, or the celebration toast.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Bone-In Filet": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's classic yellow-label Champagne body underclubs the bone-in filet's bone-enhanced buttery tenderness -- sparkling sits short of the prime cut's weight. The plate deserves Opus One, Jordan Cabernet Sauvignon, or Knob Creek 15 Year, not a sparkling. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Hold the Veuve Clicquot Brut for another course.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Broccoli Cheddar": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's biscuit-apple acidity stays alongside the broccoli cheddar's cream — the mousse refreshes against the broth, and the apple notes lift the custard. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Broccolini": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's biscuit-apple acidity sits alongside the broccolini's tender green — the lively bubbles sit with the light side, and the mineral edge frames the green plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Brussels and Belly": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's biscuit-apple acidity stays alongside the maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the mineral edge frames the green plate. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Burrata": "Yellow label Veuve Clicquot — Reims Champagne, ripe apple, white peach, biscuit, creamy mousse. The creamy body cuts burrata's cream and the biscuit plays against basil-tomato; lively acidity lifts the cheese. Peak crowd-pleaser Champagne for burrata — celebration meets classic starter. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Butternut Squash": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's biscuit-apple acidity stays alongside the squash soup's silky sweet — the mousse refreshes against the broth, and the apple notes lift the custard. Works; the pairing reads neutral at the table. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Carrot Cake": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's classic yellow-label Champagne body clashes with the carrot cake's cream-cheese-frosted spice cake -- a dry sparkling belongs with the opener, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Vin Santo, Disaronno, or Graham's 10 Year Tawny, not a sparkling. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Veuve Clicquot Brut belongs on the steak course.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Cheesecake": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's classic yellow-label Champagne body clashes with the cheesecake's dense tangy dairy custard -- a dry sparkling belongs with the opener, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Disaronno, not a sparkling. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Veuve Clicquot Brut lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Chilean Seabass": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's biscuit-apple acidity holds the line with the seabass's buttery flesh — the bright acidity frames the fish without weight, and the brioche notes meet the herb butter. Strong; the call holds at register without strain.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Chocolate Brownie": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's classic yellow-label Champagne body clashes with the brownie's fudgy cocoa-and-chocolate weight -- a dry sparkling belongs with the opener, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Louis XIII Cognac, not a sparkling. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Veuve Clicquot Brut belongs on the steak course.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Chocolate Cake": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's classic yellow-label Champagne body clashes with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body -- brut bubbles and chocolate weight refuse each other — needs sweetness, not crisp acid. The plate deserves Taylor Fladgate Vintage Bottle, Graham's 2017 Vintage Port, or Baileys Irish Cream, not a sparkling. Avoid; redirect the order — the alternatives carry it. Veuve Clicquot Brut lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Clam Chowder": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's biscuit-apple acidity reads alongside the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato — the mousse refreshes against the broth, and the apple notes lift the custard. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Cowboy Ribeye": "Veuve Clicquot Brut against the Cowboy's marbled bone-in ribeye — iconic yellow label crumples under rendered fat. Never pair. Route Cowboy to Silver Oak, Caymus, or bold bourbon; keep Veuve for starters, seafood tower, or celebration pours before the steak course.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Crab Cake": "Veuve Clicquot Brut — iconic yellow label, Reims Champagne. Ripe apple, white peach, biscuit, creamy mousse, lively acidity. The creamy body cuts romesco and the biscuit complements crab's pan-fry. Peak reliable Champagne for crab cake — crowd-pleaser meets classic starter beautifully. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Creamed Spinach": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's biscuit-apple acidity stays alongside the spinach's dairy-rich cream — the lively bubbles sit with the light side, and the apple notes lift the custard. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Creamy Potato": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's biscuit-apple acidity sits beside the potato soup's silky body — the mousse refreshes against the broth, and the apple notes lift the custard. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Creme Brulee": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's classic yellow-label Champagne body clashes with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard -- a dry sparkling belongs with the opener, not the dessert close. The plate deserves Sauternes Glass, Vin Santo, or Ron Zacapa Rum, not a sparkling. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Hold the Veuve Clicquot Brut for the steak course.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Escargot": "Yellow label Veuve — iconic Reims Champagne with ripe apple, white peach, biscuit, creamy mousse. The biscuit echoes escargot's buttered-bread French tradition directly and the creamy body cuts garlic-parsley. Strong recognizable Champagne for escargot — everyone's favorite meets the French classic.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Faroe Island Salmon": "Yellow label Veuve — Reims Champagne with apple, peach, biscuit, creamy mousse. The body cuts salmon's oil-rich flesh; preparation changes seasonally — check with kitchen for today's build. Works as iconic Champagne for salmon course across most seasonal builds — crowd-pleasing default.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Filet Mignon": "Veuve Clicquot Brut — yellow label Champagne, Pinot Noir-dominant. Ripe apple, white peach, biscuit, creamy mousse, lively acidity. The body handles butter-tender filet's lean sweetness unconventionally; biscuit echoes escargot-butter toppers. Strong Champagne-with-steak when guest wants iconic bubbles alongside filet.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|French Onion": "Veuve Clicquot Brut's biscuit-apple acidity sits alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere — the mousse-and-acid sits with the plate, and the mineral edge cuts the cheese richness. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Veuve Clicquot Brut|Grilled Caesar": "Yellow label Veuve — Reims Pinot Noir-dominant Champagne. Ripe apple, white peach, biscuit, creamy mousse. The lively acidity cuts anchovy-parmesan and the biscuit plays against grilled-romaine char. Strong iconic Champagne for the Caesar — recognizable crowd-pleaser elevates the salad.",
