  "WhistlePig 12 Year Old World|Creme Brulee": "WhistlePig 12 Year Old World's rye-spice character finds neutral with the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the rye backbone drives the brulee, and the oak softens the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "WhistlePig 12 Year Old World|Escargot": "WhistlePig 12 Year Old World's rye-spice character leans against the escargot's garlic-herb-butter savory weight: the high-rye spice register matches the buttered escargot, and the caramel rounds the herb butter. Strong; Vermont-brand rye sits with richness; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "WhistlePig 12 Year Old World|Faroe Island Salmon": "WhistlePig 12 Year Old World's rye-spice character overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon weight needs red meat, not the salmon's already-rich oils. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Save the WhistlePig 12 Year Old World for the steak course.",
  "WhistlePig 12 Year Old World|Filet Mignon": "WhistlePig 12 Year Old World with the filet — fruit-cask-finished 12-year against the 10oz cut. Strong; Old World fruit character gives the filet layered complexity but WP 15 Year's extended maturation earns excellent here.",
