  "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year|Swordfish": "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year's rye-spice character clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon's sweet weight crowds the rare crust's clean char. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Hold the WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year for the steak course.",
  "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year|The Tomahawk": "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year's rye-spice character leans against the Tomahawk's theatrical bone-in marbling and smoky char: the high-rye spice register matches the 36oz showpiece, and the rye-grain bite cuts the cut. Strong; OGD 16's aged rye-spice meets the earthy-rich at distinctive register.",
  "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year|Tomato Basil": "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year's rye-spice character leans against the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the rye-and-oak weight handles the tomato basil, and the dry-spice register brightens the bowl. Works; bonded weight a touch ambitious for the dessert.",
  "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year|Truffle Fries": "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year with truffle fries — accessible WP 100-proof against truffle-parmesan. The Canadian-sourced character cuts the richness with Vermont-brand distinctiveness. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year's rye-spice character clashes with the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon's sweet weight crowds the rare crust's clean char. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a rye whiskey. Avoid; recommend one of the alternatives. Pour the WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year on the steak course instead.",
  "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "WhistlePig PiggyBack 6 Year's rye-spice character finds neutral with the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the rye-and-oak weight handles the curry, and the rye-grain bite cuts the bowl. Works; Boss Hog's allocation story is wasted on the salad.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Asparagus": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the bourbon backbone carries the asparagus, and the caramel rounds the side. Works; BIB structure overshoots the dessert's delicacy.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with au gratin potatoes — craft 94-proof against cheese-and-cream. Strong; oak spice gives the side a distinctive frame.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Beignets": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon weight handles the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for a soup — save the collector bottle for the main course.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Bone Marrow": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with bone marrow — craft high-rye oak spice against umami fat. The pot-still character gives the marrow a distinctive frame; a conversation-starter pairing. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Bone-In Filet": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's crisp caramel-spice character frames the bone-in filet's marrow-edged tenderness — the bourbon weight grips the lean cut, and the vanilla softens the grilled char. Strong; the call lands cleanly.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Broccoli Cheddar": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the oak depth lays under the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Broccolini": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's soft-oak bourbon body sits alongside the broccolini's tender green stalks: the bourbon depth settles into the broccolini, and the oak frames the side. Works; the distinctive character is underused by the salad's simplicity.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Brussels and Belly": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with Brussels + Belly — craft 94-proof high-rye meets maple-glazed pork belly. The oak spice and rye character cut the glaze's sweetness in a way Heaven Hill BIB's straight oak can't. Excellent; the call holds at full register.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Burrata": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with burrata — fresh dairy against craft high-rye. Avoid; lead with the alts on the menu.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Butternut Squash": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the oak depth lays under the squash bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; wine-cask over-specified.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Carrot Cake": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with carrot cake — craft high-rye spice against cream cheese and cinnamon. Strong; oak spice and cake spice find each other in a distinctive way.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Cheesecake": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with cheesecake — craft high-rye against custard. Works; the oak spice is slightly over-specified for the dessert.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Chilean Seabass": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's craft high-rye oak spice clashes with the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- the oily flesh and the brown-spirit oak refuse to meet cleanly. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour. Reserve the Willett Pot Still Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Chocolate Brownie": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with the chocolate brownie — craft high-rye against cocoa. Works; for cocoa interplay, Weller 107 or Basil Hayden's Toast.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Chocolate Cake": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the caramel-spice register matches the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the 10-year depth gives the dessert substantial premium frame.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Clam Chowder": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon weight handles the chowder, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; Kentucky Owl is over-specified for a soup — save the collector bottle for the main course.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Cowboy Ribeye": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with the Cowboy Ribeye — craft high-rye against cap fat and char. The 94-proof handles the ribeye; distinct from Knob Creek's bigger-distillery 100-proof take — more craft, more oak spice. Excellent; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Crab Cake": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with crab cake — craft high-rye against delicate crab. Avoid; pour a crisp white wine.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Creamed Spinach": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with creamed spinach — craft high-rye against dairy richness. Strong; the oak spice distinct from wheated caramel takes.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Creamy Potato": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's soft-oak bourbon body reads alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the bourbon depth settles into the potato soup, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; polished aged character doesn't drive.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Creme Brulee": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the brulee's burnt-sugar custard: the bourbon weight handles the brulee, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the match reads neutral at the table.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Escargot": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's crisp caramel-spice character frames the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the whiskey weight reads cleanly against the umami plate, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; the call lands cleanly.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Faroe Island Salmon": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's craft high-rye oak spice smothers the salmon's rich oily flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; offer the alts at the table — they fit. Willett Pot Still Reserve lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Filet Mignon": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with the filet — Willett's signature craft pour, distinctive pot-still-shaped bottle. 94-proof high-rye with caramel, vanilla, and oak spice. Distinct from the Beam-side high-ryes (Knob Creek, Bulleit) — more craft-small-batch character. A distinctive filet pour with bottle theatrics tableside. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|French Onion": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the brown-spirit warmth threads the French onion, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; boutique-craft doesn't drive.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Grilled Caesar": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with the grilled Caesar — craft oak-spice against charred romaine. Strong; the distinctive character earns the Caesar in a way the everyday bourbons don't.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Gumbo": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the caramel-spice register matches the gumbo, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; the oak spice is over-specified for this dish.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's rounded-oak bourbon character reads alongside the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the honey carrots, and the oak balances the burnt-sugar edge. Works; single-barrel depth gives the dessert more than Small Batch.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|House Wedge": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with the House Wedge — iceberg and bleu against craft high-rye. Works; the distinctive character is underused by the salad's simplicity.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Kansas City": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with the KC — craft high-rye against the strip's marbling. The 94-proof oak spice gives the strip a different dimension than the bigger-distillery bourbons; a signature-character strip pour. Excellent; servers pour without second-guessing.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Loaded Potato": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the oak depth lays under the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; reliable companion, low risk.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Lobster Mac": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone finds neutral with the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the caramel-spice register matches the lobster mac, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; Caribbean Cask handles the richness at distinctive register.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Market Fish": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's craft high-rye oak spice flattens the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- oak-and-vanilla density rolls over the gentle flesh without lifting it. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Pour the Willett Pot Still Reserve on the steak course instead.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Mocha Creme": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's rounded-oak bourbon character finds neutral with the mocha creme's coffee-chocolate richness: the bourbon depth settles into the mocha creme, and the vanilla underlines the rich cream. Works; HH 20 frames the two-cut plate at collector register.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Mushroom Bisque": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the mushroom bisque's silky earthy mushroom cream: the brown-spirit warmth threads the mushroom bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; the 10-year holds without lifting.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Mushrooms": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with the mushrooms — craft high-rye against earthy umami. The oak spice layers into mushroom depth distinctively. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Peanut Butter Brownie": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone sits alongside the PB brownie's peanut-butter-and-chocolate fudge: the bourbon weight handles the PB brownie, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; composed but not a standout.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Porterhouse": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with the porterhouse — craft high-rye across strip and filet. Strong; the oak spice covers both cuts with distinctive character.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Prime Tartare": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's spice-and-caramel bourbon depth sits alongside the tartare's raw beef-and-brine umami: the caramel-spice register matches the tartare, and the oak balances the umami register. Strong; the polished aged character is a refined premium counterpoint distinct from WP's Vermont-finished approach; Fernet Branca still cuts it harder.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Rainbow Trout": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's craft high-rye oak spice smothers the trout's delicate flesh -- the brown-spirit weight pulls focus off the delicate fish protein. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Domaine de Berthiers Pouilly-Fumé, not a bourbon. Avoid; the listed alts pair where this does not. Save the Willett Pot Still Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Roast Half Chicken": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the chicken's herbed crisp-skin roast: the brown-spirit warmth threads the roast chicken, and the oak-and-spice register settles the plate. Works; the pairing holds without overshooting.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Roasted Red Pepper Chickpea": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone reads alongside the chickpea soup's roasted-pepper chickpea warmth: the brown-spirit warmth threads the chickpea soup, and the caramel rounds the bowl. Works; AE meets the char at wine-finish register.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Salt-Cured Halibut": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's craft high-rye oak spice overwhelms the halibut's salt-cured flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, St Supéry Sauvignon Blanc, or Far Niente Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Willett Pot Still Reserve belongs on the steak course.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Sauteed Garlic Spinach": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's rounded-oak bourbon character leans against the garlic spinach's garlic-buttered greens: the bourbon backbone carries the garlic spinach, and the caramel rounds the side. Works; bonded weight pushes past the soup's register slightly.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Seafood Tower": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's craft high-rye oak spice drowns out the seafood tower's chilled shellfish lineup -- sweet-oak depth flattens the briny opener instead of lifting it. The plate deserves Laurent Perrier Le Cuvée Brut, Veuve Clicquot Brut, or Pierre Gimonnet Special Club Brut, not a bourbon. Avoid; reach for any of those instead. Willett Pot Still Reserve lands on the steak course — not here.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Seared Scallops": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with seared scallops — scallop delicacy against craft high-rye. Avoid; recommend something else for this dish.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Seasonal Soup": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the seasonal soup's house seasonal build: the bourbon weight handles the seasonal soup, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; no driver pairing.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Seasonal Vegetables": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's craft high-rye oak spice leans against the seasonal vegetables' seasonal garden plate: the bourbon depth settles into the seasonal vegetables, and the vanilla softens the side. Works; rye's brightness is a gentle counterpoint.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Shrimp Bisque": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with shrimp bisque — cream-based seafood against craft high-rye. Works; oak spice sits beside the soup without driving.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Shrimp Cocktail": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with shrimp cocktail — cold shrimp against craft bourbon. Avoid; route the table to a better-fit pour.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Swordfish": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's craft high-rye oak spice clashes with the swordfish's meaty swordfish steak -- bourbon's sweet weight crowds the rare crust's clean char. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Schloss Vollrads Riesling, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; pick from the alternatives. Reserve the Willett Pot Still Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|The Tomahawk": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's grain-and-oak bourbon register rests at register with the Tomahawk's theatrical bone-in marbling and smoky char: the bourbon backbone carries the 36oz showpiece, and the vanilla underlines the rendered char. Strong; multi-distillery complexity sits with richness at craft-blender register.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Tomato Basil": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the tomato basil's bright tomato-basil acid: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the tomato basil, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; premium proof overpowers this dish.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Truffle Fries": "Willett Pot Still Reserve with truffle fries — high-rye oak spice against truffle-parmesan. The craft character gives the side more vocabulary than the everyday bourbons bring; a sophisticated side pairing. Excellent; the pairing carries cleanly.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Tuxedo-Crusted Yellowfin Tuna": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's craft high-rye oak spice overwhelms the tuna's seared-rare flesh with sesame crust -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Pommery Cuvée Louise, Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, or Elk Cove Pinot Blanc, not a bourbon. Avoid; steer the table to the alternatives. Save the Willett Pot Still Reserve for the steak course.",
  "Willett Pot Still Reserve|Vegetable Curry with Chickpeas": "Willett Pot Still Reserve's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the curry's spiced chickpea-curry warmth: the bourbon weight handles the curry, and the oak-and-spice register settles the bowl. Works; the pour's refinement is underused by the salad.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Asparagus": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth sits alongside the asparagus' green-vegetal edge: the caramel-spice register matches the asparagus, and the toffee-vanilla edge underlines the side. Works; capable alongside without driving the table.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Au Gratin Potatoes": "Au Gratin Potatoes: cheese-and-cream potatoes meet iconic Double-Oaked. Works; Woodford Double Oaked handles the richness at KY-benchmark register.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Beignets": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the beignets' warm sugar-dusted pastry: the bourbon body sits with the beignets, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; the smooth character gives the dessert a composed frame.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Bone Marrow": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked with bone marrow — iconic Double-Oaked benchmark against umami fat. Strong; Woodford Double Oaked's second-char character engages marrow at iconic-benchmark register.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Bone-In Filet": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked with the bone-in filet — Brown-Forman Double Oaked against tenderloin-with-bone. Works; Woodford Double Oaked frames the cut at KY-benchmark register.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Broccoli Cheddar": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the broccoli cheddar's cheddar-and-broccoli cream: the bourbon backbone carries the broccoli cheddar, and the vanilla rounds the cream. Works; the bourbon-and-soup pairing sits without pulling focus.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Broccolini": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the broccolini's tender green stalks: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the broccolini, and the rounded sweetness brightens the side. Works; own-plus-sourced covers both cuts without standing out.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Brussels and Belly": "Brussels and Belly: maple-glazed Brussels and pork belly meet Brown-Forman Double Oaked. Works; Woodford Double Oaked's intensified-caramel meets the glaze at KY-benchmark register.",
