  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Butternut Squash": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the butternut squash's silky sweet squash cream: the bourbon weight handles the squash bisque, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; not revelatory but well-matched registers.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Carrot Cake": "Carrot Cake: cream cheese and cinnamon meet Brown-Forman Double Oaked. Strong; Woodford Double Oaked's intensified-caramel threads the cake at KY-benchmark register.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Cheesecake": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked with cheesecake — Brown-Forman KY Double Oaked against custard. Works; Woodford Double Oaked's intensified caramel-vanilla threads the cheesecake at KY-benchmark register.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Chilean Seabass": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth smothers the seabass' buttery seabass flesh -- sweet-spirit register doubles the natural fish-richness — no contrast. The plate deserves Far Niente Chardonnay, Pommery Cuvée Louise, or Keenan Chardonnay, not a bourbon. Avoid; lead with the alternatives instead. Hold the Woodford Reserve Double Oaked for the steak course.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Chocolate Brownie": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked with the chocolate brownie — Brown-Forman KY bourbon with toasted-then-charred second barrel, iconic Double-Oaked benchmark. Excellent; Woodford Double Oaked's iconic benchmark intensified-caramel is the featured Double-Oaked-chocolate pairing — the most recognizable Double-Oaked on the menu delivering the textbook bourbon-and-chocolate pairing.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Chocolate Cake": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight reads alongside the chocolate cake's layered chocolate body: the bourbon backbone carries the chocolate cake, and the spice threads the dessert. Works; complex profile overshoots the dessert's delicacy.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Clam Chowder": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's warm-vanilla bourbon backbone leans against the chowder's creamy clam-and-potato base: the bourbon depth settles into the chowder, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; CC 43 Year is over-specified for a side; save the rare bottle for the main.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Cowboy Ribeye": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked with the cowboy ribeye — Brown-Forman Double Oaked against 26oz bone-in cap-fat. Strong; Woodford Double Oaked's intensified character frames the ribeye at KY-benchmark register.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Crab Cake": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked with crab cake — iconic Double-Oaked against delicate lump crab. Avoid; bourbon wrong for seafood. Reach for a vodka or gin.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Creamed Spinach": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked with creamed spinach — iconic Double-Oaked against dairy-rich side. Strong; Woodford Double Oaked's caramel-oak rides the cream at KY-benchmark register.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Creamy Potato": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's grain-and-oak bourbon register sits alongside the potato soup's silky-bodied cream: the oak-and-vanilla weight wraps the potato soup, and the vanilla brightens the cream. Works; the pairing is pleasant but not a standout.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Creme Brulee": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked with creme brulee — iconic Double-Oaked against vanilla custard and caramelized sugar. Excellent; Woodford Double Oaked's toasted-then-charred second-barrel caramel is the featured Double-Oaked-brulee pairing — the most recognizable Double-Oaked delivering the textbook bourbon-brulee match.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Escargot": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's bold caramel-char character finds register with the escargot's garlic-herb butter — the aged-oak depth meets the rich starter, and the caramel rounds the umami plate. Strong; reliable headline pairing.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Faroe Island Salmon": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the salmon's rich oily flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not a flaky main. The plate deserves Cristom Mt Jefferson Cuvée, Lingua Franca Avni Pinot Noir, or Elk Cove Five Mountain, not a bourbon. Avoid; the alts above are the call. Woodford Reserve Double Oaked belongs on the steak course.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Filet Mignon": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked with the filet — Brown-Forman KY Double Oaked against tenderloin. Excellent; Woodford Double Oaked's iconic intensified character frames tenderloin with KY-benchmark distinction.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|French Onion": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight finds neutral with the French onion's beef-broth-and-gruyere depth: the oak depth lays under the French onion, and the oak frames the bowl. Works; the call holds at register.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Grilled Caesar": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's caramel-and-spice bourbon weight sits alongside the Caesar's charred-romaine and anchovy edge: the bourbon weight handles the grilled Caesar, and the vanilla underlines the rendered char. Works; the private select's layered profile underserves the dessert's simplicity.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Gumbo": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's grain-and-oak bourbon register reads alongside the gumbo's spiced creole stew: the bourbon depth settles into the gumbo, and the vanilla softens the bowl. Works; OGD 16 is over-specified for an app; save for the main.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Honey Roasted Carrots": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth finds neutral with the honey carrots' honey-glazed carrot sweetness: the bourbon depth settles into the honey carrots, and the oak softens the caramelized sugar. Works; gentle composed match.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|House Wedge": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth leans against the wedge's iceberg-and-bleu cool crunch: the brown-spirit warmth threads the wedge, and the rounded sweetness brightens the bowl. Works; HH 20's aged character meets the glaze at collector register.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Kansas City": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked with the KC — iconic Double-Oaked benchmark against an 18oz strip. Excellent; Woodford Double Oaked's intensified-caramel is the featured iconic-Double-Oaked-KC pairing — the benchmark everyone recognizes.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Loaded Potato": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the loaded potato's rich loaded-potato soup: the brown-spirit warmth threads the loaded potato soup, and the vanilla folds into the cream. Works; the complex profile is over-specified for this dish.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Lobster Mac": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's rounded-oak bourbon character sits alongside the lobster mac's shellfish-in-cream indulgence: the brown-spirit warmth threads the lobster mac, and the vanilla lifts the cream. Works; safe call, not the headline.",
  "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked|Market Fish": "Woodford Reserve Double Oaked's oak-and-vanilla bourbon depth overwhelms the market fish's clean white-fish flesh -- bourbon depth belongs with red meat, not flaky white fish. The plate deserves Joseph Mellot Sancerre or Jean-Pierre Grossot Chablis, not a bourbon. Avoid; one of those is the move. Woodford Reserve Double Oaked lands on the steak course — not here.",
